window.__AAPS_INDEX__ = {"meta": {"generated": "2026-09-06T04:23:10+00:00", "counts": {"docs": 6, "threads": 53, "distilled": 446}}, "docs": [{"id": "doc:browser-build", "type": "docs", "slug": "browser-build", "title": "Browser build", "source_url": "https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/SettingUpAaps/BrowserBuild.html", "text": "Browser build\n# Browser build\n\nBuilding AAPS with GitHub Actions.\nMinimum AAPS version supported is 3.3.2.1.\n\n## Build yourself instead of download\n\nThe AAPS app (an apk file) is not available for download, due to regulations around medical devices. It is legal to build the app for your own use, but you must not give a copy to others!\nSee  FAQ page for details.\n\n## Device and software specifications for building AAPS\n\nWe recommend using an Android device. You can also use a computer or an iOS device.\nYou will need to use multiple tabs in your browser, and switch from one to the other. Example Chrome:\nYou also need a Google account so that the app can be saved in your Google Drive.\nNote\nThis wiki assumes you’re performing all operations with your cellular phone and the Chrome web browser.\n You will need to jump from tab to tab: start with all tabs closed to avoid losing yourself when switching from one to another.\n\n## 1. AAPS personal fork\n\nYou will need to secretly store your personal Android Java Key and Google Drive information in GitHub (later in the process, we will explain how).\nSince this cannot be done inside the public repository of AndroidAPS, you need to make your personal copy of the source code (called a fork).\n\n### GitHub account\n\nYou need to  create a GitHub account if you don’t have one yet.\n You can sign up with your email, or you can sign up with Google. Follow the registration and verification process.\nWhen you have an account,  sign in to GitHub .\n\n### Fork AndroidAPS\n\nOpen the official AndroidAPS repository following  this link .\nTap on the fork icon. This will create a copy inside your own account.\nScroll down the next screen and tap  Create Fork .\nNote: you can  unselect “Copy the main branch only” if you will want to build developers versions or customizations.\nNote\nYou cannot fork and you see this?\nCreate a new fork\nA fork is a copy of a repository. Forking a repository allows you to freely experiment with changes without affecting the original project. View existing forks.\nRequired fields are marked with an asterisk (*).\nNo available destinations to fork this repository.\n This means you already have an existing fork of AndroidAPS.\n Make sure it’s up to date and continue to Preparation Steps.\nWarning\nNever delete your fork without having done a backup of your secrets!\nGitHub now displays your personal copy of AndroidAPS. Leave this web browser tab open.\n\n## 2. Preparation Steps\n\n- If you are building from an Android device, install  File Manager Plus from the Google Play store.\nFile Manager Plus\nInstall  File Manager Plus from the Google Play store.\nThe app is necessary for the preliminary phase and you can safely delete it from your phone once you’ve successfully build and installed AAPS.\nCheck this is the correct app and tap Install, then Open.\nTap Next to accept the Privacy Policy.\nTap Next to allow the app to access the phone files.\nSwitch to enable access to all files.\nAllow File Manager + notifications.\nConsent to profiling.\n- Download the preparation file from here:  aaps-ci-preparation.html\nNote\n- If you open this page from within an app (via a web view), the HTML file may not download. Please copy the URL and open it in your browser instead:\n<https://github.com/nightscout/aaps-ci-preparation/releases/download/release-v1.1.2/aaps-ci-preparation.html>\nOr visit the latest release page:\n<https://github.com/nightscout/aaps-ci-preparation/releases/latest>\n2.Backup copy hosted on this site:\n- If the external link is also unavailable, you can use this backup file to download.\n aaps-ci-preparation.html\nAndroidAPS build requires private keys, that are stored in a Java KeyStore (JKS):\n- If this is your first time building AAPS (or you don’t have a an Android Studio JKS), follow  AAPS-CI Option 1 – Generate JKS to complete the setup.\nWarning\nBuilding AAPS with  Option 1 will not allow you to upgrade your existing AAPS. You will need to:\n- Export settings on your phone.\n- Copy or upload the settings file from your phone to an external location (i.e. your computer, cloud storage service…).\n- Generate a new version of the signed apk as described in Option 1 and transfer it to your phone.\n- Uninstall previous AAPS version on your phone.\n- Install new AAPS version on your phone.\n- Import settings to restore your objectives and configuration.\n- Restore your data from Nightscout.\n- If you want to use your own JKS (the one you used on a previous build of AAPS from a computer in Android Studio), you know its password and alias (key0), please choose  AAPS-CI Option 2 – Upload Existing JKS .\nThe AAPS app will be saved in your Google Cloud drive once built.\n\n### AAPS-CI Option 1 – Generate JKS\n\n- Suitable for first-time users, or those without a JKS, or who have forgotten the password or alias.\n- Here are examples using multiple platforms below.\n- Select your platform in the list below, between Android (preferred choice), iOS or Computer.\n Android\nCompatible with Android (The simplest, recommended as the first choice)\n Wiki\n\n### Open the CI preparation help file\n\nWith File Manager+, open the file  aaps-ci-preparation-html you downloaded above.\nSelect Downloads.\nAnd search for this file, tap it to open it, open it with Chrome, tap Just once.\nIt will open like this.\nSelect Generate JKS. The field below will populate with characters.\nKeep this tab open.\n\n### Create a new secret in GitHub\n\nReturn to your GitHub browser tab: your own AndroidAPS copy.\n\n- Top right, tap the  ... button\n- Select Settings in the list\nScroll down to Security and select Secrets and variables.\nNow select Actions\nScroll down to Repository secrets and tap New repository secret\nYou will see this dialog (scroll down if it’s not visible).\nLeave the tab opened like this.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the top Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\nIn the Name field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the second Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n- In the Secret field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\n- Tap Add secret.\nCheck the secret has been added, scroll down to verify.\n Video\n iOS\nCompatible with iOS (using iPad as an example)\n Computer\nUse a computer (supports Windows/Mac/Linux)\nOpen the webpage  <https://simplewebserver.org/download.html>\nInstall Simple HTTP Server\n If you are a Windows/Mac user, you can install it from the store.\n After clicking the link, you will be asked whether to allow opening it. Please choose Open Link.\nExample on Mac:\n- get → install → open\n- Click Get Started\n- Click Get Server\n- In Folder Path, select the folder where aaps-ci-preparation.html is located, and then click Create Server.\n- Seeing this screen means the server has been started.\n- Do not close Simple HTTP Server. Please switch to your browser and open\n<http://127.0.0.1:8080/aaps-ci-preparation.html>\n- For the subsequent steps, please refer to the video below, starting from 1 minute 37 seconds.\nSkip the next section and continue  here .\n---### AAPS-CI Option 2 – Upload Existing JKS\n- Suitable for users who already have a JKS and know the JKS password and alias (For  KEYSTORE_PASSWORD ,  KEY_ALIAS , and  KEY_PASSWORD , enter your actual password and alias in GitHub - those from Android Studio, see below where you used them.)\nKEY + PASSWORDS\n- Here are examples using multiple platforms below.\n- Select your platform in the list below, between Android (preferred choice) or Computer.\n Android\nCompatible with Android (The simplest, recommended as the first choice)\n Wiki\n\n### Copy your Android Studio key in your Google Cloud drive\n\nOn your computer, search for the keystore file you used to build AAPS. It is named with the extension  .jks .\nDrag it into  your Google Drive , either inside the browser or your mapped Google Drive.\nOpen File Manager Plus and select Cloud.\nAdd a Cloud location.\nChoose Google Drive.\nSelect your Google Drive account email. Tap OK.\nYour Google Cloud drive should display its contents. Now return to the app home page.\n\n### Open the CI preparation help file\n\nOpen the file  aaps-ci-preparation-html you downloaded above.\nSelect Downloads.\nAnd search for this file, tap it to open it, open it with Chrome, tap Just once.\nIt will open like this.\nScroll down to Option 2: Upload Existing JKS. Expand the interface.\nSelect Choose File.\nPick your KeyStore file from your Google Drive files.\nThe field below will populate.\nKeep this tab open.\n\n### Create a new secret in GitHub\n\nReturn to your GitHub browser tab: your own AndroidAPS copy.\n\n- Top right, tap the  ... button\n- Select Settings in the list\nScroll down to Security and select Secrets and variables.\nNow select Actions\nScroll down to Repository secrets and tap New repository secret\nYou will see this dialog (scroll down if it’s not visible).\nLeave the tab opened like this.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the top Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\nIn the Name field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the second Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n- In the Secret field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\n- Tap Add secret.\nCheck the secret has been added, scroll down to verify.\nAdd a new secret: tap the New repository secret button.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the top Copy button to copy  KEYSTORE_PASSWORD .\nNote: if you’re comfortable with typing the key names directly in GitHub you don’t need to Copy/Paste. If you’re not sure you will type exactly the same key name, continue like this. Note that you shouldn’t leave  : at the end of the key name.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n- Paste the new key name.\n- In the Secret entry, put your KeyStore password (don’t leave it empty).\n- Tap Add secret.\nCheck the secret has been added, scroll down to verify.\nTap the New repository secret button shown above.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the top Copy button to copy  KEYSTORE_ALIAS .\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n- Paste the new key name.\n- In the Secret entry, put your KeyStore Alias (usually it’s  key0 , lowercase with the number zero, not the letter O). Don’t let Android autocorrect it.\n- Tap Add secret.\nCheck the secret has been added, scroll down to verify.\nTap the New repository secret button shown above.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the top Copy button to copy  KEY_PASSWORD .\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n- Paste the new key name.\n- In the Secret entry, put your Key password (don’t leave it empty). It is usually the same than your KeyStore password.\n- Tap Add secret.\nCheck the secret has been added, scroll down to verify.\n Video\n Computer\nUse a computer (supports Windows/Mac/Linux)\nInstall Simple HTTP Server\n If you are a Windows/Mac user, you can install it from the store. After clicking the link, you will be asked whether to allow opening it. Please choose Open Link.\nExample on Mac:\n- get → install → open\n- Click Get Started\n- Click Get Server\n- In Folder Path, select the folder where aaps-ci-preparation.html is located, and then click Create Server.\n- Seeing this screen means the server has been started.\n- Do not close Simple HTTP Server. Please switch to your browser and open\n<http://127.0.0.1:8080/aaps-ci-preparation.html>\n- For the subsequent steps, please refer to the video below, starting from 2 minute 18 seconds.\n\n### AAPS-CI Google Drive Auth\n\nWarning\nNo matter which of the prior sets of instructions you followed (option 1 or option 2), you MUST add the Google Drive authorization to successfully use the Browser Build.\nNote: If you already followed this part in the video, you can now skip to  here .\nReturn to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nScroll down to the Google Drive Auth section and tap Start Auth.\nSelect your Google account.\nScroll down and accept the access. The web page needs it to obtain the Google Drive authentication key.\nTap Continue.\nThe  GDRIVE_OAUTH2 field will populate, tap the top Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\nScroll down to Repository secrets and tap New repository secret.\nIf you followed Option 1 you should see this:\nIf you followed Option 2 there will be more keys:\nIn the Name field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\nSwitch to the File Explorer Plus tab.\nTap the second Copy button.\nSwitch back to the GitHub tab.\n\n- In the Secret field, paste the text you just copied. Use a long touch on the text box to show the paste menu.\n- Tap Add secret.\nYou should have either two (option 1) or five (option 2) secrets entries now.\nGitHub will now be able to store the AAPS apk file in your Google Drive, once built.\n\n## AAPS-CI GitHub Actions to Build the AAPS APK\n\n- Suitable for general users.\n Wiki\n\n### Run the Workflow to Build the Signed APK\n\n- In your GitHub copy of AndroidAPS, select Actions.\n- Expand All Workflows.\n- Select AAPS-CI\n- Scroll down and tap Run Workflow.\n- Select the branch you want to deploy (master), the  variant (fullRelease) and tap Run Workflow.\n- You will see the message Workflow run was successfully requested. Refresh your browser page and you will be able to monitor the build progress. When the action completes, the AAPS CI action will show a green tick mark. You have successfully built the updated version of Android APS.\n\n### Install the AAPS APK\n\n- Open your Google Drive\n- Browse into AAPS, select the new version folder and you will find both the phone and Android Wear versions.\n Video\n\n### Build Version selection\n\nOnly AAPS versions from 3.3.2.1 and above will build with the Browser method.\n\n### Build Variants selection\n\nNote: both Android and Android Wear apps will be built automatically.\n\n- Select the variant you need:\n- fullRelease: For regular pump usage with full functionality.\n- aapsclientRelease, aapsclient2Release : For caregivers (requires  Nightscout )。\n- pumpcontrolRelease: To replace your pump app/controller\nVariants ending with “Debug” indicates that the APK will be built in debug mode, which is useful for developers for troubleshooting.\n\n## AAPS-CI Troubleshooting\n\n### aaps-ci-preparation web page\n\n- When you open aaps-ci-preparation.html using a file manager, it will start a temporary local server on your phone to display the webpage and receive the Google refresh token.\n- If you see the screen below, it means you have been inactive for a while, and the file manager has already shut down the local server.\n- Please reopen aaps-ci-preparation.html using the file manager app and complete the remaining steps.\n\n### Google Refresh Token Expired\n\n- Google OAuth2 refresh tokens will expire if not used for 6 months, and may also become invalid under other conditions (e.g., you have changed your Google account password, or manually revoked access). For more details, see the  Google OAuth2 documentation .\n- You will see an error indicating that the access token is invalid, as shown below:\n- If your build fails due to an expired or revoked Google refresh token, you will need to redo the  Google Drive Auth steps to obtain a new  GDRIVE_OAUTH2 token and update the secret in your GitHub repository, then re-run the build workflow.\n\n### Disable Software That May Interfere With OAUTH Verification\n\n- Disable any VPN or security app (firewall, antimalware,…) on the phone before trying to get the OAUTH key.\n\n### Check GitHub Actions Permission Settings\n\n- Make sure GitHub Actions policies are set to “Allow all actions and reusable workflows” (Settings → Actions → General).\nactions/checkout@v4 and  actions/setup-java@v4 are not allowed to be used in  xxxxx/AndroidAPS . Actions in this workflow must be: within a repository owned by  xxxxx\n---Warning\nCustomizations are usually not necessary. This is for your information ony.\n\n## If you want to add a specific commit to your branch, please use cherry-pick\n\n- Use workflow from Branch: Please enter the branch name you want to cherry-pick to.\n- Upstream Repository: Please enter the repository name you want to cherry-pick from.\n- Commit SHA: Please enter the commit SHA you want to cherry-pick.(like git commit hash)\n- Select Build Variant:  variant\n\n## CI KeyStore Export\n\nIf you want to export your stored keystore, use this method.\nThis script will export your previously configured keystore information (from Option 1 or Option 2) as a password-protected ZIP file to the  /AAPS/KeyStore directory in your Google Drive.\nWarning\nBefore using this export method, make sure your keystore and Google Drive settings have been completed.\n\n### Steps\n\n- Add ZIP Password Secret:\n- Go to your repository’s  Settings →  Secrets and variables →  Actions\n- Click  New repository secret\n- In the  Name field, enter:  ZIP_PASSWORD\n- In the  Secret field, enter your custom ZIP encryption password\n- Use only English letters and numbers for the password (no special symbols)\n- Click  Add secret\n- Run Export Workflow:\n- Go to the  Actions tab in your repository\n- Select  CI KeyStore Export\n- Click  Run workflow\n- The exported keystore ZIP file will be saved to your Google Drive"}, {"id": "doc:building-aaps", "type": "docs", "slug": "building-aaps", "title": "Building AAPS", "source_url": "https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/SettingUpAaps/BuildingAaps.html", "text": "Building AAPS\n# Building AAPS\n\n## Build yourself instead of download\n\nThe AAPS app (an apk file) is not available for download, due to regulations around medical devices. It is legal to build the app for your own use, but you must not give a copy to others!\nSee  FAQ page for details.\n---Three methods are available to build the AAPS app:\n\n### Build with a browser (recommended)\n\nYou can build the app with your smartphone using GitHub actions, and save it in your Google Drive.\nFollow these instructions.\n---### Build with Android Studio\nYou can build the app with your computer using Android Studio. This used to be the only build option, nowadays Android Studio is mostly used by developers who consider making code changes.\nFollow these instructions.\n---### Build using the command-line\nThis option is intended for those who prefer to build AAPS in local command-line, without installing Android Studio.\nFollow these instructions."}, {"id": "doc:dexcom-g7", "type": "docs", "slug": "dexcom-g7", "title": "Dexcom G7 and ONE+", "source_url": "https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/Hardware/DexcomG7.html", "text": "Dexcom G7 and ONE+\n# Dexcom G7 and ONE+\n\n## Fundamental in advance\n\nNoteworthy is the fact that the G7 and ONE+ systems, compared to the G6, do not smooth the values, neither in the app, nor in the reader. More details about this  here .\nSmoothing method\nRead  Smoothing method suggestions to use for Dexcom G7/ONE+/Stelo\n\n## 1. xDrip+ (direct connection to G7 or ONE+)\n\n- Follow the instructions here:  xDrip+ G7\n- Select xDrip+ in  ConfigBuilder, BG Source .\n- Adjust the xDrip+ settings according to the explanations on the xDrip+ settings page  xDrip+ settings\n\n## 2. Build Your Own Dexcom App (G7)\n\nOld app version\nDexcom BYODA is now a very old version of the app and cannot be updated.\n\n- Build Your Own Dexcom App (BYODA) supports local broadcast to AAPS and/or xDrip+\n- This app lets you use your Dexcom G7 with any Android smartphone.\n- Uninstall the original Dexcom app\n- Install the downloaded apk\n- Enter sensor code in patched app\n- After short time BYODA should pick-up transmitter signal\n\n## 3. Patched Dexcom G7 App (DiaKEM)\n\nNo new users\nLatest Dexcom servers update broke DiaKEM for new installs: the G7 app no longer can get through the login and onboarding process that happens on a fresh install of the app. Existing users do not experience issues for now: do not logout, wipe data, or reinstall the G7 app as that will prevent you from getting the app up and running again. If it is already running, you should be unaffected.\nNote: AAPS 3.2.0.0 or higher is required! Not available for ONE+.\n\n### Install a new patched (!) G7 app and start the sensor\n\nA patched Dexcom G7 app (DiaKEM) gives access to the Dexcom G7 data. This is not the BYODA app as this app can not receive G7 data at the moment.\n\n- Uninstall the original Dexcom app if you used it before (A running sensor session can be continued - note the sensor code before removal of the app!)\n- Download and install the patched.apk  here .\n- Enter sensor code in the patched app.\n- Follow the general recommendations for CGM hygiene and sensor placement found  here .\n- After the warm-up phase, the values are displayed as usual in the G7 app.\n\n### Configuration in AAPS\n\n- Select ‘BYODA’ in in  ConfigBuilder, BG Source - even if it is not the BYODA app!\n- If AAPS does not receive any values, switch to another BG source and then back to ‘BYODA’ to invoke the query for approving data exchange between AAPS and BYODA.\n\n## 4. xDrip+ (companion mode)\n\n- Download and install xDrip+:  xDrip\n- As data source in xDrip+ “Companion App” must be selected and under Advanced Settings > Bluetooth Settings > “Companion Bluetooth” must be enabled.\n- Select xDrip+ in in  ConfigBuilder, BG Source .\n- Adjust the xDrip+ settings according to the explanations on the xDrip+ settings page  xDrip+ settings\n\n## 5. Juggluco\n\nVersion 9.0+ required\n\n- Disable the app previously connected to the sensor: Uninstall the app or use “Force Stop.” Disable “Nearby Devices” permission in app settings. Restrict the app’s battery usage.\n- Forget the sensor in Bluetooth settings: In Android settings, find the sensor in bonded devices and select “Forget.” Dexcom G7 sensor names start with DXCM.\n- Avoid interference from other sensors: Keep old Dexcom sensors out of Bluetooth range.\n- Connect the G7 sensor to Juggluco: Open Juggluco → Left menu → Photo. Scan the data matrix on the G7 sensor’s applicator. Wait up to 5 minutes for Juggluco to find the sensor.\n- Pairing requirements: Agree to pair the sensor with Juggluco. Ensure the screen isn’t locked during pairing. If pairing fails, wait 5 minutes before trying again.\n- Exception: Wear OS watches can bond without pressing an agree button."}, {"id": "doc:omnipod-dash", "type": "docs", "slug": "omnipod-dash", "title": "Omnipod DASH", "source_url": "https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/CompatiblePumps/OmnipodDASH.html", "text": "Omnipod DASH\n# Omnipod DASH\n\nThese instructions are for configuring the  Omnipod DASH generation pump  (NOT Omnipod Eros) , available in  AAPS from version 3.0.\n\n## Omnipod DASH specifications\n\nThese are the specifications of the  Omnipod DASH (‘DASH’) and what differentiates it from the  Omnipod EROS (‘EROS’):\n\n- The DASH pods are identified by a  blue needle cap (EROS has a clear needle cap). The pods are otherwise identical in terms of physical dimensions.\n- DASH does not require a BLE link/bridge device (NO RileyLink, OrangeLink, or EmaLink needed).\n- The DASH’s Bluetooth connection is used only when sending a command (e.g a Bolus), and disconnects right after issuing the command.\n- No more “no connection to link device / pod” errors with DASH.\n- AAPS will wait for pod’s accessibility to send commands.\n- On pod activation,  AAPS will find and connect to a new DASH pod.\n- Expected range from phone: 5-10 meters (YMMV).\n\n## Omnipod DASH known AAPS constraints/issues\n\n- Android 16 requires  AAPS version 3.3.2.1 or later.\n- General advice is to run  AAPS on Android 14 or 16. Android 15 has many reported  issues from the community. However, if you do run on Android 15 you will likely need to enable Bluetooth Bonding to successfully activate and use Pods, see  General Troubleshooting for more info on the Bonding settings.\n- Temporary Basal rate changes (which occur frequently when the loop is active, especially overnight) result in under-delivery of insulin. This is effectively a hardware limitation of the Omnipod DASH. The issue has been addressed in AAPS 3.4.2.3, but the functionality is currently opt-in. Follow the  Basal Drift Fix Instructions  instructions to enable it. For more information regarding the fix see  Github Issue - 4783 for more info.\n- Dash only supports basal rate in 0.05 U/h steps. If you try to set Basal with 0.01 steps in your  AAPS profile , AAPS will not give a warning even though the pod will round up the rate into 0.05 steps. If you view POD MGMT/Pod History it will display that 0.05 basal was set. This also means the lowest basal rate allowed by the DASH in  AAPS is 0.05U/h.\n- The activation status of a Pod is stored in the settings file, if you export a settings file with an active pod. Then change to a new pod, then restore the settings from your previous export you will have now restored the old pod activation and removed the new pod activation. This is why we recommend to export settings after each pod activation to allow a restore of that pods activation state if something happens to your rig.\n- When setting a new basal profile, DASH will suspend delivery before setting the new basal  Profile . If there is a communication interruption or error, the basal profile won’t automatically re-start. See section  Resuming Insulin Delivery for details.\n- If alerts are configured, and the pod is about to expire, the pod will keep beeping until alerts are silenced, see  Silencing Pod Alerts for details.\n- There are a number of known issues with Bluetooth which can cause pod activation problems. See  Bluetooth Troubleshooting for the known issue and solutions to these problems.\n\n## Hardware/Software Requirements\n\n- Omnipod DASH is identified by the blue needle cap.\n- A Compatible Android phone with a Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) (see  Phones for more info), additionally the following information will help guide you on other key considerations around successfully activating and using the DASH on a compatible phone:\n- The  AAPS Omnipod Dash driver connects with the DASH Pod using Bluetooth.\nAAPS will automatically establish a new Bluetooth connection to the Pod every time it needs to send a command (e.g a Bolus), after sending the command the Bluetooth connection is immediately disconnected.\n- NOTE:\n- The Bluetooth connection can be interrupted/disturbed by other Bluetooth devices linked to the phone that is running  AAPS , like earbuds etc… Devices like this can cause connection errors or pod activation issues on some models of phones. It’s a good idea to review the  tested hardware setups list for known working configurations before committing to a new rig built around Omnipod DASH.\n- There are a number of known issues with Bluetooth which can cause pod activation problems (See  Troubleshooting for advice on other Bluetooth issues) specifically the  Bluetooth related issues section.\n- For  Android 15 or below: You  MUST use  Version 3.0 or newer of AAPS using the  Build APK instructions, however it’s advisable to run the latest released version.\n- For  Android 16 : you  MUST use  Version 3.3.2.1 or newer of AAPS using the  Build APK instructions, due to Android 16 changing how its Bluetooth works. Any version earlier than 3.3.2.1 will likely cause pod failures and/or activation  issues .\n- A supported  Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM)\nThe instructions below explain how to activate a new pod session using  AAPS . You should wait for your current Pod to be close expiry, as you will need to activate a new Pod with  AAPS . Once a pod is de-activated it cannot be reused/re-activated, the de-activation is final.\n\n## Before You Begin\n\nEnsure you have read and understand this whole guide, have read and understand the  Before You Begin section, as well as  Omnipod and AAPS Constraints and Issues to avoid running into a known problem.\n\n### SAFETY FIRST - You  SHOULD NOT try to connect  AAPS to a pod for the first time without having access to all of the following\n\n- Extra pods (3 or more spare)\n- Spare Insulin and MDI equipment\n- A working Omnipod PDM (In case  AAPS fails)\n- Supported Phones are a must! (See  Hardware/Software Requirements )\n- Correct version of AAPS built and installed\n\n### Your Omnipod Dash PDM will become redundant after the AAPS Dash driver activates your pod\n\n- Before using  AAPS you or your care giver would have had to manage the Pod using the Omnipod PDM (or in some regions a Phone app) to send commands to your DASH (e.g a Bolus).\n- The DASH can only facilitate a single Bluetooth device (e.g PDM or Phone) connection to manage and send commands.\n- The device that successfully activates the pod is the only device allowed to communicate with that Pod from that point forward. This means that once you activate a DASH with your Android phone using  AAPS ,  you will no longer be able to use your PDM with that pod! For the time that Pod is active the  AAPS Dash driver running on your Android phone is now the new PDM for your pod.\n- DO NOT Throw away your PDM! It is recommended to keep it around as a backup and for emergencies, for instance when your phone gets lost or  AAPS is not working correctly.\n\n### Your pod  WILL NOT stop delivering insulin when it is not connected to AAPS\n\nDefault basal rates are programmed on the pod on activation as defined in the current active  Profile .\n As long as  AAPS is operational it will send basal rate adjustment commands that run for a maximum of 120 minutes.\n When for some reason the pod does not receive any new commands (for instance because communication was lost due to Pod ➜ phone distance) the pod will automatically fall back to default basal rates as defined in your  Profile .\n\n### AAPS Profile(s) do not support 30 minute basal rate time frames\n\nIf you are new to  AAPS and are setting up your basal rate  Profile for the first time, please be aware that basal rates starting on a half-hour basis are not supported. For example, on your Omnipod PDM, if you have a basal rate of 1.1 units which starts at 09:30 and has a duration of 2 hours ending at 11:30, it is not possible replicate this exact Basal  Profile in  AAPS .\n You will need to change this 1.1 unit basal rate to a time range of either 9:00-11:00 or 10:00-12:00. Even though the DASH hardware itself supports the 30 minute basal rate  Profile increments,  AAPS does NOT support this feature.\n\n### 0U/h Profile basal rates are NOT supported in AAPS\n\nWhile the DASH does support a zero basal rate,  AAPS uses multiples of the user’s  Profile basal rate to determine automated treatment; it cannot function with a zero basal rate.\n Instead a temporary zero basal rate can be achieved through the “Disconnect pump” function, or through a combination of Disable Loop/Temp Basal Rate or Suspend Loop/Temp Basal Rate.\nNOTE: The lowest basal rate allowed by the DASH in  AAPS is 0.05U/h.\n\n## Selecting Dash in AAPS\n\nThere are  two available options to configure Omnipod in  AAPS :\n\n### Option 1: New installations\n\nWhen installing  AAPS for the first time, the  Setup Wizard will guide new users through key features and installation requirements for  AAPS .\n Select “DASH” when you reach Pump selection.\nWhen in doubt you can also select “Virtual Pump” and select “DASH” later, after setting up  AAPS (See Option 2).\n\n### Option 2: The Config Builder\n\nOn an existing installation you can select the  DASH pump from the Config builder:\nOn the top-left hand corner  hamburger menu select  Config Builder (1) ➜  Pump ➜  Dash ➜  Settings Gear (3) by selecting the  radio button (2) titled  Dash .\nSelecting the  checkbox (4) next to the  Settings Gear (3) will allow the DASH menu to be displayed as a tab in the  AAPS interface titled  DASH . Checking this box will facilitate your access to the DASH commands when using  AAPS .\nNOTE: A faster way to access the  Dash settings can be found below in the DASH settings section of this document.\n\n### Verification of Omnipod Driver Selection\n\nTo verify that you have selected the DASH in  AAPS , if you have  checked the box (4) ,  swipe to the left from the  Overview tab, where you will now see a  DASH tab on  AAPS . If this box is left unchecked, you’ll find the DASH tab in the hamburger menu upper left.\n\n## Dash Configuration\n\nSwipe left to the  DASH tab where you will be able to manage all pod functions (some of these functions are not enabled or visible without an active pod session):\n ‘Refresh’ pod connectivity and status, be able to silence pod alarms when the pod beeps\n ‘Pod Management’ (Activate, Deactivate, Play test beep, and Pod history)\n\n### Activate Pod\n\n- Navigate to the  DASH tab and click on the  POD MGMT (1) button, and then click on  Activate Pod (2) .\n- The  Fill Pod screen is displayed. Fill a new pod with  at least 80 units of insulin and listen for two beeps indicating that the pod is ready to be primed.\nNOTE: When calculating the total amount of insulin you need for 3 days, please take into account that priming the pod will use about 3-10 units.\nEnsure that the new pod and the phone running  AAPS are within close proximity of each other and click the  Next button.\nNOTE : if the error message below pops up  ‘Could not find an available pod for activation’ (this can happen), do not panic. Click on the  Retry button. In most situations activation will continue successfully.\n- On the  Initialize Pod screen, the pod will begin priming (you will hear a click followed by a series of ticking sounds as the pod primes itself).\n A green checkmark will be shown upon successful priming, and the  Next button will become enabled. Click on the  Next button to complete the pod priming initialization and display the  Attach Pod screen.\n- Next, prepare the infusion site ready to receive the new pod. Wash hands to avoid any risk of infection. Clean the infusion site by either using soap and water or an alcohol wipe to disinfect and let the skin air dry completely before proceeding.\n If you get skin irritation from the adhesive consider using a Barrier Wipe or Barrier Spray.\nRemove the pod’s blue plastic needle cap. If you see something that sticks out of the pod or it looks unusual,  STOP the process and start with a new pod. If everything looks  OK , proceed to take off the white paper backing from the adhesive and stick the pod to the selected site on your body.\nWhen finished, click on the  Next button.\n- The  Attach Pod dialog box will now appear.  click on the OK button ONLY if you are ready to deploy the cannula!\n- After pressing  OK , it may take some time before the DASH responds and inserts the cannula (1-2 minutes maximum).  Be patient!\nNOTE: Before the cannula is inserted, it is good practice to pinch the skin near the cannula insertion point. This ensures a smooth insertion of the needle and will decrease your chances of developing occlusions.\n- A green checkmark is shown on the screen, and the  Next button becomes available to select upon successful cannula insertion.\n Click on the  Next button.\n- The  Pod activated screen is displayed.\nClick on the green  Finished button.\nCongratulations! You have now started a new pod session.\n- The  Pod management menu screen should now display the  Activate Pod (1) button  disabled and the  Deactivate Pod (2) button  enabled . This is because a pod is now active and you cannot activate an additional pod without deactivating the currently active pod first.\nClick on the back button on your phone to return to the  DASH tab screen which will now display Pod information for your active pod session, including current basal rate, pod reservoir level, insulin delivered, pod errors and alerts.\nNOTE: For more details on the information displayed go to the  DASH Tab section of this document.\nNOTE: It is good practice to export settings AFTER activating the pod. Settings should be exported after each pod change and once a month, ensure you copy the exported settings file to a cloud storage location (e.g. Google Drive) or somewhere off your phone in case you loose your phone (see  Export settings ).\n\n### Deactivate Pod\n\nUnder normal circumstances, the expected lifetime of a pod is three days (72 hours) and an additional 8 hours after the pod expiration warning for a total of 80 hours of total pod usage.\nTo deactivate a pod (either from expiration or from a pod failure):\n\n- Go to the  DASH tab, click on the  POD MGMT (1) button, on the  Pod Management screen click on the  Deactivate Pod (2) button.\n- On the  Deactivate Pod screen, click on the  Next button to begin the process of deactivating the pod.\nYou will receive a confirmation beep from the pod that deactivation was successful.\n- A green checkmark will be displayed upon successful deactivation. Click on the  Next button to display the pod deactivated screen.\nYou may now remove your pod as the active session has been deactivated.\n- Click on the green button to return to the  Pod Management screen.\n- You are now on the  Pod Management menu; press the back button on your phone to return to the  DASH tab.\nVerify that the  Pod status: field displays a  No active Pod message.\n\n### Resuming Insulin Delivery\n\nNOTE : During  Profile Switches , like when using the PDM, AAPS must suspend delivery on the Pod before setting the new basal  Profile . If communication fails between the suspend and resume commands, then delivery can stay suspended, Read  Delivery suspended in the troubleshooting section for more details.\nWhen insulin delivery is suspended you will need to issue a command to instruct the active, currently suspended pod to resume insulin delivery. After the command is successfully processed, insulin will resume normal delivery using the current basal rate based on the current time from the active basal  Profile . The pod will again accept commands for bolus,  TBR , and  SMB .\n\n- Go to the  DASH tab and ensure the  Pod status (1) field displays  SUSPENDED , then press the  RESUME DELIVERY (2) button to start the process to instruct the current pod to resume normal insulin delivery. A message  RESUME DELIVERY will display in the  Pod Status (3) field.\n- When the Resume delivery command is successful, a confirmation dialog will display the message  Insulin delivery has been resumed . Click  OK to confirm and proceed.\n- The  DASH tab will update the  Pod status (1) field to display  RUNNING, and the  Resume Delivery button will no longer be displayed\n\n### Silencing Pod Alerts\n\nThe process below will show you how to acknowledge and dismiss pod beeps when the active pod time reaches the warning time limit before the pod expiration of 72 hours (3 days). This warning time limit is defined in the  Hours before shutdown Dash alerts setting. The maximum life of a pod is 80 hours (3 days 8 hours), however Insulet recommends not exceeding the 72 hours (3 days) limit.\nNOTE : The  SILENCE ALERTS (3) button is only available on the  DASH tab when the pod expiration or low reservoir alert has been triggered. If the  SILENCE ALERTS button is not visible and you hear beep sounds from the pod, try to ‘Refresh pod status’.\n\n- When the defined  Hours before shutdown warning time limit is reached, the pod will issue warning beeps to inform you that it is approaching its expiration time and a pod change will be required soon.\n You can verify this on the  DASH tab, the  Pod expires: (1) field will show the exact time the pod will expire (72 hours after activation), and the text will turn  red after this time has passed.\n Under the  Active Pod alerts (2) field the status message  Pod will expire soon is displayed. This also will trigger displaying the  SILENCE ALERTS (3) button.\n- Go to the  DASH tab and press the  SILENCE ALERTS (2) button.  AAPS sends the command to the pod to deactivate the pod expiration warning beeps and updates the  Pod status (1) field with  ACKNOWLEDGE ALERTS .\n- Upon  successful deactivation of the alerts,  2 beeps will be issued by the active pod and a confirmation dialog will display the message  Activate alerts have been Silenced . Click the  OK button to confirm and dismiss the dialog.\n- Go to the  DASH tab. Under the  Active Pod alerts field, the warning message is no longer displayed, and the active pod will no longer issue pod expiration warning beeps.\n\n### View Pod History\n\nThis section explains how to review your active pod history and filter by different action categories. The pod history tool allows you to view the actions and results committed to your currently active pod during its three days (72 - 80 hours) life.\nThis feature is helpful in verifying boluses, TBRs and basal commands that were sent to the pod. The remaining categories are useful for troubleshooting issues and determining the order of events that occurred leading up to a failure.\nNOTE: Only the last command can be uncertain . New commands  will not be sent until the  last ‘uncertain’ command becomes ‘confirmed’ or ‘denied’ . The way to ‘fix’ uncertain commands is to  ‘refresh pod status’ .\n\n- Go to the  DASH tab and press the  POD MGMT (1) button to access the  Pod Management menu and then press the  Pod history (2) button to access the pod history screen.\n- On the  Pod history screen, the default category of  All (1) is displayed, showing the  Date and Time (2) of all pod  Actions (3) and  Results (4) in reverse chronological order. Use your phone’s  back button 2 times to return to the  DASH tab in the main  AAPS interface.\n\n## DASH Tab\n\nBelow is an explanation of the layout and meaning of the icons and status fields on the  DASH tab in the main AAPS interface.\nNOTE: If any message in the  DASH tab status fields report (uncertain), then you will need to press the Refresh button to clear it and refresh the pod status.\n\n### Fields\n\n- Bluetooth Address: Displays the current bluetooth address of the connected Pod.\n- Bluetooth Status: Displays the current connection status.\n- Sequence Number: Displays the sequence number of the active POD.\n- Firmware Version: Displays the firmware version for the active connection.\n- Time on Pod: Displays the current time on the Pod.\n- Pod status: Displays the Pod status.\n- Last connection: Displays time of last communication with the Pod.\n- Moments ago - less than 20 seconds ago.\n- Less than a minute ago - more than 20 seconds but less than 60 seconds ago.\n- 1 minute ago - more than 60 seconds but less than 120 seconds (2 min)\n- XX minutes ago - more than 2 minutes ago as defined by the value of XX\n- Last bolus: Displays the amount of the last bolus sent to the active pod and how long ago it was issued in parenthesis.\n- Base Basal rate: Displays the basal rate programmed for the current time from the basal rate profile.\n- Temp basal rate: Displays the currently running Temporary Basal Rate in the following format\n- {Units per hour} @{TBR start time} ({minutes run}/{total minutes TBR will be run})\n- Example:* 0.00U/h @18:25 ( 90/120 minutes)\n- Reservoir: Displays over 50+U left when more than 50 units are left in the reservoir. Below 50 U, the exact units are displayed.\n- Total delivered: Displays the total number of units of insulin delivered from the reservoir. This includes insulin used for activating and priming.\n- Errors: Displays the last error encountered. Review the  Pod history and log files for past errors and more detailed information.\n- Active pod alerts: Reserved for currently running alerts on the active pod.\n\n### Buttons\n\n Sends a refresh command to the active pod to update communication.\n\n- Use to refresh the pod status and dismiss status fields that contain the text (uncertain).\n- See the  Troubleshooting section below for additional information.\n Navigates to the Pod management menu.\n When pressed this will disable the pod alerts beeps and notifications (expiry, low reservoir..).\n- Button is displayed only when pod time is past expiration warning time.\n- Upon successful dismissal, this icon will no longer appear.\n Resumes the currently suspended insulin delivery in the active pod.\n\n### Pod Management Menu\n\nBelow is describes the purpose of each icon on the  Pod Management menu, accessed by pressing  POD MGMT (1) button from the  DASH tab.\nThe table below describes each button and it’s function:\nButton\nFunction\n1\nAccess the Pod Mgmt settings\n2\nActivate Pod : Primes and activates a new pod.\n3\nDeactivate Pod : Deactivates the currently active pod.\n4\nPlay Test Beep : Plays a single test beep on the pod when pressed.\n5\nPod history : Displays the active pod activity history.\n\n## Dash Settings\n\nThe Dash driver settings are configurable from the top-left hand corner  hamburger menu under  Config Builder (1) ➜  Pump Dash ➜  Settings Gear (3) by selecting the  radio button (2) titled  Dash . Selecting the  checkbox (4) next to the  Settings Gear (3) will allow the Dash menu to be displayed as a tab in the  AAPS interface titled  DASH .\nNOTE: A faster way to access the  Dash settings is by accessing the  3 dot menu (1) in the upper right hand corner of the  DASH tab and selecting  Dash preferences (2) from the dropdown menu.\nThe settings groups are listed below; you can enable or disable via a toggle switch for most entries described below:\nNOTE: An asterisk (*) denotes the default setting is enabled.\n\n### Confirmation beeps\n\nProvides confirmation beeps from the pod for bolus, basal, SMB, and TBR delivery and changes.\nBolus beeps enabled: Enable or disable confirmation beeps when a bolus is delivered.\nBasal beeps enabled: Enable or disable confirmation beeps when a new basal rate is set, active basal rate is canceled or current basal rate is changed.\nSMB beeps enabled: Enable or disable confirmation beeps when a SMB is delivered.\nTBR beeps enabled: Enable or disable confirmation beeps when a TBR is set or canceled.\n\n### Alerts\n\nProvides  AAPS alerts for pod expiration, shutdown, low reservoir based on the defined threshold units.\nNOTE: an AAPS notification will ALWAYS be issued for any alert after the initial communication with the pod since the alert was triggered. Dismissing the notification will NOT dismiss the alert UNLESS automatically acknowledge Pod alerts is enabled. To MANUALLY dismiss the alert you must visit the  DASH tab and press the  Silence ALERTS button .\nExpiration reminder enabled: Enable or disable the pod expiration reminder set to trigger when the defined number of hours before shutdown is reached.\nHours before shutdown: Defines the number hours before the active pod shutdown occurs, which will then trigger the expiration reminder alert.\nLow reservoir alert enabled: Enable or disable an alert when the pod’s remaining units low reservoir limit is reached as defined in the Number of units field.\nNumber of units: The number of units at which to trigger the pod low reservoir alert.\n\n### Notifications\n\nThe Notification section allows the user to select their preferred notifications and audible phone alerts when AAPS is uncertain about the status of TBR, SMB, or bolus, and when delivery suspended events were successful.\nNOTE: These are notifications only, no audible beep alerts are made.\nSound for uncertain TBR notifications enabled: Enable or disable this setting to trigger an audible alert and visual notification when  AAPS is uncertain if a TBR was successfully set.\nSound for uncertain SMB notifications enabled: Enable or disable this setting to trigger an audible alert and visual notification when  AAPS is uncertain if an SMB was successfully delivered.\nSound for uncertain bolus notifications enabled: Enable or disable this setting to trigger an audible alert and visual notification when  AAPS is uncertain if a bolus was successfully delivered.\nSound when delivery suspended notifications enabled: Enable or disable this setting to trigger an audible alert and visual notification when suspend delivery was successfully delivered.\n\n## Actions (ACT) Tab\n\nThis tab is well documented in the main  AAPS documentation but there are a few items on this tab that are specific to how the DASH differs from tube based pumps, especially after the processes of applying a new pod.\n\n- Go to the  Actions (ACT) tab in the main  AAPS interface.\n- Under the  Careportal (1) section the  Insulin and  Cannula fields will have their  age reset to 0 days and 0 hours  after each pod change . This is done because of how the Omnipod pump is built and operates. Since the pod inserts the cannula directly into the skin at the site of the pod application, a traditional tube is not used in Omnipod pumps.  Therefore after a pod change the age of each of these values will automatically reset to zero. Pump battery age is not reported as the battery in the pod will always be more than the life of the pod (maximum 80 hours). The  pump battery and  insulin reservoir are self contained inside of each pod.\n\n### Level\n\nInsulin Level\nInsulin level displayed is the amount reported by DASH. However, the pod only reports the actual insulin reservoir level when it is below 50 units. Until then “Above 50 units” will be displayed. The amount reported is not exact: when the pod reports ‘empty’ in most cases the reservoir will still have some additional units of insulin left.\nThe DASH overview tab will display as described the below:\n\n- Above 50 Units - The pod reports more than 50 units currently in the reservoir.\n- Below 50 Units - The amount of insulin remaining in the reservoir as reported by the Pod.\nAdditional note:\n- SMS - Returns value or 50+U for SMS responses\n- Nightscout - Uploads value of 50 when over 50 units to Nightscout (version 14.07 and older). Newer versions will report a value of 50+ when over 50 units.\n\n## Known Issues Workarounds\n\nThis section covers common workarounds and settings that need to be changed to enable a feature to work around a community reported issue that has a fix. E.g. the Basal drift enable process is documented here.\n\n### Basal Drift Fix Instructions\n\nThe Omnipod Dash pump has a limitation that can cause it to deliver less basal insulin than  AAPS expects, see  Issue #4783 for more technical details.\nThe Dash uses an internal timer to determine when a basal pulse of 0.05 U is delivered. Once the timer interval elapses, the pulse is delivered. However, this timer is restarted whenever a basal rate change occurs e.g when  AAPS sends a new Basal rate.\nWhen used in combination with looping, this leads to under-delivery of basal insulin, as the algorithm updates the basal rate on the pump frequently.\nThe issue is most apparent during the night. During daytime operation, SMBs often result in a basal rate of 0, which masks the effect. In observed usage, this results in approximately 10% of the expected Total Daily Dose (TDD) not being delivered over a 24-hour period. Additionally, glucose targets are often not reached overnight, particularly after meals with prolonged glucose impact (e.g. pasta).\nNOTE: This issue is especially important to understand for people on very small dosages of insulin, Children for example.\n\n#### Enable Basal Drift Fix in AAPS\n\nYou must be running AAPS Version 3.4.2.3 or later for this feature.\nThe Basal Drift Fix is not enabled by default on AAPS.\nTo enable it:\n\n- Create an empty file named  omnipod_drift_compensation (2) in the  extra (1) subfolder of your phone  AAPS directory .\nNOTE: Ensure you check in the AAPS settings where your AAPS Directory is, and that you placed the file in the correct one, a number of several have been caught out putting the file into the wrong folder.\n- Restart  AAPS . This must be done for it to recognise the file is present and enable the drift compensation feature.\n- Please visit this  Github issue #4783 and thumbs up the first post indicating you are using this feature, we need this data to help demonstrate the feature is widely used. Once there is significant community adoption the removal of the enable file will be possible, we appreciate your support here.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nThis section covers common known issues and solutions for Omnipod DASH use with AAPS. There is also  General Troubleshooting section in the documentation that should be reviewed as it covers relevant topics for some Pod issues too.\n---## Bluetooth related issues\nFor known issues with Bluetooth connections, dropouts of pump/pods, or activation and connection issues  Bluetooth Troubleshooting\n---### Delivery suspended\n\n- There is no suspend button anymore. If you want to “suspend” the pod, you can set a zero  TBR for x minutes.\n- During  Profile Switches , DASH must suspend delivery before setting the new basal  Profile . If communication fails between the two commands, then delivery can stay suspended. When this happens:\n- There will be no insulin delivery, that includes Basal, SMB, Manual bolusing etc.\n- There might be notification that one of the commands is unconfirmed: this depends on when the failure happened.\n- AAPS will try to set the new basal profile every 15 minutes.\n- AAPS will show a notification informing that the delivery is suspended every 15 minutes, if the delivery is still suspended (resume delivery failed).\n- The  Resume delivery button will be active if the user chooses to resume delivery manually.\n- If  AAPS fails to resume delivery on its own (this happens if the pod is unreachable, sound is muted, etc), the pod will start beeping 4 times every minute for 3 minutes, then repeated every 15 minutes if delivery is still suspended for more than 20 minutes.\n- For unconfirmed commands, “refresh pod status” should confirm/deny them.\nNOTE: When you hear beeps from the pod, do not assume that delivery will continue without checking the phone, delivery might stay suspended,  so you need to check !\n---### Pod Failures\n- Pods fail occasionally due to a variety of issues, including hardware issues with the Pod itself.\n- It is best practice not to raise support / replacement cases with Insulet, since AAPS is not an approved method of using the Pods.\n- A list of fault codes can be  found here to help determine the cause.\n---### Preventing error 49 pod failures\nThis failure is related to an incorrect pod state for a command or an error during an insulin delivery command. This is when the driver and Pod disagree on the actual state. The Pod (out of a built-in safety measure) then reacts with an unrecoverable error code 49 (0x31) ending up with what is know as a “screamer”: the long irritating beep that can only be stopped by punching a hole at the appropriate location at the back of the Pod. The exact origin of a “49 pod failure” often is hard to trace. In situations that are suspected for this failure to occur (for instance on application crashes, running a development version or re-installation).\n---### Pump Unreachable Alerts\nWhen no communication can be established with the pod for a pre-configured time a “Pump unreachable” alert will be raised. Pump unreachable alerts can be configured by going to the top right-hand side three-dot menu, selecting  Preferences ➜  Local Alerts ➜  Pump unreachable threshold [min] . Recommended value is alerting after  120 minutes.\n---### Export Settings\nExporting  AAPS settings enables you to restore all your settings, and maybe more importantly, all your Objectives. You may need to restore settings to the “last known working situation” or after uninstalling/reinstalling  AAPS or in case of phone loss, reinstalling on the new phone.\nNOTE: The active pod information is included in the exported settings. If you import an “old” exported file, your actual pod will “die”. There is no other alternative. In some cases (like a  programmed phone change), you may need to use the exported file to restore  AAPS’ settings  while keeping the current active Pod . In this case it is important to only use the recently exported settings file containing the pod currently active.\nIt is good practice to do an export immediately after activating a pod . This way you will always be able to restore the current active pod in case of a problem. For instance when moving to another backup phone.\nRegularly (after each export preferably) copy your exported settings to a safe place (a cloud drive e.g. Google Drive) that is accessible by any phone when needed. This allows you to restore to a phone from anywhere in case of a phone loss or factory reset of your phone while you are not at home.\n---### Import Settings\nWARNING : Please note that importing settings will possibly import an outdated Pod status (depending when you made the last export/backup).\n As a result, there is a  risk of losing the active Pod! (see  Exporting Settings ).\n- Only try an import when no other options are available.\n- When importing settings with an active Pod, make sure the export was done with the currently active pod.\nImporting while on an active Pod: (you risk losing the Pod!)\n- Make sure you are importing settings that were recently exported with the currently active Pod!\n- Import your settings.\n- Check all preferences.\nImporting (no active Pod session)\n- Importing any recent export should work (see above)\n- Import your settings.\n- Check all preferences.\n- You may need to  Deactivate the “non existing” pod if the imported settings included any active pod data.\n---### Importing settings that contain Pod state from an inactive Pod\nWhen importing settings containing data for a Pod that is no longer active, AAPS will try to connect with it, which will obviously fail. You can not activate a new Pod in this situation.\nTo remove the old pod session:\n- “try” to de-activate the Pod. The de-activation will likely fail.\n- Select “Retry”.\n- After the second or third retry you will get the option to remove the pod.\n- Once the old pod is removed you will be able to activate a new pod.\n\n### Generic error: java.lan.illegalStateException: Trying to set a Bluetooth Address to ***, but it is already set to***\n\nIf you receive this error when attempting to Initialize a new pod  AAPS fails as it still has settings for an old pod stored in configuration.\nThis can happen if you restore from a backup, or a pod deactivation fails.\nTo resolve keep clicking on  RETRY until a  Discard option is shown, then discard. This procedure should work for De-Activating a pod too.\nYou should now be able to Activate a new pod.\n---### Reinstalling AAPS\nWhen uninstalling  AAPS you will lose all your settings, objectives and the current Pod session.  To restore them make sure you have a recent exported settings file available!\nWhen on an active Pod, make sure that you have an export for the current pod session or you will lose the currently active pod when importing older settings.\n\n- Export your settings and store a copy in a safe place (e.g Google Drive).\n- Uninstall  AAPS and restart your phone.\n- Install the new version of  AAPS .\n- Import your settings.\n- Verify all preferences (optionally import settings again).\n- Activate a new pod.\n- When done: Export current settings.\n---### Updating AAPS to a newer version\nIn most cases there is no need to uninstall. You can do an “in-place” install by starting the installation for the new version. This is also possible when on an active Pod session.\n- Export your settings.\n- Install the new  AAPS version.\n- Verify the installation was successful\n- RESUME the Pod or activate a new pod.\n- When done: Export current settings.\n---### Omnipod driver alerts\nThe Omnipod Dash driver presents a variety of unique alerts on the  Overview tab , most of them are informational and can be dismissed while some provide the user with an action requiring their input to resolve the cause of the triggered alert.\nA summary of the main alerts that you may encounter is listed below:\n- No active Pod session detected. This alert can temporarily be dismissed by pressing  SNOOZE but it will keep triggering as long as a new pod has not been activated. Once activated this alert is automatically silenced.\n- Pod suspended Informational alert that pod has been suspended.\n- Setting basal  Profile failed : Delivery might be suspended! Please manually refresh the Pod status from the Omnipod tab and resume delivery if needed.. Informational alert that the Pod basal  Profile setting has failed, and you will need to hit  Refresh on the Omnipod tab.\n- Unable to verify whether  SMB bolus succeeded. If you are sure that the Bolus didn’t succeed, you should manually delete the SMB entry from Treatments. Alert that the  SMB bolus command success could not be verified, you will need to verify the  Last bolus field on the DASH tab to see if  SMB bolus succeeded and if not remove the entry from the Treatments tab.\n- Uncertain if “task bolus/TBR/SMB” completed, please manually verify if it was successful.\n\n## Where to get help for DASH\n\nAll of the development work for the DASH is done by the community on a  volunteer basis; please keep this in mind and use the following guidelines before requesting assistance:\n\n- Level 0: Read the relevant section of this documentation to ensure you understand how the functionality with which you are experiencing difficulty is supposed to work.\n- Level 1: If you are still encountering problems that you are not able to resolve by using this document, then please go to the  #AAPS channel on  Discord by using  this invite link . There are also numerous Facebook and other groups you can ask in too (see  Getting Help )\n- Level 2: Search existing issues to see if your issue has already been reported at  Issues if it exists, please confirm/comment/add information on your problem. If not, please create a  new issue and attach  your log files .\n- Be patient - most of the members of our community consist of good-natured volunteers, and solving issues often requires time and patience from both users and developers.\nWhen requesting help come prepared with the following information to help those in the community with your specific questions and problems:\n- Android phone make and model\n- Android OS version (e.g 15 or 16)\n- Did you recently upgrade your Android OS version?\n- The version of  AAPS you are running\n- Plain english description of the problem you are facing considering some of the following things\n- Was it working before now?\n- When did it work or not work?\n- Did you make any changes to configuration or profile settings?\n- Did you pair a new bluetooth device?\n- Did you upgrade or install a new app?\n- How long was it working before it stopped working?"}, {"id": "doc:xdrip-app", "type": "docs", "slug": "xdrip-app", "title": "xDrip+ settings", "source_url": "https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/CompatibleCgms/xDrip.html", "text": "xDrip+ settings\n# xDrip+ settings\n\nIf not already set up, then download  xDrip+ .\nDisable battery optimization and allow background activity for the xDrip+ app.\nYou can safely download the  latest APK (stable) unless you need recent features or are using sensors that are being actively integrated (like G7), in which case you should use the latest  Nightly Snapshot .\n\n## Basic settings for all CGM & FGM systems\n\n### Disable Nightscout upload\n\nStarting with AAPS 3.2, you shouldn’t let any other app upload data (blood glucose and treatments) to Nightscout.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Settings (2) → Cloud Upload (3) -> Nightscout Sync (REST-API)(4) → Switch  OFF Enabled (5)\n\n#### Disable automatic calibration and treatments\n\nIf you use an older version of AAPS (before 3.2), make sure to deactivate  Automatic Calibration (7) If the checkbox for  Automatic Calibration is checked, activate  Download treatments (6) once, then remove the checkbox for  Automatic Calibration and deactivate  Download treatments again.\nTap  Extra Options (8)\nSafety warning\nYou must deactivate “Upload treatments” from xDrip+, otherwise treatments can be doubled in AAPS leading to false COB and IOB.\nDeactivate  Upload treatments (9) and make sure you will  NOT use  Back-fill data (11).\nOption  Alert on failures should also be deactivated (10). Otherwise you will get an alarm every 5 minutes in case Wi-Fi/mobile network issues or if the server is not available.\n\n### Inter-app Settings (Broadcast)\n\nIf you are going to use AAPS and the data should be forwarded to i.e. AAPS you have to activate broadcasting in xDrip+ in Inter-App settings.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Settings (2) → Inter-app settings (3) → Broadcast locally  ON (4)\nIn order for the values to be identical in AAPS with respect to xDrip+, you should activate  Send the displayed glucose value (5).\nEnable Compatible Broadcast (6).\nIf you have also activated  Accept treatments in xDrip+ and  Enable broadcasts to xDrip+ in AAPS xDrip+ plugin, then xDrip+ will receive insulin, carbs and basal rate information from AAPS.\nIf you enable  Accept Calibrations , xDrip+ will use the calibrations from AAPS. Be careful when you use this feature with Dexcom sensors: read  this first.\nRemember to disable Import Sounds to avoid xDrip+ making a ringtone every time AAPS sends a basal/profile change.\n\n#### Identify receiver\n\n- If you discover problems with local broadcast (AAPS not receiving BG values from xDrip+) go to → Hamburger Menu (1) Settings (2) → Inter-app settings (3) → Identify receiver (7) and enter  info.nightscout.androidaps for AAPS build (if you are using PumpControl build, please enter  info.nightscout.aapspumpcontrol instead!!).\n- Pay attention: Auto-correction sometimes tend to change i to capital letter. You  must use only lowercase letters when typing  info.nightscout.androidaps (or  info.nightscout.aapspumpcontrol for PumpControl). Capital I would prevent the App from receiving BG values from xDrip+.\n\n## Use AAPS to calibrate in xDrip+\n\n- If you want to be able to use AAPS to calibrate then in xDrip+ go to Settings → Interapp Compatibility → Accept Calibrations and select ON.\n- You may also want to review the options in Settings → Less Common Settings → Advanced Calibration Settings.\n\n## Dexcom G6\n\n- The Dexcom G6 transmitter can simultaneously be connected to the Dexcom receiver (or alternatively the t:slim pump) and one app on your phone.\n- When using xDrip+ as receiver uninstall Dexcom app first.  You cannot connect xDrip+ and Dexcom app with the transmitter at the same time!\n- If you need Clarity and want to profit from xDrip+ features, use the  Build Your Own Dexcom App with local broadcast to xDrip+, or use xDrip+ as a Companion app receiving notifications from the official Dexcom app.\n\n### xDrip+ version depending on G6 transmitter serial no\n\n- All G6 transmitters manufactured after fall/end 2018 are called “Firefly”. They do not allow sensor restart without  removing the transmitter , they do not send raw data. It is recommended to use the latest  Nightly Snapshot .\n- Old rebatteried transmitters and modified transmitters allow sensor life extension and restarts, they also send raw data. You can use the  latest APK (stable) .\n\n### Dexcom specific settings\n\n- Follow  these instructions to setup xDrip+.\n\n### Preemptive restarts not recommended\n\nOnly rebatteried or modified Dexcom transmitters.  Preemptive restarts do not work with standard transmitters and will stop the sensor completely: you need to  remove the transmitter to restart the sensor.\nThe automatic extension of Dexcom sensors ( preemptive restarts ) is not recommended as this might lead to “jumps” in BG values on day 9 after restart.\nTo use it safely, there are a few points to be aware of:\n\n- If you are using the native data with the calibration code in xDrip+ or Spike, the safest thing to do is not allow preemptive restarts of the sensor.\n- If you must use preemptive restarts, then make sure you insert at a time of day where you can observe the change and calibrate if necessary.\n- If you are restarting sensors, either do it without the factory calibration for safest results on days 11 and 12, or ensure you are ready to calibrate and keep an eye on variation.\n- Pre-soaking of the G6 with factory calibration is likely to give variation in results. If you do pre-soak, then to get best results, you will probably need to calibrate the sensor.\n- If you aren’t being observant about the changes that may be taking place, it may be better to revert to non-factory-calibrated mode and use the system like a G5.\nTo learn more about the details and reasons for these recommendations read the  complete article published by Tim Street at  <www.diabettech.com> .\n\n### Connect G6 transmitter for the first time\n\nFor second and following transmitters see  Extend transmitter life below.\nFollow  these instructions .\n\n### Transmitter battery status\n\n- Battery status can be controlled in system status\n → Hamburger Menu (1) → System Status (2) → If you are on the Classic Status Page (3) swipe the screen (4) to reach → G5/G6/G7 Status screen.\n- See  here for more information.\n\n### Extend transmitter life\n\n- Lifetime cannot be extended for Firefly transmitters: only rebatteried or modified transmitters.\n- Follow  these instructions for non-Firefly transmitters.\n\n### Replace transmitter\n\n- Turn original Dexcom receiver off (if used).\n- Stop sensor (only if replacing sensor).\n- Forget device in xDrip+ system status AND in smartphone’s BT settings (Will be shown as Dexcom?? whereas ?? are the last two digits of the transmitter serial no.)\n → Hamburger Menu (1) → System Status (2) → If you are not on the Classic Status Page (3) swipe the screen (4) to reach it → then tap Forget Device (5).\n- Remove transmitter (and sensor if replacing sensor). To remove transmitter without removing sensor see  this , or this video  <https://youtu.be/AAhBVsc6NZo> .\n- Put the old transmitter far away to prevent reconnection. A microwave is a perfect Faraday shield for this - but unplug power cord to be 100% sure no one is turning the microwave on.\n- Follow  these instructions .\n- Do not turn original Dexcom receiver (if used) back on before xDrip+ shows first readings.\n\n### New Sensor\n\n- Turn original Dexcom receiver off (if used).\n- Stop sensor following  these instructions .\n- Insert and then start a new sensor following  these instructions .\n\n### Retrieve sensor code\n\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → System Status (2) → If you are on the Classic Status Page (3) swipe the screen (4) to reach → G5/G6/G7 Status screen → Calibration Code.\n\n### Troubleshooting Dexcom G5/G6 and xDrip+\n\n#### Problem connecting transmitter\n\nFollow  these instructions .\n\n#### Problem when starting new sensor\n\nFollow  these instructions .\n\n## Libre 1\n\n- Setup your NFC to Bluetooth bridge in xDrip+\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Settings (2) → Less common settings (3) → Bluetooth Settings (4)\n- In Bluetooth Settings set the checkboxes exactly as in the screenshots below (5)\n- Disable watchdogs as they will reset the phone Bluetooth and interrupt your pump connection.\n- You can try to enable the following settings (7)\n- Use scanning\n- Trust Auto-Connect\n- Use Background Scans\n- If you easily lose connection to the bridge or have difficulties recovering connection,  DISABLE THEM (8).\n- Leave all other options disabled unless you know why you want to enable them.\n\n### Libre smart reader battery level\n\n- Battery level of bridges such as MiaoMiao and Bubble can be displayed in AAPS (not Blucon).\n- Details can be found on  screenshots page .\n\n### Connect Libre Transmitter & start sensor\n\n- If your sensor requires it (Libre 2 EU and Libre 1 US) install the latest out of process algorithm.\n- Your sensor must be already started using the vendor app or the reader (xDrip+ cannot start or stop Libre sensors).\n- Set the data source to Libre Bluetooth.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Settings (2) → Select Libre Bluetooth in Hardware Data source (3)\n- Scan Bluetooth and connect the bridge.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Scan Bluetooth (2) → Scan (3)\n- If xDrip+ can’t find the bridge, make sure it’s not connected to the vendor app. Put it in charge and reset it.\n- Start the sensor in xDrip+.\nSafety warning\nDo not use sensor data before the one hour warm-up is over: the values can be extremely high and cause wrong decisions in AAPS.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Start sensor (2) → Start sensor (3) → Set the exact time you started it with the reader or the vendor app. If you didn’t start it today, answer “Not Today” (4).\n\n## Libre 2 patched app\n\n- Set the data source to Libre patched app.\n→ Hamburger Menu (1) → Settings (2) → Select Libre (patched App) in Hardware Data source (3)\n- You can add  BgReading:d,xdrip libre_receiver:v under Less Common Settings->Extra Logging Settings->Extra tags for logging. This will log additional error messages for trouble shooting."}, {"id": "doc:xdrip-g7", "type": "docs", "slug": "xdrip-g7", "title": "G7, One+ or Stelo", "source_url": "https://navid200.github.io/xDrip/docs/Dexcom/G7.html", "text": "G7, One+ or Stelo\n# G7, One+ or Stelo\n\nxDrip »  Features »  xDrip & Dexcom » Dexcom G7, One+ or Stelo\nThis guide explains how to use xDrip to collect directly from G7, One+, or Stelo.\n---#### Starting (inserting) the sensor\nBefore inserting a new sensor, use a pen to mark the old one to avoid accidentally removing the wrong sensor later.\nInspect the sensor for any  damage , then follow the manufacturer’s instructions to insert it using the applicator.\n The session will start automatically once the sensor is inserted— no need to manually stop or start anything.\nTake note of the 4-digit pairing code displayed on the sensor applicator, as you’ll need it to establish connectivity later.\n---#### Establishing connectivity\n1- Only one app can collect from the transmitter at any time. If you have installed the Dexcom app or any other app that collects data from the transmitter, uninstall it. Do not start your Dexcom receiver (or a pump that gets readings directly from G7) yet. If they are already running, disable them and wait 15 minutes.\n2- Go to Android Settings −> Connected devices.\n Forget all devices named DXCM**, DX01** or DX02**, where** represents any two characters.\n3- Ensure xDrip is updated to at least the  2026.06.17 release.\n4- Set up xDrip and your phone as explained  here . Be sure to review and confirm all settings, as the QR code doesn’t configure them automatically.\n5- Ensure your old sensors are out of range or place them in a microwave. If your old sensor is still working, it’s okay as long as it’s connected to another instance of xDrip or Dexcom app. If you’re done with it, peel it off and move it away.\n6- Enter the 4-digit pairing code from the sensor applicator as the transmitter ID.\n7- Go to the  Dex status page and wait for a connection.\n If you’re using Android 10 or newer, approve the pairing request.\nIf the sensor was inserted more than 30 minutes ago, you should see readings. If it was just inserted, it will show as “warming up.” Over time, the status page will populate with additional data, including time remaining and other elements.\nOnce the  Dex Status Page shows the battery voltages, you can enable your pump or receiver.\n---#### Troubleshooting\n---#### Applicator failures\n\n#### Starting a subsequent G7 or One+\n\n#### Why no start or stop\n\n#### Grace period"}], "threads": [{"id": "thread:androidaps-1072", "type": "thread", "title": "[3.0 Beta 10/11] Crashes after start", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1072", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1072, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-12-14T23:58:39Z", "closed_at": "2022-01-06T16:52:20Z", "comment_count": 32, "comments": [{"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2021-12-15T00:50:45Z", "body": "For me either.\r\nAndroid 12\r\nGoogle Pixel 4a 5G"}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2021-12-15T01:01:22Z", "body": "Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1073...)"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2021-12-15T01:05:01Z", "body": "> Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR #1073...)\r\n\r\nCombo.\r\n\r\nMaybe due these changes: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/31a2a03efb359bd8b687c09c21b064dfb5e87f4c or/and https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/7cd22ef5e4db538583315a765deefcb73464768e"}, {"user": "happygirlnyc70", "created_at": "2021-12-15T02:05:50Z", "body": "Same issue  using both beta 10 and dev 17\r\nPixel 4a 5g\r\nAndroid 12\r\nOmnipod Eros"}, {"user": "StephenBrown2", "created_at": "2021-12-15T04:50:46Z", "body": "Same with Beta10, downgrading to Beta9 seemed to work fine, but wouldn't connect to Eros. Trying to Scan from AndroidAPS then caused it to crash repeatedly. Logs attached.\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1639543424780.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7716539/AndroidAPS_LOG_1639543424780.log.zip)\r\nPixel 5\r\nAndroid 12\r\nOmnipod Eros"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-12-15T06:04:19Z", "body": "Confirmed with\r\nPixel 5\r\nAndroid 12\r\nAkku-Check Combo & Medtronic 754"}, {"user": "jroth-haj", "created_at": "2021-12-15T07:04:37Z", "body": "Its not pump specific. The crash is also at fresh installation."}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2021-12-15T10:03:20Z", "body": "> Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR #1073...)\r\n\r\nTHANKS A LOT! :)\r\n\r\nJust built https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/afea158d0e13d668106ffe2812c693e763dd205a and it's working perfectly fine!\r\nIssues with Combo are also fixed and I assume with other pumps too!"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2021-12-15T10:05:45Z", "body": "@MilosKozak Can you release Beta 11 with this new fix?"}, {"user": "andybluenoes", "created_at": "2021-12-15T10:26:38Z", "body": "Same issue here with Beta 10\r\nApp crashes on startup\r\nPixel 4\r\nAndroid 12\r\nDash"}], "text": "[3.0 Beta 10/11] Crashes after start  Beta 10 at Pixel 5 (Android 12) \r\nUnable to initialize after fresh Installation or Update.\r\nNo logs available.\r\nNo configuration. It crashes directly after start. For me either.\r\nAndroid 12\r\nGoogle Pixel 4a 5G Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1073...) > Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR #1073...)\r\n\r\nCombo.\r\n\r\nMaybe due these changes: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/31a2a03efb359bd8b687c09c21b064dfb5e87f4c or/and https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/7cd22ef5e4db538583315a765deefcb73464768e Same issue  using both beta 10 and dev 17\r\nPixel 4a 5g\r\nAndroid 12\r\nOmnipod Eros Same with Beta10, downgrading to Beta9 seemed to work fine, but wouldn't connect to Eros. Trying to Scan from AndroidAPS then caused it to crash repeatedly. Logs attached.\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1639543424780.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7716539/AndroidAPS_LOG_1639543424780.log.zip)\r\nPixel 5\r\nAndroid 12\r\nOmnipod Eros Confirmed with\r\nPixel 5\r\nAndroid 12\r\nAkku-Check Combo & Medtronic 754 Its not pump specific. The crash is also at fresh installation. > Do you both have an Insight Pump ? (If yes I made this PR #1073...)\r\n\r\nTHANKS A LOT! :)\r\n\r\nJust built https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/afea158d0e13d668106ffe2812c693e763dd205a and it's working perfectly fine!\r\nIssues with Combo are also fixed and I assume with other pumps too! @MilosKozak Can you release Beta 11 with this new fix? Same issue here with Beta 10\r\nApp crashes on startup\r\nPixel 4\r\nAndroid 12\r\nDash"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-1311", "type": "thread", "title": "Negative IOB : shouldn't be used in insulin calculations ", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1311", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1311, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2022-02-12T07:58:16Z", "closed_at": "2022-07-25T19:11:12Z", "comment_count": 77, "comments": [{"user": "BRamine", "created_at": "2022-02-12T08:11:16Z", "body": "Another experience for me with -IOB :\n\nStarted TT for exercise, but ended up working more then intended. \nSituation is 0 COB, bg flat 100 with -0.45 IOB. TT ended and AAPS immediately started to compensate for the negative IOB and sent me straight to Hypo. \nI could have avoided that but TT again etc, but also the compensation for -IOB is completely not logic since like @robertrub said, -IOB = 0 IOB, if ∆ is not high, which in my case average ∆ was -1, can't find a reason to have insulin."}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2022-02-12T08:21:04Z", "body": "Negative IOB is required in oref algorithm.\r\nIf you want to disable it in wizard dialog, first disable COB (GA) in your screenshot..."}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2022-02-12T08:39:21Z", "body": "I don't know how negative IOB is used/useful in in OREF but the result is not good. We are obliged to cheat with high TT to prevent hypos which adds more neg IOB...\n\nI don't know what would change deactivating COB as it was 0 on my screen capture and unchecking it doesn't uncheck IOB. Once more, this is a cheat to counteract an incorrect reaction of AAPS."}, {"user": "chrisbev", "created_at": "2022-02-12T09:03:51Z", "body": "When autosens lowers to say 80% does anyone know what iob is calculated with respect to?  Is it 100% basal or 80% basal?  I've asked previously but got no replies as if 100% then changing to 80% could help, or could autosens say bleed iob another way (like cob decay) after a while?  For me I swing around plus or minus iob so 'think' settings are not too far off and autosens copes quite well with my variability but I quite often manually disconnect pump to 'help' -ve or 'prime' for +ve to hide from AAPS calculation. Just off the wall thoughts if rubbish as I don't know OREF workings please ignore."}, {"user": "BRamine", "created_at": "2022-02-12T09:35:03Z", "body": "> I don't know how negative IOB is used/useful in in OREF but the result is not good. We are obliged to cheat with high TT to prevent hypos which adds more neg IOB...\n> \n> I don't know what would change deactivating COB as it was 0 on my screen capture and unchecking it doesn't uncheck IOB. Once more, this is a cheat to counteract an incorrect reaction of AAPS.\n\nBy cheating we get even more -iob "}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2022-02-12T13:04:32Z", "body": "My answer was not to cheat, but to include or not negative IOB in wizard calculation. (after wizard you have a bolus so no more negative iob, it's just a way to limit risks of over dosing the bolus).\n\nNegative IOB is not bad when all your settings are good. If you look in detail all your IOB curves during a perfect night with a flat BG curve glued to your target. you will see that your IOB vary between positive and negative values.\nWithout negative value, the correction would be under estimated and the result worse than your perfect curve (you will get waves).\n\nYou always have insulin in your body, even with negative iob (just take a look on absolute iob that is always >0).\nNegative IOB signify lack of insulin compare to your basal profile.\n\nThe negative IOB is always the consequence of something else that is not correct (basal rate too high in your profile, sport, ...) and most of the time an hypo TT is the good way to correct the situation without cheating aaps."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-02-12T13:12:09Z", "body": "_Another theoretical example (which I happen to experience regularly):_ \r\n\r\nAAPS tries to keep my BG at target using the **perfect profile**.\r\nThen my IC is a bit off (due to todays sensitivity) and maybe I was unable to calculate carbs absorbed exactly:\r\n\r\nAAPS/0Ref will attempt to compensate for this and keeping me at target (as designed)  by some 0-temping, \r\nIt does so perfectly, no problems until .... negative -IOB gets me in a hypo.\r\n\r\n_To clarify (its what i see happing when it occurs):_\r\nNegative -IOB results into an instable system that starts cycling between lows and -IOB about every 2-3 hours:\r\n```\r\n|---> Going below target -> 0-temp -> going to target with -IOB -> addtional insulin for -IOB -->--|\r\n^------------------<-------------------------------------------------------------------------<-----|\r\n```\r\nI can only break this cycle by taking carbs to get 2 points above target (target=5.0)\r\n\r\n* TT does not work here: it only worsens by generating more -IOB\r\n* Temporary loweri"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-02-12T13:19:55Z", "body": "> You always have insulin in your body, even with negative iob (just take a look on absolute iob that is always >0).\r\n> Negative IOB signify lack of insulin compare to your basal profile.\r\n\r\nThat is just the point with -IOB. It is just a trick to calculate \"virual\" insulin that was expected but not administered.\r\nIt most certainly can be taken in account for oRef calculation. \r\nBut it should *not* be compensated for by actually injecting this \"virtual\" insulin just to get to absolute insulin at \"0\"\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-02-12T13:41:19Z", "body": "There should not be any need for \"tricks\", T-Temps or \"Basal rate lowering\" to prevent something like oRef negative -IOB from causing problems. \r\n\r\nEven after 2 years on the subject -IOB I have not seen any (acceptable) explanation on the purpose of compensating for -IOB with real insulin\r\n"}, {"user": "swissalpine", "created_at": "2022-02-12T15:25:34Z", "body": "I think you have to separate two things: Showing an insulin level below the actual basal level. This is where negative IOB makes sense and is very helpful information. Negative insulin (understood as a deviation from what the basal rate would have given) must exist and must be possible and must be enabled by the algorithm. This is a binse.\r\n\r\nThe \"enforced\" filling of the negative IOB as soon as an opportunity comes up (positive trend, calculator ...) has no logic in my eyes. Because the available insulin quantity (even if it is IOB negative), is exactly correct at this time and was also exactly so initially controlled by the algorithm! So why correct this \"correct\" amount of insulin on occasion incorrectly? ;-)\r\nThis is exactly why I have to set up automations, set Hypo-TT etc., in order to moderate this, in my eyes, usually not reasonable amount of insulin.\r\n\r\nAnd more fundamentally: I hope that AAPS will soon say goodbye to OREF and become independent.  There is so much developer po"}], "text": "Negative IOB : shouldn't be used in insulin calculations   There is a security risk with negative IOB. AAPS  always tries to inject the \"missing\" insulin which results in lows.\n\nThere is no \"negative\" IOB in our bodies. The pancreas releases or not insulin depending on BGs and their variations. It should be the same in AAPS.\n\nNegative IOB is an important information for the user (ie profile too strong) and should be indicated (message and text on the graphic) but should NOT enter in the formulas used to calculate the insulin amount to be injected.\n\n2 examples. This morning, my BGs were lower than usual (insulin working better than other mornings). AAPS does a great job and stops basal to prevent hypos. This generates negative IOB. I'm below target, no carbs. If I use the calculator, the negative IOB will be injected and I'll find myself in hypo. The calculator should not inject the negative IOB. Even without the calculator, AAPS should not try to fill in the \"missing\" insulin.\n\n![Screenshot_20220212-065218_AndroidAPS.jpg](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/153702264-f281fad6-4162-458e-bb73-3162ce35b54c.jpg)\n\n![20220212_065316.jpg](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/153702262-58051fd8-87b8-4901-b26a-cbce52672db6.jpg)\n\nExercice example. I eat carbs (that I don't tell AAPS) before exercise. I walk for 1 hour. I either didn't eat enough or the road was too steep and I ended in a negative IOB. The exercise results in insulin being more efficient. If AAPS tries to reinject the \"missing\" insulin, I'll end up in a hypo.\n\nI can't find even one reason to use negative IOB in the calculations.\n\nAAPS should alert the user that it is generating negative IOB but should never use IOB <0. \n\nIF IOB <0 THEN IOB=0 and FLAG _neg-IOB-alert_\n Another experience for me with -IOB :\n\nStarted TT for exercise, but ended up working more then intended. \nSituation is 0 COB, bg flat 100 with -0.45 IOB. TT ended and AAPS immediately started to compensate for the negative IOB and sent me straight to Hypo. \nI could have avoided that but TT again etc, but also the compensation for -IOB is completely not logic since like @robertrub said, -IOB = 0 IOB, if ∆ is not high, which in my case average ∆ was -1, can't find a reason to have insulin. Negative IOB is required in oref algorithm.\r\nIf you want to disable it in wizard dialog, first disable COB (GA) in your screenshot... I don't know how negative IOB is used/useful in in OREF but the result is not good. We are obliged to cheat with high TT to prevent hypos which adds more neg IOB...\n\nI don't know what would change deactivating COB as it was 0 on my screen capture and unchecking it doesn't uncheck IOB. Once more, this is a cheat to counteract an incorrect reaction of AAPS. When autosens lowers to say 80% does anyone know what iob is calculated with respect to?  Is it 100% basal or 80% basal?  I've asked previously but got no replies as if 100% then changing to 80% could help, or could autosens say bleed iob another way (like cob decay) after a while?  For me I swing around plus or minus iob so 'think' settings are not too far off and autosens copes quite well with my variability but I quite often manually disconnect pump to 'help' -ve or 'prime' for +ve to hide from AAPS calculation. Just off the wall thoughts if rubbish as I don't know OREF workings please ignore. > I don't know how negative IOB is used/useful in in OREF but the result is not good. We are obliged to cheat with high TT to prevent hypos which adds more neg IOB...\n> \n> I don't know what would change deactivating COB as it was 0 on my screen capture and unchecking it doesn't uncheck IOB. Once more, this is a cheat to counteract an incorrect reaction of AAPS.\n\nBy cheating we get even more -iob  My answer was not to cheat, but to include or not negative IOB in wizard calculation. (after wizard you have a bolus so no more negative iob, it's just a way to limit risks of over dosing the bolus).\n\nNegative IOB is not bad when all your settings are good. If you look in detail all your IOB curves during a perfect night with a flat BG curve glued to your target. you will see that your IOB vary between positive and negative values.\nWithout negative value, the correction would be under estimated and the result worse than your perfect curve (you will get waves).\n\nYou always have insulin in your body, even with negative iob (just take a look on absolute iob that is always >0).\nNegative IOB signify lack of insulin compare to your basal profile.\n\nThe negative IOB is always the consequence of something else that is not correct (basal rate too high in your profile, sport, ...) and most of the time an hypo TT is the good way to correct the situation without cheating aaps. _Another theoretical example (which I happen to experience regularly):_ \r\n\r\nAAPS tries to keep my BG at target using the **perfect profile**.\r\nThen my IC is a bit off (due to todays sensitivity) and maybe I was unable to calculate carbs absorbed exactly:\r\n\r\nAAPS/0Ref will attempt to compensate for this and keeping me at target (as designed)  by some 0-temping, \r\nIt does so perfectly, no problems until .... negative -IOB gets me in a hypo.\r\n\r\n_To clarify (its what i see happing when it occurs):_\r\nNegative -IOB results into an instable system that starts cycling between lows and -IOB about every 2-3 hours:\r\n```\r\n|---> Going below target -> 0-temp -> going to target with -IOB -> addtional insulin for -IOB -->--|\r\n^------------------<-------------------------------------------------------------------------<-----|\r\n```\r\nI can only break this cycle by taking carbs to get 2 points above target (target=5.0)\r\n\r\n* TT does not work here: it only worsens by generating more -IOB\r\n* Temporary loweri > You always have insulin in your body, even with negative iob (just take a look on absolute iob that is always >0).\r\n> Negative IOB signify lack of insulin compare to your basal profile.\r\n\r\nThat is just the point with -IOB. It is just a trick to calculate \"virual\" insulin that was expected but not administered.\r\nIt most certainly can be taken in account for oRef calculation. \r\nBut it should *not* be compensated for by actually injecting this \"virtual\" insulin just to get to absolute insulin at \"0\"\r\n\r\n There should not be any need for \"tricks\", T-Temps or \"Basal rate lowering\" to prevent something like oRef negative -IOB from causing problems. \r\n\r\nEven after 2 years on the subject -IOB I have not seen any (acceptable) explanation on the purpose of compensating for -IOB with real insulin\r\n I think you have to separate two things: Showing an insulin level below the actual basal level. This is where negative IOB makes sense and is very helpful information. Negative insulin (understood as a deviation from what the basal rate would have given) must exist and must be possible and must be enabled by the algorithm. This is a binse.\r\n\r\nThe \"enforced\" filling of the negative IOB as soon as an opportunity comes up (positive trend, calculator ...) has no logic in my eyes. Because the available insulin quantity (even if it is IOB negative), is exactly correct at this time and was also exactly so initially controlled by the algorithm! So why correct this \"correct\" amount of insulin on occasion incorrectly? ;-)\r\nThis is exactly why I have to set up automations, set Hypo-TT etc., in order to moderate this, in my eyes, usually not reasonable amount of insulin.\r\n\r\nAnd more fundamentally: I hope that AAPS will soon say goodbye to OREF and become independent.  There is so much developer po"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-1597", "type": "thread", "title": "Overlapping Times in basal Tab leading to wrong iob? Dev-i", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1597", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1597, "labels": ["omnipod dash"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2022-04-10T15:47:30Z", "closed_at": "2022-05-10T18:40:30Z", "comment_count": 59, "comments": [{"user": "Ede1975", "created_at": "2022-04-11T08:30:36Z", "body": "Update: i tested a couple of dev-i Versions i Compiled over the last days but did not use before, ran into the same issue. Installed Master and had no issue with that Version. Then i finally rebooted the Phone (didnt before), reinstalled latest dev-i afterwards and the issue did not occur again so far"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-04-13T11:42:28Z", "body": "is it possible you changed pump meanwhile?"}, {"user": "Ede1975", "created_at": "2022-04-13T12:01:23Z", "body": "You mean from dash to some other pump or virtual pump? No, definately not. "}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-04-14T07:41:56Z", "body": "do you have logs prior this one?"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-04-14T07:42:39Z", "body": "note: where is this from\r\n`17:02:30.229 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-53] D/DATABASE: [PumpSyncImplementation.syncTemporaryBasalWithPumpId():274]: Updated TemporaryBasal TemporaryBasal(id=28452, version=3, dateCreated=1649602950162, isValid=true, referenceId=null, interfaceIDs_backing=InterfaceIDs(nightscoutSystemId=null, nightscoutId=6251f4b9215b0200041e4d4c, pumpType=OMNIPOD_DASH, pumpSerial=4241, temporaryId=null, pumpId=-8976659072097442112, startId=null, endId=-7142919318749436032), timestamp=1649602949159, utcOffset=7200000, type=NORMAL, isAbsolute=true, rate=1.5, duration=1800000)\r\n`"}, {"user": "Ede1975", "created_at": "2022-04-14T08:27:26Z", "body": "> do you have logs prior this one?\n\nNo, unfortunately not. I am still on the same Version, did not happen again. In case it occurs again i will add new logs."}, {"user": "emmatovar27", "created_at": "2022-04-20T01:06:20Z", "body": "Hi There! I have the same issue. This happens every time the TBR is set for 30 min. The rest of TBR looks to work fine.\r\n![Screenshot_20220419-175209](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/39507448/164126009-186010bd-c76c-4cb3-a94e-5c3c46640a10.png)\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1650416536289log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/8517378/AndroidAPS_LOG_1650416536289.log.zip)\r\n\r\n Let me know if there is any additional information is needed. \r\n\r\nI'm using the dev branch from Philoul to test Autotune. \r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-04-25T18:50:16Z", "body": "Could not confirm but now seeing similar, quite a lot of this overlapping TBR's at certain times.\r\nAm running DASH while building from Philoul's Autotune PR (merged with latest dev).\r\n\r\nWill switch back building form current dev to see if it reproduces with some helpfull logging\r\n@MilosKozak Any suggestions on how to \"debug\" this. Assuming at least logfiles - anything else to watch for?\r\n(Btw: Will add logs as soon as I can repro this on current dev branch)\r\n\r\n![xxScreenshot_20220425-203657_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45144129/165153471-25fade52-d314-419b-bf44-a47b36cb20a8.jpg)\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "nicoleloop", "created_at": "2022-04-25T21:56:10Z", "body": "I am experiencing the same issues with my Dash Pods, as well as terrible bluetooth connections with the last 4 pods. In the range of the lowest, 51% to the highest being 63% connection quality."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-04-26T08:43:27Z", "body": "@vanelsberg yes, try dev and provide logs"}], "text": "Overlapping Times in basal Tab leading to wrong iob? Dev-i omnipod dash It seems tbrs have not been cancelled, Times are overlapping in basal tab\nPossibly aaps was out of reach of dash a couple of Times during the period from 14:53 to 16:53\n\n![IMG-20220410-WA0000.jpg](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/88888180/162627614-4d46bc2e-aa0b-454b-a5bb-f0dc0b09acf4.jpg)\n\n![AndroidAPS_LOG_1649605049645.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/8459360/AndroidAPS_LOG_1649605049645.log.zip) Update: i tested a couple of dev-i Versions i Compiled over the last days but did not use before, ran into the same issue. Installed Master and had no issue with that Version. Then i finally rebooted the Phone (didnt before), reinstalled latest dev-i afterwards and the issue did not occur again so far is it possible you changed pump meanwhile? You mean from dash to some other pump or virtual pump? No, definately not.  do you have logs prior this one? note: where is this from\r\n`17:02:30.229 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-53] D/DATABASE: [PumpSyncImplementation.syncTemporaryBasalWithPumpId():274]: Updated TemporaryBasal TemporaryBasal(id=28452, version=3, dateCreated=1649602950162, isValid=true, referenceId=null, interfaceIDs_backing=InterfaceIDs(nightscoutSystemId=null, nightscoutId=6251f4b9215b0200041e4d4c, pumpType=OMNIPOD_DASH, pumpSerial=4241, temporaryId=null, pumpId=-8976659072097442112, startId=null, endId=-7142919318749436032), timestamp=1649602949159, utcOffset=7200000, type=NORMAL, isAbsolute=true, rate=1.5, duration=1800000)\r\n` > do you have logs prior this one?\n\nNo, unfortunately not. I am still on the same Version, did not happen again. In case it occurs again i will add new logs. Hi There! I have the same issue. This happens every time the TBR is set for 30 min. The rest of TBR looks to work fine.\r\n![Screenshot_20220419-175209](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/39507448/164126009-186010bd-c76c-4cb3-a94e-5c3c46640a10.png)\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1650416536289log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/8517378/AndroidAPS_LOG_1650416536289.log.zip)\r\n\r\n Let me know if there is any additional information is needed. \r\n\r\nI'm using the dev branch from Philoul to test Autotune. \r\n Could not confirm but now seeing similar, quite a lot of this overlapping TBR's at certain times.\r\nAm running DASH while building from Philoul's Autotune PR (merged with latest dev).\r\n\r\nWill switch back building form current dev to see if it reproduces with some helpfull logging\r\n@MilosKozak Any suggestions on how to \"debug\" this. Assuming at least logfiles - anything else to watch for?\r\n(Btw: Will add logs as soon as I can repro this on current dev branch)\r\n\r\n![xxScreenshot_20220425-203657_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45144129/165153471-25fade52-d314-419b-bf44-a47b36cb20a8.jpg)\r\n\r\n I am experiencing the same issues with my Dash Pods, as well as terrible bluetooth connections with the last 4 pods. In the range of the lowest, 51% to the highest being 63% connection quality. @vanelsberg yes, try dev and provide logs"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-1853", "type": "thread", "title": "Omnipod EROS: There is no way to forcefully wipe/reset the pod state in case of \"emergency\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1853", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1853, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2022-06-25T07:56:25Z", "closed_at": "2022-07-09T16:17:54Z", "comment_count": 25, "comments": [{"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T07:59:26Z", "body": "Alternative \"_solution_\" to the problem would be resetting AAPS preferences or a reinstall.\r\nAn option to import \"objectives only\" would then ensure objectives are not lost\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1852\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T08:00:46Z", "body": "Remark:\r\nOmnipod DASH implementation ensures that after 3 unsuccesfull retries user is offered the option to \"forcefully\" discarding the Pod.\r\n\r\nSomething like this maybe could also be implemented for EROS but expect this would need non-trivial driver changes?\r\nExpecting forcefully wiping pod state from developer mode can be done with less impact on drive code?\r\n"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-06-25T11:13:19Z", "body": "what keys do you have to remove?"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T12:29:41Z", "body": "> what keys do you have to remove?\r\n\r\n@MilosKozak \r\nClearing string value at `content: \"AAPS.Omnipod.pod_state\"` should effectively remove the Pod on settings import.\r\n\r\nCurrently not using EROS so unable to validate. Do have 3 EROS pods reserved for dev, so can test when needed.\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T12:43:44Z", "body": "FYI: Apart from settings, some hints to implementation:\r\n\r\nThink PodState is accessible at `java/info/nightscout/androidaps/plugins/pump/omnipod/eros/manager/AapsErosPodStateManager.java`\r\nSee public methods `store/loadPodState()`\r\n\r\nAlso see also `OmnipodManager, deactivatePod()` at `java/info/nightscout/androidaps/plugins/pump/omnipod/eros/driver/manager/OmnipodManager.java`\r\nIt calls `podStateManager.discardState();` at line 504\r\n\r\nNote that when discarding state, any active Pod is lost.\r\nAs is now, user can restore state through importing settings exported for the active Pod. Importing state from settings is useful when uninstalling/reinstalling AAPS or (unsupported) moving AAPS to other hardware.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T12:46:18Z", "body": "![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45144129/175774087-fb073756-327e-4c3c-a0f1-c7a3f23de5d6.png)\r\n"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-06-25T13:39:32Z", "body": "Discard pod is not enough in this state?\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/175776063-bcef7f62-a862-417b-8a58-1a5aadc2d850.png)\r\nThis create empty pod state, only address is preserved"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T13:42:49Z", "body": "Yes, the deactivation button normally should be used to solve a problematic pod.....\r\n\r\nThe bug/problem however is that AAPS/EROS somehow gets in a state where activation unexpectedly failed and activation process can not be continued. In that state however both the \"Deactivate Pod\" and \"Discard Pod\" buttons are disabled/invisible.\r\n\r\nNot sure but I think the \"Discard\" button is only visible after failing to deactivate.\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2022-06-25T13:46:01Z", "body": "Most obvious solution would be to target this specific bug (proper error handling?). But that would mean touching driver code which you may not want at this stage?\r\n\r\nAlso in any other situation, there is still no ways to repair by wiping state ....\r\n"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2022-06-25T13:54:08Z", "body": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/00f0446c21e059f1287333fc72578daeb6f8c8c2"}], "text": "Omnipod EROS: There is no way to forcefully wipe/reset the pod state in case of \"emergency\"  **AAPS version 3.0.0.1 release and higher**\r\n**Driver: Omnipod EROS**\r\n\r\n**Problem description:**\r\nThe Omnipod EROS driver has a bug that can lead to a situation where users get stuck with a pod registration that can not be continued or discarded. Several users reported running into this problem as a result of Pod activation failure.\r\n\r\nWork around used for not losing Objectives is importing 3.0 settings in AAPS version 2.8.1, discard the Pod and then export preferences that can be imported by AAPS 3.0\r\n\r\n**Proposed work around**:\r\nUntil the actual bug is solved, but also in general, I think the EROS driver should have a way to \"wipe\" the Pod state in case of \"emergencies\". Up to AAPS version 2.8 this could be done by editing the unencrypted preference file.\r\nAs of version 3.0 this is no longer an option.\r\n\r\nHow about an option to clear Pod state when running in developer mode? This way users have an \"escape\" option to get out of situations where there is Pod state without option to Discard. For AAPS 2.8 editing the preference file was used as a last resort\r\n\r\n Alternative \"_solution_\" to the problem would be resetting AAPS preferences or a reinstall.\r\nAn option to import \"objectives only\" would then ensure objectives are not lost\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1852\r\n Remark:\r\nOmnipod DASH implementation ensures that after 3 unsuccesfull retries user is offered the option to \"forcefully\" discarding the Pod.\r\n\r\nSomething like this maybe could also be implemented for EROS but expect this would need non-trivial driver changes?\r\nExpecting forcefully wiping pod state from developer mode can be done with less impact on drive code?\r\n what keys do you have to remove? > what keys do you have to remove?\r\n\r\n@MilosKozak \r\nClearing string value at `content: \"AAPS.Omnipod.pod_state\"` should effectively remove the Pod on settings import.\r\n\r\nCurrently not using EROS so unable to validate. Do have 3 EROS pods reserved for dev, so can test when needed.\r\n FYI: Apart from settings, some hints to implementation:\r\n\r\nThink PodState is accessible at `java/info/nightscout/androidaps/plugins/pump/omnipod/eros/manager/AapsErosPodStateManager.java`\r\nSee public methods `store/loadPodState()`\r\n\r\nAlso see also `OmnipodManager, deactivatePod()` at `java/info/nightscout/androidaps/plugins/pump/omnipod/eros/driver/manager/OmnipodManager.java`\r\nIt calls `podStateManager.discardState();` at line 504\r\n\r\nNote that when discarding state, any active Pod is lost.\r\nAs is now, user can restore state through importing settings exported for the active Pod. Importing state from settings is useful when uninstalling/reinstalling AAPS or (unsupported) moving AAPS to other hardware.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45144129/175774087-fb073756-327e-4c3c-a0f1-c7a3f23de5d6.png)\r\n Discard pod is not enough in this state?\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/175776063-bcef7f62-a862-417b-8a58-1a5aadc2d850.png)\r\nThis create empty pod state, only address is preserved Yes, the deactivation button normally should be used to solve a problematic pod.....\r\n\r\nThe bug/problem however is that AAPS/EROS somehow gets in a state where activation unexpectedly failed and activation process can not be continued. In that state however both the \"Deactivate Pod\" and \"Discard Pod\" buttons are disabled/invisible.\r\n\r\nNot sure but I think the \"Discard\" button is only visible after failing to deactivate.\r\n Most obvious solution would be to target this specific bug (proper error handling?). But that would mean touching driver code which you may not want at this stage?\r\n\r\nAlso in any other situation, there is still no ways to repair by wiping state ....\r\n https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/00f0446c21e059f1287333fc72578daeb6f8c8c2"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-199", "type": "thread", "title": "Basal is On when 0 Basal is registered", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/199", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 199, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-01-08T00:30:10Z", "closed_at": "2021-01-08T10:35:55Z", "comment_count": 34, "comments": [{"user": "bartsopers", "created_at": "2021-01-08T01:53:37Z", "body": "This is once again a dangerous situation because of NS upload only was not enabled. @smokkelaar now set NS to upload only and it works now.\r\n@MilosKozak we **really** need to fix this, either by completely disabling the option to download from NS, or by not allowing NS to change the truth (= create/overwrite treatments in the present). Only the pump driver should be able to create treatments in the present."}, {"user": "bartsopers", "created_at": "2021-01-08T02:19:24Z", "body": "![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15631208/103966049-5ed9b100-515f-11eb-8ed9-dfd22d7f65da.png)\r\n@MilosKozak you can see here that this treatment keeps being bounced back from NS. You can also see it in the attached logs.\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.txt](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/5784868/AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.txt)\r\n"}, {"user": "bartsopers", "created_at": "2021-01-08T02:29:28Z", "body": "Another option would be to allow to backfill from NS once on intial setup, when no data is present yet. Anyway in the current form it is dangerous. It frequently causes all kinds of problems and it should be removed ASAP."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2021-01-08T10:35:55Z", "body": "this will be resolved by new NSClient"}], "text": "Basal is On when 0 Basal is registered  \r\n![7498e6e7-ddef-45ed-aa96-bc3393c87e2e](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35005706/103961614-246b1680-5155-11eb-9c2b-55db4a4494b5.jpeg)\r\nHypo alert right now:\r\n\r\nSo suddenly the log evedicence logs that the pump is set to 0, while the pump is actually still giving some other units.\r\nIt happens around 17:30.... unknown what exactually changed during that time.\r\nnot able to stop the problems right now, did a restart.  and don't know where to look.\r\nMore information tomorrow. when hypo is fixed and a night sleep is done.\r\n\r\n\r\n![464aea22-93fd-49b8-a8da-6cac43b29d22](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35005706/103959946-5c705a80-5151-11eb-9ef4-c7f0ecbf7f3d.jpeg)\r\n![f204bb1b-b9d4-4500-858d-3330b2244bf7](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35005706/103959947-5d08f100-5151-11eb-88b2-24426d374a06.jpeg)\r\n![Schermafbeelding 2021-01-08 013355](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35005706/103960037-9b061500-5151-11eb-89cd-73c05a0438ff.png)\r\n\r\nVersion: 2.8.0\r\nbuild: d40c5079d-2021.01.06-13-45.\r\nflavor full release.\r\n\r\nPump: omnipod with emalink\r\nsensor: FSL 2 directly in xdrip (nightly build Pre-release\r\n 2020.12.23\r\n 18885dd\r\nNightly build 23rd Dec 2020\r\n@jamorham jamorham released this 15 days ago\r\n\r\nAutomated nightly build.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nstill adding information, did commit it to early, give me an other 30 minutes\r\n\r\nReporting bugs\r\n--------------\r\n- **Note the precise time the problem occurred** and describe the circumstances and steps that caused\r\n  the problem\r\n- Note the Build version (found in the About dialog in the app, when pressing the three dots in the\r\n  upper-right corner).\r\n- Obtain the app's log files, which can be found on the phone in\r\n  _/storage/emulated/0/Android/data/info.nightscout.androidaps/_\r\n  See https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/EN/Usage/Accessing-logfiles.html\r\n- Open an issue at https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/new\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.1.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/5784577/AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.1.zip)\r\n This is once again a dangerous situation because of NS upload only was not enabled. @smokkelaar now set NS to upload only and it works now.\r\n@MilosKozak we **really** need to fix this, either by completely disabling the option to download from NS, or by not allowing NS to change the truth (= create/overwrite treatments in the present). Only the pump driver should be able to create treatments in the present. ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15631208/103966049-5ed9b100-515f-11eb-8ed9-dfd22d7f65da.png)\r\n@MilosKozak you can see here that this treatment keeps being bounced back from NS. You can also see it in the attached logs.\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.txt](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/5784868/AndroidAPS._2021-01-07_23-55-51_.txt)\r\n Another option would be to allow to backfill from NS once on intial setup, when no data is present yet. Anyway in the current form it is dangerous. It frequently causes all kinds of problems and it should be removed ASAP. this will be resolved by new NSClient"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-2323", "type": "thread", "title": "[3.1.0.3] Wear entered treatments are not received by my phone (no confirmation)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2323", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2323, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2023-01-02T22:13:06Z", "closed_at": "2024-01-24T12:45:00Z", "comment_count": 30, "comments": [{"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2023-01-03T22:49:09Z", "body": "Important information is missing on this issue:\r\n\r\n* No logs included with this issue\r\n* What AAPS release/version/build are you running (add a screen print from AAPS's about?\r\n* What phone brand/type/OS\r\n* What watch brand/type/OS\r\n* Are Phone and Watch running latest updates\r\n* How did you install the wear-full-release.apk?\r\n* What watch face are you using?\r\n\r\nDid you try uninstalling the wear app and select a stock watch face, then switch off the watch, then switch it on again and reinstall the AAPS wear app?\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2023-01-04T00:15:59Z", "body": "@vanelsberg\r\n\r\n- logs were shared via email from the app. I also referenced this Github issue number in the email. See \"Logs sent\" above. Sorry if I did it wrong.\r\n- Version number is in the title.\r\n- Phone S22 Ultra, Galaxy Watch 4 (both on latest updates)\r\n- Wear app installed via \"Wear Installer 2\". Was working for treatments then unexpectedly stopped.\r\n- Digital watch face and standard AAPS watch face have the same issue\r\n\r\nWill try the reinstall steps suggested and report back."}, {"user": "maheini", "created_at": "2023-01-05T19:49:02Z", "body": "Does your watch have the latest built of AAPS? Have you tried to rebuild & generate the latest phone .apk\r\n\r\nI'm using build 2022.12.15 on watch 4 & Huawei phone - everything is working - but just after I installed the latest build onto the watch."}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2023-01-05T20:06:17Z", "body": "I'm using 3.1.0.3"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2023-01-06T00:02:13Z", "body": "Factory reset my watch and installed the same apk I had before and it's working again. Would love to get to the bottom of it though as it seems like a fairly common problem and has happened to me twice from the same pair of apks. Loose a lot of time factory resetting the watch too reinstalling and configuring things. Appreciate it might be an Android thing too."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2023-01-09T18:51:01Z", "body": "Will testing dev I have been updating my Watch4 with new .apk versions multiply times without anu problems.\r\nAre you absolutely sure you did not by accident install a new version .APK that was build with a different signing key?\r\nThis could cause a duplicate installation, hence problems? "}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2023-01-09T21:54:22Z", "body": "100% sure on that. I built both the apks at the same time with the same key and stored them in my Google Drive where they are on thier own. Also it worked for a month. It's working again after a reinstall."}, {"user": "wootmasterslick", "created_at": "2023-01-16T20:27:55Z", "body": "Same problem here with Galaxy watch 5. Works for short time after reboot of watch then it stops. Only happens when using a stock watchface. AAPS watchface seems to work ok."}, {"user": "Aeliassen", "created_at": "2023-02-21T14:22:49Z", "body": "I have the same problem running Galaxy Watch 5 Pro. \r\nWhen using stock watchface the app stops sending commands (calculator, treatments tt). After restart of the watch the app works fine for a short while. The watch still recieves and displays data from AAPS (BG, IOB, COB) \r\n\r\nI don't think this issue happens if I use a AAPS watchface"}, {"user": "agmsd", "created_at": "2023-03-16T17:07:52Z", "body": "Yep! Not working for me as well! It was working with the previous versions! I'm using a Samsung Galaxy Watch4 Classic with Wear OS 3.5"}], "text": "[3.1.0.3] Wear entered treatments are not received by my phone (no confirmation)  Wear entered treatments are not received by my phone (no confirmation)\r\n\r\nKeys should be the same for both mobile app and wear app, as was working fine for a month after an initial issue.\r\n\r\nReporting bugs\r\n--------------\r\n- **Note the precise time the problem occurred** and describe the circumstances and steps that caused\r\n  the problem. 11:05am NZDT\r\n- Logs Sent\r\n- FB Post: https://www.facebook.com/groups/AndroidAPSUsers/posts/3438350919719634\r\n Important information is missing on this issue:\r\n\r\n* No logs included with this issue\r\n* What AAPS release/version/build are you running (add a screen print from AAPS's about?\r\n* What phone brand/type/OS\r\n* What watch brand/type/OS\r\n* Are Phone and Watch running latest updates\r\n* How did you install the wear-full-release.apk?\r\n* What watch face are you using?\r\n\r\nDid you try uninstalling the wear app and select a stock watch face, then switch off the watch, then switch it on again and reinstall the AAPS wear app?\r\n\r\n @vanelsberg\r\n\r\n- logs were shared via email from the app. I also referenced this Github issue number in the email. See \"Logs sent\" above. Sorry if I did it wrong.\r\n- Version number is in the title.\r\n- Phone S22 Ultra, Galaxy Watch 4 (both on latest updates)\r\n- Wear app installed via \"Wear Installer 2\". Was working for treatments then unexpectedly stopped.\r\n- Digital watch face and standard AAPS watch face have the same issue\r\n\r\nWill try the reinstall steps suggested and report back. Does your watch have the latest built of AAPS? Have you tried to rebuild & generate the latest phone .apk\r\n\r\nI'm using build 2022.12.15 on watch 4 & Huawei phone - everything is working - but just after I installed the latest build onto the watch. I'm using 3.1.0.3 Factory reset my watch and installed the same apk I had before and it's working again. Would love to get to the bottom of it though as it seems like a fairly common problem and has happened to me twice from the same pair of apks. Loose a lot of time factory resetting the watch too reinstalling and configuring things. Appreciate it might be an Android thing too. Will testing dev I have been updating my Watch4 with new .apk versions multiply times without anu problems.\r\nAre you absolutely sure you did not by accident install a new version .APK that was build with a different signing key?\r\nThis could cause a duplicate installation, hence problems?  100% sure on that. I built both the apks at the same time with the same key and stored them in my Google Drive where they are on thier own. Also it worked for a month. It's working again after a reinstall. Same problem here with Galaxy watch 5. Works for short time after reboot of watch then it stops. Only happens when using a stock watchface. AAPS watchface seems to work ok. I have the same problem running Galaxy Watch 5 Pro. \r\nWhen using stock watchface the app stops sending commands (calculator, treatments tt). After restart of the watch the app works fine for a short while. The watch still recieves and displays data from AAPS (BG, IOB, COB) \r\n\r\nI don't think this issue happens if I use a AAPS watchface Yep! Not working for me as well! It was working with the previous versions! I'm using a Samsung Galaxy Watch4 Classic with Wear OS 3.5"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-2329", "type": "thread", "title": "AAPS crashes when applying the setting", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2329", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2329, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2023-01-06T13:39:19Z", "closed_at": "2023-01-11T14:19:48Z", "comment_count": 30, "comments": [{"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2023-01-06T20:30:15Z", "body": "what is last dev version?"}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-07T10:25:22Z", "body": "![Screenshot_20230107-112358](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/94917775/211145679-5cecbe53-6056-478b-9741-428dafcf58d4.png)\r\n"}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-07T10:40:40Z", "body": "AAPS only crashes when I press the Settings button.\r\n![Screenshot_20230107-113346](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/94917775/211146192-ae7745e5-05e8-42c9-88e9-6c047581c5f3.jpeg)\r\n"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2023-01-07T22:41:02Z", "body": "there is already newer commit\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/211172955-1a624979-3aad-49ac-a4a1-3377443e391d.png)\r\n\r\ntry latest dev"}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-08T10:25:08Z", "body": "Thank you, I will do it immediately."}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-08T10:36:30Z", "body": "Installed the new version and still AAPS crashes when using the \"Settings\" button."}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-08T10:48:28Z", "body": "[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/10368170/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2023-01-08T11:14:14Z", "body": "there is no app start in log"}, {"user": "Viewquest", "created_at": "2023-01-08T11:16:29Z", "body": "Ok, how can the error be fixed. The version from 01/02/2023 did not have this error."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2023-01-08T11:19:09Z", "body": "do not open all preferences but only plugin preference one by one .\r\nIt's probably in some I don't use"}], "text": "AAPS crashes when applying the setting  I have the following error since the last DEV F version: If I go to settings, AAPS is terminated immediately. All other functions are still applicable. In addition, since the penultimate version, the Eop2 has been beeping when I make a profile change. Attach to the last LOG.\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1673011924856.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/10360491/AndroidAPS_LOG_1673011924856.log.zip)\r\n what is last dev version? ![Screenshot_20230107-112358](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/94917775/211145679-5cecbe53-6056-478b-9741-428dafcf58d4.png)\r\n AAPS only crashes when I press the Settings button.\r\n![Screenshot_20230107-113346](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/94917775/211146192-ae7745e5-05e8-42c9-88e9-6c047581c5f3.jpeg)\r\n there is already newer commit\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/211172955-1a624979-3aad-49ac-a4a1-3377443e391d.png)\r\n\r\ntry latest dev Thank you, I will do it immediately. Installed the new version and still AAPS crashes when using the \"Settings\" button. [AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/10368170/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n there is no app start in log Ok, how can the error be fixed. The version from 01/02/2023 did not have this error. do not open all preferences but only plugin preference one by one .\r\nIt's probably in some I don't use"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-2573", "type": "thread", "title": "[DEV 3.2.0-dev-j cd9f5e4] Problem opening preferences", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2573", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2573, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2023-06-05T19:03:29Z", "closed_at": "2023-06-14T16:16:24Z", "comment_count": 29, "comments": [{"user": "jbm76", "created_at": "2023-06-08T12:50:52Z", "body": "Good morning,\r\n\r\nThe exact same thing happened to me yesterday. AAPS crashed and I was unable to access the preferences, just as shown in the video.\r\n\r\nAAPS  dev-j compiled 01/06/2023\r\n\r\nAttach Log de AAPS ( 20:45) and screenshot of how it continuously started AAPS and when trying again to access the preferences it crashed\r\n\r\nThanks in advance\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS._2023-06-07_21-08-23_.21.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/11688308/AndroidAPS._2023-06-07_21-08-23_.21.zip)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_2023-06-08-14-43-36-27](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/45192678/01c4dc46-9c57-40b1-ae40-2da44a9fc0a3)\r\n"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2023-06-08T16:22:57Z", "body": "Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language."}, {"user": "fjpezuela", "created_at": "2023-06-08T22:38:54Z", "body": "> Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n\r\nIt could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;)"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2023-06-09T05:57:15Z", "body": "> > Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n> \r\n> It could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;)\r\n\r\nIf you had selected \"System Default\", change your phone language and check if AAPS default language is changed.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20230609_065637_AAPS](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/608650/55f87ae5-dc79-48e6-a4f7-968cb61a8b13)\r\n"}, {"user": "fjpezuela", "created_at": "2023-06-09T07:24:52Z", "body": "I've tried, but I must have it set to \"Spanish\". Thanks.\r\n> > > Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > It could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;)\r\n> \r\n> If you had selected \"System Default\", change your phone language and check if AAPS default language is changed.\r\n> \r\n> ![Screenshot_20230609_065637_AAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/608650/244604075-55f87ae5-dc79-48e6-a4f7-968cb61a8b13.jpg)\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2023-06-10T10:33:13Z", "body": "@MilosKozak Can you check if Spanish translation is OK?"}, {"user": "fjpezuela", "created_at": "2023-06-10T10:44:25Z", "body": "Yesterday I updated to the latest build with the latest modifications and now it opens correctly."}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2023-06-10T10:56:06Z", "body": "Great. Now you can close the ticket."}, {"user": "jbm76", "created_at": "2023-06-10T21:27:39Z", "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\n\r\nThis keeps failing even with the latest version dev of APPS . ( f1118e2)\r\n\r\nAfter installing it two days ago, on the third day and having \"system default\" selected as the language in the application, it has broken again in exactly the same way, not allowing access to the preferences menu.\r\n\r\nAttached video identical to the previously uploaded as well as the log of the app\r\n\r\nPlease,reopen the ticket because this is failing in latest versions of the dev.\r\n\r\n\r\nthank you very much in advance\r\n\r\n\r\nAAPS dev - j (f1118e2) \r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS._2023-06-10_21-48-53_.23.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/11713372/AndroidAPS._2023-06-10_21-48-53_.23.zip)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/45192678/6c8a18f1-ef34-4fae-9acf-0956a78875ef\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "scastanocaro", "created_at": "2023-06-11T15:46:13Z", "body": "Good afternoon\r\n\r\nI have the same problem with the version I have just compiled now and previous ones.  I can access neither to preferences nor to configuration. When I select one of both functionalities AAPS crashed. AAPS only let me access to both functionalities only betwen 2 patches, when no patch is running.\r\n\r\nThank you very much in advance"}], "text": "[DEV 3.2.0-dev-j cd9f5e4] Problem opening preferences  When opening any option that accesses anything related to preferences, the application crashes and closes. I haven't had any problems until today. I attach the logs and video.\r\n\r\nThe last error is around 20:59 (see video)\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/11655834/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/67511778/5c188225-4f53-4f0b-8a06-1b630c0c64bc\r\n\r\nThanks.\r\n Good morning,\r\n\r\nThe exact same thing happened to me yesterday. AAPS crashed and I was unable to access the preferences, just as shown in the video.\r\n\r\nAAPS  dev-j compiled 01/06/2023\r\n\r\nAttach Log de AAPS ( 20:45) and screenshot of how it continuously started AAPS and when trying again to access the preferences it crashed\r\n\r\nThanks in advance\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS._2023-06-07_21-08-23_.21.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/11688308/AndroidAPS._2023-06-07_21-08-23_.21.zip)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_2023-06-08-14-43-36-27](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/45192678/01c4dc46-9c57-40b1-ae40-2da44a9fc0a3)\r\n Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language. > Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n\r\nIt could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;) > > Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n> \r\n> It could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;)\r\n\r\nIf you had selected \"System Default\", change your phone language and check if AAPS default language is changed.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20230609_065637_AAPS](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/608650/55f87ae5-dc79-48e6-a4f7-968cb61a8b13)\r\n I've tried, but I must have it set to \"Spanish\". Thanks.\r\n> > > Do you have the same issue if the language is set to English? I can see that both of you aren't using English as default language.\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > It could be. The problem is that we can't access the preferences to change it ;)\r\n> \r\n> If you had selected \"System Default\", change your phone language and check if AAPS default language is changed.\r\n> \r\n> ![Screenshot_20230609_065637_AAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/608650/244604075-55f87ae5-dc79-48e6-a4f7-968cb61a8b13.jpg)\r\n\r\n @MilosKozak Can you check if Spanish translation is OK? Yesterday I updated to the latest build with the latest modifications and now it opens correctly. Great. Now you can close the ticket. Hello,\r\n\r\n\r\nThis keeps failing even with the latest version dev of APPS . ( f1118e2)\r\n\r\nAfter installing it two days ago, on the third day and having \"system default\" selected as the language in the application, it has broken again in exactly the same way, not allowing access to the preferences menu.\r\n\r\nAttached video identical to the previously uploaded as well as the log of the app\r\n\r\nPlease,reopen the ticket because this is failing in latest versions of the dev.\r\n\r\n\r\nthank you very much in advance\r\n\r\n\r\nAAPS dev - j (f1118e2) \r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS._2023-06-10_21-48-53_.23.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/11713372/AndroidAPS._2023-06-10_21-48-53_.23.zip)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/assets/45192678/6c8a18f1-ef34-4fae-9acf-0956a78875ef\r\n\r\n Good afternoon\r\n\r\nI have the same problem with the version I have just compiled now and previous ones.  I can access neither to preferences nor to configuration. When I select one of both functionalities AAPS crashed. AAPS only let me access to both functionalities only betwen 2 patches, when no patch is running.\r\n\r\nThank you very much in advance"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3181", "type": "thread", "title": "UAM SMBs with Libre 2", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3181", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3181, "labels": ["enhancement", "for_discussion"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2024-01-22T14:06:50Z", "closed_at": "2024-12-02T22:39:26Z", "comment_count": 43, "comments": [{"user": "painbrain81", "created_at": "2024-02-10T16:40:54Z", "body": "I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2)"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2024-02-11T10:55:40Z", "body": "> I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2)\r\n\r\nEvery smoothing makes the data \"nicer\" but add to data inaccuracy and delays. And you doubled it"}, {"user": "painbrain81", "created_at": "2024-02-11T10:58:57Z", "body": "It can be, but in my experience smooth data is always real respect \"real\" bg blood (after 15 mins between fsl2 and finger).\r\nIt depends between person and person? It could be"}, {"user": "Svagtlys", "created_at": "2024-02-14T09:17:00Z", "body": "> > I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2)\r\n> \r\n> Every smoothing makes the data \"nicer\" but add to data inaccuracy and delays. And you doubled it\r\n\r\nSorry, I don't entirely understand how the AAPS and xDrip smoothing work, but doesn't the Dexcom do smoothing all the time? So if accuracy is a concern preventing this feature for our CGM, the Freestyle 2 should have the leg up for always reporting exactly what it's reading?\r\n\r\nAt the moment, we've just been setting a temp target all the time to get this to work somewhat like we're wanting. It's not perfect, we'd really love to use autosens to adjust the target on the fly and to not have to remember to reset the target after activity or hypo, but it's been amazing for helping us out when we inevitably forget to indicate carbs for a meal or snack."}, {"user": "Svagtlys", "created_at": "2024-03-11T21:28:42Z", "body": "I just wanted to follow up on this a month later. \r\n\r\nWe've continued setting a temp target to get something close to UAMs, and we have been *much* more lax in putting in carbs (I'd say about 50% of the time we put them in before we start to eat, 30% we put them in within 20 minutes of eating, and the rest we forget for more than 20 minutes or don't remember at all). I ran a CGP report before we started doing this, and ran one just now for the duration we've been doing this, and the numbers are a bit worse now but still surprisingly close to \"We're completely on top of T1D every day because we're focusing\". We're happy to share the reports if it would provide any useful information on the effectiveness of the Libre Freestyle 2 as a UAM compatible CGM."}, {"user": "cO5Mo2", "created_at": "2024-04-10T10:43:58Z", "body": "In light of the now well-documented good performance of the freestyle Libre 3 I would love to be able to use features like autosens, UAM etc. \r\nI had absolutely zero issues with wrong or jumpy data. \r\nFL3 seems to now have a similar error correction as the dexcom sensors. Suspicious values are not sent to the phone. In such cases the sensor takes a few minutes time out. \r\n\r\nHere are two studies. One comparing dexcom G7 and Freestyle Libre 3. \r\n\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38189290/\r\n\r\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10064376/"}, {"user": "tyrex1975", "created_at": "2024-04-21T17:11:50Z", "body": "Agreed with the comments regarding SMB-always for the Libre above. AAPS is renowned for its openness of operation and fine customisable options by the user.\r\n\r\nUser acceptance of the risks involved is an obligatory feature of building your own app, yet disabling a particular feature flies in the face of this ethos.\r\n\r\nI don't even want to use SMB-always because I quite like the 'relaxed' operation of AAPS overnight when SMBs are off.\r\n\r\nBut to tell me I can't enable a feature stinks a bit, in my opinion."}, {"user": "Oscar218704", "created_at": "2024-04-23T09:15:09Z", "body": "Agree with smb always for fsl2. Already using it with a workaround with temp tarheta. Would love to use it normally"}, {"user": "koelewij", "created_at": "2024-04-29T21:19:39Z", "body": "The Libre 1 bug that was reported a very long time ago, wasn’t probably even a Libre issue, but caused by the the Bluetooth interface placed on top of it. \r\nThe issue is long gone with Libre 2. "}, {"user": "InvaderStef", "created_at": "2024-05-13T11:07:18Z", "body": "I'm in the same boat. AAPS denies \"SMB always\" and \"after carbs\".\r\nUsing Libre 3 with Juggluco and xdrip+ my personal libre data seems to be pretty stable so i would vote for a removal of these constraints for current Libre sensors, too.\r\n\r\nThe constraints even seem to make little sense as you can easily overrule them by setting temp targets... (not tested, only read here and on discord)"}], "text": "UAM SMBs with Libre 2 enhancement for_discussion This is a feature/enhancement request regarding the usage of SMBs with the Libre 2 (and potentially 3).\r\n\r\nWe started objective 9 and it seems that many of the SMB options (Enable SMB Always, Enable SMB After Carbs, and, most importantly for us, Enable UAM) are unavailable to users of the Libre 2 CGM. The listed reason in the docs is a need for data smoothing as the sensors themselves do not smooth output, but we enabled a smoothing algorithm through xDrip and still cannot use these options.\r\n\r\nWe asked about the SMB options in AAPS in the WANW Discord and were informed that the L1 had a bug that might report a flat high BG during an error event instead of reporting the error, and this was the actual reason that these SMB options were disabled for the Libre 2 and 3. A discussion ensued with various people agreeing that a flat high BG is not an issue, us included- we have only ever seen a flat low BG, and even that only once in the last year.\r\n\r\nWith both of these problems (BG noise and high BG instead of error events) not being an issue for the Libre 2 and 3, and given that the Libre sensors are approved by various agencies for use in loops, we're requesting that these limitations on SMBs be lifted, potentially with enforcement of smoothing algorithm usage. At the very least, we would like AAPS to have a way for the user to acknowledge the risks and then manually enable the SMB features through the AAPS menus. I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2) > I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2)\r\n\r\nEvery smoothing makes the data \"nicer\" but add to data inaccuracy and delays. And you doubled it It can be, but in my experience smooth data is always real respect \"real\" bg blood (after 15 mins between fsl2 and finger).\r\nIt depends between person and person? It could be > > I agree. I would add that with BOTH xdrip smoothing and aps smoothing the leveling of the blood sugar data is almost perfect (i use FSL2)\r\n> \r\n> Every smoothing makes the data \"nicer\" but add to data inaccuracy and delays. And you doubled it\r\n\r\nSorry, I don't entirely understand how the AAPS and xDrip smoothing work, but doesn't the Dexcom do smoothing all the time? So if accuracy is a concern preventing this feature for our CGM, the Freestyle 2 should have the leg up for always reporting exactly what it's reading?\r\n\r\nAt the moment, we've just been setting a temp target all the time to get this to work somewhat like we're wanting. It's not perfect, we'd really love to use autosens to adjust the target on the fly and to not have to remember to reset the target after activity or hypo, but it's been amazing for helping us out when we inevitably forget to indicate carbs for a meal or snack. I just wanted to follow up on this a month later. \r\n\r\nWe've continued setting a temp target to get something close to UAMs, and we have been *much* more lax in putting in carbs (I'd say about 50% of the time we put them in before we start to eat, 30% we put them in within 20 minutes of eating, and the rest we forget for more than 20 minutes or don't remember at all). I ran a CGP report before we started doing this, and ran one just now for the duration we've been doing this, and the numbers are a bit worse now but still surprisingly close to \"We're completely on top of T1D every day because we're focusing\". We're happy to share the reports if it would provide any useful information on the effectiveness of the Libre Freestyle 2 as a UAM compatible CGM. In light of the now well-documented good performance of the freestyle Libre 3 I would love to be able to use features like autosens, UAM etc. \r\nI had absolutely zero issues with wrong or jumpy data. \r\nFL3 seems to now have a similar error correction as the dexcom sensors. Suspicious values are not sent to the phone. In such cases the sensor takes a few minutes time out. \r\n\r\nHere are two studies. One comparing dexcom G7 and Freestyle Libre 3. \r\n\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38189290/\r\n\r\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10064376/ Agreed with the comments regarding SMB-always for the Libre above. AAPS is renowned for its openness of operation and fine customisable options by the user.\r\n\r\nUser acceptance of the risks involved is an obligatory feature of building your own app, yet disabling a particular feature flies in the face of this ethos.\r\n\r\nI don't even want to use SMB-always because I quite like the 'relaxed' operation of AAPS overnight when SMBs are off.\r\n\r\nBut to tell me I can't enable a feature stinks a bit, in my opinion. Agree with smb always for fsl2. Already using it with a workaround with temp tarheta. Would love to use it normally The Libre 1 bug that was reported a very long time ago, wasn’t probably even a Libre issue, but caused by the the Bluetooth interface placed on top of it. \r\nThe issue is long gone with Libre 2.  I'm in the same boat. AAPS denies \"SMB always\" and \"after carbs\".\r\nUsing Libre 3 with Juggluco and xdrip+ my personal libre data seems to be pretty stable so i would vote for a removal of these constraints for current Libre sensors, too.\r\n\r\nThe constraints even seem to make little sense as you can easily overrule them by setting temp targets... (not tested, only read here and on discord)"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3535", "type": "thread", "title": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Semi-tranparent dots mess up the glucose plot", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3535", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3535, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2024-11-17T11:50:09Z", "closed_at": "2024-12-05T16:10:35Z", "comment_count": 25, "comments": [{"user": "yhonatanb20", "created_at": "2024-11-17T17:53:51Z", "body": "I mean, look, this looks funny, right?\r\n![Screenshot_20241117_195232_AAPS](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45784116-2d0c-4956-b0f5-70392baa2b13)\r\n"}, {"user": "parapenT1sta", "created_at": "2024-11-17T17:56:26Z", "body": "Try with the latest commit: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/4373ecdde4a0fc3aaa3b74ae1b9da6a769007a4e"}, {"user": "yhonatanb20", "created_at": "2024-11-17T19:24:35Z", "body": "Thanks @parapenT1sta, installed latest dev, still facing same issue"}, {"user": "yhonatanb20", "created_at": "2024-11-18T07:59:36Z", "body": "@MilosKozak was commit 4373ecdde4a0fc3aaa3b74ae1b9da6a769007a4e meant to fix this issue?"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:16:31Z", "body": "Transparent means recalculated gap"}, {"user": "yhonatanb20", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:21:27Z", "body": "So I suspected. But when using average smoothing half of the values are recalculated, this makes visualization very messy:\r\n![Screenshot_20241118_101841_AAPS](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e9a025a-d015-4313-9dd2-c81d855badb8)\r\nKnowing which values are recalculated is theoretically valuable, but practically it just makes the graph much less readable..."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:23:52Z", "body": "well you should focus on why do you have so many gaps. this should be not common. for most people it's rare"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:25:52Z", "body": "because there are original values visible on top of recalculated, expecting they are backfilled later"}, {"user": "yhonatanb20", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:32:45Z", "body": "> well you should focus on why do you have so many gaps. this should be not common. for most people it's rare\r\n\r\nThese are not gaps in the readings, this results from the smoothing algorithms. I use Xdrip + G7, and \"Average Smoothing or Exponential Smoothing MUST be enabled for meaningful use of the G7 / ONE+ values.\" It is my understanding that this way inevitably many values will be \"smoothed\". Most values were recalculated by the native BYODA algorithm back on G6, right? But this did not affect visualization in AAPS because it wasn't an AAPS smoothing plugin, and I don't feel I lost valuable information there because of all points being opaque."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2024-11-18T08:39:38Z", "body": "![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eccdbd5f-412c-48dd-9372-1f5a84746032)\r\nAt time of receiving this value, previous were missing. Otherwise it would be not transparent"}], "text": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Semi-tranparent dots mess up the glucose plot  Using version 3.3.0-dev-d with xdrip-G7 as data source and average smoothing ON, some datapoints on the BG plot appear semi transparent, but in a kind of alternate way - this just complicates the graph...\r\n![Screenshot_20241117_134312_AAPS](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5c007f3-5409-4646-9686-d94ae21c8a7b)\r\n I mean, look, this looks funny, right?\r\n![Screenshot_20241117_195232_AAPS](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45784116-2d0c-4956-b0f5-70392baa2b13)\r\n Try with the latest commit: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/4373ecdde4a0fc3aaa3b74ae1b9da6a769007a4e Thanks @parapenT1sta, installed latest dev, still facing same issue @MilosKozak was commit 4373ecdde4a0fc3aaa3b74ae1b9da6a769007a4e meant to fix this issue? Transparent means recalculated gap So I suspected. But when using average smoothing half of the values are recalculated, this makes visualization very messy:\r\n![Screenshot_20241118_101841_AAPS](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e9a025a-d015-4313-9dd2-c81d855badb8)\r\nKnowing which values are recalculated is theoretically valuable, but practically it just makes the graph much less readable... well you should focus on why do you have so many gaps. this should be not common. for most people it's rare because there are original values visible on top of recalculated, expecting they are backfilled later > well you should focus on why do you have so many gaps. this should be not common. for most people it's rare\r\n\r\nThese are not gaps in the readings, this results from the smoothing algorithms. I use Xdrip + G7, and \"Average Smoothing or Exponential Smoothing MUST be enabled for meaningful use of the G7 / ONE+ values.\" It is my understanding that this way inevitably many values will be \"smoothed\". Most values were recalculated by the native BYODA algorithm back on G6, right? But this did not affect visualization in AAPS because it wasn't an AAPS smoothing plugin, and I don't feel I lost valuable information there because of all points being opaque. ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eccdbd5f-412c-48dd-9372-1f5a84746032)\r\nAt time of receiving this value, previous were missing. Otherwise it would be not transparent"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3639", "type": "thread", "title": "AAPS Client/ Websockets / BZ Sync", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3639", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3639, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2024-12-20T07:04:11Z", "closed_at": "2024-12-26T20:19:06Z", "comment_count": 30, "comments": [{"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2024-12-20T15:10:29Z", "body": "Which ns server / hosting are you using? Version of NS?"}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2024-12-20T15:16:03Z", "body": "> Which ns server / hosting are you using? Version of NS?\r\n> \r\n> I don't experience this with 10be.de NS master or dev.\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n10be.de + NS Master 15.0.2.\r\nFor me with activated WS the error occurs every few hours, on my wife's follower it doesn't work at all with activated WS."}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2024-12-20T18:01:54Z", "body": "And here are the log files from our second follower, where it is not synchronized at all with the activated websockets.\r\n[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18213885/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n"}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2024-12-20T18:06:27Z", "body": "Write in english please."}, {"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2024-12-20T20:36:47Z", "body": "Ok, so if I want to try to reproduce this, to confirm, is your setup like this?\r\nAAPS = NSClientV3 + WS = ON\r\nAAPSClient 1 and 2 = NSClientV3 + WS = OFF ? \r\n\r\nAnd just one of them sync? For me it sounds like one of your phones got some issues with either settings or permissions. But I will try this setup myself and see.\r\n\r\nMy regular setup is WS = ON with NSclientv3 on all phones. "}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2024-12-20T20:50:23Z", "body": "Not quite right.\r\n\r\nAll with NS V3\r\n\r\nMaster with NS V3 - WS Active - no problems.\r\n\r\nFollower 1 - with AAPS Client (WS Active) problems after a few hours, AND with AAPS Client2 (WS deactivated), no problems.\r\n\r\nFollower 2 - with AAPS Client (WS Active), problems straight away. Only works with WS deactivated."}, {"user": "gerison77", "created_at": "2024-12-21T08:45:09Z", "body": "Running 2 Rigs with the follwoing setups\r\n\r\nEach Rig is running: Master Blackview N6000 3.3.0-rc1 NSClient V3 websockets on and Client Blackview BV 9200 3.3.0-rc1 NSClient V3 websockets on. Servers hosted on 10be.de running **Nightscout 15.3 dev**\r\n\r\nCan't confirm that issue in this setup on 2 rigs, nor with Client 1 nor with Client 2\r\n"}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2024-12-21T11:27:12Z", "body": "That doesn't help me. I can only report my problems. \r\nJust switched all devices to 3.2.0.4 and the problem no longer exists. \r\nI posted the logs, I can't contribute anything more. I'm not a developer."}, {"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2024-12-21T11:31:19Z", "body": "Strange it works when you downgrade to 3.2 🤔\r\n\r\nI have no issues with two phones for my testrig with 3.3 dev. For the sake of it I'll test with three phones later today. If I encounter the same I'll also share logs. "}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2024-12-21T11:54:11Z", "body": "Can you confirm this issue can be reproduced 🤔.\nI mean (was not a temporary issue that can arrive from time to time in NS server, and fixed a bit later...)\nNow it works again (with 3.2.0.4), if you update rig to latest RC1, it reproduce the issue or not?\n@MilosKozak any other idea of potential root cause?"}], "text": "AAPS Client/ Websockets / BZ Sync  Since the Beta 1 version, including the Devs versions, the BZ values ​​are no longer transmitted to the AAPS client when websockets are active. The rest goes through.\r\nMaster websockets ON, AAPSCLient1 websockets OFF - works perfectly, but slowly. AAPSCLient2 websockets OFF - does not work perfectly, breaks off at some point.\r\nSince around 6:20 a.m. there has been no sync of the BZ values. Fully synchronizing NS fixes the error.\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18207147/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n![Screenshot_20241220-075303](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d272aa0-0ad0-49cd-8fba-5fc6f222efe7)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n Which ns server / hosting are you using? Version of NS? > Which ns server / hosting are you using? Version of NS?\r\n> \r\n> I don't experience this with 10be.de NS master or dev.\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n10be.de + NS Master 15.0.2.\r\nFor me with activated WS the error occurs every few hours, on my wife's follower it doesn't work at all with activated WS. And here are the log files from our second follower, where it is not synchronized at all with the activated websockets.\r\n[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18213885/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n Write in english please. Ok, so if I want to try to reproduce this, to confirm, is your setup like this?\r\nAAPS = NSClientV3 + WS = ON\r\nAAPSClient 1 and 2 = NSClientV3 + WS = OFF ? \r\n\r\nAnd just one of them sync? For me it sounds like one of your phones got some issues with either settings or permissions. But I will try this setup myself and see.\r\n\r\nMy regular setup is WS = ON with NSclientv3 on all phones.  Not quite right.\r\n\r\nAll with NS V3\r\n\r\nMaster with NS V3 - WS Active - no problems.\r\n\r\nFollower 1 - with AAPS Client (WS Active) problems after a few hours, AND with AAPS Client2 (WS deactivated), no problems.\r\n\r\nFollower 2 - with AAPS Client (WS Active), problems straight away. Only works with WS deactivated. Running 2 Rigs with the follwoing setups\r\n\r\nEach Rig is running: Master Blackview N6000 3.3.0-rc1 NSClient V3 websockets on and Client Blackview BV 9200 3.3.0-rc1 NSClient V3 websockets on. Servers hosted on 10be.de running **Nightscout 15.3 dev**\r\n\r\nCan't confirm that issue in this setup on 2 rigs, nor with Client 1 nor with Client 2\r\n That doesn't help me. I can only report my problems. \r\nJust switched all devices to 3.2.0.4 and the problem no longer exists. \r\nI posted the logs, I can't contribute anything more. I'm not a developer. Strange it works when you downgrade to 3.2 🤔\r\n\r\nI have no issues with two phones for my testrig with 3.3 dev. For the sake of it I'll test with three phones later today. If I encounter the same I'll also share logs.  Can you confirm this issue can be reproduced 🤔.\nI mean (was not a temporary issue that can arrive from time to time in NS server, and fixed a bit later...)\nNow it works again (with 3.2.0.4), if you update rig to latest RC1, it reproduce the issue or not?\n@MilosKozak any other idea of potential root cause?"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3723", "type": "thread", "title": "Persistent problem. V3+ with enabled websockets / no synchronization with client.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3723", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3723, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-01-09T12:31:25Z", "closed_at": "2025-01-13T16:48:51Z", "comment_count": 24, "comments": [{"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2025-01-09T19:19:35Z", "body": "Strange. I remember this in dev. We are using 3 phones with AAPSClient. All websockets, no issues so far. 10be.de master NS branch.\r\n\r\nWhat happens if you pause / unpause in NSClientv3 plugin? "}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2025-01-10T08:43:57Z", "body": "> What happens if you pause / unpause in NSClientv3 plugin?\r\n\r\nNothing. I've already tried everything. And as I said, there are no problems with 3.2.0.4.\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2025-01-10T14:11:02Z", "body": "Similar problem here, so adding my information here instead of creating separate issue. I have 2 kids using AAPS, I follow them continuously via AAPSClient and AAPSClient2 on my phone, and both client apps are also set up on their dad's phone and my mother's, so they can both have info when they're taking care of the kids. \r\n\r\nI posted on facebook first on 3.3.0:\r\nI have a weird problem after updating to 3.3. The problem is in AAPSclient, but not AAPSClient2, and only on my phone, not my mother's phone. Apparently BG values only download occasionally, even though they are present in nightscout so i can get them continuously on my watch, on kid's watch and everywhere else that downloads from nightscout. I've tried reinstalling the app, clearing cache, clearing data, multiple restarts on both phones, running a full sync from NS (backfilling previous data, but will not fix the ongoing problem). Before update, and after update for the other kid (AAPSClient2), data is synced continuously. \r"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-01-10T17:56:07Z", "body": "if you did test everything pm me your NS and access token"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2025-01-10T19:36:49Z", "body": "@MilosKozak I sent you a PM with nightscout link and token for one of my sites. Here are also a couple screenshots from the other kid illustrating that AAPSClient gets some info, enough to display SMB's and predictions in graph, but no BG values:\r\n![Screenshot_20250110_203016_EDVIN AAPSClient2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ffcf6934-63be-47f8-b483-d143a7a941ba)\r\n![Screenshot_20250110_202959_EDVIN AAPSClient2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9dfb7f6-a5ec-410f-bb8f-7f6b6e169d63)\r\n\r\nlogs from AAPSClient: \r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1736537594947.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18381511/AndroidAPS_LOG_1736537594947.log.zip)\r\nI'll pm you the site + token for this site as well\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2025-01-10T19:53:50Z", "body": "Since I am very nerdy today, i dug into the log and found some clues. \r\n\r\nThe last glucose value was visible in AAPSClient at 19:58:32, first reference in log is here, where it collects entries, does a bunch of tricks, I highlighted inserting BG value.\r\n\r\n19:58:32.921 [EventThread] D/NSCLIENT: [NSClientV3Service.onDataCreateUpdate$lambda$14():216]: onDataCreateUpdate: {\"colName\":\"entries\",\"doc\":{\"app\":\"AAPS\",\"date\":1736535512757,\"device\":\"Libre3\",\"direction\":\"Flat\",\"filtered\":0,\"isReadOnly\":false,\"isValid\":true,\"sgv\":163,\"type\":\"sgv\",\"unfiltered\":0,\"units\":\"mg\\/dl\",\"utcOffset\":60,\"created_at\":\"2025-01-10T18:58:32.757Z\",\"identifier\":\"a3818769-f5e8-5b2d-a1cc-d48532ae35a1\",\"srvModified\":1736535513257,\"srvCreated\":1736535513257,\"subject\":\"Kristin\"}}\r\n19:58:32.924 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-47] D/NSCLIENT: [NSClientV3Plugin$onStart$10.accept():262]: ◄ WS CREATE/UPDATE entries <i>{\"app\":\"AAPS\",\"date\":1736535512757,\"device\":\"Libre3\",\"direction\":\"Flat\",\"filtered\":0,\"isReadOnly\":false,\"isValid\":t"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-01-10T20:30:12Z", "body": "I see Pump status update but not BG. Can you confirm you upload BGs using v3 protocol?"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2025-01-10T20:34:23Z", "body": "I've enabled upload BG to NS in kid's phones AAPS. All phones using NSClientv3, both in AAPS and AAPSClient/2. Can't verify with screenshots right now, as kids and phones are with my ex until next Thursday. "}, {"user": "elgrupo123", "created_at": "2025-01-10T20:55:04Z", "body": "It's very similar for us. Two M5 stacks and several Garmin watches get the BG values ​​from NS, and there are no dropouts. I now switch the websockets OFF on the followers (it is active on the master), otherwise the NS client cannot be used properly. I can also send our NS page + password. PM to Facebook??"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-01-10T23:55:07Z", "body": "@kristinsmotz you don't have synchronized time on all phones. Set Android for automatic time synchronization"}], "text": "Persistent problem. V3+ with enabled websockets / no synchronization with client.  I have already mentioned the problem several times. 3.3.1.0 does not fix the error either. As soon as you use several AAPS clients and all have activated websockets, only 1 device runs properly for a maximum of 12 hours, after which it behaves exactly like the other follower devices, which cannot synchronize the BG values ​​with active websockets from the start. All other data arrives. Even a new, clean installation did not help. The solution is - master (websockets activated), follower (websockets deactivated).\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18361575/AndroidAPS.log)\r\n\r\n\r\n Strange. I remember this in dev. We are using 3 phones with AAPSClient. All websockets, no issues so far. 10be.de master NS branch.\r\n\r\nWhat happens if you pause / unpause in NSClientv3 plugin?  > What happens if you pause / unpause in NSClientv3 plugin?\r\n\r\nNothing. I've already tried everything. And as I said, there are no problems with 3.2.0.4.\r\n\r\n Similar problem here, so adding my information here instead of creating separate issue. I have 2 kids using AAPS, I follow them continuously via AAPSClient and AAPSClient2 on my phone, and both client apps are also set up on their dad's phone and my mother's, so they can both have info when they're taking care of the kids. \r\n\r\nI posted on facebook first on 3.3.0:\r\nI have a weird problem after updating to 3.3. The problem is in AAPSclient, but not AAPSClient2, and only on my phone, not my mother's phone. Apparently BG values only download occasionally, even though they are present in nightscout so i can get them continuously on my watch, on kid's watch and everywhere else that downloads from nightscout. I've tried reinstalling the app, clearing cache, clearing data, multiple restarts on both phones, running a full sync from NS (backfilling previous data, but will not fix the ongoing problem). Before update, and after update for the other kid (AAPSClient2), data is synced continuously. \r if you did test everything pm me your NS and access token @MilosKozak I sent you a PM with nightscout link and token for one of my sites. Here are also a couple screenshots from the other kid illustrating that AAPSClient gets some info, enough to display SMB's and predictions in graph, but no BG values:\r\n![Screenshot_20250110_203016_EDVIN AAPSClient2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ffcf6934-63be-47f8-b483-d143a7a941ba)\r\n![Screenshot_20250110_202959_EDVIN AAPSClient2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9dfb7f6-a5ec-410f-bb8f-7f6b6e169d63)\r\n\r\nlogs from AAPSClient: \r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1736537594947.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18381511/AndroidAPS_LOG_1736537594947.log.zip)\r\nI'll pm you the site + token for this site as well\r\n\r\n Since I am very nerdy today, i dug into the log and found some clues. \r\n\r\nThe last glucose value was visible in AAPSClient at 19:58:32, first reference in log is here, where it collects entries, does a bunch of tricks, I highlighted inserting BG value.\r\n\r\n19:58:32.921 [EventThread] D/NSCLIENT: [NSClientV3Service.onDataCreateUpdate$lambda$14():216]: onDataCreateUpdate: {\"colName\":\"entries\",\"doc\":{\"app\":\"AAPS\",\"date\":1736535512757,\"device\":\"Libre3\",\"direction\":\"Flat\",\"filtered\":0,\"isReadOnly\":false,\"isValid\":true,\"sgv\":163,\"type\":\"sgv\",\"unfiltered\":0,\"units\":\"mg\\/dl\",\"utcOffset\":60,\"created_at\":\"2025-01-10T18:58:32.757Z\",\"identifier\":\"a3818769-f5e8-5b2d-a1cc-d48532ae35a1\",\"srvModified\":1736535513257,\"srvCreated\":1736535513257,\"subject\":\"Kristin\"}}\r\n19:58:32.924 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-47] D/NSCLIENT: [NSClientV3Plugin$onStart$10.accept():262]: ◄ WS CREATE/UPDATE entries <i>{\"app\":\"AAPS\",\"date\":1736535512757,\"device\":\"Libre3\",\"direction\":\"Flat\",\"filtered\":0,\"isReadOnly\":false,\"isValid\":t I see Pump status update but not BG. Can you confirm you upload BGs using v3 protocol? I've enabled upload BG to NS in kid's phones AAPS. All phones using NSClientv3, both in AAPS and AAPSClient/2. Can't verify with screenshots right now, as kids and phones are with my ex until next Thursday.  It's very similar for us. Two M5 stacks and several Garmin watches get the BG values ​​from NS, and there are no dropouts. I now switch the websockets OFF on the followers (it is active on the master), otherwise the NS client cannot be used properly. I can also send our NS page + password. PM to Facebook?? @kristinsmotz you don't have synchronized time on all phones. Set Android for automatic time synchronization"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3796", "type": "thread", "title": "Unable to Install or Upgrade AAPSClient on Android 14 (Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3796", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3796, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-01-30T13:33:54Z", "closed_at": "2025-02-23T16:09:39Z", "comment_count": 22, "comments": [{"user": "emilisev", "created_at": "2025-01-30T17:32:36Z", "body": "Do you also have AAPS installed on this phone ? If yes, you need to compile AAPSClient yourself, because you can't have both compiled with different keystore."}, {"user": "yoeldk", "created_at": "2025-01-30T17:54:17Z", "body": "@emilisev I do have AAPS on my phone but that was always the case and previous versions of AAPSClient worked. As a matter of fact any  AAPSClient version prior to 3.3 (i.e 3.2.0.4) installs with no problem and that's what I'm using now.  "}, {"user": "emilisev", "created_at": "2025-01-30T17:56:22Z", "body": "Yes that's a new restriction starting from this version"}, {"user": "yoeldk", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:03:55Z", "body": "I'm sorry, but I don't understand the logic behind this change. Why should my personal AAPS be linked to AAPSClient, which is solely used to monitor my daughter's sugar levels?\nEspecially given that AAPSClient, unlike AAPS, can be downloaded directly and doesn't require compiling from scratch. "}, {"user": "emilisev", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:07:37Z", "body": "Check the doc if you don't believe me 😉 : https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/RemoteFeatures/RemoteControl.html#download-and-installation\n\nI believe it is not a decision from aaps team but some limitation induced but the android libraries used (they were updated in last version). "}, {"user": "yoeldk", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:13:14Z", "body": "I believe you, but I just don't understand the logic behind this change, especially since it works perfectly in version 3.2.0.4. If this change was imposed by Android libraries rather than the AAPSClient developers, then it's a different matter and beyond our control. I just want to make sure that this is indeed the case."}, {"user": "emilisev", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:21:44Z", "body": "I guess it has something to do with 2 aaps from the same author but different keystore, since the keystore is used to authenticate the app, but I'm no specialist "}, {"user": "yoeldk", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:25:15Z", "body": "The question is what has changed between AAPSClient 3.2.0.4 (everything works fine) vs 3.3 and up (won't install due to conflict). "}, {"user": "emilisev", "created_at": "2025-01-30T18:27:10Z", "body": "Aaps uses a lot of android librairies, and a lot of them were updated (hence the requirement for Android 11 as well), I guess that's where it comes from."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-02-23T16:09:39Z", "body": "it's android limitation. Apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. Permission is new in 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources"}], "text": "Unable to Install or Upgrade AAPSClient on Android 14 (Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra)  I  am unable to install or upgrade AAPSClient on my Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra (Android 14). I have tried both upgrading from an existing installation and performing a fresh install after clearing cache and data, but neither works.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Attempt to install the latest version of AAPSClient 3.3.1.3\n\n2. If upgrading, I get the error:\n\"App not installed as package conflicts with an existing package.\" (See attachment)\n\n3. If performing a fresh install:\nFirst, I receive a Google Play Protect warning stating that the app was built for an older Android version. (See attachment).After selecting \"Install anyway\", I get the same package conflict error.\n\nWhat I've Tried:\n\nUninstalling AAPSClient before installing the new version.\n\nClearing cache and data before uninstalling.\n\nRestarting the device after uninstalling before attempting reinstallation.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d0c93c14-a005-4111-9f79-de6dca27fcec)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6adfdaa1-fd59-4608-bd28-e4540c44d6aa) Do you also have AAPS installed on this phone ? If yes, you need to compile AAPSClient yourself, because you can't have both compiled with different keystore. @emilisev I do have AAPS on my phone but that was always the case and previous versions of AAPSClient worked. As a matter of fact any  AAPSClient version prior to 3.3 (i.e 3.2.0.4) installs with no problem and that's what I'm using now.   Yes that's a new restriction starting from this version I'm sorry, but I don't understand the logic behind this change. Why should my personal AAPS be linked to AAPSClient, which is solely used to monitor my daughter's sugar levels?\nEspecially given that AAPSClient, unlike AAPS, can be downloaded directly and doesn't require compiling from scratch.  Check the doc if you don't believe me 😉 : https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/RemoteFeatures/RemoteControl.html#download-and-installation\n\nI believe it is not a decision from aaps team but some limitation induced but the android libraries used (they were updated in last version).  I believe you, but I just don't understand the logic behind this change, especially since it works perfectly in version 3.2.0.4. If this change was imposed by Android libraries rather than the AAPSClient developers, then it's a different matter and beyond our control. I just want to make sure that this is indeed the case. I guess it has something to do with 2 aaps from the same author but different keystore, since the keystore is used to authenticate the app, but I'm no specialist  The question is what has changed between AAPSClient 3.2.0.4 (everything works fine) vs 3.3 and up (won't install due to conflict).  Aaps uses a lot of android librairies, and a lot of them were updated (hence the requirement for Android 11 as well), I guess that's where it comes from. it's android limitation. Apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. Permission is new in 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3871", "type": "thread", "title": "3.3.1.3-dev crashes when (de-)selecting the Insulin button", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3871", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3871, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-03-05T18:49:25Z", "closed_at": "2025-03-14T09:57:49Z", "comment_count": 26, "comments": [{"user": "ga-zelle", "created_at": "2025-03-05T19:01:41Z", "body": "The other 3 buttons work fine.\nI have a virtual pump (Accu-Chek Combo) selected."}, {"user": "ga-zelle", "created_at": "2025-03-05T19:21:48Z", "body": "More weird observations:\nWhen I activate all 4 buttons the next time I want to de-activte any then the Carb button is not in the regular list but moved further down. I wonder whether it is related to the overlay of the Treatment button with the dev version indicator.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0ee2594-d420-4f6c-bfaf-fbd493c7eef6)"}, {"user": "ga-zelle", "created_at": "2025-03-05T19:39:06Z", "body": "Still happening with 3.3.2.0-dev(1fdf)"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-03-05T20:13:57Z", "body": "Confirming. \nLatest dev 3.3.2.0 crashed and was unable to stop it from crashing (enable the insuline button)\nDowngraded to latest 3.3.1.3 dev to repair and get the logfile.\n\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1741205211390.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19095983/AndroidAPS_LOG_1741205211390.log.zip)"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-03-05T20:38:51Z", "body": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-03-05T21:13:10Z", "body": "Confirming fixed 👍 "}, {"user": "ga-zelle", "created_at": "2025-03-05T21:15:31Z", "body": "The preference screen initially shows the correct, new version info **3.3.2.0(1220)**\nHowever, after clicking on the selections it changes back to **3.3.1.3(hash)**."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-03-05T21:26:40Z", "body": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/8ba1a5e4166f0f9ba1e0dd504672d5633e6cc2c1"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-03-06T12:50:22Z", "body": "@MilosKozak Not seeing any version at all.\nNot on overview, not on preferences or overview preferences. What up 🤔 \n\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1741265861525.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19108654/AndroidAPS_LOG_1741265861525.log.zip)"}, {"user": "ga-zelle", "created_at": "2025-03-06T15:02:03Z", "body": "On my side everything looks fine."}], "text": "3.3.1.3-dev crashes when (de-)selecting the Insulin button  With the dev version (1985) the app restarts everytime when I:\n- click on the preferences button to show Insulin button\n- click on the preferences button to deactivate the insulin button\n\nIt the same behaviour no matter whether SMB or AUTOISF plugin is active.\n\nUnfortunately I cannot find any trace of any logfile for the last 3 days. Was there a further increase in file protection? The other 3 buttons work fine.\nI have a virtual pump (Accu-Chek Combo) selected. More weird observations:\nWhen I activate all 4 buttons the next time I want to de-activte any then the Carb button is not in the regular list but moved further down. I wonder whether it is related to the overlay of the Treatment button with the dev version indicator.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0ee2594-d420-4f6c-bfaf-fbd493c7eef6) Still happening with 3.3.2.0-dev(1fdf) Confirming. \nLatest dev 3.3.2.0 crashed and was unable to stop it from crashing (enable the insuline button)\nDowngraded to latest 3.3.1.3 dev to repair and get the logfile.\n\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1741205211390.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19095983/AndroidAPS_LOG_1741205211390.log.zip) fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e Confirming fixed 👍  The preference screen initially shows the correct, new version info **3.3.2.0(1220)**\nHowever, after clicking on the selections it changes back to **3.3.1.3(hash)**. https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/8ba1a5e4166f0f9ba1e0dd504672d5633e6cc2c1 @MilosKozak Not seeing any version at all.\nNot on overview, not on preferences or overview preferences. What up 🤔 \n\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1741265861525.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19108654/AndroidAPS_LOG_1741265861525.log.zip) On my side everything looks fine."}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-3984", "type": "thread", "title": "AAPS 3.3.3.0_dev_b froze", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3984", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3984, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-05-16T07:46:02Z", "closed_at": "2025-11-23T22:33:21Z", "comment_count": 107, "comments": [{"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-05-16T09:41:29Z", "body": "Got an other freeze to this night.\n\nSince last time I enabled everything to log as I don't know what can cause those freeze.\n\n![Screenshot_20250516_063630_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1f99de36-7be5-4ba6-a86d-706d699d3dae)\n\n![AndroidAPS_LOG_1747370162514.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20241731/AndroidAPS_LOG_1747370162514.log.zip)\n\nI just updated to latest dev this morning after the freeze, I will see if it happen again\n\nEdit : BG was back after a short time."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-05-17T08:00:46Z", "body": "> This happened several times. I look at AAPS and find out that is has frozen during the night. I thought that it was related to Play Protect but it froze again this morning (a bit before 7 AM) and Play protect is OFF.\n\nNo reason is visible in logs\n\n"}, {"user": "WesSec", "created_at": "2025-05-17T08:14:23Z", "body": "![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f655fe46-e458-405f-a5f6-24aa58053623)\n\nI experienced the same 2 times on (86fb), reboot of phone fixed it. Checked the logs and also no reason visible. It didnt crash, it just hung on the latest sate. (it showed last bg was 3 min ago, so upon checking first i didnt notice it was broken). I pulled latest commits and see if i can get a logcat dump when it happens again:\n\nExtras:\nPhone: Samsung S21FE, OneUI 6.1 (Android 14)"}, {"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-05-17T08:23:48Z", "body": "It happened on older commit (f737) but nothing in log. Can't replicate issue as it is random.\n\nI'm on Android 15 (galaxy S23)"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-05-17T09:03:35Z", "body": "`It didnt crash, it just hung on the latest state.`\n\nSame here. No crash, just froze.  No reaction to taps etc.\n\n![Screenshot_20250515_124408_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/111bd63f-4179-4a82-9b18-8a16c6132c8e)\n\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-05-17T19:26:27Z", "body": "> Same here. No crash, just froze. No reaction to taps etc.\n\nOnly AAPS freezes - other apps and phone are then still responsive?\n"}, {"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-05-17T21:08:37Z", "body": "Only AAPS,\nI'm using byoda and it still get BG as usually.\nPhone can be use as usual"}, {"user": "Rabuffulin", "created_at": "2025-05-20T08:24:32Z", "body": "o meu AAPS 3.3.2.0 também trava. O comportamento dele é parecido com o LOOP Aberto. A quantidade de hidratos informada não diminui e as correções não acontecem. O problema é aleatório. Essa noite ele não fez uma única correção e amanheci com a glicemia alta, com 60g de hidratos que foram do meu jantar de ontem. Estava ativa somente a basal programada. Quando fui na aba SMB e atualizei ele gerou uma correção e aplicou, mas se não tivesse feito isso permaneceria congelado. Agora tomei meu café da manhã e parece que está funcionando o LOOP Fechado, mas se isso ficar acontecendo eu pensei em fazer um downgrade de versão, porque na 3.3.1 isso não acontecia."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-05-21T19:17:11Z", "body": "> o meu AAPS 3.3.2.0 também trava.\n\nEnglish please?"}, {"user": "Rabuffulin", "created_at": "2025-05-21T19:20:08Z", "body": "My AAPS 3.3.2.0 also freezes. Its behavior is similar to Open Loop. The amount of carbs entered does not decrease, and corrections do not happen. The problem is random. Last night, it didn’t make a single correction, and I woke up with high blood sugar, with 60g of carbs remaining from my dinner yesterday. Only the programmed basal was active. When I went to the SMB tab and refreshed it, it generated a correction and applied it, but if I hadn’t done that, it would have remained frozen. Now I’ve had breakfast, and it looks like Closed Loop is working, but if this keeps happening, I’m considering downgrading the version because this didn’t happen in 3.3.1"}], "text": "AAPS 3.3.3.0_dev_b froze  This happened several times. I look at AAPS and find out that is has frozen during the night.\nI thought that it was related to Play Protect but it froze again this morning (a bit before 7 AM) and Play protect is OFF.\n\nAs you can see, there was a \"catch-up\" in BGs when I force closed, cleared cache and restarted AAPS.\n\n![Screenshot_20250516_092543_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/46e7859c-bc18-4c27-af40-51d162332de5)\n\nThe logs after force close and restart.\n\n![AndroidAPS_LOG_1747379627382.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20240118/AndroidAPS_LOG_1747379627382.log.zip)\n\n Got an other freeze to this night.\n\nSince last time I enabled everything to log as I don't know what can cause those freeze.\n\n![Screenshot_20250516_063630_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1f99de36-7be5-4ba6-a86d-706d699d3dae)\n\n![AndroidAPS_LOG_1747370162514.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20241731/AndroidAPS_LOG_1747370162514.log.zip)\n\nI just updated to latest dev this morning after the freeze, I will see if it happen again\n\nEdit : BG was back after a short time. > This happened several times. I look at AAPS and find out that is has frozen during the night. I thought that it was related to Play Protect but it froze again this morning (a bit before 7 AM) and Play protect is OFF.\n\nNo reason is visible in logs\n\n ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f655fe46-e458-405f-a5f6-24aa58053623)\n\nI experienced the same 2 times on (86fb), reboot of phone fixed it. Checked the logs and also no reason visible. It didnt crash, it just hung on the latest sate. (it showed last bg was 3 min ago, so upon checking first i didnt notice it was broken). I pulled latest commits and see if i can get a logcat dump when it happens again:\n\nExtras:\nPhone: Samsung S21FE, OneUI 6.1 (Android 14) It happened on older commit (f737) but nothing in log. Can't replicate issue as it is random.\n\nI'm on Android 15 (galaxy S23) `It didnt crash, it just hung on the latest state.`\n\nSame here. No crash, just froze.  No reaction to taps etc.\n\n![Screenshot_20250515_124408_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/111bd63f-4179-4a82-9b18-8a16c6132c8e)\n\n > Same here. No crash, just froze. No reaction to taps etc.\n\nOnly AAPS freezes - other apps and phone are then still responsive?\n Only AAPS,\nI'm using byoda and it still get BG as usually.\nPhone can be use as usual o meu AAPS 3.3.2.0 também trava. O comportamento dele é parecido com o LOOP Aberto. A quantidade de hidratos informada não diminui e as correções não acontecem. O problema é aleatório. Essa noite ele não fez uma única correção e amanheci com a glicemia alta, com 60g de hidratos que foram do meu jantar de ontem. Estava ativa somente a basal programada. Quando fui na aba SMB e atualizei ele gerou uma correção e aplicou, mas se não tivesse feito isso permaneceria congelado. Agora tomei meu café da manhã e parece que está funcionando o LOOP Fechado, mas se isso ficar acontecendo eu pensei em fazer um downgrade de versão, porque na 3.3.1 isso não acontecia. > o meu AAPS 3.3.2.0 também trava.\n\nEnglish please? My AAPS 3.3.2.0 also freezes. Its behavior is similar to Open Loop. The amount of carbs entered does not decrease, and corrections do not happen. The problem is random. Last night, it didn’t make a single correction, and I woke up with high blood sugar, with 60g of carbs remaining from my dinner yesterday. Only the programmed basal was active. When I went to the SMB tab and refreshed it, it generated a correction and applied it, but if I hadn’t done that, it would have remained frozen. Now I’ve had breakfast, and it looks like Closed Loop is working, but if this keeps happening, I’m considering downgrading the version because this didn’t happen in 3.3.1"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-4011", "type": "thread", "title": "Medtrum Pump unreachable after 2 minutes", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4011", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4011, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-03T11:01:24Z", "closed_at": "2025-10-21T15:33:20Z", "comment_count": 35, "comments": [{"user": "PetrMlejnek", "created_at": "2025-06-03T11:18:05Z", "body": "Demonstration video of the behavior here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pks15PPsM8c"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2025-06-05T11:39:48Z", "body": "@jbr7rr "}, {"user": "manfred-h", "created_at": "2025-06-07T08:04:06Z", "body": "I have a very similar behaviour using AAPS version 3.3.2.0 (ba55) on my Google Pixel 8a running Android 15 (BP1A.250505.005.B1).\n\nI'll have to change my pump system later this year, which is why I am running a test with 10 Nano Patches I paid for on my own. The problem has already killed two of the patches. I know of another user running a similar test and he has absolutely no problems on the exact same phone. The only difference is he uses Freestyle Libre2 as the CGM, while I use the BYODA app Petr is using with a Dexcom G6.\n\nIs it possible that BYODA/Dexcom BT might cause this misbehaviour? I'll probably run a new test with a third patch tomorrow, but I'll stop BYODA and its BT connection before that. Will collect logs and post them here then."}, {"user": "manfred-h", "created_at": "2025-06-08T15:29:55Z", "body": "> I have a very similar behaviour using AAPS version 3.3.2.0 (ba55) on my Google Pixel 8a running Android 15 (BP1A.250505.005.B1).\n> \n> I'll have to change my pump system later this year, which is why I am running a test with 10 Nano Patches I paid for on my own. The problem has already killed two of the patches. I know of another user running a similar test and he has absolutely no problems on the exact same phone. The only difference is he uses Freestyle Libre2 as the CGM, while I use the BYODA app Petr is using with a Dexcom G6.\n> \n> Is it possible that BYODA/Dexcom BT might cause this misbehaviour? I'll probably run a new test with a third patch tomorrow, but I'll stop BYODA and its BT connection before that. Will collect logs and post them here then.\n\nAs described, I ran the third test today with BYODA/Dexcom G6 BT completely disabled. For this I killed the BYODA app, cleared its cache and removed all \"Dexcom *\" connections in BT.\n\nAfter that I switched the pump driver in AAPS fro"}, {"user": "jbr7rr", "created_at": "2025-06-10T08:46:41Z", "body": "I see something weird in the logs, I need more information. \n\n@PetrMlejnek , @manfred-h Would one of you be able to test with a custom build(s) with added logging? You can re-use a patch for testing if needed (out of body ofcourse), contact me on discord and I can explain how etc."}, {"user": "manfred-h", "created_at": "2025-06-10T09:12:25Z", "body": "> I see something weird in the logs, I need more information.\n> \n> [@PetrMlejnek](https://github.com/PetrMlejnek) , [@manfred-h](https://github.com/manfred-h) Would one of you be able to test with a custom build(s) with added logging? You can re-use a patch for testing if needed (out of body ofcourse), contact me on discord and I can explain how etc.\n\n@jbr7rr : thanks for looking at the logs! I'll get a new pump base this week, but I'll definitely can add a patch to my pristine sources and build my own .apk, in order retain my local key. Will contact you on discord."}, {"user": "PetrMlejnek", "created_at": "2025-06-10T21:11:00Z", "body": "Hello @manfred-h and @jbr7rr. I tried different pump base, did not help. I also tried the \"trick\" with forcing BYODA to stop, did not help. Right now I am back to 3.3.2.0-dev-Tsunami_3.4.1 and Danai, because of #3984 that also starts to happen to me. Until #3984 is fixed, I will not install current dev version. After that I will be more than happy to test this issue #4011 with added logging."}, {"user": "manfred-h", "created_at": "2025-06-11T08:00:15Z", "body": "Hi @PetrMlejnek, thanks for testing! Too bad to hear the different pump base did not make a change! FWIW, I switched from BYODA to xDrip+ now, but did not test with the Medtrum pump again yet.\n\nI'll continue to get it to work (hopefully) by following what @jbr7rr suggested with his pumpcontrol app!"}, {"user": "PetrMlejnek", "created_at": "2025-06-11T08:06:36Z", "body": "@manfred-h Thank you for your reply. My friend @Korostensky is using AAPS 3.3.3.0-dev, Samsung phone with Android 15 and xDrip+ (instead of BYODA) and have no problems with Medtrum. So the problem really could be some BYODA + Medtrum conflict."}, {"user": "manfred-h", "created_at": "2025-06-11T08:34:10Z", "body": "@PetrMlejnek Yes, as I wrote earlier I suspected that, too. But I found successful users of Medtrum, BYODA and Android 15 in the list on Discord...\n\nI hope you didn't throw away your patches yet, as @jbr7rr wrote in some private discussion they can be reactivated for additional tests, which is where the \"aaps-pumpcontrol\" app comes into play. It is a second AAPS app, but only for testing other stuff, and which is installed next to your real AAPS app to continue using your working loop configuration. @jbr7rr will setup a separate branch for us which will emit more/changed logs to identify what might the real reason for the failures we see. So, I would encourage you to try that out, too. Shall I pull you into my communication channel I have with @jbr7rr on Discord?"}], "text": "Medtrum Pump unreachable after 2 minutes  Medtrum pump + Android 15 + BYODA: I have a problem with Medtrum pump disconnecting from phone and cannot connect back. After phone restart the pump communicates with AAPS about 2 minutes so I can get bolus or set new profile, but after this time AAPS just cannot connect with pump anymore. If I restart the phone, I can control the pump again, but again just for about 2 minutes.\n\nI use:\nSamsung Galaxy S24 Ultra (Android 15)\nBYODA 1.12.1.0 (Dexcom G6)\nAAPS 3.3.3.0-dev\nBuild: 1590206a4a-2025.05.30\nMedtrum pump (type MD8201, FW version 1.80.83)\n\nI tried and did not help:\nAAPS - Medtrum option - Scan on connection error ON/OFF\nAAPS option - BT Watchdog ON/OFF\nUninstalling and clean install of AAPS\nDifferent AAPS builds (3.3.2.0-Tsunami_3.4.1, 3.2.0.4-AutoISF)\nPlay Protect ON/OFF\nNew Metrum pump/reservoir\n\nWhat works?\nSetup above, but Danai pump\nSetup above, but my older phone (S23+ with Android 14)\n\nSome other users have no problems with AAPS 3.3.3.0-dev + Medtrum + Android 15 combo, but they don't use BYODA (but xDrip for example). So maybe there is some conflict between Medtrum and BYODA on Android 15?\n\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1748868734664.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20572245/AndroidAPS_LOG_1748868734664.log.zip) Demonstration video of the behavior here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pks15PPsM8c @jbr7rr  I have a very similar behaviour using AAPS version 3.3.2.0 (ba55) on my Google Pixel 8a running Android 15 (BP1A.250505.005.B1).\n\nI'll have to change my pump system later this year, which is why I am running a test with 10 Nano Patches I paid for on my own. The problem has already killed two of the patches. I know of another user running a similar test and he has absolutely no problems on the exact same phone. The only difference is he uses Freestyle Libre2 as the CGM, while I use the BYODA app Petr is using with a Dexcom G6.\n\nIs it possible that BYODA/Dexcom BT might cause this misbehaviour? I'll probably run a new test with a third patch tomorrow, but I'll stop BYODA and its BT connection before that. Will collect logs and post them here then. > I have a very similar behaviour using AAPS version 3.3.2.0 (ba55) on my Google Pixel 8a running Android 15 (BP1A.250505.005.B1).\n> \n> I'll have to change my pump system later this year, which is why I am running a test with 10 Nano Patches I paid for on my own. The problem has already killed two of the patches. I know of another user running a similar test and he has absolutely no problems on the exact same phone. The only difference is he uses Freestyle Libre2 as the CGM, while I use the BYODA app Petr is using with a Dexcom G6.\n> \n> Is it possible that BYODA/Dexcom BT might cause this misbehaviour? I'll probably run a new test with a third patch tomorrow, but I'll stop BYODA and its BT connection before that. Will collect logs and post them here then.\n\nAs described, I ran the third test today with BYODA/Dexcom G6 BT completely disabled. For this I killed the BYODA app, cleared its cache and removed all \"Dexcom *\" connections in BT.\n\nAfter that I switched the pump driver in AAPS fro I see something weird in the logs, I need more information. \n\n@PetrMlejnek , @manfred-h Would one of you be able to test with a custom build(s) with added logging? You can re-use a patch for testing if needed (out of body ofcourse), contact me on discord and I can explain how etc. > I see something weird in the logs, I need more information.\n> \n> [@PetrMlejnek](https://github.com/PetrMlejnek) , [@manfred-h](https://github.com/manfred-h) Would one of you be able to test with a custom build(s) with added logging? You can re-use a patch for testing if needed (out of body ofcourse), contact me on discord and I can explain how etc.\n\n@jbr7rr : thanks for looking at the logs! I'll get a new pump base this week, but I'll definitely can add a patch to my pristine sources and build my own .apk, in order retain my local key. Will contact you on discord. Hello @manfred-h and @jbr7rr. I tried different pump base, did not help. I also tried the \"trick\" with forcing BYODA to stop, did not help. Right now I am back to 3.3.2.0-dev-Tsunami_3.4.1 and Danai, because of #3984 that also starts to happen to me. Until #3984 is fixed, I will not install current dev version. After that I will be more than happy to test this issue #4011 with added logging. Hi @PetrMlejnek, thanks for testing! Too bad to hear the different pump base did not make a change! FWIW, I switched from BYODA to xDrip+ now, but did not test with the Medtrum pump again yet.\n\nI'll continue to get it to work (hopefully) by following what @jbr7rr suggested with his pumpcontrol app! @manfred-h Thank you for your reply. My friend @Korostensky is using AAPS 3.3.3.0-dev, Samsung phone with Android 15 and xDrip+ (instead of BYODA) and have no problems with Medtrum. So the problem really could be some BYODA + Medtrum conflict. @PetrMlejnek Yes, as I wrote earlier I suspected that, too. But I found successful users of Medtrum, BYODA and Android 15 in the list on Discord...\n\nI hope you didn't throw away your patches yet, as @jbr7rr wrote in some private discussion they can be reactivated for additional tests, which is where the \"aaps-pumpcontrol\" app comes into play. It is a second AAPS app, but only for testing other stuff, and which is installed next to your real AAPS app to continue using your working loop configuration. @jbr7rr will setup a separate branch for us which will emit more/changed logs to identify what might the real reason for the failures we see. So, I would encourage you to try that out, too. Shall I pull you into my communication channel I have with @jbr7rr on Discord?"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-4027", "type": "thread", "title": "No Pod activation possible since Android 16 Update", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4027", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4027, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-06-11T15:18:31Z", "closed_at": "2025-09-25T20:03:04Z", "comment_count": 56, "comments": [{"user": "nickb24", "created_at": "2025-06-11T22:42:07Z", "body": "Adding my findings. \n\nMy phone is a Pixel 7 Pro. Running Android 15 until today with no issues on the Dash pods. I was never using the Dash bond setting.\n\nToday I updated to Android 16, and the current pod continued to work with no settings change in AAPS.\n\nThen I deactivated the current pod and tried to activate a new pod. The pod fails to activate with the following error:  \"Failed to connect to pod\"\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/466797e2-4f4a-4020-9fee-8da4acd12a51)\n\nThe logcat shows the following:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/000be122-a991-45a1-8f80-37a69b8d3c91)\n\nIt fails waiting for the connection here:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ec5eba5-c57d-4754-915b-22e2647f1e0d)\n\nThis is so weird, because the same function call is used for active pods, so why was it working earlier in the day for me, but now is failing with a new pod? I also tried bonding the pod manually in the android settings and it still fails to co"}, {"user": "andyrozman", "created_at": "2025-06-11T23:36:29Z", "body": "Trying to experiment with your main diabetes phone is foolish thing... And upgrading to unsupported system is very foolish thing... There have been a lot of reports of different drivers/pumps not working with Android 15, and you go and upgrade to system (Android 16), that is even less supported... "}, {"user": "m4nnihuber", "created_at": "2025-06-12T05:06:47Z", "body": "Thanks @nickb24 workarount also works for me.\nnice find.\n\nSorry @andyrozman that was not a brilliant idea to switch to android 16 \nshort night so this will not happen again\n\nthanks to the team for finding a solution that quick\nhopefully there will be a dev version or a release soon\n\n"}, {"user": "borijess", "created_at": "2025-06-12T22:10:30Z", "body": "I think I got it. I did Fetch and Pull and did pull hotfix-a16-dash, then a rebase and it updated. Is this correct? Then build the signed APK.\n\nThis is for this hotfix. \n\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4028"}, {"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2025-06-12T22:27:57Z", "body": "Edit:\n**Please checkout branch dev332 and build apk instead, this branch is based on master with these fixes included. Will soon be updated to master**"}, {"user": "borijess", "created_at": "2025-06-12T23:09:29Z", "body": "I did it and did a right click and merge and got this. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f6d422c-bef9-4205-a44c-d6e4935f1ab4)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ba1dc58-2bb5-47da-a058-eeae6f8a4c08)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e63d784b-5ecc-412a-bcc4-bb8c717f91b9)"}, {"user": "olorinmaia", "created_at": "2025-06-12T23:14:43Z", "body": "You shouldn't get any conflicts if you checkout origin/master - then right click on it and create new branch from it - then go to origin/hotfix-a16-dash and select the two mentioned commits and right click and cherry pick"}, {"user": "borijess", "created_at": "2025-06-12T23:28:23Z", "body": "> You shouldn't get any conflicts if you checkout origin/master - then right click on it and create new branch from it - then go to origin/hotfix-a16-dash and select the two mentioned commits and right click and cherry pick\n\nI get this. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bebfe8b6-2084-4491-afb5-6075e49cbf66)"}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2025-06-13T13:24:09Z", "body": "@borijess To answer your question (right place is more here than in PR 😉), when you click in 3 dots menu > about, the build information gives the reference of latest commit, so you can check within github history.\n![Screenshot_20250613-152114_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5b3c056-3080-428b-bae4-41ba45755ce7)\n\n"}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2025-06-13T13:27:00Z", "body": "@borijess your conflicts are due to local modifications done in youŕ computer.\nSo your current code within your computer is not 100% the same than github code."}], "text": "No Pod activation possible since Android 16 Update  Did the Pixel Android 16 Update Yesterday. \nConnection to Dash wored fine so far.\nToday i tried a Pod change. \nDeactivating old Dash worked fine.\nBut there is no Activation for New Pod possibe\n\nBonding Mode didn't work too\n\nWhat are possibilitiea to check? Adding my findings. \n\nMy phone is a Pixel 7 Pro. Running Android 15 until today with no issues on the Dash pods. I was never using the Dash bond setting.\n\nToday I updated to Android 16, and the current pod continued to work with no settings change in AAPS.\n\nThen I deactivated the current pod and tried to activate a new pod. The pod fails to activate with the following error:  \"Failed to connect to pod\"\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/466797e2-4f4a-4020-9fee-8da4acd12a51)\n\nThe logcat shows the following:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/000be122-a991-45a1-8f80-37a69b8d3c91)\n\nIt fails waiting for the connection here:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ec5eba5-c57d-4754-915b-22e2647f1e0d)\n\nThis is so weird, because the same function call is used for active pods, so why was it working earlier in the day for me, but now is failing with a new pod? I also tried bonding the pod manually in the android settings and it still fails to co Trying to experiment with your main diabetes phone is foolish thing... And upgrading to unsupported system is very foolish thing... There have been a lot of reports of different drivers/pumps not working with Android 15, and you go and upgrade to system (Android 16), that is even less supported...  Thanks @nickb24 workarount also works for me.\nnice find.\n\nSorry @andyrozman that was not a brilliant idea to switch to android 16 \nshort night so this will not happen again\n\nthanks to the team for finding a solution that quick\nhopefully there will be a dev version or a release soon\n\n I think I got it. I did Fetch and Pull and did pull hotfix-a16-dash, then a rebase and it updated. Is this correct? Then build the signed APK.\n\nThis is for this hotfix. \n\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4028 Edit:\n**Please checkout branch dev332 and build apk instead, this branch is based on master with these fixes included. Will soon be updated to master** I did it and did a right click and merge and got this. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f6d422c-bef9-4205-a44c-d6e4935f1ab4)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ba1dc58-2bb5-47da-a058-eeae6f8a4c08)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e63d784b-5ecc-412a-bcc4-bb8c717f91b9) You shouldn't get any conflicts if you checkout origin/master - then right click on it and create new branch from it - then go to origin/hotfix-a16-dash and select the two mentioned commits and right click and cherry pick > You shouldn't get any conflicts if you checkout origin/master - then right click on it and create new branch from it - then go to origin/hotfix-a16-dash and select the two mentioned commits and right click and cherry pick\n\nI get this. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bebfe8b6-2084-4491-afb5-6075e49cbf66) @borijess To answer your question (right place is more here than in PR 😉), when you click in 3 dots menu > about, the build information gives the reference of latest commit, so you can check within github history.\n![Screenshot_20250613-152114_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5b3c056-3080-428b-bae4-41ba45755ce7)\n\n @borijess your conflicts are due to local modifications done in youŕ computer.\nSo your current code within your computer is not 100% the same than github code."}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-4049", "type": "thread", "title": "No more connection when ending Nano (and DASH) pods", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4049", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4049, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-07-02T17:28:24Z", "closed_at": "2025-10-05T07:54:47Z", "comment_count": 24, "comments": [{"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-07-02T17:34:04Z", "body": "![Screenshot_20250702_193249_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ba870cb-a9bf-476a-88b3-f193824696b0)\n\nThe last dev. No code change, juste minor limit modification."}, {"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-07-03T05:10:46Z", "body": "I have this issue using Omnipod dash too.\n![Screenshot_20250703_071342_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3bd03dd4-5502-4663-9ebf-83238182ab21)\n\n"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-07-03T05:46:12Z", "body": "@TheNeskik Can you add logs next time you change a pod and the error happens please ? When did this started ? I think mine started with the last dev.\n"}, {"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-07-03T05:52:32Z", "body": "\nI'm having this issue this last dev update too.\n\n![AndroidAPS._2025-07-01_19-36-01_.10.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21031067/AndroidAPS._2025-07-01_19-36-01_.10.zip)\n\nIssue appear when I'm starting a new pod\nIssue around 22h36 on my log file, line 4934\n\n"}, {"user": "TheNeskik", "created_at": "2025-07-04T20:38:24Z", "body": "![AndroidAPS_LOG_1751661223601.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21067712/AndroidAPS_LOG_1751661223601.log.zip)\n\nJust changed my pod.\nNo error on deactivate state but got two error during activation.\nFirst just before priming\nSecond just before cannula insert.\n\nCleaned my log just before changing my pod so log is cleaner :)"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-07-05T16:02:48Z", "body": "Just changed my Nano with extreme attention to detail 😉\n\nI deactivated the pod, came to the _Ok / Next_ choice window. Hit OK to \"not start\" the new pod. I got the same _pump unreachable/basal not set_ alert.\n\nSo, AFA Nano is concerned, the no connection alert comes at the end of the pod deactivation (and not when starting the new one).\n\nAfter _OK_ ing the alert window, I started the new pod normally, without any problems or alerts."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-07-08T10:49:21Z", "body": "@robertrub Confirming: seeing the same\n\n(latest AAPS-dev commits...)"}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2025-07-09T06:03:03Z", "body": "Have you found which commit is the root cause of this issue?\nOr at least what was the previous version/commit without the issue?"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-07-09T07:01:08Z", "body": "It started with the last dev. I'm on vacation (Dordogne,  superbe 🤩) and without any PC 🥰"}, {"user": "HuismanErik", "created_at": "2025-07-25T06:11:24Z", "body": "\n\nI've also encountered this error a few times now when replacing a Dash Pod.\n\nAfter reviewing the log files, I noticed that the RunningMode is set to SUSPENDED_BY_PUMP during the activation of the new Pod. However, even while the Pod is still in its activation phase — during which it shouldn't accept any commands — a CANCEL TEMPBASAL command is being sent.\n\nThis results in the Pod is in an incorrect state error, which makes sense because programming commands aren't allowed until activation is fully completed.\n\nI'm not a very frequent tester of the dev branch, so I can't say exactly when this started. However, I saw that the RunningMode system was introduced in the following commit\n\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/2e85d3be06e437d788d53b2c36aa72ffbf1d349e\n\nCould it be that this issue is related to the changes introduced in that commit?"}], "text": "No more connection when ending Nano (and DASH) pods  This happened 3 times with the deactivation of the Nano pod. Looks like deactivation terminated ok but seconds later, I get this \"pod basal injection\" error.\n\n![Screenshot_20250702_185650_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/217e69ca-42b1-41aa-a51b-c017b4047c8a)\n\nThe logs. Look around 18:57\n\n![AndroidAPS_LOG_1751475422509.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21022814/AndroidAPS_LOG_1751475422509.log.zip)\n\n ![Screenshot_20250702_193249_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ba870cb-a9bf-476a-88b3-f193824696b0)\n\nThe last dev. No code change, juste minor limit modification. I have this issue using Omnipod dash too.\n![Screenshot_20250703_071342_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3bd03dd4-5502-4663-9ebf-83238182ab21)\n\n @TheNeskik Can you add logs next time you change a pod and the error happens please ? When did this started ? I think mine started with the last dev.\n \nI'm having this issue this last dev update too.\n\n![AndroidAPS._2025-07-01_19-36-01_.10.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21031067/AndroidAPS._2025-07-01_19-36-01_.10.zip)\n\nIssue appear when I'm starting a new pod\nIssue around 22h36 on my log file, line 4934\n\n ![AndroidAPS_LOG_1751661223601.log.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21067712/AndroidAPS_LOG_1751661223601.log.zip)\n\nJust changed my pod.\nNo error on deactivate state but got two error during activation.\nFirst just before priming\nSecond just before cannula insert.\n\nCleaned my log just before changing my pod so log is cleaner :) Just changed my Nano with extreme attention to detail 😉\n\nI deactivated the pod, came to the _Ok / Next_ choice window. Hit OK to \"not start\" the new pod. I got the same _pump unreachable/basal not set_ alert.\n\nSo, AFA Nano is concerned, the no connection alert comes at the end of the pod deactivation (and not when starting the new one).\n\nAfter _OK_ ing the alert window, I started the new pod normally, without any problems or alerts. @robertrub Confirming: seeing the same\n\n(latest AAPS-dev commits...) Have you found which commit is the root cause of this issue?\nOr at least what was the previous version/commit without the issue? It started with the last dev. I'm on vacation (Dordogne,  superbe 🤩) and without any PC 🥰 \n\nI've also encountered this error a few times now when replacing a Dash Pod.\n\nAfter reviewing the log files, I noticed that the RunningMode is set to SUSPENDED_BY_PUMP during the activation of the new Pod. However, even while the Pod is still in its activation phase — during which it shouldn't accept any commands — a CANCEL TEMPBASAL command is being sent.\n\nThis results in the Pod is in an incorrect state error, which makes sense because programming commands aren't allowed until activation is fully completed.\n\nI'm not a very frequent tester of the dev branch, so I can't say exactly when this started. However, I saw that the RunningMode system was introduced in the following commit\n\nhttps://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/2e85d3be06e437d788d53b2c36aa72ffbf1d349e\n\nCould it be that this issue is related to the changes introduced in that commit?"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-4201", "type": "thread", "title": "Safety issue: can't stop an ongoing bolus after closing AAPS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4201", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4201, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2025-10-07T12:30:21Z", "closed_at": "2025-11-23T22:30:16Z", "comment_count": 50, "comments": [{"user": "andyrozman", "created_at": "2025-10-07T12:51:32Z", "body": "I would say that is by design... Closing AAPS shouldn't cancel the bolus, unless user presses the button... \n\nNow... Good question... Why did you do the \"Close All\" while bolus was executing... You need to wait until all commands are executed and then you can close your AAPS... \n\nThat small thing there is just showing that command is executed. You can cancel command only while you are in original AAPS instance and when command was issued... AND this is especially true if you are using pump which has no other way of cancelling command (pod pumps without screen and buttons)."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-10-07T20:30:56Z", "body": "Yes. By design and this is correct.\n> Why did you do the \"Close All\" while bolus was executing...\n\nI did to show that _when you do_, there is no way to stop the ongoing bolus.\n- Think about a user entering a large bolus, then realizing this was wrong and panicking - swipes/closes AAPS to stop it...\n\nWhen close/open AAPS I still can STOP the bolus from the watch. Can't see any reason why this would not be possible from AAPS?\n"}, {"user": "andyrozman", "created_at": "2025-10-07T20:45:19Z", "body": "- Think about a user entering a large bolus, then realizing this was wrong and panicking - swipes/closes AAPS to stop it...\n\nYes simple solution, press that little button with \"Stop\" text on it. I don't see anything wrong with how it works... But that is for Milos to decide..."}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-10-08T16:23:44Z", "body": "@vanelsberg I think, if you had used the \"back\" button of Android, you'd see the progression window with the stop button.\n\nEDIT : Discard my message. Just tested, _back_ doesn't bring back the progression bar."}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-10-08T20:27:57Z", "body": "**Imho**:\nAny situation where _user loses control_ over what the pump is doing is \"not be design\" and \"potentially dangerous\" 🤔"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2025-10-19T18:21:20Z", "body": "\n@MilosKozak Merged PR4229 with current dev commits.\n\n@Angus-repo No issues (used your AAPS pr-CI btw 😄)\nNICE! Works as expected ❤️ "}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-10-20T04:07:46Z", "body": "Building dev now. Will test and report."}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-10-20T09:16:53Z", "body": "@Angus-repo Works as expected but there is a small bug.\n\nI start a 0.5U bolus, Android 3 vertical bar, Close all. Open AAPS again.\n\nI see the progression bar (that part is working ok) but the total amount on top of the page is wrong. It probably shows the amount already injected when I _closed all_ \n\nThe xU injected / total yU to be injected line is correct.\n\n![Screenshot_20251020_111049_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce69d87-6faa-4e80-a9b4-d187539f2b9f)\n\n"}, {"user": "Angus-repo", "created_at": "2025-10-20T10:00:08Z", "body": "> [@Angus-repo](https://github.com/Angus-repo) Works as expected but there is a small bug.\n> \n> I start a 0.5U bolus, Android 3 vertical bar, Close all. Open AAPS again.\n> \n> I see the progression bar (that part is working ok) but the total amount on top of the page is wrong. It probably shows the amount already injected when I _closed all_\n> \n> The xU injected / total yU to be injected line is correct.\n> \n> ![Screenshot_20251020_111049_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce69d87-6faa-4e80-a9b4-d187539f2b9f)\n\n@robertrub Which type of pump are you using?"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2025-10-20T10:27:54Z", "body": "@Angus-repo The bug happens even if I quit AAPS and come back to it (without closing it).\n\nScreenshot during lunch bolus. I went to another app then back to AAPS.\n\nIt used to show the total amount on top and the _progression /total amount_ over the progression bar.\n\nI'm using the Medtrum Nano pump.\n\n![Screenshot_20251020_120253_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f8fffc1-6bf0-4404-a2da-c34251ec3122)\n\n"}], "text": "Safety issue: can't stop an ongoing bolus after closing AAPS  **AndroidAPS 3.3.3-dev**: Lates dev builds\n**Flavor**: fullrelease\n\n**Problem:**\nWhen executing a manual bolus the resulting pop-up screen will show bolus progress and a \"STOP\" button to cancel the onging bolus. _Closing the app (using Android UI \"Close All\" or swiping) does not stop the bolus by design. However, when I reopen the AAPS app it only shows the (still) ongoing bolus at the bottom of the overview screen without a STOP button to cancel._\n\nConsidering safety, one could argue that this is not acceptable\n\n**Additional info:**\nTo STOP the bolus then user has no other option then to forcefully close AAPS through settings, restart the phone, disconnect the pump or \n(when running the AAPS Wear app) using the option to cancel the bolus from the watch.\n\n_Screenprints:_\n\n**Ongoing bolus with STOP button enables canceling the ongoing bolus.**\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5f6fa0d-1814-4d58-adba-179ba4b04492)\n\n**After closing and reopening AAPS: ther is no way to STOP the ongoing bolus**\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/15cc5246-7b30-4d1b-a791-8930e97f3919)\n I would say that is by design... Closing AAPS shouldn't cancel the bolus, unless user presses the button... \n\nNow... Good question... Why did you do the \"Close All\" while bolus was executing... You need to wait until all commands are executed and then you can close your AAPS... \n\nThat small thing there is just showing that command is executed. You can cancel command only while you are in original AAPS instance and when command was issued... AND this is especially true if you are using pump which has no other way of cancelling command (pod pumps without screen and buttons). Yes. By design and this is correct.\n> Why did you do the \"Close All\" while bolus was executing...\n\nI did to show that _when you do_, there is no way to stop the ongoing bolus.\n- Think about a user entering a large bolus, then realizing this was wrong and panicking - swipes/closes AAPS to stop it...\n\nWhen close/open AAPS I still can STOP the bolus from the watch. Can't see any reason why this would not be possible from AAPS?\n - Think about a user entering a large bolus, then realizing this was wrong and panicking - swipes/closes AAPS to stop it...\n\nYes simple solution, press that little button with \"Stop\" text on it. I don't see anything wrong with how it works... But that is for Milos to decide... @vanelsberg I think, if you had used the \"back\" button of Android, you'd see the progression window with the stop button.\n\nEDIT : Discard my message. Just tested, _back_ doesn't bring back the progression bar. **Imho**:\nAny situation where _user loses control_ over what the pump is doing is \"not be design\" and \"potentially dangerous\" 🤔 \n@MilosKozak Merged PR4229 with current dev commits.\n\n@Angus-repo No issues (used your AAPS pr-CI btw 😄)\nNICE! Works as expected ❤️  Building dev now. Will test and report. @Angus-repo Works as expected but there is a small bug.\n\nI start a 0.5U bolus, Android 3 vertical bar, Close all. Open AAPS again.\n\nI see the progression bar (that part is working ok) but the total amount on top of the page is wrong. It probably shows the amount already injected when I _closed all_ \n\nThe xU injected / total yU to be injected line is correct.\n\n![Screenshot_20251020_111049_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce69d87-6faa-4e80-a9b4-d187539f2b9f)\n\n > [@Angus-repo](https://github.com/Angus-repo) Works as expected but there is a small bug.\n> \n> I start a 0.5U bolus, Android 3 vertical bar, Close all. Open AAPS again.\n> \n> I see the progression bar (that part is working ok) but the total amount on top of the page is wrong. It probably shows the amount already injected when I _closed all_\n> \n> The xU injected / total yU to be injected line is correct.\n> \n> ![Screenshot_20251020_111049_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce69d87-6faa-4e80-a9b4-d187539f2b9f)\n\n@robertrub Which type of pump are you using? @Angus-repo The bug happens even if I quit AAPS and come back to it (without closing it).\n\nScreenshot during lunch bolus. I went to another app then back to AAPS.\n\nIt used to show the total amount on top and the _progression /total amount_ over the progression bar.\n\nI'm using the Medtrum Nano pump.\n\n![Screenshot_20251020_120253_AAPS.jpg](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f8fffc1-6bf0-4404-a2da-c34251ec3122)\n\n"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-630", "type": "thread", "title": "Only to be sure that the Dev's be aware of some issues. All are in dev versions with the new database until today.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/630", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 630, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-08-13T20:01:23Z", "closed_at": "2021-09-21T13:35:25Z", "comment_count": 40, "comments": [{"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2021-08-16T06:45:17Z", "body": "Statistic: with latest updates, on my phone Samsung A40), TDD is shown much quicker than previously (3 or 4 seconds later)\r\n\r\nDisable Loop: I'll try to work on it today to propose a PR"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-16T08:22:29Z", "body": "The most important is profile switch.\r\nBecause many users are using NightScout for overview at home and will then not recognise that the switch was not done. \r\n\r\nAlso many are using Automation now. If they do a switch over it they didn't see this issue, until they use the phone and checked the overview in AAPS."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2021-08-17T15:45:58Z", "body": "I tested profile switch functionality and it works well\r\nIt happened to me that profile was not saved correctly in NS (still old values after page refresh) thus not sent to AAPS. 2nd times it did work.\r\nAAPS is a bit ahead to NS. NS still cannot distinguish between PS and effective PS thus NS may provide false data based on expectation that PS was already executed"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-17T16:18:41Z", "body": "@MilosKozak \r\nThen I can't understand that, because I tested it just now.\r\nMy active Profile is \"Freier Tag\" and I copy that into \"Freier Tag copy\", than I have done a profile switch to this new profile.\r\nAs I wrote above, the profile switch was shown in NS and also in Treatments, but AAPS is doing nothing.\r\n\r\nYou can see that also in the pump tab, nothing happened here directly after profile switch and AAPS must change the profile in the pump too. Also the main page shows the old profile name.\r\n\r\nI can handle it, because I aware of that and all profile switches works, if you first activate the standard profile, named \"Local Profile\"\r\nIn the attached pictures you can also see, that the profile switch was shown only as a NS treatment.\r\n\r\nMy System:\r\nPump - Medtronic 754\r\nRileylink - OrangeLink \r\nPhone -  Google Pixel 5\r\nAAPS - latest Dev, but happened also with all new database devs before.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210817-180008](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129762973-bfc"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-17T19:21:25Z", "body": "Thanks @Philoul ,\r\n\r\nCan you do me a favour please and test the profile switch, as described above ?\r\n\r\nOnly want to know if it is a problem on my side, or a real Dev problem."}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2021-08-17T21:45:13Z", "body": "On my side all my PS worked, but I only use NS to share my BG values with my dev phone, and I don't have PS in my current automation rules.\r\nI can make some tests in my dev phone but I didn't understand exactly what's wrong or which test I have to do 🤔..."}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-18T00:04:19Z", "body": "@Philoul \r\nTest:\r\n- First at all use local profile in AAPS instead of NS.\r\n\r\n- Make two local profiles (you can simply copy one) and name them ...say \"Workday\" and \"Weekend\".\r\n\r\n- Then activate the \"Workday\" profile. This should work, because you are coming from standard profile.\r\n\r\n- Wait a few minutes, so AAPS have time to send the new settings to the pump.\r\n\r\n- Then try to change this profile to the other one (Weekend).\r\n\r\n- Check if AAPS did this switch. You can see that on the main page and in Treatments.  In my case they are done in NS only, as you see in the pictures above.\r\n\r\nIf AAPS did this switches between this two profiles, this issue comes from my system.\r\nIf not, it comes from AAPS and must be fixed."}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2021-08-18T06:41:39Z", "body": "@Alamo04 Ok I'll test today one more time on my dev phone...\r\nSee a screenshot of an extract of previous PS done (loop phone), I always 2 lines with NS and PS (PS made between different profiles, with or without duration, percentage or timeoffset...)\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-083438_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/52934600/129849546-39966cc7-8823-412c-a748-d784ace4c36e.jpg)\r\n\r\nCan you add the correspondant screenshot of User Entries ? (latest green icon on the right of treatments) may be it could help for understanding something..."}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-18T09:55:25Z", "body": "![Screenshot_20210818-114744](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129877544-865657cb-932e-4999-abfc-f7b97358726e.png)\r\n\r\nOnly the switch between 2 different profiles dosn't work, if not one of them is the standard profile.\r\nA switch to set the profile % higher, or deeper and then switch back to 100%, is working fine."}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-08-18T16:24:55Z", "body": "@Philoul \r\nI tryed a complete clean and new Installation of AAPS.\r\n- Deinstallation of AAPS\r\n- Phone restart\r\n- New Installation of AAPS\r\n- Phone restart\r\n\r\nSame issue with Profile, as you see in attached Screenshots.\r\n\r\nEvery try to activate \"Arbeitstag\" or \"Freier Tag\" failed and was only sended to NS as done.\r\n\r\nOnly if I use the \"Lokales Profile\" and then \"Freier Tag\" both are done in \r\nNS and also in AAPS.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-181248](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129935019-4ed1aae3-77d0-42f7-b4e8-65d0c95cbd01.png)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-181242](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129935283-7b7c548b-041a-4aa8-91ea-2958155bc320.png)\r\n\r\nI hate to write with my Smartphone.😅"}], "text": "Only to be sure that the Dev's be aware of some issues. All are in dev versions with the new database until today.  - [**_Fixed by @Philoul _**]\r\nFor Philoul and Milos it works now, in my case it still doesn't work.\r\n**Profile switch is  buged.:**\r\nYou can't change your personal profile say \"Workday\" to \"Free Day.\r\nIf you do that, it was shown in NightScout as done, but AAPS is doing nothing and has still the old profile active.\r\nTo do the wanted profile switch, you have to change to the \"Local Profile\" first, then you can switch to the wanted one.\r\nBecause this Bug, the Automation  will also not work with profile switches.\r\n**- This happened only, if the Basal rate was in both profiles the same and only the Target, ISF, or IC was different.** \r\n\r\n- [**_Fixed by @Philoul_**] \r\n**Disable Loop:**\r\nIf you disable Loop, then you can't activate it again.\r\nYou have only the option to disconnect the pump. If you do that, you can activate the Loop again and reconnect the pump.\r\n\r\n- **_Fixed by Philoul, but TDD needs time_**\r\n**Statistic:**\r\nThe last fixes will not work for TDD.\r\nAll will shown now immediately,  but not TDD. \r\nTDD needs as long as before.\r\n\r\n- [**_MilosKozak says, \"AMA doesn't provide this value\"._**]\r\n**Autosense Target:**\r\nAutosense Target was not shown on main page, if you are using AMA Algorithm. \r\nIt was shown if you use SMB Algorithm. \r\n\r\n- [**_Fixed by Philoul_**]\r\n**Wrong values for Daily Basal in local profiles:**\r\nAll values of the daily Basal, in all local profiles, are showing the same number.\r\nThis is the daily basal number of the last saved, or resettet profile.\r\nIt's only a visual issue.\r\n\r\n@MilosKozak \r\nIf you have read that, you can close this issue. Wanted only that you are aware of this issues.\r\n Statistic: with latest updates, on my phone Samsung A40), TDD is shown much quicker than previously (3 or 4 seconds later)\r\n\r\nDisable Loop: I'll try to work on it today to propose a PR The most important is profile switch.\r\nBecause many users are using NightScout for overview at home and will then not recognise that the switch was not done. \r\n\r\nAlso many are using Automation now. If they do a switch over it they didn't see this issue, until they use the phone and checked the overview in AAPS. I tested profile switch functionality and it works well\r\nIt happened to me that profile was not saved correctly in NS (still old values after page refresh) thus not sent to AAPS. 2nd times it did work.\r\nAAPS is a bit ahead to NS. NS still cannot distinguish between PS and effective PS thus NS may provide false data based on expectation that PS was already executed @MilosKozak \r\nThen I can't understand that, because I tested it just now.\r\nMy active Profile is \"Freier Tag\" and I copy that into \"Freier Tag copy\", than I have done a profile switch to this new profile.\r\nAs I wrote above, the profile switch was shown in NS and also in Treatments, but AAPS is doing nothing.\r\n\r\nYou can see that also in the pump tab, nothing happened here directly after profile switch and AAPS must change the profile in the pump too. Also the main page shows the old profile name.\r\n\r\nI can handle it, because I aware of that and all profile switches works, if you first activate the standard profile, named \"Local Profile\"\r\nIn the attached pictures you can also see, that the profile switch was shown only as a NS treatment.\r\n\r\nMy System:\r\nPump - Medtronic 754\r\nRileylink - OrangeLink \r\nPhone -  Google Pixel 5\r\nAAPS - latest Dev, but happened also with all new database devs before.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210817-180008](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129762973-bfc Thanks @Philoul ,\r\n\r\nCan you do me a favour please and test the profile switch, as described above ?\r\n\r\nOnly want to know if it is a problem on my side, or a real Dev problem. On my side all my PS worked, but I only use NS to share my BG values with my dev phone, and I don't have PS in my current automation rules.\r\nI can make some tests in my dev phone but I didn't understand exactly what's wrong or which test I have to do 🤔... @Philoul \r\nTest:\r\n- First at all use local profile in AAPS instead of NS.\r\n\r\n- Make two local profiles (you can simply copy one) and name them ...say \"Workday\" and \"Weekend\".\r\n\r\n- Then activate the \"Workday\" profile. This should work, because you are coming from standard profile.\r\n\r\n- Wait a few minutes, so AAPS have time to send the new settings to the pump.\r\n\r\n- Then try to change this profile to the other one (Weekend).\r\n\r\n- Check if AAPS did this switch. You can see that on the main page and in Treatments.  In my case they are done in NS only, as you see in the pictures above.\r\n\r\nIf AAPS did this switches between this two profiles, this issue comes from my system.\r\nIf not, it comes from AAPS and must be fixed. @Alamo04 Ok I'll test today one more time on my dev phone...\r\nSee a screenshot of an extract of previous PS done (loop phone), I always 2 lines with NS and PS (PS made between different profiles, with or without duration, percentage or timeoffset...)\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-083438_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/52934600/129849546-39966cc7-8823-412c-a748-d784ace4c36e.jpg)\r\n\r\nCan you add the correspondant screenshot of User Entries ? (latest green icon on the right of treatments) may be it could help for understanding something... ![Screenshot_20210818-114744](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129877544-865657cb-932e-4999-abfc-f7b97358726e.png)\r\n\r\nOnly the switch between 2 different profiles dosn't work, if not one of them is the standard profile.\r\nA switch to set the profile % higher, or deeper and then switch back to 100%, is working fine. @Philoul \r\nI tryed a complete clean and new Installation of AAPS.\r\n- Deinstallation of AAPS\r\n- Phone restart\r\n- New Installation of AAPS\r\n- Phone restart\r\n\r\nSame issue with Profile, as you see in attached Screenshots.\r\n\r\nEvery try to activate \"Arbeitstag\" or \"Freier Tag\" failed and was only sended to NS as done.\r\n\r\nOnly if I use the \"Lokales Profile\" and then \"Freier Tag\" both are done in \r\nNS and also in AAPS.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-181248](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129935019-4ed1aae3-77d0-42f7-b4e8-65d0c95cbd01.png)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20210818-181242](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36486505/129935283-7b7c548b-041a-4aa8-91ea-2958155bc320.png)\r\n\r\nI hate to write with my Smartphone.😅"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-67", "type": "thread", "title": "UI Feedback", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/67", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 67, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-11-12T15:48:36Z", "closed_at": "2021-01-03T17:04:47Z", "comment_count": 45, "comments": [{"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2020-11-12T16:56:09Z", "body": "I like these!\r\n\r\nCan I also add to this list... I **HATE** the 3 dot menu in the top right hand corner. I have no mobility issues or anything like that described above, but I cannot tell you how often I go to press those 3 dots and end up somehow pulling down the notification/quick settings menu of my phone.\r\n\r\nThis happens all the time for me, but it is even more annoying in the middle of the night when I'm still half asleep and I get a pump disconnect alarm that can only be fixed by exiting AAPS and opening it up again. Its tough to be able to focus when you're half asleep, in the dark, trying to press the smallest of buttons on the menu to get your pump functioning again."}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2020-11-12T21:17:58Z", "body": "@jamespaulley I think it is necessary for security reasons to avoid any single click without confirmation (I do not count the number of unwanted calls and even SMS sent by my pocket!)\r\n=> unwanted several short presses everywhere on the screen are very frequent... The idea of setting a temporary profile with a single press on +10 and tempo is definitively too dangerous ...\r\n=> I never had an unwanted \"Long Press\"\r\n\r\nI understand that it can be difficult for shaky hand to long press on small zone on the top of the screen, but may be a good compromise could be:\r\n- to keep the long press but to double the heigth of the zone to make it easier\r\n- to replace the 2 menus (profile and targets) by temporary buttons with single press action (as you proposed) but only shown after the long press on upper zone... (according to zone you pressed you only show target buttons or profiles buttons)\r\n\r\n@mistermintsgh For the three dot button, if it's only to have an easy way to restart AAPS, there are sev"}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2020-11-12T21:23:36Z", "body": "@Philoul it's not just used to restart AAPS though, it's used to access any of these options\r\n![Screenshot_20201112-212110_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/42671801/98997839-191cb580-252d-11eb-8b11-5366c6704887.jpg)\r\n\r\nMy point being that the button is tiny, and it's far too close to the notification bar to be able to bit with any kind of precision.\r\n\r\nAs I said above, I particularly struggle if I'm half asleep, but I also struggle sometimes in the middle of the day when I'm fully awake!\r\n\r\nIt just needs to be bigger, or in a better position"}, {"user": "swissalpine", "created_at": "2020-11-13T05:53:39Z", "body": "There are larger buttons for temp target and profile switch in the actions tab ... No need to put them on the Home tab. Afaik all preferences can be reached via the config builder.\r\nAnd: If you enter the number directly in the dialogs, and not via the small +/- keys, the number keyboard will open.  This one has quite large numbers ... Of course this is not the one click solution you have in mind - but beside that I don't see the problem.\r\nAnd: On small devices isn't enough place to put additional buttons on the home screen without loosing the main graph."}, {"user": "jamespaulley", "created_at": "2020-11-13T16:47:08Z", "body": "Okay great feedback guys thank you. A few things are being discussed now. I'll summarise everything below. Please also see the attached PDF for mockups and explanations of everything.\r\n\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1LD6uBF8oItpcF1L3NqemBBV_qnc9hl1N/view?usp=sharing\r\n\r\n### Spacing issues at top of Overview Screen\r\n- The spacing is too tight at the top of the Overview screen. It’s hard to use. As mentioned by @mistermintsgh.\r\n- There needs to be more space around the “...” menu.\r\n- The tabs area needs more spacing top and bottom.\r\n\r\n### Concern regarding accidental single-clicks triggering dangerous action\r\nAs mentioned by @Philoul.\r\n\r\n- We can forget the idea of having buttons that immediately trigger a profile change, I agree.\r\n- I think immediate buttons for Temp Targets might still be useful, but I'm happy to drop that for now.\r\n### Long press throughout the UX\r\n- I think long-press is bad UI/UX and we should have the option of not using it. People who want it can keep it, but I "}, {"user": "Philoul", "created_at": "2020-11-13T21:42:11Z", "body": "Thank's @jamespaulley for this detailled synthesis\r\n- For Loop button, if we replace long press by a short one, I think it's necessary to add a confirmation popup because the area that can launch an action is too important (click a second time somewhere in half the screen is enough to disconnect, suspend or disable loop...)\r\n=> All buttons with single press action are followed by a confirmation popup with a small zone (Ok / Cancel)\r\n=> So if we modify this, we should replace a long press and a short press by 3 short presses (like it is done today for bottom buttons)\r\n- For profile switch I think it's a very good idea and it is easy to modify (it's always possible to select field and manually enter another value)\r\n- For Target popup, today the \"menu\" prefilled the values AND select the reason of the TT (with \"Manual\" reason as default), so if we replace selection menu, we have to add an additional information into the popup to show selected reason of the TT (I think it's a good idea too"}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2020-11-13T22:37:10Z", "body": "Suggestion on the profile switch:\r\n\r\n- Make it customisable\r\n\r\nIn the same way I can edit the quick bolus settings (I've edit the small bolus to be 0.25U, the medium bolus to be 1U, and the large bolus to be 2U) it would be could to be able to edit the +/- percentage too. Some might want 5%, some 10% some 20%. Let us choose, through the settings, which quick profile switch we want."}, {"user": "jamespaulley", "created_at": "2020-11-17T11:10:18Z", "body": "### **Loop Button**\r\nI agree that short-presses with a confirmation dialogue would be preferable over the current long-press behaviour, as described by @Philoul. My personal opinion is that 3 short presses is safer than a long click followed by a single click, but I appreciate that others might feel differently. Some users might like the long-press behaviour, so ideally there would be a settings preference for this.\r\n\r\n### Profile Switch\r\nExactly, @Philoul. I also like @mistermintsgh's suggestion for customisation of the percentage intervals for the \"+/–\" buttons on the profile switch screen.\r\n\r\n### **Temp Target Popup**\r\nExactly as described by @Philoul. Alternatively, we could leave the drop-down in place and provide the buttons as well, as seen below.\r\nhttps://i.imgur.com/Txph56A.png\r\n\r\n### **Resolution and display density**\r\n@Philoul points out that if we add too many settings to configure the interface, it'll get too complicated. That's fair enough. I think having a low-density sk"}, {"user": "guydavies", "created_at": "2020-11-17T11:56:55Z", "body": "I would prefer all.those changes to be optional. I like the system as it is.\n\nOn Tue, 17 Nov 2020, 12:10 jamespaulley, <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> *Loop Button*\n>\n> I agree that short-presses with a confirmation dialogue would be\n> preferable over the current long-press behaviour, as described by @Philoul\n> <https://github.com/Philoul>. My personal opinion is that 3 short presses\n> is safer than a long click followed by a single click, but I appreciate\n> that others might feel differently. Some users might like the long-press\n> behaviour, so ideally there would be a settings preference for this.\n> Profile Switch\n>\n> Exactly, @Philoul <https://github.com/Philoul>. I also like @mistermintsgh\n> <https://github.com/mistermintsgh>'s suggestion for customisation of the\n> percentage intervals for the \"+/–\" buttons on the profile switch screen.\n> *Temp Target Popup*\n>\n> Exactly as described by @Philoul <https://github.com/Philoul>.\n> Alternatively, we could leave the drop-down in plac"}, {"user": "4RK4N", "created_at": "2020-11-17T17:09:51Z", "body": "personally i wouldnt need those buttons either. im fine with overview long presses or actions tab for that. actions tab does exactly that alrdy. just add it as tab and swipe right once u have ur buttons for profile change and temp target.\r\nbesides they, sry to say it that way, look like pure eye cancer. (means they are really ugly)\r\nadding those button only makes the problem worse."}], "text": "UI Feedback  ### Overview Screen\r\nI thought it might be nice to have some more useful buttons on the overview screen:\r\n\r\n- Temp target buttons:\r\n  - I find setting a temp target is quite fiddly and hard. There are too many long-presses, clicks and small UI elements involved. Definitely hard for people with shaky hands, etc. It might be nice to have large buttons for these functions on the overview screen, similar to the grey buttons already present.\r\n  - User can choose which targets appear as buttons.\r\n  - The buttons either immediately apply the temp target, or prompt for a confirmation if you think that's safer.\r\n  - Maybe there could be a text area that immediately updates with the temp target that is going to be applied, once the connection to the pump has been established.\r\n- Profile switch buttons:\r\n  - Would be cool if there were -/+ buttons that jump in 10% (or user-defined) intervals. You can click the buttons multiple times (for example to set a profile of 130%), then after a short delay (2 seconds?) the profile switch is applied.\r\n  - There's also a cancel button to set the profile back to 100%.\r\n  - There could be a text area that immediately updates with the profile percentage that will be applied, once the connection to the pump has been established.\r\n  - If you think there are safety concerns with this behaviour, there could at least just be a button that opens the profile switch interface?\r\n- Loop button:\r\n  - Would be cool if we could have the option of the Loop status button (that allows disconnection of pump, etc) to be a normal button, i.e not long-press\r\n\r\n### General UI feedback\r\n- Long press is hard for people with shaky hands, especially on small buttons. Can we have the option to have all button functions without long press?\r\n- There are too many very small UI elements. These are hard to click.\r\n- Drop down menu in Temp target interface (next to \"reason\") is too small and fiddly and annoying. Can we get large buttons for each temp target instead of a drop-down list?\r\n- Percentage -/+ buttons on Profile Switch interface currently go up/down by 1%. Can we have them jump in intervals of 10%, or at least an option to have that.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/26227058/98962057-253d4e80-24fe-11eb-9475-55a9bd9ab8e2.png)\r\n\r\n I like these!\r\n\r\nCan I also add to this list... I **HATE** the 3 dot menu in the top right hand corner. I have no mobility issues or anything like that described above, but I cannot tell you how often I go to press those 3 dots and end up somehow pulling down the notification/quick settings menu of my phone.\r\n\r\nThis happens all the time for me, but it is even more annoying in the middle of the night when I'm still half asleep and I get a pump disconnect alarm that can only be fixed by exiting AAPS and opening it up again. Its tough to be able to focus when you're half asleep, in the dark, trying to press the smallest of buttons on the menu to get your pump functioning again. @jamespaulley I think it is necessary for security reasons to avoid any single click without confirmation (I do not count the number of unwanted calls and even SMS sent by my pocket!)\r\n=> unwanted several short presses everywhere on the screen are very frequent... The idea of setting a temporary profile with a single press on +10 and tempo is definitively too dangerous ...\r\n=> I never had an unwanted \"Long Press\"\r\n\r\nI understand that it can be difficult for shaky hand to long press on small zone on the top of the screen, but may be a good compromise could be:\r\n- to keep the long press but to double the heigth of the zone to make it easier\r\n- to replace the 2 menus (profile and targets) by temporary buttons with single press action (as you proposed) but only shown after the long press on upper zone... (according to zone you pressed you only show target buttons or profiles buttons)\r\n\r\n@mistermintsgh For the three dot button, if it's only to have an easy way to restart AAPS, there are sev @Philoul it's not just used to restart AAPS though, it's used to access any of these options\r\n![Screenshot_20201112-212110_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/42671801/98997839-191cb580-252d-11eb-8b11-5366c6704887.jpg)\r\n\r\nMy point being that the button is tiny, and it's far too close to the notification bar to be able to bit with any kind of precision.\r\n\r\nAs I said above, I particularly struggle if I'm half asleep, but I also struggle sometimes in the middle of the day when I'm fully awake!\r\n\r\nIt just needs to be bigger, or in a better position There are larger buttons for temp target and profile switch in the actions tab ... No need to put them on the Home tab. Afaik all preferences can be reached via the config builder.\r\nAnd: If you enter the number directly in the dialogs, and not via the small +/- keys, the number keyboard will open.  This one has quite large numbers ... Of course this is not the one click solution you have in mind - but beside that I don't see the problem.\r\nAnd: On small devices isn't enough place to put additional buttons on the home screen without loosing the main graph. Okay great feedback guys thank you. A few things are being discussed now. I'll summarise everything below. Please also see the attached PDF for mockups and explanations of everything.\r\n\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1LD6uBF8oItpcF1L3NqemBBV_qnc9hl1N/view?usp=sharing\r\n\r\n### Spacing issues at top of Overview Screen\r\n- The spacing is too tight at the top of the Overview screen. It’s hard to use. As mentioned by @mistermintsgh.\r\n- There needs to be more space around the “...” menu.\r\n- The tabs area needs more spacing top and bottom.\r\n\r\n### Concern regarding accidental single-clicks triggering dangerous action\r\nAs mentioned by @Philoul.\r\n\r\n- We can forget the idea of having buttons that immediately trigger a profile change, I agree.\r\n- I think immediate buttons for Temp Targets might still be useful, but I'm happy to drop that for now.\r\n### Long press throughout the UX\r\n- I think long-press is bad UI/UX and we should have the option of not using it. People who want it can keep it, but I  Thank's @jamespaulley for this detailled synthesis\r\n- For Loop button, if we replace long press by a short one, I think it's necessary to add a confirmation popup because the area that can launch an action is too important (click a second time somewhere in half the screen is enough to disconnect, suspend or disable loop...)\r\n=> All buttons with single press action are followed by a confirmation popup with a small zone (Ok / Cancel)\r\n=> So if we modify this, we should replace a long press and a short press by 3 short presses (like it is done today for bottom buttons)\r\n- For profile switch I think it's a very good idea and it is easy to modify (it's always possible to select field and manually enter another value)\r\n- For Target popup, today the \"menu\" prefilled the values AND select the reason of the TT (with \"Manual\" reason as default), so if we replace selection menu, we have to add an additional information into the popup to show selected reason of the TT (I think it's a good idea too Suggestion on the profile switch:\r\n\r\n- Make it customisable\r\n\r\nIn the same way I can edit the quick bolus settings (I've edit the small bolus to be 0.25U, the medium bolus to be 1U, and the large bolus to be 2U) it would be could to be able to edit the +/- percentage too. Some might want 5%, some 10% some 20%. Let us choose, through the settings, which quick profile switch we want. ### **Loop Button**\r\nI agree that short-presses with a confirmation dialogue would be preferable over the current long-press behaviour, as described by @Philoul. My personal opinion is that 3 short presses is safer than a long click followed by a single click, but I appreciate that others might feel differently. Some users might like the long-press behaviour, so ideally there would be a settings preference for this.\r\n\r\n### Profile Switch\r\nExactly, @Philoul. I also like @mistermintsgh's suggestion for customisation of the percentage intervals for the \"+/–\" buttons on the profile switch screen.\r\n\r\n### **Temp Target Popup**\r\nExactly as described by @Philoul. Alternatively, we could leave the drop-down in place and provide the buttons as well, as seen below.\r\nhttps://i.imgur.com/Txph56A.png\r\n\r\n### **Resolution and display density**\r\n@Philoul points out that if we add too many settings to configure the interface, it'll get too complicated. That's fair enough. I think having a low-density sk I would prefer all.those changes to be optional. I like the system as it is.\n\nOn Tue, 17 Nov 2020, 12:10 jamespaulley, <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> *Loop Button*\n>\n> I agree that short-presses with a confirmation dialogue would be\n> preferable over the current long-press behaviour, as described by @Philoul\n> <https://github.com/Philoul>. My personal opinion is that 3 short presses\n> is safer than a long click followed by a single click, but I appreciate\n> that others might feel differently. Some users might like the long-press\n> behaviour, so ideally there would be a settings preference for this.\n> Profile Switch\n>\n> Exactly, @Philoul <https://github.com/Philoul>. I also like @mistermintsgh\n> <https://github.com/mistermintsgh>'s suggestion for customisation of the\n> percentage intervals for the \"+/–\" buttons on the profile switch screen.\n> *Temp Target Popup*\n>\n> Exactly as described by @Philoul <https://github.com/Philoul>.\n> Alternatively, we could leave the drop-down in plac personally i wouldnt need those buttons either. im fine with overview long presses or actions tab for that. actions tab does exactly that alrdy. just add it as tab and swipe right once u have ur buttons for profile change and temp target.\r\nbesides they, sry to say it that way, look like pure eye cancer. (means they are really ugly)\r\nadding those button only makes the problem worse."}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-75", "type": "thread", "title": "AAPS+Nightscout for selfhosting (SSL)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/75", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 75, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-11-20T10:57:08Z", "closed_at": "2020-11-22T11:27:37Z", "comment_count": 38, "comments": [{"user": "TwistaTim", "created_at": "2020-11-21T12:01:32Z", "body": "Have you tried Lets encrypt. Open a basic webserver for auth then copy the key over to your private NS front end proxy or NS server directly."}, {"user": "alfureu", "created_at": "2020-11-21T12:06:21Z", "body": "Hi @Tornado-Tim, thanks for the follow-up. I am using NS from docker, and I allow access to my docker containers through Caddy with my domain. Caddy provides https by default with Let's Encrypt. My issue is that even if I have https+domain+NS, whoever knows the address (whichever robot scans the web), the NS page is accessible to the world. \r\n\r\nNow, Caddy provides a basic auth solution: https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/basicauth. Do you refer to this option? Do you think that the API secret can go through this authentication regardless?"}, {"user": "TwistaTim", "created_at": "2020-11-21T12:12:28Z", "body": "In that case, you can use a certbot for wildcard cert and DNS auth which will allow you to get your certs for NS. Since its wildcard, your NS will not need to be exposed."}, {"user": "alfureu", "created_at": "2020-11-21T14:43:50Z", "body": "Yeah, this might work. Unfortunately I have a domain with GoDaddy, and the DNS auth module is not ready yet (no experience with the Go language, so I cannot write one myself). I was wondering, will AndroidAPS accept self-signed certificates? Or it must be from signed by entities like LE?"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2020-11-21T19:48:07Z", "body": "i'm not familiar with caddy but nginx has `allow` and `deny` directives for access filtering"}, {"user": "rICTx-T1D", "created_at": "2020-11-21T21:43:27Z", "body": "When you like use a selfhosted webservice NS with private selfsigned certificate, you must import the public key in android trust store. See android setting in security selection."}, {"user": "alfureu", "created_at": "2020-11-21T21:48:55Z", "body": "Yeah, these are all way too complex solutions compared to the single and simple one: there should be a login page for NS, after entering the credentials it should allow the user to the next page. Contacting the API with the API_SECRET is fine, I am not sure how it works in the background, and whether it should happen on another port once opened to the Internet. \r\n\r\nBy this simple solution one can then expose the NS server with a reverse proxy solution - with https."}, {"user": "swissalpine", "created_at": "2020-11-22T10:38:18Z", "body": "I have a similar problem. AAPS can receive and send encrypted data to my selfhosted nightscout-docker, but AAPS cannot retain the connection. Instead of the \"ping\" I get an XHR poll error ... I have a Let's encrypt certificate for this subdomain and use a reverse proxy."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2020-11-22T11:06:24Z", "body": "![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/99902026-1bb0a500-2cbb-11eb-95a2-95aba4e909fb.png)\r\nthis is my nginx setting"}, {"user": "alfureu", "created_at": "2020-11-22T11:27:37Z", "body": "OK, I made it working with the latest NS version (I used niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7), there one needs to authenticate even for viewing the web frontend. With this I was able to open the site to the Internet.\r\n\r\nFYI, I use Caddy for securing the web with https by default (I have a domain), if this helps, I am pasting the `Caddyfile` config, which is super simple:\r\n\r\n```\r\nns.{$MY_DOMAIN} {\r\n   reverse_proxy 192.168.0.40:1337\r\n}\r\n```\r\n"}], "text": "AAPS+Nightscout for selfhosting (SSL)  I am new to the whole Nightscout+AndroidAPS ecosystem. However, I would love to try it out properly. The thing is that I have a private server, into which all my devices all connected via VPN. \r\n\r\nOn this server I would love to use Nightscout. I cloned it and I was successful in setting it up via docker. I am able to access the local and not publicly available website of Nightscout. I am really reluctant to make my Nightscout page publicly available, as I may willingly disclose my personal medical data (unwillingly I might violate also GDPR as a data-handler of my own private medical data), while also providing another vector of attack into my systems.\r\n\r\nOn the other end, AndroidAPS requires SSL connection to Nightscout, many options are simply not working without SSL. Currently AndroidAPS does not have the option to work neither with self-signed certificates, nor with disabling this requirement, as my VPN connection handles the security. I tried `engineering_mode` but I still get the error `NS URL not encrypted` (as discussed [here](https://gitter.im/MilosKozak/AndroidAPS?at=5e98840ed65bcf75b5c62918)). \r\n\r\nWould it be please possible to allow unencrypted connection from AndroidAPS to NS with all the options for those of us who are self-hosting? Unfortunately Nightscout does not provide full authentication to the main screen, which I am feeling uneasy about to share publicly. \r\n\r\n**TLDR**: Provide either full authentication to Nightscout or allow unencrypted connection from AndroidAPS to Nightscout without SSL for self-hosters.  Have you tried Lets encrypt. Open a basic webserver for auth then copy the key over to your private NS front end proxy or NS server directly. Hi @Tornado-Tim, thanks for the follow-up. I am using NS from docker, and I allow access to my docker containers through Caddy with my domain. Caddy provides https by default with Let's Encrypt. My issue is that even if I have https+domain+NS, whoever knows the address (whichever robot scans the web), the NS page is accessible to the world. \r\n\r\nNow, Caddy provides a basic auth solution: https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/basicauth. Do you refer to this option? Do you think that the API secret can go through this authentication regardless? In that case, you can use a certbot for wildcard cert and DNS auth which will allow you to get your certs for NS. Since its wildcard, your NS will not need to be exposed. Yeah, this might work. Unfortunately I have a domain with GoDaddy, and the DNS auth module is not ready yet (no experience with the Go language, so I cannot write one myself). I was wondering, will AndroidAPS accept self-signed certificates? Or it must be from signed by entities like LE? i'm not familiar with caddy but nginx has `allow` and `deny` directives for access filtering When you like use a selfhosted webservice NS with private selfsigned certificate, you must import the public key in android trust store. See android setting in security selection. Yeah, these are all way too complex solutions compared to the single and simple one: there should be a login page for NS, after entering the credentials it should allow the user to the next page. Contacting the API with the API_SECRET is fine, I am not sure how it works in the background, and whether it should happen on another port once opened to the Internet. \r\n\r\nBy this simple solution one can then expose the NS server with a reverse proxy solution - with https. I have a similar problem. AAPS can receive and send encrypted data to my selfhosted nightscout-docker, but AAPS cannot retain the connection. Instead of the \"ping\" I get an XHR poll error ... I have a Let's encrypt certificate for this subdomain and use a reverse proxy. ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11146458/99902026-1bb0a500-2cbb-11eb-95a2-95aba4e909fb.png)\r\nthis is my nginx setting OK, I made it working with the latest NS version (I used niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7), there one needs to authenticate even for viewing the web frontend. With this I was able to open the site to the Internet.\r\n\r\nFYI, I use Caddy for securing the web with https by default (I have a domain), if this helps, I am pasting the `Caddyfile` config, which is super simple:\r\n\r\n```\r\nns.{$MY_DOMAIN} {\r\n   reverse_proxy 192.168.0.40:1337\r\n}\r\n```\r\n"}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-807", "type": "thread", "title": "[AAPS3.0_beta2] NSClient - io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error - Seems to also have broken Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/807", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 807, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-10-30T02:24:42Z", "closed_at": "2021-11-04T16:09:02Z", "comment_count": 29, "comments": [{"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T02:26:42Z", "body": "Phew. I uninstalled NSClient, and reloaded the Nightscout Heroku Dynos and Nightscout came back.\r\n"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T02:42:21Z", "body": "Reinstalled NSClient and completed Wizard without NS creds. Then manually entered, and this time it started syncing status/BG. But eventually crashed the NS site again. Perhaps it's a internal server error at NS because it can't keep up with the sync?"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T03:30:37Z", "body": "Finally seems to be syncing. I turned off my two OpenAPS rigs and the NS API was able to keep up.\r\n\r\nI see data in the history viewer. But not in the main graph. I'll see if there is more syncing. But I also can't select a Profile per https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/808"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T08:07:12Z", "body": "I gave up. No plot on main graph. I went back to the old 2.X version and the plot immediately appeared."}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2021-10-30T11:46:09Z", "body": "this is not enough info to be able help you"}, {"user": "MilosKozak", "created_at": "2021-10-30T14:02:07Z", "body": "where do you host NS?"}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T18:27:19Z", "body": "Heroku / Atlas Mongo - Free. THis is probably the most common configuration so would need to be supported. I get this error with all my other clients disabled, so the load is 100% NSClient on the NS API. Might need some exponential pullback or manual rate limiting."}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-10-30T19:26:46Z", "body": "@MilosKozak would you consider enabling local BG collection from xDrip? It's something I have wanted anyway to keep the watch face and NSclient plot from NS lag."}, {"user": "savek-cc", "created_at": "2021-11-01T10:13:47Z", "body": "@old-square-eyes did the event happen when adjusting the phone time for daylight savings time? (I saw the same errors but thought it might be due to altering time and timezone in anticipation for the time rewinding 1h (combo pump)."}, {"user": "old-square-eyes", "created_at": "2021-11-01T19:27:18Z", "body": "@savek-cc, I wasn't adjusting TZ, no. It's almost certainly a Heroku instance /dyno size thing. The API gets exhausted. I can only complete the sync by turning off all other clients and constantly restarting dynos and NSclient."}], "text": "[AAPS3.0_beta2] NSClient - io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error - Seems to also have broken Nightscout  Just installed beta 2 of NSClient 3.0. To get the build to work on my Mac M1, [I had to add a new version of \"Room\" to the gradle build file.](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/68922875/room-database-is-not-working-in-mac-book-pro-m1). Not sure if that's relevant.\r\n\r\nNSClient opens on my S20 fine (had to uninstall prev version for it to install). I completed the wizard. Lots of errors in the logs.\r\n\r\nNow my NS site has gone down, so this seems pretty nasty.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"353\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25760491/139517176-b9807360-5a93-4c5a-8a8e-23109a6ac0c4.png\">\r\n\r\n<img width=\"521\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25760491/139517180-8a9a01e3-3f99-4b96-901b-0222916b7d6e.png\">\r\n Phew. I uninstalled NSClient, and reloaded the Nightscout Heroku Dynos and Nightscout came back.\r\n Reinstalled NSClient and completed Wizard without NS creds. Then manually entered, and this time it started syncing status/BG. But eventually crashed the NS site again. Perhaps it's a internal server error at NS because it can't keep up with the sync? Finally seems to be syncing. I turned off my two OpenAPS rigs and the NS API was able to keep up.\r\n\r\nI see data in the history viewer. But not in the main graph. I'll see if there is more syncing. But I also can't select a Profile per https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/808 I gave up. No plot on main graph. I went back to the old 2.X version and the plot immediately appeared. this is not enough info to be able help you where do you host NS? Heroku / Atlas Mongo - Free. THis is probably the most common configuration so would need to be supported. I get this error with all my other clients disabled, so the load is 100% NSClient on the NS API. Might need some exponential pullback or manual rate limiting. @MilosKozak would you consider enabling local BG collection from xDrip? It's something I have wanted anyway to keep the watch face and NSclient plot from NS lag. @old-square-eyes did the event happen when adjusting the phone time for daylight savings time? (I saw the same errors but thought it might be due to altering time and timezone in anticipation for the time rewinding 1h (combo pump). @savek-cc, I wasn't adjusting TZ, no. It's almost certainly a Heroku instance /dyno size thing. The API gets exhausted. I can only complete the sync by turning off all other clients and constantly restarting dynos and NSclient."}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-827", "type": "thread", "title": "2.8.2.9_dev EROS and DASH / Basal settings sent twice to pump ", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/827", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 827, "labels": ["omnipod dash", "omnipod eros"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-11-01T09:02:25Z", "closed_at": "2021-11-16T16:56:56Z", "comment_count": 24, "comments": [{"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2021-11-01T09:24:10Z", "body": "One more exemple. In one (1) a normal switch to 120% and back (theoretically *10* minutes later...) and then going back to 120% once more as the high BGs were still there. The 2nd change was sent twice.\r\n\r\nI'm sure that at 0 AM, I was sleeping and didn't validate the message in AAPS. Thus, my first supposition above is wrong.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-101340_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139650311-b82c4468-8c9c-4a5f-8623-ae45476fc941.jpg)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-101324_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139650348-97b0e3d9-51ae-4e6f-9f2b-42591b333964.jpg)\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2021-11-01T14:11:01Z", "body": "I've just did a **_manual_** profile change to 130% for 20 min and it got sent twice to the pump. Maybe it is not the automations that it the origin of the bug. Still testing..."}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2021-11-02T14:11:46Z", "body": "I believe I have also seen this with both manual and automation profile changes, using Omnipod Dash with 3.0beta2. Don't have screenshots right now, will check when AAPS phone gets home from school. "}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2021-11-02T18:21:49Z", "body": "@MilosKozak I cornered the bug :) I can duplicate 3 times in a row. I'm the best ;) ;) ;)\r\n\r\nLong press the profile rectangle, set 120% for 20 min, validate. EROS will beep once and several seconds later, ANDROID will show a message \"Basal profile set in the pump\"\r\n\r\n![img1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139922262-92d5cf6e-ead2-4240-b9a3-399da6fccfeb.jpg)\r\n\r\nRight swipe the Android message and the basals will be sent again to the pump and the same message will appear again. \r\n\r\nIf you swipe the message \"Basal profile set in pump\" the 2nd time also, it will not send the profile a third time to the pump.\r\n\r\nI hope you have enough to corner the bug in the code too. You of course is better than best as I find the bug but you can fix it :) "}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2021-11-03T19:58:59Z", "body": "Ok, it seems that I was too optimistic. It is NOT related to swiping  the Android message. It sends basal profile twice even when I don't swipe. "}, {"user": "robertrub", "created_at": "2021-11-05T12:05:05Z", "body": "I just changed for on-body DASH and I see that DASH too sends basal settings twice.\r\n\r\n![20211105_130127](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/140507704-def1bdde-80f2-406a-bcc4-f4fdd5418fc4.jpg)\r\n"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2021-11-05T20:18:29Z", "body": "I managed to catch this as well with Dash.\r\nOn 3.0beta3.\r\n\r\n![received_4415873905175826](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140573222-b8c527f1-cc86-4b75-968f-e403c5bd0b05.jpeg)\r\n"}, {"user": "vanelsberg", "created_at": "2021-11-05T22:14:02Z", "body": "**Confirming for DASH:**\r\nResetting a Temp profile to 100% is executed 2 times, both generation a notification.\r\n\r\n**Repro:**\r\n**1)** Set a Temp Profile for 120% (this will do one single Suspend/Set Basal).\r\n**2)** Wait for the \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n**3)** Execute a testbeep to mark the current time in history.\r\n**4)** Cancel the Temp Profile by setting it back 100%.\r\n**5)** Wait for the \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n**6)** Execute a testbeep to mark the current time in history.\r\n**7)** Wait for the _second_ \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n\r\nI get the notification \"Profile set OK\" and then some time after a second \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\nCheck history view and find two identical Suspend/SetBasel entries.\r\n"}, {"user": "avereha", "created_at": "2021-11-08T20:31:23Z", "body": "I was not able to reproduce this with latest dev. Can you still reproduce it?"}, {"user": "kristinsmotz", "created_at": "2021-11-08T20:48:12Z", "body": "Reproduced just now, on beta5 installed today.\r\n![received_262128052599430](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140815807-38dd5986-9c0b-483e-9d63-df7376d0de3b.jpeg)\r\n![received_961535048106098](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140815824-b27c79ee-32b0-427c-9ff3-810c00765e31.jpeg)\r\n\r\nDid a normal profile switch from overview tab - long pressing profile name, then selecting a profile. "}], "text": "2.8.2.9_dev EROS and DASH / Basal settings sent twice to pump  omnipod dash omnipod eros This happened several times but can't duplicate yet. It is NOT systematic.\r\n\r\nIt happened around 9h53\r\n\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1635756882165.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7451968/AndroidAPS_LOG_1635756882165.log.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\nI have an automation that switches the profile to 120% when I have high BGs or high positive deltas. Sometimes the basal rates are sent twice to the EROS pod. \r\n\r\nMaybe (not tested yet) it has to do with me \"Okaying\" the basal change message in AAPS as soon as it appears.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-095342_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139647528-7d51c871-5598-4e9a-9043-fa41fe8ac256.jpg)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-095426_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139647579-39b7872f-a9ab-4247-a284-90c8f895cef8.jpg)\r\n\r\nI'll attach logs. Strangely I need to edit the message in order to be able to attach a file...\r\n One more exemple. In one (1) a normal switch to 120% and back (theoretically *10* minutes later...) and then going back to 120% once more as the high BGs were still there. The 2nd change was sent twice.\r\n\r\nI'm sure that at 0 AM, I was sleeping and didn't validate the message in AAPS. Thus, my first supposition above is wrong.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-101340_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139650311-b82c4468-8c9c-4a5f-8623-ae45476fc941.jpg)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20211101-101324_AndroidAPS](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139650348-97b0e3d9-51ae-4e6f-9f2b-42591b333964.jpg)\r\n\r\n I've just did a **_manual_** profile change to 130% for 20 min and it got sent twice to the pump. Maybe it is not the automations that it the origin of the bug. Still testing... I believe I have also seen this with both manual and automation profile changes, using Omnipod Dash with 3.0beta2. Don't have screenshots right now, will check when AAPS phone gets home from school.  @MilosKozak I cornered the bug :) I can duplicate 3 times in a row. I'm the best ;) ;) ;)\r\n\r\nLong press the profile rectangle, set 120% for 20 min, validate. EROS will beep once and several seconds later, ANDROID will show a message \"Basal profile set in the pump\"\r\n\r\n![img1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/139922262-92d5cf6e-ead2-4240-b9a3-399da6fccfeb.jpg)\r\n\r\nRight swipe the Android message and the basals will be sent again to the pump and the same message will appear again. \r\n\r\nIf you swipe the message \"Basal profile set in pump\" the 2nd time also, it will not send the profile a third time to the pump.\r\n\r\nI hope you have enough to corner the bug in the code too. You of course is better than best as I find the bug but you can fix it :)  Ok, it seems that I was too optimistic. It is NOT related to swiping  the Android message. It sends basal profile twice even when I don't swipe.  I just changed for on-body DASH and I see that DASH too sends basal settings twice.\r\n\r\n![20211105_130127](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/76626474/140507704-def1bdde-80f2-406a-bcc4-f4fdd5418fc4.jpg)\r\n I managed to catch this as well with Dash.\r\nOn 3.0beta3.\r\n\r\n![received_4415873905175826](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140573222-b8c527f1-cc86-4b75-968f-e403c5bd0b05.jpeg)\r\n **Confirming for DASH:**\r\nResetting a Temp profile to 100% is executed 2 times, both generation a notification.\r\n\r\n**Repro:**\r\n**1)** Set a Temp Profile for 120% (this will do one single Suspend/Set Basal).\r\n**2)** Wait for the \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n**3)** Execute a testbeep to mark the current time in history.\r\n**4)** Cancel the Temp Profile by setting it back 100%.\r\n**5)** Wait for the \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n**6)** Execute a testbeep to mark the current time in history.\r\n**7)** Wait for the _second_ \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\n\r\nI get the notification \"Profile set OK\" and then some time after a second \"Profile set OK\" notification.\r\nCheck history view and find two identical Suspend/SetBasel entries.\r\n I was not able to reproduce this with latest dev. Can you still reproduce it? Reproduced just now, on beta5 installed today.\r\n![received_262128052599430](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140815807-38dd5986-9c0b-483e-9d63-df7376d0de3b.jpeg)\r\n![received_961535048106098](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/71758682/140815824-b27c79ee-32b0-427c-9ff3-810c00765e31.jpeg)\r\n\r\nDid a normal profile switch from overview tab - long pressing profile name, then selecting a profile. "}, {"id": "thread:androidaps-935", "type": "thread", "title": "2.8.2.10-dev Omnipod Dash - lost BT connection on 2 pods", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/935", "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 935, "labels": ["omnipod dash"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-11-15T14:45:31Z", "closed_at": "2023-08-17T14:52:28Z", "comment_count": 23, "comments": [{"user": "avereha", "created_at": "2021-11-15T19:35:33Z", "body": "After reading the logs it looks like the pod services are somehow cached on the phone:\r\n```\r\n14:56:16.737 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-54] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():28]: Discovering services\r\n14:56:16.926 [Binder:31845_4] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onServicesDiscovered():50]: OnServicesDiscovered with status: 0\r\n....\r\nightscout.androidaps.plugins.pump.omnipod.dash.driver.comm.exceptions.ConnectException: Service not found: 1a7e-4024-e3ed-4464-8b7e-751e03d0dc5f\r\n....\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot sure how to reset the Bluetooth cache on the phone and if this is possible.\r\nMy suggestion: if you get this multiple times mark the phone model as 'yellow'\r\n"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-11-15T20:45:49Z", "body": "@tswire \r\nTo clear Bluetooth Cache (Pixel 5)\r\n- go to Settings\r\n- go to  Storage\r\n- choose Apps\r\n- over the 3 dots above choose \"Show System Apps\"\r\n- search for Bluetooth \r\n- choose Bluetooth and clear the cache."}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-11-15T20:53:10Z", "body": "> @tswire To clear Bluetooth Cache (Pixel 5)\r\n> \r\n> * go to Settings\r\n> * go to  Storage\r\n> * choose Apps\r\n> * over the 3 dots above choose \"Show System Apps\"\r\n> * search for Bluetooth\r\n> * choose Bluetooth and clear the cache.\r\n\r\nwell darn, this was what I was looking for when scrambling to have it come back to life.  I will make note and if happens again, I will try this.  If successful, might be a good solution for others no matter the phone.  As long as the Pod is not screaming, it SHOULD be available to communicate with.  Kinda like Eros pods with Rileylink (or similar) when sometimes you had to restart the Rileylink and exit (3 dots) the AAPS app.  Then it would reconnect fine.  I know we are dealing with BT here.....but maybe this will help restore the connection!\r\n"}, {"user": "Alamo04", "created_at": "2021-11-15T21:16:06Z", "body": "Didn't have this Issue on Pixel 5.\r\nI'm testing Dash, but only on my 3. one."}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-12-03T01:20:36Z", "body": "Adding additional log from today with what looks like same issue at 16:38\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-02_00-00-05_.3.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7646099/AndroidAPS._2021-12-02_00-00-05_.3.zip)\r\n"}, {"user": "Lastof", "created_at": "2021-12-03T11:11:57Z", "body": "Looking at the logs from my Pixel 6 Pro which hasn't lost any pods I do have two instances of similar logs, one from the 28th with\r\n\r\n> 00:19:26.484 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():28]: Discovering services\r\n> < three sameTimeZone messsages >\r\n> 00:19:26.486 [Binder:17244_2] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onServicesDiscovered():50]: OnServicesDiscovered with status: 0\r\n> < another sameTimeZone messsage >\r\n> 00:19:26.486 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():44]: Services discovered\r\n> 00:19:26.487 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [Connection.disconnect():119]: Disconnecting closeGatt=false\r\n> 00:19:26.487 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.resetConnection():213]: Reset connection\r\n> 00:19:26.488 [Binder:17244_2] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onConnectionStateChange():38]: OnConnectionStateChange with status/state: 0/0\r\n\r\nand one from last night\r\n\r\n> 02:12:4"}, {"user": "avereha", "created_at": "2021-12-07T07:33:44Z", "body": "Added more logging in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1043, please share the logs when this happens again."}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-12-17T14:23:00Z", "body": "Adding another log based on 3rd random \"disconnect\"  See log, seems to have started at 15:58:06 and I do see a lot more logging of COMM issues. \r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-16_00-00-05_.3.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7735704/AndroidAPS._2021-12-16_00-00-05_.3.zip)\r\n "}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-12-17T23:33:52Z", "body": "adding another log where at 18:22:50 it timed out (greater than 120 seconds) on a command....never had that where it would reconnect again (and did so by my refreshing status on Dash screen in AAPS\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1639783444586.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7738282/AndroidAPS_LOG_1639783444586.log.zip)\r\n."}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-12-20T14:06:35Z", "body": "Another random disconnect on Pixel Pro 6.  Log attached, started at 22:42:37.  Was sleeping and woke up to 60 min alarm for pump unreachable....same symptoms...not reconnect possible.  This pod was from new box (new order from Omnipod) but seems to have same firmware/bluetooth as previous pod\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-19_00-00-12_.txt](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7745813/AndroidAPS._2021-12-19_00-00-12_.txt)\r\ns"}], "text": "2.8.2.10-dev Omnipod Dash - lost BT connection on 2 pods omnipod dash Reporting bugs\r\n--------------\r\n- At or around 1pm EST, AAPS lost connection to Dash Pod.  It could read what was previously stored in the Pod (maybe on last connect) but could not communicate with the Pod no matter what I did.  I tried force closing AAPS, exit (3 dots), switch Pump to Virtual and back to Dash, turn BT off then on.  Restart phone.  Nothing worked, was forced to deactivate Pod (manually)\r\n- Build version: 54b8d0613-2021.11.12-18:44 of 2.8.2.10-dev  \r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1636919800184.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7539391/AndroidAPS_LOG_1636919800184.log.zip)\r\n\r\nThis is the second of around 6 Pods that this happened to.  Running Pixel Pro 6 on Android 12\r\n After reading the logs it looks like the pod services are somehow cached on the phone:\r\n```\r\n14:56:16.737 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-54] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():28]: Discovering services\r\n14:56:16.926 [Binder:31845_4] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onServicesDiscovered():50]: OnServicesDiscovered with status: 0\r\n....\r\nightscout.androidaps.plugins.pump.omnipod.dash.driver.comm.exceptions.ConnectException: Service not found: 1a7e-4024-e3ed-4464-8b7e-751e03d0dc5f\r\n....\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot sure how to reset the Bluetooth cache on the phone and if this is possible.\r\nMy suggestion: if you get this multiple times mark the phone model as 'yellow'\r\n @tswire \r\nTo clear Bluetooth Cache (Pixel 5)\r\n- go to Settings\r\n- go to  Storage\r\n- choose Apps\r\n- over the 3 dots above choose \"Show System Apps\"\r\n- search for Bluetooth \r\n- choose Bluetooth and clear the cache. > @tswire To clear Bluetooth Cache (Pixel 5)\r\n> \r\n> * go to Settings\r\n> * go to  Storage\r\n> * choose Apps\r\n> * over the 3 dots above choose \"Show System Apps\"\r\n> * search for Bluetooth\r\n> * choose Bluetooth and clear the cache.\r\n\r\nwell darn, this was what I was looking for when scrambling to have it come back to life.  I will make note and if happens again, I will try this.  If successful, might be a good solution for others no matter the phone.  As long as the Pod is not screaming, it SHOULD be available to communicate with.  Kinda like Eros pods with Rileylink (or similar) when sometimes you had to restart the Rileylink and exit (3 dots) the AAPS app.  Then it would reconnect fine.  I know we are dealing with BT here.....but maybe this will help restore the connection!\r\n Didn't have this Issue on Pixel 5.\r\nI'm testing Dash, but only on my 3. one. Adding additional log from today with what looks like same issue at 16:38\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-02_00-00-05_.3.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7646099/AndroidAPS._2021-12-02_00-00-05_.3.zip)\r\n Looking at the logs from my Pixel 6 Pro which hasn't lost any pods I do have two instances of similar logs, one from the 28th with\r\n\r\n> 00:19:26.484 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():28]: Discovering services\r\n> < three sameTimeZone messsages >\r\n> 00:19:26.486 [Binder:17244_2] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onServicesDiscovered():50]: OnServicesDiscovered with status: 0\r\n> < another sameTimeZone messsage >\r\n> 00:19:26.486 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [ServiceDiscoverer.discoverServices():44]: Services discovered\r\n> 00:19:26.487 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [Connection.disconnect():119]: Disconnecting closeGatt=false\r\n> 00:19:26.487 [RxCachedThreadScheduler-66] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.resetConnection():213]: Reset connection\r\n> 00:19:26.488 [Binder:17244_2] D/PUMPBTCOMM: [BleCommCallbacks.onConnectionStateChange():38]: OnConnectionStateChange with status/state: 0/0\r\n\r\nand one from last night\r\n\r\n> 02:12:4 Added more logging in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1043, please share the logs when this happens again. Adding another log based on 3rd random \"disconnect\"  See log, seems to have started at 15:58:06 and I do see a lot more logging of COMM issues. \r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-16_00-00-05_.3.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7735704/AndroidAPS._2021-12-16_00-00-05_.3.zip)\r\n  adding another log where at 18:22:50 it timed out (greater than 120 seconds) on a command....never had that where it would reconnect again (and did so by my refreshing status on Dash screen in AAPS\r\n[AndroidAPS_LOG_1639783444586.log.zip](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7738282/AndroidAPS_LOG_1639783444586.log.zip)\r\n. Another random disconnect on Pixel Pro 6.  Log attached, started at 22:42:37.  Was sleeping and woke up to 60 min alarm for pump unreachable....same symptoms...not reconnect possible.  This pod was from new box (new order from Omnipod) but seems to have same firmware/bluetooth as previous pod\r\n[AndroidAPS._2021-12-19_00-00-12_.txt](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/files/7745813/AndroidAPS._2021-12-19_00-00-12_.txt)\r\ns"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1008", "type": "thread", "title": "Can't calibrate new g6 + new transmitter: \"invalid impossible slope\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1008", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1008, "labels": ["bug", "device-dexcom", "calibration"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-09-10T23:01:34Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-26T23:13:03Z", "comment_count": 46, "comments": [{"user": "lee-b", "created_at": "2019-09-10T23:12:25Z", "body": "Just tried the latest nightly.  Same issue."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-09-11T08:49:44Z", "body": "What firmware version does your new G6 transmitter report in System Status?"}, {"user": "corn49", "created_at": "2019-09-12T21:37:49Z", "body": "Hey jamorham, \n\nHaving same issue. If I am correct that this is the firmware version, it is 14a03a7-2019.05.18. In case it helps, the code is 1905181006 and downgradeable to: 1603091400.\n\nSame issue as OP. For note, I purchased this transmitter at Costco and the body appears a bit different than the others I have gotten in past. Is G6, for clarity. The transmitter SN is 8GDNQB. \n\n"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-09-12T22:03:30Z", "body": "Guys: for 8Gxxx transmitters you need to use at least the current Alpha version as the newer firmware is somewhat different. I would say use the Nightly version to be sure you have the most up to date support for it.\r\n\r\nYou also need to use ob1 collector in native mode so there should be no calibration involved."}, {"user": "corn49", "created_at": "2019-09-12T22:28:27Z", "body": "Hey jamorham,\n\nThanks for the fast response. I would talk endlessly about the difference this app makes it my life, save for fear of it seeming trite in this medium. \n\nI am running nightly build from 9.10.19 and am using OB1 in native mode. As for calibration, I am showing a straight line 98 in the app, but multiple finger pricks are 78, 76 and 81, respectively."}, {"user": "lee-b", "created_at": "2019-09-12T22:32:26Z", "body": "@jamorham my firmware version is 2.18.2.88.  SN 8GFR1G, Calibration code 5937.\r\n\r\nStill seeing this with 0e3b27181-2019.09.10, 3 which is the lately nightly available on github (from 2 days ago).   Using ob1.  Enabling/disabling the fallback doesn't seem to help."}, {"user": "lee-b", "created_at": "2019-09-15T10:28:36Z", "body": "A few additional observations:\r\n\r\n* Initial calibration still seems to actually work.  The problem is the result intepretation, and xdrip thinking that it hasn't worked.  So it stays in initial calibration state, and keeps prompting.\r\n\r\n* None of the following work, probably just due to the \"initial calibration required\" state:\r\n\r\n* Entering a normal calibration in xdrip\r\n* Choosing calibrate from a pre-existing BG sample point (point remains a square, rather than becoming a circle)\r\n* Entering a calibration from AAPS."}, {"user": "HeyImPuni", "created_at": "2019-09-21T21:17:29Z", "body": "Same issue here. Like @lee-b said, seems like that the calibrations are working fine but xDrip thinks that they got deleted - at least that's what the `Events Log` tells me."}, {"user": "lee-b", "created_at": "2019-09-28T13:17:42Z", "body": "I think xdrip is purposefully deleting them as invalid, because it misinterprets the results from the G6 transmitter, and thinks that the calibration was rejected as invalid by the G6 transmitter.\r\n\r\ni.e., the real problem seems to be that XDrip doesn't yet know how to handle the new G6 transmitter protocol's calibration method, or its calibration response code changes."}, {"user": "joshhiram", "created_at": "2019-10-02T07:31:29Z", "body": "Just changed my son's transmitter. It is serial number 81A***. Same issue. Tried alpha release and nightly release with no effect. Firmware version 1.6.5.25. Xdrip version 7d97b62-2019.09.30."}], "text": "Can't calibrate new g6 + new transmitter: \"invalid impossible slope\" bug device-dexcom calibration On the beta update channel.\r\n\r\nI changed my sensor and transmitter today, stopped & started sensor, changed the transmitter code, paired the bluetooth device, and eventually got readings.  However, calibration won't work.  The error is:\r\n\r\n\"Got invalid impossible slope calibration!\"\r\n\r\nHowever, the calibrations I've tried entering were within 0.1 mmol of the sensor value on the first attempt, and 1 mmol on the second attempt.\r\n\r\nThis is the first time I've changed transmitter with a g6.  Seems that the beta channel also updated, but I find this very hard to know for sure -- does xdrip+ even have a visible version number on updates?\r\n\r\nSeems like the slope calculation is wrong, or the validation of slopes is wrong on new transmitters, or old values are being incorrectly included in stopped / started sensors since the new beta. Just tried the latest nightly.  Same issue. What firmware version does your new G6 transmitter report in System Status? Hey jamorham, \n\nHaving same issue. If I am correct that this is the firmware version, it is 14a03a7-2019.05.18. In case it helps, the code is 1905181006 and downgradeable to: 1603091400.\n\nSame issue as OP. For note, I purchased this transmitter at Costco and the body appears a bit different than the others I have gotten in past. Is G6, for clarity. The transmitter SN is 8GDNQB. \n\n Guys: for 8Gxxx transmitters you need to use at least the current Alpha version as the newer firmware is somewhat different. I would say use the Nightly version to be sure you have the most up to date support for it.\r\n\r\nYou also need to use ob1 collector in native mode so there should be no calibration involved. Hey jamorham,\n\nThanks for the fast response. I would talk endlessly about the difference this app makes it my life, save for fear of it seeming trite in this medium. \n\nI am running nightly build from 9.10.19 and am using OB1 in native mode. As for calibration, I am showing a straight line 98 in the app, but multiple finger pricks are 78, 76 and 81, respectively. @jamorham my firmware version is 2.18.2.88.  SN 8GFR1G, Calibration code 5937.\r\n\r\nStill seeing this with 0e3b27181-2019.09.10, 3 which is the lately nightly available on github (from 2 days ago).   Using ob1.  Enabling/disabling the fallback doesn't seem to help. A few additional observations:\r\n\r\n* Initial calibration still seems to actually work.  The problem is the result intepretation, and xdrip thinking that it hasn't worked.  So it stays in initial calibration state, and keeps prompting.\r\n\r\n* None of the following work, probably just due to the \"initial calibration required\" state:\r\n\r\n* Entering a normal calibration in xdrip\r\n* Choosing calibrate from a pre-existing BG sample point (point remains a square, rather than becoming a circle)\r\n* Entering a calibration from AAPS. Same issue here. Like @lee-b said, seems like that the calibrations are working fine but xDrip thinks that they got deleted - at least that's what the `Events Log` tells me. I think xdrip is purposefully deleting them as invalid, because it misinterprets the results from the G6 transmitter, and thinks that the calibration was rejected as invalid by the G6 transmitter.\r\n\r\ni.e., the real problem seems to be that XDrip doesn't yet know how to handle the new G6 transmitter protocol's calibration method, or its calibration response code changes. Just changed my son's transmitter. It is serial number 81A***. Same issue. Tried alpha release and nightly release with no effect. Firmware version 1.6.5.25. Xdrip version 7d97b62-2019.09.30."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1009", "type": "thread", "title": "Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1009", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1009, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-09-11T00:46:41Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-18T18:44:40Z", "comment_count": 47, "comments": [{"user": "Webifi", "created_at": "2019-09-11T15:00:31Z", "body": "Not exactly sure what fixed it, but it's working now on my Pixel 3a.\r\n\r\nThings I did:\r\n1. Disabled collection in xdrip.\r\n2. Installed Dexcom G5 Mobile app (modified version that allows use on unsupported devices), restarted phone, and wasn't able to get the transmitter working with the dexcom app either.\r\n3. Changed the device name of my phone's Bluetooth to something shorter, without spaces, apostrophes, etc.\r\n4. Restarted phone again.  Dexcom G5 app started to be able to communicate with transmitter.\r\n5. Uninstalled Dexcom G5, re-enabled G5 collection in xdrip. xdrip was now able to communicate with the transmitter.\r\n"}, {"user": "IsaacRoitman", "created_at": "2019-09-14T17:08:33Z", "body": "Having the exact same issue on my Pixel 3a XL ever since changing the sensor yesterday; no Bluetooth connection and seeing \"No valid timestamp stored for transmitter\".  \r\n\r\nStill not working after changing the phone / BT name."}, {"user": "Webifi", "created_at": "2019-09-14T20:05:54Z", "body": "I ran into the issue again after closing this issue, but fumbling for a bit was able to clear it up.  Still not exactly sure what fixed it as my \"fix\" was more analogous to a monkey pounding on the keyboard, doing most of this with my BG hovering around 40-60 mg/dL .  (Love xdrip, but its UI does require way too much cognitive load for me in that state.)\r\n\r\nProbably the most relevant things I did while flailing about:\r\n1. Set scan for G5 constantly.\r\n2. Removed any G5 pairings in the phone's Bluetooth settings.\r\n3. Restarted phone. (both restart, and power off, power on.)\r\n4. Opened up the phone's bluetooth pairing screen and Xdrip in split screen mode.  Keeping the phone awake, waited for the G5 to pop up on the phone's Bluetooth list (didn't pair it there), and hit \"RESTART COLLECTOR\" in Xdrip's \"Classic Status Page\", then switched to \"G5/G6 Status\" and waited for a successful connection.  (Probably did 3 & 4 a half dozen times before it started to work again.)\r\n\r\nBeen working for ab"}, {"user": "IsaacRoitman", "created_at": "2019-09-14T20:20:35Z", "body": "Glad it's working for you!\n\nIn an effort to troubleshoot I tried going back to the G6 receiver... It also couldn't find or pair with the transmitter.\n\nSo I'm assuming the transmitter is defective, just spoke to Dexcom support and they are sending a replacement.\n________________________________\nFrom: Webifi <notifications@github.com>\nSent: Saturday, September 14, 2019 4:06:01 PM\nTo: NightscoutFoundation/xDrip <xDrip@noreply.github.com>\nCc: Isaac Roitman <isaac_roitman@hotmail.com>; Comment <comment@noreply.github.com>\nSubject: Re: [NightscoutFoundation/xDrip] Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5 (#1009)\n\n\nI ran into the issue again after closing this issue, but fumbling for a bit was able to clear it up. Still not exactly sure what fixed it as my \"fix\" was more analogous to a monkey pounding on the keyboard.\n\nThings I did, in random order while flailing about:\n\n  1.  Set scan for G5 constantly.\n  2.  Removed any G5 pairings in the phone's Bluetooth settings.\n  3.  Restarted phone. (both restart, "}, {"user": "nsghub", "created_at": "2019-09-18T08:51:30Z", "body": "Do you still having errors? I am also using a Pixel 3a, but did not upgrade to Android 10 yet."}, {"user": "Webifi", "created_at": "2019-09-18T16:13:57Z", "body": "Working so far.   Not sure if/when I'll run in to issues again, nor am I exactly sure what I did to fix it."}, {"user": "nsghub", "created_at": "2019-09-28T14:52:52Z", "body": "I've also upgraded my Pixel 3a to Android 10. Missed the first reading but that was probably because the setup was still running afert the first reboot. Since then no issues, runs as fine as with Android 9."}, {"user": "IsaacRoitman", "created_at": "2019-09-29T02:16:03Z", "body": "Looks good now!  Was actually a defective Dexcom transmitter and not the Android 10 upgrade, just weird timing.\n________________________________\nFrom: nsghub <notifications@github.com>\nSent: Saturday, September 28, 2019 10:53:00 AM\nTo: NightscoutFoundation/xDrip <xDrip@noreply.github.com>\nCc: Isaac Roitman <isaac_roitman@hotmail.com>; Comment <comment@noreply.github.com>\nSubject: Re: [NightscoutFoundation/xDrip] Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5 (#1009)\n\n\nI've also upgraded my Pixel 3a to Android 10. Missed the first reading but that was probably because the setup was still running afert the first reboot. Since then no issues, runs as fine as with Android 9.\n\n—\nYou are receiving this because you commented.\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1009?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMUPPY6SOFL5G7BT2BARBJ3QL5VUZA5CNFSM4IVN6SYKYY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOD723KWY#issuecomment-536196443>, or mute t"}, {"user": "nshtg", "created_at": "2019-10-03T18:55:49Z", "body": "My transmitter was working perfectly until I upgraded to Android 10; Now the brainstate is caught in \"scanning\" forever and no values are received.\r\n\r\nMy Dexcom receiver worked for an hour and then it stopped receiving data too.\r\n\r\n@jamorham Maybe XDrip+ in combination with Android 10 is killing the transmitters?!\r\n\r\nEdit: Using Dexcom G6."}, {"user": "gregorybel", "created_at": "2019-10-03T19:16:02Z", "body": "it looks like android 10 has some strange/new behaviours with BLE bonding."}], "text": "Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5  Anyone have any luck with xDrip on a Google Pixel 3a running android 10 connecting to Dexcom G5?\r\n\r\nMy logs show continuous \"No valid timestamp stored for transmitter: 41U5BR\", and Classic Status Page says \"Bluetooth Device: None Set\".  Was working with a Moto G6 before. Not exactly sure what fixed it, but it's working now on my Pixel 3a.\r\n\r\nThings I did:\r\n1. Disabled collection in xdrip.\r\n2. Installed Dexcom G5 Mobile app (modified version that allows use on unsupported devices), restarted phone, and wasn't able to get the transmitter working with the dexcom app either.\r\n3. Changed the device name of my phone's Bluetooth to something shorter, without spaces, apostrophes, etc.\r\n4. Restarted phone again.  Dexcom G5 app started to be able to communicate with transmitter.\r\n5. Uninstalled Dexcom G5, re-enabled G5 collection in xdrip. xdrip was now able to communicate with the transmitter.\r\n Having the exact same issue on my Pixel 3a XL ever since changing the sensor yesterday; no Bluetooth connection and seeing \"No valid timestamp stored for transmitter\".  \r\n\r\nStill not working after changing the phone / BT name. I ran into the issue again after closing this issue, but fumbling for a bit was able to clear it up.  Still not exactly sure what fixed it as my \"fix\" was more analogous to a monkey pounding on the keyboard, doing most of this with my BG hovering around 40-60 mg/dL .  (Love xdrip, but its UI does require way too much cognitive load for me in that state.)\r\n\r\nProbably the most relevant things I did while flailing about:\r\n1. Set scan for G5 constantly.\r\n2. Removed any G5 pairings in the phone's Bluetooth settings.\r\n3. Restarted phone. (both restart, and power off, power on.)\r\n4. Opened up the phone's bluetooth pairing screen and Xdrip in split screen mode.  Keeping the phone awake, waited for the G5 to pop up on the phone's Bluetooth list (didn't pair it there), and hit \"RESTART COLLECTOR\" in Xdrip's \"Classic Status Page\", then switched to \"G5/G6 Status\" and waited for a successful connection.  (Probably did 3 & 4 a half dozen times before it started to work again.)\r\n\r\nBeen working for ab Glad it's working for you!\n\nIn an effort to troubleshoot I tried going back to the G6 receiver... It also couldn't find or pair with the transmitter.\n\nSo I'm assuming the transmitter is defective, just spoke to Dexcom support and they are sending a replacement.\n________________________________\nFrom: Webifi <notifications@github.com>\nSent: Saturday, September 14, 2019 4:06:01 PM\nTo: NightscoutFoundation/xDrip <xDrip@noreply.github.com>\nCc: Isaac Roitman <isaac_roitman@hotmail.com>; Comment <comment@noreply.github.com>\nSubject: Re: [NightscoutFoundation/xDrip] Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5 (#1009)\n\n\nI ran into the issue again after closing this issue, but fumbling for a bit was able to clear it up. Still not exactly sure what fixed it as my \"fix\" was more analogous to a monkey pounding on the keyboard.\n\nThings I did, in random order while flailing about:\n\n  1.  Set scan for G5 constantly.\n  2.  Removed any G5 pairings in the phone's Bluetooth settings.\n  3.  Restarted phone. (both restart,  Do you still having errors? I am also using a Pixel 3a, but did not upgrade to Android 10 yet. Working so far.   Not sure if/when I'll run in to issues again, nor am I exactly sure what I did to fix it. I've also upgraded my Pixel 3a to Android 10. Missed the first reading but that was probably because the setup was still running afert the first reboot. Since then no issues, runs as fine as with Android 9. Looks good now!  Was actually a defective Dexcom transmitter and not the Android 10 upgrade, just weird timing.\n________________________________\nFrom: nsghub <notifications@github.com>\nSent: Saturday, September 28, 2019 10:53:00 AM\nTo: NightscoutFoundation/xDrip <xDrip@noreply.github.com>\nCc: Isaac Roitman <isaac_roitman@hotmail.com>; Comment <comment@noreply.github.com>\nSubject: Re: [NightscoutFoundation/xDrip] Google Pixel 3a, Dexcom G5 (#1009)\n\n\nI've also upgraded my Pixel 3a to Android 10. Missed the first reading but that was probably because the setup was still running afert the first reboot. Since then no issues, runs as fine as with Android 9.\n\n—\nYou are receiving this because you commented.\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1009?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMUPPY6SOFL5G7BT2BARBJ3QL5VUZA5CNFSM4IVN6SYKYY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOD723KWY#issuecomment-536196443>, or mute t My transmitter was working perfectly until I upgraded to Android 10; Now the brainstate is caught in \"scanning\" forever and no values are received.\r\n\r\nMy Dexcom receiver worked for an hour and then it stopped receiving data too.\r\n\r\n@jamorham Maybe XDrip+ in combination with Android 10 is killing the transmitters?!\r\n\r\nEdit: Using Dexcom G6. it looks like android 10 has some strange/new behaviours with BLE bonding."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1058", "type": "thread", "title": "Broadcast data to Xdrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1058", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1058, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-10-16T06:46:53Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-01T00:55:09Z", "comment_count": 13, "comments": [{"user": "MasterPlexus", "created_at": "2019-10-16T09:13:55Z", "body": "This is dependent on several things. \r\n- Wich data you want to send (is it something new, or established known datafileds)?\r\n- from.where this want to be transfered\r\n\r\nGenerally you can produce intends to transfer data to a other app. Normally this must be implemented on sender app and receiver app. And booth apps should know that there is an allowed receiver... So without any further information it is not easy to give a suggestion, as also other ways of transferring of data is possible (web pull, Export Import and so.on)..."}, {"user": "WalkingMyRoad", "created_at": "2019-10-17T00:14:56Z", "body": "Sorry, I didn't elaborate completely.\r\nwe are CGM company named POCTech Co.,Ltd. ,Similar to Dexcome. We already have our own sensors and app named POCTech Care Mobile in googleplay store. we want send our glucose data to xDrip via Broadcast .\r\nWe have successfully passed the data to Androidaps. we also want to do this in xDrip.\r\nSorry for the slow response due to the time zone problem\r\n\r\n\r\n> This is dependent on several things.\r\n> \r\n> * Wich data you want to send (is it something new, or established known datafileds)?\r\n> * from.where this want to be transfered\r\n> \r\n> Generally you can produce intends to transfer data to a other app. Normally this must be implemented on sender app and receiver app. And booth apps should know that there is an allowed receiver... So without any further information it is not easy to give a suggestion, as also other ways of transferring of data is possible (web pull, Export Import and so.on)...\r\n\r\nSorry, I didn't elaborate completely.\r\nwe are CGM company n"}, {"user": "MasterPlexus", "created_at": "2019-10-17T19:41:29Z", "body": "Normally this should not be not a big problem. But it will be better to place it as an extra intend to xdrip imo, so it is clear selectable for the receiver.\r\n\r\nNormally the best is, if someone who has also one or more of your sensors, and some experiences in coding, to implement it in xdrip, or as Xdrip is open source, so it is open to you to give a pull request for implementing the processing of the data receiving from your app. \r\n\r\nUnder the line I see not that this will not be possible, but at the end @jamorham has to decide when a pull request comes up... "}, {"user": "WalkingMyRoad", "created_at": "2019-10-21T07:32:36Z", "body": "> Normally this should not be not a big problem. But it will be better to place it as an extra intend to xdrip imo, so it is clear selectable for the receiver.\r\n> \r\n> Normally the best is, if someone who has also one or more of your sensors, and some experiences in coding, to implement it in xdrip, or as Xdrip is open source, so it is open to you to give a pull request for implementing the processing of the data receiving from your app.\r\n> \r\n> Under the line I see not that this will not be possible, but at the end @jamorham has to decide when a pull request comes up...\r\n\r\nThank you for your reply ,  i think implementting it in xdrip is very diffcult , so i want our app as an open souece in Hardware Data Source.\r\n![Screenshot_20191021-152015_xDrip+](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67184706-e9c57300-f416-11e9-8182-4d4a365e82ce.jpg)\r\n\r\nwe do the same in AndroidAps.\r\n![Screenshot_20191021-151340](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67184832-301ad200-f417-1"}, {"user": "MasterPlexus", "created_at": "2019-10-21T08:38:46Z", "body": "@WalkingMyRoad That was what I mean. I did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in xDrip. \r\nI see the implementation in AndroidAPS, and it looks like not that complex, but I'm not that deep in handling Intends.  But as far as I could see, you should add in your app als that the intends will be send to xdrip in addition (at the moment in your screenshot I see `intend.setPackage(packageNameAndroidaps);`\r\nand I'm not sure that xDrip could receive it, as it is not placed for it."}, {"user": "tzachi-dar", "created_at": "2019-10-21T16:35:28Z", "body": "If you only want to send BG data as intents, you can do that, but the user will have to select things that are not related to your CGM. Are you sure it is a good thing to do?\r\n\r\nIf yes, I can point you on how to do it."}, {"user": "WalkingMyRoad", "created_at": "2019-10-22T01:30:11Z", "body": "> If you only want to send BG data as intents, you can do that, but the user will have to select things that are not related to your CGM. Are you sure it is a good thing to do?\r\n> \r\n> If yes, I can point you on how to do it.\r\n\r\nBecause we don't collect users' data to the cloud, but we need to give users a way to watch their children's blood sugar at home. Xdrip is the best choice. For now, we only want to send BG data as intents, but how to give xdrip compliant coding parameters , please give some Suggestions and examples."}, {"user": "WalkingMyRoad", "created_at": "2019-10-22T01:42:27Z", "body": "> @WalkingMyRoad That was what I mean. I did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in xDrip.\r\n> I see the implementation in AndroidAPS, and it looks like not that complex, but I'm not that deep in handling Intends. But as far as I could see, you should add in your app als that the intends will be send to xdrip in addition (at the moment in your screenshot I see `intend.setPackage(packageNameAndroidaps);`\r\n> and I'm not sure that xDrip could receive it, as it is not placed for it.\r\n\r\nWe designed a switch option to let users choose which application to transfer data to. every switch sets different package.\r\n![Screenshot_20191022-093730](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67254493-e92ceb00-f4af-11e9-92e3-94d4ef098ebf.png)\r\nOf course, we will add xdrip if the test passes.\r\n"}, {"user": "tzachi-dar", "created_at": "2019-10-22T20:33:01Z", "body": "Here is the way that the oop sends data back to xDrip:\nhttps://github.com/tzachi-dar/LibreOOPAlgorithm/blob/8ac65ad064f19a1b259ddf18b6382bc74b61e2f0/app/src/main/java/com/hg4/oopalgorithm/oopalgorithm/IntentsReceiver.java#L120\n\nYou can send it on the same way.\nFor this to work, your users will have to configure xDrip according to\nthe following instructions:\n\n1) Install xDrip\n2) Choose libre as the sensor type.\n3) Choose miaomiao\n4) Go to settings->hw data source and choose libre wifi\n5) Go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000\n6) Start a new sensor (answer not today).\n7) Go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set \"use\noop algorithm\"\n\nThis configuration is far from being intuitive, but users will see the BG\nand alerts will work and so on.\n\nOn Tue, 22 Oct 2019 at 04:42, minyc <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> @WalkingMyRoad <https://github.com/WalkingMyRoad> That was what I mean. I\n> did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in x"}, {"user": "emaragkos", "created_at": "2020-01-10T18:16:10Z", "body": "Hey there all!\r\n@WalkingMyRoad are you planning to implement the connection between POCTech and xDrip?\r\nAlso do you have any documentation about connecting POCTech with Nightscout and Androidaps\r\nThank you :)"}], "text": "Broadcast data to Xdrip  Dear developer,\r\ncan i send data to xDrip like AndroidAps ? if i can, How should i do?\r\nThank you very much for your recovery.\r\n\r\nmore\r\nIf you are interested in learning about us, please contact me at gitter.I tried to contact you, but I didn't get a response, Or please give me an email to contact you.\r\n\r\n This is dependent on several things. \r\n- Wich data you want to send (is it something new, or established known datafileds)?\r\n- from.where this want to be transfered\r\n\r\nGenerally you can produce intends to transfer data to a other app. Normally this must be implemented on sender app and receiver app. And booth apps should know that there is an allowed receiver... So without any further information it is not easy to give a suggestion, as also other ways of transferring of data is possible (web pull, Export Import and so.on)... Sorry, I didn't elaborate completely.\r\nwe are CGM company named POCTech Co.,Ltd. ,Similar to Dexcome. We already have our own sensors and app named POCTech Care Mobile in googleplay store. we want send our glucose data to xDrip via Broadcast .\r\nWe have successfully passed the data to Androidaps. we also want to do this in xDrip.\r\nSorry for the slow response due to the time zone problem\r\n\r\n\r\n> This is dependent on several things.\r\n> \r\n> * Wich data you want to send (is it something new, or established known datafileds)?\r\n> * from.where this want to be transfered\r\n> \r\n> Generally you can produce intends to transfer data to a other app. Normally this must be implemented on sender app and receiver app. And booth apps should know that there is an allowed receiver... So without any further information it is not easy to give a suggestion, as also other ways of transferring of data is possible (web pull, Export Import and so.on)...\r\n\r\nSorry, I didn't elaborate completely.\r\nwe are CGM company n Normally this should not be not a big problem. But it will be better to place it as an extra intend to xdrip imo, so it is clear selectable for the receiver.\r\n\r\nNormally the best is, if someone who has also one or more of your sensors, and some experiences in coding, to implement it in xdrip, or as Xdrip is open source, so it is open to you to give a pull request for implementing the processing of the data receiving from your app. \r\n\r\nUnder the line I see not that this will not be possible, but at the end @jamorham has to decide when a pull request comes up...  > Normally this should not be not a big problem. But it will be better to place it as an extra intend to xdrip imo, so it is clear selectable for the receiver.\r\n> \r\n> Normally the best is, if someone who has also one or more of your sensors, and some experiences in coding, to implement it in xdrip, or as Xdrip is open source, so it is open to you to give a pull request for implementing the processing of the data receiving from your app.\r\n> \r\n> Under the line I see not that this will not be possible, but at the end @jamorham has to decide when a pull request comes up...\r\n\r\nThank you for your reply ,  i think implementting it in xdrip is very diffcult , so i want our app as an open souece in Hardware Data Source.\r\n![Screenshot_20191021-152015_xDrip+](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67184706-e9c57300-f416-11e9-8182-4d4a365e82ce.jpg)\r\n\r\nwe do the same in AndroidAps.\r\n![Screenshot_20191021-151340](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67184832-301ad200-f417-1 @WalkingMyRoad That was what I mean. I did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in xDrip. \r\nI see the implementation in AndroidAPS, and it looks like not that complex, but I'm not that deep in handling Intends.  But as far as I could see, you should add in your app als that the intends will be send to xdrip in addition (at the moment in your screenshot I see `intend.setPackage(packageNameAndroidaps);`\r\nand I'm not sure that xDrip could receive it, as it is not placed for it. If you only want to send BG data as intents, you can do that, but the user will have to select things that are not related to your CGM. Are you sure it is a good thing to do?\r\n\r\nIf yes, I can point you on how to do it. > If you only want to send BG data as intents, you can do that, but the user will have to select things that are not related to your CGM. Are you sure it is a good thing to do?\r\n> \r\n> If yes, I can point you on how to do it.\r\n\r\nBecause we don't collect users' data to the cloud, but we need to give users a way to watch their children's blood sugar at home. Xdrip is the best choice. For now, we only want to send BG data as intents, but how to give xdrip compliant coding parameters , please give some Suggestions and examples. > @WalkingMyRoad That was what I mean. I did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in xDrip.\r\n> I see the implementation in AndroidAPS, and it looks like not that complex, but I'm not that deep in handling Intends. But as far as I could see, you should add in your app als that the intends will be send to xdrip in addition (at the moment in your screenshot I see `intend.setPackage(packageNameAndroidaps);`\r\n> and I'm not sure that xDrip could receive it, as it is not placed for it.\r\n\r\nWe designed a switch option to let users choose which application to transfer data to. every switch sets different package.\r\n![Screenshot_20191022-093730](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12733707/67254493-e92ceb00-f4af-11e9-92e3-94d4ef098ebf.png)\r\nOf course, we will add xdrip if the test passes.\r\n Here is the way that the oop sends data back to xDrip:\nhttps://github.com/tzachi-dar/LibreOOPAlgorithm/blob/8ac65ad064f19a1b259ddf18b6382bc74b61e2f0/app/src/main/java/com/hg4/oopalgorithm/oopalgorithm/IntentsReceiver.java#L120\n\nYou can send it on the same way.\nFor this to work, your users will have to configure xDrip according to\nthe following instructions:\n\n1) Install xDrip\n2) Choose libre as the sensor type.\n3) Choose miaomiao\n4) Go to settings->hw data source and choose libre wifi\n5) Go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000\n6) Start a new sensor (answer not today).\n7) Go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set \"use\noop algorithm\"\n\nThis configuration is far from being intuitive, but users will see the BG\nand alerts will work and so on.\n\nOn Tue, 22 Oct 2019 at 04:42, minyc <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> @WalkingMyRoad <https://github.com/WalkingMyRoad> That was what I mean. I\n> did not stated to implement the hole connection to be implemented in x Hey there all!\r\n@WalkingMyRoad are you planning to implement the connection between POCTech and xDrip?\r\nAlso do you have any documentation about connecting POCTech with Nightscout and Androidaps\r\nThank you :)"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1061", "type": "thread", "title": "Android 10 BLE + G6 - Stuck in \"scanning\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1061", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1061, "labels": ["bluetooth", "android10+"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-10-18T16:48:44Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-01T01:04:12Z", "comment_count": 208, "comments": [{"user": "17gubbar", "created_at": "2019-10-22T20:57:56Z", "body": "Same problem"}, {"user": "lkpod", "created_at": "2019-10-23T18:41:47Z", "body": "Same problem."}, {"user": "nshtg", "created_at": "2019-10-23T19:04:58Z", "body": "Does my fix (\"Forget device\" in System status screen of XDrip) work for you too? For me it's an 100% success rate so far!"}, {"user": "17gubbar", "created_at": "2019-10-23T19:48:01Z", "body": "It works, but i found a workaround for the problem now read #1067 :)"}, {"user": "17gubbar", "created_at": "2019-10-23T19:49:38Z", "body": "Also besure to turn of bt watchdog and untick the ob1 collector allowed to unbond."}, {"user": "ThoR294", "created_at": "2019-10-25T11:19:03Z", "body": "This did help, but mine keeps asking for calibrations right after I hit forget device.  im on a pixel 4 xl.\r\n\r\nok, i think it FINALLY worked.  it rejected my calibrations, then a few minutes later it says warming up\r\n"}, {"user": "borijess", "created_at": "2019-10-29T20:53:42Z", "body": "I have the same issue. OnePlus 7 pro on Android 10 beta 4. "}, {"user": "borijess", "created_at": "2019-10-29T21:12:26Z", "body": "> Also besure to turn of bt watchdog and untick the ob1 collector allowed to unbond.\r\n\r\nCan you post a pic of your settings here?\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20191029-160131__01](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18737358/67809544-e2c9e080-fa66-11e9-88c7-1221636252df.jpg)\r\n![Screenshot_20191029-160136](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18737358/67809546-e2c9e080-fa66-11e9-976d-7a3ac7de0d0c.jpg)\r\n"}, {"user": "yumtime", "created_at": "2019-11-01T19:17:13Z", "body": "Same issue with pixel 3 android 10. Getting this error:\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20191101-151301](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/37127272/68050002-abec0880-fcba-11e9-98ca-f6557a350b7b.png)\r\n"}, {"user": "edisiENt", "created_at": "2019-11-03T18:29:59Z", "body": "Same issues on OnePlus 7 Pro Android 10.0.1 with G6.  Reverted phone back to Android 9.5 & saw good operation.  OnePlus refreshed my BT firmware, returned to 10.0.1 and BT problems returned.  Other BT devices (audio & car) work fine.  XDrip to G6 is the only BT problem I'm seeing.  G6 drops occur even while BT audio device is operating.\r\n\r\nWhile phone is charging, link to G6 is solid & works all night.  Within minutes of unplugging from power, Xdrip looses connection to G6 sensor."}], "text": "Android 10 BLE + G6 - Stuck in \"scanning\" bluetooth android10+ I have a reproduceable problem with XDrip being stuck in Scanning.\r\n\r\n1) Reboot the device on Android 10\r\n2) Brain state is stuck in scanning\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n1) Forget device in G5/G6 Status screen\r\n2) Next cycle it sucessfully reconnects and works from that point on... Until I reboot again/or the transmitter fails to connect once because of range etc.\r\n\r\nOneplus 7 Pro on the official Android 10 Version. Newest XDrip Nightly from October 11. Same problem Same problem. Does my fix (\"Forget device\" in System status screen of XDrip) work for you too? For me it's an 100% success rate so far! It works, but i found a workaround for the problem now read #1067 :) Also besure to turn of bt watchdog and untick the ob1 collector allowed to unbond. This did help, but mine keeps asking for calibrations right after I hit forget device.  im on a pixel 4 xl.\r\n\r\nok, i think it FINALLY worked.  it rejected my calibrations, then a few minutes later it says warming up\r\n I have the same issue. OnePlus 7 pro on Android 10 beta 4.  > Also besure to turn of bt watchdog and untick the ob1 collector allowed to unbond.\r\n\r\nCan you post a pic of your settings here?\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20191029-160131__01](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18737358/67809544-e2c9e080-fa66-11e9-88c7-1221636252df.jpg)\r\n![Screenshot_20191029-160136](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18737358/67809546-e2c9e080-fa66-11e9-976d-7a3ac7de0d0c.jpg)\r\n Same issue with pixel 3 android 10. Getting this error:\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20191101-151301](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/37127272/68050002-abec0880-fcba-11e9-98ca-f6557a350b7b.png)\r\n Same issues on OnePlus 7 Pro Android 10.0.1 with G6.  Reverted phone back to Android 9.5 & saw good operation.  OnePlus refreshed my BT firmware, returned to 10.0.1 and BT problems returned.  Other BT devices (audio & car) work fine.  XDrip to G6 is the only BT problem I'm seeing.  G6 drops occur even while BT audio device is operating.\r\n\r\nWhile phone is charging, link to G6 is solid & works all night.  Within minutes of unplugging from power, Xdrip looses connection to G6 sensor."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1084", "type": "thread", "title": "Issues with New \"firefly\" G6 transmitter (serial# 8G... or 8H...)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1084", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1084, "labels": ["bug", "device-dexcom-reset"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-11-10T05:49:47Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-27T00:19:44Z", "comment_count": 59, "comments": [{"user": "zothen", "created_at": "2019-11-12T04:06:44Z", "body": "Same for me."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-11-12T09:59:25Z", "body": "Which xDrip+ version are you using? If not very recent please switch to Alpha update channel and try that."}, {"user": "xannasavin", "created_at": "2019-11-12T11:43:00Z", "body": "So I have just started today my 8G Transmitter with the latest Alpha version of xDrip+ and in the beginning, for about 3hrs it collected the date and then suddenly stopped. \r\nThe Dexcom Receiver still works, but xDrip does not connect since hours. restarted phone, bluetooth, collector and everything but nothing works.\r\nWith the 80 Transmitter used till today it worked quite well, so the problem has to be with the 8G one."}, {"user": "xannasavin", "created_at": "2019-11-12T11:49:58Z", "body": "ok, so after 3hrs - just after this comment - I tried a step I read somewhere else and now I have at least 1 new data. \r\nOn the system status screen I clicked on \"forget device\" and restarted the data collector. Not sure if that helped any or if it was just coincidence.\r\nI also got some backfill of data, which is nice, though it was pretty annyoing to not have any update for 3hrs.\r\nNot sure what more information you need for bug tracing?"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-11-12T13:25:22Z", "body": "@xannasavin which version of android are you using?"}, {"user": "zothen", "created_at": "2019-11-12T13:44:36Z", "body": "I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\nkeep a reliable connection.\n\nMy phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasavin> which version of android are\n> you using?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1084?email_source=notifications&email_token=AAIIFWTKKKOZDXVGYCCXF4LQTKVEXA5CNFSM4JLLAWS2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOED2HLLQ#issuecomment-552891822>,\n> or unsubscribe\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIIFWR2G72NUFDB6F5DO6LQTKVEXANCNFSM4JLLAWSQ>\n> .\n>\n"}, {"user": "zothen", "created_at": "2019-11-12T13:58:02Z", "body": "To elaborate, the main problem for me is if I have one connection problem\nfor any reason, it won't automatically reconnect.  Restarting the collector\nnever works.  I have to forget the device and restart the collector and\nonly after many tries will it reconnect.\n\nI've tried all of the G5/G6 debug options with no luck.  Have also tried\nsome of the Bluetooth debug options as well.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:44 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n\n> I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\n> keep a reliable connection.\n>\n> My phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n>\n> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n>\n>> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasavin> which version of android are\n>> you using?\n>>\n>> —\n>> You are receiving this because you commented.\n>> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n>> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1084?email_source=notifications&email_token=AAIIFWTKKKOZDXVG"}, {"user": "zothen", "created_at": "2019-11-12T13:59:57Z", "body": "\"only after many tries\"\n\nI meant only after I repeat my actions of forgetting the device and\nrestarting the collector will it final reconnect and work for some limited\ntime.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:57 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n\n> To elaborate, the main problem for me is if I have one connection problem\n> for any reason, it won't automatically reconnect.  Restarting the collector\n> never works.  I have to forget the device and restart the collector and\n> only after many tries will it reconnect.\n>\n> I've tried all of the G5/G6 debug options with no luck.  Have also tried\n> some of the Bluetooth debug options as well.\n>\n> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:44 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n>\n>> I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\n>> keep a reliable connection.\n>>\n>> My phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n>>\n>> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n>>\n>>> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasa"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-11-12T14:13:13Z", "body": "@zothen I think this is an android 10 issue unrelated to the type of transmitter"}, {"user": "cbadams7", "created_at": "2019-11-12T14:19:34Z", "body": "@jamorham I'm running 9, Android 8S Active updated software today"}], "text": "Issues with New \"firefly\" G6 transmitter (serial# 8G... or 8H...) bug device-dexcom-reset Recieved two new transmitters for my dexcom G6 with serial numbers beginning in 8G. Attempted multiple times to follow instructions listed here https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/EN/Configuration/xdrip.html but with no success. I will sometimes recieved a few minutes of reading but eventually xdrips+ will no longer report current values. Please help! Really need this to work for an upcoming triathlon! Same for me. Which xDrip+ version are you using? If not very recent please switch to Alpha update channel and try that. So I have just started today my 8G Transmitter with the latest Alpha version of xDrip+ and in the beginning, for about 3hrs it collected the date and then suddenly stopped. \r\nThe Dexcom Receiver still works, but xDrip does not connect since hours. restarted phone, bluetooth, collector and everything but nothing works.\r\nWith the 80 Transmitter used till today it worked quite well, so the problem has to be with the 8G one. ok, so after 3hrs - just after this comment - I tried a step I read somewhere else and now I have at least 1 new data. \r\nOn the system status screen I clicked on \"forget device\" and restarted the data collector. Not sure if that helped any or if it was just coincidence.\r\nI also got some backfill of data, which is nice, though it was pretty annyoing to not have any update for 3hrs.\r\nNot sure what more information you need for bug tracing? @xannasavin which version of android are you using? I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\nkeep a reliable connection.\n\nMy phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasavin> which version of android are\n> you using?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1084?email_source=notifications&email_token=AAIIFWTKKKOZDXVGYCCXF4LQTKVEXA5CNFSM4JLLAWS2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOED2HLLQ#issuecomment-552891822>,\n> or unsubscribe\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIIFWR2G72NUFDB6F5DO6LQTKVEXANCNFSM4JLLAWSQ>\n> .\n>\n To elaborate, the main problem for me is if I have one connection problem\nfor any reason, it won't automatically reconnect.  Restarting the collector\nnever works.  I have to forget the device and restart the collector and\nonly after many tries will it reconnect.\n\nI've tried all of the G5/G6 debug options with no luck.  Have also tried\nsome of the Bluetooth debug options as well.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:44 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n\n> I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\n> keep a reliable connection.\n>\n> My phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n>\n> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n>\n>> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasavin> which version of android are\n>> you using?\n>>\n>> —\n>> You are receiving this because you commented.\n>> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n>> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1084?email_source=notifications&email_token=AAIIFWTKKKOZDXVG \"only after many tries\"\n\nI meant only after I repeat my actions of forgetting the device and\nrestarting the collector will it final reconnect and work for some limited\ntime.\n\nOn Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:57 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n\n> To elaborate, the main problem for me is if I have one connection problem\n> for any reason, it won't automatically reconnect.  Restarting the collector\n> never works.  I have to forget the device and restart the collector and\n> only after many tries will it reconnect.\n>\n> I've tried all of the G5/G6 debug options with no luck.  Have also tried\n> some of the Bluetooth debug options as well.\n>\n> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:44 AM Rob Lee <robertdavidlee@gmail.com> wrote:\n>\n>> I'm a new xDrip user also with a brand new 8G G6 transmitter, and I can't\n>> keep a reliable connection.\n>>\n>> My phone is Pixel 4 XL with Android 10.\n>>\n>> On Tue, Nov 12, 2019, 7:25 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n>>\n>>> @xannasavin <https://github.com/xannasa @zothen I think this is an android 10 issue unrelated to the type of transmitter @jamorham I'm running 9, Android 8S Active updated software today"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1279", "type": "thread", "title": "Dexcom G6 / 8G tx: every 5mins \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" & \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1279", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1279, "labels": ["duplicate", "device-dexcom", "bluetooth"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-03-21T21:39:49Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-27T18:21:07Z", "comment_count": 48, "comments": [{"user": "m-goetz", "created_at": "2020-03-29T16:30:15Z", "body": "Same device (8G), firmware and settings and I get the same error messages. Very annoying noise in the logs, but it doesn't seem to break anything.\r\n"}, {"user": "doc77", "created_at": "2020-04-03T23:38:36Z", "body": "Same thing here. Trying to figure out what causes it, but so far no luck."}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-04T17:50:58Z", "body": "More strange behaviour: menu item \"Initial Calibration\" stays all the time even after calibrating with this function. Is this normal? Why is it still called \"initial\"? \r\n\r\nIn my case I can only calibrate with this function - the syringe always gives me \"Invalid Impossible Slope Calibration\" errors... I've seen many tipps mentioning for 8G only the syringe calibrabration function should be used. This does not work in my case or is the error message wrong and it still works? Would it be possible to correct these functions with a new xDrip+ release?"}, {"user": "doc77", "created_at": "2020-04-07T17:16:47Z", "body": "@emp-00  This is the exact behavior of my xDrip+ installation. \r\n\r\nAlso, I had to re-pair my watch (SSW3), and cannot get xDrip+ to load on the watch. I wonder if there is any relationship?"}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-07T18:43:02Z", "body": "@doc77 I don't have a watch, just xDrip+ on smartphone - maybe we have one or two \"wrong/bad\" settings en/disabled others don't have? we need somebody with a working setup to compare settings - I have posted my \"main\" settings above but maybe the issue is hidden in a different feature?"}, {"user": "doc77", "created_at": "2020-04-07T19:45:51Z", "body": "@emp-00   I have the same settings and Dexcom firmware. I have already tried turning off what was on, and turning on what was off. But, doing it one at a time. Didn't help. Currently, I'm using native, OB1, go on without calibrations, G6 Support, and OB1 initiate bonding and allow OB1 unbundling.\r\n\r\nI've also downgraded xDrip+ by a few versions, since re upgraded to the most current.\r\n\r\nI don't know what else to try."}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-07T21:00:54Z", "body": "Maybe it's our phone? I'm on Samsung A8. \r\nOr maybe everybody with 8G+ has these errors but nobody cares?"}, {"user": "doc77", "created_at": "2020-04-08T00:14:49Z", "body": "@emp-00  I'm on the Samsung Note 8. It might have something to do with the way Samsung BLE handles GATT.  I think that this is what the Samsung Workaround is supposed to take care of. I disabled it, but it still showed as active in System Status.\r\n\r\nBut this is way beyond my knowledge of Android."}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-08T18:56:42Z", "body": "So we both are on Samsungs! That's a lead. Here come my \"Bluetooth Settings\" (under Less Common Settings):\r\n\r\nAll settings OFF except for these five: Turn BT on, BT Watchdog, G5 BT Watchdog, Use Background Scans, Allow blucon unbonding.\r\n\r\nI remember I had changed one or two of these options when I started with G6 (80/81 tx's) half a year ago. Does anybody know the default settings in this menu? We could try reverting to defaults and see if this helps!\r\n"}, {"user": "doc77", "created_at": "2020-04-08T21:18:54Z", "body": "@emp-00  I already cycled all the Bluetooth settings on and off. Didn't hurt function, but made no difference in the log."}], "text": "Dexcom G6 / 8G tx: every 5mins \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" & \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\" duplicate device-dexcom bluetooth Since using 8G transmitters my error log shows always the same errors every 5 mins, see below. Error messages: \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" & \"Failed to write DisconnectTxMessage\" with \"GATT expection\" etc.\r\n\r\n- G6 Firmware 2.18.2.88 and running xDrip+ nightly 2020-03-11 [same with previous versions]\r\n- Using G5/G6 settings OB1, Native, Allow OB1 unbonding and Allow OB1 initiate bonding; all remaining options are OFF.\r\n\r\nFor the rest everyhing's working fine but these error messages are really annoying. Anyone else having these issues? How to turn it off?\r\n\r\n![Image1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/60714349/77237026-a25d3180-6bc4-11ea-9aef-6f1871665bed.jpg) Same device (8G), firmware and settings and I get the same error messages. Very annoying noise in the logs, but it doesn't seem to break anything.\r\n Same thing here. Trying to figure out what causes it, but so far no luck. More strange behaviour: menu item \"Initial Calibration\" stays all the time even after calibrating with this function. Is this normal? Why is it still called \"initial\"? \r\n\r\nIn my case I can only calibrate with this function - the syringe always gives me \"Invalid Impossible Slope Calibration\" errors... I've seen many tipps mentioning for 8G only the syringe calibrabration function should be used. This does not work in my case or is the error message wrong and it still works? Would it be possible to correct these functions with a new xDrip+ release? @emp-00  This is the exact behavior of my xDrip+ installation. \r\n\r\nAlso, I had to re-pair my watch (SSW3), and cannot get xDrip+ to load on the watch. I wonder if there is any relationship? @doc77 I don't have a watch, just xDrip+ on smartphone - maybe we have one or two \"wrong/bad\" settings en/disabled others don't have? we need somebody with a working setup to compare settings - I have posted my \"main\" settings above but maybe the issue is hidden in a different feature? @emp-00   I have the same settings and Dexcom firmware. I have already tried turning off what was on, and turning on what was off. But, doing it one at a time. Didn't help. Currently, I'm using native, OB1, go on without calibrations, G6 Support, and OB1 initiate bonding and allow OB1 unbundling.\r\n\r\nI've also downgraded xDrip+ by a few versions, since re upgraded to the most current.\r\n\r\nI don't know what else to try. Maybe it's our phone? I'm on Samsung A8. \r\nOr maybe everybody with 8G+ has these errors but nobody cares? @emp-00  I'm on the Samsung Note 8. It might have something to do with the way Samsung BLE handles GATT.  I think that this is what the Samsung Workaround is supposed to take care of. I disabled it, but it still showed as active in System Status.\r\n\r\nBut this is way beyond my knowledge of Android. So we both are on Samsungs! That's a lead. Here come my \"Bluetooth Settings\" (under Less Common Settings):\r\n\r\nAll settings OFF except for these five: Turn BT on, BT Watchdog, G5 BT Watchdog, Use Background Scans, Allow blucon unbonding.\r\n\r\nI remember I had changed one or two of these options when I started with G6 (80/81 tx's) half a year ago. Does anybody know the default settings in this menu? We could try reverting to defaults and see if this helps!\r\n @emp-00  I already cycled all the Bluetooth settings on and off. Didn't hurt function, but made no difference in the log."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1310", "type": "thread", "title": "G6 / 8G: \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1310", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1310, "labels": ["bug", "device-dexcom", "calibration"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-04-18T12:57:41Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-14T12:28:27Z", "comment_count": 46, "comments": [{"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-21T01:22:58Z", "body": "I've been having the same issue, but I think it's only when I enter a calibration code of 0000 (e.g. when I restart a sensor). Is that the same for you?"}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-21T18:50:53Z", "body": "Thanks for the feedback but clear \"NO\" - I am always entering the calibration code, see in screenshot below (here 7171). Do you see the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item? In my case it's always there and this is the only way for me to enter calibrations. Anybody else having this issue?\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/60714349/79902358-a83b7200-8411-11ea-915b-a6335eebf08c.png)\r\n"}, {"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-21T20:28:30Z", "body": "Yes, I do have the \"Initial Calibration\" item in the menu, and it is the only way I can currently calibrate. I also get the exact same errors that you're describing. I had this issue previously and a complete wipe and re-install of xDrip fixed it. However, I ended up back in the same scenario, but I haven't yet identified the specific trigger. I assumed it was the sensor restart, but it appears that's not the case. I'll let you know if it goes back to normal after starting a new sensor (probably within a couple days). If not, I'll wipe and pay more attention as I configure things to see if I can pinpoint the trigger.\r\n\r\nSome more details about my config:\r\n\r\n- Original Pixel, running Android 10\r\n- xDrip version: d0011d1-2020.03.25\r\n\r\n- Data Source: G6 Native\r\n- Status page:\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1320751/79910633-0b66dd80-83ed-11ea-97db-1c0d720a8f48.png\" width=\"50%\">\r\n- G5/G6 Settings\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1320751/79910650-10c"}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-21T20:37:02Z", "body": "I also do sensor restarts (stop session, pop out, wait 15min, pop back in => start session). When re-starting I always enter the initial calibration code (never used 0000 before). My G5/G6 debug settings differ in some switches (see my config above). So all of that's is probably not the trigger...\r\n\r\nI have done frequent xDrip updates by downloading a more recent nightly or by using the auto-update function. Currently we're both using the same version 03/25 - we could upgrade to the latest alpha from April 19th but probably this does not fix our problem - I'm monitoring the changelog and saw no hint these updates solve our problem.\r\n\r\nMaybe @jamorham or any other specialist can have a look and give us a good hint. I'm sure we're not the only ones...\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-23T04:26:23Z", "body": "Just documenting some troubleshooting. I started a new sensor with the calibration code. After warmup, I get the same rejection errors and see the Initial Calibration option in the hamburger menu. I backed up my settings, uninstalled xDrip, reinstalled, and restored the settings. I ignored all prompts to start the sensor (since it was already started). Once connected again, I was in the same situation. Next, I stopped the sensor, uninstalled xDrip, popped out the transmitter, reinstalled, and did **not** restore settings. Followed setup and wizard as if setting up for the first time. I'll report back with my findings once warmup is done and I'm awake."}, {"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-23T17:37:25Z", "body": "Unfortunately, no luck. In addition to the steps mentioned above, I\r\n-  Started the sensor using the https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/8c4987f16f5481f73ecdbe62de2c26cc7fe7d218 version (buddy said it was working for him)\r\n- Started the sensor using Dexcom's app before switching to xDrip\r\n\r\nneither of which fixed the issue.\r\n\r\nNext, I'm going to dive into the code to investigate the specific errors to see if I can figure anything out from that perspective."}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-23T18:52:47Z", "body": "Thanks @justinthomas ... Here's the code - looks like xDrip is confused by somehow reading a wrong timestamp thinking the current time is \"older than 1 hour\" ? Is this a bug or a wrong setting in our phones? I'm using \"automatic date and time provided by network\" in my Android settings. Time displayed is correct. So maybe xDrip is in a different \"timezone\"??? I travelled from EU to the US and back 8 weeks ago. Maybe this confused xDrip? Had no issues with wrong timestamps during my travels though...\r\n\r\npublic static void addCalibration(final int glucose, final long timestamp) {\r\n            final long since = msSince(timestamp);\r\n[...]\r\n            if (**since > HOUR_IN_MS**) {\r\n                final String msg = \"**Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter**: \" + glucose + \" @ \" + JoH.dateTimeText(timestamp);\r\n                JoH.static_toast_long(msg);\r\n                UserError.Log.wtf(TAG, msg);\r\n                return;\r\n            }\r\n"}, {"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-26T17:02:50Z", "body": "I have good news to help get functional again! I downgraded to the [2019.10.27 Nightly Build](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.10.27) and calibration seems to work now. I had an issue with Bluetooth dropping communication, but I think it was because I had a permission set incorrectly. I'm not giving up on digging in deeper, but I just needed something stable to fall back to for own psychological well-being. @emp-00, hopefully this will help you as well!\r\n\r\nThe G5/G6 settings I currently have toggled **on** for this version:\r\n- Use the OB1 Collector\r\n- Native Algorithm\r\n- Go on without calibrations\r\n- G6 Support\r\n- Allow OB1 unbonding\r\n- Allow OB1 initiate bonding\r\n- Authenticate G5 before each read\r\n\r\n@emp-00, following up on your message...\r\n\r\nI doubt it's a wrong phone setting since I haven't changed anything in my phone other than downgrading the version of xDrip. I'm curious, did you happen to start a transmitter in a different timezone? Though, I don"}, {"user": "justinthomas", "created_at": "2020-04-26T17:08:44Z", "body": "Oh, another thing to note is that the Initial Calibration section of the hamburger menu is still there in my current working configuration, so it's presence is not sufficient to claim that the ideal calibration approach is not working.\r\n\r\nInstead of checking that menu, I've been monitoring the G5/G6 status tab to ensure that a single calibration is queued immediately after an attempt to calibrate, and then confirming that the calibration was transmitted and accepted by the transmitter by viewing the Events Log. Note that when using the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item, it queues two calibrations even if only one is entered, but the ideal calibration approach only queues one."}, {"user": "emp-00", "created_at": "2020-04-26T17:30:48Z", "body": "Thanks justinthomas for your efforts! That's encouraging! \r\n\r\nI have JUST restarted my tx after another 10 days: first reading +100 mg/dL too high (as \"always\") and calibrated down by -20% with the Initial Calibration function. As you mentioned always (2) calibrations are queued with this method, confirmed. Tx accepted this first calibration! Damn I'm LUCKY :-) !! The last time I did this I had to restart once more due to \"confused calibration\" messages. Does anybody know if 20% or a fixed -XX mg/dL is the limit which makes the tx accept calibrations? And how long must I wait until the next calibrations step can be entered without crash?\r\n\r\nNow I JUST saw your posting. I have to wait now for 1 or better 2 hours (anbody knows better?) before the next calibration (I'm still almost 50 mg/dL off). Then I will try the syringe again. Have changed my settings as per your suggestion above (switched these 2 ON: \"Go on without Calibrations\" and \"Authenticate G5 before each...\"). Maybe this is do"}], "text": "G6 / 8G: \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\" bug device-dexcom calibration - G6 8Gxxxx, Firmware 2.18.2.88 and running xDrip+ nightly 2020-03-25\r\n- Using G5/G6 settings OB1, Native, Allow OB1 unbonding and Allow OB1 initiate bonding; all remaining options are OFF.\r\n\r\nWhen calibrating using the **syringe icon** I always get the error message \"_Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter_\" (see screenshot). Why is that? \r\n\r\nRunning xDrip+ on Samsung A8 - phone's time setting is fine, see also timestamp in screenshot. I can only calibrate with the \"Initial Calibration\" menu, this works most of the time but people are recommending always using the syringe calibration. Does not work for me :-(\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/60714349/79638182-96916a80-8184-11ea-99ba-50f036c0e622.png) I've been having the same issue, but I think it's only when I enter a calibration code of 0000 (e.g. when I restart a sensor). Is that the same for you? Thanks for the feedback but clear \"NO\" - I am always entering the calibration code, see in screenshot below (here 7171). Do you see the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item? In my case it's always there and this is the only way for me to enter calibrations. Anybody else having this issue?\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/60714349/79902358-a83b7200-8411-11ea-915b-a6335eebf08c.png)\r\n Yes, I do have the \"Initial Calibration\" item in the menu, and it is the only way I can currently calibrate. I also get the exact same errors that you're describing. I had this issue previously and a complete wipe and re-install of xDrip fixed it. However, I ended up back in the same scenario, but I haven't yet identified the specific trigger. I assumed it was the sensor restart, but it appears that's not the case. I'll let you know if it goes back to normal after starting a new sensor (probably within a couple days). If not, I'll wipe and pay more attention as I configure things to see if I can pinpoint the trigger.\r\n\r\nSome more details about my config:\r\n\r\n- Original Pixel, running Android 10\r\n- xDrip version: d0011d1-2020.03.25\r\n\r\n- Data Source: G6 Native\r\n- Status page:\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1320751/79910633-0b66dd80-83ed-11ea-97db-1c0d720a8f48.png\" width=\"50%\">\r\n- G5/G6 Settings\r\n<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1320751/79910650-10c I also do sensor restarts (stop session, pop out, wait 15min, pop back in => start session). When re-starting I always enter the initial calibration code (never used 0000 before). My G5/G6 debug settings differ in some switches (see my config above). So all of that's is probably not the trigger...\r\n\r\nI have done frequent xDrip updates by downloading a more recent nightly or by using the auto-update function. Currently we're both using the same version 03/25 - we could upgrade to the latest alpha from April 19th but probably this does not fix our problem - I'm monitoring the changelog and saw no hint these updates solve our problem.\r\n\r\nMaybe @jamorham or any other specialist can have a look and give us a good hint. I'm sure we're not the only ones...\r\n\r\n Just documenting some troubleshooting. I started a new sensor with the calibration code. After warmup, I get the same rejection errors and see the Initial Calibration option in the hamburger menu. I backed up my settings, uninstalled xDrip, reinstalled, and restored the settings. I ignored all prompts to start the sensor (since it was already started). Once connected again, I was in the same situation. Next, I stopped the sensor, uninstalled xDrip, popped out the transmitter, reinstalled, and did **not** restore settings. Followed setup and wizard as if setting up for the first time. I'll report back with my findings once warmup is done and I'm awake. Unfortunately, no luck. In addition to the steps mentioned above, I\r\n-  Started the sensor using the https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/8c4987f16f5481f73ecdbe62de2c26cc7fe7d218 version (buddy said it was working for him)\r\n- Started the sensor using Dexcom's app before switching to xDrip\r\n\r\nneither of which fixed the issue.\r\n\r\nNext, I'm going to dive into the code to investigate the specific errors to see if I can figure anything out from that perspective. Thanks @justinthomas ... Here's the code - looks like xDrip is confused by somehow reading a wrong timestamp thinking the current time is \"older than 1 hour\" ? Is this a bug or a wrong setting in our phones? I'm using \"automatic date and time provided by network\" in my Android settings. Time displayed is correct. So maybe xDrip is in a different \"timezone\"??? I travelled from EU to the US and back 8 weeks ago. Maybe this confused xDrip? Had no issues with wrong timestamps during my travels though...\r\n\r\npublic static void addCalibration(final int glucose, final long timestamp) {\r\n            final long since = msSince(timestamp);\r\n[...]\r\n            if (**since > HOUR_IN_MS**) {\r\n                final String msg = \"**Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter**: \" + glucose + \" @ \" + JoH.dateTimeText(timestamp);\r\n                JoH.static_toast_long(msg);\r\n                UserError.Log.wtf(TAG, msg);\r\n                return;\r\n            }\r\n I have good news to help get functional again! I downgraded to the [2019.10.27 Nightly Build](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.10.27) and calibration seems to work now. I had an issue with Bluetooth dropping communication, but I think it was because I had a permission set incorrectly. I'm not giving up on digging in deeper, but I just needed something stable to fall back to for own psychological well-being. @emp-00, hopefully this will help you as well!\r\n\r\nThe G5/G6 settings I currently have toggled **on** for this version:\r\n- Use the OB1 Collector\r\n- Native Algorithm\r\n- Go on without calibrations\r\n- G6 Support\r\n- Allow OB1 unbonding\r\n- Allow OB1 initiate bonding\r\n- Authenticate G5 before each read\r\n\r\n@emp-00, following up on your message...\r\n\r\nI doubt it's a wrong phone setting since I haven't changed anything in my phone other than downgrading the version of xDrip. I'm curious, did you happen to start a transmitter in a different timezone? Though, I don Oh, another thing to note is that the Initial Calibration section of the hamburger menu is still there in my current working configuration, so it's presence is not sufficient to claim that the ideal calibration approach is not working.\r\n\r\nInstead of checking that menu, I've been monitoring the G5/G6 status tab to ensure that a single calibration is queued immediately after an attempt to calibrate, and then confirming that the calibration was transmitted and accepted by the transmitter by viewing the Events Log. Note that when using the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item, it queues two calibrations even if only one is entered, but the ideal calibration approach only queues one. Thanks justinthomas for your efforts! That's encouraging! \r\n\r\nI have JUST restarted my tx after another 10 days: first reading +100 mg/dL too high (as \"always\") and calibrated down by -20% with the Initial Calibration function. As you mentioned always (2) calibrations are queued with this method, confirmed. Tx accepted this first calibration! Damn I'm LUCKY :-) !! The last time I did this I had to restart once more due to \"confused calibration\" messages. Does anybody know if 20% or a fixed -XX mg/dL is the limit which makes the tx accept calibrations? And how long must I wait until the next calibrations step can be entered without crash?\r\n\r\nNow I JUST saw your posting. I have to wait now for 1 or better 2 hours (anbody knows better?) before the next calibration (I'm still almost 50 mg/dL off). Then I will try the syringe again. Have changed my settings as per your suggestion above (switched these 2 ON: \"Go on without Calibrations\" and \"Authenticate G5 before each...\"). Maybe this is do"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1394", "type": "thread", "title": "Libre 2 - (xDrip+ + LibreLink patched) vs. (xDrip+ + MiaoMiao2)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1394", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1394, "labels": ["question", "device-libre"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-08-01T20:51:11Z", "closed_at": "2020-11-24T22:55:52Z", "comment_count": 105, "comments": [{"user": "twinko", "created_at": "2020-08-03T11:34:05Z", "body": "Should be the same, both use the data from the freestyle libre sensor 2 itself. With the patched app you dont need an extra device, that already made my decision for the patched app. In my oppinion miaomiao is only helpfluu if you use libre 1 sensors. Perhaps if you are a looper (having a automated pump aswell) the miaomiao can have advanteges, but i dont do that thats why i cant tell."}, {"user": "DavidAGInnovation", "created_at": "2020-08-03T11:40:45Z", "body": "But I thought that the patched app gave you the processed values by Abbott, and MiaoMiao just the raw values. Isn't that true?"}, {"user": "twinko", "created_at": "2020-08-03T12:09:24Z", "body": "Both (miamia and libre) use a routine to handle the raw data. Im not 100% sure about the miaomiao algorithm and didnt found a comparison between both, but i guess the libre one is tested a lot :)"}, {"user": "jomonba1", "created_at": "2020-08-04T06:53:59Z", "body": "Hi,\r\nI've just received my first FreeStyle Libre 2 sensor (until yesterday I was using Libre 1). I was very happy with my Miao Miao 2 and Xdrip, but now I found that is not working anymore (I get the \"Checksum failed\" error everytime, there's no way to make it works).\r\nThen, you guys wrote above that we don't need the Miao Miao 2 anymore, we can use the LibreLink app patched with xDrip+??? is there any guide to do that? where/how can I find the patched app??\r\nThank you!"}, {"user": "twinko", "created_at": "2020-08-04T09:37:57Z", "body": "@jomonba1 read this guide. at the bottom its in englisch:\r\nhttps://github.com/TinoKossmann/LibreLink-xDrip-Patch\r\nIf you read this here is another guide for how to youse xdrip in combination with the patched libre app\r\nhttps://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/EN/Configuration/xdrip.html#xdrip-freestyle-libre (you can change the language on the left side of the page)"}, {"user": "teleriddler", "created_at": "2020-08-04T10:33:51Z", "body": "Having used both setups as well as MM1 and Libre 1 before, I am now confidently using Libre2 with only the patched app.  \r\n\r\nRecently I was calibrating the Libre2 in XDrip+ and I have now stopped that completely.  Reason being is that calibrations were always throwing off the values.  I get that the slope calibration should provide a better approximation but in my experience it was not working well.   I did all the right things, wait until BG is stable, do a sensor change, no carbs for 3 hours prior, low stress during calibration, initial calibration of 2 BG tests.   Then the next few days I would do a calibration when I woke up as BG was stable from during the previous night.   \r\n\r\nA user on Gitter (twinko, I think) mentioned that they were not using calibrations with Libre2, this peaked my interest so I set aside 2 weeks to try this.   Here is what I found.   \r\n\r\n**Setup:**  Libre2 with LibreLink patched app.   XDrip+ and AAPS (Eros-0.3-2.7 build for Omnipod)\r\n\r\n**Goal:**  Minimalist"}, {"user": "jomonba1", "created_at": "2020-08-04T17:26:49Z", "body": "@twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\nLet me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\nThen, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard...  - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will  send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct???"}, {"user": "DavidAGInnovation", "created_at": "2020-08-04T17:58:38Z", "body": "> @twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\n> Let me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\n> Then, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard... - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct???\r\n\r\nCorrect."}, {"user": "twinko", "created_at": "2020-08-05T08:35:42Z", "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> @twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\n> Let me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\n> Then, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard... - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct???\r\n\r\nas mentiones by David, yes tahts correct. No worries, just follow the guides step by step, its not that hard."}, {"user": "JimZam", "created_at": "2020-08-05T14:38:14Z", "body": "@teleriddler  You can insert the new sensor at night and have two sensors for 6-8 hours so next morning, when the old sensor expires, all you have to do is scan the new sensor and wait one hour. That way you will probably avoid the 6 hours of wrong data.\r\n\r\nIn my case xDrip+ loses data quite often and I have to scan the sensor to make it work again. I don't know if it's a xDrip or patched app problem. Next time I'll activate Alarms in LibreLink and see if they work despite xDrip don't to try to isolate the problem. Have you had any data losing problem?\r\nRegards"}], "text": "Libre 2 - (xDrip+ + LibreLink patched) vs. (xDrip+ + MiaoMiao2) question device-libre I'm new to the FreeStyle Libre 2, and I was wondering what would you choose (and why) if you had the opportunity. Which method gives you the most accurate results, LibreLink 2.3 patched app with xDrip+, or the MiaoMiao2 with xDrip+?\r\n\r\nThank you for time and effort, and waiting for your opinions! Should be the same, both use the data from the freestyle libre sensor 2 itself. With the patched app you dont need an extra device, that already made my decision for the patched app. In my oppinion miaomiao is only helpfluu if you use libre 1 sensors. Perhaps if you are a looper (having a automated pump aswell) the miaomiao can have advanteges, but i dont do that thats why i cant tell. But I thought that the patched app gave you the processed values by Abbott, and MiaoMiao just the raw values. Isn't that true? Both (miamia and libre) use a routine to handle the raw data. Im not 100% sure about the miaomiao algorithm and didnt found a comparison between both, but i guess the libre one is tested a lot :) Hi,\r\nI've just received my first FreeStyle Libre 2 sensor (until yesterday I was using Libre 1). I was very happy with my Miao Miao 2 and Xdrip, but now I found that is not working anymore (I get the \"Checksum failed\" error everytime, there's no way to make it works).\r\nThen, you guys wrote above that we don't need the Miao Miao 2 anymore, we can use the LibreLink app patched with xDrip+??? is there any guide to do that? where/how can I find the patched app??\r\nThank you! @jomonba1 read this guide. at the bottom its in englisch:\r\nhttps://github.com/TinoKossmann/LibreLink-xDrip-Patch\r\nIf you read this here is another guide for how to youse xdrip in combination with the patched libre app\r\nhttps://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/EN/Configuration/xdrip.html#xdrip-freestyle-libre (you can change the language on the left side of the page) Having used both setups as well as MM1 and Libre 1 before, I am now confidently using Libre2 with only the patched app.  \r\n\r\nRecently I was calibrating the Libre2 in XDrip+ and I have now stopped that completely.  Reason being is that calibrations were always throwing off the values.  I get that the slope calibration should provide a better approximation but in my experience it was not working well.   I did all the right things, wait until BG is stable, do a sensor change, no carbs for 3 hours prior, low stress during calibration, initial calibration of 2 BG tests.   Then the next few days I would do a calibration when I woke up as BG was stable from during the previous night.   \r\n\r\nA user on Gitter (twinko, I think) mentioned that they were not using calibrations with Libre2, this peaked my interest so I set aside 2 weeks to try this.   Here is what I found.   \r\n\r\n**Setup:**  Libre2 with LibreLink patched app.   XDrip+ and AAPS (Eros-0.3-2.7 build for Omnipod)\r\n\r\n**Goal:**  Minimalist @twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\nLet me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\nThen, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard...  - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will  send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct??? > @twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\n> Let me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\n> Then, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard... - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct???\r\n\r\nCorrect. > \r\n> \r\n> @twinko Hi! thank you for your reply!!!\r\n> Let me say that I am quite noob with this, I am using the FreeStyle libre sensors since last 6 moths and as I said, I was very happy with my MM2 + FreeStyle libre 1 + xDrip app... now I've got the Libre 2 and nothing is working...\r\n> Then, if I understood properly, I won't need the MM2 anymore, is that correct? If I am able to patch the LibreLink App (not sure if I will... I think it will bevery hard... - no videos on youtube, shit shit shit - ) it will send the data to the xDrip app via BT, without the MM2 device? is that correct???\r\n\r\nas mentiones by David, yes tahts correct. No worries, just follow the guides step by step, its not that hard. @teleriddler  You can insert the new sensor at night and have two sensors for 6-8 hours so next morning, when the old sensor expires, all you have to do is scan the new sensor and wait one hour. That way you will probably avoid the 6 hours of wrong data.\r\n\r\nIn my case xDrip+ loses data quite often and I have to scan the sensor to make it work again. I don't know if it's a xDrip or patched app problem. Next time I'll activate Alarms in LibreLink and see if they work despite xDrip don't to try to isolate the problem. Have you had any data losing problem?\r\nRegards"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1474", "type": "thread", "title": "Freestyle Libre 3 support", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1474", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1474, "labels": ["question", "device-libre", "status-waiting", "status-postponed"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-10-20T21:03:11Z", "closed_at": "2021-11-08T04:34:50Z", "comment_count": 67, "comments": [{"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2020-10-21T03:50:10Z", "body": "Abbott just announced the Libre 3. It is not available yet. Hence, nobody can start implementing support or investigate whether it is possible or not."}, {"user": "schrackschorsch", "created_at": "2021-08-04T14:22:56Z", "body": "libre 3 is now available in Germany. The libre-app for ios is ready. The app for android soon will be available.\r\nhttps://www.freestylelibre.de/libre/freestyle-libre-3-entdecken.html"}, {"user": "marekmand", "created_at": "2021-09-16T20:29:40Z", "body": "Shouldn't be this ticket reopened since FL3 is available publicly in Germany?\r\nI don't see any reason to postpone this anymore."}, {"user": "renele", "created_at": "2021-10-05T16:59:22Z", "body": "any update on this or where can we track progress or is something blocking ?"}, {"user": "yoshimo", "created_at": "2021-10-05T18:23:52Z", "body": "The missing android app makes analysis harder "}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2021-10-05T19:21:28Z", "body": "It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app."}, {"user": "Owncloudp", "created_at": "2021-10-05T20:40:31Z", "body": "https://apkdownload.com.de/apk/1525101160/freestyle-libre-3-de\r\n\r\nHere is it - Not officially Release until now... "}, {"user": "yoshimo", "created_at": "2021-10-23T16:48:05Z", "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app.\r\n\r\nif you had a sensor or 2, would you be able to attempt an integration before the android app is officially released?"}, {"user": "birdfly", "created_at": "2021-11-08T04:30:33Z", "body": "> https://apkdownload.com.de/apk/1525101160/freestyle-libre-3-de\r\n> \r\n> Here is it - Not officially Release until now...\r\n\r\nbut the link is not available, better share apk directly if you have it "}], "text": "Freestyle Libre 3 support question device-libre status-waiting status-postponed Recently Freestyle Libre 3 was launched in Europe providing GCM, readings are now through Bluetooth instead of NFC.\r\nIs there any move to support it?\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n* https://abbott.mediaroom.com/2020-09-28-Abbotts-FreeStyle-R-Libre-3-System-Receives-CE-Mark-Features-Worlds-Smallest-Thinnest-Sensor-with-Best-in-Class-Performance-at-the-Same-Low-Cost-for-People-with-Diabetes Abbott just announced the Libre 3. It is not available yet. Hence, nobody can start implementing support or investigate whether it is possible or not. libre 3 is now available in Germany. The libre-app for ios is ready. The app for android soon will be available.\r\nhttps://www.freestylelibre.de/libre/freestyle-libre-3-entdecken.html Shouldn't be this ticket reopened since FL3 is available publicly in Germany?\r\nI don't see any reason to postpone this anymore. any update on this or where can we track progress or is something blocking ? The missing android app makes analysis harder  It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app. https://apkdownload.com.de/apk/1525101160/freestyle-libre-3-de\r\n\r\nHere is it - Not officially Release until now...  > \r\n> \r\n> It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app.\r\n\r\nif you had a sensor or 2, would you be able to attempt an integration before the android app is officially released? > https://apkdownload.com.de/apk/1525101160/freestyle-libre-3-de\r\n> \r\n> Here is it - Not officially Release until now...\r\n\r\nbut the link is not available, better share apk directly if you have it "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1494", "type": "thread", "title": "Android 10+ asks every 5 minutes for pairing with Dexcom transmitter", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1494", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1494, "labels": ["device-dexcom", "bluetooth", "android10+"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2020-11-01T09:25:19Z", "closed_at": "2020-11-15T13:37:28Z", "comment_count": 195, "comments": [{"user": "vitalykekukh", "created_at": "2020-11-01T09:35:04Z", "body": "After upgrade to oct 2020 android samsung a50 every 5 minutes xdrip 2020 asks for dexcom bluetooth connection when syncing. If you do not agree with the request to connect the dexcom bluetooth sensor, xdrip sync does not work.\r\nThe xdrip app released in 2019 works fine. Synchronization of the smartphone and dexcom takes place without a request.\r\nHow to remove the request to connect dexcom via bluetooth on the a50 smartphone on xdrip later edition of xdrip?"}, {"user": "BKrueckeberg", "created_at": "2020-11-04T03:20:28Z", "body": "I am experiencing what I believe may be the same issue. xDrip making a bluetooth pairing request for the Dexcom \r\ntransmitter every couple of minutes. It is extremely annoying and frustrating.\r\n\r\nThis is on a Samsung Galaxy S10 and started happening with the last phone update yesterday.\r\n\r\nGalaxy S10 (SM-G973U1)\r\nBuild Number : G973U1UES4ETJ3\r\nAndroid version : Q(Android 10)\r\nRelease Date : 2020-11-02\r\nSecurity patch level : 2020-11-01\r\n\r\n2020.07.13 e14bae1\r\n\r\nHave not been able to work around this :(\r\n\r\n![20201103_221738](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/59528752/98065513-c18e9380-1e22-11eb-976f-20032d0a120b.jpg)\r\n"}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2020-11-04T06:27:25Z", "body": "@BKrueckeberg Can you confirm that the nightly from [May 18, 2019](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) works for you?\r\n\r\n@vitalykekukh Please help us by finding the latest version which works for you."}, {"user": "vitalykekukh", "created_at": "2020-11-04T06:42:10Z", "body": "now this version works well\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18\r\n"}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2020-11-04T06:46:37Z", "body": "@vitalykekukh Now, I'm confused. What is the difference between the latest comments with respect to the release tag? Please can you remove redundant comments and just edit a (potentially) wrong comment?"}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2020-11-04T06:55:49Z", "body": "@vitalykekukh I cannot believe that [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) is the latest version which works because there are only Libre-related changes in [2019.05.19](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.19), for instance. It would be really helpful to find the latest tagged version which works for you. Please can you try newer versions of every month after May, 2019 until you found a breaking version and than go stepwise back the tags?"}, {"user": "avidprogrammerc", "created_at": "2020-11-04T14:13:02Z", "body": "I am having the same issue on my Pixel 5. I tried the May 19 version but the same thing happened"}, {"user": "BKrueckeberg", "created_at": "2020-11-04T15:15:17Z", "body": "I tried the [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) build on my Samsung Galaxy S10. \r\n\r\nI am NOT experiencing the ongoing Bluetooth pairing requests anymore BUT am also loosing transmitter connection after only a handful of successfully received signals. I am seeing 'Aggressively restarting collector service due to lack of reception backoff' being logged every couple of minutes.\r\n\r\nBottom line is that the [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) doesn't work. Please let me know how I can support you in figuring out a solution!\r\n\r\nThanks"}, {"user": "vitalykekukh", "created_at": "2020-11-04T16:34:39Z", "body": "The difference between the old and new versions of Android is the enhanced Bluetooth security system. The developers claim that hackers can steal data from a smartphone via Bluetooth. So in the new version of Android, they have enabled an additional pairing request. \r\nThe 2019 version of xdrip is permanently paired via Bluetooth. To save battery power, the 2020 versions connect via Bluetooth every 5 minutes and then disconnect. Therefore, when paired, Android recognizes the pairing as connecting a new device and issues a request to the smartphone user. In this situation, either the xdrip developers in the new versions will make permanent pairing via Bluetooth, or the Android developers will make it possible to make a one-time request to pair with a known (allowed) device."}, {"user": "BKrueckeberg", "created_at": "2020-11-04T19:02:37Z", "body": "Thanks for the explanation @vitalykekukh. That would make sense based on what I am experiencing with my phone. \r\n\r\nDo you happen to know with what version this power save feature was added exactly? I have tried the 2019.05.18 version but this hasn't worked well for me either (due to other issues)."}], "text": "Android 10+ asks every 5 minutes for pairing with Dexcom transmitter device-dexcom bluetooth android10+ After updating in October 2020 from android to samsung a50 every 5 minutes xdrip 2020 asks for dexcom Bluetooth connections. The xdrip app released in 2019 works fine.\r\nHow to remove the request to connect dexcom via bluetooth on a50 smartphone? After upgrade to oct 2020 android samsung a50 every 5 minutes xdrip 2020 asks for dexcom bluetooth connection when syncing. If you do not agree with the request to connect the dexcom bluetooth sensor, xdrip sync does not work.\r\nThe xdrip app released in 2019 works fine. Synchronization of the smartphone and dexcom takes place without a request.\r\nHow to remove the request to connect dexcom via bluetooth on the a50 smartphone on xdrip later edition of xdrip? I am experiencing what I believe may be the same issue. xDrip making a bluetooth pairing request for the Dexcom \r\ntransmitter every couple of minutes. It is extremely annoying and frustrating.\r\n\r\nThis is on a Samsung Galaxy S10 and started happening with the last phone update yesterday.\r\n\r\nGalaxy S10 (SM-G973U1)\r\nBuild Number : G973U1UES4ETJ3\r\nAndroid version : Q(Android 10)\r\nRelease Date : 2020-11-02\r\nSecurity patch level : 2020-11-01\r\n\r\n2020.07.13 e14bae1\r\n\r\nHave not been able to work around this :(\r\n\r\n![20201103_221738](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/59528752/98065513-c18e9380-1e22-11eb-976f-20032d0a120b.jpg)\r\n @BKrueckeberg Can you confirm that the nightly from [May 18, 2019](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) works for you?\r\n\r\n@vitalykekukh Please help us by finding the latest version which works for you. now this version works well\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18\r\n @vitalykekukh Now, I'm confused. What is the difference between the latest comments with respect to the release tag? Please can you remove redundant comments and just edit a (potentially) wrong comment? @vitalykekukh I cannot believe that [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) is the latest version which works because there are only Libre-related changes in [2019.05.19](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.19), for instance. It would be really helpful to find the latest tagged version which works for you. Please can you try newer versions of every month after May, 2019 until you found a breaking version and than go stepwise back the tags? I am having the same issue on my Pixel 5. I tried the May 19 version but the same thing happened I tried the [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) build on my Samsung Galaxy S10. \r\n\r\nI am NOT experiencing the ongoing Bluetooth pairing requests anymore BUT am also loosing transmitter connection after only a handful of successfully received signals. I am seeing 'Aggressively restarting collector service due to lack of reception backoff' being logged every couple of minutes.\r\n\r\nBottom line is that the [2019.05.18](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2019.05.18) doesn't work. Please let me know how I can support you in figuring out a solution!\r\n\r\nThanks The difference between the old and new versions of Android is the enhanced Bluetooth security system. The developers claim that hackers can steal data from a smartphone via Bluetooth. So in the new version of Android, they have enabled an additional pairing request. \r\nThe 2019 version of xdrip is permanently paired via Bluetooth. To save battery power, the 2020 versions connect via Bluetooth every 5 minutes and then disconnect. Therefore, when paired, Android recognizes the pairing as connecting a new device and issues a request to the smartphone user. In this situation, either the xdrip developers in the new versions will make permanent pairing via Bluetooth, or the Android developers will make it possible to make a one-time request to pair with a known (allowed) device. Thanks for the explanation @vitalykekukh. That would make sense based on what I am experiencing with my phone. \r\n\r\nDo you happen to know with what version this power save feature was added exactly? I have tried the 2019.05.18 version but this hasn't worked well for me either (due to other issues)."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1647", "type": "thread", "title": "xDrip confuses G5 with a G6 and performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1647", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1647, "labels": ["bug", "device-dexcom", "calibration", "device-dexcom-transmitter"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-02-17T13:16:55Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-28T14:43:00Z", "comment_count": 52, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2021-02-17T19:01:46Z", "body": "The screenshot implies that a bloodtest was delivered from a bluetooth connected glucose meter which it believes was ~9000 seconds old. If the finger stick test was just done recently then we need to determine if the clock on the meter is correct or if there is an issue with the user's local timezone vs the clock on the meter and if that is the source of the >1 hour rejection message. It may also be (more likely?) that there were multiple tests synced from the meter and that only one of those was used and the other rejected which is why there is a report of success and also rejection in the screenshot.\r\n\r\nWe also want to know the transmitter firmware version to determine the issue regarding raw."}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-02-17T19:04:12Z", "body": "You are talking to him in the Gitter room.\r\nThe firmware version is 1.0.4.15."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2021-02-17T19:40:29Z", "body": "Please try the 17th Feb nightly to see if it resolves the issue."}, {"user": "viq", "created_at": "2021-02-18T00:56:03Z", "body": "Sorry for screenshot, attaching what happened when I calibrated using the `2021.02.17` version. I don't know where this \"calibration beyond 4 days\" is coming from. The dot from syncing with glucometer appears right there, and clicking on it is how initiate calibration \r\n\r\n![xdrip_logs](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/639461/108288118-575ced00-718c-11eb-9767-834b8a594d56.png)\r\n"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-02-18T00:59:43Z", "body": "If you tap on the top left menu button, and on calibration graph, what does it show?  Is it empty, or does it show your initial calibrations?"}, {"user": "viq", "created_at": "2021-02-18T01:03:10Z", "body": "It does show some calibrations. Currently it shows three from today, and one from 5 days ago."}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-02-18T01:06:23Z", "body": "Did you just update to the new version and calibrated?\r\nOr, did you start the sensor after updating and then, calibrated?"}, {"user": "viq", "created_at": "2021-02-18T04:03:55Z", "body": "Update and (single) calibrate.\n"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-02-18T04:08:45Z", "body": "OK\r\nPlease let us know the next time you start the sensor.  Only then, will you have to provide initial calibrations again.  Only then, will you know if the issue has ben resolved or not."}, {"user": "viq", "created_at": "2021-02-18T05:53:57Z", "body": "Sensor session should be restarted in a few hours, so we should know soon."}], "text": "xDrip confuses G5 with a G6 and performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6 bug device-dexcom calibration device-dexcom-transmitter ### Expected behavior\r\nDexcom G5 can be used in Native mode.  But, since G5 sends raw data, you can still access the calibration graph.  And xDrip removes \"Initial calibration\" from the menu after initial calibrations have been submitted and replaces it with \"Add calibration\".\r\n\r\n### Your environment\r\nThe problem was observed with the February 11, 2021 release, and February 3, 2021.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\nCalibrations are sent to the transmitter and are accepted by the G5 transmitter.  However, xDrip logs show they are rejected by xDrip.\r\n![tempFileForShare_20210216-234941](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/51497406/108206590-96d7fa80-70f4-11eb-93a3-64454447f949.jpg)\r\n\r\nLogs show calibrations have been rejected.\r\nNo access to adding calibration in the top left menu as only initial calibration is shown there.\r\nNo access to calibration graph.\r\nEmpty calibration data table.\r\n\r\nThe symptoms match the behavior of xDrip with a device that does not send raw data like a Firefly G6,\r\n\r\nAfter installing the January 29, 2021 version, the problem was resolved. \r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce the behavior:\r\nInstall xDrip release February 11, 2021\r\nStart a G5 sensor in native mode\r\nApply initial calibrations\r\nCheck calibration data table, or check the logs.\r\n\r\n@viq:hackerspace.pl reported this in the Gitter room.\r\nAnother individual reported it on facebook where the calibration graph being missing and the calibration data table being empty were reported.\r\nThe calibration rejection logs were reported by both users. The screenshot implies that a bloodtest was delivered from a bluetooth connected glucose meter which it believes was ~9000 seconds old. If the finger stick test was just done recently then we need to determine if the clock on the meter is correct or if there is an issue with the user's local timezone vs the clock on the meter and if that is the source of the >1 hour rejection message. It may also be (more likely?) that there were multiple tests synced from the meter and that only one of those was used and the other rejected which is why there is a report of success and also rejection in the screenshot.\r\n\r\nWe also want to know the transmitter firmware version to determine the issue regarding raw. You are talking to him in the Gitter room.\r\nThe firmware version is 1.0.4.15. Please try the 17th Feb nightly to see if it resolves the issue. Sorry for screenshot, attaching what happened when I calibrated using the `2021.02.17` version. I don't know where this \"calibration beyond 4 days\" is coming from. The dot from syncing with glucometer appears right there, and clicking on it is how initiate calibration \r\n\r\n![xdrip_logs](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/639461/108288118-575ced00-718c-11eb-9767-834b8a594d56.png)\r\n If you tap on the top left menu button, and on calibration graph, what does it show?  Is it empty, or does it show your initial calibrations? It does show some calibrations. Currently it shows three from today, and one from 5 days ago. Did you just update to the new version and calibrated?\r\nOr, did you start the sensor after updating and then, calibrated? Update and (single) calibrate.\n OK\r\nPlease let us know the next time you start the sensor.  Only then, will you have to provide initial calibrations again.  Only then, will you know if the issue has ben resolved or not. Sensor session should be restarted in a few hours, so we should know soon."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1648", "type": "thread", "title": "WearOS 'Apps on Your Phone' support being depricated by Google - XDrip WearOS functionality becoming un-usable", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1648", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1648, "labels": ["bug", "question", "breaking"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-02-17T19:55:56Z", "closed_at": "2023-01-09T02:05:46Z", "comment_count": 50, "comments": [{"user": "rudysroost", "created_at": "2021-02-17T21:28:49Z", "body": "Does anyone know when the support will be terminated? I was just about to\nbuy a Ticwatch to use as a collector instead of my Pixel 5. If I have to\nsideload onto the Ticwatch, I may just not bother.\n\nThanks,\nScott\n\n\nOn Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:56 PM Dave Acklam <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> Google is terminating support for Android-app-bundled WearOS watch-apps\n> in-favor of requiring all watch-apps to be hosted on the Play Store.\n>\n> XDrip uses the 'old method' (watch app bundled inside phone version),\n> which means that XDrip WearOS support will break for new installs (and\n> re-installs), as it will not be possible to install the WearOS xdrip app\n> anymore.\n>\n> Fix involves either:\n> A) breaking-out the WearOS app into it's own separately downloadable APK\n> and posting it along with adb sideload instructions\n> -or-\n> B) Getting it listed on the play-store.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n>"}, {"user": "dcacklam", "created_at": "2021-02-17T21:30:44Z", "body": "March 10th\nhttps://9to5google.com/2021/02/12/wear-os-legacy-apps/\n\nOn Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:29 PM rudysroost <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> Does anyone know when the support will be terminated? I was just about to\n> buy a Ticwatch to use as a collector instead of my Pixel 5. If I have to\n> sideload onto the Ticwatch, I may just not bother.\n>\n> Thanks,\n> Scott\n>\n>\n> On Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:56 PM Dave Acklam <notifications@github.com>\n> wrote:\n>\n> > Google is terminating support for Android-app-bundled WearOS watch-apps\n> > in-favor of requiring all watch-apps to be hosted on the Play Store.\n> >\n> > XDrip uses the 'old method' (watch app bundled inside phone version),\n> > which means that XDrip WearOS support will break for new installs (and\n> > re-installs), as it will not be possible to install the WearOS xdrip app\n> > anymore.\n> >\n> > Fix involves either:\n> > A) breaking-out the WearOS app into it's own separately downloadable APK\n> > and posting it along with adb sideload in"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-02-17T23:53:55Z", "body": "Edit - 2025:\nTo reach the developers, to ask questions, please use discussions:\nhttps://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/discussions \n  \n---  \n  \nThis neither seems to be a bug nor a feature request.\nPlease use the support channels for everything else:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/xDripG5\nhttps://gitter.im/jamorham/xDrip-plus\nThanks"}, {"user": "AEI-SteffenG", "created_at": "2021-03-02T13:55:48Z", "body": "A solution already seems to exist: http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/xda-developers/ShsH/~3/lLbxmCuZfV8/ - still it may become necessary to extract the wearable apk before sideloading."}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2021-03-10T06:38:00Z", "body": "@Navid200 where can the wear APKs be downloaded? From today on they are needed in San unbundled way."}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-10T12:43:10Z", "body": "@AdrianLxM This is presented to anyone who opens a new issue now.\r\n![Screenshot 2021-03-10 073712](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/51497406/110630550-7fc87d80-8173-11eb-9a27-c8d549168fd3.png)\r\n\r\nI know that there are questions that the user community have and they have been using the issue platform to ask them.  A decision was made to ask the user community to help by asking the questions from the other users first.  We also want to improve documentation.\r\nThat was the reason I closed this, to follow the requirements from everyone.\r\n\r\nIf you disagree with the approach we have taken, in coordinating the open issues, I would appreciate it if you discuss with jamorham and tolot27.\r\n\r\nThanks for reopening this.  I will now tag it as a question and leave it open.\r\n\r\nThanks for all your help and support, past and present."}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2021-03-10T12:44:46Z", "body": "I would tag it as bug if wearOS no longer works!"}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2021-03-10T13:33:57Z", "body": "#693 comes in my mind. :open_mouth:"}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2021-03-11T00:37:44Z", "body": "While a release to play would have the highest convenience factor, it's unrealistic.\n\nIf the build system would add the wear.apk signed with the same key, it would be possible to side load it. It needs to be signed with the same key in order to communicate with the phone."}, {"user": "dcacklam", "created_at": "2021-03-11T01:03:10Z", "body": "Since this is my post originally, a thought:\r\n\r\nWhat if the XDrip+ phone app was packaged with the required scripts/executables/etc to have a 'sideload app to watch' button in the app, which would then perform similar functionality to (http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/xda-developers/ShsH/~3/lLbxmCuZfV8/) but only for the xDrip+ watch-app rather than as a general purpose solution? \r\n\r\nMake it so that all a user has to do, is enable sideloading on the watch, then go into the XDrip phone-app's settings -> watch-settings -> 'Android Wear' menu, and click 'sideload app to watch'...\r\n\r\nA FAQ entry on allowing ADB/side-loading permissions would be needed, of course. "}], "text": "WearOS 'Apps on Your Phone' support being depricated by Google - XDrip WearOS functionality becoming un-usable bug question breaking Google is terminating support for Android-app-bundled WearOS watch-apps in-favor of requiring all watch-apps to be hosted on the Play Store.\r\n\r\nXDrip uses the 'old method' (watch app bundled inside phone version), which means that XDrip WearOS support will break for new installs (and re-installs), as it will not be possible to install the WearOS xdrip app anymore.\r\n\r\nFix involves either:\r\nA) breaking-out the WearOS app into it's own separately downloadable APK and posting it along with instructions on how to adb-sideload it *to the watch*\r\n-or-\r\nB) Getting it listed on the play-store.  Does anyone know when the support will be terminated? I was just about to\nbuy a Ticwatch to use as a collector instead of my Pixel 5. If I have to\nsideload onto the Ticwatch, I may just not bother.\n\nThanks,\nScott\n\n\nOn Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:56 PM Dave Acklam <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> Google is terminating support for Android-app-bundled WearOS watch-apps\n> in-favor of requiring all watch-apps to be hosted on the Play Store.\n>\n> XDrip uses the 'old method' (watch app bundled inside phone version),\n> which means that XDrip WearOS support will break for new installs (and\n> re-installs), as it will not be possible to install the WearOS xdrip app\n> anymore.\n>\n> Fix involves either:\n> A) breaking-out the WearOS app into it's own separately downloadable APK\n> and posting it along with adb sideload instructions\n> -or-\n> B) Getting it listed on the play-store.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> March 10th\nhttps://9to5google.com/2021/02/12/wear-os-legacy-apps/\n\nOn Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:29 PM rudysroost <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> Does anyone know when the support will be terminated? I was just about to\n> buy a Ticwatch to use as a collector instead of my Pixel 5. If I have to\n> sideload onto the Ticwatch, I may just not bother.\n>\n> Thanks,\n> Scott\n>\n>\n> On Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 1:56 PM Dave Acklam <notifications@github.com>\n> wrote:\n>\n> > Google is terminating support for Android-app-bundled WearOS watch-apps\n> > in-favor of requiring all watch-apps to be hosted on the Play Store.\n> >\n> > XDrip uses the 'old method' (watch app bundled inside phone version),\n> > which means that XDrip WearOS support will break for new installs (and\n> > re-installs), as it will not be possible to install the WearOS xdrip app\n> > anymore.\n> >\n> > Fix involves either:\n> > A) breaking-out the WearOS app into it's own separately downloadable APK\n> > and posting it along with adb sideload in Edit - 2025:\nTo reach the developers, to ask questions, please use discussions:\nhttps://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/discussions \n  \n---  \n  \nThis neither seems to be a bug nor a feature request.\nPlease use the support channels for everything else:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/xDripG5\nhttps://gitter.im/jamorham/xDrip-plus\nThanks A solution already seems to exist: http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/xda-developers/ShsH/~3/lLbxmCuZfV8/ - still it may become necessary to extract the wearable apk before sideloading. @Navid200 where can the wear APKs be downloaded? From today on they are needed in San unbundled way. @AdrianLxM This is presented to anyone who opens a new issue now.\r\n![Screenshot 2021-03-10 073712](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/51497406/110630550-7fc87d80-8173-11eb-9a27-c8d549168fd3.png)\r\n\r\nI know that there are questions that the user community have and they have been using the issue platform to ask them.  A decision was made to ask the user community to help by asking the questions from the other users first.  We also want to improve documentation.\r\nThat was the reason I closed this, to follow the requirements from everyone.\r\n\r\nIf you disagree with the approach we have taken, in coordinating the open issues, I would appreciate it if you discuss with jamorham and tolot27.\r\n\r\nThanks for reopening this.  I will now tag it as a question and leave it open.\r\n\r\nThanks for all your help and support, past and present. I would tag it as bug if wearOS no longer works! #693 comes in my mind. :open_mouth: While a release to play would have the highest convenience factor, it's unrealistic.\n\nIf the build system would add the wear.apk signed with the same key, it would be possible to side load it. It needs to be signed with the same key in order to communicate with the phone. Since this is my post originally, a thought:\r\n\r\nWhat if the XDrip+ phone app was packaged with the required scripts/executables/etc to have a 'sideload app to watch' button in the app, which would then perform similar functionality to (http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/xda-developers/ShsH/~3/lLbxmCuZfV8/) but only for the xDrip+ watch-app rather than as a general purpose solution? \r\n\r\nMake it so that all a user has to do, is enable sideloading on the watch, then go into the XDrip phone-app's settings -> watch-settings -> 'Android Wear' menu, and click 'sideload app to watch'...\r\n\r\nA FAQ entry on allowing ADB/side-loading permissions would be needed, of course. "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1664", "type": "thread", "title": "Device is marked as bonded but we are being asked to bond so attempting to unbond first", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1664", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1664, "labels": ["question", "device-dexcom-transmitter"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-03-02T20:00:19Z", "closed_at": "2023-01-09T02:10:52Z", "comment_count": 78, "comments": [{"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-02T20:29:24Z", "body": "I have already asked the user if she had an old phone with xDrip or Dexcom app on it.\r\nWaiting for a response."}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-02T21:32:02Z", "body": "I hope that it is another device that is competing for attention and causing the unbonding.  I will update as soon as I hear back.\r\nSo, I am closing this.    \r\nBut, we can still use it to communicate.  So, please let me know if you have any ideas."}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-03T01:02:54Z", "body": "The only other device is the Dexcom receiver. "}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-03-10T21:12:50Z", "body": "Adding to this. \r\n\r\nSamsung Galaxy S21 Ultra\r\nAndroid 11\r\nFeb 1, 2021 Security patch (most updated version)\r\nDexcom G6\r\nAll xdrip settings correct based on posted recommendations\r\nRunning xdrip nightly Feb 11th version (was on most recent with same problem, downgraded to Feb 11th, no change)\r\nHappens daily but randomly.  Cannot find trigger.  Only have Galaxy Watch paired as other device. \r\nI reinstalled xdrip (over existing), \"forgot\" transmitter in System status, asked to repair minutes later.  nothing seems to fix.\r\n<img width=\"350\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30097654/110698274-719e4f80-81bb-11eb-92fb-29aeec6956d7.jpg\" /> <img width=\"350\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30097654/110698284-74994000-81bb-11eb-8dbc-72329739819a.jpg\" />"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-10T21:15:59Z", "body": "Would you please try the latest xDrip release, March 8, 2021?"}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-03-10T21:30:19Z", "body": "will do and report back here"}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-03-11T01:56:39Z", "body": "Same issue after updating to march nightly. "}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2021-03-11T09:20:34Z", "body": "Can you use the log upload when this has happened fairly recently and include some reference in the log upload that I can use to identify yours. Also what firmware version is reported on the G6 status page?"}, {"user": "tswire", "created_at": "2021-03-11T12:08:02Z", "body": "Many disconnects last night. How do I upload the log? "}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-03-11T12:50:10Z", "body": "Go to event logs.\r\nAt the bottom, tap on \"Upload Logs\".\r\n\r\nInclude in the message 1664_tswire\r\n\r\nAlso, please post a screenshot of your system status page here, which shows the firmware version (2.27.2.98)."}], "text": "Device is marked as bonded but we are being asked to bond so attempting to unbond first question device-dexcom-transmitter xDrip version: 2020.11.27\r\n\r\nG6 8K\r\n\r\nMoto G Power (2020)\r\n\r\nIt is Andoid 10, not 11.\r\n\r\nAll xDrip settings are the recommended settings.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\nAfter the user taps on pair in response to the pair request once, the pair request should never appear again.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\nThis is not the frequent pair request.   xDrip has already been updated to November 27, 2020.  \r\nBut, occasionally (once every few days), the device unpairs.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce the behavior:\r\nI cannot reproduce this issue\r\n\r\n![1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/51497406/109706634-3078c080-7b67-11eb-9472-7f7c8182725c.jpg)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n@nickb24    @jamorham \r\nI'm so sorry for tagging you guys.  I have never seen this before.  It is on facebook.  I don't understand why this happens.\r\n I have already asked the user if she had an old phone with xDrip or Dexcom app on it.\r\nWaiting for a response. I hope that it is another device that is competing for attention and causing the unbonding.  I will update as soon as I hear back.\r\nSo, I am closing this.    \r\nBut, we can still use it to communicate.  So, please let me know if you have any ideas. The only other device is the Dexcom receiver.  Adding to this. \r\n\r\nSamsung Galaxy S21 Ultra\r\nAndroid 11\r\nFeb 1, 2021 Security patch (most updated version)\r\nDexcom G6\r\nAll xdrip settings correct based on posted recommendations\r\nRunning xdrip nightly Feb 11th version (was on most recent with same problem, downgraded to Feb 11th, no change)\r\nHappens daily but randomly.  Cannot find trigger.  Only have Galaxy Watch paired as other device. \r\nI reinstalled xdrip (over existing), \"forgot\" transmitter in System status, asked to repair minutes later.  nothing seems to fix.\r\n<img width=\"350\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30097654/110698274-719e4f80-81bb-11eb-92fb-29aeec6956d7.jpg\" /> <img width=\"350\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30097654/110698284-74994000-81bb-11eb-8dbc-72329739819a.jpg\" /> Would you please try the latest xDrip release, March 8, 2021? will do and report back here Same issue after updating to march nightly.  Can you use the log upload when this has happened fairly recently and include some reference in the log upload that I can use to identify yours. Also what firmware version is reported on the G6 status page? Many disconnects last night. How do I upload the log?  Go to event logs.\r\nAt the bottom, tap on \"Upload Logs\".\r\n\r\nInclude in the message 1664_tswire\r\n\r\nAlso, please post a screenshot of your system status page here, which shows the firmware version (2.27.2.98)."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-1859", "type": "thread", "title": "XDrip+ is causing audio to pause", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1859", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1859, "labels": ["bluetooth"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2021-10-21T12:47:06Z", "closed_at": "2021-10-26T20:56:19Z", "comment_count": 47, "comments": [{"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-10-21T13:55:00Z", "body": "Another user, on facebook, has experienced the same, with Pixel 4a, after having updated to Android 12.\r\nHe then switched to the Dexcom app, on the same phone, and the issue persisted.  "}, {"user": "BenMc19", "created_at": "2021-10-21T17:38:15Z", "body": "Came here to make this post, glad (I guess?) to see that it's not just me.  Just so weird how this just started happening a few days ago.  Nothing has been updated on my phone's side (Samsung S20 FE, Android 11, September 1, 2021 security patch) or on the Xdrip side.  Very strange."}, {"user": "abehrens", "created_at": "2021-10-21T18:59:01Z", "body": "Seeing the same behavior on my pixel 5.  Tried silencing all notifications for the app and it didn't do the trick.  Does not occur when playing from the speaker, only via bluetooth.   (Edit) Security patch is from October 5 2021, xdrip version 17cbf0-2021.03.08"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2021-10-21T19:16:07Z", "body": "@BenMc19 @abehrens and anyone else experiencing this, would you please include what Android version you have experienced this on?"}, {"user": "abehrens", "created_at": "2021-10-21T19:20:27Z", "body": "Happened on Android 11, just updated to 12 and same behavior."}, {"user": "DaveGee281", "created_at": "2021-10-22T00:04:53Z", "body": "It started happening to me on a Samsung Galaxy S8+ which uses Android 9. \r\n\r\nFor the past 2 weeks, my Bluetooth ear buds disconnect every 5 minutes when Xdrip+ connects to the Dexcom transmitter and downloads BG data from the transmitter to the phone. I need to manually restart the earbuds. \r\nI'm using Xdrip version 17cbcf0=2021.03.08."}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2021-10-22T05:01:57Z", "body": "> The problem persists after uninstalling xDrip+ and installing the native Dexcom app. Prior to installing the Dexcom app I forgot the transmitter in the Bluetooth settings and reboot the phone.\r\n\r\nThis indicates a bug in the Bluetooth stack since at least two apps are affected."}, {"user": "tolot27", "created_at": "2021-10-22T05:07:58Z", "body": "@abehrens and others: Please edit your previous comments and add your security patch level."}, {"user": "bryanw20", "created_at": "2021-10-22T13:16:41Z", "body": "Thanks for starting this; I haven't made time to comment just yet. I think I'm the other user @Navid200  mentioned.\r\n\r\nI also have a pixel 4a; everything (almost) worked fine on droid 11; but then the phone upgraded to 12.\r\nThe only problem I had on 11 was with my soundcore brand devices AND amzifit band 5. Only those brands would garble the music on every 5min send tot he watch face. If I disabled the watch in xdrip, no more audio problems.  Sorry I deleted that xdrip ver & installed the newest one, but it was the 'offchute' built specific for amazift band 5, a slight change from the miband 5 version.\r\n\r\nSo currently I'm running 17cbcf0-2021.03.08 code 2103081944   NOT running the amazift band 5 (it is connected to the phone's BT; but I can't make it work with this ver of xdrip yet. But I have the audio issuse when it's been 'forgotten' in the phone bt menu)\r\n\r\nAs mentioned when DEX 6 sends it's signal; bt audio is paused, regardless of brand (I tried 3) or app playing audio/video.\r\nI"}, {"user": "BenMc19", "created_at": "2021-10-22T13:24:37Z", "body": "I just don't understand how this could have been affected this past week. I listen to Bluetooth audio everyday, so i can tell you exactly when it started happening. I got the September update nearly 4 weeks ago, and this just started happening beginning of this week. \r\n\r\nSo in theory nothing on my phone changed. Xdrip didn't change. And the transmitter didn't change. You guys are smarter than me with this stuff but just doesn't make sense. If I can offer any other info to help just let me know. "}], "text": "XDrip+ is causing audio to pause bluetooth XDrip+ version c98a3c4-2021.10.17 is causing audio to pause when playing music/podcasts over Bluetooth.\r\n\r\nThe issue happens when the connection is made with the transmitter every 5 minutes; I've been able to reproduce it will all of my Bluetooth headphones and car Bluetooth.\r\n\r\nI am using a Pixel 4a on Android 12 with a G6 transmitter.\r\n\r\nThe issue was present on Android 11 with XDrip+ version c98a3c4-2021.10.17 too.  I tried the previous nightly and the issue did not resolve itself.  This issue was not present previously.\r\n\r\nI've tried resetting all Bluetooth devices and deleting and reinstalling xDrip+.  I have submitted logs.\r\n\r\nThe problem persists after uninstalling xDrip+ and installing the native Dexcom app.  Prior to installing the Dexcom app I forgot the transmitter in the Bluetooth settings and reboot the phone.\r\n\r\nThank you for looking into this.\r\n\r\nUPDATE: The issue seems to be coming for the Roku app.  Deleting the Roku app resolves the issue. Another user, on facebook, has experienced the same, with Pixel 4a, after having updated to Android 12.\r\nHe then switched to the Dexcom app, on the same phone, and the issue persisted.   Came here to make this post, glad (I guess?) to see that it's not just me.  Just so weird how this just started happening a few days ago.  Nothing has been updated on my phone's side (Samsung S20 FE, Android 11, September 1, 2021 security patch) or on the Xdrip side.  Very strange. Seeing the same behavior on my pixel 5.  Tried silencing all notifications for the app and it didn't do the trick.  Does not occur when playing from the speaker, only via bluetooth.   (Edit) Security patch is from October 5 2021, xdrip version 17cbf0-2021.03.08 @BenMc19 @abehrens and anyone else experiencing this, would you please include what Android version you have experienced this on? Happened on Android 11, just updated to 12 and same behavior. It started happening to me on a Samsung Galaxy S8+ which uses Android 9. \r\n\r\nFor the past 2 weeks, my Bluetooth ear buds disconnect every 5 minutes when Xdrip+ connects to the Dexcom transmitter and downloads BG data from the transmitter to the phone. I need to manually restart the earbuds. \r\nI'm using Xdrip version 17cbcf0=2021.03.08. > The problem persists after uninstalling xDrip+ and installing the native Dexcom app. Prior to installing the Dexcom app I forgot the transmitter in the Bluetooth settings and reboot the phone.\r\n\r\nThis indicates a bug in the Bluetooth stack since at least two apps are affected. @abehrens and others: Please edit your previous comments and add your security patch level. Thanks for starting this; I haven't made time to comment just yet. I think I'm the other user @Navid200  mentioned.\r\n\r\nI also have a pixel 4a; everything (almost) worked fine on droid 11; but then the phone upgraded to 12.\r\nThe only problem I had on 11 was with my soundcore brand devices AND amzifit band 5. Only those brands would garble the music on every 5min send tot he watch face. If I disabled the watch in xdrip, no more audio problems.  Sorry I deleted that xdrip ver & installed the newest one, but it was the 'offchute' built specific for amazift band 5, a slight change from the miband 5 version.\r\n\r\nSo currently I'm running 17cbcf0-2021.03.08 code 2103081944   NOT running the amazift band 5 (it is connected to the phone's BT; but I can't make it work with this ver of xdrip yet. But I have the audio issuse when it's been 'forgotten' in the phone bt menu)\r\n\r\nAs mentioned when DEX 6 sends it's signal; bt audio is paused, regardless of brand (I tried 3) or app playing audio/video.\r\nI I just don't understand how this could have been affected this past week. I listen to Bluetooth audio everyday, so i can tell you exactly when it started happening. I got the September update nearly 4 weeks ago, and this just started happening beginning of this week. \r\n\r\nSo in theory nothing on my phone changed. Xdrip didn't change. And the transmitter didn't change. You guys are smarter than me with this stuff but just doesn't make sense. If I can offer any other info to help just let me know. "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-222", "type": "thread", "title": "Feature Request: Show full Glucose Reading in Notification bar", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/222", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 222, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2017-11-30T11:41:10Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-22T17:04:54Z", "comment_count": 55, "comments": [{"user": "gitanO0", "created_at": "2017-12-01T07:17:13Z", "body": "+1"}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2017-12-01T07:36:13Z", "body": "When I last looked at it, google removed the possibility to add text there (at least for non-system apps) - and also the possibility to add dynamically rendered icons. Too many apps where pushing advertisement there, without the possibility for the user to know what app it was :/\r\nNewer versions of Android might get (have gotten) the possibility to do that again?\r\n\r\nWhat apps then usually did was exchanging the icon. Having a range from 40 to 400, this would mean more than 360 icons for mg/dl alone. Additionally those for mmol/l."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2017-12-01T09:05:20Z", "body": "Even if it is possible to dynamically render the icon I believe its going to be limited to a tiny space and getting 3 digits in there is going to pretty difficult and for it to be readable."}, {"user": "gitanO0", "created_at": "2017-12-01T18:50:37Z", "body": "What about some sort of middle ground... perhaps three or four icons:  red:  low, green:  in range, yellow: high... or some such thing."}, {"user": "micro17", "created_at": "2017-12-02T11:38:17Z", "body": "Great to see that my suggetion receives attention.Thanks for this!\r\n\r\nIm running the Pixel 2 XL with Android Oreo. Im not sure how AccuBattery implements this feature as im not really an expert in that regard...\r\n\r\n\r\nPerhaps ill photoshop a mockup to see if 3 digits would be feasible. But Im hopeful that it would fit the space as accubattery uses 2 digits + the circle.\r\n\r\nThe color solution depends on the android version youre running. From my experience Android Oreo converts every notification with colored icons to b/w. "}, {"user": "gitanO0", "created_at": "2017-12-04T17:27:10Z", "body": "Well... I guess the takeaway here is that \"more information is better\".  Currently the status bar icon of a static xdrip symbol brings very little to no \"information\" value.  There are certainly tons of apps, such as this weather app I use that successfully show dynamic info in that space... such as the current temp (which in \"f\" can range from -xx to +xxx temps).  So, it certainly is possible.  The heartache seems to be on the implementation side... all the work to make icons with each BG value.  So, the bottom line is... is the value gained by having a dynamic status bar icon greater than the work involved?  I'd certainly volunteer my time in the grunt work of creating those BG png files.  We'd be looking at what... Maybe an \"L\" symbol for 40 and lower... then 41 -> 300 or so?  Then an \"H\" for high?"}, {"user": "Klaus3d3", "created_at": "2017-12-06T11:19:20Z", "body": "Hi there,\r\n\r\nmy guess is that a dynamic xdrip symbol will also bring that information on an always on display wich ist a feature i'd really like.\r\nTo bring the BG-Level on the AOD it would maybe also possible use to the static note, wich you can put on the AOD. If this is a string, wich is somewhere found in the systems settings, it should be possible to dynamize it. Or maybe, similar to gitanO0s request, changing the color of the AOD Clock should be easely done and should work for all AOD generations, i guess. "}, {"user": "TheDonDan", "created_at": "2018-01-05T23:03:37Z", "body": "+1"}, {"user": "Klaus3d3", "created_at": "2018-01-29T13:27:25Z", "body": "Hi there, i think this should'nt be any problem at all with since Marshmallow seems to accept Text as Icon. I made myself an app with Tasker and autonotification to show the value in the notification bar and on AOD. So it should'nt be any problem to do this directly from XDrip+.\r\nSee: https://www.google.de/amp/s/amp.reddit.com/r/tasker/comments/4sarl0/dev_autonotification_updates_full_status_bar_icon/"}, {"user": "Klaus3d3", "created_at": "2018-02-08T15:53:39Z", "body": "@jamorham \r\n@AdrianLxM \r\n\r\nfrom api 23 + i had luck with this code for a 2 -3 character long String as notification icon.\r\nThe Textsize will be dynamicly changed to fit into the icon.\r\n\r\nString text =\"99\";\r\n\r\n        public void ClickButton (View view) {\r\n        Paint paint = new Paint();\r\n        Integer width = (int) getResources().getDimension(android.R.dimen.notification_large_icon_width);\r\n        Integer height = (int) getResources().getDimension(android.R.dimen.notification_large_icon_height);\r\n        paint.setStyle(Paint.Style.FILL);\r\n        paint.setColor(Color.WHITE);\r\n        paint.setAntiAlias(true);\r\n        paint.setTypeface(Typeface.MONOSPACE);\r\n        paint.setTextAlign(Paint.Align.LEFT);\r\n        paint.setTextSize(16);\r\n        Rect bounds = new Rect();\r\n        paint.getTextBounds(text, 0, text.length(), bounds);\r\n        float textsize = 16 * width / bounds.width();\r\n        paint.setTextSize(textsize);\r\n        Bitmap bitmap = Bitmap.createBitmap(width, height, "}], "text": "Feature Request: Show full Glucose Reading in Notification bar  Hi,\r\n\r\nfirst I want to thank all contributors for this great app! Makes my life with Type 1 a lot easier.\r\n\r\nHope its OK to request a feature this way.\r\n\r\nI have an application named AccuBattery which always shows the battey percentage as an Notification bar Icon. I would love to see this implemented with the current BG Reading.\r\n\r\nThanks Max\r\n\r\n![screenshot_20171130-122221_li 2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8474446/33429049-83f13818-d5cb-11e7-8c92-a47518c9887d.jpg)\r\n\r\n +1 When I last looked at it, google removed the possibility to add text there (at least for non-system apps) - and also the possibility to add dynamically rendered icons. Too many apps where pushing advertisement there, without the possibility for the user to know what app it was :/\r\nNewer versions of Android might get (have gotten) the possibility to do that again?\r\n\r\nWhat apps then usually did was exchanging the icon. Having a range from 40 to 400, this would mean more than 360 icons for mg/dl alone. Additionally those for mmol/l. Even if it is possible to dynamically render the icon I believe its going to be limited to a tiny space and getting 3 digits in there is going to pretty difficult and for it to be readable. What about some sort of middle ground... perhaps three or four icons:  red:  low, green:  in range, yellow: high... or some such thing. Great to see that my suggetion receives attention.Thanks for this!\r\n\r\nIm running the Pixel 2 XL with Android Oreo. Im not sure how AccuBattery implements this feature as im not really an expert in that regard...\r\n\r\n\r\nPerhaps ill photoshop a mockup to see if 3 digits would be feasible. But Im hopeful that it would fit the space as accubattery uses 2 digits + the circle.\r\n\r\nThe color solution depends on the android version youre running. From my experience Android Oreo converts every notification with colored icons to b/w.  Well... I guess the takeaway here is that \"more information is better\".  Currently the status bar icon of a static xdrip symbol brings very little to no \"information\" value.  There are certainly tons of apps, such as this weather app I use that successfully show dynamic info in that space... such as the current temp (which in \"f\" can range from -xx to +xxx temps).  So, it certainly is possible.  The heartache seems to be on the implementation side... all the work to make icons with each BG value.  So, the bottom line is... is the value gained by having a dynamic status bar icon greater than the work involved?  I'd certainly volunteer my time in the grunt work of creating those BG png files.  We'd be looking at what... Maybe an \"L\" symbol for 40 and lower... then 41 -> 300 or so?  Then an \"H\" for high? Hi there,\r\n\r\nmy guess is that a dynamic xdrip symbol will also bring that information on an always on display wich ist a feature i'd really like.\r\nTo bring the BG-Level on the AOD it would maybe also possible use to the static note, wich you can put on the AOD. If this is a string, wich is somewhere found in the systems settings, it should be possible to dynamize it. Or maybe, similar to gitanO0s request, changing the color of the AOD Clock should be easely done and should work for all AOD generations, i guess.  +1 Hi there, i think this should'nt be any problem at all with since Marshmallow seems to accept Text as Icon. I made myself an app with Tasker and autonotification to show the value in the notification bar and on AOD. So it should'nt be any problem to do this directly from XDrip+.\r\nSee: https://www.google.de/amp/s/amp.reddit.com/r/tasker/comments/4sarl0/dev_autonotification_updates_full_status_bar_icon/ @jamorham \r\n@AdrianLxM \r\n\r\nfrom api 23 + i had luck with this code for a 2 -3 character long String as notification icon.\r\nThe Textsize will be dynamicly changed to fit into the icon.\r\n\r\nString text =\"99\";\r\n\r\n        public void ClickButton (View view) {\r\n        Paint paint = new Paint();\r\n        Integer width = (int) getResources().getDimension(android.R.dimen.notification_large_icon_width);\r\n        Integer height = (int) getResources().getDimension(android.R.dimen.notification_large_icon_height);\r\n        paint.setStyle(Paint.Style.FILL);\r\n        paint.setColor(Color.WHITE);\r\n        paint.setAntiAlias(true);\r\n        paint.setTypeface(Typeface.MONOSPACE);\r\n        paint.setTextAlign(Paint.Align.LEFT);\r\n        paint.setTextSize(16);\r\n        Rect bounds = new Rect();\r\n        paint.getTextBounds(text, 0, text.length(), bounds);\r\n        float textsize = 16 * width / bounds.width();\r\n        paint.setTextSize(textsize);\r\n        Bitmap bitmap = Bitmap.createBitmap(width, height, "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-3582", "type": "thread", "title": "xDrip followers sync feature dead after Google FCM API removed on 22.07.2024", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3582", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3582, "labels": ["sync"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2024-07-23T09:18:04Z", "closed_at": "2024-09-30T11:48:50Z", "comment_count": 48, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2024-07-23T10:58:45Z", "body": "This is being worked on right now."}, {"user": "ireneusz-ptak", "created_at": "2024-07-23T11:01:08Z", "body": "Thanks, can you provide any estimates? Because this time #aLotOfPeopleAreWaiting ;)"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2024-07-23T11:08:13Z", "body": "@ireneusz-ptak jamorham stated already in the discussion that he was working on it.\r\nYet, you went ahead and opened this issue.\r\nHe then stated here that he was working on it.  \r\n\r\nThanks for reporting the underlying root cause.  You have helped us a lot by doing that.\r\nThank you so much.\r\n\r\nCan I ask you to please do us a favor?\r\nWould you please not ask for a schedule?\r\n\r\nYou don't know how grateful I am to you for having reported the root cause.  But, please remember that jamorham is a volunteer as well.   \r\n\r\nIf he needs help, I am available to give him a hand.   \r\nI know that this is critical.  I am not denying that.  What we need now is patience on the user part so that we can focus on the problem and fix it.\r\nThanks"}, {"user": "ireneusz-ptak", "created_at": "2024-07-23T11:20:29Z", "body": "> @ireneusz-ptak jamorham stated already in the discussion that he was working on it. Yet, you went ahead and opened this issue.\r\n\r\nNo, I didn't - the issue was opened before. And I did it because you said the issue was on Google side and we just need to wait for it to work.\r\n\r\n> Can I ask you to please do us a favor? Would you please not ask for a schedule?\r\n\r\nI'm not asking for a schedule, I know how such investigations work, I did at lot of them.\r\n \r\n> But, please remember that jamorham is a volunteer as well.\r\n\r\nYep, me too.\r\n\r\n> If he needs help, I am available to give him a hand. I know that this is critical. I am not denying that. What we need now is patience on the user part so that we can focus on the problem and fix it. Thanks\r\n\r\nI know it's an open source project that relies on volunteer work, but there's responsibility with that. A lot of people are using this feature to monitor their kids remotely (especially during vacation time). I think there's nothing wrong to ask if w"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2024-07-23T11:23:29Z", "body": "I would like to have something out today but that is a very tight time schedule and needs plenty of things to go right but it is my number 1 priority and I recognise how important the follower feature is."}, {"user": "ireneusz-ptak", "created_at": "2024-07-23T11:26:20Z", "body": "> I would like to have something out today but that is a very tight time schedule and needs plenty of things to go right but it is my number 1 priority and I recognise how important the follower feature is.\r\n\r\nThanks, fingers crossed."}, {"user": "tloczekt", "created_at": "2024-07-23T12:08:34Z", "body": "maybe this is a temporary (not elegant) solution ?\r\n![obraz](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2de212ff-9bdf-4874-a0fc-ec5830dbb566)\r\n\r\n![obraz](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd457c3d-70c0-465b-bf58-ca42c8d61c53)\r\n\r\n\r\nFCM deprecation extension request\r\n\r\nFirebase can be individually extended for a specific time.\r\nI hope this way we can buy some time for modification."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2024-07-23T12:53:42Z", "body": "Yes I have already requested an extension but they may not be inclined to help us."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2024-07-23T13:32:45Z", "body": "I am making good progress and the chance of an update today is increasing."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2024-07-23T16:36:40Z", "body": "There is a new nightly available which is intended to resolve this issue. Please test. thanks"}], "text": "xDrip followers sync feature dead after Google FCM API removed on 22.07.2024 sync I know, I didn't consult the developers first, but that's not a \"bug\", just a major f*ck up... so I'm just trying to get @jamorham attention :)\r\n\r\n### Subject of the issue\r\nGoogle FCM old API was removed yesterday causing major issue for all xdrip followers. It seems it was announced a year ago, but nothing was done in this time.\r\nhttps://firebase.google.com/support/faq#deprecated-api-shutdown\r\n\r\nNot an mobile expert but I really hope that Firebase SDK upgrade (15.0.0 -> 24.0.0) in xDrip should be enough to fix the problem.\r\n\r\n### Your environment\r\nDoesn't matter - all apps using the FCM messaging API are affected.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\nFollowers working like two days ago\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\nCommunication between master and followers broken using default sync.\r\n This is being worked on right now. Thanks, can you provide any estimates? Because this time #aLotOfPeopleAreWaiting ;) @ireneusz-ptak jamorham stated already in the discussion that he was working on it.\r\nYet, you went ahead and opened this issue.\r\nHe then stated here that he was working on it.  \r\n\r\nThanks for reporting the underlying root cause.  You have helped us a lot by doing that.\r\nThank you so much.\r\n\r\nCan I ask you to please do us a favor?\r\nWould you please not ask for a schedule?\r\n\r\nYou don't know how grateful I am to you for having reported the root cause.  But, please remember that jamorham is a volunteer as well.   \r\n\r\nIf he needs help, I am available to give him a hand.   \r\nI know that this is critical.  I am not denying that.  What we need now is patience on the user part so that we can focus on the problem and fix it.\r\nThanks > @ireneusz-ptak jamorham stated already in the discussion that he was working on it. Yet, you went ahead and opened this issue.\r\n\r\nNo, I didn't - the issue was opened before. And I did it because you said the issue was on Google side and we just need to wait for it to work.\r\n\r\n> Can I ask you to please do us a favor? Would you please not ask for a schedule?\r\n\r\nI'm not asking for a schedule, I know how such investigations work, I did at lot of them.\r\n \r\n> But, please remember that jamorham is a volunteer as well.\r\n\r\nYep, me too.\r\n\r\n> If he needs help, I am available to give him a hand. I know that this is critical. I am not denying that. What we need now is patience on the user part so that we can focus on the problem and fix it. Thanks\r\n\r\nI know it's an open source project that relies on volunteer work, but there's responsibility with that. A lot of people are using this feature to monitor their kids remotely (especially during vacation time). I think there's nothing wrong to ask if w I would like to have something out today but that is a very tight time schedule and needs plenty of things to go right but it is my number 1 priority and I recognise how important the follower feature is. > I would like to have something out today but that is a very tight time schedule and needs plenty of things to go right but it is my number 1 priority and I recognise how important the follower feature is.\r\n\r\nThanks, fingers crossed. maybe this is a temporary (not elegant) solution ?\r\n![obraz](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2de212ff-9bdf-4874-a0fc-ec5830dbb566)\r\n\r\n![obraz](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd457c3d-70c0-465b-bf58-ca42c8d61c53)\r\n\r\n\r\nFCM deprecation extension request\r\n\r\nFirebase can be individually extended for a specific time.\r\nI hope this way we can buy some time for modification. Yes I have already requested an extension but they may not be inclined to help us. I am making good progress and the chance of an update today is increasing. There is a new nightly available which is intended to resolve this issue. Please test. thanks"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-3688", "type": "thread", "title": "xDrip does not recognise new G7 sensor, despite correct code, and it working on Tandem T-slim pump", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3688", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3688, "labels": ["invalid"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2024-09-28T07:43:55Z", "closed_at": "2024-09-28T10:54:19Z", "comment_count": 7, "comments": [{"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2024-09-28T10:54:19Z", "body": "I think I asked you to bring this to GitHub.\r\nIf yes, thanks for doing it.\r\nBut, I didn't ask you to convert it to an issue.\r\nPlease let it be a discussion. If it turns out that needs to be converted to an issue, it will be."}], "text": "xDrip does not recognise new G7 sensor, despite correct code, and it working on Tandem T-slim pump invalid ### Discussed in https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/discussions/3687\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **shrewsdog** September 28, 2024</sup>\r\nIssue is xDrip not recognising a new sensor (which is working on Tandem T-Slim pump).  System Status has correct TX ID for new sensor, but transmitter days and battery voltages are clearly for the old transmitter as days are 10, and voltage a 280 and b 176. Data source is shown as G6/G7/1/1+ Transmitter, and xDrip version is dfcbe80-20240917.  Phone is Motorola Moto g(6) Play.\r\n\r\nCatalogue of errors by me.  Had G7 on day nine.  Had been erratic, so inserted new one early.  Then realised I needed to stop the first one.  Used stop sensor which stopped both (at this point I believed I had not paired sensor 2).  Then removed the 2 sensor TXs from bluetooth list on my phone and rebooted.  Inserted sensor 3, paired it with pump which is receiving data correctly.  New TX ID on phone is correct, but the status page is showing the old day nine sensor and battery data, and the main page records sensor error and 'Ends 7.48' tomorrow.  I opted to put an incorrect TX ID in Xdrip, allowed it to try to connect, and when it failed reinputted the correct TX, but no change.\r\n\r\nBoth the expiring sensor and its replacement have been sat in microwave for hours.  Applicator code for new sensor is correct. \r\n\r\nIt is as though the tx data for the first sensor is 'locked' on the phone.  </div> I think I asked you to bring this to GitHub.\r\nIf yes, thanks for doing it.\r\nBut, I didn't ask you to convert it to an issue.\r\nPlease let it be a discussion. If it turns out that needs to be converted to an issue, it will be."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-440", "type": "thread", "title": "Miaomiao & Samsung connection", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/440", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 440, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-05-15T09:17:34Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-25T17:25:48Z", "comment_count": 83, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-05-15T12:37:18Z", "body": "Which xDrip version are you using? See `System Status` menu item for details.\r\n\r\nThe Galaxy S8 is reported to work well with miaomiao and pairing is not normally ever done with it."}, {"user": "Felix2020", "created_at": "2018-05-15T14:30:41Z", "body": "I tried few versions in result with the same problem. \r\nLast version: 0acd72c-2018.05.11\r\nCode: 1805112149\r\nDowngradable to: 1603091400"}, {"user": "simonsis1002", "created_at": "2018-05-25T21:24:58Z", "body": "Hello, i have a similar Problem with damsung galaxy s5 and rhe miaimiao. ErrorLog says always: checksum failed. After some time I have all readings... seems to be a Bluetooth Setting Problem...\r\nCan someone help me?\r\nXdrip+ Version:3534dc9-2018.05.21"}, {"user": "simonsis1002", "created_at": "2018-05-26T09:34:34Z", "body": "Which Datasource is correct for the miaomiao?libre bluetooth?"}, {"user": "hjortling", "created_at": "2018-05-27T10:33:04Z", "body": "I'm also now experiencing similar issues .\r\nWorked without any issues for almost 5 days, after that the connection is very unstable. \r\n\r\nHave tried to reboot phone, turn of and on Bluetooth, restarting collector, forgetting device, charging the phone and MiaoMiao etc. \r\nSelecting miaomiao in Bluetooth scan view , results in message that device is connecting but no connection is created.\r\nOnce when I tried to connect to the MiaoMiao using the phone native bluetooth view, it said that the connection was refused, but then xDrip+ got a connection and withheld i for around eight hours. Then back to the initial issue, but using native connection trick did not work any more.\r\nAlso sent logs from xDrip+  \r\n\r\nRunning \r\nxDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21, code 1805211807, on a Samsung S8 (SM-G950F),    \r\n\r\n![screenshot_20180527-093242_xdrip](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8505344/40583912-fc31d640-6197-11e8-9616-2fb165aaad8b.jpg)\r\n\r\nAndroid version 8.0.0:\r\n![screenshot_20180527-102642_set"}, {"user": "hjortling", "created_at": "2018-05-27T16:20:23Z", "body": "Additional Info to previous comment \r\nInstalled Spike on an old iPhone 5S, and it found and connected to the MiaoMiao directly, no need to reset the MiaoMiao. Yet to see if it maintains connection though. Don't know if that adds any extra info, but I thought I would add it anyway :)"}, {"user": "hjortling", "created_at": "2018-05-29T19:34:13Z", "body": "Maybe I am spamming...but here is some more info...\r\nUninstalled and reinstalled xDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21, with no luck.\r\nDid a factory reset on the phone and reinstalled xDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21 and TADA!!!, suddenly everything was working again, did calibration and got readings. Set up Nightscout REST Url. wich also worked. Then I continued reinstalling some apps: Libre Link, Samsung Pay, BankID (a swedish identification app) and Swish (a swedish mobile money transfer app), then i realized that xDrip+ was not able to read values anymore, i got values for about 35 minutes... \r\nTried to do all the tricks, and at the end I tried to stop and restart the sensor, then I saw that the 'waiting for initial data' dialog was a bit different.\r\nWhen doing the initial setup, the dialog said  'Receiving Data from Tomato Collector' while when doing the sensor stop, start it said 'Receiving Data from LimiTTer Collector',\r\n could that mean anything?\r\nInitial:\r\n![screenshot_collector_tomato"}, {"user": "smashburn", "created_at": "2018-05-30T17:27:29Z", "body": "Same thing for me on S9.  Very unstable Bluetooth connection.  Refuses to even connect now"}, {"user": "KennyZR", "created_at": "2018-05-31T12:07:19Z", "body": "Same issue here on S8+ , I got it working 1 time for 4 days, but now it refuses to connect. Galaxy S7 Edge works flawlessly and connects instantly. "}, {"user": "mpifferi", "created_at": "2018-06-07T07:42:03Z", "body": "I have the same problem with S7 after upgrade to Oreo. I am not able to have Connected in the connection status."}], "text": "Miaomiao & Samsung connection  When using the miaomiao reader on a Samsung S8, xDrip won't automatically update readings until a new pairing request is requested in the phones bluetooth settings. \r\n\r\nHave given xDrip as many privileges as I can but still won't update any readings following the initial backlog until a new pairing is requested. Which xDrip version are you using? See `System Status` menu item for details.\r\n\r\nThe Galaxy S8 is reported to work well with miaomiao and pairing is not normally ever done with it. I tried few versions in result with the same problem. \r\nLast version: 0acd72c-2018.05.11\r\nCode: 1805112149\r\nDowngradable to: 1603091400 Hello, i have a similar Problem with damsung galaxy s5 and rhe miaimiao. ErrorLog says always: checksum failed. After some time I have all readings... seems to be a Bluetooth Setting Problem...\r\nCan someone help me?\r\nXdrip+ Version:3534dc9-2018.05.21 Which Datasource is correct for the miaomiao?libre bluetooth? I'm also now experiencing similar issues .\r\nWorked without any issues for almost 5 days, after that the connection is very unstable. \r\n\r\nHave tried to reboot phone, turn of and on Bluetooth, restarting collector, forgetting device, charging the phone and MiaoMiao etc. \r\nSelecting miaomiao in Bluetooth scan view , results in message that device is connecting but no connection is created.\r\nOnce when I tried to connect to the MiaoMiao using the phone native bluetooth view, it said that the connection was refused, but then xDrip+ got a connection and withheld i for around eight hours. Then back to the initial issue, but using native connection trick did not work any more.\r\nAlso sent logs from xDrip+  \r\n\r\nRunning \r\nxDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21, code 1805211807, on a Samsung S8 (SM-G950F),    \r\n\r\n![screenshot_20180527-093242_xdrip](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8505344/40583912-fc31d640-6197-11e8-9616-2fb165aaad8b.jpg)\r\n\r\nAndroid version 8.0.0:\r\n![screenshot_20180527-102642_set Additional Info to previous comment \r\nInstalled Spike on an old iPhone 5S, and it found and connected to the MiaoMiao directly, no need to reset the MiaoMiao. Yet to see if it maintains connection though. Don't know if that adds any extra info, but I thought I would add it anyway :) Maybe I am spamming...but here is some more info...\r\nUninstalled and reinstalled xDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21, with no luck.\r\nDid a factory reset on the phone and reinstalled xDrip plus: 3534dc9-2018.05.21 and TADA!!!, suddenly everything was working again, did calibration and got readings. Set up Nightscout REST Url. wich also worked. Then I continued reinstalling some apps: Libre Link, Samsung Pay, BankID (a swedish identification app) and Swish (a swedish mobile money transfer app), then i realized that xDrip+ was not able to read values anymore, i got values for about 35 minutes... \r\nTried to do all the tricks, and at the end I tried to stop and restart the sensor, then I saw that the 'waiting for initial data' dialog was a bit different.\r\nWhen doing the initial setup, the dialog said  'Receiving Data from Tomato Collector' while when doing the sensor stop, start it said 'Receiving Data from LimiTTer Collector',\r\n could that mean anything?\r\nInitial:\r\n![screenshot_collector_tomato Same thing for me on S9.  Very unstable Bluetooth connection.  Refuses to even connect now Same issue here on S8+ , I got it working 1 time for 4 days, but now it refuses to connect. Galaxy S7 Edge works flawlessly and connects instantly.  I have the same problem with S7 after upgrade to Oreo. I am not able to have Connected in the connection status."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-4442", "type": "thread", "title": "Dexcom G7 15 day sensor, backfill not working.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/4442", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 4442, "labels": ["device-dexcom"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2026-03-13T16:42:29Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-06T22:03:06Z", "comment_count": 9, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2026-03-27T13:14:54Z", "body": "I think this should be resolved in today's nightly. Please test and let me know. Thanks."}, {"user": "rICTx-T1D", "created_at": "2026-03-28T07:57:28Z", "body": "Backfilling also not working on new g7 sensor from manufactured date after 2025-12 with FW version: 32.192.109.40,  see #4471 "}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2026-03-28T08:23:46Z", "body": "@rICTx-T1D have you tried the latest nightly build?"}, {"user": "rICTx-T1D", "created_at": "2026-03-29T05:20:32Z", "body": "@jamorham today, I update last nightly and it should be fixed... Because timezone/timeshift to Asia, Iam delayed at newest version :)"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2026-03-30T17:19:22Z", "body": "@rICTx-T1D I'm sorry I don't really understand your comment. Do you know if the fix is working now?"}, {"user": "rICTx-T1D", "created_at": "2026-03-31T13:55:09Z", "body": "@jamorham yes it is fixed"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2026-04-01T07:54:49Z", "body": "@billymild can you also confirm the fix is working? thanks"}, {"user": "Navid200", "created_at": "2026-04-06T22:03:06Z", "body": "Update to any Nightly release after 2026.04.01 and this should be working fine."}], "text": "Dexcom G7 15 day sensor, backfill not working. device-dexcom I'm on the new Dexcom G7 15 day sensor. xDrip nightly build works with the sensors and can receive data. Warmup worked perfectly as well. \r\n\r\nI tried using the official dexcom app and it does backfill data correctly. I can provide logs or other data as needed. Navid Fo did send me a test app, but I have not installed it yet. I use xDrip with AAPS for looping.\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @billymild in https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/discussions/4417_ I think this should be resolved in today's nightly. Please test and let me know. Thanks. Backfilling also not working on new g7 sensor from manufactured date after 2025-12 with FW version: 32.192.109.40,  see #4471  @rICTx-T1D have you tried the latest nightly build? @jamorham today, I update last nightly and it should be fixed... Because timezone/timeshift to Asia, Iam delayed at newest version :) @rICTx-T1D I'm sorry I don't really understand your comment. Do you know if the fix is working now? @jamorham yes it is fixed @billymild can you also confirm the fix is working? thanks Update to any Nightly release after 2026.04.01 and this should be working fine."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-504", "type": "thread", "title": "Add support for Medtrum A6 CGM", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/504", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 504, "labels": ["enhancement", "device-medtrum"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-07-13T10:29:00Z", "closed_at": "2021-08-07T02:09:40Z", "comment_count": 62, "comments": [{"user": "Menor3", "created_at": "2018-07-15T17:28:29Z", "body": "I am down to test it"}, {"user": "StuArnold", "created_at": "2018-07-16T14:00:13Z", "body": "My daughter should be getting a Medtrum in the next few weeks. If it happens will be interested and happy to test.\r\n\r\n "}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-07-18T14:43:53Z", "body": "I am making good progress with this. I will let you know when I have anything to test."}, {"user": "Menor3", "created_at": "2018-07-18T14:54:17Z", "body": "Nice one, can't wait to test it out. The medtrum application is pretty bad and it drains the battery like CRAZY."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-07-19T13:34:46Z", "body": "Ok, I think I have a lot of stuff working now. I'm getting data from the sensor. We have the option to use the A6 native algorithm or the xDrip algorithm. \r\n\r\nI'm going to make it an option which to show as the primary number and then plot the alternate algorithm as a trace behind it so we can work out which may be the most useful. There may need some tuning to work properly with xDrip calibration algorithm which as a lot of dex style assumptions in it."}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-07-19T16:40:48Z", "body": "Okay the July 19th nightly contains support for the Medtrum A6. Its about 2000+ lines of code so far!\r\n\r\nTo get it to work you should select Medtrum A6 in the hardware data source settings section. Then use `Bluetooth Scan` to identify the A6 transmitter. It isn't always discoverable so you often have to keep clicking scan until it shows up. If its not attached to your body then pop it in the charging doc and after a few seconds it should be visible.  When you see it click on it to select it.\r\n\r\nNow select `Start Sensor` in xDrip (assuming it is connected to a sensor) and you should start to get it gathering data. Use the `System Status` menu item and the `Medtrum` tab to see what the collector is doing.\r\n\r\nOnce you have calibrated it then you can also go back to the `Settings` page and below the `Data Source` you can choose to use either the native algorithm of the A6 or the xDrip algorithm on the raw data. I am very interested to know whether xDrip algorithm works successfully with i"}, {"user": "Menor3", "created_at": "2018-07-19T19:11:20Z", "body": "Where exactly I can download this new version?"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-07-19T20:30:50Z", "body": "@Menor3 switch to the Nightly update channel, see instructions here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/wiki/How-to-get-the-Nightlies-on-Automatic-Update"}, {"user": "Menor3", "created_at": "2018-07-20T12:00:59Z", "body": "Do you think that having xdrip and easysense app open at the same time may cause the transmitter to lost the signal, so I have to restart it?"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-07-20T13:20:14Z", "body": "I think there is a very strong chance that the official app can interfere. You can try force stopping it from the android system settings for apps and see if that can temporarily stop it running while you test xDrip. "}], "text": "Add support for Medtrum A6 CGM enhancement device-medtrum This work is in progress now.\r\n\r\nThis ticket replaces: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/408\r\n\r\n@kimbersdiabetic @dimis28 @tim2000s @sulkaharo if you know of any interested parties who would be able to test the support when it is ready, it would be great if they could make themselves known here. I am down to test it My daughter should be getting a Medtrum in the next few weeks. If it happens will be interested and happy to test.\r\n\r\n  I am making good progress with this. I will let you know when I have anything to test. Nice one, can't wait to test it out. The medtrum application is pretty bad and it drains the battery like CRAZY. Ok, I think I have a lot of stuff working now. I'm getting data from the sensor. We have the option to use the A6 native algorithm or the xDrip algorithm. \r\n\r\nI'm going to make it an option which to show as the primary number and then plot the alternate algorithm as a trace behind it so we can work out which may be the most useful. There may need some tuning to work properly with xDrip calibration algorithm which as a lot of dex style assumptions in it. Okay the July 19th nightly contains support for the Medtrum A6. Its about 2000+ lines of code so far!\r\n\r\nTo get it to work you should select Medtrum A6 in the hardware data source settings section. Then use `Bluetooth Scan` to identify the A6 transmitter. It isn't always discoverable so you often have to keep clicking scan until it shows up. If its not attached to your body then pop it in the charging doc and after a few seconds it should be visible.  When you see it click on it to select it.\r\n\r\nNow select `Start Sensor` in xDrip (assuming it is connected to a sensor) and you should start to get it gathering data. Use the `System Status` menu item and the `Medtrum` tab to see what the collector is doing.\r\n\r\nOnce you have calibrated it then you can also go back to the `Settings` page and below the `Data Source` you can choose to use either the native algorithm of the A6 or the xDrip algorithm on the raw data. I am very interested to know whether xDrip algorithm works successfully with i Where exactly I can download this new version? @Menor3 switch to the Nightly update channel, see instructions here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/wiki/How-to-get-the-Nightlies-on-Automatic-Update Do you think that having xdrip and easysense app open at the same time may cause the transmitter to lost the signal, so I have to restart it? I think there is a very strong chance that the official app can interfere. You can try force stopping it from the android system settings for apps and see if that can temporarily stop it running while you test xDrip. "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-616", "type": "thread", "title": "Eversense Integration", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/616", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 616, "labels": ["enhancement", "device-eversense"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-10-08T18:47:13Z", "closed_at": "2024-01-10T16:51:42Z", "comment_count": 52, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-10-10T20:19:48Z", "body": "Yes it may well be possible, but the normal procedure for doing a feasibility study on that approach is for me to request that someone sends me the relevant hardware to test with. As far as I know that isn't going to be possible with Eversense because it is surgically implanted. So unless someone actually wearing one is going to do the development work it is much more difficult to achieve."}, {"user": "BernhardRo", "created_at": "2018-10-11T19:06:41Z", "body": "Well, it is possible. Only the sensor is surgically implanted. The transmitter, which is the part with Bluetooth and therefore the part to communicate with, is put on the skin and can easily been removed and applied again. I am wearing one and have some development experience, but absolutely no idea about debugging a Bluetooth data stream (and I am also not in developing android java applications)..."}, {"user": "BernhardRo", "created_at": "2018-10-20T23:07:48Z", "body": "Hello,\r\nI have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements.\r\nThen I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required. Disadvantage: modified apk for Eversense required, which is still needed...\r\nI have not uploaded anything. Is anyone interested in this?"}, {"user": "jm991", "created_at": "2018-12-12T17:34:49Z", "body": "Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't have Android Wear support."}, {"user": "stugeo1", "created_at": "2018-12-12T21:55:46Z", "body": ">           Hello,\r\n> I have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements.\r\n> Then I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required. Disadvantage: modified apk for Eversense required, which is still needed...\r\n> I have not uploaded anything. Is anyone interested in this?\r\n\r\nHi BernhardRo - I am very interested!!\r\n\r\nI'm on my second EversenseXL now after being impressed with the first one and wanting to continue, however, I really need to be able to see the data on an android watch as i'm training for a marathon and can't keep stopping to look at my phone :(  \r\n\r\nHave tried to get the data into xDrip / Nightscout and have followed the modification of the Android Eversense App from you. \r\n\r\nThe app is working fine but have fallen at the final hurdle as I can't work out how to read the data from oth"}, {"user": "BernhardRo", "created_at": "2018-12-12T22:53:16Z", "body": "Hello,\r\nMy solution is running quite well for me.  It needs the modified Eversense App and the Esel App.  With this it is possible to get your CGM data from Eversense to xDrip. \r\nEverything is availabe here:\r\nhttps://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "cvh2019", "created_at": "2019-02-05T21:34:53Z", "body": "> Hello,\r\n> My solution is running quite well for me. It needs the modified Eversense App and the Esel App. With this it is possible to get your CGM data from Eversense to xDrip.\r\n> Everything is availabe here:\r\n> https://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\n\r\nHi Bernhard, \r\n\r\ni think there is as new version of the official Eversense App released in Dec 2018. No idea what they changed. However I guess it´s a good idea to use the latest version. Could you build a modified Eversense App based on the latest official version? Or let us know how you did it exactly? \r\n\r\nThanks! "}, {"user": "steigermobil", "created_at": "2019-03-19T06:28:09Z", "body": "> Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't have Android Wear support.\r\n\r\nhey jm991, that would be perfect if you can integrate eversense completly in the xdrip app. i use the eversense app with xdrip, but now I want to buy a smartwatch and then i need to have xdrip with full access to the evensense cgm, so that i dont need my smartphone all the time.\r\nPlease help all the eversense user :-) "}, {"user": "stugeo1", "created_at": "2019-03-19T06:42:34Z", "body": "This would be amazing. It's all working for me now and has been a game\nchanger on my training runs for a marathon but as you say needs the phone.\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 19 Mar 2019, 06:28 steigermobil, <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense\n> today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was\n> interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything\n> I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be\n> amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't\n> have Android Wear support.\n>\n> hey jm991, that would be perfect if you can integrate eversense completly\n> in the xdrip app. i use the eversense app with xdrip, but now I want to buy\n> a smartwatch and then i need to have xdrip with full access to the\n> evensense cgm, so that i dont need my smartphone all the time.\n> Please help all the eversense user :-)\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you c"}, {"user": "gridlockedjaw", "created_at": "2019-06-20T19:00:26Z", "body": "Theres a new version in the US. Can anyone patch the new 2.0.103 US version?"}], "text": "Eversense Integration enhancement device-eversense Hello,\r\nI'm not very happy with the current Eversense integration in xDrip via the Esel companion app. Actually, it looks like this app is not further beeing developed, then this app needs su access, and therefore a rooted android phone - something I do not want. And the app needs a running Roche/Senseonics Eversense app. Therefore it is for example not possible to have a smartwatch standalone solution.\r\nWouldn't it be possible to integrate the bluetooth comminication with the Eversense Transmitter in xDrip and use it as an complete standalone alternative to the Eversense App (but with the official app working in parallel on the same device)?\r\nRegards,\r\nBernhard Yes it may well be possible, but the normal procedure for doing a feasibility study on that approach is for me to request that someone sends me the relevant hardware to test with. As far as I know that isn't going to be possible with Eversense because it is surgically implanted. So unless someone actually wearing one is going to do the development work it is much more difficult to achieve. Well, it is possible. Only the sensor is surgically implanted. The transmitter, which is the part with Bluetooth and therefore the part to communicate with, is put on the skin and can easily been removed and applied again. I am wearing one and have some development experience, but absolutely no idea about debugging a Bluetooth data stream (and I am also not in developing android java applications)... Hello,\r\nI have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements.\r\nThen I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required. Disadvantage: modified apk for Eversense required, which is still needed...\r\nI have not uploaded anything. Is anyone interested in this? Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't have Android Wear support. >           Hello,\r\n> I have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements.\r\n> Then I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required. Disadvantage: modified apk for Eversense required, which is still needed...\r\n> I have not uploaded anything. Is anyone interested in this?\r\n\r\nHi BernhardRo - I am very interested!!\r\n\r\nI'm on my second EversenseXL now after being impressed with the first one and wanting to continue, however, I really need to be able to see the data on an android watch as i'm training for a marathon and can't keep stopping to look at my phone :(  \r\n\r\nHave tried to get the data into xDrip / Nightscout and have followed the modification of the Android Eversense App from you. \r\n\r\nThe app is working fine but have fallen at the final hurdle as I can't work out how to read the data from oth Hello,\r\nMy solution is running quite well for me.  It needs the modified Eversense App and the Esel App.  With this it is possible to get your CGM data from Eversense to xDrip. \r\nEverything is availabe here:\r\nhttps://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\n\r\n > Hello,\r\n> My solution is running quite well for me. It needs the modified Eversense App and the Esel App. With this it is possible to get your CGM data from Eversense to xDrip.\r\n> Everything is availabe here:\r\n> https://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\n\r\nHi Bernhard, \r\n\r\ni think there is as new version of the official Eversense App released in Dec 2018. No idea what they changed. However I guess it´s a good idea to use the latest version. Could you build a modified Eversense App based on the latest official version? Or let us know how you did it exactly? \r\n\r\nThanks!  > Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't have Android Wear support.\r\n\r\nhey jm991, that would be perfect if you can integrate eversense completly in the xdrip app. i use the eversense app with xdrip, but now I want to buy a smartwatch and then i need to have xdrip with full access to the evensense cgm, so that i dont need my smartphone all the time.\r\nPlease help all the eversense user :-)  This would be amazing. It's all working for me now and has been a game\nchanger on my training runs for a marathon but as you say needs the phone.\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 19 Mar 2019, 06:28 steigermobil, <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> Hi I'm a longtime xdrip user and just got implanted with an EverSense\n> today. I am a developer and have a contact within EverSense who was\n> interested in getting support in xDrip for their device. Is there anything\n> I can do to help? Having full native xDrip support for EverSense would be\n> amazing since the EverSense app only works with a few devices and doesn't\n> have Android Wear support.\n>\n> hey jm991, that would be perfect if you can integrate eversense completly\n> in the xdrip app. i use the eversense app with xdrip, but now I want to buy\n> a smartwatch and then i need to have xdrip with full access to the\n> evensense cgm, so that i dont need my smartphone all the time.\n> Please help all the eversense user :-)\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you c Theres a new version in the US. Can anyone patch the new 2.0.103 US version?"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-628", "type": "thread", "title": "Android 9 - xDrip+ - Miaomiao - BT disconnecting", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/628", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 628, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-10-16T08:38:35Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-06T18:34:58Z", "comment_count": 52, "comments": [{"user": "Mr-Enigma", "created_at": "2018-10-16T11:11:05Z", "body": "try turning \"use scanning\" and \"trust auto connect\" off i dont have them on and havnt had issues for awhile"}, {"user": "Denksi", "created_at": "2018-10-16T11:36:32Z", "body": "i deaktivated it now, but i think i did it already....\r\ni think the problem is not only by bluetooth, also by GPS, like i wrote, when the smartphone is not used he is loosing the connection.\r\nI will inform how the status is tomorrw latest"}, {"user": "gregorybel", "created_at": "2018-10-18T07:02:16Z", "body": "when you have issue, could you please look in system status and check connection status? is it connected?\r\n\r\nI am fighting with a bug now ans would like to know if other people see same issue. it seems xdrip thinks itnis connected but in fact not.\r\n\r\notherwise GATT close should be better oFF."}, {"user": "opasha", "created_at": "2018-10-24T12:01:48Z", "body": "Did you try locking the xDrip+ app in Recents? Test with that. I have the same setup except on Oreo 8.1 on Mi Max 3. Miui is very aggressive with Oreo on killing apps so you have to autostart them in app info settings and keep the important ones including magisk (for root) locked. "}, {"user": "Denksi", "created_at": "2019-01-11T07:56:33Z", "body": "Hello sorry for not informing long time, but i got a child :)\r\n\r\n@ gregorybel:\r\nunder Android i don't see if Miaomiao is connectet, i just see Miaomiao under xDrip,\r\nalso when xDrip gets no data, and i click to Bluetooth surch, i see there my Miaomiao, and some secounds later all other Bluetooth devices, so it looks like that he is connected but in a sleep mode....\r\nI will test the GATT - OFF, the next days and inform you.\r\n\r\n@ opasha:\r\nwhat you meen with locking xDrip in recents? xDrip has all Android Option for Battery Saving deactivated, and all possible permissions what xDrip can get.\r\nxDrip is every Time open, when he is not getting the data ."}, {"user": "gooliegoogoo", "created_at": "2019-04-04T21:35:34Z", "body": "This is happening to me too, seems similar to OP except I can go for many hours w/out a disconnect, seems to happen once every day or two?  \r\n\r\n- Android 9, patch level April 5, 2019\r\n- Pixel 3 phone, Hardware vMP1.0\r\n- xDrip v 14fecb8-2019.01.10\r\n- Miaomiao (not sure how to check version info?)\r\n\r\nSymptoms - able to connect and things seem fine, then after some time will show 'disconnect' in system status.  Aggressive reconnect is on, so I see it trying to reconnect on it's own but it continues to fail.  If I then 'Bluethooth Scan' and manually tap, it will sometimes start working again, although other times it takes a few times for this to work. \r\n\r\nI\"m a new user to all this so I don't have too many data points.  Overall this isn't too big a deal during the day as I've been able to restart it, but it's very frustrating after I got to sleep as I'll then not get any data for that night.  \r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "renegadeandy", "created_at": "2019-04-20T22:26:13Z", "body": "I just had this same problem for today after an Android 9 upgrade caused me to disconnect all day.\r\n\r\nI fixed by doing:\r\n\r\nxDrip+ -> Settings -> Less common settings -> Bluetooth settings -> Disable Trust Android Auto Connect -- Perhaps xDrip+ should query the android version and set this to disabled if it detects android 9.x?\r\n"}, {"user": "ahaverty", "created_at": "2019-05-08T08:53:27Z", "body": "I did the same as @renegadeandy and my miaomiao reconnected within a few seconds.\r\n_I upgraded my One Plus 3 to android 9 yesterday and was disconnected all night unknowingly._"}, {"user": "ahaverty", "created_at": "2019-05-14T07:31:52Z", "body": "I was wrong, it's still disconnecting most nights and sometimes is very temperamental when trying to reconnect it. "}, {"user": "JosephLaMule", "created_at": "2019-05-14T08:48:28Z", "body": "Hi, i exactly have the same issue with my oneplus5..."}], "text": "Android 9 - xDrip+ - Miaomiao - BT disconnecting  Hello,\r\n\r\nI did the update on my OnePlus6 to Android 9, since that, i hat oftan Bluetooth disconnection to my Miaomiao.\r\nSince Android 9 i realy need to have GPS also active (my GPS problem under Android 8 are now wie 9 mutch less than before - but I don't have any option to change the GPS settings)\r\nBluethooth connection to Miaomia ofer xDrip+ is working fine,\r\nBUT when i sit longer (I don't knwo how long 10-30 minutes +++) xDrip is loosing the connection to Miaomiao, and is not able to connet again (also not when he is deactivating and activation bluethooth) I need to go to Bluethooth scan on xdrip - klick Miaomiao and in 70% the connection is working again (the other 30% i need to go some steps with the smartphone, or do the task x tipes)\r\nWhen i driving with the car, or make a walk, or play with the smartphone -  I don't have the problems.\r\n\r\nthat are my bluetooth settings under xdrip (under Android is is showable for everyone)\r\n(i need to translate back from German to English, so i hole i you know what i mean):\r\nBluetooth activation - ON\r\nBluetooth-Watchdog - ON\r\nG5 ... - OFF\r\nClosing GATT in not connection - ON\r\nUse Scanning - ON\r\nTrust Auto-Connect - ON\r\nrest is OFF\r\n\r\nHopefully some of you can help me. - br Alexander try turning \"use scanning\" and \"trust auto connect\" off i dont have them on and havnt had issues for awhile i deaktivated it now, but i think i did it already....\r\ni think the problem is not only by bluetooth, also by GPS, like i wrote, when the smartphone is not used he is loosing the connection.\r\nI will inform how the status is tomorrw latest when you have issue, could you please look in system status and check connection status? is it connected?\r\n\r\nI am fighting with a bug now ans would like to know if other people see same issue. it seems xdrip thinks itnis connected but in fact not.\r\n\r\notherwise GATT close should be better oFF. Did you try locking the xDrip+ app in Recents? Test with that. I have the same setup except on Oreo 8.1 on Mi Max 3. Miui is very aggressive with Oreo on killing apps so you have to autostart them in app info settings and keep the important ones including magisk (for root) locked.  Hello sorry for not informing long time, but i got a child :)\r\n\r\n@ gregorybel:\r\nunder Android i don't see if Miaomiao is connectet, i just see Miaomiao under xDrip,\r\nalso when xDrip gets no data, and i click to Bluetooth surch, i see there my Miaomiao, and some secounds later all other Bluetooth devices, so it looks like that he is connected but in a sleep mode....\r\nI will test the GATT - OFF, the next days and inform you.\r\n\r\n@ opasha:\r\nwhat you meen with locking xDrip in recents? xDrip has all Android Option for Battery Saving deactivated, and all possible permissions what xDrip can get.\r\nxDrip is every Time open, when he is not getting the data . This is happening to me too, seems similar to OP except I can go for many hours w/out a disconnect, seems to happen once every day or two?  \r\n\r\n- Android 9, patch level April 5, 2019\r\n- Pixel 3 phone, Hardware vMP1.0\r\n- xDrip v 14fecb8-2019.01.10\r\n- Miaomiao (not sure how to check version info?)\r\n\r\nSymptoms - able to connect and things seem fine, then after some time will show 'disconnect' in system status.  Aggressive reconnect is on, so I see it trying to reconnect on it's own but it continues to fail.  If I then 'Bluethooth Scan' and manually tap, it will sometimes start working again, although other times it takes a few times for this to work. \r\n\r\nI\"m a new user to all this so I don't have too many data points.  Overall this isn't too big a deal during the day as I've been able to restart it, but it's very frustrating after I got to sleep as I'll then not get any data for that night.  \r\n\r\n I just had this same problem for today after an Android 9 upgrade caused me to disconnect all day.\r\n\r\nI fixed by doing:\r\n\r\nxDrip+ -> Settings -> Less common settings -> Bluetooth settings -> Disable Trust Android Auto Connect -- Perhaps xDrip+ should query the android version and set this to disabled if it detects android 9.x?\r\n I did the same as @renegadeandy and my miaomiao reconnected within a few seconds.\r\n_I upgraded my One Plus 3 to android 9 yesterday and was disconnected all night unknowingly._ I was wrong, it's still disconnecting most nights and sometimes is very temperamental when trying to reconnect it.  Hi, i exactly have the same issue with my oneplus5..."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-648", "type": "thread", "title": "Improve support for Finowatch / Finow Q1 PRO", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/648", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 648, "labels": ["device-watch"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-10-28T21:51:50Z", "closed_at": "2021-11-04T20:38:28Z", "comment_count": 47, "comments": [{"user": "tzachi-dar", "created_at": "2018-10-28T22:54:59Z", "body": "As a collector of miaomiao this works well.\r\nThe q1 pro itself is a very low end watch. Battery might last from 7 hours to 18 hours with no good reason.\r\nkeyboard is almost useless. screen is low quality. (I guess that this is what you can get for 75 usd).\r\nThat said,  I'm not aware of issues as a collector."}, {"user": "svirito4ka", "created_at": "2018-10-29T18:04:42Z", "body": "I used the watch Finow Q1 Pro with G5 as a collector in old mode, trying almost all versions of xDrip+ starting from August this year. The readings were received with intervals of 5 minutes and were transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. But there was no stability, packet capture percentage was about 50-70 %. The collector used to terminate work when the charge was below 30 %. Ticked wakelocks and watchdogs could not prevent failure in operation. I think it depends on the in-build algorithm of energy saving. The battery life was 8-10 hours, Wi-Fi was disabled, BT and 3G were enabled, brightness was at the lowest level, and I made just a couple of messages (or calls).\r\nAlso I tried to use this watch as a collector in OB1 mode (including Native Algorithm). The readings were received with intervals of 10 minutes and were transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. This interval was inacceptable for me, so I left this mode. "}, {"user": "gordan1987", "created_at": "2018-11-30T14:01:47Z", "body": "My daughter use Finow Q1 Pro with G5(FW. 1.0.4.10).I set up them as a collector in OB1 mode with out native mode.In G5 Debug Settings mark only Use the OB1 Collector and Allow OB1 initiate bonding. And disable all in less common settings relates to bluetooth. Install root on watch and disabled all unused apps. Packet capture percentage about 85-95%.The readings  received with intervals of 5 minutes and  transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. \r\nBut some time watch lose connection totally, helps only restart watch, or start receive data with intervals of 10 minutes. After 5 minutes when it no get data  I check in System Status - G5 Status - Phone Service Status it's show that it stuck on Connection request.\r\nSo I set up alarm on missing reading and just rerstart watch.\r\nAnd if I start mess with in less common settings or G5 Debug Settings I get no change in connections. \r\n"}, {"user": "svirito4ka", "created_at": "2018-12-01T13:35:12Z", "body": "gordan1987, did you manage to unlock the bootloader on the finow q1 pro watch? This question was also asked @jamorham in gitter on 18th Nov. I think he has some ideas for improving collector service of this watch. And hope he is planning to realize “wearDemiGod” mode for this watch."}, {"user": "gordan1987", "created_at": "2018-12-02T12:09:25Z", "body": "I upload all for [rooting to Mega](https://mega.nz/#F!fQkiyC7L!3NhHK9DpAO6bqVApPXnncA)\r\n"}, {"user": "lmiekus", "created_at": "2019-01-02T22:54:35Z", "body": "I have enabled verbose longing for OB1 collector on this watch for Dexcom G6 sensor. The logs with the problematic situation as described by gordan1987 have been uploaded through xdrip with the information \"#648\" and my email address (lmiekus@gmail.com) The problem appeared at 23:10, since that time watch was unable to connect to the sensors. Only after restarting watch the connection have been restored . If you have any other questions please let me know. I am also attaching the exact configuration of the phone with all the important settings.\r\n[Settings.docx](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/files/2722310/Settings.docx)\r\n"}, {"user": "gordan1987", "created_at": "2019-01-09T11:08:59Z", "body": "It would be nice if xDrip had a possibility to restart the clock, if no data received. For me this only way to restore receiving data. "}, {"user": "lmiekus", "created_at": "2019-01-09T20:20:10Z", "body": "Did you thought about trying less common settings > Bluetooth settings > Timer value for BT Watchdog  set to 6 minutes and Bluetooth Watchdog checkbox ticked? I am occasionally getting lost connections as described by you, we usually do smartwatch restart to solve it. But I am planing to try this option too.  That option to set timer value is not possible in last stable version of xdrip+. I found this one in nightly from 28.12.2018. "}, {"user": "gordan1987", "created_at": "2019-01-10T07:48:10Z", "body": "I try set Timer value to 6 minutes in nightly. Still no luck, only restart helps.\r\n\r\n"}, {"user": "svirito4ka", "created_at": "2019-01-10T09:23:03Z", "body": "Did someone try to run the old collector (without OB1) on this watch? On Russian diabet forum, people says that it works well with G5 transmitter. Also they say this watch works reliably with blucon and Miao-Miao (transmitters for Libre sensor)."}], "text": "Improve support for Finowatch / Finow Q1 PRO device-watch What is the current situation with xDrip+ support on this device? What are the issues? Please let me know! thanks As a collector of miaomiao this works well.\r\nThe q1 pro itself is a very low end watch. Battery might last from 7 hours to 18 hours with no good reason.\r\nkeyboard is almost useless. screen is low quality. (I guess that this is what you can get for 75 usd).\r\nThat said,  I'm not aware of issues as a collector. I used the watch Finow Q1 Pro with G5 as a collector in old mode, trying almost all versions of xDrip+ starting from August this year. The readings were received with intervals of 5 minutes and were transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. But there was no stability, packet capture percentage was about 50-70 %. The collector used to terminate work when the charge was below 30 %. Ticked wakelocks and watchdogs could not prevent failure in operation. I think it depends on the in-build algorithm of energy saving. The battery life was 8-10 hours, Wi-Fi was disabled, BT and 3G were enabled, brightness was at the lowest level, and I made just a couple of messages (or calls).\r\nAlso I tried to use this watch as a collector in OB1 mode (including Native Algorithm). The readings were received with intervals of 10 minutes and were transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. This interval was inacceptable for me, so I left this mode.  My daughter use Finow Q1 Pro with G5(FW. 1.0.4.10).I set up them as a collector in OB1 mode with out native mode.In G5 Debug Settings mark only Use the OB1 Collector and Allow OB1 initiate bonding. And disable all in less common settings relates to bluetooth. Install root on watch and disabled all unused apps. Packet capture percentage about 85-95%.The readings  received with intervals of 5 minutes and  transmitted to the Nightscout by the watch through 3G. \r\nBut some time watch lose connection totally, helps only restart watch, or start receive data with intervals of 10 minutes. After 5 minutes when it no get data  I check in System Status - G5 Status - Phone Service Status it's show that it stuck on Connection request.\r\nSo I set up alarm on missing reading and just rerstart watch.\r\nAnd if I start mess with in less common settings or G5 Debug Settings I get no change in connections. \r\n gordan1987, did you manage to unlock the bootloader on the finow q1 pro watch? This question was also asked @jamorham in gitter on 18th Nov. I think he has some ideas for improving collector service of this watch. And hope he is planning to realize “wearDemiGod” mode for this watch. I upload all for [rooting to Mega](https://mega.nz/#F!fQkiyC7L!3NhHK9DpAO6bqVApPXnncA)\r\n I have enabled verbose longing for OB1 collector on this watch for Dexcom G6 sensor. The logs with the problematic situation as described by gordan1987 have been uploaded through xdrip with the information \"#648\" and my email address (lmiekus@gmail.com) The problem appeared at 23:10, since that time watch was unable to connect to the sensors. Only after restarting watch the connection have been restored . If you have any other questions please let me know. I am also attaching the exact configuration of the phone with all the important settings.\r\n[Settings.docx](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/files/2722310/Settings.docx)\r\n It would be nice if xDrip had a possibility to restart the clock, if no data received. For me this only way to restore receiving data.  Did you thought about trying less common settings > Bluetooth settings > Timer value for BT Watchdog  set to 6 minutes and Bluetooth Watchdog checkbox ticked? I am occasionally getting lost connections as described by you, we usually do smartwatch restart to solve it. But I am planing to try this option too.  That option to set timer value is not possible in last stable version of xdrip+. I found this one in nightly from 28.12.2018.  I try set Timer value to 6 minutes in nightly. Still no luck, only restart helps.\r\n\r\n Did someone try to run the old collector (without OB1) on this watch? On Russian diabet forum, people says that it works well with G5 transmitter. Also they say this watch works reliably with blucon and Miao-Miao (transmitters for Libre sensor)."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-663", "type": "thread", "title": "Samsung October patch causing signal loss issues", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/663", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 663, "labels": ["bluetooth"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-11-02T11:54:43Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-20T17:49:51Z", "comment_count": 136, "comments": [{"user": "gregorybel", "created_at": "2018-11-02T17:37:40Z", "body": "- set Trust Auto Connect to on\r\n- reboot phone\r\n- reset MM\r\n\r\nid still issue, please provide logs or at least some screenshots from logs, I am digging into that part od Code"}, {"user": "gregorybel", "created_at": "2018-11-02T17:39:41Z", "body": "other try:\r\n- Trust Auto Connect to off\r\n- close GATT on disconnect to on\r\n- reset MM\r\n- reboot phone"}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2018-11-02T21:29:21Z", "body": "I had to turn trust auto connect off originally as it was causing disconnect. Have turned back on but no change in result.\r\n\r\nPhone and MM have both been restarted/reset numerous times over last 24 hours including after changing settings.\r\n\r\nLogs have just been uploaded from within xDrip\r\n\r\nI can't seem to copy the log text so hopefully this will work to embed a picture.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.imagebam.com/image/c935491018264624\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://thumbs2.imagebam.com/95/f9/f1/c935491018264624.jpg\" alt=\"imagebam.com\"></a> "}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2018-11-03T12:13:13Z", "body": "Last time this happened we had to wait for Samsung's next update which came shortly afterwards and fixed the bluetooth functions they had broken."}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2018-11-03T17:50:38Z", "body": "I hope not jamorham! The updates come fairly frequently, but would still be looking towards the end of November before the next one, and hoping Samsung manage to update what they've broken in that.\r\n\r\nI'll keep tinkering, and if it means having to do a software reset or firmware downgrade then that's what I'll have to do."}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2018-11-04T19:23:50Z", "body": "It seems that as long as you never lock your phone or close the app it maintains connection, but obviously this isn't realistic to do.\r\n\r\nPossible that there's been some kind of change to Bluetooth sleep/shutdown settings because of the Samsung update, and could this be worked around with an xDrip update?"}, {"user": "gregorybel", "created_at": "2018-11-05T13:39:32Z", "body": "are you sure Xdrip is not being killed by Android? "}, {"user": "mistermintsgh", "created_at": "2018-11-05T13:42:26Z", "body": "Absolutely certain. I've made sure it isn't, and never has been, on any list of apps to close for battery optimisation, freeing up RAM or whatever else. "}, {"user": "bordeb", "created_at": "2018-11-05T16:49:58Z", "body": "For Libre + miaomiao I am using now galaxy A8 (2018) android 8.0.0and xDrip+ variant build and for miaomiao to be consistently connected I needed to manually put the xdrip app under \"unmonitored apps\" within battery settings of the phone.\r\n\r\nI don't know what has been changed in latest samsung software update, but it is not the same for all phones. For instance,  S9 release notes doesn't mention Bluetooth changes, while A8 (2018) does. So I am reluctant for now to apply latest updates because it works great with previous version."}, {"user": "yarmatr", "created_at": "2018-11-05T19:33:08Z", "body": "I'm seeing exactly the same thing reported by @mistermintsgh.  I'm using Xdrip on a Note 9 and it was working perfectly until immediately following the latest phone update.  Xdrip will connect and read sugars properly so long as the phone is in active use, but as soon as it is locked, I get no more measurements.  I've tried tweaking all the settings described above and nothing has helped.  I switched back to the Dexcom app to confirm the transmitter and sensor are working properly and it is working without any issues, so something else is going on specific to Xdrip.  I'm happy providing logs or anything else that may aid in debugging further, just let me know which settings you'd like me to apply before gathering the logs.  "}], "text": "Samsung October patch causing signal loss issues bluetooth Samsung released the October update/security patch recently which was installed on my S9+ on 31st October (I assume that the S9, Note 9 and potentially other 2018 Samsung phones got the update on or around the same time).\r\n\r\nSince then I am having frequent \"signal not received\" issues with the MiaoMiao, however Bluetooth **_is_** connected according to the system status screen. No other items or settings on my phone or in xDrip have changed other than this update.\r\n\r\n- Bluetooth is on\r\n- Trust auto connect is turned off\r\n- Bluetooth watchdog is on\r\n- All other settings under Bluetooth menu are off - set Trust Auto Connect to on\r\n- reboot phone\r\n- reset MM\r\n\r\nid still issue, please provide logs or at least some screenshots from logs, I am digging into that part od Code other try:\r\n- Trust Auto Connect to off\r\n- close GATT on disconnect to on\r\n- reset MM\r\n- reboot phone I had to turn trust auto connect off originally as it was causing disconnect. Have turned back on but no change in result.\r\n\r\nPhone and MM have both been restarted/reset numerous times over last 24 hours including after changing settings.\r\n\r\nLogs have just been uploaded from within xDrip\r\n\r\nI can't seem to copy the log text so hopefully this will work to embed a picture.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.imagebam.com/image/c935491018264624\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://thumbs2.imagebam.com/95/f9/f1/c935491018264624.jpg\" alt=\"imagebam.com\"></a>  Last time this happened we had to wait for Samsung's next update which came shortly afterwards and fixed the bluetooth functions they had broken. I hope not jamorham! The updates come fairly frequently, but would still be looking towards the end of November before the next one, and hoping Samsung manage to update what they've broken in that.\r\n\r\nI'll keep tinkering, and if it means having to do a software reset or firmware downgrade then that's what I'll have to do. It seems that as long as you never lock your phone or close the app it maintains connection, but obviously this isn't realistic to do.\r\n\r\nPossible that there's been some kind of change to Bluetooth sleep/shutdown settings because of the Samsung update, and could this be worked around with an xDrip update? are you sure Xdrip is not being killed by Android?  Absolutely certain. I've made sure it isn't, and never has been, on any list of apps to close for battery optimisation, freeing up RAM or whatever else.  For Libre + miaomiao I am using now galaxy A8 (2018) android 8.0.0and xDrip+ variant build and for miaomiao to be consistently connected I needed to manually put the xdrip app under \"unmonitored apps\" within battery settings of the phone.\r\n\r\nI don't know what has been changed in latest samsung software update, but it is not the same for all phones. For instance,  S9 release notes doesn't mention Bluetooth changes, while A8 (2018) does. So I am reluctant for now to apply latest updates because it works great with previous version. I'm seeing exactly the same thing reported by @mistermintsgh.  I'm using Xdrip on a Note 9 and it was working perfectly until immediately following the latest phone update.  Xdrip will connect and read sugars properly so long as the phone is in active use, but as soon as it is locked, I get no more measurements.  I've tried tweaking all the settings described above and nothing has helped.  I switched back to the Dexcom app to confirm the transmitter and sensor are working properly and it is working without any issues, so something else is going on specific to Xdrip.  I'm happy providing logs or anything else that may aid in debugging further, just let me know which settings you'd like me to apply before gathering the logs.  "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-677", "type": "thread", "title": "Eversense CGM", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/677", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 677, "labels": ["device-eversense"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2018-11-07T15:03:48Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-18T12:17:58Z", "comment_count": 47, "comments": [{"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2018-11-07T17:27:17Z", "body": "Which version of ESEL do you use?\r\nThe traditional one: Did you make sure your phone is not only rooted but also has sqlite3 installed?\r\n\r\nThe new one that does not need root: Did you patch the Eversens app on your own or get the apk from somewhere?"}, {"user": "xLevelster", "created_at": "2018-11-07T17:55:35Z", "body": "Hey thanks for your fast response. I am using the newest Eversense XL for 7 days now. I did not know that I have to patch the Eversense App, since I did not find anything about how to set it up, so I just used the newest xDrip Apk and the latest version of Eversense CGM from the PlayStore. How can I get that patched Eversense App?"}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2018-11-07T19:33:11Z", "body": "You do need the companion app \"ESEL\": https://github.com/AdrianLxM/Esel/\r\n\r\nAt the moment you do have to build it for yourself. As up until recently you had to be quite tech-savvy anyway (flash another operating system onto the phone) this was the way to go.\r\n\r\nWe are working on a more user-friendly option now that you don't have to root the phone anymore."}, {"user": "BernhardRo", "created_at": "2018-12-12T22:55:25Z", "body": "There is an easier solution availabe as well:\r\nhttps://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\nThis does not require a rooted phone and no compiling..."}, {"user": "tremor", "created_at": "2019-01-03T08:37:00Z", "body": "@xLevelster: Can you provide some informations regarding the system itself? How long does the battery of the transmitter last? Is it easy to remove it (for snorkeling/diving) and attach again? How accurate is it? What  happens when you don't calibrate twice a day?"}, {"user": "xLevelster", "created_at": "2019-01-03T11:04:47Z", "body": "Battery lasts up to 36 hours. It is very easy to remove because it is just sticked to your skin with an adhesive. For me it is super accurate. You won't get any readings after 2 hours when you don't calibrate."}, {"user": "BernhardRo", "created_at": "2019-01-04T20:04:57Z", "body": "Yes, the battery lasts for about 36h, but it takes only roughly 10 min to reload it. Therefore it is no problem to easily take it off every day (e.g. before taking a shower) and reload it. For me, this is even an advantage as my skin had problems with the 14 days of wearing a freestyle libre. With eversense my skin gets a break and a new plaster every day and with this I have no problems at all.\r\nIn terms of accuracy: the values are somehow noisy, but accurate."}, {"user": "tremor", "created_at": "2019-01-08T10:34:02Z", "body": "Can you fix it without a plaster with armband or 3d printed holder?"}, {"user": "xLevelster", "created_at": "2019-01-08T12:37:10Z", "body": "> Can you fix it without a plaster with armband or 3d printed holder?\r\n\r\nYes not really necessary but that should work, depending on how good it stays over the sensor."}, {"user": "tremor", "created_at": "2019-01-08T20:37:00Z", "body": "I ask because I have to remove it on some days more than once when I go diving..."}], "text": "Eversense CGM device-eversense I don't get any data when connceting the Eversense to xDrip, can anybody solve this problem?  Which version of ESEL do you use?\r\nThe traditional one: Did you make sure your phone is not only rooted but also has sqlite3 installed?\r\n\r\nThe new one that does not need root: Did you patch the Eversens app on your own or get the apk from somewhere? Hey thanks for your fast response. I am using the newest Eversense XL for 7 days now. I did not know that I have to patch the Eversense App, since I did not find anything about how to set it up, so I just used the newest xDrip Apk and the latest version of Eversense CGM from the PlayStore. How can I get that patched Eversense App? You do need the companion app \"ESEL\": https://github.com/AdrianLxM/Esel/\r\n\r\nAt the moment you do have to build it for yourself. As up until recently you had to be quite tech-savvy anyway (flash another operating system onto the phone) this was the way to go.\r\n\r\nWe are working on a more user-friendly option now that you don't have to root the phone anymore. There is an easier solution availabe as well:\r\nhttps://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk\r\nThis does not require a rooted phone and no compiling... @xLevelster: Can you provide some informations regarding the system itself? How long does the battery of the transmitter last? Is it easy to remove it (for snorkeling/diving) and attach again? How accurate is it? What  happens when you don't calibrate twice a day? Battery lasts up to 36 hours. It is very easy to remove because it is just sticked to your skin with an adhesive. For me it is super accurate. You won't get any readings after 2 hours when you don't calibrate. Yes, the battery lasts for about 36h, but it takes only roughly 10 min to reload it. Therefore it is no problem to easily take it off every day (e.g. before taking a shower) and reload it. For me, this is even an advantage as my skin had problems with the 14 days of wearing a freestyle libre. With eversense my skin gets a break and a new plaster every day and with this I have no problems at all.\r\nIn terms of accuracy: the values are somehow noisy, but accurate. Can you fix it without a plaster with armband or 3d printed holder? > Can you fix it without a plaster with armband or 3d printed holder?\r\n\r\nYes not really necessary but that should work, depending on how good it stays over the sensor. I ask because I have to remove it on some days more than once when I go diving..."}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-734", "type": "thread", "title": "Unihertz Atom Bluetooth Connection Lost Dexcom G6", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/734", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 734, "labels": ["help"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-01-06T06:20:47Z", "closed_at": "2020-09-29T12:04:12Z", "comment_count": 122, "comments": [{"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-01-08T23:30:03Z", "body": "It sounds like the phone's bluetooth stack has problems. I don't have one of these phones to test with. If anyone can loan me one I should be able to discover more quite quickly."}, {"user": "AdrianLxM", "created_at": "2019-01-08T23:45:18Z", "body": "The Atom BT stack is quite messed up it seems.\r\nI also have problems keeping the BT connection up with a combo pump and with a Dana RS. So neither BLE nor older BT standards seem to work reliably.\r\n\r\nIt would be good if you could contact the tech support of unihertz. They will give you a guide how to send them system logs. I hope if they get them with different setups they will find a fix.\r\nI don't have much hope as the December update still had the may security patch level of android :("}, {"user": "tech-support-unihertz", "created_at": "2019-01-09T02:14:37Z", "body": "Hi, We are the technical support of unihertz.\r\nAs the document <log-check-20190109.pdf> describes, can Xdrip app give some instructions and why is it broken?\r\n[log-check-20190109.pdf](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/files/2739098/log-check-20190109.pdf)\r\n"}, {"user": "2flea", "created_at": "2019-01-09T09:11:23Z", "body": "Hey guys, I am currently using ATOM (latest firmware) together with xDrip (latest nightly) reading G6 and AAPS (latest dev) with Dana RS pump. It works so far (> 1-2 weeks) without the need to do regular restarts. \r\nWhen I try to add my Sony SWR50 I get BT communication problems - mostly with AAPS. \r\n\r\nI was in contact with Unihertz since I got the phone back in October and we have tried to identify what's amiss (I guess the log above is from mine from end of Nov) but without any success. \r\n\r\nI really would like to use the ATOM with my setup together with a smartwatch - this would be my idea of a perfect system for looping.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if I can help with any testing.\r\n\r\nI have made screenshots of my current system and app settings for your reference: https://photos.app.goo.gl/bi8axT9pnRTHBuH9A\r\n\r\n-------------\r\nAdrian, Unihertz says on their ATOM FB group that the patch level was updated with their latest FW but not recognized by Google. \r\n![image](https://user-images.githubu"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-01-09T09:51:44Z", "body": "@tech-support-unihertz I am the developer of the OB1G5Service. The dexcom transmitter wakes up periodically (every 5 minutes) for a short period of time and during that wake up window we need to connect to it to retrieve the data.  That is what the service is doing.\r\n\r\nI don't have an atom device to test here in the lab but the reports from users have been that the whole phone needs to be rebooted which in my experience implies that it is quite likely the android bluetooth subsystem itself is crashing."}, {"user": "tech-support-unihertz", "created_at": "2019-01-09T11:54:56Z", "body": "@jamorham Can you help analyze this log? (Thanks for the log provider @2flea  :)\r\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/0f2cmdvxjqmt5ni/mtklog_20181127.zip?dl=0\r\nFrom the log analysis, Bluetooth data interaction is normal from 21:02 to 21:38. At 21:39:38 seconds, because there is no data interaction, Bluetooth switches to IDLE mode, causing the connection to be disconnected. \r\nCan you tell us if the xdrip app received an error code when the problem occurred?"}, {"user": "2flea", "created_at": "2019-01-09T12:28:58Z", "body": "As far as I remember the log set above was done with the pre-release firmware including the \"Bluetooth has stopped\" message not the current version. Also I had different settings in the Atom battery saving. \r\n@tech-support-unihertz, @jamorham I can provide new log data with the current setup and then with the Sony smartwatch if you want. Let me know if should add anything special in xDrip log settings."}, {"user": "roco5", "created_at": "2019-01-09T14:17:30Z", "body": "Hey guys, I am also currently using ATOM (latest firmware) together with xDrip (latest nightly) reading G6, and fitbit versa and have struggled to keep a connection to bluetooth when adding a smartwatch (Fitbit Versa) to the configuration.\r\n\r\n**History:  \r\nTest1:**  Tried atom and versa with xdrip and **Atom October firmware**. Tested every battery, fitbit, and collector setting combination imaginable with no joy.\r\n**Result1:** Had tons of connection drops and the only way to resolve them was to reboot phone.  Happened every few hours.\r\n\r\n**Test2:**  Updated **atom firmware to November (latest)** and tuned xdrip, fitbit,  and android settings.  Also \"Forgot\" Sensor in Bluetooth, and let xdrip populate a new Dexcom Bluetooth connection. Still using versa smartwatch.\r\n**Result2:**  Seemed to stay connected a little better, but still had disconnects when the phone was out of range and brought back into range.  Many unrecoverable disconnects a day that required rebooting the phone to solve"}, {"user": "jamorham", "created_at": "2019-02-12T10:22:38Z", "body": "I have received a unihertz atom phone to test with. It is early days, but my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip.\r\n\r\n`PowerSaveService: forceStopThirdApp processName: com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip  pid: 6814, packageName:com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip`\r\n\r\nThis happens even though the custom setting for the app \"`Background activity`\" is enabled for xDrip and that xDrip is already supposed to be excluded from battery optimization via its standard android runtime permission for the same. \r\n\r\nThe MTK setting for `Intelligent power saving standby` is also disabled as well as `battery saver` in the general battery settings.\r\n\r\nxDrip is running a foreground service and does not target oreo sdk (targets sdk 23)\r\n\r\nThis is running on an atom with build number `20181130`\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell the custom setting for whether `Background activity` is allowed for a specific app either is not implemented or doesn't wo"}, {"user": "roco5", "created_at": "2019-02-13T00:52:22Z", "body": "Could someone from Unihertz please comment on what can be done to get this\nfixed, so that we can use the phones and watches effectively with Bluetooth\nCGM softwares?\n\nOn Tue, Feb 12, 2019, 5:22 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> I have received a unihertz atom phone to test with. It is early days, but\n> my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers\n> power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip.\n>\n> PowerSaveService: forceStopThirdApp processName:\n> com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip pid: 6814, packageName:com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip\n>\n> This happens even though the custom setting for the app \"Background\n> activity\" is enabled for xDrip and that xDrip is already supposed to be\n> excluded from battery optimization via its standard android runtime\n> permission for the same.\n>\n> The MTK setting for Intelligent power saving standby is also disabled as\n> well as battery saver in the general battery settings.\n>\n> xDrip is running a foreground service "}], "text": "Unihertz Atom Bluetooth Connection Lost Dexcom G6 help Xdrip will not stay connected to the sensor, as after about 15-20 mins of being disconnected, xdrip phone gets stuck in the \"Scanning\" state  and the only way I can get it to connect again, after losing the connection, is to restart the phone.  I have tested seemingly every setting in xdrip, android, fitbit, and specific to atom, and can't say that any configuration has helped at all.\r\n\r\n**Settings:** \r\nUnihertz Atom running new November 2018 build of firmware\r\nXdrip 12/27/2018 Nightly Build\r\nFitbit Versa running Glance and new 3.0 software\r\n\r\n**Observations:**\r\n- The connection seems very stable between sensor and xdrip when the phone and sensor are in range - to get readings.  When the phone goes out of range for more than 1 or two readings, the data stops getting captured from the sensor and the phone gets stuck \"Scanning\".  The only way I know how to resolve this is to reboot the phone (Restarting the collector does not seem to reslove this.)\r\n\r\n- One user has suggested that when they try to use SSW3 watch and atom phone, with xdrip, they have the same connectivity problems I do, but when they don't use the watch the phone functions much better.  I have a Fitbit Versa with updated 3.0 Fitbit firmware and need to be able to use the phone and watch combination, so I am reluctant to call it a problem using a watch.  \r\n\r\n- It also seems possible that after watching a video or surfing on the phone, the phone misses a couple of readings and gets stuck scanning as well, but I have not completely verified this.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n\r\nThe phone has a perfect form factor for a collector, and I would very much like to work with you to get it to function properly, for me and for others.  Thank you for your assistance. It sounds like the phone's bluetooth stack has problems. I don't have one of these phones to test with. If anyone can loan me one I should be able to discover more quite quickly. The Atom BT stack is quite messed up it seems.\r\nI also have problems keeping the BT connection up with a combo pump and with a Dana RS. So neither BLE nor older BT standards seem to work reliably.\r\n\r\nIt would be good if you could contact the tech support of unihertz. They will give you a guide how to send them system logs. I hope if they get them with different setups they will find a fix.\r\nI don't have much hope as the December update still had the may security patch level of android :( Hi, We are the technical support of unihertz.\r\nAs the document <log-check-20190109.pdf> describes, can Xdrip app give some instructions and why is it broken?\r\n[log-check-20190109.pdf](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/files/2739098/log-check-20190109.pdf)\r\n Hey guys, I am currently using ATOM (latest firmware) together with xDrip (latest nightly) reading G6 and AAPS (latest dev) with Dana RS pump. It works so far (> 1-2 weeks) without the need to do regular restarts. \r\nWhen I try to add my Sony SWR50 I get BT communication problems - mostly with AAPS. \r\n\r\nI was in contact with Unihertz since I got the phone back in October and we have tried to identify what's amiss (I guess the log above is from mine from end of Nov) but without any success. \r\n\r\nI really would like to use the ATOM with my setup together with a smartwatch - this would be my idea of a perfect system for looping.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if I can help with any testing.\r\n\r\nI have made screenshots of my current system and app settings for your reference: https://photos.app.goo.gl/bi8axT9pnRTHBuH9A\r\n\r\n-------------\r\nAdrian, Unihertz says on their ATOM FB group that the patch level was updated with their latest FW but not recognized by Google. \r\n![image](https://user-images.githubu @tech-support-unihertz I am the developer of the OB1G5Service. The dexcom transmitter wakes up periodically (every 5 minutes) for a short period of time and during that wake up window we need to connect to it to retrieve the data.  That is what the service is doing.\r\n\r\nI don't have an atom device to test here in the lab but the reports from users have been that the whole phone needs to be rebooted which in my experience implies that it is quite likely the android bluetooth subsystem itself is crashing. @jamorham Can you help analyze this log? (Thanks for the log provider @2flea  :)\r\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/0f2cmdvxjqmt5ni/mtklog_20181127.zip?dl=0\r\nFrom the log analysis, Bluetooth data interaction is normal from 21:02 to 21:38. At 21:39:38 seconds, because there is no data interaction, Bluetooth switches to IDLE mode, causing the connection to be disconnected. \r\nCan you tell us if the xdrip app received an error code when the problem occurred? As far as I remember the log set above was done with the pre-release firmware including the \"Bluetooth has stopped\" message not the current version. Also I had different settings in the Atom battery saving. \r\n@tech-support-unihertz, @jamorham I can provide new log data with the current setup and then with the Sony smartwatch if you want. Let me know if should add anything special in xDrip log settings. Hey guys, I am also currently using ATOM (latest firmware) together with xDrip (latest nightly) reading G6, and fitbit versa and have struggled to keep a connection to bluetooth when adding a smartwatch (Fitbit Versa) to the configuration.\r\n\r\n**History:  \r\nTest1:**  Tried atom and versa with xdrip and **Atom October firmware**. Tested every battery, fitbit, and collector setting combination imaginable with no joy.\r\n**Result1:** Had tons of connection drops and the only way to resolve them was to reboot phone.  Happened every few hours.\r\n\r\n**Test2:**  Updated **atom firmware to November (latest)** and tuned xdrip, fitbit,  and android settings.  Also \"Forgot\" Sensor in Bluetooth, and let xdrip populate a new Dexcom Bluetooth connection. Still using versa smartwatch.\r\n**Result2:**  Seemed to stay connected a little better, but still had disconnects when the phone was out of range and brought back into range.  Many unrecoverable disconnects a day that required rebooting the phone to solve I have received a unihertz atom phone to test with. It is early days, but my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip.\r\n\r\n`PowerSaveService: forceStopThirdApp processName: com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip  pid: 6814, packageName:com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip`\r\n\r\nThis happens even though the custom setting for the app \"`Background activity`\" is enabled for xDrip and that xDrip is already supposed to be excluded from battery optimization via its standard android runtime permission for the same. \r\n\r\nThe MTK setting for `Intelligent power saving standby` is also disabled as well as `battery saver` in the general battery settings.\r\n\r\nxDrip is running a foreground service and does not target oreo sdk (targets sdk 23)\r\n\r\nThis is running on an atom with build number `20181130`\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell the custom setting for whether `Background activity` is allowed for a specific app either is not implemented or doesn't wo Could someone from Unihertz please comment on what can be done to get this\nfixed, so that we can use the phones and watches effectively with Bluetooth\nCGM softwares?\n\nOn Tue, Feb 12, 2019, 5:22 AM JamOrHam <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n\n> I have received a unihertz atom phone to test with. It is early days, but\n> my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers\n> power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip.\n>\n> PowerSaveService: forceStopThirdApp processName:\n> com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip pid: 6814, packageName:com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip\n>\n> This happens even though the custom setting for the app \"Background\n> activity\" is enabled for xDrip and that xDrip is already supposed to be\n> excluded from battery optimization via its standard android runtime\n> permission for the same.\n>\n> The MTK setting for Intelligent power saving standby is also disabled as\n> well as battery saver in the general battery settings.\n>\n> xDrip is running a foreground service "}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-764", "type": "thread", "title": "checksum failed with xdrip, miaomiao and Freestyle Libre 2", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/764", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 764, "labels": ["bug", "device-libre", "device-miaomiao"], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-01-28T17:50:27Z", "closed_at": "2021-03-20T19:19:37Z", "comment_count": 53, "comments": [{"user": "dabear", "created_at": "2019-01-28T20:34:03Z", "body": "Libre 2 is currently not supported due to encryption. "}, {"user": "brucke", "created_at": "2019-01-29T16:22:59Z", "body": "thx :) i thought so.\r\nMaybe i can fix it ;) "}, {"user": "jason3109", "created_at": "2019-02-12T14:35:29Z", "body": "My wife just got a miaomiao and hers is doing the same thing. Were you able to ever get them to link up and not say checksum failed?"}, {"user": "tzachi-dar", "created_at": "2019-02-17T15:13:39Z", "body": "Libre 2 is currently not supported due to encryption."}, {"user": "dq1967", "created_at": "2019-03-04T11:56:38Z", "body": "I get a lot of checksum errors with Miaomiao and Libre (version 1).  I understand it is related to the contact between the MiaoMiao and the libre, but I am not so sure.  I get a multiple dropped signals and checksum errors in xDrip+ but none in Glimp using the same sensor / Miaomiao setup.  Is there a way to turn down xDrips sensitivity to these errors?"}, {"user": "filipedanunes", "created_at": "2019-03-17T23:37:33Z", "body": "@bruke any development 😉?"}, {"user": "brainopera", "created_at": "2019-03-19T00:31:09Z", "body": "I'm also getting checksum error on the a new libre one sensor. Reads fine on my libre reader device. Been happy past few months and trying to wrap my head around this issue. "}, {"user": "brucke", "created_at": "2019-03-24T10:38:39Z", "body": "@filipedanunes : i started the first analysis but i have to less experience for that.\r\nAt the moment i have no further informations. "}, {"user": "brucke", "created_at": "2019-03-24T10:39:01Z", "body": "sorry wrong button :) "}, {"user": "pgraham9999", "created_at": "2019-03-31T22:59:59Z", "body": "Where can I find the log files?"}], "text": "checksum failed with xdrip, miaomiao and Freestyle Libre 2 bug device-libre device-miaomiao Hi,\r\n\r\nsince i have the new version of Freestyle Libre Version **2** i get the error message \"checksum failed\".\r\n\r\nSamsung Galaxy S9\r\nAndroid Version 8.0.0\r\nFreestyle Libre 2 \r\nxdrip+ Version 20190125-41e549\r\n\r\nI tired: \r\n- start new sensor (more than once) \r\n- restart bluetooth\r\n- restart mobile phone\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat can i do? \r\nIs the current version of xdrip able to scan values from Freestyle Libre 2? \r\nCould the new version of Freestyle Libre 2 the problem? \r\n\r\n\r\n![screenshot_20190128-185119_xdrip](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6576396/51855546-d4129980-232d-11e9-9345-961f889beeb3.jpg)\r\n![screenshot_20190128-184808_xdrip](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6576396/51855569-df65c500-232d-11e9-8683-0282bd9f7989.jpg)\r\n\r\n Libre 2 is currently not supported due to encryption.  thx :) i thought so.\r\nMaybe i can fix it ;)  My wife just got a miaomiao and hers is doing the same thing. Were you able to ever get them to link up and not say checksum failed? Libre 2 is currently not supported due to encryption. I get a lot of checksum errors with Miaomiao and Libre (version 1).  I understand it is related to the contact between the MiaoMiao and the libre, but I am not so sure.  I get a multiple dropped signals and checksum errors in xDrip+ but none in Glimp using the same sensor / Miaomiao setup.  Is there a way to turn down xDrips sensitivity to these errors? @bruke any development 😉? I'm also getting checksum error on the a new libre one sensor. Reads fine on my libre reader device. Been happy past few months and trying to wrap my head around this issue.  @filipedanunes : i started the first analysis but i have to less experience for that.\r\nAt the moment i have no further informations.  sorry wrong button :)  Where can I find the log files?"}, {"id": "thread:xdrip-980", "type": "thread", "title": "Restart sensor and preemptive restarts option no longer works with new transmitter SN 81xxxx", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980", "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 980, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "created_at": "2019-08-12T21:21:24Z", "closed_at": "2021-02-26T21:33:53Z", "comment_count": 74, "comments": [{"user": "definitivequestion", "created_at": "2019-09-04T12:49:37Z", "body": "I am using a G6 transmitter with serial number: 815UKC and firmware 1.6.5.25 and preemptive restarts are working with a nightly build (can't find the exact version)."}, {"user": "cyrusbyte", "created_at": "2019-09-04T13:19:29Z", "body": "Mine Says firmware version 1.6.5.27 and is 81CYXX im on alpha version 2019.08.20.. you can see the version under the classic status page in system status"}, {"user": "definitivequestion", "created_at": "2019-09-04T14:18:50Z", "body": "I am using 33fe112-2019.08.19 xDrip. It says my code is: 1908191229 which is downgradable to 1603091400. I did encounter a similar problem back in July. Since I don't care about my security settings here is my XDrip QR code with settings that work for me: xdpref:eJwtjEEOwiAQAP+yZw/dLgjxhkC/QVjZGmLjwdIYa/y7JHqdycwbnnXPj5K2rRY4gZmLMUUzXkjUKIaZM4rYPLMQDgQHyMuSVmmt3q9r+tU9bN38Vzd5dXB0KmL0ypNz1tkhhvM4kdeBFAbnNXy+15kmCA== ."}, {"user": "bpedman", "created_at": "2019-10-02T03:40:18Z", "body": "My sensor is 81F6XX firmware 1.6.5.27 and restarts are not working anymore either. I'm currently on build ff2c822-2019.09.24\r\n\r\nI uploaded logs as well."}, {"user": "joshhiram", "created_at": "2019-10-02T17:38:01Z", "body": "We got transmitter 81A*** to show \"please wait for warm up\" message, but a\nfew seconds later, it popped up and said G6 sensor failed.  It still\ncounted down the warm up, and then began prompting for calibrations!  It\nwouldn't get passed that.  So, we had to go to the official Dexcom app to\nstart it, which it did just fine.  Xdrip nightly 9-30 and alpha release\ndidn't have an effect.\n\nOn Tue, Oct 1, 2019 at 9:40 PM Brandon Pedersen <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> My sensor is 81F6XX firmware 1.6.5.27 and restarts are not working anymore\n> either. I'm currently on build ff2c822\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/ff2c8228dc1f38520d5a2ee780fc9bd012ddf2dc>\n> -2019.09.24\n>\n> I uploaded logs as well.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=ACA2BKYVR5ZDUIAASK7EQZTQMQJ2PA5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3P"}, {"user": "Ugitsisgv", "created_at": "2019-10-07T12:08:23Z", "body": "Using G6 with Nightly transmitter 815LPP. Preemptive restart says \"not capable.\"  Transmitter is on day 17. Not sure how to restart sensor in 2 days. "}, {"user": "definitivequestion", "created_at": "2019-10-07T13:13:58Z", "body": "If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first page of the status screen (the one with version information)?"}, {"user": "Ugitsisgv", "created_at": "2019-10-07T17:22:45Z", "body": "Thanks for the reply. Two questions.\n\nWhat is the Faraday cage trick?\n\nWhat do I do about the sensor code if I start manually?\n\nThanks for the assist.\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/u"}, {"user": "Ugitsisgv", "created_at": "2019-10-07T19:00:17Z", "body": "How do I disable advanced time travel feature?\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AMGWEYOJCP3U6W42XAXGW53QNMYZ3ANCNFSM4ILFDPZQ>\n> .\n>\n"}, {"user": "Ugitsisgv", "created_at": "2019-10-07T19:01:44Z", "body": "Here is what is on the first page.\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AMGWEYOJCP3U6W42XAXGW53QNMYZ3ANCNFSM4ILFDPZQ>\n> .\n>\n"}], "text": "Restart sensor and preemptive restarts option no longer works with new transmitter SN 81xxxx  I received a new transmitter and now with the preemptive session restart set I keep getting errors. \"Native Sensor is now Stopped: Sensor Failed Start\" then \" Native sensor is now marked FAILED: Sensor Failed Start\" then \"Session Start Failed: Invalid\". It has been working on the last two transmitters that started with SN 80xxxx, but on the new one stating with SN 81xxxx is when i started getting these errors. Seems the only way to restart the sensor was to start it using the dexcom receiver and then i get the \"Warming up\" message on both xdrip and dexcom and have to wait the two hour warm up. I am using a G6 transmitter with serial number: 815UKC and firmware 1.6.5.25 and preemptive restarts are working with a nightly build (can't find the exact version). Mine Says firmware version 1.6.5.27 and is 81CYXX im on alpha version 2019.08.20.. you can see the version under the classic status page in system status I am using 33fe112-2019.08.19 xDrip. It says my code is: 1908191229 which is downgradable to 1603091400. I did encounter a similar problem back in July. Since I don't care about my security settings here is my XDrip QR code with settings that work for me: xdpref:eJwtjEEOwiAQAP+yZw/dLgjxhkC/QVjZGmLjwdIYa/y7JHqdycwbnnXPj5K2rRY4gZmLMUUzXkjUKIaZM4rYPLMQDgQHyMuSVmmt3q9r+tU9bN38Vzd5dXB0KmL0ypNz1tkhhvM4kdeBFAbnNXy+15kmCA== . My sensor is 81F6XX firmware 1.6.5.27 and restarts are not working anymore either. I'm currently on build ff2c822-2019.09.24\r\n\r\nI uploaded logs as well. We got transmitter 81A*** to show \"please wait for warm up\" message, but a\nfew seconds later, it popped up and said G6 sensor failed.  It still\ncounted down the warm up, and then began prompting for calibrations!  It\nwouldn't get passed that.  So, we had to go to the official Dexcom app to\nstart it, which it did just fine.  Xdrip nightly 9-30 and alpha release\ndidn't have an effect.\n\nOn Tue, Oct 1, 2019 at 9:40 PM Brandon Pedersen <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> My sensor is 81F6XX firmware 1.6.5.27 and restarts are not working anymore\n> either. I'm currently on build ff2c822\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/ff2c8228dc1f38520d5a2ee780fc9bd012ddf2dc>\n> -2019.09.24\n>\n> I uploaded logs as well.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=ACA2BKYVR5ZDUIAASK7EQZTQMQJ2PA5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3P Using G6 with Nightly transmitter 815LPP. Preemptive restart says \"not capable.\"  Transmitter is on day 17. Not sure how to restart sensor in 2 days.  If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first page of the status screen (the one with version information)? Thanks for the reply. Two questions.\n\nWhat is the Faraday cage trick?\n\nWhat do I do about the sensor code if I start manually?\n\nThanks for the assist.\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/u How do I disable advanced time travel feature?\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AMGWEYOJCP3U6W42XAXGW53QNMYZ3ANCNFSM4ILFDPZQ>\n> .\n>\n Here is what is on the first page.\n\nOn Mon, Oct 7, 2019, 9:14 AM definitivequestion <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> If you are getting not capable, you may have to manually restart and go\n> through another warm up period. You may try disabling the advanced time\n> travel features. If you have the official Dexcom receiver, you can probably\n> trick it into restarting with the Faraday cage trick. What is on the first\n> page of the status screen (the one with version information)?\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980?email_source=notifications&email_token=AMGWEYMBYZLNRA4G5FGNVZLQNMYZ3A5CNFSM4ILFDPZ2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEAQI36Y#issuecomment-539004411>,\n> or mute the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AMGWEYOJCP3U6W42XAXGW53QNMYZ3ANCNFSM4ILFDPZQ>\n> .\n>\n"}], "distilled": [{"id": "distilled:androidaps-101", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 101, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 101, "title": "Make \"INFO: Pump unreachable\" notification actionable?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/101", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/101", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user wants to tap the \"INFO: Pump Unreachable\" notification and go directly to the Medtronic tab, but currently the notification is not actionable. Some users report that the notification may not appear at all, only an alarm sound and in-app banner, and the sound can only be stopped by force-closing the app.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a single root cause. It discusses that notifications are informational and commands are retried automatically, and that Android may disable notification channels after multiple dismissals, but no definitive cause is confirmed.", "fix": "The feature request was implemented in pull request #258, which made the notification actionable. For the missing notification issue, AdrianLxM suggests checking that all notification channels for AAPS are enabled in App-Info, as Android may ask to disable notifications after dismissing them multiple times.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic"], "evidence_quote": "Thanks @StephenBrown2 for the feature request. It was not much work and will bring a lot of value! https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/258", "text": "Make \"INFO: Pump unreachable\" notification actionable? The user wants to tap the \"INFO: Pump Unreachable\" notification and go directly to the Medtronic tab, but currently the notification is not actionable. Some users report that the notification may not appear at all, only an alarm sound and in-app banner, and the sound can only be stopped by force-closing the app. The thread does not establish a single root cause. It discusses that notifications are informational and commands are retried automatically, and that Android may disable notification channels after multiple dismissals, but no definitive cause is confirmed. The feature request was implemented in pull request #258, which made the notification actionable. For the missing notification issue, AdrianLxM suggests checking that all notification channels for AAPS are enabled in App-Info, as Android may ask to disable notifications after dismissing them multiple times. Medtronic Medtronic Thanks @StephenBrown2 for the feature request. It was not much work and will bring a lot of value! https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/258"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1024", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1024, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1024, "title": "v2.8.2 - Loop not executing every 5 mins even when a TB needs changing", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1024", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1024", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Loop is not executing every 5 mins even though a TB needs changing. Manually pressing 'run now' or setting a new action like a TT makes the loop run. Autosens seems to be changing value with each new BG.", "cause": "The root cause is too much concurrent changes in DB which is preventing AS calculation to finish.", "fix": "The issue cannot be resolved in version 2.8. The user is advised to wait for version 3.0 where this has been improved.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["android 10"], "driver_tags": ["BYOD app"], "evidence_quote": "the root cause is too much concurrent changes in DB which is preventing AS calculation to finish. I'm unable to resolve it in 2.8 In 3.0 this has been improved a lot", "text": "v2.8.2 - Loop not executing every 5 mins even when a TB needs changing Loop is not executing every 5 mins even though a TB needs changing. Manually pressing 'run now' or setting a new action like a TT makes the loop run. Autosens seems to be changing value with each new BG. The root cause is too much concurrent changes in DB which is preventing AS calculation to finish. The issue cannot be resolved in version 2.8. The user is advised to wait for version 3.0 where this has been improved. Dexcom G6 android 10 BYOD app the root cause is too much concurrent changes in DB which is preventing AS calculation to finish. I'm unable to resolve it in 2.8 In 3.0 this has been improved a lot"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1069", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1069, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1069, "title": "Pixel Pro 6 Android 12 no longer connects to Dash", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1069", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1069", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On Pixel Pro 6 with Android 12, after updating AndroidAPS, the app no longer connects to the Dash pod. The issue starts with a BT connection permission issue. In-session updates do not work, but a clean install and activating a new pod works.", "cause": "The issue is related to a Bluetooth connection permission that is requested during pod activation. In-session updates do not prompt for this permission, so the connection fails. The problem was fixed in a later dev version (dev 18) which prompts for the permission.", "fix": "Update to AndroidAPS dev 18 (or later) which prompts for the required Bluetooth permission and allows connection to the Dash pod. Alternatively, perform a clean install and activate a new pod to grant the permission.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["Dash"], "evidence_quote": "It seems most recent commits for Dev 18 has fixed this. not sure if each new version will prompt a new BT permission but it forced me to request that permission and then connected to Dash pod.", "text": "Pixel Pro 6 Android 12 no longer connects to Dash On Pixel Pro 6 with Android 12, after updating AndroidAPS, the app no longer connects to the Dash pod. The issue starts with a BT connection permission issue. In-session updates do not work, but a clean install and activating a new pod works. The issue is related to a Bluetooth connection permission that is requested during pod activation. In-session updates do not prompt for this permission, so the connection fails. The problem was fixed in a later dev version (dev 18) which prompts for the permission. Update to AndroidAPS dev 18 (or later) which prompts for the required Bluetooth permission and allows connection to the Dash pod. Alternatively, perform a clean install and activate a new pod to grant the permission. Dash Android 12 Dash It seems most recent commits for Dev 18 has fixed this. not sure if each new version will prompt a new BT permission but it forced me to request that permission and then connected to Dash pod."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1085", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1085, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1085, "title": "[3.0-beta9] NSClient - Incorrect vertical position of BG check on graph", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1085", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1085", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "BG check entries entered in AAPS appear at incorrect vertical position on the NSClient graph, and the value is not shown in the BG check entry on NSClient side. The value appears converted incorrectly (e.g., 30 mmol/L becomes 1.7 mmol/L).", "cause": "The thread identifies a unit conversion bug where the glucose unit is incorrectly changed from MMOL to MGDL when the therapy event is received on the other phone, causing the value to be misinterpreted.", "fix": "The issue was reported to the NS team as an NS bug. No specific fix is provided in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nsclient", "byoda"], "evidence_quote": "I confirm the bug, there is a wrong unit change somewhere between source phone and destination phone (see below send and received values in log)", "text": "[3.0-beta9] NSClient - Incorrect vertical position of BG check on graph BG check entries entered in AAPS appear at incorrect vertical position on the NSClient graph, and the value is not shown in the BG check entry on NSClient side. The value appears converted incorrectly (e.g., 30 mmol/L becomes 1.7 mmol/L). The thread identifies a unit conversion bug where the glucose unit is incorrectly changed from MMOL to MGDL when the therapy event is received on the other phone, causing the value to be misinterpreted. The issue was reported to the NS team as an NS bug. No specific fix is provided in the thread.  nsclient byoda I confirm the bug, there is a wrong unit change somewhere between source phone and destination phone (see below send and received values in log)"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-109", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 109, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 109, "title": "Carbs recommendation does not match calculator", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/109", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/109", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Carbs required icon was flashing red saying 29g required, but the calculator says 0.61 units needed. The user expects these to be in sync.", "cause": "The bolus calculator is a basic equation based on current situation, while the carbs required announcement uses oref1 which considers current and future predictions, so they are not meant to match.", "fix": "No code fix; the issue was resolved by clarifying in documentation that the two values have different meanings and should not be compared. The user offered to create a PR to docs.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["oref1", "bolus wizard", "carb suggestion"], "evidence_quote": "The meaning of the results is different: Wizard tells you what to do to be in range after DIA [h] (which is perfectly OK when calculating food) Announcement is describing current situation", "text": "Carbs recommendation does not match calculator Carbs required icon was flashing red saying 29g required, but the calculator says 0.61 units needed. The user expects these to be in sync. The bolus calculator is a basic equation based on current situation, while the carbs required announcement uses oref1 which considers current and future predictions, so they are not meant to match. No code fix; the issue was resolved by clarifying in documentation that the two values have different meanings and should not be compared. The user offered to create a PR to docs.  oref1 bolus wizard carb suggestion The meaning of the results is different: Wizard tells you what to do to be in range after DIA [h] (which is perfectly OK when calculating food) Announcement is describing current situation"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1117", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1117, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1117, "title": "DASH / EROS Show either percentage or units of bolus already injected", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1117", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1117", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The watch face can tell the percentage of the bolus injected but not the app. It would be helpful to show the percentage, or even better, the units, of bolus already injected on the phone interface too.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DASH", "EROS"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dash", "eros", "insight"], "evidence_quote": "The watch face can tell me the percentage of the bolus injected but not the app :( It would be helpful to show the percentage, or even better, the units, of bolus already injected on the phone interface too.", "text": "DASH / EROS Show either percentage or units of bolus already injected The watch face can tell the percentage of the bolus injected but not the app. It would be helpful to show the percentage, or even better, the units, of bolus already injected on the phone interface too.   DASH EROS dash eros insight The watch face can tell me the percentage of the bolus injected but not the app :( It would be helpful to show the percentage, or even better, the units, of bolus already injected on the phone interface too."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1141", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1141, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1141, "title": "[3.0beta11] NSClient does not see temp target", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1141", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1141", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When a temp target is set either manually or via automation on AAPS phone, it cannot be seen on NSClient phone. The temp target appears in AAPS but not in NSClient's Treatments - temp target tab. It was observed that the issue occurs when an automation sets both a temp target and a temp profile.", "cause": "The issue is related to a bug in Nightscout (NS), specifically in the dev version. A commit on the nightscout dev caused the problem, and a fix was created in pull request #7285 but not yet part of NS.", "fix": "The user reverted their Nightscout site to master and could see temp targets in NSClient. The maintainer created a fix in https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/pull/7285 but it is not yet part of NS.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I decided to revert to master on my nightscout site and can now see temp targets in NSClient. I suspect this commit on the nightscout dev is what caused this issue: https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/commit/aca8d5ab492f1e356c36f340102044dc961d82aa#diff-5a16ec3fb169ae3b2b0b4d0a810080d451c8910345d86280d1cc2c67d4a178a0", "text": "[3.0beta11] NSClient does not see temp target When a temp target is set either manually or via automation on AAPS phone, it cannot be seen on NSClient phone. The temp target appears in AAPS but not in NSClient's Treatments - temp target tab. It was observed that the issue occurs when an automation sets both a temp target and a temp profile. The issue is related to a bug in Nightscout (NS), specifically in the dev version. A commit on the nightscout dev caused the problem, and a fix was created in pull request #7285 but not yet part of NS. The user reverted their Nightscout site to master and could see temp targets in NSClient. The maintainer created a fix in https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/pull/7285 but it is not yet part of NS.   I decided to revert to master on my nightscout site and can now see temp targets in NSClient. I suspect this commit on the nightscout dev is what caused this issue: https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/commit/aca8d5ab492f1e356c36f340102044dc961d82aa#diff-5a16ec3fb169ae3b2b0b4d0a810080d451c8910345d86280d1cc2c67d4a178a0"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1169", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1169, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1169, "title": "3.0rc1 SMB disabled ", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1169", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1169", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "SMBs are disabled in AAPS 3.0rc1 even though they are enabled in configuration. The user is using xDrip+ (slave) as the glucose source on the test system.", "cause": "The BG source (xDrip+ Sync Follower) does not support SMB always and the user does not enter carbs, so COB is always zero and SMB is forced disabled.", "fix": "Use a BG source that supports SMB always, or enter carbs to have COB > 0. The user notes that xDrip+ Sync Follower is not allowed as BG source for SMB.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["xDrip+", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip+ Sync Follower", "xDrip+ master", "xDrip+ slave"], "evidence_quote": "From what I see you are using BG source not supporting SMB always and you don't enter carbs. Thus COB is always zero and SMB is forced disabled", "text": "3.0rc1 SMB disabled  SMBs are disabled in AAPS 3.0rc1 even though they are enabled in configuration. The user is using xDrip+ (slave) as the glucose source on the test system. The BG source (xDrip+ Sync Follower) does not support SMB always and the user does not enter carbs, so COB is always zero and SMB is forced disabled. Use a BG source that supports SMB always, or enter carbs to have COB > 0. The user notes that xDrip+ Sync Follower is not allowed as BG source for SMB. xDrip+ Dexcom G6 xDrip+ Sync Follower xDrip+ master xDrip+ slave From what I see you are using BG source not supporting SMB always and you don't enter carbs. Thus COB is always zero and SMB is forced disabled"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1184", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1184, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1184, "title": "AndroidAPS doesn't take BG value in main window", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1184", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1184", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "AndroidAPS home screen shows a crossed-out BG value while xDrip+ tab and xDrip+ app show current BG readings. This happens after being away from the phone for some time; when new readings arrive, they appear in the xDrip+ tab but not in the main screen, and are not used in calculations until after another 5 minutes.", "cause": "AAPS did not receive any data from xDrip for a period (e.g., 15 minutes or 25 minutes) according to logs, and the phone was in a strange state during that time. The issue was not definitively resolved; it was closed for inactivity.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": ["EVENT logging → enabled", "GLUCOSE logging → enabled"], "devices": ["Poco F3", "Libre 2", "Miaomiao2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip+", "native Xdrip BT connection", "OOP2", "tomato"], "evidence_quote": "anyway AAPS didn't receive any data from xdrip for 15 min", "text": "AndroidAPS doesn't take BG value in main window AndroidAPS home screen shows a crossed-out BG value while xDrip+ tab and xDrip+ app show current BG readings. This happens after being away from the phone for some time; when new readings arrive, they appear in the xDrip+ tab but not in the main screen, and are not used in calculations until after another 5 minutes. AAPS did not receive any data from xDrip for a period (e.g., 15 minutes or 25 minutes) according to logs, and the phone was in a strange state during that time. The issue was not definitively resolved; it was closed for inactivity.  Poco F3 Libre 2 Miaomiao2 xDrip+ native Xdrip BT connection OOP2 tomato anyway AAPS didn't receive any data from xdrip for 15 min"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1188", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1188, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1188, "title": "Improve UI-interaction to change viewrange on overview (feature request)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1188", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1188", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user finds the current UI interaction to change the view range on the overview (tab-hold-and-wait for rendering) tedious and unresponsive, often overshooting the desired range and having to repeat the process.", "cause": null, "fix": "The issue was resolved in the current v3.2 UI, as stated by vanelsberg: 'Solved for current v3.2 UI...'", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Solved for current v3.2 UI...", "text": "Improve UI-interaction to change viewrange on overview (feature request) The user finds the current UI interaction to change the view range on the overview (tab-hold-and-wait for rendering) tedious and unresponsive, often overshooting the desired range and having to repeat the process.  The issue was resolved in the current v3.2 UI, as stated by vanelsberg: 'Solved for current v3.2 UI...'   Solved for current v3.2 UI..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1190", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1190, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1190, "title": "V3 RC2 Bug : Message new version available", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1190", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1190", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users receive a message stating that a new version is available, with warnings that closed loop will stop in a week and 14 days, even though they have the latest RC version installed (RC2 or RC3). The message appears once every 24 hours.", "cause": "The message appears once every 24 hours, depending on when the last version check was done, as explained by MilosKozak.", "fix": "No fix is provided in the thread; the maintainer explains the behavior but does not offer a solution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "once in 24h. depends on when the last check was done", "text": "V3 RC2 Bug : Message new version available Users receive a message stating that a new version is available, with warnings that closed loop will stop in a week and 14 days, even though they have the latest RC version installed (RC2 or RC3). The message appears once every 24 hours. The message appears once every 24 hours, depending on when the last version check was done, as explained by MilosKozak. No fix is provided in the thread; the maintainer explains the behavior but does not offer a solution.   once in 24h. depends on when the last check was done"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1199", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1199, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1199, "title": "RC3 / BYODA calibration / red triangle still there", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1199", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1199", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When calibrating a Dexcom G6 via BYODA shortly after the last BG reading (around 4 minutes), a duplicate BG entry appears in AAPS and a red triangle is shown.", "cause": "The issue is related to the timing of calibration relative to the BG reading from the transmitter, causing a duplicate BG entry in AAPS. The exact root cause is not fully explained, but it is specific to G6 and not the same as the G5 fix.", "fix": "MilosKozak applied a second fix (commit 900c5db0dc71c63ddef5e93586fbcd9b58588375) which resolved the issue. The user confirmed that after this fix, calibrating 12 seconds before a new BG read did not produce a duplicate.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "BYODA"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["BYODA", "native G6"], "evidence_quote": "Seems like the 2nd try is the good one :) Just tested at 12 sec before new BG read and didn't have a double in AAPS", "text": "RC3 / BYODA calibration / red triangle still there When calibrating a Dexcom G6 via BYODA shortly after the last BG reading (around 4 minutes), a duplicate BG entry appears in AAPS and a red triangle is shown. The issue is related to the timing of calibration relative to the BG reading from the transmitter, causing a duplicate BG entry in AAPS. The exact root cause is not fully explained, but it is specific to G6 and not the same as the G5 fix. MilosKozak applied a second fix (commit 900c5db0dc71c63ddef5e93586fbcd9b58588375) which resolved the issue. The user confirmed that after this fix, calibrating 12 seconds before a new BG read did not produce a duplicate. Dexcom G6 BYODA BYODA native G6 Seems like the 2nd try is the good one :) Just tested at 12 sec before new BG read and didn't have a double in AAPS"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-122", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 122, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 122, "title": "no way to get watch face installed through playstore-apps on phone...etc...", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/122", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/122", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Since the dev version, the AAPS watch face does not get installed via the Play Store app on the phone; no AAPS is displayed, so there is no way to install it. Building the AAPS APK is fine, the wear.apk is there and not empty, but the watch face does not appear on the watch.", "cause": "The cause was identified as a problem in the build process of the dev version, which was later fixed by a change in the APK build process (referenced as #198).", "fix": "The fix was to restore the APK build process via pull request #198, which resolved the issue for users.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana RS", "poco f1", "fossil sport", "Fossil G5", "Fossil 5 Gen"], "android_versions": ["Android 9", "Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["wear.apk", "adb", "sideloading", "Play Store"], "evidence_quote": "Apk build process will be restored with #198. @AdrianLxM, many thanks for your work!", "text": "no way to get watch face installed through playstore-apps on phone...etc... Since the dev version, the AAPS watch face does not get installed via the Play Store app on the phone; no AAPS is displayed, so there is no way to install it. Building the AAPS APK is fine, the wear.apk is there and not empty, but the watch face does not appear on the watch. The cause was identified as a problem in the build process of the dev version, which was later fixed by a change in the APK build process (referenced as #198). The fix was to restore the APK build process via pull request #198, which resolved the issue for users. Dana RS poco f1 fossil sport Fossil G5 Fossil 5 Gen Android 9 Android 10 wear.apk adb sideloading Play Store Apk build process will be restored with #198. @AdrianLxM, many thanks for your work!"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1221", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1221, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1221, "title": "Nightscout crashes with AndroidAPS 3.0 RC3", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1221", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1221", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When making a profile change through NS Client, Nightscout crashes and needs a Dyno restart. The issue occurs with AndroidAPS 3.0 RC3 and Nightscout 14.2.5, but there was no problem with version 2.8.2.1.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. MilosKozak mentions a PR with a fix but not merged, and suggests clearing treatment collection. mountrcg observes duplicated SGV entries in NS DB, but MilosKozak states duplicated values were not coming from AAPS because AAPS always fills 'isValid' field.", "fix": "The only solution mentioned is to clear the treatment collection in Nightscout, as stated by MilosKozak. There is also a PR (nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#7284) with a fix but not merged yet.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DanaRS", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NS Client", "bridge", "BYODA", "xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "i§m getting this one too time to time. there is a PR with fix but is not merged yet https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/pull/7284 the only solution now is clear treatment collection", "text": "Nightscout crashes with AndroidAPS 3.0 RC3 When making a profile change through NS Client, Nightscout crashes and needs a Dyno restart. The issue occurs with AndroidAPS 3.0 RC3 and Nightscout 14.2.5, but there was no problem with version 2.8.2.1. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. MilosKozak mentions a PR with a fix but not merged, and suggests clearing treatment collection. mountrcg observes duplicated SGV entries in NS DB, but MilosKozak states duplicated values were not coming from AAPS because AAPS always fills 'isValid' field. The only solution mentioned is to clear the treatment collection in Nightscout, as stated by MilosKozak. There is also a PR (nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#7284) with a fix but not merged yet. DanaRS Dexcom G6 NS Client bridge BYODA xDrip i§m getting this one too time to time. there is a PR with fix but is not merged yet https://github.com/nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor/pull/7284 the only solution now is clear treatment collection"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1288", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1288, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1288, "title": "Omnipod and DASH tabs force closes AAPS if phone language is set to \"Danish\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1288", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1288", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When the phone language is set to Danish, opening the Omnipod or DASH tabs in AAPS force closes the app, especially when the pod has less than 50 units left. Changing the phone language to English resolves the issue.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the crashes are caused by wrong translations in the Danish language strings, which lead to force closes when opening the Omnipod/DASH tabs.", "fix": "The fix is to correct the wrong translations. AAPS was updated so that wrong translations no longer cause crashes and fall back to English text, reporting issues via Crashlytics (referenced in PR #1329). Users can also work around by changing the phone language to English.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod", "DASH", "Eros"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Wrong translations should no longer cause crashes and should fall back to the English text and report an issue via Crashlytics. #1329", "text": "Omnipod and DASH tabs force closes AAPS if phone language is set to \"Danish\" When the phone language is set to Danish, opening the Omnipod or DASH tabs in AAPS force closes the app, especially when the pod has less than 50 units left. Changing the phone language to English resolves the issue. The thread identifies that the crashes are caused by wrong translations in the Danish language strings, which lead to force closes when opening the Omnipod/DASH tabs. The fix is to correct the wrong translations. AAPS was updated so that wrong translations no longer cause crashes and fall back to English text, reporting issues via Crashlytics (referenced in PR #1329). Users can also work around by changing the phone language to English. Omnipod DASH Eros Android 12  Wrong translations should no longer cause crashes and should fall back to the English text and report an issue via Crashlytics. #1329"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1308", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1308, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1308, "title": "Large NSClient time display", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1308", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1308", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The time display in NSClient is massive on the top right side, taking up space and preventing the BG value from being completely visible when there is a double digit BG value or if the font size of the phone is increased.", "cause": null, "fix": "A PR (#1436) scaled down the text size, but the thread does not confirm if it resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I scaled down the text size in PR #1436 could you validate this works for you well for your device?", "text": "Large NSClient time display The time display in NSClient is massive on the top right side, taking up space and preventing the BG value from being completely visible when there is a double digit BG value or if the font size of the phone is increased.  A PR (#1436) scaled down the text size, but the thread does not confirm if it resolved the issue.   I scaled down the text size in PR #1436 could you validate this works for you well for your device?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1359", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1359, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1359, "title": "Riley Link Orange can't connect with dev branch", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1359", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1359", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "RileyLink Orange cannot connect with dev branch; state stuck at initialization of RileyLink. No permission request notification appears. Connection works with master branch.", "cause": "The problem is the RL check for permission before connect code, specifically in RileyLinkBLE.kt connectGattInternal where the condition uses >= Build.VERSION_CODES.S, causing the permission request not to appear on Android 12.", "fix": "Change the condition in RileyLinkBLE.kt from `if (config.PUMPDRIVERS && Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.S && ...` to `if (config.PUMPDRIVERS && Build.VERSION.SDK_INT > Build.VERSION_CODES.S && ...` to bypass the permission check and allow connection.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["RileyLink Orange", "EmaLink", "RileyLink"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["Omnipod Eros driver", "MDT"], "evidence_quote": "It's the RL check for permission before connect code the problem https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/b1d45833c5570910142e78ba39a8322b4039a9d5", "text": "Riley Link Orange can't connect with dev branch RileyLink Orange cannot connect with dev branch; state stuck at initialization of RileyLink. No permission request notification appears. Connection works with master branch. The problem is the RL check for permission before connect code, specifically in RileyLinkBLE.kt connectGattInternal where the condition uses >= Build.VERSION_CODES.S, causing the permission request not to appear on Android 12. Change the condition in RileyLinkBLE.kt from `if (config.PUMPDRIVERS && Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.S && ...` to `if (config.PUMPDRIVERS && Build.VERSION.SDK_INT > Build.VERSION_CODES.S && ...` to bypass the permission check and allow connection. RileyLink Orange EmaLink RileyLink Android 10 Android 12 Omnipod Eros driver MDT It's the RL check for permission before connect code the problem https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/b1d45833c5570910142e78ba39a8322b4039a9d5"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1394", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1394, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1394, "title": "Entrys in the treatment menu only partially visible", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1394", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1394", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "In the treatment menu, entries are only partially visible and can therefore no longer be deleted (at least in portrait mode). Even when setting font size to small, the full line is not visible. In AndroidAPS 3.1.0 the issue is worse, and also affects the start screen where the amount of insulin remaining in the cartridge is not visible.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S20 FE"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In the treatment menu, entries are only partially visible and can therefore no longer be deleted (at least in portrait mode).", "text": "Entrys in the treatment menu only partially visible In the treatment menu, entries are only partially visible and can therefore no longer be deleted (at least in portrait mode). Even when setting font size to small, the full line is not visible. In AndroidAPS 3.1.0 the issue is worse, and also affects the start screen where the amount of insulin remaining in the cartridge is not visible.   Samsung Galaxy S20 FE  In the treatment menu, entries are only partially visible and can therefore no longer be deleted (at least in portrait mode)."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1395", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1395, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1395, "title": "SMB bolus cancelled without alerts - OmnipodDash - DynISF specific", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1395", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1395", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "SMB boluses are cancelled without alerts, causing no SMB delivery for hours. Logs show 'SMB bolus canceled' after a long connection time. The issue occurs with DynISF and Omnipod Dash, but works with OpenAPS SMB.", "cause": "The SMB bolus is cancelled because the execution (start of delivery) took longer than 1 minute (the limit). The delay is due to the phone being busy (e.g., right after app start) and the pump connection taking too long.", "fix": "No explicit fix is provided, but the maintainer explains the cancellation is due to the execution taking longer than 1 minute. The user suggests it may be a problem between their cheap phone and the pump, implying a need for faster connection.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DynISF", "OpenAPS SMB"], "evidence_quote": "sorry right, canceled because the execution (start of delivery) took longer than 3 min", "text": "SMB bolus cancelled without alerts - OmnipodDash - DynISF specific SMB boluses are cancelled without alerts, causing no SMB delivery for hours. Logs show 'SMB bolus canceled' after a long connection time. The issue occurs with DynISF and Omnipod Dash, but works with OpenAPS SMB. The SMB bolus is cancelled because the execution (start of delivery) took longer than 1 minute (the limit). The delay is due to the phone being busy (e.g., right after app start) and the pump connection taking too long. No explicit fix is provided, but the maintainer explains the cancellation is due to the execution taking longer than 1 minute. The user suggests it may be a problem between their cheap phone and the pump, implying a need for faster connection. Omnipod Dash DynISF OpenAPS SMB sorry right, canceled because the execution (start of delivery) took longer than 3 min"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1425", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1425, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1425, "title": "Minor esthetic bug : Black on gray text", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1425", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1425", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Black text/buttons appear on gray background in preference settings and other areas, making them hard to see. This occurs in various dialogs and number pickers.", "cause": "The text color on buttons is based on `colorPrimary`, and the night theming is not using the default style correctly. The main activity is not in the real dark mode.", "fix": "The issue is solved in the Themeswitcher branch for light and dark mode, and there are plans to merge it in the future. A fix is planned by osodebailar to address the root cause.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The text color on buttons are based on `colorPrimary`. The night theming, is not using the default style correctly. This requires a bit of rework.", "text": "Minor esthetic bug : Black on gray text Black text/buttons appear on gray background in preference settings and other areas, making them hard to see. This occurs in various dialogs and number pickers. The text color on buttons is based on `colorPrimary`, and the night theming is not using the default style correctly. The main activity is not in the real dark mode. The issue is solved in the Themeswitcher branch for light and dark mode, and there are plans to merge it in the future. A fix is planned by osodebailar to address the root cause. Android 10  The text color on buttons are based on `colorPrimary`. The night theming, is not using the default style correctly. This requires a bit of rework."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1506", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1506, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1506, "title": "DST Dana RS stuck at reading history", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1506", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1506", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After DST, AAPS is stuck at reading the pump history. Manually fixing the pump time and resetting APS databases did nothing. The message disappears after some time, but looping and setting temp ratios do not work. Users cannot bolus.", "cause": "The issue may be caused by communication affected by a connected smartwatch if the phone's Bluetooth stack is not good.", "fix": "The solution is to delete history in DanaRS. The procedure is: go to pump, unlock, then while pressing - at the same time press + sign and arrow, appears password 0000, then enter 4, 9, 8, 9 in that order, then message then delete history. Alternatively, manually bolusing on the pump helps. Also, disabling wifi from the watch improved the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DanaRS"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DanaRS"], "evidence_quote": "The solution is “delete history” in DanaRS. The procedure is 1. go to pump 2. Unlock 3. Then while pressing - at the same time press + sign and arrow 4. Appears password 0000 5. Go to third 0 and put 4 6. Go to fourth 0 put 9 7. Go to first 0 put 8 8. Go to second 0 put 9 9. All in this order 10. Message then delete history.", "text": "DST Dana RS stuck at reading history After DST, AAPS is stuck at reading the pump history. Manually fixing the pump time and resetting APS databases did nothing. The message disappears after some time, but looping and setting temp ratios do not work. Users cannot bolus. The issue may be caused by communication affected by a connected smartwatch if the phone's Bluetooth stack is not good. The solution is to delete history in DanaRS. The procedure is: go to pump, unlock, then while pressing - at the same time press + sign and arrow, appears password 0000, then enter 4, 9, 8, 9 in that order, then message then delete history. Alternatively, manually bolusing on the pump helps. Also, disabling wifi from the watch improved the issue. DanaRS DanaRS The solution is “delete history” in DanaRS. The procedure is 1. go to pump 2. Unlock 3. Then while pressing - at the same time press + sign and arrow 4. Appears password 0000 5. Go to third 0 and put 4 6. Go to fourth 0 put 9 7. Go to first 0 put 8 8. Go to second 0 put 9 9. All in this order 10. Message then delete history."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1545", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1545, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1545, "title": "LGS after update - closed loop not working", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1545", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1545", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating AAPS to version 3.0.0.1, the closed loop stops working after a few minutes and falls back to Low Glucose Suspend (LGS). The user has reinstalled the app multiple times, restarted the phone, and reconnected the pump, but the issue persists.", "cause": "The red triangle warning 'BG too close' indicates that BGs are not reliable, which prevents the loop from closing. This is not a bug.", "fix": "The user needs to delete the unreliable BG readings (the red triangle) to allow the loop to close. The thread suggests that this is a known issue and not a bug.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["ACCU-CHEK Spirit Combo"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["ruffy"], "evidence_quote": "You can't close the loop because of the red triangle (BGs are not reliable). This is not a bug.", "text": "LGS after update - closed loop not working After updating AAPS to version 3.0.0.1, the closed loop stops working after a few minutes and falls back to Low Glucose Suspend (LGS). The user has reinstalled the app multiple times, restarted the phone, and reconnected the pump, but the issue persists. The red triangle warning 'BG too close' indicates that BGs are not reliable, which prevents the loop from closing. This is not a bug. The user needs to delete the unreliable BG readings (the red triangle) to allow the loop to close. The thread suggests that this is a known issue and not a bug. ACCU-CHEK Spirit Combo ruffy You can't close the loop because of the red triangle (BGs are not reliable). This is not a bug."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1588", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1588, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1588, "title": "BUG : stuck in temp basal", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1588", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1588", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After stopping the loop, the basal does not kick in; a temp basal of 0 U/h with duration 4800 minutes is stuck and cannot be cancelled from Actions. The DASH tab shows no temp basal, but the main page shows 0 U/h.", "cause": "The bug might be related to AAPS restarting; after phone battery died and restart, the duration was 4800 minutes. It was later believed fixed by PR #1715.", "fix": "Activation of a new DASH solved the problem for one user; another user found that changing profile repeatedly can reset it. The issue was closed as fixed by PR #1715.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DASH"], "evidence_quote": "I belive this bug was fixed with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1715", "text": "BUG : stuck in temp basal After stopping the loop, the basal does not kick in; a temp basal of 0 U/h with duration 4800 minutes is stuck and cannot be cancelled from Actions. The DASH tab shows no temp basal, but the main page shows 0 U/h. The bug might be related to AAPS restarting; after phone battery died and restart, the duration was 4800 minutes. It was later believed fixed by PR #1715. Activation of a new DASH solved the problem for one user; another user found that changing profile repeatedly can reset it. The issue was closed as fixed by PR #1715. DASH DASH I belive this bug was fixed with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1715"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1597", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1597, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1597, "title": "Overlapping Times in basal Tab leading to wrong iob? Dev-i", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1597", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1597", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Temporary basal rates are not cancelled and their times overlap in the basal tab, potentially leading to wrong IOB calculations. The issue is reported with the Omnipod DASH pump.", "cause": "Testing in the thread indicates the overlapping TBRs occur when Nightscout sync is enabled: with NSClient paused, overlap did not reproduce for extended periods, and it returned after unpausing NSClient. MilosKozak observed that AAPS appears to be updating old records, pointing to Nightscout-sync-triggered updates of old temporary basal records as the likely cause.", "fix": "The thread states the issue is hopefully fixed by PR #1715. During investigation, pausing NSClient / disabling Nightscout sync was used as the effective workaround.", "settings_changed": ["NSClient → Paused"], "devices": ["Omnipod DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dash", "nightscout sync", "nsclient"], "evidence_quote": "hopefully fixed by #1715 open new issue if the problem persists", "text": "Overlapping Times in basal Tab leading to wrong iob? Dev-i Temporary basal rates are not cancelled and their times overlap in the basal tab, potentially leading to wrong IOB calculations. The issue is reported with the Omnipod DASH pump. Testing in the thread indicates the overlapping TBRs occur when Nightscout sync is enabled: with NSClient paused, overlap did not reproduce for extended periods, and it returned after unpausing NSClient. MilosKozak observed that AAPS appears to be updating old records, pointing to Nightscout-sync-triggered updates of old temporary basal records as the likely cause. The thread states the issue is hopefully fixed by PR #1715. During investigation, pausing NSClient / disabling Nightscout sync was used as the effective workaround. Omnipod DASH dash nightscout sync nsclient hopefully fixed by #1715 open new issue if the problem persists"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1610", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1610, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1610, "title": "SMS Communicator Not Sending Response in Dev i but still works in Master (tried on multiple phones)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1610", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1610", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "SMS communicator is not sending a response (but will still implement commands). This problem first began when switching from master to dev branch. Tried on multiple phones (S9, Jelly 2, Atom and Note 10) and it's not working on any of them. Master still works fine.", "cause": "The issue was resolved by a commit, but the thread does not explicitly state the root cause.", "fix": "Resolved by commit 6f358bc0c80b902b0abbf6b0dbd77a88b035ee24.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6f358bc0c80b902b0abbf6b0dbd77a88b035ee24", "text": "SMS Communicator Not Sending Response in Dev i but still works in Master (tried on multiple phones) SMS communicator is not sending a response (but will still implement commands). This problem first began when switching from master to dev branch. Tried on multiple phones (S9, Jelly 2, Atom and Note 10) and it's not working on any of them. Master still works fine. The issue was resolved by a commit, but the thread does not explicitly state the root cause. Resolved by commit 6f358bc0c80b902b0abbf6b0dbd77a88b035ee24.   resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6f358bc0c80b902b0abbf6b0dbd77a88b035ee24"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1621", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1621, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1621, "title": "OLD BUG : Activate/Deactivate pod buttons are lit", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1621", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1621", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Both pod activate and deactivate buttons are turned ON (lit, not grayed) all the time, regardless of whether a pod is activated or not.", "cause": "The bug was introduced by styling changes in a recent build, as previously it was caused by styling changes. The issue was resolved in a later build.", "fix": "Update to the latest dev build (e.g., commit 49af54) which works again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The latest (49af54) works again.", "text": "OLD BUG : Activate/Deactivate pod buttons are lit Both pod activate and deactivate buttons are turned ON (lit, not grayed) all the time, regardless of whether a pod is activated or not. The bug was introduced by styling changes in a recent build, as previously it was caused by styling changes. The issue was resolved in a later build. Update to the latest dev build (e.g., commit 49af54) which works again.   The latest (49af54) works again."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1680", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1680, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1680, "title": "Calibrations entered in XDrip cause NSClient to crash", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1680", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1680", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When BG calibrations are entered in XDrip, it causes NSClient to crash. This makes it difficult to manage remotely via NSClient. The problem started after updating to AAPS v3.0.0.1.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly state the root cause, but it is implied that calibrations entered in xDrip are passed to AAPS (NSClient) and then uploaded to Nightscout, causing a crash. The fix commit likely addresses the underlying issue.", "fix": "Fixed by commit 6212bafcee0023fef452faa49b41eeb8ae9c6efa.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre2", "xDrip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OOP2", "NSClient"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6212bafcee0023fef452faa49b41eeb8ae9c6efa", "text": "Calibrations entered in XDrip cause NSClient to crash When BG calibrations are entered in XDrip, it causes NSClient to crash. This makes it difficult to manage remotely via NSClient. The problem started after updating to AAPS v3.0.0.1. The thread does not explicitly state the root cause, but it is implied that calibrations entered in xDrip are passed to AAPS (NSClient) and then uploaded to Nightscout, causing a crash. The fix commit likely addresses the underlying issue. Fixed by commit 6212bafcee0023fef452faa49b41eeb8ae9c6efa. Libre2 xDrip OOP2 NSClient fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6212bafcee0023fef452faa49b41eeb8ae9c6efa"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1698", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1698, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1698, "title": "Wear App stops connecting/synchronizing after installing 3.0.0.2-dev-j  Commit#3d9b08e5 (compatibility break?)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1698", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1698", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After installing AndroidAPS 3.0.0.2-dev-j build #3d9b08e5, the Android Wear app stopped synchronizing. The app seems not to be connected, and Wear->RESEND DATA and Wear->OPEN SETTINGS ON WEAR have no effect.", "cause": "The Wear app version (release) is not compatible with the dev-j build of AndroidAPS due to big reorganization inside Wear dev-j.", "fix": "Update the Wear app to the current dev version. Later commits fixed tiles and other issues, but some problems remained; the final commit referenced suggests opening a new issue if something else remains.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy Watch4 44mm", "TicWatch Pro", "Galaxy Wear 4 watch"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["wear app"], "evidence_quote": "You have to update also Wear.", "text": "Wear App stops connecting/synchronizing after installing 3.0.0.2-dev-j  Commit#3d9b08e5 (compatibility break?) After installing AndroidAPS 3.0.0.2-dev-j build #3d9b08e5, the Android Wear app stopped synchronizing. The app seems not to be connected, and Wear->RESEND DATA and Wear->OPEN SETTINGS ON WEAR have no effect. The Wear app version (release) is not compatible with the dev-j build of AndroidAPS due to big reorganization inside Wear dev-j. Update the Wear app to the current dev version. Later commits fixed tiles and other issues, but some problems remained; the final commit referenced suggests opening a new issue if something else remains. Samsung Galaxy Watch4 44mm TicWatch Pro Galaxy Wear 4 watch Android 10 Android 11 wear app You have to update also Wear."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1707", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1707, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1707, "title": "Strange watch face numbers and no arrow", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1707", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1707", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "On AndroidAPS watch faces, the glucose value appears duplicated, the trend arrow is missing or unreadable, and the date display shows wrong values (e.g., '52' instead of day name, '52 MAY' instead of date). Also, watch face settings crash when scrolling to end, and only the Actions tile works.", "cause": "The issue was caused by bugs in the AndroidAPS dev build, which were fixed by specific commits. The duplicate numbers and missing arrow were fixed by commit e01647d496e405d3ae9617ae76f353147181ec02, and the IOB display was fixed by commit 7ef313e4aa22acd10571842f1dcfe36400c34fc7. The settings crash was resolved by uninstalling and reinstalling the watch app.", "fix": "Update to the latest build that includes the fixes (commits e01647d496e405d3ae9617ae76f353147181ec02 and 7ef313e4aa22acd10571842f1dcfe36400c34fc7). For the settings crash, uninstall the watch app and install it again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["TicWatch Pro", "TicWatch Pro 3 GPS 1853"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear os"], "evidence_quote": "The main screen already shows the trend arrow and the glucose value does not appear twice. TT Tiles are still not working.", "text": "Strange watch face numbers and no arrow On AndroidAPS watch faces, the glucose value appears duplicated, the trend arrow is missing or unreadable, and the date display shows wrong values (e.g., '52' instead of day name, '52 MAY' instead of date). Also, watch face settings crash when scrolling to end, and only the Actions tile works. The issue was caused by bugs in the AndroidAPS dev build, which were fixed by specific commits. The duplicate numbers and missing arrow were fixed by commit e01647d496e405d3ae9617ae76f353147181ec02, and the IOB display was fixed by commit 7ef313e4aa22acd10571842f1dcfe36400c34fc7. The settings crash was resolved by uninstalling and reinstalling the watch app. Update to the latest build that includes the fixes (commits e01647d496e405d3ae9617ae76f353147181ec02 and 7ef313e4aa22acd10571842f1dcfe36400c34fc7). For the settings crash, uninstall the watch app and install it again. TicWatch Pro TicWatch Pro 3 GPS 1853 wear os The main screen already shows the trend arrow and the glucose value does not appear twice. TT Tiles are still not working."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1726", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1726, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1726, "title": "Wear OS DigitalStyle watchface time is missing minutes", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1726", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1726", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "On the latest 3.0.0.2 dev k build 49163c43d, the digitalstyle watch face seems to have font issues (too big when set to AM/PM vs 24 hr) or missing info in the time.", "cause": "The hourString function in DateUtil.kt uses format \"hha\" which includes the AM/PM marker, causing the time display to be too big or missing minutes in AM/PM mode.", "fix": "Change the format string in hourString from \"hha\" to \"hh\" when not in 24-hour format.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "If this class\n```\nfun hourString(mills: Long): String {\n        var format = \"hha\"\n        if (android.text.format.DateFormat.is24HourFormat(context)) {\n            format = \"HH\"\n        }\n        return DateTime(mills).toString(DateTimeFormat.forPattern(format))\n    }\n```\nin\ninfo/nightscout/androidaps/utils/DateUtil.kt\n\nis changed to \n```\nfun hourString(mills: Long): String {\n        var format = \"hh\"\n        if (android.text.format.DateFormat.is24HourFormat(context)) {\n            format = \"HH\"\n        }\n        return DateTime(mills).toString(DateTimeFormat.forPattern(format))\n    }\n```\n\nThe display looks correct.", "text": "Wear OS DigitalStyle watchface time is missing minutes On the latest 3.0.0.2 dev k build 49163c43d, the digitalstyle watch face seems to have font issues (too big when set to AM/PM vs 24 hr) or missing info in the time. The hourString function in DateUtil.kt uses format \"hha\" which includes the AM/PM marker, causing the time display to be too big or missing minutes in AM/PM mode. Change the format string in hourString from \"hha\" to \"hh\" when not in 24-hour format.   If this class\n```\nfun hourString(mills: Long): String {\n        var format = \"hha\"\n        if (android.text.format.DateFormat.is24HourFormat(context)) {\n            format = \"HH\"\n        }\n        return DateTime(mills).toString(DateTimeFormat.forPattern(format))\n    }\n```\nin\ninfo/nightscout/androidaps/utils/DateUtil.kt\n\nis changed to \n```\nfun hourString(mills: Long): String {\n        var format = \"hh\"\n        if (android.text.format.DateFormat.is24HourFormat(context)) {\n            format = \"HH\"\n        }\n        return DateTime(mills).toString(DateTimeFormat.forPattern(format))\n    }\n```\n\nThe display looks correct."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1727", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1727, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1727, "title": "Wear App: Tiles not communicating with app on phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1727", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1727", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When trying to enter carbs using the AndroidAPS tiles on a Galaxy Watch 4, the confirmation dialog no longer appears and the carbs are not sent to the phone. The issue occurs intermittently and is not fixed by reinstalling the wear app or resetting the watch.", "cause": "The current dev wear code is not compatible with xDrip watchfaces anymore (communication has changed). The tiles are part of the AAPS watch face and may not work when an xDrip watchface is active.", "fix": "Use an AAPS watchface (e.g., AAPS DigitalStyle) instead of an xDrip watchface. Also ensure the same version of AAPS and WEAR is used.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Galaxy Watch 4", "Samsung s21FE", "Dexcom G6", "Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["BYODA", "xdrip watchface", "tiles"], "evidence_quote": "current dev wear code is not compatible with xdrip watchfaces anymore (comm has changed) You must use the same version of AAPS and WEAR to keep it working", "text": "Wear App: Tiles not communicating with app on phone When trying to enter carbs using the AndroidAPS tiles on a Galaxy Watch 4, the confirmation dialog no longer appears and the carbs are not sent to the phone. The issue occurs intermittently and is not fixed by reinstalling the wear app or resetting the watch. The current dev wear code is not compatible with xDrip watchfaces anymore (communication has changed). The tiles are part of the AAPS watch face and may not work when an xDrip watchface is active. Use an AAPS watchface (e.g., AAPS DigitalStyle) instead of an xDrip watchface. Also ensure the same version of AAPS and WEAR is used. Galaxy Watch 4 Samsung s21FE Dexcom G6 Omnipod Dash BYODA xdrip watchface tiles current dev wear code is not compatible with xdrip watchfaces anymore (comm has changed) You must use the same version of AAPS and WEAR to keep it working"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1741", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1741, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1741, "title": "[3.0.0.2-dev-k] \"Error CGM data unchanged for the past ~45m...\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1741", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1741", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User reports receiving an error message 'CGM data unchanged for the past ~45m...' even though CGM data was changing (values ranged from 4.7 to 5.1 mmol). The error cleared after about 30 minutes.", "cause": "The error is by design in AAPS for Libre sensors (FSL2 with patched LibreLink). It is a protection against a state where the FSL reports a constant (wrong) value for a longer time. The check uses delta and average delta over the period, which was close to zero in this case.", "fix": "No fix provided; it is by design. The restriction is not present when using Dexcom.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["FSL2", "LibreLink"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["patched LibreLink"], "evidence_quote": "then it's by OAPS design. it's protection from state when FSL report constant (wrong) value for a longer time This restriction is not while using Dexcom", "text": "[3.0.0.2-dev-k] \"Error CGM data unchanged for the past ~45m...\" User reports receiving an error message 'CGM data unchanged for the past ~45m...' even though CGM data was changing (values ranged from 4.7 to 5.1 mmol). The error cleared after about 30 minutes. The error is by design in AAPS for Libre sensors (FSL2 with patched LibreLink). It is a protection against a state where the FSL reports a constant (wrong) value for a longer time. The check uses delta and average delta over the period, which was close to zero in this case. No fix provided; it is by design. The restriction is not present when using Dexcom. FSL2 LibreLink patched LibreLink then it's by OAPS design. it's protection from state when FSL report constant (wrong) value for a longer time This restriction is not while using Dexcom"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1743", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1743, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1743, "title": "No syncing between NSClients -> AAPS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1743", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1743", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Actions taken from NSClient are not synced to AAPS master, for example entering carbs or setting a temp target like 'eating soon', although they are synced to Nightscout. Syncing the other way from AAPS to NSClients and Nightscout works fine.", "cause": "For one user, the issue was fixed by building and installing NSClient2, suggesting something was corrupted on previous installation. Another user reported that upgrading to NS Dev did not work, but NSClient2 worked.", "fix": "Build and install NSClient2, which works fine. Upgrading to NS Dev did not work.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nsclient", "nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "Issue fixed for my case. Built and installed NSClient2 which works fine. Upgrading to NS Dev did not work. Apparently something was corrupted on previous installation.", "text": "No syncing between NSClients -> AAPS Actions taken from NSClient are not synced to AAPS master, for example entering carbs or setting a temp target like 'eating soon', although they are synced to Nightscout. Syncing the other way from AAPS to NSClients and Nightscout works fine. For one user, the issue was fixed by building and installing NSClient2, suggesting something was corrupted on previous installation. Another user reported that upgrading to NS Dev did not work, but NSClient2 worked. Build and install NSClient2, which works fine. Upgrading to NS Dev did not work.  nsclient nightscout Issue fixed for my case. Built and installed NSClient2 which works fine. Upgrading to NS Dev did not work. Apparently something was corrupted on previous installation."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1760", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1760, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1760, "title": "Last Dev crash at start", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1760", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1760", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Last dev crash systematically at start. Clean install did not help. User is on Samsung s10e Android 12 One UI 4.1 with Omnipod Dash. Crash appears with the last update for Dash.", "cause": "The crash was caused by the Wear module not being updated, leading to crashes at start. The Dash pod state deserialization error was not the cause.", "fix": "Disable the Wear module or update the Wear app to match the main app version. After updating Wear, the issue was resolved.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["omnipod dash", "wear"], "evidence_quote": "Crashs were cause by the wear module not by dash.", "text": "Last Dev crash at start Last dev crash systematically at start. Clean install did not help. User is on Samsung s10e Android 12 One UI 4.1 with Omnipod Dash. Crash appears with the last update for Dash. The crash was caused by the Wear module not being updated, leading to crashes at start. The Dash pod state deserialization error was not the cause. Disable the Wear module or update the Wear app to match the main app version. After updating Wear, the issue was resolved. Omnipod Dash Android 12 omnipod dash wear Crashs were cause by the wear module not by dash."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1768", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1768, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1768, "title": "Wrong IOB, because boluses are shown twice", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1768", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1768", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "In AndroidAPS 3.0, some meal-boluses and SMBs are shown twice in the treatments-tab, while the pump shows them only once, leading to incorrect (too high) IOB.", "cause": "The timestamp of a bolus was not adjusted to the time it was actually received by the pump; it kept the time the command was sent. This caused a mismatch when pairing with pump history, leading to duplicate entries. This behavior was lost during refactoring to Kotlin and new database code.", "fix": "Adjust the timestamp of the bolus entry to the time it was received on the pump (instead of the time the command was sent), so that when history is read, the bolus can be correctly paired with the pump history entry. This fix is implemented in branch bug1768_2xbolus and PR #1825.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic 754", "Samsung A52 5G", "S22 Ultra", "522 OL Pro", "Rileylink W2"], "android_versions": ["Android 12.0"], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic", "Rileylink", "OL"], "evidence_quote": "So when we do bolus on pump, before entry is written into database, timestamp is adjusted (it doesn't contain previous timestamp, when AAPS/orefx sent bolus command, but timestamp when bolus was received on pump), so when history comes back it will easily be tied to actual bolus record. This might prevent double bolus...", "text": "Wrong IOB, because boluses are shown twice In AndroidAPS 3.0, some meal-boluses and SMBs are shown twice in the treatments-tab, while the pump shows them only once, leading to incorrect (too high) IOB. The timestamp of a bolus was not adjusted to the time it was actually received by the pump; it kept the time the command was sent. This caused a mismatch when pairing with pump history, leading to duplicate entries. This behavior was lost during refactoring to Kotlin and new database code. Adjust the timestamp of the bolus entry to the time it was received on the pump (instead of the time the command was sent), so that when history is read, the bolus can be correctly paired with the pump history entry. This fix is implemented in branch bug1768_2xbolus and PR #1825. Medtronic 754 Samsung A52 5G S22 Ultra 522 OL Pro Rileylink W2 Android 12.0 Medtronic Rileylink OL So when we do bolus on pump, before entry is written into database, timestamp is adjusted (it doesn't contain previous timestamp, when AAPS/orefx sent bolus command, but timestamp when bolus was received on pump), so when history comes back it will easily be tied to actual bolus record. This might prevent double bolus..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1792", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1792, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1792, "title": "Can't stop \"pump unreachable\" alarm", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1792", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1792", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User gets a 'pump unreachable' alarm that beeps repeatedly in the middle of the night. Pressing OK or doing a manual refresh does not stop it; there is no visible window with buttons to stop it. Swiping away AAPS messages, refreshing pod status, or quitting AAPS via the 3-dots menu does not stop the alarm (AAPS restarts itself and the alarm continues, sometimes with a different sound). Only force stopping AAPS and clearing cache memory stops the alarm.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A maintainer (MilosKozak) commented 'it seems to be only concurrecy issue...' after reviewing logs, but no specific cause is confirmed.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix. Workarounds mentioned by the user include force stopping AAPS and clearing cache, or quitting AAPS via the 3-dots menu (which sometimes stops the alarm immediately). The maintainer made logging improvements and asked for new logs, but no permanent fix is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dash pod", "G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Dash pod", "G6"], "evidence_quote": "I had to force stop AAPS and empty cache memory to stop the alarm.", "text": "Can't stop \"pump unreachable\" alarm User gets a 'pump unreachable' alarm that beeps repeatedly in the middle of the night. Pressing OK or doing a manual refresh does not stop it; there is no visible window with buttons to stop it. Swiping away AAPS messages, refreshing pod status, or quitting AAPS via the 3-dots menu does not stop the alarm (AAPS restarts itself and the alarm continues, sometimes with a different sound). Only force stopping AAPS and clearing cache memory stops the alarm. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A maintainer (MilosKozak) commented 'it seems to be only concurrecy issue...' after reviewing logs, but no specific cause is confirmed. The thread does not state a definitive fix. Workarounds mentioned by the user include force stopping AAPS and clearing cache, or quitting AAPS via the 3-dots menu (which sometimes stops the alarm immediately). The maintainer made logging improvements and asked for new logs, but no permanent fix is provided. Dash pod G6 Dash pod G6 I had to force stop AAPS and empty cache memory to stop the alarm."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1816", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1816, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1816, "title": "Considering lowest possible basal value willst profile reduction", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1816", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1816", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Cannot set the profile to a lower rate than 100% because at least one basal value is already at the lowest possible value (e.g., 0.05 units on Omnipod DASH), preventing definition of a lower profile for sports.", "cause": "The profile reduction logic does not consider the pump's minimum basal rate, so it tries to reduce values already at the minimum, causing an error.", "fix": "No fix was implemented; the issue was closed. Suggested workarounds include preparing an extra profile (not just %) and switching to it, or using diluted insulin.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I suggest to enhance the logic of profile reduction by considering the lowest possible minimum that the pump is able to handle.", "text": "Considering lowest possible basal value willst profile reduction Cannot set the profile to a lower rate than 100% because at least one basal value is already at the lowest possible value (e.g., 0.05 units on Omnipod DASH), preventing definition of a lower profile for sports. The profile reduction logic does not consider the pump's minimum basal rate, so it tries to reduce values already at the minimum, causing an error. No fix was implemented; the issue was closed. Suggested workarounds include preparing an extra profile (not just %) and switching to it, or using diluted insulin. Omnipod DASH  I suggest to enhance the logic of profile reduction by considering the lowest possible minimum that the pump is able to handle."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1853", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1853, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1853, "title": "Omnipod EROS: There is no way to forcefully wipe/reset the pod state in case of \"emergency\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1853", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1853", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The Omnipod EROS driver has a bug that can lead to a situation where users get stuck with a pod registration that can not be continued or discarded. Several users reported running into this problem as a result of Pod activation failure. In that state both the 'Deactivate Pod' and 'Discard Pod' buttons are disabled/invisible.", "cause": "The underlying problem is in not discarding/handling pod state correctly. The 'Discard' button is active and responsive but pressing it does not have the expected effect (no errors), assuming the underlying code does not allow discarding while the pump is in this state.", "fix": "A fix is being prepared through issue #1882, and the commit 00f0446c21e059f1287333fc72578daeb6f8c8c2 is proposed to be left in (developer mode) as an optional escape. The workaround for not losing objectives is importing 3.0 settings in AAPS version 2.8.1, discard the Pod and then export preferences that can be imported by AAPS 3.0.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod EROS", "Omnipod DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["omnipod eros", "omnipod dash", "developer mode"], "evidence_quote": "Discarding Pod is not Discarding properly.... Think I found the (underlying) problem is in not discarding/handling pod state correctly. Have to look into this ... Will do a PR this week", "text": "Omnipod EROS: There is no way to forcefully wipe/reset the pod state in case of \"emergency\" The Omnipod EROS driver has a bug that can lead to a situation where users get stuck with a pod registration that can not be continued or discarded. Several users reported running into this problem as a result of Pod activation failure. In that state both the 'Deactivate Pod' and 'Discard Pod' buttons are disabled/invisible. The underlying problem is in not discarding/handling pod state correctly. The 'Discard' button is active and responsive but pressing it does not have the expected effect (no errors), assuming the underlying code does not allow discarding while the pump is in this state. A fix is being prepared through issue #1882, and the commit 00f0446c21e059f1287333fc72578daeb6f8c8c2 is proposed to be left in (developer mode) as an optional escape. The workaround for not losing objectives is importing 3.0 settings in AAPS version 2.8.1, discard the Pod and then export preferences that can be imported by AAPS 3.0. Omnipod EROS Omnipod DASH omnipod eros omnipod dash developer mode Discarding Pod is not Discarding properly.... Think I found the (underlying) problem is in not discarding/handling pod state correctly. Have to look into this ... Will do a PR this week"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-186", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 186, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 186, "title": "[2.8] TDD in Statistics is misscalculated", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/186", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/186", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In AAPS 2.8, the Total Daily Dose (TDD) for today is shown as zero, and the Average 8 days results are corrupted. After a phone restart, statistics show completely different and obviously corrupted results, with a repeating value of 25.62 (the user's base basal insulin). Pre-migration data (before upgrading to 2.8) cannot be loaded, showing no TIR and average for days before installation.", "cause": "The issue appears to be related to data migration from version 2.7.0 to 2.8.0. The user migrated on January 3rd, which is the last day with correct numbers. The problem seems to resolve itself once all data has been logged under version 2.8, as the user confirmed that statistics became correct after all days were under 2.8.", "fix": "The problem resolved itself after waiting several days until all statistics were logged under version 2.8. The user confirmed: 'The Statistics are correctly calculated now that all of them have been logged under 2.8 version.' No specific setting change was required.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The Statistics are correctly calculated now that all of them have been logged under 2.8 version.", "text": "[2.8] TDD in Statistics is misscalculated In AAPS 2.8, the Total Daily Dose (TDD) for today is shown as zero, and the Average 8 days results are corrupted. After a phone restart, statistics show completely different and obviously corrupted results, with a repeating value of 25.62 (the user's base basal insulin). Pre-migration data (before upgrading to 2.8) cannot be loaded, showing no TIR and average for days before installation. The issue appears to be related to data migration from version 2.7.0 to 2.8.0. The user migrated on January 3rd, which is the last day with correct numbers. The problem seems to resolve itself once all data has been logged under version 2.8, as the user confirmed that statistics became correct after all days were under 2.8. The problem resolved itself after waiting several days until all statistics were logged under version 2.8. The user confirmed: 'The Statistics are correctly calculated now that all of them have been logged under 2.8 version.' No specific setting change was required.   The Statistics are correctly calculated now that all of them have been logged under 2.8 version."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1877", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1877, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1877, "title": "In Bolus calculator the insulin coloring in dark blue is hard to read", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1877", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1877", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "In the Bolus calculator, the insulin value (IE) is colored dark blue, which is hard to read on a dark background, especially for visually impaired users. The contrast between the blue text and the black background is insufficient.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "if you have a dark background, then the blue of the insulin value is hard to read for visually impaired users.", "text": "In Bolus calculator the insulin coloring in dark blue is hard to read In the Bolus calculator, the insulin value (IE) is colored dark blue, which is hard to read on a dark background, especially for visually impaired users. The contrast between the blue text and the black background is insufficient.     if you have a dark background, then the blue of the insulin value is hard to read for visually impaired users."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1891", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1891, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1891, "title": "AAPS 3.0.0.2 Dash Pod Activation problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1891", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1891", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User is unable to activate a new Dash pod using AAPS 3.0.0.2 on a Samsung A21 phone with Android 12. After multiple retries, activation fails with error: 'Generic error: java.lang.illegalStateException: Trying to set Bluetooth Address to E2:D9:61:24:51:E0, but it is already set to CA:C8:61:24:51:E0'.", "cause": "According to maintainer Theodoor, the issue is likely due to older Pod firmware versions distributed in Canada and the US, combined with Android 11/12, where specific phones are unable to 'see' the DASH Pod. The error suggests AAPS is seeing an unknown DASH Pod in the neighborhood with a different Bluetooth address.", "fix": "No definitive fix. Maintainer suggests resetting the Bluetooth app (clear cache and memory, force close, reboot) and ensuring no other DASH Pods are nearby. However, he states this is Pod/Phone hardware related and there is no solution; user may try different phone hardware.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dash Pod", "Samsung A21", "Samsung A51"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["BYODA", "XDrip"], "evidence_quote": "We found Pods running older Firmware versions are still distributed in CA and the US. We have reports from users running Android version 11 and/or 12 experiencing the problem where specific phones are unable to \"see\" the DASH Pod.", "text": "AAPS 3.0.0.2 Dash Pod Activation problem User is unable to activate a new Dash pod using AAPS 3.0.0.2 on a Samsung A21 phone with Android 12. After multiple retries, activation fails with error: 'Generic error: java.lang.illegalStateException: Trying to set Bluetooth Address to E2:D9:61:24:51:E0, but it is already set to CA:C8:61:24:51:E0'. According to maintainer Theodoor, the issue is likely due to older Pod firmware versions distributed in Canada and the US, combined with Android 11/12, where specific phones are unable to 'see' the DASH Pod. The error suggests AAPS is seeing an unknown DASH Pod in the neighborhood with a different Bluetooth address. No definitive fix. Maintainer suggests resetting the Bluetooth app (clear cache and memory, force close, reboot) and ensuring no other DASH Pods are nearby. However, he states this is Pod/Phone hardware related and there is no solution; user may try different phone hardware. Dash Pod Samsung A21 Samsung A51 Android 12 BYODA XDrip We found Pods running older Firmware versions are still distributed in CA and the US. We have reports from users running Android version 11 and/or 12 experiencing the problem where specific phones are unable to \"see\" the DASH Pod."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1920", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1920, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1920, "title": "3.1.0 White Theme Problems", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1920", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1920", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using Light Theme on a Pixel 5 App crashes and can't be restarted. Keeps on crashing and AAPS doesn't open again. Same behavior reported on OnePlus 3 and OnePlus 8 Pro.", "cause": "The crash is caused by an InflateException in the overview_fragment layout when switching to light theme, as shown in the logcat.", "fix": "The issue was solved with pull request #1926, which likely fixed the layout inflation error.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 5", "OnePlus 3", "OnePlus 8 Pro"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "solved with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1926", "text": "3.1.0 White Theme Problems When using Light Theme on a Pixel 5 App crashes and can't be restarted. Keeps on crashing and AAPS doesn't open again. Same behavior reported on OnePlus 3 and OnePlus 8 Pro. The crash is caused by an InflateException in the overview_fragment layout when switching to light theme, as shown in the logcat. The issue was solved with pull request #1926, which likely fixed the layout inflation error. Pixel 5 OnePlus 3 OnePlus 8 Pro  solved with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/1926"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1947", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1947, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1947, "title": "max_iob = 0 after upgrading to AAPS 3.1.0? Maybe due to new objectives questions?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1947", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1947", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After upgrading to AAPS 3.1.0, new objectives questions appeared, and the restriction to max_iob = 0 seems to apply. Even after answering the questions correctly, max_iob remains 0 under the loop tab.", "cause": "The issue was caused by misconfiguration: the Loop APS mode was set to LGS instead of Closed Loop, which enforces max_iob = 0.", "fix": "Change the Loop APS mode setting from LGS to Closed Loop in the settings.", "settings_changed": ["Loop APS mode → Closed Loop"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "And in the settings about Loop APS mode, I found the setting to change it from LGS to Closed Loop and - et voîla - objective 7 is green", "text": "max_iob = 0 after upgrading to AAPS 3.1.0? Maybe due to new objectives questions? After upgrading to AAPS 3.1.0, new objectives questions appeared, and the restriction to max_iob = 0 seems to apply. Even after answering the questions correctly, max_iob remains 0 under the loop tab. The issue was caused by misconfiguration: the Loop APS mode was set to LGS instead of Closed Loop, which enforces max_iob = 0. Change the Loop APS mode setting from LGS to Closed Loop in the settings.   And in the settings about Loop APS mode, I found the setting to change it from LGS to Closed Loop and - et voîla - objective 7 is green"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1948", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1948, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1948, "title": "Both 3.1.0.1 full-release and its dev version have a bluetooth permission error", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1948", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1948", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating to 3.1.0.1, a bluetooth permission error occurs in both full-release and dev versions. The user could not find a setting to enable bluetooth for AAPS and rolled back to 3.1.0-dev.", "cause": "The issue was triggered by the 3.1.0.1 code, affecting Android versions 9, 10, and 11, but not Android 12. The maintainer could replicate on an older phone.", "fix": "The maintainer fixed the issue in master.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana R", "Dana-i"], "android_versions": ["Android 9", "Android 10", "Android 11", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "fixed in master", "text": "Both 3.1.0.1 full-release and its dev version have a bluetooth permission error After updating to 3.1.0.1, a bluetooth permission error occurs in both full-release and dev versions. The user could not find a setting to enable bluetooth for AAPS and rolled back to 3.1.0-dev. The issue was triggered by the 3.1.0.1 code, affecting Android versions 9, 10, and 11, but not Android 12. The maintainer could replicate on an older phone. The maintainer fixed the issue in master. Dana R Dana-i Android 9 Android 10 Android 11 Android 12  fixed in master"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1956", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1956, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1956, "title": "[3.1.0] [master or dev] Error \"Wrong pump device\" on virtual pump after restart", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1956", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1956", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After restarting AAPS, when using a virtual pump, giving insulin or using the calculator results in an error 'Wrong pump device' and an empty progress bar. The error message fills the screen and may truncate the graph. The insulin injection is not saved to database or Nightscout when the error occurs.", "cause": "The thread identifies this as a bug in the Java code, not a configuration issue. The error is caused by a bug in the app's code, as stated by a user and confirmed by the maintainer's fix commit.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by a commit (3f3cdde53bcff139515cf9cdfb9bb5dbd68a4ca2) in the AndroidAPS repository. No specific user-facing fix is described; the resolution is a code fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["virtual pump", "Accu Check Combo", "Dana-I"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["virtual pump", "Combo", "Dana-I", "NSClient"], "evidence_quote": "resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3f3cdde53bcff139515cf9cdfb9bb5dbd68a4ca2", "text": "[3.1.0] [master or dev] Error \"Wrong pump device\" on virtual pump after restart After restarting AAPS, when using a virtual pump, giving insulin or using the calculator results in an error 'Wrong pump device' and an empty progress bar. The error message fills the screen and may truncate the graph. The insulin injection is not saved to database or Nightscout when the error occurs. The thread identifies this as a bug in the Java code, not a configuration issue. The error is caused by a bug in the app's code, as stated by a user and confirmed by the maintainer's fix commit. The issue was resolved by a commit (3f3cdde53bcff139515cf9cdfb9bb5dbd68a4ca2) in the AndroidAPS repository. No specific user-facing fix is described; the resolution is a code fix. virtual pump Accu Check Combo Dana-I virtual pump Combo Dana-I NSClient resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3f3cdde53bcff139515cf9cdfb9bb5dbd68a4ca2"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-1962", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1962, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 1962, "title": "Connection to galaxy watch 4 is not recognized by AAPS 3.1.0.2", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1962", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/1962", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After update to 3.1.0.2 and reinstall of the wear app on Galaxy watch 4, AAPS does not recognize the connection to the watch. The connection app is Samsung Wear and not Google Wear app. In version 3.0.0.2 the app sends data to the watch but actions from the watch didn't affect AAPS phone app.", "cause": "The watch app needs to be signed with the same key as the phone app. When installing via Android Studio debug process, the signingConfigs in the build.gradle file of the wear app must be set accordingly.", "fix": "Set signingConfigs in the 'build.gradle' file of the wear app to use the same signing key as the main app when installing via Android Studio debug process.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Galaxy watch 4", "Samsung Watch 4", "TicWatch"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear app", "samsung wear", "wear os app"], "evidence_quote": "The watch app need to be sign in the same key like the app. In case of installation using idea, debug process, you will need to set signingConfigs in \"build.gradle\" file of the wear.", "text": "Connection to galaxy watch 4 is not recognized by AAPS 3.1.0.2 After update to 3.1.0.2 and reinstall of the wear app on Galaxy watch 4, AAPS does not recognize the connection to the watch. The connection app is Samsung Wear and not Google Wear app. In version 3.0.0.2 the app sends data to the watch but actions from the watch didn't affect AAPS phone app. The watch app needs to be signed with the same key as the phone app. When installing via Android Studio debug process, the signingConfigs in the build.gradle file of the wear app must be set accordingly. Set signingConfigs in the 'build.gradle' file of the wear app to use the same signing key as the main app when installing via Android Studio debug process. Galaxy watch 4 Samsung Watch 4 TicWatch wear app samsung wear wear os app The watch app need to be sign in the same key like the app. In case of installation using idea, debug process, you will need to set signingConfigs in \"build.gradle\" file of the wear."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-199", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 199, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 199, "title": "Basal is On when 0 Basal is registered", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/199", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/199", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The user got a hypo alert because AAPS/log evidence reported the pump was set to 0 basal while the pump was actually still delivering insulin. The problem started around 17:30 without a known trigger, and a restart did not immediately stop it.", "cause": "Nightscout (NS) upload only was not enabled, so AAPS was downloading from NS. NS was bouncing back/corrupting treatment data and could create or overwrite current treatments, including a false 0-basal treatment, that did not match what the pump was actually doing.", "fix": "Set NS to upload only in AndroidAPS; the user did this and it worked. Commenters also recommended completely disabling continuous download from NS and adding a warning, while the maintainer said the issue would be resolved by the new NSClient.", "settings_changed": ["NS → upload only"], "devices": ["omnipod with emalink"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["ns", "emalink", "xdrip", "nsclient"], "evidence_quote": "This is once again a dangerous situation because of NS upload only was not enabled. @smokkelaar now set NS to upload only and it works now.", "text": "Basal is On when 0 Basal is registered The user got a hypo alert because AAPS/log evidence reported the pump was set to 0 basal while the pump was actually still delivering insulin. The problem started around 17:30 without a known trigger, and a restart did not immediately stop it. Nightscout (NS) upload only was not enabled, so AAPS was downloading from NS. NS was bouncing back/corrupting treatment data and could create or overwrite current treatments, including a false 0-basal treatment, that did not match what the pump was actually doing. Set NS to upload only in AndroidAPS; the user did this and it worked. Commenters also recommended completely disabling continuous download from NS and adding a warning, while the maintainer said the issue would be resolved by the new NSClient. omnipod with emalink ns emalink xdrip nsclient This is once again a dangerous situation because of NS upload only was not enabled. @smokkelaar now set NS to upload only and it works now."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2004", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2004, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2004, "title": "[3.1.0.3] - AAPS uses the 5 minute backfilled BG from Xdrip instead of current reading", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2004", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2004", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When xdrip misses a BG due to BT connection issues and backfills on reconnection, AAPS briefly shows the current BG then switches to the backfilled (older) value, displaying a stale reading until the next one arrives.", "cause": "The thread identifies that AAPS receives both the current and backfilled values but displays the older backfilled one, likely because it uses the last received value rather than the most recent timestamp. Some participants argue it's an xDrip issue, but later evidence suggests it's an AAPS issue.", "fix": "A patch by @asquelt (also committed by Milos) fixes the issue by changing the query to select the most recent glucose value. The fix is in the dev branch.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G5 transmitter", "xDrip", "BYODA"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "broadcast", "BYODA"], "evidence_quote": "The patch by @asquelt seems to have fixed it for me. It does seem to make the query slightly slower but not to a point that its worse than the situation before.", "text": "[3.1.0.3] - AAPS uses the 5 minute backfilled BG from Xdrip instead of current reading When xdrip misses a BG due to BT connection issues and backfills on reconnection, AAPS briefly shows the current BG then switches to the backfilled (older) value, displaying a stale reading until the next one arrives. The thread identifies that AAPS receives both the current and backfilled values but displays the older backfilled one, likely because it uses the last received value rather than the most recent timestamp. Some participants argue it's an xDrip issue, but later evidence suggests it's an AAPS issue. A patch by @asquelt (also committed by Milos) fixes the issue by changing the query to select the most recent glucose value. The fix is in the dev branch. G5 transmitter xDrip BYODA xdrip broadcast BYODA The patch by @asquelt seems to have fixed it for me. It does seem to make the query slightly slower but not to a point that its worse than the situation before."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2055", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2055, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2055, "title": "SMBs often fail [3.1.0.3] [DASH]", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2055", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2055", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After an initial SMB has been successfully given, subsequent SMBs often fail for a few loop cycles, resulting in high BG. This started after upgrading from 3.0.3 to 3.1.0.3. There is no notification in AAPS or system when SMBs fail.", "cause": "The SMB command is canceled because both basal and SMB are present in the result, and the SMB command has a timeout of one minute from the original calculation, but the basal command consumes that time. The SMB is canceled due to the timeout check in CommandSMBBolus.kt.", "fix": "The fix was implemented by MilosKozak in commit baab2dad4c50ff9e3ab7d93660f2204d3c2ffcf5. The fix was confirmed by rustymonkey after testing for 36 hours on Boost_Test_Platform, all SMBs were delivered successfully.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod DASH", "Omnipod Eros", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["BYODA", "BYOD"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/baab2dad4c50ff9e3ab7d93660f2204d3c2ffcf5", "text": "SMBs often fail [3.1.0.3] [DASH] After an initial SMB has been successfully given, subsequent SMBs often fail for a few loop cycles, resulting in high BG. This started after upgrading from 3.0.3 to 3.1.0.3. There is no notification in AAPS or system when SMBs fail. The SMB command is canceled because both basal and SMB are present in the result, and the SMB command has a timeout of one minute from the original calculation, but the basal command consumes that time. The SMB is canceled due to the timeout check in CommandSMBBolus.kt. The fix was implemented by MilosKozak in commit baab2dad4c50ff9e3ab7d93660f2204d3c2ffcf5. The fix was confirmed by rustymonkey after testing for 36 hours on Boost_Test_Platform, all SMBs were delivered successfully. Omnipod DASH Omnipod Eros Dexcom G6 Android 11 Android 12 BYODA BYOD fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/baab2dad4c50ff9e3ab7d93660f2204d3c2ffcf5"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2062", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2062, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2062, "title": "No correction by tab \"Treatments\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2062", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2062", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating to 3.1.0.3-dev-a, the user can no longer delete or correct an incorrect bolus entry using the 'Treatments' button. Clicking the trash can icon does nothing; no selection checkboxes appear.", "cause": "A regression introduced in a recent development version broke the delete functionality in the Treatments screen.", "fix": "The fix was implemented by Milos in commit 0ccc5bf. Users should update to a version that includes this commit.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DanaRS", "Dexcom G6", "Oneplus 6", "Pixel 5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Dash", "XDrip", "Byoda"], "evidence_quote": "Milos fixed this with [0ccc5bf](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0ccc5bfdfcb7f3f17f18d47594a8b3f42ca1bcd4)", "text": "No correction by tab \"Treatments\" After updating to 3.1.0.3-dev-a, the user can no longer delete or correct an incorrect bolus entry using the 'Treatments' button. Clicking the trash can icon does nothing; no selection checkboxes appear. A regression introduced in a recent development version broke the delete functionality in the Treatments screen. The fix was implemented by Milos in commit 0ccc5bf. Users should update to a version that includes this commit. DanaRS Dexcom G6 Oneplus 6 Pixel 5 Dash XDrip Byoda Milos fixed this with [0ccc5bf](https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0ccc5bfdfcb7f3f17f18d47594a8b3f42ca1bcd4)"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2063", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2063, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2063, "title": "XHR poll error ", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2063", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2063", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When setting up AAPS Nightscout settings with https://mynasdns:4443, AAPS systematically gets 'xhr poll error'. The connection appears to be established on the NAS side and data seems to arrive, but AAPS is stuck on the error.", "cause": "The issue is related to the reverse proxy configuration on the NAS; specifically, the protocol used for the connection. The user found that selecting WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy resolved the issue.", "fix": "Select WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy of the NAS.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The only thing to do was to select WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy of the NAS.", "text": "XHR poll error  When setting up AAPS Nightscout settings with https://mynasdns:4443, AAPS systematically gets 'xhr poll error'. The connection appears to be established on the NAS side and data seems to arrive, but AAPS is stuck on the error. The issue is related to the reverse proxy configuration on the NAS; specifically, the protocol used for the connection. The user found that selecting WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy resolved the issue. Select WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy of the NAS.   The only thing to do was to select WebSocket instead of HTTP on the reverse proxy of the NAS."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2067", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2067, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2067, "title": "[3.1.0.3] Loop stuck on basal rate despite instance of low BG. Pump unreachable issue?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2067", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2067", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Loop was stuck on basal rate for ~5 hours despite low BG of 62, with no SMBs or rate changes. A pump unreachable error was signaled at 9:30, and normal behavior returned after restarting AAPS. The issue recurred later with the app stuck on an SMB request and pump stuck on basal rate since ~6:30 AM.", "cause": "The thread suggests the issue is related to unreliable Bluetooth connection between AAPS and the pump, possibly due to the phone (Realme 8). The user notes that restarting AAPS immediately reconnects the pump, and the problem stopped after switching phones.", "fix": "Restarting AAPS (exiting and restarting the app) immediately reconnects the pump and resolves the issue. The user also suggests that switching to a different phone resolved the problem.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omni Eros", "Emalink", "G5 BYODA"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["BYODA", "Emalink"], "evidence_quote": "I'll close this. I think the main problem was with unreliable BT connection with that phone (Realme 8). Since I moved to another phone this hasn't recurred significantly...", "text": "[3.1.0.3] Loop stuck on basal rate despite instance of low BG. Pump unreachable issue? Loop was stuck on basal rate for ~5 hours despite low BG of 62, with no SMBs or rate changes. A pump unreachable error was signaled at 9:30, and normal behavior returned after restarting AAPS. The issue recurred later with the app stuck on an SMB request and pump stuck on basal rate since ~6:30 AM. The thread suggests the issue is related to unreliable Bluetooth connection between AAPS and the pump, possibly due to the phone (Realme 8). The user notes that restarting AAPS immediately reconnects the pump, and the problem stopped after switching phones. Restarting AAPS (exiting and restarting the app) immediately reconnects the pump and resolves the issue. The user also suggests that switching to a different phone resolved the problem. Omni Eros Emalink G5 BYODA BYODA Emalink I'll close this. I think the main problem was with unreliable BT connection with that phone (Realme 8). Since I moved to another phone this hasn't recurred significantly..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2130", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2130, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2130, "title": "[3.1.0.2] Loop suddenly stops invoking", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2130", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2130", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Loop is not activated on new BG readings. The app sometimes misses new readings, as seen on overview screen (prediction lines extending from previous reading) and loop screen (last run more than 5 min ago). Occurs daily, no logs generated at time of issue.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. One user reports the problem stopped after updating to Android 13, suggesting OS interference, but this is not confirmed by maintainers.", "fix": "The thread suggests updating to the latest dev version (which reportedly resolved the issue for one user) and updating to Android 13 (which stopped the problem for another user). However, no specific configuration change is stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 13"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The problem stopped reoccurring when updated to android 13 (One UI 5) some 3 weeks ago!!!!!!! Probably my OS was interfering...", "text": "[3.1.0.2] Loop suddenly stops invoking Loop is not activated on new BG readings. The app sometimes misses new readings, as seen on overview screen (prediction lines extending from previous reading) and loop screen (last run more than 5 min ago). Occurs daily, no logs generated at time of issue. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. One user reports the problem stopped after updating to Android 13, suggesting OS interference, but this is not confirmed by maintainers. The thread suggests updating to the latest dev version (which reportedly resolved the issue for one user) and updating to Android 13 (which stopped the problem for another user). However, no specific configuration change is stated. Android 12 Android 13  The problem stopped reoccurring when updated to android 13 (One UI 5) some 3 weeks ago!!!!!!! Probably my OS was interfering..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2222", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2222, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2222, "title": "[Bug] [Combov2] [Latest dev] Preferences tab craches on Android 12", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2222", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2222", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The preferences tab crashes on Android 12 (Samsung Galaxy Flip 4) and the user cannot pair a combo. Other preference screens on other tabs work fine. The problem also occurs on Android 10 and Android 13, but not on Android 11 with the same build.", "cause": "The crash is caused by a ClassCastException where a String cannot be cast to Integer in SharedPreferences, likely due to a wrong value type stored in preferences. The issue appears when settings are imported, as a clean installation without imported data does not crash.", "fix": "The fix is to ignore wrong values in preferences, implemented in commit 57c96770b06aceb6d7868a923bc7e30d6032d88f. Users can also work around by doing a clean installation without importing settings.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy Flip 4", "Jelly 2", "Samsung Galaxy S9"], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 11", "Android 10", "Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["Combov2", "Combo v2", "openAPS SMB", "Overview"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/57c96770b06aceb6d7868a923bc7e30d6032d88f (only ignore wrong value in preferences)", "text": "[Bug] [Combov2] [Latest dev] Preferences tab craches on Android 12 The preferences tab crashes on Android 12 (Samsung Galaxy Flip 4) and the user cannot pair a combo. Other preference screens on other tabs work fine. The problem also occurs on Android 10 and Android 13, but not on Android 11 with the same build. The crash is caused by a ClassCastException where a String cannot be cast to Integer in SharedPreferences, likely due to a wrong value type stored in preferences. The issue appears when settings are imported, as a clean installation without imported data does not crash. The fix is to ignore wrong values in preferences, implemented in commit 57c96770b06aceb6d7868a923bc7e30d6032d88f. Users can also work around by doing a clean installation without importing settings. Samsung Galaxy Flip 4 Jelly 2 Samsung Galaxy S9 Android 12 Android 11 Android 10 Android 13 Combov2 Combo v2 openAPS SMB Overview fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/57c96770b06aceb6d7868a923bc7e30d6032d88f (only ignore wrong value in preferences)"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2239", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2239, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2239, "title": "[EOPATCH2] unable to change profile", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2239", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2239", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "User reports being unable to do a (temp) profile change on AAPS 3.1.0.3-dev-c-nscv3. Another user reports same problem with eoPatch: after initial pairing profile changes worked, but after about 2 hours the profile was unable to switch back from a 130% temp profile.", "cause": "The pump does not accept profile change during active mode. Specifically, the function setNewBasalProfile returns early when a bolus is active, but also when a temp basal is active, which prevents profile changes.", "fix": "The issue was fixed by a commit (0c833d087ba0bdd57824cfa92a3fa28eb7d5db0c). A workaround is to suspend the pump from the eopatch screen and re-enable it, which allows the driver to set the profile again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["eoPatch"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["eopatch"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0c833d087ba0bdd57824cfa92a3fa28eb7d5db0c", "text": "[EOPATCH2] unable to change profile User reports being unable to do a (temp) profile change on AAPS 3.1.0.3-dev-c-nscv3. Another user reports same problem with eoPatch: after initial pairing profile changes worked, but after about 2 hours the profile was unable to switch back from a 130% temp profile. The pump does not accept profile change during active mode. Specifically, the function setNewBasalProfile returns early when a bolus is active, but also when a temp basal is active, which prevents profile changes. The issue was fixed by a commit (0c833d087ba0bdd57824cfa92a3fa28eb7d5db0c). A workaround is to suspend the pump from the eopatch screen and re-enable it, which allows the driver to set the profile again. eoPatch eopatch fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0c833d087ba0bdd57824cfa92a3fa28eb7d5db0c"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-227", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 227, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 227, "title": "Since Update 2.8.1.1 history is empty", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/227", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/227", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Since updating to version 2.8.1.1, the history tab is totally empty regardless of the selected date. The issue is observed in both original and modified AAPS versions, and also in later versions like 2.8.2.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Like the title says, since update to 2.8.1.1 the history is totally empty. Doesn't matter how date I select nothings gets loaded.", "text": "Since Update 2.8.1.1 history is empty Since updating to version 2.8.1.1, the history tab is totally empty regardless of the selected date. The issue is observed in both original and modified AAPS versions, and also in later versions like 2.8.2.     Like the title says, since update to 2.8.1.1 the history is totally empty. Doesn't matter how date I select nothings gets loaded."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2272", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2272, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2272, "title": "Pod is not reached!", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2272", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2272", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User reports error messages 'Pod is not reached!' and another error message after updating to version DEV-D Build 40bbafe14a since December 4th. The user is unable to provide the required logs.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I have the version DEV-D , Build 40bbafe14a since December 4th. installed and get the following error messages:", "text": "Pod is not reached! User reports error messages 'Pod is not reached!' and another error message after updating to version DEV-D Build 40bbafe14a since December 4th. The user is unable to provide the required logs.     I have the version DEV-D , Build 40bbafe14a since December 4th. installed and get the following error messages:"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2300", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2300, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2300, "title": "[DEV] NSClient keeps re-uploading profiles 2 times per minute", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2300", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2300", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "AAPS keeps syncing (resending) the profile with Nightscout 2 times per minute, causing the database to grow larger and larger. The issue starts after a profile switch or directly after upgrading to certain dev versions.", "cause": "The profile upload is not acknowledged by Nightscout, leading to repeated uploads. The issue was fixed by a commit that addressed profile store upload.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by commit 3472f0f83e81164869453e580094677ceb1e5b73, which fixed the profile store upload. Users also used a Python script to remove duplicate profile entries from MongoDB.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Boyda", "XDrip"], "evidence_quote": "profile store upload fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3472f0f83e81164869453e580094677ceb1e5b73", "text": "[DEV] NSClient keeps re-uploading profiles 2 times per minute AAPS keeps syncing (resending) the profile with Nightscout 2 times per minute, causing the database to grow larger and larger. The issue starts after a profile switch or directly after upgrading to certain dev versions. The profile upload is not acknowledged by Nightscout, leading to repeated uploads. The issue was fixed by a commit that addressed profile store upload. The issue was resolved by commit 3472f0f83e81164869453e580094677ceb1e5b73, which fixed the profile store upload. Users also used a Python script to remove duplicate profile entries from MongoDB. Dexcom G6 Boyda XDrip profile store upload fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3472f0f83e81164869453e580094677ceb1e5b73"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2302", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2302, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2302, "title": "time of sync on xDrip and AAPS 3.1.0.3-dev-f dont match", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2302", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2302", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The time between sensor readings is not synchronized between xDrip and AAPS even with Smoothing disabled. AAPS reading from xDrip shows different timestamps, with BG every 6 minutes instead of 5, causing AAPS to not work between readings.", "cause": "The issue is caused by data arriving every 6 minutes instead of 5 minutes or less, likely due to OOP2 reading every 2 minutes (3 readings = 6 minutes) or a Bluetooth issue.", "fix": "The issue was fixed in the newest version of AAPS. For users with 6-minute data, the maintainer advised resolving the primary issue by ensuring data arrives every 5 minutes or less, possibly by asking xDrip developers about OOP2 issues.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre2", "xDrip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OOP2", "patched app"], "evidence_quote": "Until now its working fine, the issue was fixed at newest version. thanks", "text": "time of sync on xDrip and AAPS 3.1.0.3-dev-f dont match The time between sensor readings is not synchronized between xDrip and AAPS even with Smoothing disabled. AAPS reading from xDrip shows different timestamps, with BG every 6 minutes instead of 5, causing AAPS to not work between readings. The issue is caused by data arriving every 6 minutes instead of 5 minutes or less, likely due to OOP2 reading every 2 minutes (3 readings = 6 minutes) or a Bluetooth issue. The issue was fixed in the newest version of AAPS. For users with 6-minute data, the maintainer advised resolving the primary issue by ensuring data arrives every 5 minutes or less, possibly by asking xDrip developers about OOP2 issues. Libre2 xDrip OOP2 patched app Until now its working fine, the issue was fixed at newest version. thanks"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2329", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2329, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2329, "title": "AAPS crashes when applying the setting", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2329", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2329", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Since a recent DEV build, AAPS is terminated immediately when going to Settings or pressing the Settings button. All other functions remain applicable. One user also reports the Eop2 beeping on profile changes.", "cause": "The crashes are traced to an outdated DEV build, specifically commit 7ad13882ef. MilosKozak states the data shown is only a build date, not the actual version, and that the issue is fixed in a newer commit.", "fix": "Upgrade to the latest DEV build.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["byoda", "xdrip"], "evidence_quote": "I see crashes comming from 7ad13882ef The data is only date of build, not version", "text": "AAPS crashes when applying the setting Since a recent DEV build, AAPS is terminated immediately when going to Settings or pressing the Settings button. All other functions remain applicable. One user also reports the Eop2 beeping on profile changes. The crashes are traced to an outdated DEV build, specifically commit 7ad13882ef. MilosKozak states the data shown is only a build date, not the actual version, and that the issue is fixed in a newer commit. Upgrade to the latest DEV build.  byoda xdrip I see crashes comming from 7ad13882ef The data is only date of build, not version"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2349", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2349, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2349, "title": "Keine Notizen zu Nightscout in Android APS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2349", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2349", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user reports that notes entered in AAPS under the carbohydrates button are not transferred to Nightscout. The notes appear in treatments/user input in AAPS but do not arrive in Nightscout.", "cause": null, "fix": "The maintainer tested with dev version and Nightscout 14.2.6 and found notes are visible on Nightscout when hovering over entries. The user later closed the issue after trying Nightscout 15.0.0 and AAPS 3.1.0.3, but no definitive fix was stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I just tested the behaviour with the dev 2022.12.15 and Nightscout version 14.2.6. Everything is working as intended - notes are visible on Nightscout - a bit hidden thought. Notes are only visible if you **hover over the entries**.", "text": "Keine Notizen zu Nightscout in Android APS The user reports that notes entered in AAPS under the carbohydrates button are not transferred to Nightscout. The notes appear in treatments/user input in AAPS but do not arrive in Nightscout.  The maintainer tested with dev version and Nightscout 14.2.6 and found notes are visible on Nightscout when hovering over entries. The user later closed the issue after trying Nightscout 15.0.0 and AAPS 3.1.0.3, but no definitive fix was stated. Android 11  I just tested the behaviour with the dev 2022.12.15 and Nightscout version 14.2.6. Everything is working as intended - notes are visible on Nightscout - a bit hidden thought. Notes are only visible if you **hover over the entries**."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2351", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2351, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2351, "title": "[DEV][NSC V3] Pod/Canula change not reported to NS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2351", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2351", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Pod and cannula changes are not reported to Nightscout (NS). The user switched from Insight to DASH and placed a new pod, but the pod change is not registered in NS. CAGE shows 4+ days from when using NSC V1. Manual entry via actions tab also does not work.", "cause": "The Nightscout server rejected the treatment upload with HTTP 400 error: 'Field date cannot be modified by the client'. This caused the upload to fail and the queue to stall, preventing subsequent records from being sent.", "fix": "The developer changed the processing to continue with upload when an error occurs, allowing subsequent records to be sent despite the faulty one.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Insight", "DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSC V3", "NSClientV3Plugin"], "evidence_quote": "I changed processing to continue with upload when error occurs. Update", "text": "[DEV][NSC V3] Pod/Canula change not reported to NS Pod and cannula changes are not reported to Nightscout (NS). The user switched from Insight to DASH and placed a new pod, but the pod change is not registered in NS. CAGE shows 4+ days from when using NSC V1. Manual entry via actions tab also does not work. The Nightscout server rejected the treatment upload with HTTP 400 error: 'Field date cannot be modified by the client'. This caused the upload to fail and the queue to stall, preventing subsequent records from being sent. The developer changed the processing to continue with upload when an error occurs, allowing subsequent records to be sent despite the faulty one. Insight DASH NSC V3 NSClientV3Plugin I changed processing to continue with upload when error occurs. Update"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2361", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2361, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2361, "title": "Change from NSv3 to NSv1 : no more connection", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2361", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2361", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After switching from NSv3 to NSv1 in AAPS, the app cannot connect to Nightscout web, showing an error, while switching back to NSv3 restores connectivity. The Nightscout site is functional and the API secret is correct.", "cause": "The thread suggests that NSv1 may not be compatible with Nightscout v15 (dev), as indicated by a Discord message referenced by robertrub. However, this is not fully confirmed, and some users report v1 works fine with dev.", "fix": "The issue was closed by robertrub after noting that v1 doesn't work with NS v15 according to a Discord message. No specific fix was provided; users either stay on NSv3 or continue using NSv1 if it works.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["NSv1", "NSv3", "NSC v1", "NSC v3"], "evidence_quote": "as your message on Discord AAPS, it seems normal that v1 doesn't work with NS v15", "text": "Change from NSv3 to NSv1 : no more connection After switching from NSv3 to NSv1 in AAPS, the app cannot connect to Nightscout web, showing an error, while switching back to NSv3 restores connectivity. The Nightscout site is functional and the API secret is correct. The thread suggests that NSv1 may not be compatible with Nightscout v15 (dev), as indicated by a Discord message referenced by robertrub. However, this is not fully confirmed, and some users report v1 works fine with dev. The issue was closed by robertrub after noting that v1 doesn't work with NS v15 according to a Discord message. No specific fix was provided; users either stay on NSv3 or continue using NSv1 if it works. Dexcom G6 Android 13 NSv1 NSv3 NSC v1 NSC v3 as your message on Discord AAPS, it seems normal that v1 doesn't work with NS v15"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2383", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2383, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2383, "title": "[3.1.0.3] NSClient synchronisation stops loop and is extemely slow", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2383", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2383", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "NSClient upload queue has ~180k entries and after 4.5 hours only down to ~160k, then stagnates at ~90k. Restarting NSClient, AAPS, NS, or phone doesn't help. While NSClient is uploading, the loop stops working (manual runs show 'no APS selected').", "cause": "The thread suggests a race condition or busy phone causing the loop to stop, but maintainer MilosKozak states it's not intended and is a result of busy phone, and that disabling broadcast will speed up the process. The exact root cause is not definitively established.", "fix": "Disabling local broadcast and upload to NS in xDrip+ allowed uploading all data in a couple of hours. Also, pausing NSClient makes the loop work. MilosKozak suggests trying dev branch as sync has been improved, and mentions sync is new in 3.2.", "settings_changed": ["local broadcast → disabled", "upload to NS in XDrip+ → disabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClient", "xDrip+", "local broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "This is unlikely, as deactivating the local broadcast and upload to NS in XDrip+ enabled us to upload all data in a couple of hours.", "text": "[3.1.0.3] NSClient synchronisation stops loop and is extemely slow NSClient upload queue has ~180k entries and after 4.5 hours only down to ~160k, then stagnates at ~90k. Restarting NSClient, AAPS, NS, or phone doesn't help. While NSClient is uploading, the loop stops working (manual runs show 'no APS selected'). The thread suggests a race condition or busy phone causing the loop to stop, but maintainer MilosKozak states it's not intended and is a result of busy phone, and that disabling broadcast will speed up the process. The exact root cause is not definitively established. Disabling local broadcast and upload to NS in xDrip+ allowed uploading all data in a couple of hours. Also, pausing NSClient makes the loop work. MilosKozak suggests trying dev branch as sync has been improved, and mentions sync is new in 3.2.  NSClient xDrip+ local broadcast This is unlikely, as deactivating the local broadcast and upload to NS in XDrip+ enabled us to upload all data in a couple of hours."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2424", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2424, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2424, "title": "When syncing to xDrip, only BG and basals are uploaded.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2424", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2424", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When syncing to xDrip, treatments (Carbs & bolus) are missing. Only BG and basals are uploaded.", "cause": "The issue is caused by xDrip not implementing the necessary functionality to receive all data from AAPS.", "fix": "Update to xDrip latest nightly version (2023.06.17) and enable 'Enable Broadcast to xDrip+' and 'Send status line to xDrip+' in AAPS.", "settings_changed": ["Enable Broadcast to xDrip+ → enabled", "Send status line to xDrip+ → enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "Issue fixed with xDrip latest nightly version: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2023.06.17", "text": "When syncing to xDrip, only BG and basals are uploaded. When syncing to xDrip, treatments (Carbs & bolus) are missing. Only BG and basals are uploaded. The issue is caused by xDrip not implementing the necessary functionality to receive all data from AAPS. Update to xDrip latest nightly version (2023.06.17) and enable 'Enable Broadcast to xDrip+' and 'Send status line to xDrip+' in AAPS.  broadcast Issue fixed with xDrip latest nightly version: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2023.06.17"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2426", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2426, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2426, "title": "NEW INFO Dev-h tdd calculation doesnt work in stats tab", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2426", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2426", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "TDD calculation in the stats tab doesn't work anymore; it sometimes takes 15-30 seconds to calculate graphs, and the history browser also stopped working. The issue is intermittent and not resolved by resetting stats or cleaning the database.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["dana-i"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Tdd calculation doesnt work anymore. Maybe related. Also notice really slow refresh of main screen calculations. (takes regularly 15 Till 30 secs to calculate all graphs).", "text": "NEW INFO Dev-h tdd calculation doesnt work in stats tab TDD calculation in the stats tab doesn't work anymore; it sometimes takes 15-30 seconds to calculate graphs, and the history browser also stopped working. The issue is intermittent and not resolved by resetting stats or cleaning the database.   dana-i  Tdd calculation doesnt work anymore. Maybe related. Also notice really slow refresh of main screen calculations. (takes regularly 15 Till 30 secs to calculate all graphs)."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2444", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2444, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2444, "title": "DanaRS pump: Re-pair needed after change from 26.02.2023", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2444", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2444", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After a change on 26.02.2023, the DanaRS pump requires re-pairing frequently (twice in 5 days), even during normal operation, which is annoying and disruptive.", "cause": "The problem is between phone and pump; Dana pumps don't have a way to check if encryption keys are ok, so when the pump doesn't respond, AAPS clears the encryption keys after some attempts, leading to re-pairing.", "fix": "The code causing the issue was removed (commit f651f721e00b71fd2c5a1bec7f92f4a21a5a12d7). The user eventually switched to Dana-i pump to avoid the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DanaRS", "Dana-i", "Pixel5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DanaRS", "Dana-i", "BYODA"], "evidence_quote": "The problem is between phone and pump. On your place I'd try different phone first Sadly Dana pumps don't have a way to check if encryptions keys are ok. Pump simply doesn't respond. Thus reaction of AAPS to not responding pump (after some attempts) is clearing the encryption keys", "text": "DanaRS pump: Re-pair needed after change from 26.02.2023 After a change on 26.02.2023, the DanaRS pump requires re-pairing frequently (twice in 5 days), even during normal operation, which is annoying and disruptive. The problem is between phone and pump; Dana pumps don't have a way to check if encryption keys are ok, so when the pump doesn't respond, AAPS clears the encryption keys after some attempts, leading to re-pairing. The code causing the issue was removed (commit f651f721e00b71fd2c5a1bec7f92f4a21a5a12d7). The user eventually switched to Dana-i pump to avoid the issue. DanaRS Dana-i Pixel5 DanaRS Dana-i BYODA The problem is between phone and pump. On your place I'd try different phone first Sadly Dana pumps don't have a way to check if encryptions keys are ok. Pump simply doesn't respond. Thus reaction of AAPS to not responding pump (after some attempts) is clearing the encryption keys"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2448", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2448, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2448, "title": "[DEV] Status Line is not showing all information", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2448", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2448", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The Statusline shows the date of the last reservoir change and the age of the battery, but not their values. On the Action Screen only parts of the value are shown. In landscape mode it works fine.", "cause": null, "fix": "Selecting 'Skin: Low resolution skin' in settings hides some labels, but not all. The issue was addressed in a commit by MilosKozak.", "settings_changed": ["Skin: Low resolution skin"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "If you select \"Skin: Low resolution skin\" in the settings, then the superfluous, space-eating labels like \"Alter:\" and \"Abgegeben:\" are hidden.", "text": "[DEV] Status Line is not showing all information The Statusline shows the date of the last reservoir change and the age of the battery, but not their values. On the Action Screen only parts of the value are shown. In landscape mode it works fine.  Selecting 'Skin: Low resolution skin' in settings hides some labels, but not all. The issue was addressed in a commit by MilosKozak.   If you select \"Skin: Low resolution skin\" in the settings, then the superfluous, space-eating labels like \"Alter:\" and \"Abgegeben:\" are hidden."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2449", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2449, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2449, "title": "AAPSClient missing entries from AAPS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2449", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2449", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Treatments entered by AAPS (carbs and boluses) are not reflected on AAPSClient, despite websockets being ON on both devices. Other users report similar issues with treatments not appearing or not being taken into account, and profile sync problems.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It suggests possible websocket reconnection issues and notes that the issue has been improved in later versions.", "fix": "The thread indicates that the issue has been improved in later versions (dev-i and later). A user reported that restarting Heroku dynos and performing a full sync from AAPS fixed profile sync issues. No specific configuration change is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["websockets", "v3 API", "NSClient"], "evidence_quote": "this has been improved. open new issue if this re-appear", "text": "AAPSClient missing entries from AAPS Treatments entered by AAPS (carbs and boluses) are not reflected on AAPSClient, despite websockets being ON on both devices. Other users report similar issues with treatments not appearing or not being taken into account, and profile sync problems. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It suggests possible websocket reconnection issues and notes that the issue has been improved in later versions. The thread indicates that the issue has been improved in later versions (dev-i and later). A user reported that restarting Heroku dynos and performing a full sync from AAPS fixed profile sync issues. No specific configuration change is provided. Android 12 Android 11 websockets v3 API NSClient this has been improved. open new issue if this re-appear"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2523", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2523, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2523, "title": "Glucomen daypump patch activation problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2523", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2523", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When connecting a new patch, the screen rotates from vertical to horizontal, causing the app to restart the connection process. The user is unable to reconnect with the patch and must use a new one. Other users report similar issues: the app gets stuck in a loop during patch activation, or gets stuck on 'Connecting' after pairing.", "cause": "The issue appears to be related to an Android pairing problem, as indicated by the log showing a StartBondTask error. The exact root cause is not fully identified, but it is linked to the pairing process.", "fix": "The issue was reportedly resolved by commit fba804b2cb29e7ca25bad43a696bd77e1bf54fdf, but some users still experienced problems after updating. One user suggests wrapping the old pod and paired watch in aluminum foil to prevent interference with the Bluetooth connection. No definitive fix is provided for all cases.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Glucomen day pump", "Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["eopatch", "ble"], "evidence_quote": "resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/fba804b2cb29e7ca25bad43a696bd77e1bf54fdf", "text": "Glucomen daypump patch activation problem When connecting a new patch, the screen rotates from vertical to horizontal, causing the app to restart the connection process. The user is unable to reconnect with the patch and must use a new one. Other users report similar issues: the app gets stuck in a loop during patch activation, or gets stuck on 'Connecting' after pairing. The issue appears to be related to an Android pairing problem, as indicated by the log showing a StartBondTask error. The exact root cause is not fully identified, but it is linked to the pairing process. The issue was reportedly resolved by commit fba804b2cb29e7ca25bad43a696bd77e1bf54fdf, but some users still experienced problems after updating. One user suggests wrapping the old pod and paired watch in aluminum foil to prevent interference with the Bluetooth connection. No definitive fix is provided for all cases. Glucomen day pump Omnipod Dash Android 13 eopatch ble resolved by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/fba804b2cb29e7ca25bad43a696bd77e1bf54fdf"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2524", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2524, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2524, "title": "[DEV] DASH: Temp basal cancelled/stopped by pod for unkown reason, AAPS History not updated", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2524", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2524", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A temp basal of 0 U/h for 600 minutes was set on an Omnipod DASH, but after about 4 hours and 15 minutes the pod stopped the temp basal and resumed its programmed basal rate, while AAPS still showed the temp basal as active. The pod's delivery status changed from TEMP_BASAL_ACTIVE to BASAL_ACTIVE, but AAPS history and status were not updated.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify the root cause. It is suspected that the issue is related to how AAPS handles long-duration temp basals in manual mode (loop disabled), possibly due to a serialization or command handling problem. The user jbr7rr notes that Loop (iOS) had a similar problem and implemented a workaround.", "fix": "A workaround was implemented in pull request #2531, which fixes the core issue so that all basal rates work for all TBR rates. No other fix is stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dash"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dash"], "evidence_quote": "Hey! I think the serialization is not the problem, as Loop (iOS) had the same problem, I implemented a work around for the core issue in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/2531 which has been tested exenstivly, and with that fix all basal rates works for all TBR rates", "text": "[DEV] DASH: Temp basal cancelled/stopped by pod for unkown reason, AAPS History not updated A temp basal of 0 U/h for 600 minutes was set on an Omnipod DASH, but after about 4 hours and 15 minutes the pod stopped the temp basal and resumed its programmed basal rate, while AAPS still showed the temp basal as active. The pod's delivery status changed from TEMP_BASAL_ACTIVE to BASAL_ACTIVE, but AAPS history and status were not updated. The thread does not definitively identify the root cause. It is suspected that the issue is related to how AAPS handles long-duration temp basals in manual mode (loop disabled), possibly due to a serialization or command handling problem. The user jbr7rr notes that Loop (iOS) had a similar problem and implemented a workaround. A workaround was implemented in pull request #2531, which fixes the core issue so that all basal rates work for all TBR rates. No other fix is stated. Dash dash Hey! I think the serialization is not the problem, as Loop (iOS) had the same problem, I implemented a work around for the core issue in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/2531 which has been tested exenstivly, and with that fix all basal rates works for all TBR rates"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2561", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2561, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2561, "title": "Bolus delivery % only for cob and Carbs !?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2561", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2561", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The option 'Deliver this part of bolus wizard result' applies to all components of the bolus wizard calculation, which can lead to overdosing when multiple consecutive carb entries are made within a short time period. For example, entering 60g of carbs in one entry results in 2.93U, but entering 45g then 15g results in 4.02U total, which is more than needed.", "cause": "The bolus wizard calculates a single dose for the end of DIA and applies the 'Deliver this part of bolus wizard result' percentage to all components (BG, trend, IOB, etc.), not just to carbs. This causes overdosing when multiple carb entries are made because each entry gets the full percentage applied, leading to cumulative insulin that exceeds the intended dose.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6616be42791eb8ced53ee6ec2d1f878c1629c897. The commit likely changes the behavior so that the percentage applies only to carbs (COB and new carbs), as proposed by szantos.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The option \"Deliver this part of bolus wizard result\" does what it says, but does it safely represent most user's intention? An overdosing may occur if there are multiple consecutive carb entries within a short time period.", "text": "Bolus delivery % only for cob and Carbs !? The option 'Deliver this part of bolus wizard result' applies to all components of the bolus wizard calculation, which can lead to overdosing when multiple consecutive carb entries are made within a short time period. For example, entering 60g of carbs in one entry results in 2.93U, but entering 45g then 15g results in 4.02U total, which is more than needed. The bolus wizard calculates a single dose for the end of DIA and applies the 'Deliver this part of bolus wizard result' percentage to all components (BG, trend, IOB, etc.), not just to carbs. This causes overdosing when multiple carb entries are made because each entry gets the full percentage applied, leading to cumulative insulin that exceeds the intended dose. The issue was resolved by a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6616be42791eb8ced53ee6ec2d1f878c1629c897. The commit likely changes the behavior so that the percentage applies only to carbs (COB and new carbs), as proposed by szantos.   The option \"Deliver this part of bolus wizard result\" does what it says, but does it safely represent most user's intention? An overdosing may occur if there are multiple consecutive carb entries within a short time period."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2573", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2573, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2573, "title": "[DEV 3.2.0-dev-j cd9f5e4] Problem opening preferences", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2573", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2573", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When opening any option that accesses anything related to preferences, the application crashes and closes. The problem recurs days later or right after an EOPatch2 patch activation, and can be temporarily relieved by switching the pump plugin or deactivating the patch.", "cause": "The EOPatch2 plugin appears to be responsible; after an EOPatch2 patch activation the preferences become inaccessible, while selecting another pump (e.g. Virtual Pump) or deactivating the patch restores access.", "fix": "MilosKozak stated 'temporary fixed by' commit a5774b6e2eb398311c80e9e00c01bede82978633. Users also found switching the pump plugin away from EOPatch2 (e.g. to Virtual Pump) or deactivating the patch temporarily allowed preferences to open.", "settings_changed": ["Pump plugin → Virtual Pump"], "devices": ["EOPatch2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["eopatch2"], "evidence_quote": "temporary fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/a5774b6e2eb398311c80e9e00c01bede82978633", "text": "[DEV 3.2.0-dev-j cd9f5e4] Problem opening preferences When opening any option that accesses anything related to preferences, the application crashes and closes. The problem recurs days later or right after an EOPatch2 patch activation, and can be temporarily relieved by switching the pump plugin or deactivating the patch. The EOPatch2 plugin appears to be responsible; after an EOPatch2 patch activation the preferences become inaccessible, while selecting another pump (e.g. Virtual Pump) or deactivating the patch restores access. MilosKozak stated 'temporary fixed by' commit a5774b6e2eb398311c80e9e00c01bede82978633. Users also found switching the pump plugin away from EOPatch2 (e.g. to Virtual Pump) or deactivating the patch temporarily allowed preferences to open. EOPatch2 eopatch2 temporary fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/a5774b6e2eb398311c80e9e00c01bede82978633"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2581", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2581, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2581, "title": "Double arrows DOWN when BGs are going UP !!", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2581", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2581", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AAPS displays double DOWN arrows even though BG numbers are going up, while the BG source (xDrip) shows the correct arrow. The issue occurs intermittently and is resolved by restarting the phone.", "cause": "The thread identifies the cause as related to the smoothing algorithm in AAPS, as the problem occurs when smoothing is enabled and stops when it is disabled. The issue may be triggered by jumpy BG readings.", "fix": "The fix is to disable the smoothing algorithm in AAPS, or restart the phone as a temporary workaround. A commit was made to address the issue.", "settings_changed": ["Smoothing → off"], "devices": ["xDrip", "G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["smoothing"], "evidence_quote": "I confirm that it is smoothing related. Smoothing was off thill this morning. I set it back ON and an hour later, I get the double down arrows...", "text": "Double arrows DOWN when BGs are going UP !! AAPS displays double DOWN arrows even though BG numbers are going up, while the BG source (xDrip) shows the correct arrow. The issue occurs intermittently and is resolved by restarting the phone. The thread identifies the cause as related to the smoothing algorithm in AAPS, as the problem occurs when smoothing is enabled and stops when it is disabled. The issue may be triggered by jumpy BG readings. The fix is to disable the smoothing algorithm in AAPS, or restart the phone as a temporary workaround. A commit was made to address the issue. xDrip G6 smoothing I confirm that it is smoothing related. Smoothing was off thill this morning. I set it back ON and an hour later, I get the double down arrows..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2582", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2582, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2582, "title": "After application startup loop fails with \"Pump not initialized!\" until manual connection to pump initiated", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2582", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2582", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Whenever AAPS is (re)started, loop is not functional, failing with \"Pump not initialized!\" error, until manual connection to pump is initiated. It may be hours in this state before a manual connection will be made, after which everything works.", "cause": "The primary reason is that the pump disconnects unexpectedly, which is an error state.", "fix": "AAPS can recover from this state now better after a commit (1d6a48d01dcd16a5767940f9e04e3003af60e713) in dev; after a few minutes it connects to pump and succeeds with dosing changes without manual intervention.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana R"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["integrated pump driver"], "evidence_quote": "primary reason is that pump disconnects unexpectly which is an error state. AAPS can recover from this state now better", "text": "After application startup loop fails with \"Pump not initialized!\" until manual connection to pump initiated Whenever AAPS is (re)started, loop is not functional, failing with \"Pump not initialized!\" error, until manual connection to pump is initiated. It may be hours in this state before a manual connection will be made, after which everything works. The primary reason is that the pump disconnects unexpectedly, which is an error state. AAPS can recover from this state now better after a commit (1d6a48d01dcd16a5767940f9e04e3003af60e713) in dev; after a few minutes it connects to pump and succeeds with dosing changes without manual intervention. Dana R Android 13 integrated pump driver primary reason is that pump disconnects unexpectly which is an error state. AAPS can recover from this state now better"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2587", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2587, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2587, "title": "Error Compiling Dev branch", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2587", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2587", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When compiling the dev branch of AndroidAPS with Android Studio, the nsClientRelease variant fails with error: Task 'assembleNsclientRelease' not found in project ':app'. Some candidates are: 'assembleAapsclientRelease'. The fullRelease variant compiles fine.", "cause": "The nsclientRelease is an old name; the dev branch uses aapsclientRelease.", "fix": "Clone the project, switch to dev branch, and sync the project in Android Studio so that the aapsclient variant appears.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "nsclientRelease is old name. Dev is using aapsclientRelease", "text": "Error Compiling Dev branch When compiling the dev branch of AndroidAPS with Android Studio, the nsClientRelease variant fails with error: Task 'assembleNsclientRelease' not found in project ':app'. Some candidates are: 'assembleAapsclientRelease'. The fullRelease variant compiles fine. The nsclientRelease is an old name; the dev branch uses aapsclientRelease. Clone the project, switch to dev branch, and sync the project in Android Studio so that the aapsclient variant appears.   nsclientRelease is old name. Dev is using aapsclientRelease"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2612", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2612, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2612, "title": "AAPS only sporadically receives the BG values from XDrip. DEV-j", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2612", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2612", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "BG values arrive very irregularly in AAPS, sometimes with a 2 hour break. The problem only occurs in the DEV version, not in Master. Also, sync between master and follower via NS V3 is unreliable, while the old method works cleanly.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Initial suggestions point to xDrip+ background/power management issues, but the reporter notes the problem is specific to the DEV version. Later, a maintainer found that setting 'Identify receiver' in xDrip+ fixed it for them, but the original reporter could not confirm. The thread ends with the reporter suspecting an xDrip problem after trying a different xDrip version.", "fix": "No definitive fix is stated. One participant (vanelsberg) resolved the issue for themselves by setting 'Settings -> Inter-app settings -> Identify receiver' in xDrip+, but the original reporter could not confirm this fix. The reporter later found that using a different xDrip version (from blaqone/xDrip) worked better but not perfectly.", "settings_changed": ["Identify receiver → set (in xDrip+ Inter-app settings)"], "devices": ["xDrip", "Juggluco"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["broadcast", "xDrip collector"], "evidence_quote": "Needed to set _Settings -> Inter-app settings -> Identify receiver_ to get it working (https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/Configuration/xdrip.html#xdrip-identify-receiver) So my bad: has been long since I tested xDrip+ for BG source. Never needed to set this so overlooked that option.", "text": "AAPS only sporadically receives the BG values from XDrip. DEV-j BG values arrive very irregularly in AAPS, sometimes with a 2 hour break. The problem only occurs in the DEV version, not in Master. Also, sync between master and follower via NS V3 is unreliable, while the old method works cleanly. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Initial suggestions point to xDrip+ background/power management issues, but the reporter notes the problem is specific to the DEV version. Later, a maintainer found that setting 'Identify receiver' in xDrip+ fixed it for them, but the original reporter could not confirm. The thread ends with the reporter suspecting an xDrip problem after trying a different xDrip version. No definitive fix is stated. One participant (vanelsberg) resolved the issue for themselves by setting 'Settings -> Inter-app settings -> Identify receiver' in xDrip+, but the original reporter could not confirm this fix. The reporter later found that using a different xDrip version (from blaqone/xDrip) worked better but not perfectly. xDrip Juggluco Android 12 broadcast xDrip collector Needed to set _Settings -> Inter-app settings -> Identify receiver_ to get it working (https://wiki.aaps.app/en/latest/Configuration/xdrip.html#xdrip-identify-receiver) So my bad: has been long since I tested xDrip+ for BG source. Never needed to set this so overlooked that option."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2626", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2626, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2626, "title": "[dev-j AND 3.2RC1] AAPS or AAPSClient pushing multiple profile database records to NS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2626", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2626", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating to dev-j or 3.2RC1, AAPS or AAPSClient (or both) send new profile database records to Nightscout with every loop run or more frequently, creating multiple records with new Created and StartDate values. This fills the MongoDB database and can be stopped by pausing NSClient on both apps.", "cause": "The issue appears to be caused by AAPSClient: when a profile edited on AAPS is received on AAPSClient, AAPSClient responds by pushing a new profile record to the database (with the oldest profile as defaultProfile), which is then pushed back to the database from AAPS after being received there from Nightscout/NSClient. This creates an update loop.", "fix": "The issue was resolved in commit 919c79ebf9cf77b0e0ec486858092764bf8aad62. As a workaround, users can keep 'receive profile store' off on AAPS, or use NSClientV3 instead of V1.", "settings_changed": ["Receive profile store → off"], "devices": ["FSL3", "Juggluco", "AAPS", "AAPSClient", "Fitbit Versa"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClientV1", "NSClientV3", "profile store"], "evidence_quote": "It seems to me the issue is AAPSClient. If profile is edited on AAPS phone, and that profile record (newest profile as defaultProfile) is received on AAPSClient phone, AAPSClient responds by pushing a new profile record to db (with the oldest profile in that record as defaultProfile), which is then pushed back to db from AAPS after being received there from nightscout/NSClient.", "text": "[dev-j AND 3.2RC1] AAPS or AAPSClient pushing multiple profile database records to NS After updating to dev-j or 3.2RC1, AAPS or AAPSClient (or both) send new profile database records to Nightscout with every loop run or more frequently, creating multiple records with new Created and StartDate values. This fills the MongoDB database and can be stopped by pausing NSClient on both apps. The issue appears to be caused by AAPSClient: when a profile edited on AAPS is received on AAPSClient, AAPSClient responds by pushing a new profile record to the database (with the oldest profile as defaultProfile), which is then pushed back to the database from AAPS after being received there from Nightscout/NSClient. This creates an update loop. The issue was resolved in commit 919c79ebf9cf77b0e0ec486858092764bf8aad62. As a workaround, users can keep 'receive profile store' off on AAPS, or use NSClientV3 instead of V1. FSL3 Juggluco AAPS AAPSClient Fitbit Versa NSClientV1 NSClientV3 profile store It seems to me the issue is AAPSClient. If profile is edited on AAPS phone, and that profile record (newest profile as defaultProfile) is received on AAPSClient phone, AAPSClient responds by pushing a new profile record to db (with the oldest profile in that record as defaultProfile), which is then pushed back to db from AAPS after being received there from nightscout/NSClient."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2726", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2726, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2726, "title": "BUG: Double down arrows are back", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2726", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2726", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "AAPS shows double down arrows even when glucose is stable or rising, and the arrows can get stuck or appear intermittently. The issue occurs with Dexcom G6 sensors and xDrip, and has been observed across multiple versions.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is speculated that the issue may be related to sensor age, compression lows, or faulty readings, and that xDrip+ in native mode may not provide a trend arrow, causing AAPS to default to double down.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided in the thread. Some users report the arrows stop by themselves. One user suggests that AAPS should calculate trend arrow internally when xDrip+ does not provide one, but no solution is confirmed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "xDrip", "xDrip+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode", "smoothing"], "evidence_quote": "It seem to happen mostly after a compression low or faulty reading. xDrip+ in native mode (G6) then show no trend arrow. When this happens AAPS always show double down arrow. @MilosKozak what does AAPS do if xDrip+ doesn't provide trend arrrow? When smoothing BG data within AAPS, shouldn't AAPS calculate trend arrow also internally?", "text": "BUG: Double down arrows are back AAPS shows double down arrows even when glucose is stable or rising, and the arrows can get stuck or appear intermittently. The issue occurs with Dexcom G6 sensors and xDrip, and has been observed across multiple versions. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is speculated that the issue may be related to sensor age, compression lows, or faulty readings, and that xDrip+ in native mode may not provide a trend arrow, causing AAPS to default to double down. No definitive fix is provided in the thread. Some users report the arrows stop by themselves. One user suggests that AAPS should calculate trend arrow internally when xDrip+ does not provide one, but no solution is confirmed. Dexcom G6 xDrip xDrip+ native mode smoothing It seem to happen mostly after a compression low or faulty reading. xDrip+ in native mode (G6) then show no trend arrow. When this happens AAPS always show double down arrow. @MilosKozak what does AAPS do if xDrip+ doesn't provide trend arrrow? When smoothing BG data within AAPS, shouldn't AAPS calculate trend arrow also internally?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2790", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2790, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2790, "title": "Wear tiles, menus and settings aren't translated for Norwegian language", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2790", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2790", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "In the wear app for AAPS/AAPSClient, most icons in tiles, menu text, and settings are not translated to Norwegian, even though the main AAPS app is translated. Only 'Cancel' appears as 'Avbryt' in the temp-target tile; other tiles and settings remain in English. Changing AAPS language to English changes 'Avbryt' to 'Cancel', but other tiles stay English regardless of AAPS language.", "cause": "The Norwegian translation is associated with the language code 'no' (Norwegian), but Android's default system language for Norway is Norwegian Bokmål, which uses the code 'nb'. The app's resources are in 'values-no-rNO', but Android expects 'values-nb-rNO' for Norwegian Bokmål, so the translations are not applied.", "fix": "Create a new subfolder 'values-nb-rNO' in wear resources and copy the string file from 'values-no-rNO' into it. This fixed the tiles translation issue locally. Additionally, Norwegian Bokmål was added to Crowdin and the old Norwegian translations were uploaded, and the fix was confirmed in dev build fdc9ac1b.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I asked @olorinmaia to create within wear resources a new subfolder `values-nb-rNO` and copy paste in it the string file included into `values-no-rNO` => It fixed the tiles translation issue for him...", "text": "Wear tiles, menus and settings aren't translated for Norwegian language In the wear app for AAPS/AAPSClient, most icons in tiles, menu text, and settings are not translated to Norwegian, even though the main AAPS app is translated. Only 'Cancel' appears as 'Avbryt' in the temp-target tile; other tiles and settings remain in English. Changing AAPS language to English changes 'Avbryt' to 'Cancel', but other tiles stay English regardless of AAPS language. The Norwegian translation is associated with the language code 'no' (Norwegian), but Android's default system language for Norway is Norwegian Bokmål, which uses the code 'nb'. The app's resources are in 'values-no-rNO', but Android expects 'values-nb-rNO' for Norwegian Bokmål, so the translations are not applied. Create a new subfolder 'values-nb-rNO' in wear resources and copy the string file from 'values-no-rNO' into it. This fixed the tiles translation issue locally. Additionally, Norwegian Bokmål was added to Crowdin and the old Norwegian translations were uploaded, and the fix was confirmed in dev build fdc9ac1b.   I asked @olorinmaia to create within wear resources a new subfolder `values-nb-rNO` and copy paste in it the string file included into `values-no-rNO` => It fixed the tiles translation issue for him..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2839", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2839, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2839, "title": "[DEV] Crash on trying to enter minutes in TT window", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2839", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2839", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "App crash when trying to enter duration in temp target dialog. Pressing the minutes field causes keyboard to pop up and app crashes. Also occurs in bolus assistant when numeric keyboard is used.", "cause": "NullPointerException in DigitsKeyListenerWithComma.filter due to Android java lib not properly marked @Nullable.", "fix": "Update to the commit that fixes the @Nullable annotation issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 13"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "try to update Androd java lib was not properly marked @Nullable", "text": "[DEV] Crash on trying to enter minutes in TT window App crash when trying to enter duration in temp target dialog. Pressing the minutes field causes keyboard to pop up and app crashes. Also occurs in bolus assistant when numeric keyboard is used. NullPointerException in DigitsKeyListenerWithComma.filter due to Android java lib not properly marked @Nullable. Update to the commit that fixes the @Nullable annotation issue. Android 11 Android 13  try to update Androd java lib was not properly marked @Nullable"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2844", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2844, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2844, "title": "3.2.0-dev-k Application expired", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2844", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2844", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The 3.2.0-dev-k application expires on startup, dropping into 'Open Loop'.", "cause": "The version tag 'dev-k' was already used and has an expiry date of 2023-09-05, so the app thinks it has expired.", "fix": "The developer updated the version in the dev branch, fixing the mistake.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Version tag \"dev-k\" was already used and has expiry date 2023-09-05. Needs fixing.", "text": "3.2.0-dev-k Application expired The 3.2.0-dev-k application expires on startup, dropping into 'Open Loop'. The version tag 'dev-k' was already used and has an expiry date of 2023-09-05, so the app thinks it has expired. The developer updated the version in the dev branch, fixing the mistake.   Version tag \"dev-k\" was already used and has expiry date 2023-09-05. Needs fixing."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2848", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2848, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2848, "title": "[DEV-M] Widget is broken", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2848", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2848", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The widget is frozen after the update, re-adding (after deleting) is not possible. Widget is available but will not install.", "cause": "The issue is likely related to Samsung One UI 5.x, as multiple users with Samsung phones experienced the problem, while others on Pixel devices did not. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but a fix was provided in PR #2850.", "fix": "Including PR #2850 (by HuismanErik) in the build fixed the widget issue. Users confirmed that after applying this change, the widget can be added again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung S21FE", "Samsung Z Flip 4", "Samsung Fold 4", "Pixel 4a", "Pixel 6 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I did a reinstall with this change https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/2850 and it fixed the Widget", "text": "[DEV-M] Widget is broken The widget is frozen after the update, re-adding (after deleting) is not possible. Widget is available but will not install. The issue is likely related to Samsung One UI 5.x, as multiple users with Samsung phones experienced the problem, while others on Pixel devices did not. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but a fix was provided in PR #2850. Including PR #2850 (by HuismanErik) in the build fixed the widget issue. Users confirmed that after applying this change, the widget can be added again. Samsung S21FE Samsung Z Flip 4 Samsung Fold 4 Pixel 4a Pixel 6 Pro Android 13  I did a reinstall with this change https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/2850 and it fixed the Widget"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2881", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2881, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2881, "title": "Medtrum pump driver default setting and concerns", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2881", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2881", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The Medtrum Nano pump driver does not default to the pump standard settings (terminate after three days and 8 hours grace period) and does not support low reservoir and empty alerts, which can cause issues overnight and when out for the day.", "cause": "The driver's default settings and lack of support for low reservoir and empty alerts were not aligned with pump standard behavior.", "fix": "The driver was updated to enable patch expiration by default and add an option to show non-critical pump alerts including low reservoir warning at 20 units. Also, the no connection alarm is forced to enabled with 30 minutes threshold for the Medtrum driver.", "settings_changed": ["Patch expiration → enabled by default", "Option to show non critical pump alerts → enabled by default", "key_enable_pump_unreachable_alert → true", "key_pump_unreachable_threshold_minutes → 30"], "devices": ["Medtrum Nano"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "Patch expiration enabled by default\n- Option to show non critical pump alerts (enabled by default) including low reservoir warning at 20units.", "text": "Medtrum pump driver default setting and concerns The Medtrum Nano pump driver does not default to the pump standard settings (terminate after three days and 8 hours grace period) and does not support low reservoir and empty alerts, which can cause issues overnight and when out for the day. The driver's default settings and lack of support for low reservoir and empty alerts were not aligned with pump standard behavior. The driver was updated to enable patch expiration by default and add an option to show non-critical pump alerts including low reservoir warning at 20 units. Also, the no connection alarm is forced to enabled with 30 minutes threshold for the Medtrum driver. Medtrum Nano medtrum Patch expiration enabled by default\n- Option to show non critical pump alerts (enabled by default) including low reservoir warning at 20units."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2883", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2883, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2883, "title": "AAPS back-fills BG gaps with interpolated values (dangerous)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2883", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2883", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After a sensor change and bad calibration, there is a gap between last and new BG values. AAPS fills the gap with interpolated values, which can show a rise instead of the actual fall, potentially leading to dangerous behavior. This happens even with smoothing disabled.", "cause": "The gap filling behavior has been present since the first version of AAPS, but was not displayed in older versions. It is used for calculation purposes (e.g., COB calculation) and no BG is added to the actual data.", "fix": "No fix was provided in the thread. The maintainer states that the behavior is intentional and time-proved, and that it is only for calculation purposes.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Dexcom G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["exponential smoothing", "smoothing", "interpolation"], "evidence_quote": "filling the gap was always there. in older versions this was not displayed without interpolation COB calculation would not be working", "text": "AAPS back-fills BG gaps with interpolated values (dangerous) After a sensor change and bad calibration, there is a gap between last and new BG values. AAPS fills the gap with interpolated values, which can show a rise instead of the actual fall, potentially leading to dangerous behavior. This happens even with smoothing disabled. The gap filling behavior has been present since the first version of AAPS, but was not displayed in older versions. It is used for calculation purposes (e.g., COB calculation) and no BG is added to the actual data. No fix was provided in the thread. The maintainer states that the behavior is intentional and time-proved, and that it is only for calculation purposes. Dexcom G6 Dexcom G7 exponential smoothing smoothing interpolation filling the gap was always there. in older versions this was not displayed without interpolation COB calculation would not be working"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2884", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2884, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2884, "title": "Extreme battery drain with latest dev-m and DynISF using.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2884", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2884", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "With the latest dev version, battery drains in hours instead of days, and the smartphone becomes very warm. The issue occurs when using DynISF, but also reported without DynISF.", "cause": "The battery drain was caused by xDrip sync, as identified by MilosKozak, and fixed in a commit. However, the issue reappeared in a later dev version when using DynISF, but was resolved after further updates.", "fix": "The fix was to update to the latest dev version that included the xDrip sync fix. Additionally, deactivating Automation in settings helped for one user, and switching from DynISF to SMB temporarily resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["Automation → deactivated"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip sync", "DynISF", "SMB"], "evidence_quote": "caused by xdrip sync", "text": "Extreme battery drain with latest dev-m and DynISF using. With the latest dev version, battery drains in hours instead of days, and the smartphone becomes very warm. The issue occurs when using DynISF, but also reported without DynISF. The battery drain was caused by xDrip sync, as identified by MilosKozak, and fixed in a commit. However, the issue reappeared in a later dev version when using DynISF, but was resolved after further updates. The fix was to update to the latest dev version that included the xDrip sync fix. Additionally, deactivating Automation in settings helped for one user, and switching from DynISF to SMB temporarily resolved the issue.  xdrip sync DynISF SMB caused by xdrip sync"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2890", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2890, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2890, "title": "Dev M and RC2 AAPS Client missing BG's and regular updates", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2890", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2890", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "AAPSClient misses BG updates and regular updates, even with all power savings off. Updates can be obtained by pausing websockets and restarting, while NSClient receives regular updates.", "cause": null, "fix": "Improved in a commit (b870de1e078696a842b934287edf09c7754b313d), but the issue persists for BG updates.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["websockets", "NSClientV3"], "evidence_quote": "improved in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/b870de1e078696a842b934287edf09c7754b313d", "text": "Dev M and RC2 AAPS Client missing BG's and regular updates AAPSClient misses BG updates and regular updates, even with all power savings off. Updates can be obtained by pausing websockets and restarting, while NSClient receives regular updates.  Improved in a commit (b870de1e078696a842b934287edf09c7754b313d), but the issue persists for BG updates.  websockets NSClientV3 improved in https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/b870de1e078696a842b934287edf09c7754b313d"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2938", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2938, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2938, "title": "Nightscout : missing BGs", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2938", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2938", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "In AAPS, when set to update Nightscout only when charging, the last BGs are not filled up, leaving holes in the BGs on Nightscout. Full resync does not fill the holes.", "cause": "The missing BG backfill was a Nightscout bug, not an AAPS bug.", "fix": "Updating Nightscout to v15.0.2 Dev resolved the backfill issue; when on charge, AAPS backfills the BGs and there are no more holes.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["xDrip", "G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["v3", "v1", "xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "Good news : the missing BG backfill was a NS bug. Now, when on charge, AAPS is backfilling the BGs. There are no more holes.", "text": "Nightscout : missing BGs In AAPS, when set to update Nightscout only when charging, the last BGs are not filled up, leaving holes in the BGs on Nightscout. Full resync does not fill the holes. The missing BG backfill was a Nightscout bug, not an AAPS bug. Updating Nightscout to v15.0.2 Dev resolved the backfill issue; when on charge, AAPS backfills the BGs and there are no more holes. xDrip G6 v3 v1 xDrip Good news : the missing BG backfill was a NS bug. Now, when on charge, AAPS is backfilling the BGs. There are no more holes."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2947", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2947, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2947, "title": "AndroidAPS 3.2 dev hangs after pressing NSClientV3 \"switch on\" button", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2947", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2947", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When trying to activate the NSClientV3 option in the Configurator, the button turns gray but the app hangs and becomes unresponsive. Restarting the app, clearing cache, and restarting the phone do not help.", "cause": "The issue was an Android-specific problem, likely a bug in the app that was fixed by a commit.", "fix": "Updating to a build that includes commit 2b89a78102afa47cf7d4a3b0a771facd74293ec1 resolved the problem.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 14", "Android 12", "Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["NSClientV3", "NSClientV1"], "evidence_quote": "With this update the problem is solved.", "text": "AndroidAPS 3.2 dev hangs after pressing NSClientV3 \"switch on\" button When trying to activate the NSClientV3 option in the Configurator, the button turns gray but the app hangs and becomes unresponsive. Restarting the app, clearing cache, and restarting the phone do not help. The issue was an Android-specific problem, likely a bug in the app that was fixed by a commit. Updating to a build that includes commit 2b89a78102afa47cf7d4a3b0a771facd74293ec1 resolved the problem. Android 14 Android 12 Android 13 NSClientV3 NSClientV1 With this update the problem is solved."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2966", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2966, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2966, "title": "[RC2] NSClientV3 FullSync only gets 2 days of TDD.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2966", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2966", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Fresh install of AAPS 3.2, NSClientV3, all checkboxes to 'download data from NS', made Full sync. Loaded BG data, treatments, etc, but statistics shows only 2 days of TDD. So DynISF does not work correctly right from start and needs another 5 days to fill the required tdd7 data. While it exists in NS and simply must be downloaded on full sync. History browser shows BG values, TT changes, notes and sensor change/cannula replacement events for these days, but not bolus/carbs treatments.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the issue is related to how treatments are sent to NS. Specifically, a request using 'created_at'$gt returns only TempBasals and TempTargets, while a request using 'date'$gt returns Boluses. This suggests that the sync is not fetching bolus data correctly due to the query parameter used.", "fix": "The fix is a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9b4d9b788b1715c7fc662596ceade69e2862ef8a. The thread does not describe the exact change, but it is the resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClientV3", "full sync"], "evidence_quote": "Seems that I've found the reason. This request returns ONLY TempBasals and TempTargets api/v3/treatments?sort=date&**created_at**$gt=2023-10-21T04:28:26.411Z&limit=500 This requests returns Boluses api/v3/treatments?sort=date&**date**$gt=2023-10-21T04:28:26.411Z&limit=500 Seems to be related to how treatments are sent to NS.", "text": "[RC2] NSClientV3 FullSync only gets 2 days of TDD. Fresh install of AAPS 3.2, NSClientV3, all checkboxes to 'download data from NS', made Full sync. Loaded BG data, treatments, etc, but statistics shows only 2 days of TDD. So DynISF does not work correctly right from start and needs another 5 days to fill the required tdd7 data. While it exists in NS and simply must be downloaded on full sync. History browser shows BG values, TT changes, notes and sensor change/cannula replacement events for these days, but not bolus/carbs treatments. The thread identifies that the issue is related to how treatments are sent to NS. Specifically, a request using 'created_at'$gt returns only TempBasals and TempTargets, while a request using 'date'$gt returns Boluses. This suggests that the sync is not fetching bolus data correctly due to the query parameter used. The fix is a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9b4d9b788b1715c7fc662596ceade69e2862ef8a. The thread does not describe the exact change, but it is the resolution.  NSClientV3 full sync Seems that I've found the reason. This request returns ONLY TempBasals and TempTargets api/v3/treatments?sort=date&**created_at**$gt=2023-10-21T04:28:26.411Z&limit=500 This requests returns Boluses api/v3/treatments?sort=date&**date**$gt=2023-10-21T04:28:26.411Z&limit=500 Seems to be related to how treatments are sent to NS."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2977", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2977, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2977, "title": "[Safety Question/Discussion] Change in bolus wizard - 100% Bolus", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2977", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2977", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A change in the Bolus Wizard causes the bolus percentage to be ignored (i.e., 100% is used) when CGM is not available, which could lead to users unintentionally delivering a 100% bolus instead of their usual lower percentage, potentially causing overdosing and serious hypos.", "cause": "The change in BolusWizard: if CGM is not available, the percentage is ignored and 100% is used. This is a deliberate design decision, but it may override user-set percentages without warning.", "fix": "The thread discusses that the behavior can be adjusted via Engineering mode, specifically the 'Old glycemia time threshold [min]' setting, which defaults to 16 minutes and can be changed. Additionally, users can manually change the percentage in the dialog. No code fix is proposed; the discussion suggests adding warnings or user-configurable defaults.", "settings_changed": ["Old glycemia time threshold [min] → 16 (default, adjustable in Engineering mode)"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Engineering mode adds another entry below that, \"Old glycemia time threshold [min]\", with a default of 16 minutes and a minimum of 6 minutes.", "text": "[Safety Question/Discussion] Change in bolus wizard - 100% Bolus A change in the Bolus Wizard causes the bolus percentage to be ignored (i.e., 100% is used) when CGM is not available, which could lead to users unintentionally delivering a 100% bolus instead of their usual lower percentage, potentially causing overdosing and serious hypos. The change in BolusWizard: if CGM is not available, the percentage is ignored and 100% is used. This is a deliberate design decision, but it may override user-set percentages without warning. The thread discusses that the behavior can be adjusted via Engineering mode, specifically the 'Old glycemia time threshold [min]' setting, which defaults to 16 minutes and can be changed. Additionally, users can manually change the percentage in the dialog. No code fix is proposed; the discussion suggests adding warnings or user-configurable defaults.   Engineering mode adds another entry below that, \"Old glycemia time threshold [min]\", with a default of 16 minutes and a minimum of 6 minutes."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2980", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2980, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2980, "title": "Exponential smoothing shows raw value", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2980", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2980", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Using master version 3.2.0.1 and exponential smoothing plugin, the graph is smoothed and dynISF plugin uses smoothed values, but the value that AAPS shows is the raw value received either by juggluco or xdrip, using libre 2. In previous versions the bg value shown was the smoothed one.", "cause": "The thread initially discusses whether showing raw value is intended. MilosKozak explains that it is currently designed to show real value because recalculated smoothed value may shift in time, and later states that in actual 3.2 code smoothed value is displayed, raw value used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available).", "fix": "MilosKozak states that checking the actual 3.2 code, smoothed value is displayed, and raw value is used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available). This indicates the issue is resolved in the code, but no explicit user action is given.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["exponential smoothing", "xdrip", "juggluco"], "evidence_quote": "Checking the actual 3.2 code and smoothed value is displayed Raw value is used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available)", "text": "Exponential smoothing shows raw value Using master version 3.2.0.1 and exponential smoothing plugin, the graph is smoothed and dynISF plugin uses smoothed values, but the value that AAPS shows is the raw value received either by juggluco or xdrip, using libre 2. In previous versions the bg value shown was the smoothed one. The thread initially discusses whether showing raw value is intended. MilosKozak explains that it is currently designed to show real value because recalculated smoothed value may shift in time, and later states that in actual 3.2 code smoothed value is displayed, raw value used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available). MilosKozak states that checking the actual 3.2 code, smoothed value is displayed, and raw value is used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available). This indicates the issue is resolved in the code, but no explicit user action is given. Libre 2 G6 exponential smoothing xdrip juggluco Checking the actual 3.2 code and smoothed value is displayed Raw value is used only when bucketed data is not generated (less than 4 recent values available)"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2981", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2981, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2981, "title": "watchface shows a question mark instead of a trend arrow", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2981", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2981", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Since the update to AAPS 3.2, the watchface often shows a question mark instead of a trend arrow, with no identifiable pattern and across all trend directions.", "cause": "The issue was on the phone side: the trend arrow sent to the watch was 'invalid' or 'unknown', as seen in logs where data received included a Flat trendArrow but SingleData sent to watch was unknown.", "fix": "A code change in commit ff0d327a157cbbf58328be70f0094829d13050e5 resolved the problem; after installing the dev version with this change, the trend arrow shows as expected.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "it looks like this code change resolved my problem. The trend arrow shows up as expected. No more question marks.", "text": "watchface shows a question mark instead of a trend arrow Since the update to AAPS 3.2, the watchface often shows a question mark instead of a trend arrow, with no identifiable pattern and across all trend directions. The issue was on the phone side: the trend arrow sent to the watch was 'invalid' or 'unknown', as seen in logs where data received included a Flat trendArrow but SingleData sent to watch was unknown. A code change in commit ff0d327a157cbbf58328be70f0094829d13050e5 resolved the problem; after installing the dev version with this change, the trend arrow shows as expected. Dexcom G7 xDrip it looks like this code change resolved my problem. The trend arrow shows up as expected. No more question marks."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-2990", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2990, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 2990, "title": "3.1.0.3 + 3.2.0.1 No Pump (Dana RS) Pairing possible", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2990", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/2990", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "In the pairing process the pump goes into communication according to the pairing codes, the arrows appear but then the process stops. This happens reliably 12 times in a row with a DANA RS V3 from 03/2023, while another older RS works well.", "cause": "The pairing dialogue doesn't get scrollable when showing more content than the current device resolution allows, so the user isn't able to reach the 'cancel / ok' buttons. This is a small device/screen issue.", "fix": "Workaround was connecting pump via big-screen phone and import saved settings to Jelly. Additionally, a commit was made to fix the issue (bfacfd925590d458d08fd29ddbf09dcc3fd91996).", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana RS"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["pairing"], "evidence_quote": "Issue detected/solved, it was a display resolution problem. The pairing dialogue doesn't get scrollable when showing more content than the current device resolution allows, so the user isn't able to reach the \"cancel / ok\" buttons (or can't even guess they are there).", "text": "3.1.0.3 + 3.2.0.1 No Pump (Dana RS) Pairing possible In the pairing process the pump goes into communication according to the pairing codes, the arrows appear but then the process stops. This happens reliably 12 times in a row with a DANA RS V3 from 03/2023, while another older RS works well. The pairing dialogue doesn't get scrollable when showing more content than the current device resolution allows, so the user isn't able to reach the 'cancel / ok' buttons. This is a small device/screen issue. Workaround was connecting pump via big-screen phone and import saved settings to Jelly. Additionally, a commit was made to fix the issue (bfacfd925590d458d08fd29ddbf09dcc3fd91996). Dana RS pairing Issue detected/solved, it was a display resolution problem. The pairing dialogue doesn't get scrollable when showing more content than the current device resolution allows, so the user isn't able to reach the \"cancel / ok\" buttons (or can't even guess they are there)."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3001", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3001, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3001, "title": "Discussion: Why open loop when DST ?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3001", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3001", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "During the summer/winter time change, the user experienced a 3-hour open loop with the DASH pump, while another user with Medtrum did not. The issue is that AAPS opens the loop for a period after DST change.", "cause": "The thread discusses that when time shifts backwards, database values get duplicates in time, and IOB and COB calculations become invalid. Also, for DASH, the pump time update requires user confirmation, and the loop is opened during this period.", "fix": "No definitive fix is stated. Suggestions include automating the time update and profile sending after DST change, but there is disagreement and safety concerns. The thread does not conclude with a resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["DASH", "Medtrum"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dash", "medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "As AAPS knows IOB and COB at the moment of the change, the only thing that can change between 2AM and 3AM is the profile. It would be good if, after the time change, AAPS sends new time to pump, then sends active profile to pump automatically.", "text": "Discussion: Why open loop when DST ? During the summer/winter time change, the user experienced a 3-hour open loop with the DASH pump, while another user with Medtrum did not. The issue is that AAPS opens the loop for a period after DST change. The thread discusses that when time shifts backwards, database values get duplicates in time, and IOB and COB calculations become invalid. Also, for DASH, the pump time update requires user confirmation, and the loop is opened during this period. No definitive fix is stated. Suggestions include automating the time update and profile sending after DST change, but there is disagreement and safety concerns. The thread does not conclude with a resolution. DASH Medtrum dash medtrum As AAPS knows IOB and COB at the moment of the change, the only thing that can change between 2AM and 3AM is the profile. It would be good if, after the time change, AAPS sends new time to pump, then sends active profile to pump automatically."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3031", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3031, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3031, "title": "3.2.0.1 Increased connection Problems with Omnipod Dash", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3031", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3031", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Since updating to 3.2, the user experiences increased connection problems with Omnipod Dash, including errors where AAPS is unsure if SMB were delivered or profile changes didn't work, and a Pod-Fault error 095 ALARM_WIRE_TEST_OPEN_GROUND.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. The user later reports that after upgrading phone from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poco X6 Pro on stock OS, the problems went away, suggesting a phone/OS issue, but this is not confirmed.", "fix": "The user resolved the issue by upgrading their phone from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poco X6 Pro on stock OS, which made the problems go away. No specific configuration change was stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DASH"], "evidence_quote": "I have now upgraded my phone (from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poxo X6 Pro on stock OS, and the problems went away. So I guess it was a phone/lineage problem?", "text": "3.2.0.1 Increased connection Problems with Omnipod Dash Since updating to 3.2, the user experiences increased connection problems with Omnipod Dash, including errors where AAPS is unsure if SMB were delivered or profile changes didn't work, and a Pod-Fault error 095 ALARM_WIRE_TEST_OPEN_GROUND. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. The user later reports that after upgrading phone from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poco X6 Pro on stock OS, the problems went away, suggesting a phone/OS issue, but this is not confirmed. The user resolved the issue by upgrading their phone from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poco X6 Pro on stock OS, which made the problems go away. No specific configuration change was stated. Omnipod Dash DASH I have now upgraded my phone (from Poco F3 on Lineage OS to Poxo X6 Pro on stock OS, and the problems went away. So I guess it was a phone/lineage problem?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3039", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3039, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3039, "title": "After upgrading to 3.2.0.1 it is not possible to connect to a new pod (Omnipod Dash)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3039", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3039", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After upgrading to AAPS 3.2.0.1, connecting to a new Omnipod Dash pod fails with a 'Generic error: java.security.InvalidKeyException: Banned public key' error. The user can connect to a new pod with version 3.1.0.3, then upgrade to 3.2.0.1 and everything works, but direct connection with 3.2.0.1 fails.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suggested that the issue may be phone-specific (Xiaomi F21 Pro) or related to a specific OS version, but no definitive cause is confirmed.", "fix": "The thread suggests several workarounds: resetting the phone to factory state, disconnecting all BT devices except BYODA, disabling background apps, uninstalling and reinstalling AAPS, and for the Xiaomi F21 Pro specifically, flashing a different (Russian) version of the phone's firmware. However, no single fix is confirmed as the resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["Omnipod Dash"], "evidence_quote": "The solution is to burn a new version to the device The Russian version and all based on it work without problems", "text": "After upgrading to 3.2.0.1 it is not possible to connect to a new pod (Omnipod Dash) After upgrading to AAPS 3.2.0.1, connecting to a new Omnipod Dash pod fails with a 'Generic error: java.security.InvalidKeyException: Banned public key' error. The user can connect to a new pod with version 3.1.0.3, then upgrade to 3.2.0.1 and everything works, but direct connection with 3.2.0.1 fails. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suggested that the issue may be phone-specific (Xiaomi F21 Pro) or related to a specific OS version, but no definitive cause is confirmed. The thread suggests several workarounds: resetting the phone to factory state, disconnecting all BT devices except BYODA, disabling background apps, uninstalling and reinstalling AAPS, and for the Xiaomi F21 Pro specifically, flashing a different (Russian) version of the phone's firmware. However, no single fix is confirmed as the resolution. Omnipod Dash Android 11 Omnipod Dash The solution is to burn a new version to the device The Russian version and all based on it work without problems"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3143", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3143, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3143, "title": "Wear : Data layer foreground notification", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3143", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3143", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On the latest dev build, a persistent 'Data layer foreground notification' appears on the watch and cannot be dismissed. Turning off the notification disables all AAPS notifications on the watch.", "cause": "The notification was added to keep the background service running on Android 10+ so that complications work, but it results in a permanent notification that cannot be removed.", "fix": "As a workaround, users can disable the notification channel via the watch's developer options: App Notifications -> All watch apps -> AAPS -> Data layer Foreground Service Channel: OFF. Later dev builds may have improved the behavior.", "settings_changed": ["Data layer Foreground Service Channel → OFF"], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy Watch 4", "Pixel Watch 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 13", "Android 14"], "driver_tags": ["wear", "foreground service", "notification channel"], "evidence_quote": "With current dev-builds, on the Samsung Galaxy Watch 4, I can hide the ongoing notification through developer menu settings on Watch: `App Notifications -> All watch apps -> AAPS -> Data layer Foreground Service Channel: OFF`", "text": "Wear : Data layer foreground notification On the latest dev build, a persistent 'Data layer foreground notification' appears on the watch and cannot be dismissed. Turning off the notification disables all AAPS notifications on the watch. The notification was added to keep the background service running on Android 10+ so that complications work, but it results in a permanent notification that cannot be removed. As a workaround, users can disable the notification channel via the watch's developer options: App Notifications -> All watch apps -> AAPS -> Data layer Foreground Service Channel: OFF. Later dev builds may have improved the behavior. Samsung Galaxy Watch 4 Pixel Watch 2 Android 13 Android 14 wear foreground service notification channel With current dev-builds, on the Samsung Galaxy Watch 4, I can hide the ongoing notification through developer menu settings on Watch: `App Notifications -> All watch apps -> AAPS -> Data layer Foreground Service Channel: OFF`"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3155", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3155, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3155, "title": "Switching Porfile via NSclient V3 doesn't work with APPS 3.0.2.3 and NS 15.02", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3155", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3155", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After creating a new profile with new basal rates in Nightscout profile manager, switching to this profile in Nightscout is not effected on AAPS 3.0.2.3 app with NSClient V3 enabled unless switching to NSClient V1. Profile switch in NS at 7:02 was effected in AAPS directly after switching to NSClient V1 at 8:35.", "cause": "Entries made in NS Website require NS 1 API; the issue is known when using V3 API.", "fix": "Use NSClient V1 for profile switches made on the Nightscout website, or use AAPS Client for profile switches.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nsclient v3", "nsclient v1", "v3 api", "v1 api"], "evidence_quote": "But I read now, that entries made in NS Website require NS 1 so. The issue is known.", "text": "Switching Porfile via NSclient V3 doesn't work with APPS 3.0.2.3 and NS 15.02 After creating a new profile with new basal rates in Nightscout profile manager, switching to this profile in Nightscout is not effected on AAPS 3.0.2.3 app with NSClient V3 enabled unless switching to NSClient V1. Profile switch in NS at 7:02 was effected in AAPS directly after switching to NSClient V1 at 8:35. Entries made in NS Website require NS 1 API; the issue is known when using V3 API. Use NSClient V1 for profile switches made on the Nightscout website, or use AAPS Client for profile switches.  nsclient v3 nsclient v1 v3 api v1 api But I read now, that entries made in NS Website require NS 1 so. The issue is known."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3173", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3173, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3173, "title": "Error in dynamicISF algorithm", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3173", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3173", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In version dev3.3.0 build on 14.01.24 the dynamicISF gives an abnormal result. The dynamicISF adjustment factor changes to 0 without user interaction, causing an abnormal high ISF.", "cause": "The dynamicISF adjustment factor was set to 0 without user interaction, possibly due to a bug in the app. The code only reads the value, so it should not change by itself, but multiple users reported it happening after updating to latest dev.", "fix": "Manually set the dynamicISF adjustment factor back to the desired value (e.g., 100% or previous value like 80) in preferences. A commit was made to address the issue.", "settings_changed": ["dynamicISF adjustment factor → 100%", "dynamicISF adjustment factor → 80"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I've entered preferences to check the value (did not edit it), and it was zero. I've set it back to the normal value, but 1 loop run was affected, and I had a similar high ISF.", "text": "Error in dynamicISF algorithm In version dev3.3.0 build on 14.01.24 the dynamicISF gives an abnormal result. The dynamicISF adjustment factor changes to 0 without user interaction, causing an abnormal high ISF. The dynamicISF adjustment factor was set to 0 without user interaction, possibly due to a bug in the app. The code only reads the value, so it should not change by itself, but multiple users reported it happening after updating to latest dev. Manually set the dynamicISF adjustment factor back to the desired value (e.g., 100% or previous value like 80) in preferences. A commit was made to address the issue.   I've entered preferences to check the value (did not edit it), and it was zero. I've set it back to the normal value, but 1 loop run was affected, and I had a similar high ISF."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3181", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3181, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3181, "title": "UAM SMBs with Libre 2", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3181", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3181", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users of Libre 2 and Libre 3 cannot enable SMB options such as Enable SMB Always, Enable SMB After Carbs, and Enable UAM because AndroidAPS has these options disabled for Libre CGM users, even when smoothing is enabled. The issue requests that these limitations be lifted or made overridable by the user after acknowledging risks.", "cause": "The restriction is tied to an old Libre 1 issue where a MiaoMiao or similar Bluetooth interface could report flat BG values instead of an error during signal loss; this led to SMB features being gated for Libre-family sensors. For newer Libre sensors, the remaining blocker is that AAPS only allows these features when the BG source provides proper sensor identification.", "fix": "MilosKozak committed change 0771b6d which makes Libre 2 and Libre 3 work with SMB Always once the BG source provides proper identification.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "Libre 3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "juggluco", "miaomiao"], "evidence_quote": "this https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0771b6d8fa1acda6c15a46fa675718db29c12dc6 makes libre 2&3 working with SMB always once BG source provide proper identification", "text": "UAM SMBs with Libre 2 Users of Libre 2 and Libre 3 cannot enable SMB options such as Enable SMB Always, Enable SMB After Carbs, and Enable UAM because AndroidAPS has these options disabled for Libre CGM users, even when smoothing is enabled. The issue requests that these limitations be lifted or made overridable by the user after acknowledging risks. The restriction is tied to an old Libre 1 issue where a MiaoMiao or similar Bluetooth interface could report flat BG values instead of an error during signal loss; this led to SMB features being gated for Libre-family sensors. For newer Libre sensors, the remaining blocker is that AAPS only allows these features when the BG source provides proper sensor identification. MilosKozak committed change 0771b6d which makes Libre 2 and Libre 3 work with SMB Always once the BG source provides proper identification. Libre 2 Libre 3 xdrip juggluco miaomiao this https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/0771b6d8fa1acda6c15a46fa675718db29c12dc6 makes libre 2&3 working with SMB always once BG source provide proper identification"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3192", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3192, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3192, "title": "Dev 3.30 latest DynISF error with activation", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3192", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3192", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When turning on DynISF on the latest dev version, an error banner appears a few moments later and repeats itself.", "cause": null, "fix": "The issue can be resolved by removing APS results.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dynisf"], "evidence_quote": "can be resolved by removing APS resuts", "text": "Dev 3.30 latest DynISF error with activation When turning on DynISF on the latest dev version, an error banner appears a few moments later and repeats itself.  The issue can be resolved by removing APS results.  dynisf can be resolved by removing APS resuts"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3226", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3226, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3226, "title": "[DEV] Error \"Profile sensitivity value\" is out of hard limits when enabling \"Dynamic sensitivity\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3226", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3226", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When enabling \"Dynamic sensitivity\" in SMB plugin after running with it disabled, an error \"Profile sensitivity value is out of hard limits\" appears on the next loop run. The error disappears after the next BG arrival. The issue is reproducible.", "cause": "The error message is misleading and seems related to variable_sens as used in DynamicISF. If not yet calculated, variable_sens may get assigned 0.0 or 1.0 which triggers the message.", "fix": "Fixed in commit 80fd9e4d8be5f72858954b491675bc92f14a07e7.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dynamic sensitivity", "smb", "dynamicisf"], "evidence_quote": "However, my impression was that the message text is very misleading because it seems related to variable_sens as used in DynamicISF and has nothing to do with the pump profile sensitivity. If not yet calculated then variabale_sens may get assigned 0.0 or 1.0 which triggers the message.", "text": "[DEV] Error \"Profile sensitivity value\" is out of hard limits when enabling \"Dynamic sensitivity\" When enabling \"Dynamic sensitivity\" in SMB plugin after running with it disabled, an error \"Profile sensitivity value is out of hard limits\" appears on the next loop run. The error disappears after the next BG arrival. The issue is reproducible. The error message is misleading and seems related to variable_sens as used in DynamicISF. If not yet calculated, variable_sens may get assigned 0.0 or 1.0 which triggers the message. Fixed in commit 80fd9e4d8be5f72858954b491675bc92f14a07e7.  dynamic sensitivity smb dynamicisf However, my impression was that the message text is very misleading because it seems related to variable_sens as used in DynamicISF and has nothing to do with the pump profile sensitivity. If not yet calculated then variabale_sens may get assigned 0.0 or 1.0 which triggers the message."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3259", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3259, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3259, "title": "Accu-Check Insight Bluetooth Pairing \"Connection failed\" on P7 Android 14 QPR2 update", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3259", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3259", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After an Android 14 QPR2 update on Pixel 7, the phone cannot reach the Accu-Chek Insight pump, and Bluetooth pairing fails with 'Connection failed' when the phone lists the pump. It was working before without issues.", "cause": "The issue was caused by a recent Android QPR2 update that broke the Bluetooth connection between Pixel 7 and the Insight pump. Google messed up with the bluetooth firmware/security patch tagging, and GrapheneOS implemented it from AOSP, which broke things.", "fix": "The changes were reverted by GrapheneOS developers, and after that all was good. The issue was resolved by reverting the problematic Bluetooth changes.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Accu-Chek Insight", "Pixel 7"], "android_versions": ["Android 14"], "driver_tags": ["Insight driver"], "evidence_quote": "apparently Google messed up with the bluetooth firmware/security patch tagging, the devs at GrapheneOS implemented it quickly from AOSP and it broke things. Since then they reverted the changes, so all good now.", "text": "Accu-Check Insight Bluetooth Pairing \"Connection failed\" on P7 Android 14 QPR2 update After an Android 14 QPR2 update on Pixel 7, the phone cannot reach the Accu-Chek Insight pump, and Bluetooth pairing fails with 'Connection failed' when the phone lists the pump. It was working before without issues. The issue was caused by a recent Android QPR2 update that broke the Bluetooth connection between Pixel 7 and the Insight pump. Google messed up with the bluetooth firmware/security patch tagging, and GrapheneOS implemented it from AOSP, which broke things. The changes were reverted by GrapheneOS developers, and after that all was good. The issue was resolved by reverting the problematic Bluetooth changes. Accu-Chek Insight Pixel 7 Android 14 Insight driver apparently Google messed up with the bluetooth firmware/security patch tagging, the devs at GrapheneOS implemented it quickly from AOSP and it broke things. Since then they reverted the changes, so all good now."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3264", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3264, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3264, "title": "History Browser date picker substracts one day (Android 14)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3264", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3264", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When selecting a date in the History Browser date picker and pressing OK, the date shown is one day prior to the selected date. The issue also occurs in other date pickers, such as when inserting a CGM sensor from the Action tab.", "cause": "The issue is a bug in Google's material-components library, triggered when the phone timezone is set to GMT-5 (e.g., EST).", "fix": "A workaround was implemented in commit 50a3fe0f5ef367b1ad1c8cc700ab6d439623b217.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 7a", "Pixel 4a 5G", "Samsung S24 Ultra"], "android_versions": ["Android 14"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "it seems to be a bug in google's library. Reported https://github.com/material-components/material-components-android/issues/4373", "text": "History Browser date picker substracts one day (Android 14) When selecting a date in the History Browser date picker and pressing OK, the date shown is one day prior to the selected date. The issue also occurs in other date pickers, such as when inserting a CGM sensor from the Action tab. The issue is a bug in Google's material-components library, triggered when the phone timezone is set to GMT-5 (e.g., EST). A workaround was implemented in commit 50a3fe0f5ef367b1ad1c8cc700ab6d439623b217. Pixel 7a Pixel 4a 5G Samsung S24 Ultra Android 14  it seems to be a bug in google's library. Reported https://github.com/material-components/material-components-android/issues/4373"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3266", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3266, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3266, "title": "Enable SMB always while using xdrip in companion app mode and dexcom g7 original app", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3266", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3266", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using xdrip in companion app mode fetching bg values from dexcom g7 app, AAPS 3.2.0.3 will not allow SMB to be enabled always. The user wants G7 users to be able to use the latest dexcom g7 app including Clarity and still have hCL/fCL possibility in AAPS.", "cause": "xDrip does not send which sensor the data comes from in companion app mode, so AAPS cannot determine if the data is from a G7 or e.g. a Medtronic sensor. Therefore AAPS cannot enable SMB always for G7 companion mode.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by using a newer AAPS version; testing on AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d (Build 986125e7e8) showed that SMB/closed loop now works with xDrip companion app.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["dexcom g7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["companion app mode", "xdrip", "dexcom g7 app"], "evidence_quote": "I tested it today on AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d (Build 986125e7e8) and now it seems to work! Closed loop possible even with xdrip companion app, nice!", "text": "Enable SMB always while using xdrip in companion app mode and dexcom g7 original app When using xdrip in companion app mode fetching bg values from dexcom g7 app, AAPS 3.2.0.3 will not allow SMB to be enabled always. The user wants G7 users to be able to use the latest dexcom g7 app including Clarity and still have hCL/fCL possibility in AAPS. xDrip does not send which sensor the data comes from in companion app mode, so AAPS cannot determine if the data is from a G7 or e.g. a Medtronic sensor. Therefore AAPS cannot enable SMB always for G7 companion mode. The issue was resolved by using a newer AAPS version; testing on AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d (Build 986125e7e8) showed that SMB/closed loop now works with xDrip companion app. dexcom g7 companion app mode xdrip dexcom g7 app I tested it today on AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d (Build 986125e7e8) and now it seems to work! Closed loop possible even with xdrip companion app, nice!"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3268", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3268, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3268, "title": "[Medtrum Nano]: BT -> Connection timed out", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3268", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3268", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user reports Bluetooth connection timeouts with the Medtrum Nano pump, where the pump becomes unreachable and takes minutes to connect or fails to connect, requiring multiple exits from AAPS to reconnect. The issue occurs intermittently, including after bolus attempts.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but a fix was proposed and tested via pull request #3270, which resolved the Bluetooth issues for the original reporter.", "fix": "The fix was to test and use the changes from pull request #3270, which was merged into dev and resolved the Bluetooth connection timeouts for the original reporter.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtrum Nano", "OnePlus 12", "OnePlus 10 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 15"], "driver_tags": ["Medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "Can you test with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/3270 ? Can you let it run for a couple of days and see if it fixes it? After that pls report back and send logs", "text": "[Medtrum Nano]: BT -> Connection timed out The user reports Bluetooth connection timeouts with the Medtrum Nano pump, where the pump becomes unreachable and takes minutes to connect or fails to connect, requiring multiple exits from AAPS to reconnect. The issue occurs intermittently, including after bolus attempts. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but a fix was proposed and tested via pull request #3270, which resolved the Bluetooth issues for the original reporter. The fix was to test and use the changes from pull request #3270, which was merged into dev and resolved the Bluetooth connection timeouts for the original reporter. Medtrum Nano OnePlus 12 OnePlus 10 Pro Android 15 Medtrum Can you test with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/3270 ? Can you let it run for a couple of days and see if it fixes it? After that pls report back and send logs"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3284", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3284, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3284, "title": "MEDTRUM Nano disconnecting", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3284", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3284", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating with PR 3270, the pump becomes unreachable after an accidental disconnection (long phone distance) and is no longer available. To reconnect, the user must exit and restart the application.", "cause": "The device needs to scan to properly wake up or reset the Bluetooth when a connection attempt fails, but the new code does not scan on every connection error.", "fix": "A new option in the Medtrum settings (customized connection preset) was added via PR 3381. Enabling this option resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["customized connection preset option → enabled"], "devices": ["MEDTRUM Nano", "KOSPET Optimus2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "Can you test with: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/3381 And enabling the new option that is present in the medtrum settings ?", "text": "MEDTRUM Nano disconnecting After updating with PR 3270, the pump becomes unreachable after an accidental disconnection (long phone distance) and is no longer available. To reconnect, the user must exit and restart the application. The device needs to scan to properly wake up or reset the Bluetooth when a connection attempt fails, but the new code does not scan on every connection error. A new option in the Medtrum settings (customized connection preset) was added via PR 3381. Enabling this option resolved the issue. MEDTRUM Nano KOSPET Optimus2 Android 10 medtrum Can you test with: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/3381 And enabling the new option that is present in the medtrum settings ?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3318", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3318, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3318, "title": "Failed bolus error message when bolus was delivered", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3318", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3318", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When giving a bolus via AAPS, the app reports 'Bolus reported an error' and shows bolus delivery failed, but the bolus is actually delivered by the pump. This occurs intermittently, and when using the bolus wizard, entered carbs are deleted while the delivered insulin gets logged.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Combo", "G6", "Xiaomi A2 Lite"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Combo driver"], "evidence_quote": "I gave my daughter 2.1u of insulin directly using AAPS and got the \"Bolus reported an error\" message (please see screenshot), but I know that the bolus was definitely delivered by the Combo pump", "text": "Failed bolus error message when bolus was delivered When giving a bolus via AAPS, the app reports 'Bolus reported an error' and shows bolus delivery failed, but the bolus is actually delivered by the pump. This occurs intermittently, and when using the bolus wizard, entered carbs are deleted while the delivered insulin gets logged.   Combo G6 Xiaomi A2 Lite Combo driver I gave my daughter 2.1u of insulin directly using AAPS and got the \"Bolus reported an error\" message (please see screenshot), but I know that the bolus was definitely delivered by the Combo pump"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3321", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3321, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3321, "title": "Pump doesn't automatically reconnect like it used to", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3321", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3321", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After updating to v3.2.0.4, every time the user changes the cartridge or battery of their Accu-chek Insight pump, AAPS does not automatically reestablish connection. The user must manually go to the pump tab and click 'refresh' to reconnect, otherwise the closed loop is not engaged and blood glucose levels go out of whack.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Philoul suggests that the pump must be restarted after cartridge/battery change and that AAPS can only connect when the pump is started, but the user insists the pump is started. Philoul also mentions that communication requires the pump screen to be black, and that after waiting for the screen to turn black, connection should be automatic. No specific bug or change is identified.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Philoul suggests ensuring the pump is restarted after cartridge change and waiting for the pump screen to turn black (about 1 minute) before expecting automatic reconnection. The user is asked to provide logs for further investigation.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Accu-chek Insight"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Insight driver"], "evidence_quote": "Communication needs at least to have a black screen on the pump, so immediatly after battery/cartridge change or after any user action on pump, you will have to wait until pump screen turn black (about 1 min according to user timeout). Then nothing else to do, on the next loop run with a required update on pump, communication is automatic without any additional manual action from user...", "text": "Pump doesn't automatically reconnect like it used to After updating to v3.2.0.4, every time the user changes the cartridge or battery of their Accu-chek Insight pump, AAPS does not automatically reestablish connection. The user must manually go to the pump tab and click 'refresh' to reconnect, otherwise the closed loop is not engaged and blood glucose levels go out of whack. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Philoul suggests that the pump must be restarted after cartridge/battery change and that AAPS can only connect when the pump is started, but the user insists the pump is started. Philoul also mentions that communication requires the pump screen to be black, and that after waiting for the screen to turn black, connection should be automatic. No specific bug or change is identified. No definitive fix is provided. Philoul suggests ensuring the pump is restarted after cartridge change and waiting for the pump screen to turn black (about 1 minute) before expecting automatic reconnection. The user is asked to provide logs for further investigation. Accu-chek Insight Insight driver Communication needs at least to have a black screen on the pump, so immediatly after battery/cartridge change or after any user action on pump, you will have to wait until pump screen turn black (about 1 min according to user timeout). Then nothing else to do, on the next loop run with a required update on pump, communication is automatic without any additional manual action from user..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3343", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3343, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3343, "title": "Auto-increase CHO and not decrease problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3343", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3343", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "CHO (carbs) inserted with calc or normally do not decrease with time, sometimes auto-increase, which is dangerous. For example, 189 CHO eaten at 18:25 remained 70 CHO the next morning and then increased to 80 CHO after 10 minutes without any action. Other users report slower than usual carb reduction.", "cause": "The COB value is calculated using ISF. When ISF changes drastically (as with DynISF), COB changes accordingly, potentially causing increases or slower decay. The thread also explains that COB decay depends on deviation and ISF, and that a higher ISF can slow absorption.", "fix": "Turn OFF DynISF to test if COB values return to normal. Additionally, COB decaying is improved in version 3.3.0-dev-e.", "settings_changed": ["DynISF → OFF"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OpenAPS SMB", "DynISF"], "evidence_quote": "The COB value (residual CHO) is calculated using ISF. When your ISF changes drastically (as it happens with DynISF), your COB will change too. If you turn _OFF_ DynISF, you can check if COB values get back to normal.", "text": "Auto-increase CHO and not decrease problem CHO (carbs) inserted with calc or normally do not decrease with time, sometimes auto-increase, which is dangerous. For example, 189 CHO eaten at 18:25 remained 70 CHO the next morning and then increased to 80 CHO after 10 minutes without any action. Other users report slower than usual carb reduction. The COB value is calculated using ISF. When ISF changes drastically (as with DynISF), COB changes accordingly, potentially causing increases or slower decay. The thread also explains that COB decay depends on deviation and ISF, and that a higher ISF can slow absorption. Turn OFF DynISF to test if COB values return to normal. Additionally, COB decaying is improved in version 3.3.0-dev-e.  OpenAPS SMB DynISF The COB value (residual CHO) is calculated using ISF. When your ISF changes drastically (as it happens with DynISF), your COB will change too. If you turn _OFF_ DynISF, you can check if COB values get back to normal."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-335", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 335, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 335, "title": "Tidepool", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/335", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/335", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User requests feature support for Tidepool, as healthcare professionals use Tidepool as main source for BG and insulin data, and Nightscout is not widely accepted by physicians. Currently xDrip allows uploading but with very limited support.", "cause": "Tidepool's API does not support uploading all data, particularly the profile, which is a big problem. The Tidepool plugin exists but is disabled because data cannot be uploaded correctly.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tidepool", "nightscout", "xdrip"], "evidence_quote": "Problem is that Tidepool doesn't allow to upload everything (profile is big problem), and until they extend their APIs there is nothing for us to do.", "text": "Tidepool User requests feature support for Tidepool, as healthcare professionals use Tidepool as main source for BG and insulin data, and Nightscout is not widely accepted by physicians. Currently xDrip allows uploading but with very limited support. Tidepool's API does not support uploading all data, particularly the profile, which is a big problem. The Tidepool plugin exists but is disabled because data cannot be uploaded correctly.   tidepool nightscout xdrip Problem is that Tidepool doesn't allow to upload everything (profile is big problem), and until they extend their APIs there is nothing for us to do."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3363", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3363, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3363, "title": "SECURITY discussion : temporary profile change", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3363", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3363", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "There is a security issue with temporary profile changes: when a user sets a temp profile change with a duration, the pump receives a new profile. If the phone is lost or broken, the user is stuck with a wrong profile on the pump, which is a risk.", "cause": "The thread discusses the risk but does not establish a single root cause; it is a design concern about sending a new profile to the pump for temporary changes.", "fix": "The thread does not state a resolution; it is a discussion with various opinions. No fix is agreed upon.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In case 2, if the phone is lost/broken, the user is stuck with a wrong profile on the pump. That is a risk. It can be and should be reduced.", "text": "SECURITY discussion : temporary profile change There is a security issue with temporary profile changes: when a user sets a temp profile change with a duration, the pump receives a new profile. If the phone is lost or broken, the user is stuck with a wrong profile on the pump, which is a risk. The thread discusses the risk but does not establish a single root cause; it is a design concern about sending a new profile to the pump for temporary changes. The thread does not state a resolution; it is a discussion with various opinions. No fix is agreed upon.   In case 2, if the phone is lost/broken, the user is stuck with a wrong profile on the pump. That is a risk. It can be and should be reduced."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3365", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3365, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3365, "title": "Medtrum: Priming screen returns to Change Patch screen", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3365", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3365", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When starting priming, the screen immediately returns to the Change Patch screen, with a very short failure message not shown on overview. The process of reading activation status never finishes. This can happen multiple times, sometimes leading to patch discard.", "cause": "The thread suggests a possible timeout in the script when taking too long to apply the patch, and also a possible misunderstanding between the driver and the patch. One user found that running the 'Security' app's 'Boost speed' before patch change prevents the issue, implying a performance-related cause.", "fix": "The user dar-kod found that running the 'Security' application's 'Boost speed' before patch change prevents the problem. Another user suggests having everything ready before starting the process to avoid timeout.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtrum"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["Medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "I have an old Poco F3 with HyperOS, Android 13. It has an application called \"Security\". If this application is started before the patch change and you run \"Boost speed\", this problem does not occur at all.", "text": "Medtrum: Priming screen returns to Change Patch screen When starting priming, the screen immediately returns to the Change Patch screen, with a very short failure message not shown on overview. The process of reading activation status never finishes. This can happen multiple times, sometimes leading to patch discard. The thread suggests a possible timeout in the script when taking too long to apply the patch, and also a possible misunderstanding between the driver and the patch. One user found that running the 'Security' app's 'Boost speed' before patch change prevents the issue, implying a performance-related cause. The user dar-kod found that running the 'Security' application's 'Boost speed' before patch change prevents the problem. Another user suggests having everything ready before starting the process to avoid timeout. Medtrum Android 13 Medtrum I have an old Poco F3 with HyperOS, Android 13. It has an application called \"Security\". If this application is started before the patch change and you run \"Boost speed\", this problem does not occur at all."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3375", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3375, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3375, "title": "Communication failure in Omnipod Dash", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3375", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3375", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Users of the Blackview n6000 device report an error every few hours that AAPS does not find the pod, the official bluetooth app crashes until the device crashes and restarts. The only solution found is to turn off bluetooth until AAPS direct protocol finds the pump with bluetooth off, then turn it back on so Dexcom continues to work. Some users experience no communication with the pod for several hours, and sometimes the Google Play Service application crashes.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. There is speculation about a conflict with the Diakem app (Dexcom G7 app) and possible Bluetooth instability on the Blackview n6000, but no confirmed cause.", "fix": "No definitive fix is stated. Workarounds mentioned include turning Bluetooth off and on again, uninstalling the DASH app, or shutting down the Diakem app to re-establish connection. However, these are not universally effective, and the maintainer suggests changing the phone if connection is unreliable.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Blackview n6000", "Omnipod Dash", "Dexcom G6", "Dexcom G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["AAPS", "DASH app", "Diakem app", "BYODA"], "evidence_quote": "I believe there is nothing we can do on AAPS side. Change your phone if the connection is not reliable", "text": "Communication failure in Omnipod Dash Users of the Blackview n6000 device report an error every few hours that AAPS does not find the pod, the official bluetooth app crashes until the device crashes and restarts. The only solution found is to turn off bluetooth until AAPS direct protocol finds the pump with bluetooth off, then turn it back on so Dexcom continues to work. Some users experience no communication with the pod for several hours, and sometimes the Google Play Service application crashes. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. There is speculation about a conflict with the Diakem app (Dexcom G7 app) and possible Bluetooth instability on the Blackview n6000, but no confirmed cause. No definitive fix is stated. Workarounds mentioned include turning Bluetooth off and on again, uninstalling the DASH app, or shutting down the Diakem app to re-establish connection. However, these are not universally effective, and the maintainer suggests changing the phone if connection is unreliable. Blackview n6000 Omnipod Dash Dexcom G6 Dexcom G7 AAPS DASH app Diakem app BYODA I believe there is nothing we can do on AAPS side. Change your phone if the connection is not reliable"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3415", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3415, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3415, "title": "Dark and bright green dots change..", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3415", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3415", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After changing transmitters, the dark and bright green dots in the graphs change status/color often, even when the phone is near the G6 and xDrip is receiving BGs regularly.", "cause": "The issue is related to the recalculated data code when there is a slide of the 5 min delays when G6 transmitters are changed. The problem stops 36 hours after transmitter change.", "fix": "The issue was resolved in issue #3413, but the specific fix is not described in this thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6", "xDrip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "Stopping smoothing in AAPS does NOT stop the dot problem..The end of 36 hours after transmitter change stops the problem. So, the \"culprit\" is with/around the recalculated data code (when there is a \"slide\" of the 5 min delays when the G6 transmitters are changes).", "text": "Dark and bright green dots change.. After changing transmitters, the dark and bright green dots in the graphs change status/color often, even when the phone is near the G6 and xDrip is receiving BGs regularly. The issue is related to the recalculated data code when there is a slide of the 5 min delays when G6 transmitters are changed. The problem stops 36 hours after transmitter change. The issue was resolved in issue #3413, but the specific fix is not described in this thread. G6 xDrip xDrip Stopping smoothing in AAPS does NOT stop the dot problem..The end of 36 hours after transmitter change stops the problem. So, the \"culprit\" is with/around the recalculated data code (when there is a \"slide\" of the 5 min delays when the G6 transmitters are changes)."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3457", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3457, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3457, "title": "Frequent restarting", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3457", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3457", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AndroidAPS frequently restarts (assumed crashing) at random intervals not more than 30 minutes on a OnePlus 6T. Nightscout server synchronization also fails until the app is force-stopped, cache cleared, and restarted, needing to be done multiple times per day.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user found that enabling 'Allow background activity' for AAPS stopped the restarts, suggesting the OS was restricting background activity.", "fix": "Enabling the 'Allow background activity' setting for AAPS resolved the restarts for one user (Kaapeli64). Another suggestion was to disable Google Play Services, but that was not confirmed as a fix.", "settings_changed": ["Allow background activity → enabled"], "devices": ["OnePlus 6T", "OnePlus Nord 2T 5G", "Libre 3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["juggluco", "xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "Well, I stumbled into this \"Allow background activity\" setting, enabled it for AAPS, and now I don't see restarts any more.", "text": "Frequent restarting AndroidAPS frequently restarts (assumed crashing) at random intervals not more than 30 minutes on a OnePlus 6T. Nightscout server synchronization also fails until the app is force-stopped, cache cleared, and restarted, needing to be done multiple times per day. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user found that enabling 'Allow background activity' for AAPS stopped the restarts, suggesting the OS was restricting background activity. Enabling the 'Allow background activity' setting for AAPS resolved the restarts for one user (Kaapeli64). Another suggestion was to disable Google Play Services, but that was not confirmed as a fix. OnePlus 6T OnePlus Nord 2T 5G Libre 3 juggluco xDrip Well, I stumbled into this \"Allow background activity\" setting, enabled it for AAPS, and now I don't see restarts any more."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3492", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3492, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3492, "title": "Negative carbs ?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3492", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3492", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After entering negative carbs to correct overestimated carbs, the main screen shows negative carbs, and COB becomes negative. The negative carbs should erase carbs from COB but should not generate negative carbs.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is implied that the negative carb entry causes the COB to go negative due to a bug in the calculation.", "fix": "A commit was suggested by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9f3cbe21505da570054f06f86dc8f2b0c6841d9a. Users were asked to test it, and one user reported they couldn't reproduce after that.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "try with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9f3cbe21505da570054f06f86dc8f2b0c6841d9a", "text": "Negative carbs ? After entering negative carbs to correct overestimated carbs, the main screen shows negative carbs, and COB becomes negative. The negative carbs should erase carbs from COB but should not generate negative carbs. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is implied that the negative carb entry causes the COB to go negative due to a bug in the calculation. A commit was suggested by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9f3cbe21505da570054f06f86dc8f2b0c6841d9a. Users were asked to test it, and one user reported they couldn't reproduce after that.   try with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/9f3cbe21505da570054f06f86dc8f2b0c6841d9a"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3535", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3535, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3535, "title": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Semi-tranparent dots mess up the glucose plot", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3535", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3535", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d with xDrip-G7 as data source and average smoothing ON, some datapoints on the BG plot appear semi-transparent in an alternating way, complicating the graph. The transparent points change places all the time and are not related to missing values.", "cause": "The semi-transparent dots indicate recalculated (smoothed) values. They appear when there are gaps in the data at the time of receiving a value, causing the value to be recalculated later. This is more common with G7 due to its built-in transmitter and sensor changes, and with xDrip as data source.", "fix": "No definitive fix was provided. The issue may resolve after a sensor change or after ~48 hours. Some users suggest it is a cosmetic issue that does not affect loop performance. MilosKozak suggested focusing on why there are so many gaps, but the user clarified it's due to smoothing algorithms.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["xDrip-G7", "G7", "G6", "xDrip", "BYODA"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "BYODA", "average smoothing", "smoothing"], "evidence_quote": "Transparent means recalculated gap", "text": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Semi-tranparent dots mess up the glucose plot In AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d with xDrip-G7 as data source and average smoothing ON, some datapoints on the BG plot appear semi-transparent in an alternating way, complicating the graph. The transparent points change places all the time and are not related to missing values. The semi-transparent dots indicate recalculated (smoothed) values. They appear when there are gaps in the data at the time of receiving a value, causing the value to be recalculated later. This is more common with G7 due to its built-in transmitter and sensor changes, and with xDrip as data source. No definitive fix was provided. The issue may resolve after a sensor change or after ~48 hours. Some users suggest it is a cosmetic issue that does not affect loop performance. MilosKozak suggested focusing on why there are so many gaps, but the user clarified it's due to smoothing algorithms. xDrip-G7 G7 G6 xDrip BYODA xdrip BYODA average smoothing smoothing Transparent means recalculated gap"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3555", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3555, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3555, "title": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Cannot do \"Maintenance/Import Settings\" and \"Wear/Load Watchface\" because AAPS crashes immediatelly.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3555", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3555", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "On a Samsung Galaxy S21 5G with Android 14, after updating to AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d, selecting custom watchfaces or importing settings causes AAPS to crash immediately. Later versions give an error about accessing the file system when trying to access certain folders or files.", "cause": "The root cause was determined to be corruption in the phone's Android file system, not an issue with AAPS itself.", "fix": "Performing a factory reset of the phone and restoring the installation resolved the issue. After reset, AAPS directory can be .../Internal Storage/AAPS, and import settings and custom watchfaces work normally.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S21 5G"], "android_versions": ["Android 14"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "After more extensive testing I am sure that now it works and the root cause was some corruption in my phone Android file system.", "text": "[Dev 3.3.0-dev-d] Cannot do \"Maintenance/Import Settings\" and \"Wear/Load Watchface\" because AAPS crashes immediatelly. On a Samsung Galaxy S21 5G with Android 14, after updating to AAPS 3.3.0-dev-d, selecting custom watchfaces or importing settings causes AAPS to crash immediately. Later versions give an error about accessing the file system when trying to access certain folders or files. The root cause was determined to be corruption in the phone's Android file system, not an issue with AAPS itself. Performing a factory reset of the phone and restoring the installation resolved the issue. After reset, AAPS directory can be .../Internal Storage/AAPS, and import settings and custom watchfaces work normally. Samsung Galaxy S21 5G Android 14  After more extensive testing I am sure that now it works and the root cause was some corruption in my phone Android file system."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3620", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3620, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3620, "title": "[Dev] NSv3/v1 is spamming/duplicating entries in log", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3620", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3620", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AAPS and AAPSClient on the same phone are spamming/duplicating entries in the log, seen with TBR and TT. This makes sync slower between client and AAPS. Also, when requesting the devicestatus collection of the API, almost every 5 minutes there are 2 entries a few seconds apart.", "cause": "The maintainer states that the status is generated on more places (not only after enact) for example for cases like open loop, failed enact etc. This is considered correct behavior.", "fix": "The maintainer added logging to show the reason for the duplicate status generation. No specific fix was provided; the issue was considered correct behavior.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSv3", "NSv1"], "evidence_quote": "from my point of view it's correct. Status is generated on more places (not only after enact) for example for cases like open loop, failed enact etc. I added logging anyway so you can see the reason", "text": "[Dev] NSv3/v1 is spamming/duplicating entries in log AAPS and AAPSClient on the same phone are spamming/duplicating entries in the log, seen with TBR and TT. This makes sync slower between client and AAPS. Also, when requesting the devicestatus collection of the API, almost every 5 minutes there are 2 entries a few seconds apart. The maintainer states that the status is generated on more places (not only after enact) for example for cases like open loop, failed enact etc. This is considered correct behavior. The maintainer added logging to show the reason for the duplicate status generation. No specific fix was provided; the issue was considered correct behavior.  NSv3 NSv1 from my point of view it's correct. Status is generated on more places (not only after enact) for example for cases like open loop, failed enact etc. I added logging anyway so you can see the reason"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3659", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3659, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3659, "title": "3.3 rc1 stop insulin dosing below bg value doesn't work with \"tdd based sens ratio for basal and target\" enabled", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3659", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3659", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "With 'tdd based sens ratio for basal and target' enabled, basal insulin delivery continues even when blood glucose is below the threshold, whereas disabling that setting immediately stops basal as expected.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. A participant suggests that the modification to ISF calculation might cause the oref1 algorithm to calculate values higher than target, leading to insulin dosing, but this is speculative.", "fix": "The user decided to leave the 'tdd based sens ratio' setting off to achieve expected behavior on low bg values. No other fix is provided.", "settings_changed": ["tdd based sens ratio for basal and target → off"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Turning of \"  tdd based sens ratio... “immediately stopt basal as expected based on bg level.", "text": "3.3 rc1 stop insulin dosing below bg value doesn't work with \"tdd based sens ratio for basal and target\" enabled With 'tdd based sens ratio for basal and target' enabled, basal insulin delivery continues even when blood glucose is below the threshold, whereas disabling that setting immediately stops basal as expected. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. A participant suggests that the modification to ISF calculation might cause the oref1 algorithm to calculate values higher than target, leading to insulin dosing, but this is speculative. The user decided to leave the 'tdd based sens ratio' setting off to achieve expected behavior on low bg values. No other fix is provided.   Turning of \"  tdd based sens ratio... “immediately stopt basal as expected based on bg level."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3662", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3662, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3662, "title": "RC 3.3.0 Bugs that I found, ", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3662", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3662", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After upgrading to RC 3.3.0, the user experiences an alarm after one missing CGM value, a cannula change warning that stays red even after changing the cannula, and degraded algorithm performance (TIR dropped from ~95% to ~88%, TDD increased from 42 to 49, inconsistent blood sugar trends). The user also reports that the new optional sensitivity feature causes horrible algorithm settings and that downgrading to Master causes database incompatibility.", "cause": "The cannula status light issue is caused by the status light settings being set to 0, likely due to an upgrade from 3.2 to 3.3. The alarm after one missing CGM value is considered too aggressive by a commenter. The algorithm issues are attributed to the new optional sensitivity feature, which the user deactivated after one day.", "fix": "For the cannula status light issue, the user should go to settings > overview > status lights and set the values manually. For the missing CGM alarm, a commenter suggests finding a way not to notify until many more BGs are missed. For database issues after downgrade, a full sync with NSClient v3 is a workaround. The user reverted to Master to resolve algorithm issues.", "settings_changed": ["status lights → set manually (was 0)"], "devices": ["DanaRS", "Pixel 5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DynISF"], "evidence_quote": "Go to settings > overview > status lights. I guess some of them are set to 0. Can you confirm this?", "text": "RC 3.3.0 Bugs that I found,  After upgrading to RC 3.3.0, the user experiences an alarm after one missing CGM value, a cannula change warning that stays red even after changing the cannula, and degraded algorithm performance (TIR dropped from ~95% to ~88%, TDD increased from 42 to 49, inconsistent blood sugar trends). The user also reports that the new optional sensitivity feature causes horrible algorithm settings and that downgrading to Master causes database incompatibility. The cannula status light issue is caused by the status light settings being set to 0, likely due to an upgrade from 3.2 to 3.3. The alarm after one missing CGM value is considered too aggressive by a commenter. The algorithm issues are attributed to the new optional sensitivity feature, which the user deactivated after one day. For the cannula status light issue, the user should go to settings > overview > status lights and set the values manually. For the missing CGM alarm, a commenter suggests finding a way not to notify until many more BGs are missed. For database issues after downgrade, a full sync with NSClient v3 is a workaround. The user reverted to Master to resolve algorithm issues. DanaRS Pixel 5 DynISF Go to settings > overview > status lights. I guess some of them are set to 0. Can you confirm this?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3694", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3694, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3694, "title": "Gap between Automation Buttons too big on small phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3694", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3694", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The automation buttons are too big on a small phone (e.g. Cubot KingKong Mini3), with too much space between buttons and lost space within each button, causing text to be cropped.", "cause": null, "fix": "Improved the layout by reducing padding within each button and adding icons for each action, as implemented in commit 3751ef73ce017691aa434a46e53175c194dd3688 and further refined in 56aaf854.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Cubot KingKong Mini3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "improved here https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3751ef73ce017691aa434a46e53175c194dd3688", "text": "Gap between Automation Buttons too big on small phone The automation buttons are too big on a small phone (e.g. Cubot KingKong Mini3), with too much space between buttons and lost space within each button, causing text to be cropped.  Improved the layout by reducing padding within each button and adding icons for each action, as implemented in commit 3751ef73ce017691aa434a46e53175c194dd3688 and further refined in 56aaf854. Cubot KingKong Mini3  improved here https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/3751ef73ce017691aa434a46e53175c194dd3688"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3703", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3703, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3703, "title": "Dynamicisf not starting", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3703", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3703", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating from 3.2 to 3.3 by uninstalling and installing, the user gets messages 'Returning to smb not enough data' and 'returning to profile sensitivity not enough data reason tdd miss'. Even after syncing to Nightscout, the issue persists.", "cause": "The cause is that the user did not have 7 days of TDD data available, likely because they uninstalled and reinstalled instead of updating, and the sync settings were not fully enabled to download all necessary data.", "fix": "Enable all sync options in NSClientV3 and perform a full sync. The user confirmed that turning everything on when syncing resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["NSClientV3 sync options → all enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClientV3", "NSClientV1", "full sync"], "evidence_quote": "Turning everything on when syncing did the trick", "text": "Dynamicisf not starting After updating from 3.2 to 3.3 by uninstalling and installing, the user gets messages 'Returning to smb not enough data' and 'returning to profile sensitivity not enough data reason tdd miss'. Even after syncing to Nightscout, the issue persists. The cause is that the user did not have 7 days of TDD data available, likely because they uninstalled and reinstalled instead of updating, and the sync settings were not fully enabled to download all necessary data. Enable all sync options in NSClientV3 and perform a full sync. The user confirmed that turning everything on when syncing resolved the issue.  NSClientV3 NSClientV1 full sync Turning everything on when syncing did the trick"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3706", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3706, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3706, "title": "[3.3] AAPSClient displays several OpenAps statuses", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3706", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3706", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AAPSClient displays several data coming from deviceStatus, showing both current and outdated OpenAPS statuses without differentiation.", "cause": "The display shows the last enacted and last suggested entries, which can be different times or same time, and this behavior has always been so.", "fix": "MilosKozak added text to differentiate the entries via commits, but the issue remains that AAPSClient doesn't display line feeds and the enacted entry may not match real pump actions.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "First is last enacted, second is last sugested", "text": "[3.3] AAPSClient displays several OpenAps statuses AAPSClient displays several data coming from deviceStatus, showing both current and outdated OpenAPS statuses without differentiation. The display shows the last enacted and last suggested entries, which can be different times or same time, and this behavior has always been so. MilosKozak added text to differentiate the entries via commits, but the issue remains that AAPSClient doesn't display line feeds and the enacted entry may not match real pump actions.   First is last enacted, second is last sugested"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3723", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3723, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3723, "title": "Persistent problem. V3+ with enabled websockets / no synchronization with client.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3723", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3723", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using multiple AAPS clients with websockets enabled, only one device runs properly for up to 12 hours, then it stops synchronizing BG values. Other data (pump, openaps) still arrives. Disabling websockets on followers resolves the issue.", "cause": "BGs are coming 0.5 seconds in the future, which doesn't pass validation.", "fix": "The development version (commit f751b76) fixed the bug; installing that version resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["websockets", "NSClientv3", "Juggluco", "xDrip", "BYODA"], "evidence_quote": "it's the same issue. BGs are comming 0,5sec in the future, which doesn't pass validation", "text": "Persistent problem. V3+ with enabled websockets / no synchronization with client. When using multiple AAPS clients with websockets enabled, only one device runs properly for up to 12 hours, then it stops synchronizing BG values. Other data (pump, openaps) still arrives. Disabling websockets on followers resolves the issue. BGs are coming 0.5 seconds in the future, which doesn't pass validation. The development version (commit f751b76) fixed the bug; installing that version resolved the issue. Libre3 websockets NSClientv3 Juggluco xDrip BYODA it's the same issue. BGs are comming 0,5sec in the future, which doesn't pass validation"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3732", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3732, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3732, "title": "Unable to change DynamicISF Adjustment Factor % Value", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3732", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3732", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After upgrading from 3.2.0.4 to 3.3.1.0, the user cannot adjust the DynamicISF Adjustment Factor % Value in OpenAPS SMB preferences. After inputting a new value and clicking OK, it continues to show the old value.", "cause": "The issue was caused by a bug that occurred when downgrading from 3.3 to 3.2, activating the dynisf plugin and adjusting the factor, then upgrading back to 3.3. The bug was fixed by a specific commit.", "fix": "The fix is to apply the commit 7c000911068903ed7477c1fcb9d80dc88a893baf, which resolves the issue. A workaround is to uninstall and reinstall AAPS, import settings, and do a full sync with NSClientv3.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dynisf", "OpenAPS SMB"], "evidence_quote": "Confirming this fixed the issue.", "text": "Unable to change DynamicISF Adjustment Factor % Value After upgrading from 3.2.0.4 to 3.3.1.0, the user cannot adjust the DynamicISF Adjustment Factor % Value in OpenAPS SMB preferences. After inputting a new value and clicking OK, it continues to show the old value. The issue was caused by a bug that occurred when downgrading from 3.3 to 3.2, activating the dynisf plugin and adjusting the factor, then upgrading back to 3.3. The bug was fixed by a specific commit. The fix is to apply the commit 7c000911068903ed7477c1fcb9d80dc88a893baf, which resolves the issue. A workaround is to uninstall and reinstall AAPS, import settings, and do a full sync with NSClientv3.  dynisf OpenAPS SMB Confirming this fixed the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3735", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3735, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3735, "title": "[Wear] Complications designated Tap for action stops working a short while after app/tile is visited", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3735", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3735", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On Wear OS, tapping complications configured for 'Tap for action' fails to start the action after a few minutes of inactivity, unless the user visits a tile or app right before. This issue occurs on external watchfaces with complications and was present in versions 3.1, 3.2, and 3.3.", "cause": null, "fix": "The issue was fixed in a development branch (https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/tree/complication) by MilosKozak, and confirmed working by the reporter after building the wear app from that branch.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung GW 4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear", "complications", "tiles"], "evidence_quote": "I've built wear app based on https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/tree/complication - You seemed to have fixed this issue. Great job :)", "text": "[Wear] Complications designated Tap for action stops working a short while after app/tile is visited On Wear OS, tapping complications configured for 'Tap for action' fails to start the action after a few minutes of inactivity, unless the user visits a tile or app right before. This issue occurs on external watchfaces with complications and was present in versions 3.1, 3.2, and 3.3.  The issue was fixed in a development branch (https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/tree/complication) by MilosKozak, and confirmed working by the reporter after building the wear app from that branch. Samsung GW 4 wear complications tiles I've built wear app based on https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/tree/complication - You seemed to have fixed this issue. Great job :)"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3749", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3749, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3749, "title": "3.3.1.2 Continual Bluetooth Pairing Requests", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3749", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3749", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After upgrading from 3.3.1.0 to 3.3.1.2, the user receives a series of 3 Bluetooth pairing requests each time AAPS connects to the Omnipod Dash pod. Accepting the pairing request breaks connectivity between AAPS and the pod, and the phone is flooded with pairing requests every few minutes.", "cause": "The issue is specific to AndroidAPS 3.3.1.2 and Android 15, as rolling back to 3.3.1.0 resolves the problem. A maintainer suggests reverting a change for Dash in the Master branch or making it an option defaulted off.", "fix": "Roll back to AndroidAPS 3.3.1.0 to avoid the Bluetooth pairing requests. A maintainer suggests reverting the change for Dash in the Master branch or making it an option in Dash settings defaulted off.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 15"], "driver_tags": ["Dash"], "evidence_quote": "I've confirmed it's 3.3.3.2 specific as I've rolled back to 3.3.1.0 and the Bluetooth prompts went away.", "text": "3.3.1.2 Continual Bluetooth Pairing Requests After upgrading from 3.3.1.0 to 3.3.1.2, the user receives a series of 3 Bluetooth pairing requests each time AAPS connects to the Omnipod Dash pod. Accepting the pairing request breaks connectivity between AAPS and the pod, and the phone is flooded with pairing requests every few minutes. The issue is specific to AndroidAPS 3.3.1.2 and Android 15, as rolling back to 3.3.1.0 resolves the problem. A maintainer suggests reverting a change for Dash in the Master branch or making it an option defaulted off. Roll back to AndroidAPS 3.3.1.0 to avoid the Bluetooth pairing requests. A maintainer suggests reverting the change for Dash in the Master branch or making it an option in Dash settings defaulted off. Omnipod Dash Android 15 Dash I've confirmed it's 3.3.3.2 specific as I've rolled back to 3.3.1.0 and the Bluetooth prompts went away."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3796", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3796, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3796, "title": "Unable to Install or Upgrade AAPSClient on Android 14 (Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3796", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3796", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Unable to install or upgrade AAPSClient on Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra (Android 14). Upgrading gives 'App not installed as package conflicts with an existing package.' Fresh install gives Google Play Protect warning and then same package conflict error.", "cause": "Android limitation: apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. A new permission in AAPSClient 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources causes conflict with AAPS installed on same phone, which is signed with a different keystore.", "fix": "Compile AAPSClient yourself with the same keystore as AAPS, or do not have both AAPS and AAPSClient installed on the same phone.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra"], "android_versions": ["Android 14"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "it's android limitation. Apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. Permission is new in 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources", "text": "Unable to Install or Upgrade AAPSClient on Android 14 (Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra) Unable to install or upgrade AAPSClient on Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra (Android 14). Upgrading gives 'App not installed as package conflicts with an existing package.' Fresh install gives Google Play Protect warning and then same package conflict error. Android limitation: apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. A new permission in AAPSClient 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources causes conflict with AAPS installed on same phone, which is signed with a different keystore. Compile AAPSClient yourself with the same keystore as AAPS, or do not have both AAPS and AAPSClient installed on the same phone. Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra Android 14  it's android limitation. Apps that use the same permission must be signed with the same key. Permission is new in 3.3 to allow sending data to watch from multiple sources"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3797", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3797, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3797, "title": "[Bug 3.3.1.3] AAPSclient does not fetch data from NS", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3797", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3797", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AAPSClient suddenly stops receiving data from NS several times a day. Hitting 'deliver now' fetches data at once. Occurs with or without websockets. Started on version 3.3.1.3.", "cause": "The issue is caused by glucose data not being uploaded to Nightscout using NSClientV3. If data is uploaded by another app (e.g., Juggluco) using v1 or not v3, AAPSClient using v3 will not receive it.", "fix": "Ensure that the glucose data is uploaded to Nightscout using NSClientV3. For Juggluco users, enable 'xdrip Broadcast' in Juggluco and set glucose source in AAPS to xDrip+, and configure AAPS to save glucose values to Nightscout. Alternatively, one user fixed it by deactivating nightscout cloud upload in xdrip+ application.", "settings_changed": ["xdrip Broadcast → enabled", "glucose source → xDrip+", "nightscout cloud upload → deactivated"], "devices": ["Juggluco"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClientV3", "NSClientV1", "xdrip Broadcast", "xDrip+"], "evidence_quote": "If you don't receive data using v3 it only does mean it is not uploaded using v3. This is directly against best practice to let only AAPS upload to NS", "text": "[Bug 3.3.1.3] AAPSclient does not fetch data from NS AAPSClient suddenly stops receiving data from NS several times a day. Hitting 'deliver now' fetches data at once. Occurs with or without websockets. Started on version 3.3.1.3. The issue is caused by glucose data not being uploaded to Nightscout using NSClientV3. If data is uploaded by another app (e.g., Juggluco) using v1 or not v3, AAPSClient using v3 will not receive it. Ensure that the glucose data is uploaded to Nightscout using NSClientV3. For Juggluco users, enable 'xdrip Broadcast' in Juggluco and set glucose source in AAPS to xDrip+, and configure AAPS to save glucose values to Nightscout. Alternatively, one user fixed it by deactivating nightscout cloud upload in xdrip+ application. Juggluco NSClientV3 NSClientV1 xdrip Broadcast xDrip+ If you don't receive data using v3 it only does mean it is not uploaded using v3. This is directly against best practice to let only AAPS upload to NS"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3798", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3798, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3798, "title": "[Bug] - Bolus Wizard does not correctly display negative units", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3798", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3798", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In the Bolus Wizard/Calculator, positive IOB is displayed as a positive number instead of a negative number that should be deducted from the calculated dose. Additionally, any negative number in the right column causes the 'U' after the figure to wrap to the next line, and the bottom of the U is truncated.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause for the sign change; it is a regression from version 3.2.0.4 to 3.3.1.3. The wrapping issue is attributed to the user's larger font size on their device.", "fix": "The fix for the sign issue was merged in PR #3831, which corrected the math notation to show negative numbers with a minus sign. For the wrapping issue, reducing the character size on the phone makes the 'U' fit on the same line.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Google Pixel 9 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 14"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I focused on getting correct math notation in wizard calc log so when you sum them all up it will be the bolus you will administer in the end.", "text": "[Bug] - Bolus Wizard does not correctly display negative units In the Bolus Wizard/Calculator, positive IOB is displayed as a positive number instead of a negative number that should be deducted from the calculated dose. Additionally, any negative number in the right column causes the 'U' after the figure to wrap to the next line, and the bottom of the U is truncated. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause for the sign change; it is a regression from version 3.2.0.4 to 3.3.1.3. The wrapping issue is attributed to the user's larger font size on their device. The fix for the sign issue was merged in PR #3831, which corrected the math notation to show negative numbers with a minus sign. For the wrapping issue, reducing the character size on the phone makes the 'U' fit on the same line. Google Pixel 9 Pro Android 14  I focused on getting correct math notation in wizard calc log so when you sum them all up it will be the bolus you will administer in the end."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-3871", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3871, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 3871, "title": "3.3.1.3-dev crashes when (de-)selecting the Insulin button", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3871", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/3871", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In dev version 1985, the app restarts every time when clicking on the preferences button to show or deactivate the Insulin button. The other three buttons work fine. The issue occurs regardless of whether SMB or AUTOISF plugin is active.", "cause": "The crash was fixed by a commit, but the thread does not explicitly state the root cause. Later, a separate issue about version text readability in dark theme was discussed, but the original crash cause is not described.", "fix": "The crash was fixed by commit 6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e. For the version text readability issue, a fix was proposed in PR #3879.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Accu-Chek Combo"], "android_versions": ["Android 13", "Android 14"], "driver_tags": ["virtual pump"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e", "text": "3.3.1.3-dev crashes when (de-)selecting the Insulin button In dev version 1985, the app restarts every time when clicking on the preferences button to show or deactivate the Insulin button. The other three buttons work fine. The issue occurs regardless of whether SMB or AUTOISF plugin is active. The crash was fixed by a commit, but the thread does not explicitly state the root cause. Later, a separate issue about version text readability in dark theme was discussed, but the original crash cause is not described. The crash was fixed by commit 6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e. For the version text readability issue, a fix was proposed in PR #3879. Accu-Chek Combo Android 13 Android 14 virtual pump fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/6018b405d72ba47222e1279092b12d63c4fcc87e"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4011", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4011, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4011, "title": "Medtrum Pump unreachable after 2 minutes", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4011", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4011", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Medtrum pump disconnects from the phone and AAPS cannot reconnect after about 2 minutes; restarting the phone restores control for only about 2 minutes before the pump becomes unreachable again.", "cause": "The MyBMW app's Nearby devices permission interferes with the Medtrum pump's Bluetooth connection to AAPS on Android 15/16, causing the pump to become unreachable after about 2 minutes.", "fix": "Remove/disable the 'Nearby devices permission' for the MyBMW app and decline the request to grant it; this resolves the Medtrum pump connection loss.", "settings_changed": ["Nearby devices permission → removed"], "devices": ["Medtrum pump"], "android_versions": ["Android 15", "Android 14", "Android 16"], "driver_tags": ["byoda", "xdrip+", "medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "Hello, I have no problem using BMW app without \"Nearby devices permission\". After removing the permission app asked me if I want to grant these permission, I clicked no and it does not bother me anymore.", "text": "Medtrum Pump unreachable after 2 minutes Medtrum pump disconnects from the phone and AAPS cannot reconnect after about 2 minutes; restarting the phone restores control for only about 2 minutes before the pump becomes unreachable again. The MyBMW app's Nearby devices permission interferes with the Medtrum pump's Bluetooth connection to AAPS on Android 15/16, causing the pump to become unreachable after about 2 minutes. Remove/disable the 'Nearby devices permission' for the MyBMW app and decline the request to grant it; this resolves the Medtrum pump connection loss. Medtrum pump Android 15 Android 14 Android 16 byoda xdrip+ medtrum Hello, I have no problem using BMW app without \"Nearby devices permission\". After removing the permission app asked me if I want to grant these permission, I clicked no and it does not bother me anymore."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4027", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4027, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4027, "title": "No Pod activation possible since Android 16 Update", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4027", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4027", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating a Pixel phone to Android 16, deactivating an old Omnipod DASH pod works, but activating a new pod fails with 'Failed to connect to pod'. Manual bonding mode also does not work, while an already-active pod continues to work.", "cause": "The Android 16 update exposes a compatibility bug in AAPS's DASH connection code that prevents activation of new pods, requiring a code hotfix.", "fix": "Update to AAPS 3.3.2.1 (which contains the fix), or build the dev332 branch; alternatively apply the hotfix-a16-dash commits 6153bc4 and 39dd2e6 to master. A temporary workaround is to activate the pod on a backup phone and import the settings export into the main phone.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dash", "Pixel 7 Pro", "Pixel 6", "Pixel 7a", "Pixel 8 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 16", "Android 15"], "driver_tags": ["dash"], "evidence_quote": "Fix for android 16 is merged to master in 3.3.2.1 - based on multiple reports from A16 users I believe this issue can be closed @MilosKozak", "text": "No Pod activation possible since Android 16 Update After updating a Pixel phone to Android 16, deactivating an old Omnipod DASH pod works, but activating a new pod fails with 'Failed to connect to pod'. Manual bonding mode also does not work, while an already-active pod continues to work. The Android 16 update exposes a compatibility bug in AAPS's DASH connection code that prevents activation of new pods, requiring a code hotfix. Update to AAPS 3.3.2.1 (which contains the fix), or build the dev332 branch; alternatively apply the hotfix-a16-dash commits 6153bc4 and 39dd2e6 to master. A temporary workaround is to activate the pod on a backup phone and import the settings export into the main phone. Dash Pixel 7 Pro Pixel 6 Pixel 7a Pixel 8 Pro Android 16 Android 15 dash Fix for android 16 is merged to master in 3.3.2.1 - based on multiple reports from A16 users I believe this issue can be closed @MilosKozak"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4049", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4049, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4049, "title": "No more connection when ending Nano (and DASH) pods", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4049", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4049", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After deactivating a Nano or DASH pod, an alert 'pod basal injection' or 'pump unreachable/basal not set' appears, and the pump becomes unreachable. The issue occurs systematically after each pod deactivation and also during activation of a new pod.", "cause": "The issue was traced to a specific commit (874ea86) that introduced changes causing the pump to be in an incorrect state during pod deactivation/activation, leading to the alert. The problem was fixed by a later commit (b92d228a).", "fix": "The fix was implemented in commit b92d228a, which resolved the problem for both DASH and Medtrum Nano pods. Users confirmed that after applying this commit, the alert no longer appears after deactivation.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtrum Nano", "Omnipod DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtrum", "DASH"], "evidence_quote": "Tested commit #b92d228a: fixes the problem for DASH.", "text": "No more connection when ending Nano (and DASH) pods After deactivating a Nano or DASH pod, an alert 'pod basal injection' or 'pump unreachable/basal not set' appears, and the pump becomes unreachable. The issue occurs systematically after each pod deactivation and also during activation of a new pod. The issue was traced to a specific commit (874ea86) that introduced changes causing the pump to be in an incorrect state during pod deactivation/activation, leading to the alert. The problem was fixed by a later commit (b92d228a). The fix was implemented in commit b92d228a, which resolved the problem for both DASH and Medtrum Nano pods. Users confirmed that after applying this commit, the alert no longer appears after deactivation. Medtrum Nano Omnipod DASH Medtrum DASH Tested commit #b92d228a: fixes the problem for DASH."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4070", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4070, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4070, "title": "No more UAM ??", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4070", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4070", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User reports that no UAM (unannounced meal) bars appear on the graphs for several weeks, despite having IOB greater than 2x basal rate and UAM enabled in settings. Multiple users confirm the issue persists on dev and master versions.", "cause": "The thread identifies that using AAPS sensitivity (instead of Oref1 sensitivity) disables UAM detection. The user states: 'If you use AAPS sensibility, you loose UAM. Using Oref1 sensitivity brings back the UAM.'", "fix": "Switch sensitivity plugin from AAPS to Oref1 sensitivity. The user reports that setting Oref1 sensitivity restores UAM bars.", "settings_changed": ["Sensitivity plugin → Oref1"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Issue probably solved. If you use _AAPS sensibility_, you loose UAM. Using Oref1 sensitivity brings back the UAM.", "text": "No more UAM ?? User reports that no UAM (unannounced meal) bars appear on the graphs for several weeks, despite having IOB greater than 2x basal rate and UAM enabled in settings. Multiple users confirm the issue persists on dev and master versions. The thread identifies that using AAPS sensitivity (instead of Oref1 sensitivity) disables UAM detection. The user states: 'If you use AAPS sensibility, you loose UAM. Using Oref1 sensitivity brings back the UAM.' Switch sensitivity plugin from AAPS to Oref1 sensitivity. The user reports that setting Oref1 sensitivity restores UAM bars.   Issue probably solved. If you use _AAPS sensibility_, you loose UAM. Using Oref1 sensitivity brings back the UAM."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4182", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4182, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4182, "title": "AAPS Dev/Debug - LeakCanary results", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4182", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4182", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "LeakCanary reports memory leaks and OutOfMemoryError's during heap analysis while running AAPS dev/debug builds. The user reports leaks occurring when changing Automations and continuously updating leak results.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. MilosKozak's analysis shows unreachable objects related to Equil pairing fragments, but the user questions how Equil gets involved as it was not active.", "fix": "No fix is stated in the thread. The maintainer says reports are welcome but not necessary to hunt for them specifically.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Equil"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Equil Pairing"], "evidence_quote": "Equil Pairing:", "text": "AAPS Dev/Debug - LeakCanary results LeakCanary reports memory leaks and OutOfMemoryError's during heap analysis while running AAPS dev/debug builds. The user reports leaks occurring when changing Automations and continuously updating leak results. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. MilosKozak's analysis shows unreachable objects related to Equil pairing fragments, but the user questions how Equil gets involved as it was not active. No fix is stated in the thread. The maintainer says reports are welcome but not necessary to hunt for them specifically. Equil Equil Pairing Equil Pairing:"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4270", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4270, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4270, "title": "Nano : continous pump unreachable alert", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4270", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4270", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since yesterday, I started getting Nano pump unreachable alerts, all the time. Loop works normally except the errors. Downgrading to dev-c 27/10 solves the problem.", "cause": "The issue was introduced by a commit on the dev branch, likely related to changes around pump connection handling. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but the fix commit is referenced.", "fix": "Fixed by commit 5be253f4c18f95d7fff1db5782bbaa4a6dea494b. Users should update to a version that includes this commit.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Nano", "Medtrum", "DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/5be253f4c18f95d7fff1db5782bbaa4a6dea494b", "text": "Nano : continous pump unreachable alert Since yesterday, I started getting Nano pump unreachable alerts, all the time. Loop works normally except the errors. Downgrading to dev-c 27/10 solves the problem. The issue was introduced by a commit on the dev branch, likely related to changes around pump connection handling. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but the fix commit is referenced. Fixed by commit 5be253f4c18f95d7fff1db5782bbaa4a6dea494b. Users should update to a version that includes this commit. Nano Medtrum DASH Medtrum fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/5be253f4c18f95d7fff1db5782bbaa4a6dea494b"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4360", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4360, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4360, "title": "Bug : Medtrum manual bolus progression window", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4360", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4360", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When using manual bolus with Medtrum Nano pump, the bolus progression window initially shows the amount injected with the last bolus/SMB, then after 1 second shows the actual bolus being delivered, and then disappears after a few seconds. Tapping the line at the bottom of the UI does not bring it back.", "cause": "The issue is Medtrum-specific and comes from NotificationPacket::handleNormalBolus where at start of a new bolus as a first message is sent result of last bolus (bolusCompleted = true, bolusDelivered = size_of_last_bolus).", "fix": "The fix is in PR #4364 which resets the Medtrum bolus progress to zero when starting a bolus. This was merged by MilosKozak.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtrum Nano"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtrum"], "evidence_quote": "It's metrum specific and it comes from: `NotificationPacket::handleNormalBolus` where at start of a new bolus as a first message is sent result of last bolus ie: `bolusCompleted = true` `bolusDelivered = size_of_last_bolus`", "text": "Bug : Medtrum manual bolus progression window When using manual bolus with Medtrum Nano pump, the bolus progression window initially shows the amount injected with the last bolus/SMB, then after 1 second shows the actual bolus being delivered, and then disappears after a few seconds. Tapping the line at the bottom of the UI does not bring it back. The issue is Medtrum-specific and comes from NotificationPacket::handleNormalBolus where at start of a new bolus as a first message is sent result of last bolus (bolusCompleted = true, bolusDelivered = size_of_last_bolus). The fix is in PR #4364 which resets the Medtrum bolus progress to zero when starting a bolus. This was merged by MilosKozak. Medtrum Nano Medtrum It's metrum specific and it comes from: `NotificationPacket::handleNormalBolus` where at start of a new bolus as a first message is sent result of last bolus ie: `bolusCompleted = true` `bolusDelivered = size_of_last_bolus`"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4389", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4389, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4389, "title": "AAPS Xdrip sends continuously and keeps app awake and burns battery", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4389", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4389", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Phone becomes warm when not in use, battery usage shows AAPS taking 80% and draining 30% in a couple of hours. Xdrip logs in AAPS show it continuously sending hundreds of BG readings repeatedly, and once it approaches the end of the queue, it falls back several hundred readings and starts again. This goes on continuously until the app is force killed.", "cause": "The issue is triggered when a new BG entry arrives and is added to the queue while the Xdrip queue send is being processed, causing the queue resend to loop and never recover. This was observed when Juggluco sends a BG entry to AAPS in the middle of a sync.", "fix": "The issue was fixed by a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/854833857f4b872db0966f3acc01422062eba574. Additionally, a workaround is to force kill the app, and configuration advice includes disabling sending of BG from AAPS when using xDrip as source, and ensuring only xDrip sends BG data to NS.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 3", "Juggluco", "xDrip", "AAPS"], "android_versions": ["Android 16"], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "broadcast", "NSClientV3", "NSClientv1", "full sync"], "evidence_quote": "Latest theory based on some trial and error CrimsonKage is doing there is that while Xdrip queue send is being processed, if a new entry arrives and is added to the queue this queue resend issue happens and never recovers.", "text": "AAPS Xdrip sends continuously and keeps app awake and burns battery Phone becomes warm when not in use, battery usage shows AAPS taking 80% and draining 30% in a couple of hours. Xdrip logs in AAPS show it continuously sending hundreds of BG readings repeatedly, and once it approaches the end of the queue, it falls back several hundred readings and starts again. This goes on continuously until the app is force killed. The issue is triggered when a new BG entry arrives and is added to the queue while the Xdrip queue send is being processed, causing the queue resend to loop and never recover. This was observed when Juggluco sends a BG entry to AAPS in the middle of a sync. The issue was fixed by a commit referenced by MilosKozak: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/854833857f4b872db0966f3acc01422062eba574. Additionally, a workaround is to force kill the app, and configuration advice includes disabling sending of BG from AAPS when using xDrip as source, and ensuring only xDrip sends BG data to NS. Libre 3 Juggluco xDrip AAPS Android 16 xdrip broadcast NSClientV3 NSClientv1 full sync Latest theory based on some trial and error CrimsonKage is doing there is that while Xdrip queue send is being processed, if a new entry arrives and is added to the queue this queue resend issue happens and never recovers."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4519", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4519, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4519, "title": "Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A Orange Pro fails to connect.", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4519", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4519", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating to version 3.4.0.0 on a XIAOMI 14 phone, the Orange Pro Link app is unable to connect to the Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A insulin pump. After the first successful connection, the basal rate can be read, and the pump's time and settings can be retrieved. However, during subsequent connection attempts, the pump status shows a connection failure. It is impossible to connect to the pump to deliver bolus insulin or adjust the basal rate. Version 3.3.2.1 functions properly without these issues.", "cause": "The issue is caused by a migration bug in the Medtronic Encoding setting during version upgrade to 3.4.0.0. The display names for FourByteSixByteLocal and FourByteSixByteRileyLink were swapped in the code, leading to incorrect encoding behavior after upgrade.", "fix": "Go to the 'Medtronic Encoding' setting and switch the option from one to another (toggle it). This completely fixed the issue. A pull request #4526 was created to fix the underlying bug, and it is recommended to mention in release notes that if pump work is unstable after upgrade to or from 3.4.0.0, try switching the Medtronic Encoding setting.", "settings_changed": ["Medtronic Encoding → toggled between options"], "devices": ["Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A", "Orange Pro Link"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["RileyLink", "Medtronic"], "evidence_quote": "I proposed to go to the \"Medtronic Encoding\" setting and just switch the option from one to another. And that completely fixed the issue.", "text": "Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A Orange Pro fails to connect. After updating to version 3.4.0.0 on a XIAOMI 14 phone, the Orange Pro Link app is unable to connect to the Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A insulin pump. After the first successful connection, the basal rate can be read, and the pump's time and settings can be retrieved. However, during subsequent connection attempts, the pump status shows a connection failure. It is impossible to connect to the pump to deliver bolus insulin or adjust the basal rate. Version 3.3.2.1 functions properly without these issues. The issue is caused by a migration bug in the Medtronic Encoding setting during version upgrade to 3.4.0.0. The display names for FourByteSixByteLocal and FourByteSixByteRileyLink were swapped in the code, leading to incorrect encoding behavior after upgrade. Go to the 'Medtronic Encoding' setting and switch the option from one to another (toggle it). This completely fixed the issue. A pull request #4526 was created to fix the underlying bug, and it is recommended to mention in release notes that if pump work is unstable after upgrade to or from 3.4.0.0, try switching the Medtronic Encoding setting. Medtronic 722 Version 2.2A Orange Pro Link RileyLink Medtronic I proposed to go to the \"Medtronic Encoding\" setting and just switch the option from one to another. And that completely fixed the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4521", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4521, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4521, "title": "No automatic upload to Tidepool", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4521", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4521", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Upload to Nightscout happens automatically, but no upload is made to Tidepool even after waiting more than 24 hours. Sometimes tapping on upload now asks for user ID and password, then uploads, but it does not keep uploading.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suspected to be a regression in version 3.4.0.0, possibly related to connection options blocking uploads even when restrictions are met, or a change to OAUTH2.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix. A workaround that temporarily worked was logging out and back in under the Tidepool menu in AAPS, but it stopped again. The issue was reported to be working fine with version 3.4.2.0.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "This was solved for me by Jim Kelly on facebook. I had to tap on logout under the Tidepool menu in AAPS. Then, tap on login in the same menu and enter the credentials again in the browser that comes up. Since then, 14 hours ago, it has been uploading a new value every 5 minutes with a 3-hour delay non-stop.", "text": "No automatic upload to Tidepool Upload to Nightscout happens automatically, but no upload is made to Tidepool even after waiting more than 24 hours. Sometimes tapping on upload now asks for user ID and password, then uploads, but it does not keep uploading. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suspected to be a regression in version 3.4.0.0, possibly related to connection options blocking uploads even when restrictions are met, or a change to OAUTH2. The thread does not state a definitive fix. A workaround that temporarily worked was logging out and back in under the Tidepool menu in AAPS, but it stopped again. The issue was reported to be working fine with version 3.4.2.0.   This was solved for me by Jim Kelly on facebook. I had to tap on logout under the Tidepool menu in AAPS. Then, tap on login in the same menu and enter the credentials again in the browser that comes up. Since then, 14 hours ago, it has been uploading a new value every 5 minutes with a 3-hour delay non-stop."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4539", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4539, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4539, "title": "AAPS 3.4.0.0 - Gaps in network coverage when I leave the Wi-Fi network", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4539", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4539", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When leaving and reconnecting to Wi-Fi, missing CGM data is not uploaded to Nightscout, and recording gaps are not filled. This started after updating to AAPS 3.4.0.0. The gaps only appear in Nightscout; AAPS and Dexcom app show no gaps.", "cause": "The thread identifies a bug in Nightscout rendering: Nightscout must be restarted to see backfilled data, but AAPSClient recognizes everything correctly.", "fix": "Restarting the Nightscout server displays the missing values. The issue is a bug in Nightscout rendering, not in AAPS.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G7"], "android_versions": ["Android 16"], "driver_tags": ["original Dexcom APP", "Xdrip+", "AAPS", "companion app"], "evidence_quote": "There is a bug in NS rendering (NS must be restarted to see backfilled data) but AAPSClient recognize everything correctly", "text": "AAPS 3.4.0.0 - Gaps in network coverage when I leave the Wi-Fi network When leaving and reconnecting to Wi-Fi, missing CGM data is not uploaded to Nightscout, and recording gaps are not filled. This started after updating to AAPS 3.4.0.0. The gaps only appear in Nightscout; AAPS and Dexcom app show no gaps. The thread identifies a bug in Nightscout rendering: Nightscout must be restarted to see backfilled data, but AAPSClient recognizes everything correctly. Restarting the Nightscout server displays the missing values. The issue is a bug in Nightscout rendering, not in AAPS. Dexcom G7 Android 16 original Dexcom APP Xdrip+ AAPS companion app There is a bug in NS rendering (NS must be restarted to see backfilled data) but AAPSClient recognize everything correctly"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4566", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4566, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4566, "title": "Feature Request: Ability to backfill to Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4566", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4566", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "If Nightscout upload fails for any reason, it would help to be able to upload past data to fill gaps. The user switched Nightscout sites for an experiment and when switching back, had a gap of about 40 minutes. Full synchronization does not fill it.", "cause": "AAPS has the first Nightscout server '_id' already populated in its database for data that was successfully created in Nightscout. Data with a Nightscout '_id' are not synced again, so when switching to another Nightscout instance, the data is not uploaded.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. MilosKozak states that with NSCv3 Fullsync uploads all data stored in AAPS database, and that AAPS tracks db changes and stores last successful timestamp, so enabling upload continues from there. However, tests by Navid200 and psonnera showed full sync did not fill the gap. psonnera suggests deleting the '_id' in AAPS might help but could generate duplicates. No concrete resolution is given.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSCv3", "fullsync", "full synchronization", "backfill"], "evidence_quote": "For AAPS, data with a Nightscout \"_id\" don't need to be sync'd with Nightscout since they should be already present. And this is why it fails to upload to another Nightscout instance.", "text": "Feature Request: Ability to backfill to Nightscout If Nightscout upload fails for any reason, it would help to be able to upload past data to fill gaps. The user switched Nightscout sites for an experiment and when switching back, had a gap of about 40 minutes. Full synchronization does not fill it. AAPS has the first Nightscout server '_id' already populated in its database for data that was successfully created in Nightscout. Data with a Nightscout '_id' are not synced again, so when switching to another Nightscout instance, the data is not uploaded. No definitive fix is provided. MilosKozak states that with NSCv3 Fullsync uploads all data stored in AAPS database, and that AAPS tracks db changes and stores last successful timestamp, so enabling upload continues from there. However, tests by Navid200 and psonnera showed full sync did not fill the gap. psonnera suggests deleting the '_id' in AAPS might help but could generate duplicates. No concrete resolution is given.  NSCv3 fullsync full synchronization backfill For AAPS, data with a Nightscout \"_id\" don't need to be sync'd with Nightscout since they should be already present. And this is why it fails to upload to another Nightscout instance."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-46", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 46, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 46, "title": "AAPS not sending basal to xDrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/46", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/46", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Since updating to AAPS version 2.7, xDrip does not receive basal data. It receives carbs and bolus (via Nightscout) but not basals. Some users report xDrip not receiving any treatments when there is no internet connection, and basal display in xDrip has not worked for years.", "cause": "AAPS never sent basals to xDrip; xDrip was parsing them from watch data, which was about to fail. Additionally, nsclient may stop broadcasting locally when there is no internet connection.", "fix": "Enable the xDrip Statusline plugin from the config builder to see basal rate in the status line, but this does not fix the basal plot in xDrip. No definitive fix is provided in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic 554", "Dexcom G6", "Omnipod Eros", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1"], "driver_tags": ["local broadcast", "NSClient", "statusline", "watch data"], "evidence_quote": "AAPS never sent basals to xDrip. xDrip was parsing those from the watch data. That was about to fail.", "text": "AAPS not sending basal to xDrip Since updating to AAPS version 2.7, xDrip does not receive basal data. It receives carbs and bolus (via Nightscout) but not basals. Some users report xDrip not receiving any treatments when there is no internet connection, and basal display in xDrip has not worked for years. AAPS never sent basals to xDrip; xDrip was parsing them from watch data, which was about to fail. Additionally, nsclient may stop broadcasting locally when there is no internet connection. Enable the xDrip Statusline plugin from the config builder to see basal rate in the status line, but this does not fix the basal plot in xDrip. No definitive fix is provided in the thread. Medtronic 554 Dexcom G6 Omnipod Eros Libre 2 Android 8.1 local broadcast NSClient statusline watch data AAPS never sent basals to xDrip. xDrip was parsing those from the watch data. That was about to fail."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4619", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4619, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4619, "title": "FEATURE REQUEST : Complication for active 'Temporary Target' and the remaining time", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4619", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4619", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user requests a complication for active 'Temporary Target' and the remaining time, so his son can see if automations have been triggered or how long a temporary target remains active.", "cause": null, "fix": "Implemented in PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4717 - New BR/TT complication merged to dev. Both wear and phone app must be updated for it to work.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Implemented in PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4717 - Feel free to check out. Awaiting merge.", "text": "FEATURE REQUEST : Complication for active 'Temporary Target' and the remaining time The user requests a complication for active 'Temporary Target' and the remaining time, so his son can see if automations have been triggered or how long a temporary target remains active.  Implemented in PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4717 - New BR/TT complication merged to dev. Both wear and phone app must be updated for it to work.   Implemented in PR https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/4717 - Feel free to check out. Awaiting merge."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4664", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4664, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4664, "title": "AAPS 3.4.1.0 and 3.4.2.1 not sending Treatments to Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4664", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4664", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating AAPS from DEV 3.4.0.0 to 3.4.1.0 and 3.4.2.1, treatments are not sent to Nightscout (on Northflank). Device statuses are sent, but the queue number in NSV3 tab increases and only a full sync brings it to 0, after which it rises again. The 'ADD Treatments' option does not appear in the NSClient tab.", "cause": "The issue is caused by the Medtronic driver, as identified by MilosKozak.", "fix": "A fix was provided by andyrozman in a branch (issue_4664) that enables refreshes including history reading. The user confirmed that after installing the fix, treatments upload correctly and the queue drops to 0.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic pump"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic"], "evidence_quote": "Issue is Medtronic driver @andyrozman", "text": "AAPS 3.4.1.0 and 3.4.2.1 not sending Treatments to Nightscout After updating AAPS from DEV 3.4.0.0 to 3.4.1.0 and 3.4.2.1, treatments are not sent to Nightscout (on Northflank). Device statuses are sent, but the queue number in NSV3 tab increases and only a full sync brings it to 0, after which it rises again. The 'ADD Treatments' option does not appear in the NSClient tab. The issue is caused by the Medtronic driver, as identified by MilosKozak. A fix was provided by andyrozman in a branch (issue_4664) that enables refreshes including history reading. The user confirmed that after installing the fix, treatments upload correctly and the queue drops to 0. Medtronic pump Medtronic Issue is Medtronic driver @andyrozman"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-474", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 474, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 474, "title": "AAPS 2.8.2 not connecting to Orangelink on Samsung a20e", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/474", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/474", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After initial successful connection, AAPS 2.8.2 fails to reconnect to OrangeLink on Samsung a20e. RileyLink Status on MEDTRONIC page remains in 'RileyLink initialization...' state. Logs show BLE write failures and 'BT Device not supported' errors. nRF Connect app also fails to connect with GATT error 133.", "cause": "The thread identifies that Samsung devices may have Bluetooth stack issues after AAPS crashes, leaving BLE in a blocked state. Also, a separate issue (#476) with Medtronic history processing causing crashes is identified as the root cause of the crashes that lead to the BLE problem.", "fix": "Workaround: delete OrangeLink from AAPS, remove batteries, reboot phone, reinsert batteries, and reconnect. Also, pairing the phone with an unrelated device (e.g., speakers) sometimes helps. The issue may be resolved in AAPS 3.0 beta builds, but still occurs occasionally. For persistent cases, the OL must be removed from AAPS and re-added after power cycling.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["OrangeLink", "Samsung a20e", "Samsung S7", "Nexus 5x", "Medtronic 722"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["RileyLink", "OrangeLink", "BLE"], "evidence_quote": "After million of attempts I got connected with one trick: paired phone with some unrelated device - speakers. It probably touched something in Bluetooth stack and enabled connections to OrangeLink again (while clearing of cache and data of system Bluetooth app was not helping).", "text": "AAPS 2.8.2 not connecting to Orangelink on Samsung a20e After initial successful connection, AAPS 2.8.2 fails to reconnect to OrangeLink on Samsung a20e. RileyLink Status on MEDTRONIC page remains in 'RileyLink initialization...' state. Logs show BLE write failures and 'BT Device not supported' errors. nRF Connect app also fails to connect with GATT error 133. The thread identifies that Samsung devices may have Bluetooth stack issues after AAPS crashes, leaving BLE in a blocked state. Also, a separate issue (#476) with Medtronic history processing causing crashes is identified as the root cause of the crashes that lead to the BLE problem. Workaround: delete OrangeLink from AAPS, remove batteries, reboot phone, reinsert batteries, and reconnect. Also, pairing the phone with an unrelated device (e.g., speakers) sometimes helps. The issue may be resolved in AAPS 3.0 beta builds, but still occurs occasionally. For persistent cases, the OL must be removed from AAPS and re-added after power cycling. OrangeLink Samsung a20e Samsung S7 Nexus 5x Medtronic 722 Android 11 RileyLink OrangeLink BLE After million of attempts I got connected with one trick: paired phone with some unrelated device - speakers. It probably touched something in Bluetooth stack and enabled connections to OrangeLink again (while clearing of cache and data of system Bluetooth app was not helping)."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4811", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4811, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4811, "title": "Omnipod Dash just stopped working", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4811", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4811", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The pod worked fine for about 12 hours. After it delivered a bolus, a few minutes after, it started beeping. AAPS showed that it could not connect to the pod.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash"], "android_versions": ["Android 16"], "driver_tags": ["omnipod dash"], "evidence_quote": "The pod worked fine for about 12 hours. After it delivered a bolus, a few minutes after, it started beeping. AAPS showed that it could not connect to the pod.", "text": "Omnipod Dash just stopped working The pod worked fine for about 12 hours. After it delivered a bolus, a few minutes after, it started beeping. AAPS showed that it could not connect to the pod.   Omnipod Dash Android 16 omnipod dash The pod worked fine for about 12 hours. After it delivered a bolus, a few minutes after, it started beeping. AAPS showed that it could not connect to the pod."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4887", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4887, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4887, "title": "Dev AAPS crashing after latest build", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4887", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4887", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After updating to the latest dev build, the app starts saying 'updating database' and then crashes after a while. The previous version from May 15th works fine.", "cause": null, "fix": "Re-installing the app fixed the issue for one user, but additional import of settings was needed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Re-installing the app fixed the issue for me. Setting needed additional import", "text": "Dev AAPS crashing after latest build After updating to the latest dev build, the app starts saying 'updating database' and then crashes after a while. The previous version from May 15th works fine.  Re-installing the app fixed the issue for one user, but additional import of settings was needed.   Re-installing the app fixed the issue for me. Setting needed additional import"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-4927", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4927, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 4927, "title": "Battery drain issue", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4927", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/4927", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After switching from a Samsung A71 to a Pixel 10, AndroidAPS background processes drain 45-50% of battery, causing the phone to last only about 9 hours on a full charge with minimal use. The phone also runs constantly warm.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. The user speculates it might be a stuck process from the initial OS update, but this is not confirmed.", "fix": "The issue resolved itself after the phone completely discharged and was recharged, which apparently cleared a stuck process. No specific action was taken by the user to fix it.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung A71", "Pixel 10", "Pixel Watch 2", "Pixel 7 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 16"], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic Guardian", "xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "So whatever was causing the drainage, must've been some stuck proccess that was there from when I first set up the phone. And the complete drain that happened today did some hard reset or something.", "text": "Battery drain issue After switching from a Samsung A71 to a Pixel 10, AndroidAPS background processes drain 45-50% of battery, causing the phone to last only about 9 hours on a full charge with minimal use. The phone also runs constantly warm. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. The user speculates it might be a stuck process from the initial OS update, but this is not confirmed. The issue resolved itself after the phone completely discharged and was recharged, which apparently cleared a stuck process. No specific action was taken by the user to fix it. Samsung A71 Pixel 10 Pixel Watch 2 Pixel 7 Pro Android 16 Medtronic Guardian xDrip So whatever was causing the drainage, must've been some stuck proccess that was there from when I first set up the phone. And the complete drain that happened today did some hard reset or something."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-5040", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 5040, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 5040, "title": "Equil - connect timeout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/5040", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/5040", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In version 3.2.4.5, when attempting to perform a bolus, even through the calculator, there is no connection. The timer counts down, but no insulin is delivered. The same situation occurs when attempting to change the reservoir.", "cause": "A regression introduced between versions 3.4.2.2 and 3.4.2.3 caused the issue, which was addressed by changes in the dev3 branch.", "fix": "Build from the dev3 branch with the specific commit 03ea9f72f5ef45dc8e9d1fef9e5213df6180f9f8, which fixed the bolus and reservoir change issues. Version 3.4.2.6 was released with the fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Equil"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Something that appeared between 3.4.2.2 and 3.4.2.3 is causing the problem.", "text": "Equil - connect timeout In version 3.2.4.5, when attempting to perform a bolus, even through the calculator, there is no connection. The timer counts down, but no insulin is delivered. The same situation occurs when attempting to change the reservoir. A regression introduced between versions 3.4.2.2 and 3.4.2.3 caused the issue, which was addressed by changes in the dev3 branch. Build from the dev3 branch with the specific commit 03ea9f72f5ef45dc8e9d1fef9e5213df6180f9f8, which fixed the bolus and reservoir change issues. Version 3.4.2.6 was released with the fix. Equil  Something that appeared between 3.4.2.2 and 3.4.2.3 is causing the problem."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-527", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 527, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 527, "title": "Lyumjev U200/ML", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/527", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/527", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Request to make an adjustment in AndroidAPS to use Lyumjev U200/ml safely. The discussion revolves around the need for support for U200 insulin concentration in AndroidAPS, with concerns about safety and usability.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Request to make an adjustment in AndroidAPS to use Lyumjev U200/ml safely.", "text": "Lyumjev U200/ML Request to make an adjustment in AndroidAPS to use Lyumjev U200/ml safely. The discussion revolves around the need for support for U200 insulin concentration in AndroidAPS, with concerns about safety and usability.     Request to make an adjustment in AndroidAPS to use Lyumjev U200/ml safely."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-598", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 598, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 598, "title": "APS doesn't not respond to BG readings", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/598", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/598", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "BG is changing every 5 min but APS doesn't run sometimes for 25 min, requiring pressing 'run now' to act accordingly. The issue recurs despite reinstalling the app.", "cause": "MilosKozak identified that the problem is no BG data reaching AAPS, possibly due to sensor out of range or sleeping Dexcom app.", "fix": "No definitive fix was provided; MilosKozak suggested turning off AUTOSENS logging to get better logs, and the user was asked to provide logs from the right period. The issue remained unresolved.", "settings_changed": ["AUTOSENS logging → off"], "devices": ["Dexcom"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Dexcom app"], "evidence_quote": "I see execution 17:23:46 and then new BG @17:33:37 so your problem is no BG data. It can be sensor out of range or sleeping Dexcom app", "text": "APS doesn't not respond to BG readings BG is changing every 5 min but APS doesn't run sometimes for 25 min, requiring pressing 'run now' to act accordingly. The issue recurs despite reinstalling the app. MilosKozak identified that the problem is no BG data reaching AAPS, possibly due to sensor out of range or sleeping Dexcom app. No definitive fix was provided; MilosKozak suggested turning off AUTOSENS logging to get better logs, and the user was asked to provide logs from the right period. The issue remained unresolved. Dexcom Dexcom app I see execution 17:23:46 and then new BG @17:33:37 so your problem is no BG data. It can be sensor out of range or sleeping Dexcom app"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-600", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 600, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 600, "title": "2.8.2 master / Arrow direction bug", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/600", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/600", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In AAPS 2.8.2, the arrow direction on the main screen is often horizontal even when glucose is rising or falling, while the AAPS watchface and xDrip+ show a correct sloped arrow. This discrepancy is confusing and potentially dangerous.", "cause": "AAPS main screen uses the arrow direction provided by the BG source (e.g., xDrip+ or Dexcom app), which may be calculated differently (e.g., using a longer time interval or updated history values) than the arrow calculated by AAPS for the watchface, which uses a 5-minute delta. This can lead to different arrows between the phone and watchface.", "fix": "The issue was addressed in a commit (d43393e2af7f6133b267e04967e8fc2b70149d16) that likely changed the arrow calculation logic, but the exact fix is not described in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "xDrip+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip+", "G6"], "evidence_quote": "AAPS shows arrow sent by source (calculated with G6 method), watchfaxe and other apps show calculated arrows (calculated with 5min Delta) => With my example AAPS will show the flat arrow sent by G6 APP (even if calculated short delta is +8 mg/dl) while all other app will calculate a 45° up arrow", "text": "2.8.2 master / Arrow direction bug In AAPS 2.8.2, the arrow direction on the main screen is often horizontal even when glucose is rising or falling, while the AAPS watchface and xDrip+ show a correct sloped arrow. This discrepancy is confusing and potentially dangerous. AAPS main screen uses the arrow direction provided by the BG source (e.g., xDrip+ or Dexcom app), which may be calculated differently (e.g., using a longer time interval or updated history values) than the arrow calculated by AAPS for the watchface, which uses a 5-minute delta. This can lead to different arrows between the phone and watchface. The issue was addressed in a commit (d43393e2af7f6133b267e04967e8fc2b70149d16) that likely changed the arrow calculation logic, but the exact fix is not described in the thread. Dexcom G6 xDrip+ xDrip+ G6 AAPS shows arrow sent by source (calculated with G6 method), watchfaxe and other apps show calculated arrows (calculated with 5min Delta) => With my example AAPS will show the flat arrow sent by G6 APP (even if calculated short delta is +8 mg/dl) while all other app will calculate a 45° up arrow"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-628", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 628, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 628, "title": " BG recalculation fallback 2.8.2.2 dev 06/08/2021 and old", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/628", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/628", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The loop breaks without errors, often during the night, leading to high blood sugar. The user notices that SMB no longer delivers, LOOP indicates no APS selected, and sensitivity shows NeN. The issue occurs with default settings but not with a modified version that increases the fallback threshold to 200.", "cause": "The issue is related to the fallback threshold in BG recalculation. The user reports that with default settings the problem occurs often, while with a modified version that increases the fallback threshold to 200 it never happens. The developer later fixed it via a commit.", "fix": "The issue was fixed by a commit: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f790c06b27235a8be929ef04cc007d13bf08b1c7", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Eversense"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["broadcast", "PersistentNotificationPlugin"], "evidence_quote": "fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f790c06b27235a8be929ef04cc007d13bf08b1c7", "text": " BG recalculation fallback 2.8.2.2 dev 06/08/2021 and old The loop breaks without errors, often during the night, leading to high blood sugar. The user notices that SMB no longer delivers, LOOP indicates no APS selected, and sensitivity shows NeN. The issue occurs with default settings but not with a modified version that increases the fallback threshold to 200. The issue is related to the fallback threshold in BG recalculation. The user reports that with default settings the problem occurs often, while with a modified version that increases the fallback threshold to 200 it never happens. The developer later fixed it via a commit. The issue was fixed by a commit: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f790c06b27235a8be929ef04cc007d13bf08b1c7 Eversense broadcast PersistentNotificationPlugin fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f790c06b27235a8be929ef04cc007d13bf08b1c7"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-637", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 637, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 637, "title": "2.8.2.2 Dev : can't restart loop if stopped", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/637", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/637", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "In 2.8.2.2 dev, if the loop is stopped from the main page, it cannot be restarted from the main UI; the user must go to settings/config generator to reactivate the loop. Also, when activated, a strange '364days (deactivated ?)' appears under the button.", "cause": "The issue is partially caused by a bug in disabling the loop, and there is a constraint that prevents direct switching from open loop to closed loop. The exact cause for the inability to restart after stopping is not fully identified in the thread.", "fix": "The issue was reported as 'should be resolved now' by MilosKozak, and a user confirmed that disconnecting/reconnecting pump works and extending disconnection time is possible. However, the original reporter later stated it is only partially solved: open loop to closed loop works, but stopping and restarting from main UI still requires going to config generator. No specific fix or workaround is provided for the remaining issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "should be resolved now", "text": "2.8.2.2 Dev : can't restart loop if stopped In 2.8.2.2 dev, if the loop is stopped from the main page, it cannot be restarted from the main UI; the user must go to settings/config generator to reactivate the loop. Also, when activated, a strange '364days (deactivated ?)' appears under the button. The issue is partially caused by a bug in disabling the loop, and there is a constraint that prevents direct switching from open loop to closed loop. The exact cause for the inability to restart after stopping is not fully identified in the thread. The issue was reported as 'should be resolved now' by MilosKozak, and a user confirmed that disconnecting/reconnecting pump works and extending disconnection time is possible. However, the original reporter later stated it is only partially solved: open loop to closed loop works, but stopping and restarting from main UI still requires going to config generator. No specific fix or workaround is provided for the remaining issue.   should be resolved now"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-645", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 645, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 645, "title": "[2.8.2.2 Dev] Sometimes manual bolus are not correctly recorded in database", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/645", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/645", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Manual boluses (and sometimes SMBs) are correctly delivered by the pump but not recorded in the database, so they are missing from the IOB graph and Treatment tab, though they appear in User Entry and pump history. This occurs intermittently with Accu-Chek Insight pump.", "cause": "The calculated date from the pump event is shifted one day before compared to the real timestamp, causing the bolus to be considered already recorded and not updated in the database.", "fix": "Philoul states 'I'll fix this bug very quickly.' The fix is to correct the date calculation in the Insight driver's processBolusDeliveredEvent.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Accu-Chek Insight"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Insight driver", "pumpSync"], "evidence_quote": "SMB correctly recorded in deliverTreatment ID is found in readHistory during the process of processBolusDeliveredEvent from pump, but the calculated date from pump event is shifted one day before compared to real timestamp (strange because this calculation was not modified during update of the plugin for new database) => I'll fix this bug very quickly.", "text": "[2.8.2.2 Dev] Sometimes manual bolus are not correctly recorded in database Manual boluses (and sometimes SMBs) are correctly delivered by the pump but not recorded in the database, so they are missing from the IOB graph and Treatment tab, though they appear in User Entry and pump history. This occurs intermittently with Accu-Chek Insight pump. The calculated date from the pump event is shifted one day before compared to the real timestamp, causing the bolus to be considered already recorded and not updated in the database. Philoul states 'I'll fix this bug very quickly.' The fix is to correct the date calculation in the Insight driver's processBolusDeliveredEvent. Accu-Chek Insight Insight driver pumpSync SMB correctly recorded in deliverTreatment ID is found in readHistory during the process of processBolusDeliveredEvent from pump, but the calculated date from pump event is shifted one day before compared to real timestamp (strange because this calculation was not modified during update of the plugin for new database) => I'll fix this bug very quickly."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-664", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 664, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 664, "title": "[Medtronic] Automation-triggered profile % changes cause lost pump connections", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/664", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/664", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Automation rules that change the profile % can trigger MDT pump connection failures that persist until AAPS and RL are restarted. The issue occurs occasionally when rules trigger, and is more frequent when rules are enabled. Deleting the app cache resolves the problem for a week+, while restarting the phone/Orangelink only temporarily resolves it.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It speculates that it might be a combination of profile change, microbolus, and temp basal, but no conclusive cause is established.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by testing on AAPS 3.0 B3-B5 and AAPS 2.8.2.10 dev build 2021-11-11, where the problem could no longer be replicated. The thread also notes that deleting the app cache solves the problem for a week+, but this is a workaround, not a permanent fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["MDT 554", "MDT 722", "OrangeLink", "RileyLink"], "android_versions": ["Android 8", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic", "RileyLink", "OrangeLink"], "evidence_quote": "Tested AAPS 2.8.2.10 dev build 2021-11-11 11:40am on an S7 running Android 11 (Pixel Experience) connecting to an MDT 554 via an Orangelink and am no longer able to replicate this. Closing.", "text": "[Medtronic] Automation-triggered profile % changes cause lost pump connections Automation rules that change the profile % can trigger MDT pump connection failures that persist until AAPS and RL are restarted. The issue occurs occasionally when rules trigger, and is more frequent when rules are enabled. Deleting the app cache resolves the problem for a week+, while restarting the phone/Orangelink only temporarily resolves it. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It speculates that it might be a combination of profile change, microbolus, and temp basal, but no conclusive cause is established. The issue was resolved by testing on AAPS 3.0 B3-B5 and AAPS 2.8.2.10 dev build 2021-11-11, where the problem could no longer be replicated. The thread also notes that deleting the app cache solves the problem for a week+, but this is a workaround, not a permanent fix. MDT 554 MDT 722 OrangeLink RileyLink Android 8 Android 11 Medtronic RileyLink OrangeLink Tested AAPS 2.8.2.10 dev build 2021-11-11 11:40am on an S7 running Android 11 (Pixel Experience) connecting to an MDT 554 via an Orangelink and am no longer able to replicate this. Closing."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-67", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 67, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 67, "title": "UI Feedback", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/67", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/67", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The UI requires long-presses and small touch targets for frequent actions such as setting temp targets, profile switches, and disconnecting the pump, which is difficult for people with shaky hands or when half asleep. The top-right 3-dot menu is described as tiny and too close to the notification bar, causing accidental pulls of the notification shade.", "cause": null, "fix": "A contributor stated that most proposals discussed in the thread were included in the dev branch, and mentioned work in PR nightscout/AndroidAPS#76; no specific configuration steps or values were provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I think most of proposals discussed here are now included in dev branch.", "text": "UI Feedback The UI requires long-presses and small touch targets for frequent actions such as setting temp targets, profile switches, and disconnecting the pump, which is difficult for people with shaky hands or when half asleep. The top-right 3-dot menu is described as tiny and too close to the notification bar, causing accidental pulls of the notification shade.  A contributor stated that most proposals discussed in the thread were included in the dev branch, and mentioned work in PR nightscout/AndroidAPS#76; no specific configuration steps or values were provided.   I think most of proposals discussed here are now included in dev branch."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-692", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 692, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 692, "title": "Dev pb with Dana smb and tbr", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/692", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/692", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "In some cases, an error message about wrong TBR value appears in the loop page. When this occurs, if a SMB is scheduled, it will not be sent to the pump until the TBR value becomes correct. The problem fixes itself later during the rise, but reappears when glucose becomes stable. The issue occurs with Dana RS, not with Dana-i or Dash.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. MilosKozak initially suspected a pump driver issue, but later stated that the TBR setting really failed as reported by the pump, and suggested updating the pump firmware. No definitive cause is confirmed.", "fix": "MilosKozak suggested updating the pump firmware using the AnyDana upgrade kit, and later referenced a commit (0dbfa6182f996674c3ab72aa1fc19684d8cc00ae) that hopefully resolves the issue. No specific configuration change is stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana RS"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DanaRSPlugin", "temp basal", "SMB", "TBR"], "evidence_quote": "this time setting of TBR really failed (reported by pump) as this usually works, i'd try update the firmware in pump", "text": "Dev pb with Dana smb and tbr In some cases, an error message about wrong TBR value appears in the loop page. When this occurs, if a SMB is scheduled, it will not be sent to the pump until the TBR value becomes correct. The problem fixes itself later during the rise, but reappears when glucose becomes stable. The issue occurs with Dana RS, not with Dana-i or Dash. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. MilosKozak initially suspected a pump driver issue, but later stated that the TBR setting really failed as reported by the pump, and suggested updating the pump firmware. No definitive cause is confirmed. MilosKozak suggested updating the pump firmware using the AnyDana upgrade kit, and later referenced a commit (0dbfa6182f996674c3ab72aa1fc19684d8cc00ae) that hopefully resolves the issue. No specific configuration change is stated. Dana RS DanaRSPlugin temp basal SMB TBR this time setting of TBR really failed (reported by pump) as this usually works, i'd try update the firmware in pump"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-717", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 717, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 717, "title": "[Dev 2.8.2.5-dev] NSClient Full Sync Kills Nightscout?", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/717", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/717", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "AndroidAPS 2.8.2.5-dev with Nightscout 14.2.3 crashes the Nightscout site on Heroku; it only works when NSClient is paused and after restarting dynos. The issue occurs even with xDrip Cloud Upload disabled. Later reports include queue numbers in NSClient (e.g., 341, 311,764) and errors like 'xhr poll error'.", "cause": "The thread identifies that pressing the 'Full Sync' button in NSClient causes AndroidAPS to send a lot of information, crashing Nightscout. A clean installation resolves it temporarily, but the issue recurs after pressing Full Sync again.", "fix": "Perform a clean installation of AndroidAPS: clear storage from AndroidAPS, then import settings after the first app start. This resolved the issue for the original reporter. Later, the issue was reported solved with AndroidAPS 3.0-beta1. For some, changing MongoDB Node.js version to 3.7 or later appeared to help temporarily.", "settings_changed": ["MongoDB Node.js version → 3.7 or later"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClient", "Full Sync"], "evidence_quote": "I found the \"problem\". AndroidAPS was sending a \"lot\" of information and making my Nightscout crash, I cleared storage from AndroidAPS, and import my settings after the first app start and now the issue is solved.", "text": "[Dev 2.8.2.5-dev] NSClient Full Sync Kills Nightscout? AndroidAPS 2.8.2.5-dev with Nightscout 14.2.3 crashes the Nightscout site on Heroku; it only works when NSClient is paused and after restarting dynos. The issue occurs even with xDrip Cloud Upload disabled. Later reports include queue numbers in NSClient (e.g., 341, 311,764) and errors like 'xhr poll error'. The thread identifies that pressing the 'Full Sync' button in NSClient causes AndroidAPS to send a lot of information, crashing Nightscout. A clean installation resolves it temporarily, but the issue recurs after pressing Full Sync again. Perform a clean installation of AndroidAPS: clear storage from AndroidAPS, then import settings after the first app start. This resolved the issue for the original reporter. Later, the issue was reported solved with AndroidAPS 3.0-beta1. For some, changing MongoDB Node.js version to 3.7 or later appeared to help temporarily.  NSClient Full Sync I found the \"problem\". AndroidAPS was sending a \"lot\" of information and making my Nightscout crash, I cleared storage from AndroidAPS, and import my settings after the first app start and now the issue is solved."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-75", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 75, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 75, "title": "AAPS+Nightscout for selfhosting (SSL)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/75", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/75", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "AndroidAPS requires an SSL connection to Nightscout, but the user wants to self-host Nightscout privately on a VPN without public exposure. The user tried engineering_mode but still gets the error 'NS URL not encrypted', and Nightscout lacks full authentication for its web frontend, so they are reluctant to expose it publicly.", "cause": "AndroidAPS does not allow unencrypted or self-signed certificate connections to Nightscout, and Nightscout's web frontend does not provide full authentication, preventing secure public exposure via reverse proxy.", "fix": "Use a newer Nightscout version (e.g. niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7) that requires authentication even for viewing the web frontend, then expose the Nightscout site to the internet using HTTPS via a reverse proxy such as Caddy.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "OK, I made it working with the latest NS version (I used niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7), there one needs to authenticate even for viewing the web frontend. With this I was able to open the site to the Internet.", "text": "AAPS+Nightscout for selfhosting (SSL) AndroidAPS requires an SSL connection to Nightscout, but the user wants to self-host Nightscout privately on a VPN without public exposure. The user tried engineering_mode but still gets the error 'NS URL not encrypted', and Nightscout lacks full authentication for its web frontend, so they are reluctant to expose it publicly. AndroidAPS does not allow unencrypted or self-signed certificate connections to Nightscout, and Nightscout's web frontend does not provide full authentication, preventing secure public exposure via reverse proxy. Use a newer Nightscout version (e.g. niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7) that requires authentication even for viewing the web frontend, then expose the Nightscout site to the internet using HTTPS via a reverse proxy such as Caddy.   OK, I made it working with the latest NS version (I used niepi/cgm-remote-monitor:14.0.7), there one needs to authenticate even for viewing the web frontend. With this I was able to open the site to the Internet."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-797", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 797, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 797, "title": "Issues when using Nightscout as BG source", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/797", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/797", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using Nightscout as BG source with imported AAPS 2 settings, profile activation fails with errors like 'Profile low target 4.8 is out of hard limits' and 'NO PROFILE SET' on Overview. BG data appears on NSClient tab but not on Overview. Issues occur when AAPS is allowed to sync with Nightscout during initial setup.", "cause": "The thread suggests that profile data synced from Nightscout interferes with the local profile, even after editing, and that AAPS 3.0 automatically enables 'Receive profile store' NSClient setting when importing old settings, which may cause out-of-range profile values to be downloaded.", "fix": "The issue was mostly resolved in beta 5, but the user suggests that AAPS should not automatically enable 'Receive profile store' when importing settings configured to use a Local Profile. The maintainer explains that new settings are defaulted and such nuances are impossible to process.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Nightscout", "Dexcom", "Medtronic"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClient BG", "XDRIP+", "Nightscout", "profile sync"], "evidence_quote": "unless I'm misunderstanding things, if a user imports settings configured to use a Local Profile, then AAPS shouldn't automatically enable 'Receive profile store' NSClient setting.", "text": "Issues when using Nightscout as BG source When using Nightscout as BG source with imported AAPS 2 settings, profile activation fails with errors like 'Profile low target 4.8 is out of hard limits' and 'NO PROFILE SET' on Overview. BG data appears on NSClient tab but not on Overview. Issues occur when AAPS is allowed to sync with Nightscout during initial setup. The thread suggests that profile data synced from Nightscout interferes with the local profile, even after editing, and that AAPS 3.0 automatically enables 'Receive profile store' NSClient setting when importing old settings, which may cause out-of-range profile values to be downloaded. The issue was mostly resolved in beta 5, but the user suggests that AAPS should not automatically enable 'Receive profile store' when importing settings configured to use a Local Profile. The maintainer explains that new settings are defaulted and such nuances are impossible to process. Nightscout Dexcom Medtronic NSClient BG XDRIP+ Nightscout profile sync unless I'm misunderstanding things, if a user imports settings configured to use a Local Profile, then AAPS shouldn't automatically enable 'Receive profile store' NSClient setting."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-798", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 798, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 798, "title": "[3.0-beta1] Medtronic SMBs show as Meal Boluses as well as Incorrect IOB calculation from temp basals", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/798", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/798", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Using Medtronic, SMBs initially show correctly, but after 10-15 minutes get changed to appear as meal boluses. Also, when AAPS has set a 0 temp basal for 30 or 90 minutes, it is applying the full negative IOB even though a new rate is set after the next loop, so the full duration is deducted even though the rate only ran for a few minutes.", "cause": "Zero TBR are not time limited; when a normal TBR is cancelled, a cancel command (rate=0, duration=0) appears in history, but this does not happen for standard Zero TBR, so the duration shown and used is always the full one.", "fix": "The fix was implemented by andyrozman in a branch and later checked in. The user siggy226 confirmed that after installing the correct build, the fix looked good. The fix addresses both the SMB display issue and the Zero TBR duration issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic"], "evidence_quote": "It seems that Zero TBR are not time limited (when normal TBR is cancelled we get cancel command in history (rate=0, duration=0), this doesn't happen if we have standard Zero TBR, so duration shown (and taken by us is always full one)... The problem was there since the beginning and nobody noticed this before...", "text": "[3.0-beta1] Medtronic SMBs show as Meal Boluses as well as Incorrect IOB calculation from temp basals Using Medtronic, SMBs initially show correctly, but after 10-15 minutes get changed to appear as meal boluses. Also, when AAPS has set a 0 temp basal for 30 or 90 minutes, it is applying the full negative IOB even though a new rate is set after the next loop, so the full duration is deducted even though the rate only ran for a few minutes. Zero TBR are not time limited; when a normal TBR is cancelled, a cancel command (rate=0, duration=0) appears in history, but this does not happen for standard Zero TBR, so the duration shown and used is always the full one. The fix was implemented by andyrozman in a branch and later checked in. The user siggy226 confirmed that after installing the correct build, the fix looked good. The fix addresses both the SMB display issue and the Zero TBR duration issue. Medtronic Medtronic It seems that Zero TBR are not time limited (when normal TBR is cancelled we get cancel command in history (rate=0, duration=0), this doesn't happen if we have standard Zero TBR, so duration shown (and taken by us is always full one)... The problem was there since the beginning and nobody noticed this before..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-80", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 80, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 80, "title": "Insight Pump data not shown on Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/80", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/80", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user reports that AndroidAPS connects to the Accu-Chek Insight pump, collects data, and the NS Client uploads data to Nightscout, but pump-related data is not shown. All other data uploads correctly.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. The user speculates it might be a bug related to VPN routing, where pump data is not uploaded when using OpenVPN, but this is not confirmed.", "fix": "The user found that rebooting the phone after disconnecting from VPN caused the pump data to appear in Nightscout. No permanent fix is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Accu-Chek Insight"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NS Client"], "evidence_quote": "As soon as I disconnect from VPN and restart the phone, the pump data is uploaded correctly, but in this case Diabox cannot upload the BG results to NS.", "text": "Insight Pump data not shown on Nightscout The user reports that AndroidAPS connects to the Accu-Chek Insight pump, collects data, and the NS Client uploads data to Nightscout, but pump-related data is not shown. All other data uploads correctly. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. The user speculates it might be a bug related to VPN routing, where pump data is not uploaded when using OpenVPN, but this is not confirmed. The user found that rebooting the phone after disconnecting from VPN caused the pump data to appear in Nightscout. No permanent fix is provided. Accu-Chek Insight NS Client As soon as I disconnect from VPN and restart the phone, the pump data is uploaded correctly, but in this case Diabox cannot upload the BG results to NS."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-807", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 807, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 807, "title": "[AAPS3.0_beta2] NSClient - io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error - Seems to have also broken Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/807", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/807", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After installing NSClient 3.0 beta2, the user sees io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error in logs, and the Nightscout site goes down. Reinstalling NSClient and manually entering credentials allows syncing but eventually crashes the NS site again; data appears in history viewer but not on the main graph.", "cause": "The thread speculates that the NS API is overwhelmed by NSClient's sync/upload load, possibly because the free Heroku dyno cannot keep up; developer MilosKozak added an option to slow down NS upload, implying upload rate is a factor.", "fix": "Users report downgrading to NSClient 2.8 resolves the issue; developer added an option to slow down NS upload (commit ae399f0bf5b40d81905dac979aba1153baede364).", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["S20"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nsclient", "nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "i added option to slow down NS upload", "text": "[AAPS3.0_beta2] NSClient - io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error - Seems to have also broken Nightscout After installing NSClient 3.0 beta2, the user sees io.socket.engineio.client.EngineIOException:xhr poll error in logs, and the Nightscout site goes down. Reinstalling NSClient and manually entering credentials allows syncing but eventually crashes the NS site again; data appears in history viewer but not on the main graph. The thread speculates that the NS API is overwhelmed by NSClient's sync/upload load, possibly because the free Heroku dyno cannot keep up; developer MilosKozak added an option to slow down NS upload, implying upload rate is a factor. Users report downgrading to NSClient 2.8 resolves the issue; developer added an option to slow down NS upload (commit ae399f0bf5b40d81905dac979aba1153baede364). S20 nsclient nightscout i added option to slow down NS upload"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-808", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 808, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 808, "title": "[AAPS3.0_beta3] NSClient - Cant select local Profile, and can't download NS Profile (was beta2)", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/808", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/808", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In AAPS 3.0 beta3, the user cannot select a local profile and cannot download a Nightscout profile. Even after creating a manual local profile and activating it, NSClient still says 'NO PROFILE SET' and no data appears on the plot.", "cause": "In v3.0 only local profiles are allowed; using NS profiles directly is not permitted. Also, MAX DIA is limited to 7 hours, so a DIA greater than 7 prevents profile selection.", "fix": "Change DIA to 7 or less to allow selection. Download NS profiles into local profiles and sync them, but use only local profiles. The button text issue was fixed by commit 3a33529307da30810ae273123cda12cb0f1743f6.", "settings_changed": ["DIA → 7"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClient", "Nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "In v3.0 only local profiles are allowed. You can download NS profiles into your local profiles and sync them, but using is only allowed for local profiles. Perhaps that's the problem ?", "text": "[AAPS3.0_beta3] NSClient - Cant select local Profile, and can't download NS Profile (was beta2) In AAPS 3.0 beta3, the user cannot select a local profile and cannot download a Nightscout profile. Even after creating a manual local profile and activating it, NSClient still says 'NO PROFILE SET' and no data appears on the plot. In v3.0 only local profiles are allowed; using NS profiles directly is not permitted. Also, MAX DIA is limited to 7 hours, so a DIA greater than 7 prevents profile selection. Change DIA to 7 or less to allow selection. Download NS profiles into local profiles and sync them, but use only local profiles. The button text issue was fixed by commit 3a33529307da30810ae273123cda12cb0f1743f6.  NSClient Nightscout In v3.0 only local profiles are allowed. You can download NS profiles into your local profiles and sync them, but using is only allowed for local profiles. Perhaps that's the problem ?"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-827", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 827, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 827, "title": "2.8.2.9_dev EROS and DASH / Basal settings sent twice to pump", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/827", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/827", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When changing a temporary basal profile (e.g., to 120% or back to 100%), the basal settings are sometimes sent twice to the Omnipod EROS or DASH pump, resulting in duplicate 'Basal profile set in the pump' notifications and duplicate entries in the pump history. This occurs with both manual and automation profile changes, and is not systematic.", "cause": "The issue is related to Nightscout (NS) synchronization. When NSClient is enabled (not paused), the basal profile change is sent twice to the pump. When NSClient is paused, the duplicate send does not occur.", "fix": "The issue was fixed by a commit referenced in the thread: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f48dcc77e23d499ab0c1af8499ce9ce8ed574ba1. No specific user action is given as a workaround.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["EROS", "DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NSClient", "Nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "It is related to NS. In AAPS, I pause NS, I change back and forth a couple of times the profile between 100% and 120%. There are no double sends to the pod. As soon as I unpause NS in AAPS, basal is sent once more to the pod.", "text": "2.8.2.9_dev EROS and DASH / Basal settings sent twice to pump When changing a temporary basal profile (e.g., to 120% or back to 100%), the basal settings are sometimes sent twice to the Omnipod EROS or DASH pump, resulting in duplicate 'Basal profile set in the pump' notifications and duplicate entries in the pump history. This occurs with both manual and automation profile changes, and is not systematic. The issue is related to Nightscout (NS) synchronization. When NSClient is enabled (not paused), the basal profile change is sent twice to the pump. When NSClient is paused, the duplicate send does not occur. The issue was fixed by a commit referenced in the thread: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f48dcc77e23d499ab0c1af8499ce9ce8ed574ba1. No specific user action is given as a workaround. EROS DASH NSClient Nightscout It is related to NS. In AAPS, I pause NS, I change back and forth a couple of times the profile between 100% and 120%. There are no double sends to the pod. As soon as I unpause NS in AAPS, basal is sent once more to the pod."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-830", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 830, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 830, "title": "[2.8.2] AndroidAPS forgets it just bolussed/issues double bolus", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/830", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/830", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "AndroidAPS sometimes forgets it just bolussed (SMB) and also sometimes issues a double bolus (SMB) within a minute. When re-reading pump history, AndroidAPS doesn't know those boluses were SMBs but thinks the user entered them on the pump. The issue has occurred multiple times and is not reproducible.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A maintainer (andyrozman) suggests that the driver thinks SMB is Corr after history is read, which will be fixed with issue #798, and that the double bolus might be due to the first bolus needing longer to be issued (pump communication). Later, MilosKozak notes that 2.8.2 code is outdated and suggests testing 3.0.", "fix": "No definitive fix is stated. The thread suggests that the SMB-as-Corr issue will be fixed with issue #798, and MilosKozak recommends testing 3.0 because 2.8.2 code is mostly rewritten. The issue is closed for inactivity.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic 554/523", "RileyLink", "Dexcom G6", "Combo"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["Medtronic", "Combo", "xdrip"], "evidence_quote": "That driver thinks SMB is Corr (after history is read) will be fixed with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/798, we can look at double bolus issue then... But this is really weird... Unless we receive 2 boluses we wouldn't issue 2 of them, but what might happen is that first bolus needs longer to be issued (pump communication)...", "text": "[2.8.2] AndroidAPS forgets it just bolussed/issues double bolus AndroidAPS sometimes forgets it just bolussed (SMB) and also sometimes issues a double bolus (SMB) within a minute. When re-reading pump history, AndroidAPS doesn't know those boluses were SMBs but thinks the user entered them on the pump. The issue has occurred multiple times and is not reproducible. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A maintainer (andyrozman) suggests that the driver thinks SMB is Corr after history is read, which will be fixed with issue #798, and that the double bolus might be due to the first bolus needing longer to be issued (pump communication). Later, MilosKozak notes that 2.8.2 code is outdated and suggests testing 3.0. No definitive fix is stated. The thread suggests that the SMB-as-Corr issue will be fixed with issue #798, and MilosKozak recommends testing 3.0 because 2.8.2 code is mostly rewritten. The issue is closed for inactivity. Medtronic 554/523 RileyLink Dexcom G6 Combo Android 11 Medtronic Combo xdrip That driver thinks SMB is Corr (after history is read) will be fixed with https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/798, we can look at double bolus issue then... But this is really weird... Unless we receive 2 boluses we wouldn't issue 2 of them, but what might happen is that first bolus needs longer to be issued (pump communication)..."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-854", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 854, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 854, "title": "DASH : Not urgent / Text correction while injection", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/854", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/854", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "During Omnipod (EROS and DASH) injection, the injection window shows a text that incorrectly states the total amount has been injected while the injection is still in progress. The text is misleading and not informative.", "cause": "The French translation of the text is incorrect; the English text is correct. The issue is a translation problem, not a code issue.", "fix": "The fix is to correct the French translation in Crowdin. The text string is identified as 'bolusdelivering' and is used by other pumps to show updated amount during injection, so a new string will be created for the correct context.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod EROS", "Omnipod DASH"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Omnipod"], "evidence_quote": "Yes, the text in English is correct, the translation in French is not. I think the fix should be implemented in Crowdin.", "text": "DASH : Not urgent / Text correction while injection During Omnipod (EROS and DASH) injection, the injection window shows a text that incorrectly states the total amount has been injected while the injection is still in progress. The text is misleading and not informative. The French translation of the text is incorrect; the English text is correct. The issue is a translation problem, not a code issue. The fix is to correct the French translation in Crowdin. The text string is identified as 'bolusdelivering' and is used by other pumps to show updated amount during injection, so a new string will be created for the correct context. Omnipod EROS Omnipod DASH Omnipod Yes, the text in English is correct, the translation in French is not. I think the fix should be implemented in Crowdin."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-862", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 862, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 862, "title": "Dana I not showing TDD", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/862", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/862", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Using Dana I pump with AndroidAPS Beta3 ver 4 and previously ver3, the TDD (Total Daily Dose) is not totaling the units. It only shows data for days that AAPS has data for, not loading older data from the pump.", "cause": "The pump history records before the pump was set up in AAPS are ignored. Only data from setting up the pump in AAPS is accepted.", "fix": "The issue is that only data from setting up the pump in AAPS is accepted; older data is not taken into account. The user was informed that it works as intended after understanding this.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana I", "DanaRS v3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Dana I", "DanaRS"], "evidence_quote": "only data from settin up pump in AAPS is accepted", "text": "Dana I not showing TDD Using Dana I pump with AndroidAPS Beta3 ver 4 and previously ver3, the TDD (Total Daily Dose) is not totaling the units. It only shows data for days that AAPS has data for, not loading older data from the pump. The pump history records before the pump was set up in AAPS are ignored. Only data from setting up the pump in AAPS is accepted. The issue is that only data from setting up the pump in AAPS is accepted; older data is not taken into account. The user was informed that it works as intended after understanding this. Dana I DanaRS v3 Dana I DanaRS only data from settin up pump in AAPS is accepted"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-890", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 890, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 890, "title": "[3.0 beta5] Issue with TBR value -Dash", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/890", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/890", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When there is no overwritten TBR and basal rate is according to profile, the Overview screen shows TBR 0U/H and it is not possible to use CANCEL TBR in ACTIONS tab. In Dash Tab there is no value in TBR, and in Nightscout basal rate is visible as normal rate according to profile settings. When TBR is different it works and can be cancelled, but cancellation leads to TBR 0 U/H, not possible to set own TBR value.", "cause": "A buggy TBR was set sometime in the last 3 days, likely from an SMS command, and it persists for ~3 days. The issue is related to switching between Dash and Eros pumps after activating a pod.", "fix": "Wait for the 'bad' TBR to expire (~3 days). The issue was fixed with commit 85178ee19ff628dfe4422409973c6f8ae7b511b5.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Omnipod Dash", "Eros"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Dash", "Eros"], "evidence_quote": "Should be fixed with: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/85178ee19ff628dfe4422409973c6f8ae7b511b5", "text": "[3.0 beta5] Issue with TBR value -Dash When there is no overwritten TBR and basal rate is according to profile, the Overview screen shows TBR 0U/H and it is not possible to use CANCEL TBR in ACTIONS tab. In Dash Tab there is no value in TBR, and in Nightscout basal rate is visible as normal rate according to profile settings. When TBR is different it works and can be cancelled, but cancellation leads to TBR 0 U/H, not possible to set own TBR value. A buggy TBR was set sometime in the last 3 days, likely from an SMS command, and it persists for ~3 days. The issue is related to switching between Dash and Eros pumps after activating a pod. Wait for the 'bad' TBR to expire (~3 days). The issue was fixed with commit 85178ee19ff628dfe4422409973c6f8ae7b511b5. Omnipod Dash Eros Dash Eros Should be fixed with: https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/85178ee19ff628dfe4422409973c6f8ae7b511b5"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-897", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 897, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 897, "title": "(3.0beta5) Frozen screen/app crashes/update basal profile error", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/897", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/897", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Screen freezes sometimes when switching profile, app crashes with 'wait or close' message, connection with Combo pump appears slower, and 'Update of basal profile failed' error occurs at night or during the day.", "cause": "The root cause is not definitively identified. Suspicions include a possible ringbuffer overrun inside the Combo pump, or an issue triggered by Android 12, but no conclusive cause was established.", "fix": "No definitive fix was found. User tried increasing sleep period in SetBasalProfileCommand from 50 to 200/250, resetting Bluetooth/WiFi/mobile, and reinstalling AAPS and Ruffy, but without success. Switching to a different phone (Samsung S21 Ultra with Android 11) resolved the freezes but basal profile update errors persisted.", "settings_changed": ["sleep period in SetBasalProfileCommand → 200", "sleep period in SetBasalProfileCommand → 250"], "devices": ["Combo", "Dexcom G6", "Google Pixel 4XL", "Samsung S21 Ultra"], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["Ruffy", "Combo", "Build your own app"], "evidence_quote": "I have done this change to 200 several days ago and build a new apk. I don't see any changes :(. Or do I something wrong? I have also tried 250.", "text": "(3.0beta5) Frozen screen/app crashes/update basal profile error Screen freezes sometimes when switching profile, app crashes with 'wait or close' message, connection with Combo pump appears slower, and 'Update of basal profile failed' error occurs at night or during the day. The root cause is not definitively identified. Suspicions include a possible ringbuffer overrun inside the Combo pump, or an issue triggered by Android 12, but no conclusive cause was established. No definitive fix was found. User tried increasing sleep period in SetBasalProfileCommand from 50 to 200/250, resetting Bluetooth/WiFi/mobile, and reinstalling AAPS and Ruffy, but without success. Switching to a different phone (Samsung S21 Ultra with Android 11) resolved the freezes but basal profile update errors persisted. Combo Dexcom G6 Google Pixel 4XL Samsung S21 Ultra Android 12 Android 11 Ruffy Combo Build your own app I have done this change to 200 several days ago and build a new apk. I don't see any changes :(. Or do I something wrong? I have also tried 250."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-9", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 9, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 9, "title": "[2.7] no \"import settings\" possible because of small display size and no scrolling possible", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/9", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/9", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "On a Jelly Pro phone with small display, the import settings dialog cannot be scrolled, so the user cannot click 'OK' or 'import'. Also, the Confirm button in Objective 3 is only accessible in landscape mode.", "cause": "The summary dialog in PrefImportSummaryDialog.kt does not allow scrolling on ultra-small screens.", "fix": "The fix was implemented by osodebailar in pull request #15, which introduced new layout files for small-height and landscape devices with a fixed and scrollable table. The user can also workaround by commenting out lines 46 and 79 in PrefImportSummaryDialog.kt to hide the summary table.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Jelly Pro", "Unihertz Atom"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "It is obviously error with summary dialog, which does not allow scrolling on ultra-small screens. I will fix that. In the meantime - hack mentioned above will allow to import prefs.", "text": "[2.7] no \"import settings\" possible because of small display size and no scrolling possible On a Jelly Pro phone with small display, the import settings dialog cannot be scrolled, so the user cannot click 'OK' or 'import'. Also, the Confirm button in Objective 3 is only accessible in landscape mode. The summary dialog in PrefImportSummaryDialog.kt does not allow scrolling on ultra-small screens. The fix was implemented by osodebailar in pull request #15, which introduced new layout files for small-height and landscape devices with a fixed and scrollable table. The user can also workaround by commenting out lines 46 and 79 in PrefImportSummaryDialog.kt to hide the summary table. Jelly Pro Unihertz Atom  It is obviously error with summary dialog, which does not allow scrolling on ultra-small screens. I will fix that. In the meantime - hack mentioned above will allow to import prefs."}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-919", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 919, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 919, "title": "Dana wrong password", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/919", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/919", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating to version 2.8.2.1 and importing settings from 2.6.2, the user gets an error that the pump password is incorrect and cannot make a bolus. The pump is connected and password is correct, and reverting to 2.6.2 works.", "cause": "In version 2.6.2, the password was not verified for RS v1 pump, but in 2.8.2 it is. The user has an old Dana Diabecare pump (Dana R from 2013) with old firmware that cannot change the default password using code 3463, so the password verification fails.", "fix": "The thread suggests that the user may need to upgrade the pump firmware to v2 to be able to change the pump password using code 3463, or find the password from log files. The user contacted the producer and confirmed password change is not possible on their pump.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dana Diabecare", "Dana R"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["DanaR"], "evidence_quote": "in 2.6.2 password was not verified for RS v1 pump. In 2.8.2 it is", "text": "Dana wrong password After updating to version 2.8.2.1 and importing settings from 2.6.2, the user gets an error that the pump password is incorrect and cannot make a bolus. The pump is connected and password is correct, and reverting to 2.6.2 works. In version 2.6.2, the password was not verified for RS v1 pump, but in 2.8.2 it is. The user has an old Dana Diabecare pump (Dana R from 2013) with old firmware that cannot change the default password using code 3463, so the password verification fails. The thread suggests that the user may need to upgrade the pump firmware to v2 to be able to change the pump password using code 3463, or find the password from log files. The user contacted the producer and confirmed password change is not possible on their pump. Dana Diabecare Dana R Android 11 DanaR in 2.6.2 password was not verified for RS v1 pump. In 2.8.2 it is"}, {"id": "distilled:androidaps-951", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 951, "repo": "nightscout/AndroidAPS", "number": 951, "title": "[3.0-beta6] SMB are converted to meal bolus on app restart", "html_url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/951", "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/issues/951", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When restarting AAPS, all past SMB are converted to meal bolus in the graph. This happens after the pump history is read from the Combo.", "cause": "The issue was specific to the Combo pump driver, where reading pump history on app start caused SMB to be converted to meal bolus.", "fix": "Fixed by commit f5faa3492288b97b49284e116c29720f50194560.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Combo", "xDrip+/G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Combo", "xDrip+", "local broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "it was combo specific issue. fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f5faa3492288b97b49284e116c29720f50194560", "text": "[3.0-beta6] SMB are converted to meal bolus on app restart When restarting AAPS, all past SMB are converted to meal bolus in the graph. This happens after the pump history is read from the Combo. The issue was specific to the Combo pump driver, where reading pump history on app start caused SMB to be converted to meal bolus. Fixed by commit f5faa3492288b97b49284e116c29720f50194560. Combo xDrip+/G6 Combo xDrip+ local broadcast it was combo specific issue. fixed by https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/commit/f5faa3492288b97b49284e116c29720f50194560"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1000", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1000, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1000, "title": "Xdrip With Miao Miao 2", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1000", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1000", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Users ask if Miao Miao 2 works with xDrip using Libre 1. Later reports say the Miao Miao 2 connects in xDrip but no readings are received; the event log shows 'Got null pointer trying to set CCCD descriptor'.", "cause": "Older xDrip versions had a bug triggering 'Got null pointer trying to set CCCD descriptor' when connecting to Miao Miao 2, which prevented glucose readings.", "fix": "Update to the latest xDrip version for Miao Miao 2 support (for example the 2019.11.22 release linked by the maintainer); a special test build was also reported to fix the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Miao Miao 2", "Libre 1", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["android 10"], "driver_tags": ["libre bluetooth", "tomato app", "oop", "nightscout", "patched app"], "evidence_quote": "Please update to latest xdrip version for the work with MM2.", "text": "Xdrip With Miao Miao 2 Users ask if Miao Miao 2 works with xDrip using Libre 1. Later reports say the Miao Miao 2 connects in xDrip but no readings are received; the event log shows 'Got null pointer trying to set CCCD descriptor'. Older xDrip versions had a bug triggering 'Got null pointer trying to set CCCD descriptor' when connecting to Miao Miao 2, which prevented glucose readings. Update to the latest xDrip version for Miao Miao 2 support (for example the 2019.11.22 release linked by the maintainer); a special test build was also reported to fix the issue. Miao Miao 2 Libre 1 Libre 2 android 10 libre bluetooth tomato app oop nightscout patched app Please update to latest xdrip version for the work with MM2."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1007", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1007, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1007, "title": "Amazfit GTR", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1007", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1007", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users request Amazfit GTR syncing with xDrip so glucose/BG values can appear on the watch; activating the Amazfit Service does not show anything on the watch, and no official GTR watchface/plugin is available.", "cause": "No Amazfit GTR plugin/support has been implemented in the NightscoutFoundation xDrip repo; only Amazfit Pace/Stratos were compatible for graph watchfaces at the time, and the GTR/GTS line is otherwise unsupported.", "fix": "A user-reported workaround was to pair the GTR through xDrip's Mi Band menu by entering the watch's Bluetooth MAC, restarting the watch, and then installing a custom GTR watchface (built from external instructions/tools, e.g. Artem/bigdigital's xDrip-miband and Patreon posts) to receive BG notifications. The GTR 42 also requires a 42mm watchface.", "settings_changed": ["Amazfit Service → activated"], "devices": ["Amazfit GTR"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["miband", "amazfit service", "watchface"], "evidence_quote": "I got connection GTR and xdrip via miband menu. Put MAC of my GTR and restarted watch.", "text": "Amazfit GTR Users request Amazfit GTR syncing with xDrip so glucose/BG values can appear on the watch; activating the Amazfit Service does not show anything on the watch, and no official GTR watchface/plugin is available. No Amazfit GTR plugin/support has been implemented in the NightscoutFoundation xDrip repo; only Amazfit Pace/Stratos were compatible for graph watchfaces at the time, and the GTR/GTS line is otherwise unsupported. A user-reported workaround was to pair the GTR through xDrip's Mi Band menu by entering the watch's Bluetooth MAC, restarting the watch, and then installing a custom GTR watchface (built from external instructions/tools, e.g. Artem/bigdigital's xDrip-miband and Patreon posts) to receive BG notifications. The GTR 42 also requires a 42mm watchface. Amazfit GTR miband amazfit service watchface I got connection GTR and xdrip via miband menu. Put MAC of my GTR and restarted watch."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1012", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1012, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1012, "title": "Project doesn't build", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1012", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1012", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The project fails to build with Android Studio 3.5, with errors in wear dependencies and manifest merger failures. Users report various build errors and difficulty getting the project to compile.", "cause": "The build failures are due to regressions introduced by Android Studio and poor stewardship of the maven repositories by Google, as stated by jamorham. Specific issues include missing wearable dependencies and manifest merger conflicts.", "fix": "Workarounds include using Android Studio 3.4.1, uninstalling and cleaning Android Studio caches, and manually editing build files. wkochFPV provided specific steps: uncheck 'Only sync the active variant' in settings, add a meta-data element with tools:replace to the wear manifest, and change the google-services classpath to 3.2.0. Later, the project builds with current versions after merging PR #1160.", "settings_changed": ["Only sync the active variant → unchecked", "google-services classpath → 'com.google.gms:google-services:3.2.0'"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "With these changes, the apk builds without errors.", "text": "Project doesn't build The project fails to build with Android Studio 3.5, with errors in wear dependencies and manifest merger failures. Users report various build errors and difficulty getting the project to compile. The build failures are due to regressions introduced by Android Studio and poor stewardship of the maven repositories by Google, as stated by jamorham. Specific issues include missing wearable dependencies and manifest merger conflicts. Workarounds include using Android Studio 3.4.1, uninstalling and cleaning Android Studio caches, and manually editing build files. wkochFPV provided specific steps: uncheck 'Only sync the active variant' in settings, add a meta-data element with tools:replace to the wear manifest, and change the google-services classpath to 3.2.0. Later, the project builds with current versions after merging PR #1160.   With these changes, the apk builds without errors."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1020", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1020, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1020, "title": "Libre OOP algorithm no data / missed signal", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1020", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1020", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When using the out of process Libre algorithm, xDrip+ stops showing new data and shows a signal missed message. Deselecting the algorithm makes it work again.", "cause": "The issue was not definitively resolved; the user initially had trouble installing the OOP algorithm APK, but after installing it correctly it worked. Later, after changing sensors, readings differed from the Libre reader, but no root cause was established.", "fix": "The user resolved the initial problem by installing the OOP algorithm APK correctly (with Android Studio on the computer). Later, after sensor change, the issue persisted and no fix was confirmed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 14 day sensor", "MiaoMiao 2", "Samsung Note 9", "Libre 1"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["out of process Libre algorithm", "OOP algorithm", "libreoop"], "evidence_quote": "Thank you for your help, it's working as it should now. Readings are the same as libre and updates just as regularly.", "text": "Libre OOP algorithm no data / missed signal When using the out of process Libre algorithm, xDrip+ stops showing new data and shows a signal missed message. Deselecting the algorithm makes it work again. The issue was not definitively resolved; the user initially had trouble installing the OOP algorithm APK, but after installing it correctly it worked. Later, after changing sensors, readings differed from the Libre reader, but no root cause was established. The user resolved the initial problem by installing the OOP algorithm APK correctly (with Android Studio on the computer). Later, after sensor change, the issue persisted and no fix was confirmed. Libre 14 day sensor MiaoMiao 2 Samsung Note 9 Libre 1 out of process Libre algorithm OOP algorithm libreoop Thank you for your help, it's working as it should now. Readings are the same as libre and updates just as regularly."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1033", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1033, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1033, "title": "Xdrip+ cant connect with Limitter. Android 9.0", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1033", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1033", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After updating to Android 9.0 on LG G6, xDrip+ cannot connect to LimiTTer collector, stuck at receiving data. Other users report similar issues with MiaoMiao.", "cause": null, "fix": "Performing a factory reset of the phone resolved the issue for one user, though it chose Tomato instead of LimiTTer. A maintainer suggested trying 'Use Scanning' and 'Trust Auto-Connect' advanced bluetooth settings and ensuring latest nightly version.", "settings_changed": ["Use Scanning", "Trust Auto-Connect"], "devices": ["LimiTTer", "MiaoMiao"], "android_versions": ["Android 9.0"], "driver_tags": ["LimiTTer collector", "MiaoMiao"], "evidence_quote": "I've just performed a factory reset and it looks like it did the trick, though it chose Tomato as the, instead of LimiTTer. This is on the latest nightly version.", "text": "Xdrip+ cant connect with Limitter. Android 9.0 After updating to Android 9.0 on LG G6, xDrip+ cannot connect to LimiTTer collector, stuck at receiving data. Other users report similar issues with MiaoMiao.  Performing a factory reset of the phone resolved the issue for one user, though it chose Tomato instead of LimiTTer. A maintainer suggested trying 'Use Scanning' and 'Trust Auto-Connect' advanced bluetooth settings and ensuring latest nightly version. LimiTTer MiaoMiao Android 9.0 LimiTTer collector MiaoMiao I've just performed a factory reset and it looks like it did the trick, though it chose Tomato as the, instead of LimiTTer. This is on the latest nightly version."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1035", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1035, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1035, "title": "Nightscout URL should support tokens", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1035", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1035", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip supports Nightscout uploading and following using a URL of the form https://API_SECRET@my.nightscout.place/api/v1, where the username is used as the auth token. The API_SECRET is too secret and hard to revoke, so the user attempted to use a token as the username instead, but it was rejected by cgm-remote-monitor. The user requests that URLs support token access.", "cause": "The thread does not identify a single root cause. It suggests that Nightscout's cgm-remote-monitor rejected the token when used as a username in the URL, and that HTTP basic auth is not supported. Later, a user found that setting the environment variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\" allowed token-based access.", "fix": "The thread reports that setting the Nightscout environment variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\" allows token-based access. Additionally, a user confirmed that using a custom Access Token (created from the Admin Tools menu) before the @ symbol in the REST API URL works in xDrip+.", "settings_changed": ["AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES → denied"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout", "token", "api secret"], "evidence_quote": "Ha, found a solution by surprise: I have to set the env var AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\". I really went through the possible vars but just didn't recognize it. My bad.", "text": "Nightscout URL should support tokens xDrip supports Nightscout uploading and following using a URL of the form https://API_SECRET@my.nightscout.place/api/v1, where the username is used as the auth token. The API_SECRET is too secret and hard to revoke, so the user attempted to use a token as the username instead, but it was rejected by cgm-remote-monitor. The user requests that URLs support token access. The thread does not identify a single root cause. It suggests that Nightscout's cgm-remote-monitor rejected the token when used as a username in the URL, and that HTTP basic auth is not supported. Later, a user found that setting the environment variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\" allowed token-based access. The thread reports that setting the Nightscout environment variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\" allows token-based access. Additionally, a user confirmed that using a custom Access Token (created from the Admin Tools menu) before the @ symbol in the REST API URL works in xDrip+.  nightscout token api secret Ha, found a solution by surprise: I have to set the env var AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES to \"denied\". I really went through the possible vars but just didn't recognize it. My bad."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1045", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1045, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1045, "title": "Database Import should not overwrite existing data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1045", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1045", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When importing an old database into xDrip+ on a new phone, the existing data is overwritten, causing loss of new values. Also, after import, the calibration for a running Dexcom G6 sensor is lost, forcing recalibration with blood.", "cause": "The current procedure is a complete restore of a backup database, which overwrites all existing data. The menu item is incorrectly named 'Import database' when it actually performs a restore.", "fix": "The menu item was renamed from 'Import' to 'Restore' to clarify behavior. There is no capability to import without overwriting; users should transfer the database before setting up the new phone as a collector. For Android 11 issues, refer to issue #1705.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Libre", "MiaoMiao 1"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 8.1", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth bridge", "cloud backup"], "evidence_quote": "We have renamed the menu item from \"Import\" to \"Restore\" to avoid this confusion. There is currently no capability to import a database leaving the existing database intact.", "text": "Database Import should not overwrite existing data When importing an old database into xDrip+ on a new phone, the existing data is overwritten, causing loss of new values. Also, after import, the calibration for a running Dexcom G6 sensor is lost, forcing recalibration with blood. The current procedure is a complete restore of a backup database, which overwrites all existing data. The menu item is incorrectly named 'Import database' when it actually performs a restore. The menu item was renamed from 'Import' to 'Restore' to clarify behavior. There is no capability to import without overwriting; users should transfer the database before setting up the new phone as a collector. For Android 11 issues, refer to issue #1705. Dexcom G6 Libre MiaoMiao 1 Android 11 Android 8.1 Android 12 Bluetooth bridge cloud backup We have renamed the menu item from \"Import\" to \"Restore\" to avoid this confusion. There is currently no capability to import a database leaving the existing database intact."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1048", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1048, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1048, "title": "Latest TicWatch Pro does not work reliably, as a Standalone Collector", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1048", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1048", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "TicWatch Pro does not work reliably as a standalone collector. It stays running in standalone mode for between 2 to 12 hours at best, then stops collecting, always losing connection overnight. Restarting the collector on the watch resumes it temporarily.", "cause": "The main problem seems to be that the TicWatch is handled/recognized as a Bluetooth headset.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["TicWatch Pro", "TicWatch Pro 3", "TicWatch Pro 3 GPS", "TicWatch E2", "Fossil Gen4", "Fossil Sport", "Miaomiao", "Miaomiao 2", "Libre sensor 14 day UK version", "Libre 2", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android OS version 9"], "driver_tags": ["standalone collector", "wear collection", "force wear collection", "Bluetooth", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "The main problem seem to be that the TicWatch is handled/recognized as a Bluetooth headset.", "text": "Latest TicWatch Pro does not work reliably, as a Standalone Collector TicWatch Pro does not work reliably as a standalone collector. It stays running in standalone mode for between 2 to 12 hours at best, then stops collecting, always losing connection overnight. Restarting the collector on the watch resumes it temporarily. The main problem seems to be that the TicWatch is handled/recognized as a Bluetooth headset.  TicWatch Pro TicWatch Pro 3 TicWatch Pro 3 GPS TicWatch E2 Fossil Gen4 Fossil Sport Miaomiao Miaomiao 2 Libre sensor 14 day UK version Libre 2 Dexcom G6 Android OS version 9 standalone collector wear collection force wear collection Bluetooth collector The main problem seem to be that the TicWatch is handled/recognized as a Bluetooth headset."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1056", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1056, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1056, "title": "xdrip shows no data from libre2 Patch", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1056", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1056", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After installing the patched Libre2 app and the newest xDrip on an S8 with Android 9, no BG values appear in xDrip. The user chose 'libre patched app' as data source, files and location permissions are ON for the LibreApp, and all alarms are on in the LibreApp, but no data is received.", "cause": "The issue was resolved by deleting the Bluetooth file, as suggested in a linked ticket. Additionally, for some users, the problem was caused by the phone being on silent mode, which prevented the Libre2 app from setting alarms, and switching to vibration mode fixed it.", "fix": "Delete the Bluetooth file (as per the linked ticket) to resolve the issue. For others, ensure the phone is not on silent mode; set it to vibration or sound to allow the Libre2 app to set alarms.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre2"], "android_versions": ["Android 9", "Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["patched app", "Libre2 (patched App)"], "evidence_quote": "@k2s: bluetooth file delete solved the problem!!!!!", "text": "xdrip shows no data from libre2 Patch After installing the patched Libre2 app and the newest xDrip on an S8 with Android 9, no BG values appear in xDrip. The user chose 'libre patched app' as data source, files and location permissions are ON for the LibreApp, and all alarms are on in the LibreApp, but no data is received. The issue was resolved by deleting the Bluetooth file, as suggested in a linked ticket. Additionally, for some users, the problem was caused by the phone being on silent mode, which prevented the Libre2 app from setting alarms, and switching to vibration mode fixed it. Delete the Bluetooth file (as per the linked ticket) to resolve the issue. For others, ensure the phone is not on silent mode; set it to vibration or sound to allow the Libre2 app to set alarms. Libre2 Android 9 Android 10 patched app Libre2 (patched App) @k2s: bluetooth file delete solved the problem!!!!!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1057", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1057, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1057, "title": "ANdroid Auto", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1057", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1057", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User requests Android Auto support in xDrip to hear/see blood glucose readings while driving, but xDrip readings do not appear on Android Auto display.", "cause": null, "fix": "The thread suggests using Android APS with a virtual pump to get xDrip data to Android Auto, or using the CarNotifier app to put notifications onto Android Auto.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["android auto", "android aps", "carnotifier"], "evidence_quote": "I found an app that will put the notification onto android auto, it is much better than AndroidAPS. It is CarNotifier.", "text": "ANdroid Auto User requests Android Auto support in xDrip to hear/see blood glucose readings while driving, but xDrip readings do not appear on Android Auto display.  The thread suggests using Android APS with a virtual pump to get xDrip data to Android Auto, or using the CarNotifier app to put notifications onto Android Auto.  android auto android aps carnotifier I found an app that will put the notification onto android auto, it is much better than AndroidAPS. It is CarNotifier."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1058", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1058, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1058, "title": "Broadcast data to Xdrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1058", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1058", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A CGM company (POCTech) wants to send glucose data from their app (POCTech Care Mobile) to xDrip via broadcast intents, similar to how they send data to AndroidAPS. They ask how to do it and request guidance on compliant coding parameters.", "cause": null, "fix": "tzachi-dar provided instructions: send data via intents similar to LibreOOPAlgorithm's IntentsReceiver, and configure xDrip with specific steps: install xDrip, choose Libre as sensor type, choose Miaomiao, go to settings->hw data source and choose Libre wifi, go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000, start a new sensor (answer not today), go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set 'use oop algorithm'.", "settings_changed": ["sensor type → Libre", "hw data source → Libre wifi", "list of receivers → 127.0.0.1:5000", "use oop algorithm → ON"], "devices": ["POCTech Care Mobile"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["broadcast", "intents", "Libre wifi", "oop algorithm"], "evidence_quote": "For this to work, your users will have to configure xDrip according to the following instructions: 1) Install xDrip 2) Choose libre as the sensor type. 3) Choose miaomiao 4) Go to settings->hw data source and choose libre wifi 5) Go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000 6) Start a new sensor (answer not today). 7) Go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set \"use oop algorithm\"", "text": "Broadcast data to Xdrip A CGM company (POCTech) wants to send glucose data from their app (POCTech Care Mobile) to xDrip via broadcast intents, similar to how they send data to AndroidAPS. They ask how to do it and request guidance on compliant coding parameters.  tzachi-dar provided instructions: send data via intents similar to LibreOOPAlgorithm's IntentsReceiver, and configure xDrip with specific steps: install xDrip, choose Libre as sensor type, choose Miaomiao, go to settings->hw data source and choose Libre wifi, go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000, start a new sensor (answer not today), go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set 'use oop algorithm'. POCTech Care Mobile broadcast intents Libre wifi oop algorithm For this to work, your users will have to configure xDrip according to the following instructions: 1) Install xDrip 2) Choose libre as the sensor type. 3) Choose miaomiao 4) Go to settings->hw data source and choose libre wifi 5) Go to list of receivers and enter 127.0.0.1:5000 6) Start a new sensor (answer not today). 7) Go to settings->less common settings->other misc options-> and set \"use oop algorithm\""}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-106", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 106, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 106, "title": "uploader Battery Stuck on latest release", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/106", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/106", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The battery status got stuck at 2% on the Sony Z3C used as an uploader after updating to version 1704030800. Deleting documents, restarting Azure, and rebooting the phone had no effect, and the issue disappeared after rolling back to version 1701201513.", "cause": "The xDripKit bridge/wixel device was reporting a bogus/stuck 2-3% battery value, and this bridge battery reading was uploaded to Nightscout and shown in the battery pill, so the correct Sony uploader battery percentage was not displayed.", "fix": "Update to the 25 April Nightly and uncheck 'Upload bridge battery' under Cloud Upload -> API Upload -> Extra Options to stop uploading the broken bridge battery to Nightscout. Optionally set DEVICESTATUS_ADVANCED=true in Nightscout environment variables to see the individual battery values on hover. The user confirmed unchecking the option resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["DEVICESTATUS_ADVANCED → true", "Upload bridge battery → unchecked"], "devices": ["Sony Z3C", "Dexcom G4", "wixel"], "android_versions": ["android 6.0.1"], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "wixel", "xbridge", "nightscout", "bridge battery", "api upload"], "evidence_quote": "Okay, so the 25th April Nightly contains a new option within `Cloud Upload` -> `API Upload` -> `Extra Options` which is a checkbox for `Upload bridge battery` which you can uncheck if your bridge battery sensor is broken and this should stop it being uploaded to Nightscout.", "text": "uploader Battery Stuck on latest release The battery status got stuck at 2% on the Sony Z3C used as an uploader after updating to version 1704030800. Deleting documents, restarting Azure, and rebooting the phone had no effect, and the issue disappeared after rolling back to version 1701201513. The xDripKit bridge/wixel device was reporting a bogus/stuck 2-3% battery value, and this bridge battery reading was uploaded to Nightscout and shown in the battery pill, so the correct Sony uploader battery percentage was not displayed. Update to the 25 April Nightly and uncheck 'Upload bridge battery' under Cloud Upload -> API Upload -> Extra Options to stop uploading the broken bridge battery to Nightscout. Optionally set DEVICESTATUS_ADVANCED=true in Nightscout environment variables to see the individual battery values on hover. The user confirmed unchecking the option resolved the issue. Sony Z3C Dexcom G4 wixel android 6.0.1 xdrip wixel xbridge nightscout bridge battery api upload Okay, so the 25th April Nightly contains a new option within `Cloud Upload` -> `API Upload` -> `Extra Options` which is a checkbox for `Upload bridge battery` which you can uncheck if your bridge battery sensor is broken and this should stop it being uploaded to Nightscout."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1069", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1069, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1069, "title": "Dexcom G6 issues with Android 10 Pixel 4", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1069", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1069", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user tried to run the setup wizard on the Dexcom G6 and had issues connecting. After disabling Trust Auto Connect and OB1 Collector, it bonded, but the app does not utilize the calibration code and requires manual calibrations, behaving like a G5. Another user reports the sensor keeps rejecting calibrations, and another has connection drops after a few missed readings.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user found that turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue, but another user suggests it might be a battery saving measure interfering with repeated BLE connections.", "fix": "One user confirmed that turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue. Another user found that setting Bluetooth AVRCP to version 1.3 in developer settings helped with reconnection reliability, but it is not a final solution.", "settings_changed": ["Allow Ob1 Unbonding → off", "Bluetooth AVRCP → 1.3"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Pixel 4", "Pixel 4 XL"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["OB1 Collector", "Native Mode", "Trust Auto Connect"], "evidence_quote": "Confirmed turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue for me. Xdrip works with the G6 code with no issues now.", "text": "Dexcom G6 issues with Android 10 Pixel 4 The user tried to run the setup wizard on the Dexcom G6 and had issues connecting. After disabling Trust Auto Connect and OB1 Collector, it bonded, but the app does not utilize the calibration code and requires manual calibrations, behaving like a G5. Another user reports the sensor keeps rejecting calibrations, and another has connection drops after a few missed readings. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user found that turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue, but another user suggests it might be a battery saving measure interfering with repeated BLE connections. One user confirmed that turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue. Another user found that setting Bluetooth AVRCP to version 1.3 in developer settings helped with reconnection reliability, but it is not a final solution. Dexcom G6 Pixel 4 Pixel 4 XL Android 10 OB1 Collector Native Mode Trust Auto Connect Confirmed turning off Allow Ob1 Unbonding fixed the issue for me. Xdrip works with the G6 code with no issues now."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1092", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1092, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1092, "title": "never works, various error messages: G6 SENSOR FAILED, G6 Start Failed; No signal", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1092", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1092", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The app never works reliably, showing various errors like G6 SENSOR FAILED, G6 Start Failed, No signal, and calibration rejected. The user has tried multiple troubleshooting steps, and it only worked for about a day before failing.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that some transmitters with serial starting with 81 may not work with preemptive restarts, but this is contradicted by another user. The issue remains unresolved.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix. One user suggests turning off preemptive restarts, and another suggests turning off OB1 mode and using it like a G5, but these are not confirmed. The issue was closed due to inactivity.", "settings_changed": ["preemptive restarts → off", "OB1 → off (suggested)"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Samsung Galaxy S7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native algorithm", "OB1"], "evidence_quote": "Turning off preemptive restarts fixed it for me. Try it and see if it will work. I guess some of the transmitters work with it and some do not", "text": "never works, various error messages: G6 SENSOR FAILED, G6 Start Failed; No signal The app never works reliably, showing various errors like G6 SENSOR FAILED, G6 Start Failed, No signal, and calibration rejected. The user has tried multiple troubleshooting steps, and it only worked for about a day before failing. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that some transmitters with serial starting with 81 may not work with preemptive restarts, but this is contradicted by another user. The issue remains unresolved. The thread does not state a definitive fix. One user suggests turning off preemptive restarts, and another suggests turning off OB1 mode and using it like a G5, but these are not confirmed. The issue was closed due to inactivity. Dexcom G6 Samsung Galaxy S7 native algorithm OB1 Turning off preemptive restarts fixed it for me. Try it and see if it will work. I guess some of the transmitters work with it and some do not"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-111", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 111, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 111, "title": "XDrip not backfilling data to nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/111", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/111", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "xDrip+ is uploading current blood sugar readings to Nightscout, but it has not uploaded several months of back data after about 18 hours of setup.", "cause": "xDrip+ will not load data that was not set to be uploaded when it was created.", "fix": "The latest nightly has an option to backfill data. Find it in Settings -> Cloud Upload -> API Upload -> Extra Options -> Back fill data.", "settings_changed": ["Back fill data → enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout", "uploader queue", "API Upload"], "evidence_quote": "The latest nightly has an option to backfill data. Find it in `Settings` -> `Cloud Upload` -> `API Upload` -> `Extra Options` ->`Back fill data`", "text": "XDrip not backfilling data to nightscout xDrip+ is uploading current blood sugar readings to Nightscout, but it has not uploaded several months of back data after about 18 hours of setup. xDrip+ will not load data that was not set to be uploaded when it was created. The latest nightly has an option to backfill data. Find it in Settings -> Cloud Upload -> API Upload -> Extra Options -> Back fill data.  nightscout uploader queue API Upload The latest nightly has an option to backfill data. Find it in `Settings` -> `Cloud Upload` -> `API Upload` -> `Extra Options` ->`Back fill data`"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1117", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1117, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1117, "title": "Basal Insulin in XDrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1117", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1117", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user asks if there is a way to add basal insulin (e.g., Tresiba) in xDrip, as currently only bolus insulin can be logged. They mention using xDrip with a Miaomiao 2 on a Oneplus 6.", "cause": null, "fix": "A developer suggests installing the latest nightly and enabling the 'Multiple Insulins' preference option within 'Predictive Simulation Settings', noting a bug may require a phone reboot. However, they advise against including injected basal insulin in the prediction model as there is no model for it.", "settings_changed": ["Multiple Insulins → enabled"], "devices": ["Miaomiao 2", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightly", "predictive simulation settings"], "evidence_quote": "Try installing the latest nightly and enable the `Multiple Insulins` preference option which is within the `Predictive Simulation Settings` - Due to a bug in the current version you may need to reboot your phone before this actually takes effect but then you can specify basal insulin as a treatment type if that is what you are looking for.", "text": "Basal Insulin in XDrip The user asks if there is a way to add basal insulin (e.g., Tresiba) in xDrip, as currently only bolus insulin can be logged. They mention using xDrip with a Miaomiao 2 on a Oneplus 6.  A developer suggests installing the latest nightly and enabling the 'Multiple Insulins' preference option within 'Predictive Simulation Settings', noting a bug may require a phone reboot. However, they advise against including injected basal insulin in the prediction model as there is no model for it. Miaomiao 2 Libre nightly predictive simulation settings Try installing the latest nightly and enable the `Multiple Insulins` preference option which is within the `Predictive Simulation Settings` - Due to a bug in the current version you may need to reboot your phone before this actually takes effect but then you can specify basal insulin as a treatment type if that is what you are looking for."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-112", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 112, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 112, "title": "New 'Add Treatment' Dialog", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/112", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/112", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The current add treatment entry is slow to navigate, and users have misentered information because carb, insulin, and time are not visible all at once until the confirmation screen shows, requiring cancel and restart. Also, the current dialog occasionally causes errors due to forgetting to use 24h notation.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I have misentered information because carb, insulin, and time are not visible all at once untll the confirmation screen shows but then I have to cancel and start over.", "text": "New 'Add Treatment' Dialog The current add treatment entry is slow to navigate, and users have misentered information because carb, insulin, and time are not visible all at once until the confirmation screen shows, requiring cancel and restart. Also, the current dialog occasionally causes errors due to forgetting to use 24h notation.     I have misentered information because carb, insulin, and time are not visible all at once untll the confirmation screen shows but then I have to cancel and start over."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1130", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1130, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1130, "title": "Android 10 alerts not working", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1130", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1130", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating to Android 10, audio alerts for highs and lows no longer sound, though notifications and vibration may still occur. The user reports sleeping through hypos because the phone no longer speaks alerts like it did with Android 9.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause, but a workaround suggests that the notification channel for xDrip was set to silent in Android 10, overriding app and system settings.", "fix": "The user found a workaround: long-press the persistent xDrip notification, ensure the switch for 'Uncategorised notifications' is on, and set it to 'Alert' instead of 'Silent'.", "settings_changed": ["Uncategorised notifications → Alert"], "devices": ["Galaxy S10+", "Xperia XZ2 Compact"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I've long pressed the persistent xDrip notification, then made sure that the switch for Uncategorised notifications is on and that they are set to Alert (see screenshot) For some reason, this radio button is set to silent, even if all the notification settings in the phone and the app are set to ignore silent/DND. It seems to have fixed the issue", "text": "Android 10 alerts not working After updating to Android 10, audio alerts for highs and lows no longer sound, though notifications and vibration may still occur. The user reports sleeping through hypos because the phone no longer speaks alerts like it did with Android 9. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause, but a workaround suggests that the notification channel for xDrip was set to silent in Android 10, overriding app and system settings. The user found a workaround: long-press the persistent xDrip notification, ensure the switch for 'Uncategorised notifications' is on, and set it to 'Alert' instead of 'Silent'. Galaxy S10+ Xperia XZ2 Compact Android 10  I've long pressed the persistent xDrip notification, then made sure that the switch for Uncategorised notifications is on and that they are set to Alert (see screenshot) For some reason, this radio button is set to silent, even if all the notification settings in the phone and the app are set to ignore silent/DND. It seems to have fixed the issue"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1137", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1137, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1137, "title": "Wear OS watchface ambient mode brightness", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1137", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1137", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The ambient mode of the Wear OS watchface is too bright, making it hard to sleep. The user requests a brightness selector or a configurable color for low color mode.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Can someone add a selector for brightness on the ambient mode? It's so bright that i can't even sleep with that flashlight lol", "text": "Wear OS watchface ambient mode brightness The ambient mode of the Wear OS watchface is too bright, making it hard to sleep. The user requests a brightness selector or a configurable color for low color mode.     Can someone add a selector for brightness on the ambient mode? It's so bright that i can't even sleep with that flashlight lol"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1141", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1141, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1141, "title": "considering speed of glucose changing and compare to blood glucose level", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1141", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1141", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user reports that Libre 2 sensor readings are delayed compared to blood glucose readings, especially when glucose is changing rapidly, and asks if xDrip+ accounts for this delay.", "cause": "The thread discusses that Libre 2 values are delayed because they come from interstitial fluid, which lags behind blood glucose. The maintainer explains that this delay is inherent to all CGMs and varies per person and situation.", "fix": "No fix was implemented. The maintainer suggests calibrating only when the trend is flat and closes the issue without merging the proposed equation.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Libre 2"], "evidence_quote": "The libre 2 raw values are wrong, because they are always delayed. Thes come from interstitial fluid and are not equal to the blood sugar concentration. With my equation this deficiency can be solved.", "text": "considering speed of glucose changing and compare to blood glucose level The user reports that Libre 2 sensor readings are delayed compared to blood glucose readings, especially when glucose is changing rapidly, and asks if xDrip+ accounts for this delay. The thread discusses that Libre 2 values are delayed because they come from interstitial fluid, which lags behind blood glucose. The maintainer explains that this delay is inherent to all CGMs and varies per person and situation. No fix was implemented. The maintainer suggests calibrating only when the trend is flat and closes the issue without merging the proposed equation. Libre 2 Libre 2 The libre 2 raw values are wrong, because they are always delayed. Thes come from interstitial fluid and are not equal to the blood sugar concentration. With my equation this deficiency can be solved."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1148", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1148, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1148, "title": "How to Remove Sync Follower", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1148", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1148", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After changing smartphone for a follower, the old follower cannot be removed and xDrip shows the message 'No follower sync for: xxx time' because the old follower phone is turned off.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The follower will likely expire automatically after a while. If you want to cut off an active follower (which I don't think is what you're talking about here) then you would change the group sync security key.", "text": "How to Remove Sync Follower After changing smartphone for a follower, the old follower cannot be removed and xDrip shows the message 'No follower sync for: xxx time' because the old follower phone is turned off.     The follower will likely expire automatically after a while. If you want to cut off an active follower (which I don't think is what you're talking about here) then you would change the group sync security key."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1152", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1152, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1152, "title": "Multiple Insulin types as a treatment don't work.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1152", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1152", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When entering a Lantus treatment in the most recent nightly build of xDrip, the treatment is recorded and simulated as Fiasp instead. Other users report Lantus shown as Humalog, and basal graphing treats all insulin as one entity.", "cause": "The insulin type selection is reset if you change to the blood test/carb/time screens. Also, basal insulin display and predictive simulation are not implemented yet.", "fix": "Workaround: enter time/carbs/blood test first and make the insulin dose the last thing you add. For basal graphing, it is not functional yet; developers state basal doses are not included in predictive simulations.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "For me, it appears that the insulin type selection is reset if you change over to the blood test/carb/time screens. Just a little bug. Workaround is to enter your time/carbs/blood test first and make the insulin dose the last thing you add.", "text": "Multiple Insulin types as a treatment don't work. When entering a Lantus treatment in the most recent nightly build of xDrip, the treatment is recorded and simulated as Fiasp instead. Other users report Lantus shown as Humalog, and basal graphing treats all insulin as one entity. The insulin type selection is reset if you change to the blood test/carb/time screens. Also, basal insulin display and predictive simulation are not implemented yet. Workaround: enter time/carbs/blood test first and make the insulin dose the last thing you add. For basal graphing, it is not functional yet; developers state basal doses are not included in predictive simulations.   For me, it appears that the insulin type selection is reset if you change over to the blood test/carb/time screens. Just a little bug. Workaround is to enter your time/carbs/blood test first and make the insulin dose the last thing you add."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1153", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1153, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1153, "title": "Improvement: define Tresiba in Insulin Profiles", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1153", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1153", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Users request the ability to define Tresiba insulin in xDrip's insulin profiles, as it is not currently supported. They note that substituting other basal insulins like Lantus is not accurate.", "cause": "The thread discusses that Tresiba's activity curve does not match a linear trapezoid and has a flat profile with zero onset-time, peak at the beginning, and 42h duration, but with an efficiency-accumulation effect after continuous daily usage. This behavior is new to xDrip's prediction logic and requires a model for stacking and long duration, which is not currently implemented.", "fix": "No resolution is provided in the thread. The issue is closed and consolidated into issue #1898, but no specific fix or workaround is stated.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "its curve doesn't really match a linear trapezoid; it seems like a flat one with zero onset-time, peak at the beginning and 42h duration BUT with some kind of efficiency-accumulation after 3 days of (continuous daily) usage.... Such concepts like \"efficiency-accumulation\" are new to xdrip's prediction logic.", "text": "Improvement: define Tresiba in Insulin Profiles Users request the ability to define Tresiba insulin in xDrip's insulin profiles, as it is not currently supported. They note that substituting other basal insulins like Lantus is not accurate. The thread discusses that Tresiba's activity curve does not match a linear trapezoid and has a flat profile with zero onset-time, peak at the beginning, and 42h duration, but with an efficiency-accumulation effect after continuous daily usage. This behavior is new to xDrip's prediction logic and requires a model for stacking and long duration, which is not currently implemented. No resolution is provided in the thread. The issue is closed and consolidated into issue #1898, but no specific fix or workaround is stated.   its curve doesn't really match a linear trapezoid; it seems like a flat one with zero onset-time, peak at the beginning and 42h duration BUT with some kind of efficiency-accumulation after 3 days of (continuous daily) usage.... Such concepts like \"efficiency-accumulation\" are new to xdrip's prediction logic."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1154", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1154, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1154, "title": "Contribution: PDF report generator", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1154", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1154", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Doctors often want reports that usually come from proprietary software, but xDrip+ users may not want their data stored in corporate cloud systems. The issue proposes a PDF report generator that parses the sqlite database directly to generate day plots, daily patterns with percentiles, carbs/bolus and ratio plots, and text stats.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I've written a PDF report generator for exactly this purpose. It parses the sqlite db directly and generates day plots as well as the daily pattern with percentiles that all doctors seem to love, plus carbs/bolus and ratio plots, Text stats and so on.", "text": "Contribution: PDF report generator Doctors often want reports that usually come from proprietary software, but xDrip+ users may not want their data stored in corporate cloud systems. The issue proposes a PDF report generator that parses the sqlite database directly to generate day plots, daily patterns with percentiles, carbs/bolus and ratio plots, and text stats.     I've written a PDF report generator for exactly this purpose. It parses the sqlite db directly and generates day plots as well as the daily pattern with percentiles that all doctors seem to love, plus carbs/bolus and ratio plots, Text stats and so on."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1159", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1159, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1159, "title": "\"re-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged\" in alert is not working properly", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1159", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1159", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Alerts using a 5-minute 're-raise' time are triggered after 1 minute regardless of the set value. The issue occurs when using the ascending volume profile.", "cause": "The 're-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged' feature does not work with the ascending volume profile, because the ascending profile is designed to increase alert strength every minute.", "fix": "The issue is not a bug but a design conflict. To avoid the behavior, use a non-ascending sound profile. Alternatively, a feature request could be made to allow configuring the rate of volume increase, but this is not currently implemented.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "This feature is not working with ascending profile, since ascending profile means that the alert will get stronger every minute.", "text": "\"re-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged\" in alert is not working properly Alerts using a 5-minute 're-raise' time are triggered after 1 minute regardless of the set value. The issue occurs when using the ascending volume profile. The 're-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged' feature does not work with the ascending volume profile, because the ascending profile is designed to increase alert strength every minute. The issue is not a bug but a design conflict. To avoid the behavior, use a non-ascending sound profile. Alternatively, a feature request could be made to allow configuring the rate of volume increase, but this is not currently implemented.   This feature is not working with ascending profile, since ascending profile means that the alert will get stronger every minute."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-116", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 116, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 116, "title": "Regular database backups to Google Drive", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/116", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/116", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users request a feature for regular database backups to Google Drive, as they want to avoid losing history if they lose their phone.", "cause": null, "fix": "The feature was implemented via a daily database save that occurs before the daily purge. To enable, go to Settings, Less Common Settings, Save Database Daily. The database is stored locally in the xDrip folder, and to sync to cloud, use an external sync app like FolderSync.", "settings_changed": ["Save Database Daily → enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "To enable, left hamburger -> Settings, Less Common Settings, Save Database Daily.", "text": "Regular database backups to Google Drive Users request a feature for regular database backups to Google Drive, as they want to avoid losing history if they lose their phone.  The feature was implemented via a daily database save that occurs before the daily purge. To enable, go to Settings, Less Common Settings, Save Database Daily. The database is stored locally in the xDrip folder, and to sync to cloud, use an external sync app like FolderSync.   To enable, left hamburger -> Settings, Less Common Settings, Save Database Daily."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1161", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1161, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1161, "title": "Samsung Note 10+ Update", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1161", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1161", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After a Samsung update (ui2.0), the phone and Miaomiao transmitter will no longer communicate.", "cause": null, "fix": "Uncheck almost every Bluetooth option in the Xdrip Bluetooth menu except the first one ('Turn Bluetooth on if switched off'), reset the Miaomiao, and completely shut down and restart the phone.", "settings_changed": ["Turn Bluetooth on if switched off → checked (only one checked)"], "devices": ["Samsung Note 10+", "Miaomiao", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "almost every Bluetooth option needs to be unchecked in the Xdrip Bluetooth menu with the exception of the very first one which is 'Turn Bluetooth on if switched off'", "text": "Samsung Note 10+ Update After a Samsung update (ui2.0), the phone and Miaomiao transmitter will no longer communicate.  Uncheck almost every Bluetooth option in the Xdrip Bluetooth menu except the first one ('Turn Bluetooth on if switched off'), reset the Miaomiao, and completely shut down and restart the phone. Samsung Note 10+ Miaomiao Libre bluetooth almost every Bluetooth option needs to be unchecked in the Xdrip Bluetooth menu with the exception of the very first one which is 'Turn Bluetooth on if switched off'"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1166", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1166, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1166, "title": "Make SMB microbolus threshold configurable", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1166", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1166", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Values <= 0.3u are displayed as SMB (as a triangle) in xDrip, but SMB sometimes delivers 0.4u/0.5u microboluses. There is no option to configure the threshold, and xDrip does not differentiate between loop SMB and manual boluses that are very small.", "cause": "xDrip has a decluttering feature that for insulin treatments less than or equal to 0.3 units, the value is not shown and the symbol is a triangle. This causes small manual boluses to be displayed as SMB.", "fix": "Disable the decluttering feature by disabling the setting: Settings > Display settings > Graph settings > Show micro bolus icons. This will show all insulin treatments the same way regardless of value.", "settings_changed": ["Show micro bolus icons → disabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "You can disable this decluttering feature. To do that, disable the following: Settings > Display settings > Graph settings > Show micro bolus icons", "text": "Make SMB microbolus threshold configurable Values <= 0.3u are displayed as SMB (as a triangle) in xDrip, but SMB sometimes delivers 0.4u/0.5u microboluses. There is no option to configure the threshold, and xDrip does not differentiate between loop SMB and manual boluses that are very small. xDrip has a decluttering feature that for insulin treatments less than or equal to 0.3 units, the value is not shown and the symbol is a triangle. This causes small manual boluses to be displayed as SMB. Disable the decluttering feature by disabling the setting: Settings > Display settings > Graph settings > Show micro bolus icons. This will show all insulin treatments the same way regardless of value.   You can disable this decluttering feature. To do that, disable the following: Settings > Display settings > Graph settings > Show micro bolus icons"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1186", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1186, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1186, "title": "Tizen os", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1186", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1186", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user wants to use xDrip on a Samsung Galaxy Active 2 watch as a standalone collector (directly from a transmitter like Miaomiao) without needing a phone, and asks if a Tizen OS version can be developed for the Galaxy Store.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Galaxy Active 2", "Miaomiao"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["collector"], "evidence_quote": "We want it to be a collector, not communicating with phone but directly with the miaomiao using xdrip.", "text": "Tizen os The user wants to use xDrip on a Samsung Galaxy Active 2 watch as a standalone collector (directly from a transmitter like Miaomiao) without needing a phone, and asks if a Tizen OS version can be developed for the Galaxy Store.   Galaxy Active 2 Miaomiao collector We want it to be a collector, not communicating with phone but directly with the miaomiao using xdrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1190", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1190, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1190, "title": "XDrip G5, Android 10, Oneplus 7 Pro phone ", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1190", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1190", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "During sleeping hours, the phone loses connection to the G5 every night, but connectivity is good during the day. The issue occurs when the phone is not plugged in and not in use for more than about 40 minutes. Restarting the collector via System Status reconnects.", "cause": "The thread suggests that Android 10's deep sleep or doze mode, possibly combined with OnePlus's aggressive battery saving, is causing the connection loss. The original poster later states that either a phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip resolved the issue, but no definitive root cause is established.", "fix": "The original poster reports that the issue resolved after either a phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip, but no specific fix is stated. A workaround mentioned is keeping the System Status page open in xDrip to guarantee sync.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Either a Phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip resolved this issue.", "text": "XDrip G5, Android 10, Oneplus 7 Pro phone  During sleeping hours, the phone loses connection to the G5 every night, but connectivity is good during the day. The issue occurs when the phone is not plugged in and not in use for more than about 40 minutes. Restarting the collector via System Status reconnects. The thread suggests that Android 10's deep sleep or doze mode, possibly combined with OnePlus's aggressive battery saving, is causing the connection loss. The original poster later states that either a phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip resolved the issue, but no definitive root cause is established. The original poster reports that the issue resolved after either a phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip, but no specific fix is stated. A workaround mentioned is keeping the System Status page open in xDrip to guarantee sync. G5 Android 10  Either a Phone firmware update or a newer version of xDrip resolved this issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1199", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1199, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1199, "title": "G6 sensor restarts on 81XXXX transmitter", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1199", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1199", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Preemptive sensor restarts for Dexcom G6 are failing: the sensor goes to 'sensor failed', then attempts restart and ends up in a 2-hour warmup loop, repeatedly failing and restarting. This behavior occurs with 81XXXX and 8H transmitters.", "cause": "The problem is with the firmware on the 'firefly' transmitters (8H and some others). When Dexcom started using these new transmitters, restarts no longer worked on them. Preemptive restart only works if the firmware version is 1.6.5.25, which includes all 81XXXX and some 81XXXX.", "fix": "For transmitters with firmware 1.6.5.25, preemptive restart works. For others, the only way to restart requires temporary removal of the transmitter from the sensor, shorting the sensor pins to skip the 30-minute wait, then reinserting and restarting with the original calibration code. Detailed instructions are available on Facebook or Gitter.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "81XXXX transmitter", "8H transmitter"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["preemptive restart", "restart", "firefly transmitter"], "evidence_quote": "You can only perform preemptive restart if the firmware version (shown on system status page) is 1.6.5.25. That include all 81XXXX and some of 81XXXX. If the serial number does not start with 80 or 81, the only way to restart requires temporary removal of the transmitter from the sensor.", "text": "G6 sensor restarts on 81XXXX transmitter Preemptive sensor restarts for Dexcom G6 are failing: the sensor goes to 'sensor failed', then attempts restart and ends up in a 2-hour warmup loop, repeatedly failing and restarting. This behavior occurs with 81XXXX and 8H transmitters. The problem is with the firmware on the 'firefly' transmitters (8H and some others). When Dexcom started using these new transmitters, restarts no longer worked on them. Preemptive restart only works if the firmware version is 1.6.5.25, which includes all 81XXXX and some 81XXXX. For transmitters with firmware 1.6.5.25, preemptive restart works. For others, the only way to restart requires temporary removal of the transmitter from the sensor, shorting the sensor pins to skip the 30-minute wait, then reinserting and restarting with the original calibration code. Detailed instructions are available on Facebook or Gitter. Dexcom G6 81XXXX transmitter 8H transmitter preemptive restart restart firefly transmitter You can only perform preemptive restart if the firmware version (shown on system status page) is 1.6.5.25. That include all 81XXXX and some of 81XXXX. If the serial number does not start with 80 or 81, the only way to restart requires temporary removal of the transmitter from the sensor."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-120", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 120, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 120, "title": "Adding onetouch verio flex?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/120", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/120", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The OneTouch Verio Flex meter can pair and sync with its own app, but xDrip+ gets timeout errors when trying to sync (\"Timed out on : get new glucose records\"). Later reports describe intermittent auto-sync and missed connections after meter sync.", "cause": "The meter does not comply with the standard Bluetooth glucose meter protocol that xDrip already supports, so it requires special code for its unique protocol. Later intermittent connection issues may be due to Android Bluetooth stacks flaking out.", "fix": "Jamorham added support for the Verio Flex in the June 8th nightly build. For intermittent drops, turning the meter off/on and toggling the Bluetooth glucose meter setting off/on in xDrip can trigger a sync.", "settings_changed": ["auto calibrate → enabled"], "devices": ["Verio Flex"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.0", "Android 6", "Android 4.4"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "glucose meter", "onetouch app"], "evidence_quote": "I have added support for the Verio Flex with about 500 lines of code in the June 8th nightly.", "text": "Adding onetouch verio flex? The OneTouch Verio Flex meter can pair and sync with its own app, but xDrip+ gets timeout errors when trying to sync (\"Timed out on : get new glucose records\"). Later reports describe intermittent auto-sync and missed connections after meter sync. The meter does not comply with the standard Bluetooth glucose meter protocol that xDrip already supports, so it requires special code for its unique protocol. Later intermittent connection issues may be due to Android Bluetooth stacks flaking out. Jamorham added support for the Verio Flex in the June 8th nightly build. For intermittent drops, turning the meter off/on and toggling the Bluetooth glucose meter setting off/on in xDrip can trigger a sync. Verio Flex Android 7.0 Android 6 Android 4.4 bluetooth glucose meter onetouch app I have added support for the Verio Flex with about 500 lines of code in the June 8th nightly."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1200", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1200, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1200, "title": "Problems with LinearTrapezoidInsulin.java [Incorrect Boundary Conditions]", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1200", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1200", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The LinearTrapezoidInsulin.java equations have incorrect boundary conditions because the value of 'onset' is not properly accounted for when applying boundary conditions during integration. This causes IOB values at transition points to not match, resulting in a kink in the IOB curve, and IOB does not become zero at the end of the insulin duration. The impact is more pronounced for insulins with larger onset and shorter life, such as Toujeo.", "cause": "The root cause is that the algorithm calculating IOB and iActivity was completely changed. The old algorithm needed a stepwise schema to calculate iActivity, while the new one uses a formula. The old algorithm has a one-step decay (5 minutes) before 'time', causing a timeshift. As a result, treatments.ioBForGraph_new starts exactly one timeslice before 'time' of the old one, and the new algorithm has to compensate. This timeshift leads to the observed issues, including IOB not being zero at the end.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix that was implemented. The user peeyes-dev provided updated equations and code, and stephencmorton confirmed they look correct, but there is no statement that they were merged or that a specific fix was applied. The issue was closed due to inactivity.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "major root cause of our identified issues one to three is that the algorithm calculating IOB and iactivity has been completely changed. the \"old\" algorithm needed a really stepwise schema to calculate iActivity - the new one has a formula to calculate it and thus doesn't need it. So the \"old\" one has a one step decay (5 minutes) before \"time\" and that's a (lets say) timeshift.", "text": "Problems with LinearTrapezoidInsulin.java [Incorrect Boundary Conditions] The LinearTrapezoidInsulin.java equations have incorrect boundary conditions because the value of 'onset' is not properly accounted for when applying boundary conditions during integration. This causes IOB values at transition points to not match, resulting in a kink in the IOB curve, and IOB does not become zero at the end of the insulin duration. The impact is more pronounced for insulins with larger onset and shorter life, such as Toujeo. The root cause is that the algorithm calculating IOB and iActivity was completely changed. The old algorithm needed a stepwise schema to calculate iActivity, while the new one uses a formula. The old algorithm has a one-step decay (5 minutes) before 'time', causing a timeshift. As a result, treatments.ioBForGraph_new starts exactly one timeslice before 'time' of the old one, and the new algorithm has to compensate. This timeshift leads to the observed issues, including IOB not being zero at the end. The thread does not state a definitive fix that was implemented. The user peeyes-dev provided updated equations and code, and stephencmorton confirmed they look correct, but there is no statement that they were merged or that a specific fix was applied. The issue was closed due to inactivity.   major root cause of our identified issues one to three is that the algorithm calculating IOB and iactivity has been completely changed. the \"old\" algorithm needed a really stepwise schema to calculate iActivity - the new one has a formula to calculate it and thus doesn't need it. So the \"old\" one has a one step decay (5 minutes) before \"time\" and that's a (lets say) timeshift."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1236", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1236, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1236, "title": "I made a website for sharing working configs", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1236", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1236", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The issue is not a problem report but an announcement of a website for sharing working/broken configurations for xDrip+ after Android updates. The author expresses fear of Android updates breaking xDrip+ functionality.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I am always afraid of installing android updates since they broke the xdrip+ app functionality a few times in the past. I made a website where we can share working/broken configurations.", "text": "I made a website for sharing working configs The issue is not a problem report but an announcement of a website for sharing working/broken configurations for xDrip+ after Android updates. The author expresses fear of Android updates breaking xDrip+ functionality.     I am always afraid of installing android updates since they broke the xdrip+ app functionality a few times in the past. I made a website where we can share working/broken configurations."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1237", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1237, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1237, "title": "LibreLink App 2.4", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1237", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1237", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User asks if xDrip works with the new LibreLink App 2.4, which Abbott claims is more precise especially for low BGs, and what they need to do.", "cause": "The new LibreLink app version needs to be patched to work with xDrip, but no one has adopted the patches to the new version. The extraction method may not change precision between old and new versions.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["LibreLink"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["patch"], "evidence_quote": "The problem is, that the new app needs to be patched, but this is hardly liunked to a specific version of LibreLink.", "text": "LibreLink App 2.4 User asks if xDrip works with the new LibreLink App 2.4, which Abbott claims is more precise especially for low BGs, and what they need to do. The new LibreLink app version needs to be patched to work with xDrip, but no one has adopted the patches to the new version. The extraction method may not change precision between old and new versions.  LibreLink patch The problem is, that the new app needs to be patched, but this is hardly liunked to a specific version of LibreLink."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1240", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1240, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1240, "title": "Ongoing notification wakes up display every 5 minutes.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1240", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1240", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The ongoing notification from xDrip wakes up the display every 5 minutes on a Google Pixel XL with Android 10, unless the notification is set to 'silent' in Android settings. The user wants to keep the notification visible at the top without waking the display.", "cause": "The issue is likely due to Android phone settings, such as 'wake screen for notifications' under Display -> Lock Screen settings, rather than an xDrip issue.", "fix": "Turn off 'wake screen for notifications' under Display -> Lock Screen settings on the phone. Alternatively, set the xDrip notification to 'silent' or disable floating notifications and lock screen notifications for the specific notification channel.", "settings_changed": ["wake screen for notifications → off"], "devices": ["Google Pixel XL", "Xiaomi Redmi Note 9 Pro", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["patched app"], "evidence_quote": "Maybe it's actually an Android setting. I have \"wake screen for notifications\" turned on under \"Display\" -> \"Lock Screen\" settings. I'll try turning it off and waiting to see if that changes the behavior.", "text": "Ongoing notification wakes up display every 5 minutes. The ongoing notification from xDrip wakes up the display every 5 minutes on a Google Pixel XL with Android 10, unless the notification is set to 'silent' in Android settings. The user wants to keep the notification visible at the top without waking the display. The issue is likely due to Android phone settings, such as 'wake screen for notifications' under Display -> Lock Screen settings, rather than an xDrip issue. Turn off 'wake screen for notifications' under Display -> Lock Screen settings on the phone. Alternatively, set the xDrip notification to 'silent' or disable floating notifications and lock screen notifications for the specific notification channel. Google Pixel XL Xiaomi Redmi Note 9 Pro Libre 2 Android 10 Android 9 patched app Maybe it's actually an Android setting. I have \"wake screen for notifications\" turned on under \"Display\" -> \"Lock Screen\" settings. I'll try turning it off and waiting to see if that changes the behavior."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1254", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1254, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1254, "title": "Android 10 with Pixel 3XL", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1254", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1254", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After upgrading to Android 10 on Pixel 3XL, no successful sensor sessions. Transmitter shows connected in xDrip+ but not under phone Bluetooth settings. Sensor start fails or says 'sensor stopped'.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Possible factors discussed include outdated xDrip version, transmitter/sensor session mismatch, Bluetooth name with space, and Trust Auto-Connect setting, but none confirmed.", "fix": "No definitive fix was confirmed. Suggested actions included updating to latest nightly/alpha, stopping and starting sensor, removing space from Bluetooth name, and disabling Trust Auto-Connect, but user reported no success.", "settings_changed": ["Bluetooth AVRCP → 1.3", "OB1 debugging → enabled", "Bluetooth name → Pixel3aXL (removed space)", "Trust Auto-Connect → disabled"], "devices": ["Pixel 3XL", "Pixel 3a", "Pixel 3a XL", "G6 transmitter", "MiaoMiao"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth", "transmitter", "sensor"], "evidence_quote": "I've updated to the latest. It's still telling me that the sensor is stopped but it's still connecting to it.", "text": "Android 10 with Pixel 3XL After upgrading to Android 10 on Pixel 3XL, no successful sensor sessions. Transmitter shows connected in xDrip+ but not under phone Bluetooth settings. Sensor start fails or says 'sensor stopped'. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Possible factors discussed include outdated xDrip version, transmitter/sensor session mismatch, Bluetooth name with space, and Trust Auto-Connect setting, but none confirmed. No definitive fix was confirmed. Suggested actions included updating to latest nightly/alpha, stopping and starting sensor, removing space from Bluetooth name, and disabling Trust Auto-Connect, but user reported no success. Pixel 3XL Pixel 3a Pixel 3a XL G6 transmitter MiaoMiao Android 10 Bluetooth transmitter sensor I've updated to the latest. It's still telling me that the sensor is stopped but it's still connecting to it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1266", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1266, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1266, "title": "Ghost fingerprick calibration values entered.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1266", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1266", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Users report ghost fingerstick calibration values appearing in xDrip+ that they did not enter, often hours after a real reading, and these phantom values are used for calibration, skewing the calibration curve and causing incorrect glucose readings.", "cause": "The issue is caused by the automatic calibration feature, specifically the setting 'Use Treatment BG values' set to 'Automatic', which queues fingerstick readings entered via the Treatments dialog and processes them later, applying them to the current sensor reading instead of the past one.", "fix": "Disable automatic calibration (turn off auto-calibration or set 'Use Treatment BG values' to 'never use them') to stop ghost calibrations from occurring.", "settings_changed": ["Use Treatment BG values → Automatic (was set to this, causing issue)", "auto-calibration → off"], "devices": ["MiaoMiao 2", "Libre", "Samsung galaxy s9+", "Contour Next One", "Libre2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["nightscout", "bluetooth glucose meter", "auto-calibration", "treatment"], "evidence_quote": "Right after I reported this issue, I switched auto-calibration off, and can confirm that stops it from occurring.", "text": "Ghost fingerprick calibration values entered. Users report ghost fingerstick calibration values appearing in xDrip+ that they did not enter, often hours after a real reading, and these phantom values are used for calibration, skewing the calibration curve and causing incorrect glucose readings. The issue is caused by the automatic calibration feature, specifically the setting 'Use Treatment BG values' set to 'Automatic', which queues fingerstick readings entered via the Treatments dialog and processes them later, applying them to the current sensor reading instead of the past one. Disable automatic calibration (turn off auto-calibration or set 'Use Treatment BG values' to 'never use them') to stop ghost calibrations from occurring. MiaoMiao 2 Libre Samsung galaxy s9+ Contour Next One Libre2 Android 10 nightscout bluetooth glucose meter auto-calibration treatment Right after I reported this issue, I switched auto-calibration off, and can confirm that stops it from occurring."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1269", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1269, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1269, "title": "Screen rotation issue.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1269", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1269", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After rotating from portrait to landscape and back to portrait, the screen does not properly resize. This started after installing the Feb 20 nightly and persists in later nightlies on Android 10 devices.", "cause": "The issue appears to be caused by Android 10, as updating to Android 11 resolved it for users. The thread suggests it is a problem caused by Android.", "fix": "Updating to Android 11 resolved the issue for users. For those unable to update, installing the latest manufacturer updates may help, but no definitive fix is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 4 XL", "Pixel 3", "Mi A2", "Motorola G Power"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Incidentally, updating to Android 11 fixed it", "text": "Screen rotation issue. After rotating from portrait to landscape and back to portrait, the screen does not properly resize. This started after installing the Feb 20 nightly and persists in later nightlies on Android 10 devices. The issue appears to be caused by Android 10, as updating to Android 11 resolved it for users. The thread suggests it is a problem caused by Android. Updating to Android 11 resolved the issue for users. For those unable to update, installing the latest manufacturer updates may help, but no definitive fix is provided. Pixel 4 XL Pixel 3 Mi A2 Motorola G Power Android 10 Android 11  Incidentally, updating to Android 11 fixed it"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1272", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1272, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1272, "title": "Sensor restarts never work - Pixel 4 XL Transmitter 8H", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1272", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1272", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Sensor restarts never work on Pixel 4 XL with Transmitter 8H. The user is unable to restart the sensor, even though they usually can with their Ticwatch Pro.", "cause": "The issue is specific to 81 - 8H transmitters. A new hardware/firmware version was discovered and coded as not being capable of preemptive restarts.", "fix": "Workaround: remove the transmitter from the sensor by unlatching it from the sides, wait 15 minutes, put it back in, and start the sensor again. Use an iFixit spudger or two old glucose test strips to safely unlatch.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 4 XL", "Transmitter 8H", "Ticwatch Pro"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["transmitter", "sensor restart"], "evidence_quote": "The only thing that works for me for now is removing transmitter from the sensor by unlatching it from the sides, waiting for 15 minutes, putting back in, and starting the sensor again.", "text": "Sensor restarts never work - Pixel 4 XL Transmitter 8H Sensor restarts never work on Pixel 4 XL with Transmitter 8H. The user is unable to restart the sensor, even though they usually can with their Ticwatch Pro. The issue is specific to 81 - 8H transmitters. A new hardware/firmware version was discovered and coded as not being capable of preemptive restarts. Workaround: remove the transmitter from the sensor by unlatching it from the sides, wait 15 minutes, put it back in, and start the sensor again. Use an iFixit spudger or two old glucose test strips to safely unlatch. Pixel 4 XL Transmitter 8H Ticwatch Pro transmitter sensor restart The only thing that works for me for now is removing transmitter from the sensor by unlatching it from the sides, waiting for 15 minutes, putting back in, and starting the sensor again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1279", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1279, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1279, "title": "Dexcom G6 / 8G tx: every 5mins \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" & \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1279", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1279", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since using 8G Dexcom transmitters, xDrip+ logs the same errors every 5 minutes: \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" and \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\", along with \"Failed to write DisconnectTxMessage\" GATT exceptions. Blood glucose readings continue to work, but the repeated error messages are annoying and clutter the event log.", "cause": "A debug discovery of the Dexcom device shows the authentication characteristic (F8083535-849E-531C-C594-30F1F86A4EA5) advertises as WRITE and INDICATE, while xDrip attempts to do a READ operation in Ob1G5StateMachine, producing the repeated GATT read failures on Firefly transmitters.", "fix": "The xDrip main repository did not fix the authentication code itself; instead, logging was changed so the errors are suppressed or appear much less frequently. Users are advised to update to a recent release (e.g., Feb. 11, 2021) to stop seeing the log messages. A separate user fork/branch (firefly_transmitter) contains a code-level fix for the read operation, but it was not merged as a clean PR at the time.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["ob1", "native"], "evidence_quote": "The authentication was not enhanced, only the logging has been changed to not show the errors in most cases.", "text": "Dexcom G6 / 8G tx: every 5mins \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" & \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\" Since using 8G Dexcom transmitters, xDrip+ logs the same errors every 5 minutes: \"Could not read after AuthRequestTX\" and \"Could not read reply to auth challenge\", along with \"Failed to write DisconnectTxMessage\" GATT exceptions. Blood glucose readings continue to work, but the repeated error messages are annoying and clutter the event log. A debug discovery of the Dexcom device shows the authentication characteristic (F8083535-849E-531C-C594-30F1F86A4EA5) advertises as WRITE and INDICATE, while xDrip attempts to do a READ operation in Ob1G5StateMachine, producing the repeated GATT read failures on Firefly transmitters. The xDrip main repository did not fix the authentication code itself; instead, logging was changed so the errors are suppressed or appear much less frequently. Users are advised to update to a recent release (e.g., Feb. 11, 2021) to stop seeing the log messages. A separate user fork/branch (firefly_transmitter) contains a code-level fix for the read operation, but it was not merged as a clean PR at the time. Dexcom G6 Android 9 ob1 native The authentication was not enhanced, only the logging has been changed to not show the errors in most cases."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-128", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 128, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 128, "title": "Push CGM data to Diabetes:M app", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/128", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/128", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The issue requests a feature to push CGM data from xDrip to the Diabetes:M app, but the effort was abandoned because the Diabetes:M app will not display data points closer than 15 minutes apart, making it useless for CGM data.", "cause": "The Diabetes:M app and its developers refuse to display data points closer than 15 minutes apart, which is unacceptable for CGM data.", "fix": "No fix was implemented; the issue was closed by the author due to the Diabetes:M app's limitation and lack of cooperation from its developers.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I abandoned this project for the simple reason that the diabetes:m crew/app won't allow data closer than 15 minutes to be used or displayed. That makes the diabetes:m app useless for CGM data.", "text": "Push CGM data to Diabetes:M app The issue requests a feature to push CGM data from xDrip to the Diabetes:M app, but the effort was abandoned because the Diabetes:M app will not display data points closer than 15 minutes apart, making it useless for CGM data. The Diabetes:M app and its developers refuse to display data points closer than 15 minutes apart, which is unacceptable for CGM data. No fix was implemented; the issue was closed by the author due to the Diabetes:M app's limitation and lack of cooperation from its developers.   I abandoned this project for the simple reason that the diabetes:m crew/app won't allow data closer than 15 minutes to be used or displayed. That makes the diabetes:m app useless for CGM data."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1287", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1287, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1287, "title": "BG reading missed and silent mode", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1287", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1287", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The 'BG reading missed' alarm does not override silent mode, so when the phone is on silent at night, missed readings are not alerted, potentially missing dangerous glucose drops. Some users also report that the alarm does not ring or vibrate even when the phone is not in silent mode.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a root cause; it is identified as a missing feature or bug in xDrip's alert handling for missed readings.", "fix": "No fix is provided in the thread; the issue is closed as a duplicate of issue #1147, suggesting users follow that issue for resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung S7", "Samsung S10e", "Samsung S7 Edge", "Samsung A8", "Samsung S10"], "android_versions": ["Android 9"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The problem is with the XDrip functionality, which doesn't allow to override silent mode for the \"BG reading missing\" alerts.", "text": "BG reading missed and silent mode The 'BG reading missed' alarm does not override silent mode, so when the phone is on silent at night, missed readings are not alerted, potentially missing dangerous glucose drops. Some users also report that the alarm does not ring or vibrate even when the phone is not in silent mode. The thread does not establish a root cause; it is identified as a missing feature or bug in xDrip's alert handling for missed readings. No fix is provided in the thread; the issue is closed as a duplicate of issue #1147, suggesting users follow that issue for resolution. Samsung S7 Samsung S10e Samsung S7 Edge Samsung A8 Samsung S10 Android 9  The problem is with the XDrip functionality, which doesn't allow to override silent mode for the \"BG reading missing\" alerts."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1297", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1297, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1297, "title": "Connectivity problem reaching Share servers", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1297", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1297", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since approximately 8.30am CET on April 9th I get the problem \"Connectivity problem reaching Share servers\". I use dexcom share/ follow to get readings for my xdrip app and nightscout website. The website didn't get readings since ca. 1am the same day. So both sources have a problem getting share data. Interestingly enough, my dexcom follower through the official app still get readings without any changes. The exact wording in the event log of xdrip is the following: \"Get Share Data Failed: java.io.EOFException: End of input at line 1 column 1 path $\"", "cause": "It seems that the problem is because of other character then a-z in the user name. See the discussion in nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#5608. Unfortunately you can't switch the user name. You have to set up a new account.", "fix": "You have to set up a new Dexcom account with a username containing only a-z characters. Instructions are provided in a linked document.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom Share", "xDrip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dexcom share", "follow", "nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "It seems that the problem is because of other character then a-z in the user name. See the discussion in nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#5608 Unfortunately you can't switch the user name. You have to set up a new account.", "text": "Connectivity problem reaching Share servers Since approximately 8.30am CET on April 9th I get the problem \"Connectivity problem reaching Share servers\". I use dexcom share/ follow to get readings for my xdrip app and nightscout website. The website didn't get readings since ca. 1am the same day. So both sources have a problem getting share data. Interestingly enough, my dexcom follower through the official app still get readings without any changes. The exact wording in the event log of xdrip is the following: \"Get Share Data Failed: java.io.EOFException: End of input at line 1 column 1 path $\" It seems that the problem is because of other character then a-z in the user name. See the discussion in nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#5608. Unfortunately you can't switch the user name. You have to set up a new account. You have to set up a new Dexcom account with a username containing only a-z characters. Instructions are provided in a linked document. Dexcom Share xDrip dexcom share follow nightscout It seems that the problem is because of other character then a-z in the user name. See the discussion in nightscout/cgm-remote-monitor#5608 Unfortunately you can't switch the user name. You have to set up a new account."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1308", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1308, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1308, "title": "Enabling OOP calibration", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1308", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1308", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user requests enabling the 'OOP algorithm calibration' checkbox in xDrip+ settings. They report that without calibration, BG values from OOP algorithm are systematically far from a glucose meter, and they had to manually edit settings XML to enable it.", "cause": "The OOP algorithm has a low boundary of 39 mg/dl, making it impossible to get values below that. If calibration is enabled, it could cause missed hypoglycemia because the algorithm cannot output values below the threshold, leading to inaccurate low readings.", "fix": "The maintainers decided not to enable the checkbox due to safety concerns about missing low glucose scenarios. No fix was provided; the feature remains disabled.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre2", "Miaomiao2", "xDrip+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OOP", "calibration"], "evidence_quote": "The algorithm has A low boundary of 39 mgdl. I.e. It is not possible to get values below that. Enabling this feature might be unsafe as you can miss out on certain low glucose scenarios.", "text": "Enabling OOP calibration The user requests enabling the 'OOP algorithm calibration' checkbox in xDrip+ settings. They report that without calibration, BG values from OOP algorithm are systematically far from a glucose meter, and they had to manually edit settings XML to enable it. The OOP algorithm has a low boundary of 39 mg/dl, making it impossible to get values below that. If calibration is enabled, it could cause missed hypoglycemia because the algorithm cannot output values below the threshold, leading to inaccurate low readings. The maintainers decided not to enable the checkbox due to safety concerns about missing low glucose scenarios. No fix was provided; the feature remains disabled. Libre2 Miaomiao2 xDrip+ OOP calibration The algorithm has A low boundary of 39 mgdl. I.e. It is not possible to get values below that. Enabling this feature might be unsafe as you can miss out on certain low glucose scenarios."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1310", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1310, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1310, "title": "G6 / 8G: \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1310", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1310", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When calibrating with the syringe icon, the error \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\" is shown, and only the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item works. Multiple users report the same issue with G6 transmitters/sensors.", "cause": "The error appears because xDrip's timestamp check sees the calibration as older than one hour (since > HOUR_IN_MS is true), but the underlying reason is not definitively identified. Some speculate timezone changes or an xDrip regression after the 2019.10.27 nightly caused it; Navid200 later states the transmitter actually accepts calibrations and the xDrip logs are confusing.", "fix": "Enable 'Advanced Calibration/Automatic Calibration (experimental)' — after doing this, syringe calibrations are sent and accepted by the transmitter. Justinthomas also successfully reverted to the 2019.10.27 nightly build, and Jamorham said the 26 May nightly should resolve related issues.", "settings_changed": ["Advanced Calibration/Automatic Calibration (experimental) → ON", "Go on without Calibrations → ON", "Authenticate G5 before each read → ON"], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["native", "ob1"], "evidence_quote": "I additionally switched **\"Advanced Calibration/Automatic Calibration (experimental)\" ON** ---> now when using the syringe \"(1) calibration\" is sent to the tx and it's accepted, showing in Event Log!!", "text": "G6 / 8G: \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\" When calibrating with the syringe icon, the error \"Cannot send calibration older than 1 hour to transmitter\" is shown, and only the \"Initial Calibration\" menu item works. Multiple users report the same issue with G6 transmitters/sensors. The error appears because xDrip's timestamp check sees the calibration as older than one hour (since > HOUR_IN_MS is true), but the underlying reason is not definitively identified. Some speculate timezone changes or an xDrip regression after the 2019.10.27 nightly caused it; Navid200 later states the transmitter actually accepts calibrations and the xDrip logs are confusing. Enable 'Advanced Calibration/Automatic Calibration (experimental)' — after doing this, syringe calibrations are sent and accepted by the transmitter. Justinthomas also successfully reverted to the 2019.10.27 nightly build, and Jamorham said the 26 May nightly should resolve related issues. G6 Android 10 native ob1 I additionally switched **\"Advanced Calibration/Automatic Calibration (experimental)\" ON** ---> now when using the syringe \"(1) calibration\" is sent to the tx and it's accepted, showing in Event Log!!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1328", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1328, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1328, "title": "xdrip+ isn't Responding", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1328", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1328", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip+ throws 'isn't responding' errors every few minutes, even after clearing settings and updating to the most current nightly. The app works and readings are received, but the warning pops up about every 30 seconds regardless of the app in use.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that incorrect or non-recommended settings may be the cause, and that every instance of this error has been addressed by adjusting xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required.", "fix": "Adjust xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required, using recommended settings. For Dexcom, ensure settings match the G5 Recommended Settings wiki. For Libre/MiaoMiao, ask for recommended settings in support channels. Additionally, enabling 'Save Database Daily' and setting 'Glucose Retention' to 90 days may help by shrinking the database.", "settings_changed": ["Save Database Daily → enabled", "Glucose Retention → 90"], "devices": ["Dexcom G5", "Libre 1", "MiaoMiao 1"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tomato", "libre 1 via miao mao 1", "G5/G6 Debug Settings", "Force G5 to UI Thread"], "evidence_quote": "So far, every instance of this error I have seen has been addressed by adjusting xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required. There was a Dexcom collector case where changing all the Bluetooth and G5/G6 Debug settings to recommended settings stopped the issue.", "text": "xdrip+ isn't Responding xDrip+ throws 'isn't responding' errors every few minutes, even after clearing settings and updating to the most current nightly. The app works and readings are received, but the warning pops up about every 30 seconds regardless of the app in use. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that incorrect or non-recommended settings may be the cause, and that every instance of this error has been addressed by adjusting xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required. Adjust xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required, using recommended settings. For Dexcom, ensure settings match the G5 Recommended Settings wiki. For Libre/MiaoMiao, ask for recommended settings in support channels. Additionally, enabling 'Save Database Daily' and setting 'Glucose Retention' to 90 days may help by shrinking the database. Dexcom G5 Libre 1 MiaoMiao 1 tomato libre 1 via miao mao 1 G5/G6 Debug Settings Force G5 to UI Thread So far, every instance of this error I have seen has been addressed by adjusting xDrip settings to only what is absolutely required. There was a Dexcom collector case where changing all the Bluetooth and G5/G6 Debug settings to recommended settings stopped the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1329", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1329, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1329, "title": "Support Libre Pro sensors", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1329", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1329", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User is trying to connect a Libre Pro sensor with a BluCon to xDrip+ latest nightly build. After initial calibration, xDrip gives a flat line of bg values (same value as calibrated).", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre Pro", "BluCon"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["BluCon", "LinkBluCon", "Tomato", "Miao Miao"], "evidence_quote": "But every time after I do the initial calibration, xdrip gives a flat line of bg values i.e. the same value I calibrated with What could I be doing wrong?", "text": "Support Libre Pro sensors User is trying to connect a Libre Pro sensor with a BluCon to xDrip+ latest nightly build. After initial calibration, xDrip gives a flat line of bg values (same value as calibrated).   Libre Pro BluCon BluCon LinkBluCon Tomato Miao Miao But every time after I do the initial calibration, xdrip gives a flat line of bg values i.e. the same value I calibrated with What could I be doing wrong?"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1335", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1335, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1335, "title": "libre 2 oop algorithm", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1335", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1335", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using the OOP algorithm with Libre 2, calibrated values are transferred to AndroidAPS, but uncalibrated values are transmitted to Nightscout, making evaluation or monitoring by Nightscout incorrect.", "cause": "The OOP algorithm cannot be calibrated, and the raw data from Libre 2 has a minimum value of 40, which prevents large intercept calibration. The thread also indicates that the issue is related to the calibration plugin not being applied to data sent to Nightscout.", "fix": "RainerTischnet describes a workaround: connect MM2 with xDrip, enable OOP algorithm, then in settings/advanced settings/advanced calibration choose 'xDrip original', calibrate, then export settings to XML, edit the XML to set 'calibrate_external_libre_algorithm' to true, import settings back, and set calibration plugin to none. This allows normal calibration to run with Nightscout and AAPS.", "settings_changed": ["calibrate_external_libre_algorithm → true", "calibration plugin → none"], "devices": ["Libre 2", "Libre-2", "Libre-1", "Libre1", "Libre2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["oop", "OOP", "MM2", "librelink patched", "xDrip original", "calibration plugin"], "evidence_quote": "the trick is: connect the mm2 with xdrip, enable oop algorithm. if you see the values. settings / advanced settings / advanced calibration choose xdrip original. back to the xdrip start desktop. then there should be a P now. now you have to calibrate first. then save import / export settings. settings on SD card. save all settings on sd card. I don't have an SD card. the backup can be found under download / xdrip-export. I use the total commander app to send the xml to google drive. then edit on pc xml with notepad ++ enable true at calibrate_external_libre_algorithm.", "text": "libre 2 oop algorithm When using the OOP algorithm with Libre 2, calibrated values are transferred to AndroidAPS, but uncalibrated values are transmitted to Nightscout, making evaluation or monitoring by Nightscout incorrect. The OOP algorithm cannot be calibrated, and the raw data from Libre 2 has a minimum value of 40, which prevents large intercept calibration. The thread also indicates that the issue is related to the calibration plugin not being applied to data sent to Nightscout. RainerTischnet describes a workaround: connect MM2 with xDrip, enable OOP algorithm, then in settings/advanced settings/advanced calibration choose 'xDrip original', calibrate, then export settings to XML, edit the XML to set 'calibrate_external_libre_algorithm' to true, import settings back, and set calibration plugin to none. This allows normal calibration to run with Nightscout and AAPS. Libre 2 Libre-2 Libre-1 Libre1 Libre2 oop OOP MM2 librelink patched xDrip original calibration plugin the trick is: connect the mm2 with xdrip, enable oop algorithm. if you see the values. settings / advanced settings / advanced calibration choose xdrip original. back to the xdrip start desktop. then there should be a P now. now you have to calibrate first. then save import / export settings. settings on SD card. save all settings on sd card. I don't have an SD card. the backup can be found under download / xdrip-export. I use the total commander app to send the xml to google drive. then edit on pc xml with notepad ++ enable true at calibrate_external_libre_algorithm."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1350", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1350, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1350, "title": "Libre-2: no options to save calibrated values neither to upload them to Nightscout. Help needed", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1350", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1350", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users with Libre-2 cannot calibrate sensor data or upload calibrated values to Nightscout; native values are always used, and calibration attempts are rejected or reset. The native readings are often much lower than finger prick values, and the +-20 mg/dl calibration limit is insufficient.", "cause": "The Libre-2 native data cannot be calibrated properly; OOP rejects calibrations and the patched app only allows a limited offset. The data table and Nightscout uploads contain only native values, not calibrated ones.", "fix": "Calibration of Libre 2 is now possible using mm/blucon/bubble transmitters, as announced by tzachi-dar. Instructions are provided at the LibreOOPAlgorithm Gitter channel. The issue was closed as a duplicate, noting that sync of calibrated values is requested in #475 and will be merged with #1090.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre-2", "Libre 2", "MM2", "MM 1", "bubble", "blucon"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["OOP", "patched app", "mm/blucon/bubble", "plugin"], "evidence_quote": "We now have the possibility to calibrate libre 2 (using mm/blucon/bubble). Should also work on android 10.", "text": "Libre-2: no options to save calibrated values neither to upload them to Nightscout. Help needed Users with Libre-2 cannot calibrate sensor data or upload calibrated values to Nightscout; native values are always used, and calibration attempts are rejected or reset. The native readings are often much lower than finger prick values, and the +-20 mg/dl calibration limit is insufficient. The Libre-2 native data cannot be calibrated properly; OOP rejects calibrations and the patched app only allows a limited offset. The data table and Nightscout uploads contain only native values, not calibrated ones. Calibration of Libre 2 is now possible using mm/blucon/bubble transmitters, as announced by tzachi-dar. Instructions are provided at the LibreOOPAlgorithm Gitter channel. The issue was closed as a duplicate, noting that sync of calibrated values is requested in #475 and will be merged with #1090. Libre-2 Libre 2 MM2 MM 1 bubble blucon Android 10 OOP patched app mm/blucon/bubble plugin We now have the possibility to calibrate libre 2 (using mm/blucon/bubble). Should also work on android 10."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1360", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1360, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1360, "title": "xDrip notification cascading", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1360", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1360", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When swiping down from the top of the display, xDrip notifications are cascading (stacked) instead of being displayed as before. This behavior started with versions after February 14, 2020 and is reproducible on HTC U11 with Android 9.", "cause": "The issue is likely caused by commit 28d7b85 from PR #1101, as suggested by tolot27.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["HTC U11"], "android_versions": ["Android 9"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "It looks like it is caused by the commit 28d7b85 from PR #1101.", "text": "xDrip notification cascading When swiping down from the top of the display, xDrip notifications are cascading (stacked) instead of being displayed as before. This behavior started with versions after February 14, 2020 and is reproducible on HTC U11 with Android 9. The issue is likely caused by commit 28d7b85 from PR #1101, as suggested by tolot27.  HTC U11 Android 9  It looks like it is caused by the commit 28d7b85 from PR #1101."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1371", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1371, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1371, "title": "Calibration for Freestyle Libre2 not working any more", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1371", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1371", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After migrating to Freestyle Libre2 using Bluetooth, calibration is fixed at a slope of 1.0, which does not match the user's experience. Slopes up to 1.6 are not properly covered by xDrip+, leading to poor insulin administration.", "cause": "The calibration for Freestyle Libre2 is fixed at a slope of 1.0, which is incorrect for the user's sensor data.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by using a special version of xDrip (tzachi-dar's fork) along with OOP2, which allows calibration of Libre2. The user must install OOP2, then install the special xDrip version, choose 'libre bluetooth' as the sensor, start the sensor, scan it, and after about 15 minutes a calibration prompt appears.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Freestyle Libre2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["libre bluetooth", "OOP2", "patched app"], "evidence_quote": "We now have the possibility to calibrate libre 2 (using mm/blucon/bubble).", "text": "Calibration for Freestyle Libre2 not working any more After migrating to Freestyle Libre2 using Bluetooth, calibration is fixed at a slope of 1.0, which does not match the user's experience. Slopes up to 1.6 are not properly covered by xDrip+, leading to poor insulin administration. The calibration for Freestyle Libre2 is fixed at a slope of 1.0, which is incorrect for the user's sensor data. The issue was resolved by using a special version of xDrip (tzachi-dar's fork) along with OOP2, which allows calibration of Libre2. The user must install OOP2, then install the special xDrip version, choose 'libre bluetooth' as the sensor, start the sensor, scan it, and after about 15 minutes a calibration prompt appears. Freestyle Libre2 libre bluetooth OOP2 patched app We now have the possibility to calibrate libre 2 (using mm/blucon/bubble)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1374", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1374, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1374, "title": "Decreased G6 capture rate due to Corona/Covid 19 exposure API", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1374", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1374", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After installing Germany's official Covid 19 exposure notification app, capture rate has decreased significantly down to from 1 reading in 20 minutes at best, though it's usually at 1 reading per hour. The logs imply multiple things not working: unable to connect, invalid authentication, or invalid keep alive requests.", "cause": "The issue is likely caused by time sensitive interference with Google's exposure notification framework, as suggested by the user and the German Corona App developers. However, the exact root cause is not definitively established; it appears to be related to the Bluetooth changes introduced by Google for the Corona App.", "fix": "The issue may be resolved by updating to the November 15, 2020 nightly build (fixing #1494) as reported by t1dast, or by enabling both 'minimize scanning' and 'avoid scanning' options in xDrip settings as suggested by jamorham. However, Gimbli74 reported that the November 15 build did not work for them, and the issue was closed due to inactivity.", "settings_changed": ["Minimize Scanning → off (tried, reduced problem)", "minimize scanning → on (suggested)", "avoid scanning → on (suggested)"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 8", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["patched G6 app", "companion app"], "evidence_quote": "After the November 15 update fixing #1494, I turned on the tracing again and it has not caused any trouble with the capture rate for 15 hrs, as opposed to my previous test three weeks ago. Finally, I think the problem might be solved :)", "text": "Decreased G6 capture rate due to Corona/Covid 19 exposure API After installing Germany's official Covid 19 exposure notification app, capture rate has decreased significantly down to from 1 reading in 20 minutes at best, though it's usually at 1 reading per hour. The logs imply multiple things not working: unable to connect, invalid authentication, or invalid keep alive requests. The issue is likely caused by time sensitive interference with Google's exposure notification framework, as suggested by the user and the German Corona App developers. However, the exact root cause is not definitively established; it appears to be related to the Bluetooth changes introduced by Google for the Corona App. The issue may be resolved by updating to the November 15, 2020 nightly build (fixing #1494) as reported by t1dast, or by enabling both 'minimize scanning' and 'avoid scanning' options in xDrip settings as suggested by jamorham. However, Gimbli74 reported that the November 15 build did not work for them, and the issue was closed due to inactivity. Dexcom G6 Android 10 Android 8 Android 9 patched G6 app companion app After the November 15 update fixing #1494, I turned on the tracing again and it has not caused any trouble with the capture rate for 15 hrs, as opposed to my previous test three weeks ago. Finally, I think the problem might be solved :)"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1392", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1392, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1392, "title": "[Feature Request] Offset for first 24 hours on restarted G6 sensor", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1392", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1392", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "On a restarted G6 sensor, the first 24 hours of readings are consistently out by +2 mmol/l, which can cause closed loop systems to overdose insulin.", "cause": "The thread discusses that the offset is likely due to trauma compensation required for new sensors, but for restarted sensors it is not helpful. It is not a simple constant offset but likely a slow decay or logarithmic decrease.", "fix": "No fix was implemented. The maintainers advise against restarting G6 sensors and recommend calibrating after a restart instead of applying a fixed offset.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["G6 Native"], "evidence_quote": "The safest course of action is not to restart. If you choose to restart, the safest course of action is to calibrate.", "text": "[Feature Request] Offset for first 24 hours on restarted G6 sensor On a restarted G6 sensor, the first 24 hours of readings are consistently out by +2 mmol/l, which can cause closed loop systems to overdose insulin. The thread discusses that the offset is likely due to trauma compensation required for new sensors, but for restarted sensors it is not helpful. It is not a simple constant offset but likely a slow decay or logarithmic decrease. No fix was implemented. The maintainers advise against restarting G6 sensors and recommend calibrating after a restart instead of applying a fixed offset. G6 G6 Native The safest course of action is not to restart. If you choose to restart, the safest course of action is to calibrate."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1394", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1394, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1394, "title": "Libre 2 - (xDrip+ + LibreLink patched) vs. (xDrip+ + MiaoMiao2)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1394", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1394", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User asks which method gives more accurate results for the FreeStyle Libre 2: LibreLink 2.3 patched app with xDrip+ or MiaoMiao2 with xDrip+. Later commenters report Libre 2 not working with MiaoMiao transmitters (e.g., 'Checksum failed', no data) and ask for instructions to use the patched app.", "cause": "The thread concludes the MiaoMiao transmitter is unnecessary and less accurate with Libre 2. The MiaoMiao2 approach has a great disadvantage of false 'calibrations' in xDrip+, and MiaoMiao transmitters can fail to work with Libre 2 (Checksum failed / no data). Libre 2 can transmit directly to xDrip+ through a patched LibreLink app.", "fix": "Use the patched LibreLink app with xDrip+ instead of a MiaoMiao transmitter. Start the sensor with the patched app; no extra transmitter is needed. Guides referenced include LibreLink-xDrip-Patch and AndroidAPS xDrip Libre documentation.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["FreeStyle Libre 2", "MiaoMiao2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["librelink patched", "oopalgorithm", "direct connection"], "evidence_quote": "Nowadays, having used the patched app for months and comparing it with my first results using Libre 2 + MM2, I can strongly assure that **THE PATCHED APP GIVES FAR BETTER RESULTS than the MM2**, having this last one as a great disadvantage the false \"calibrations\" in xDrip+.", "text": "Libre 2 - (xDrip+ + LibreLink patched) vs. (xDrip+ + MiaoMiao2) User asks which method gives more accurate results for the FreeStyle Libre 2: LibreLink 2.3 patched app with xDrip+ or MiaoMiao2 with xDrip+. Later commenters report Libre 2 not working with MiaoMiao transmitters (e.g., 'Checksum failed', no data) and ask for instructions to use the patched app. The thread concludes the MiaoMiao transmitter is unnecessary and less accurate with Libre 2. The MiaoMiao2 approach has a great disadvantage of false 'calibrations' in xDrip+, and MiaoMiao transmitters can fail to work with Libre 2 (Checksum failed / no data). Libre 2 can transmit directly to xDrip+ through a patched LibreLink app. Use the patched LibreLink app with xDrip+ instead of a MiaoMiao transmitter. Start the sensor with the patched app; no extra transmitter is needed. Guides referenced include LibreLink-xDrip-Patch and AndroidAPS xDrip Libre documentation. FreeStyle Libre 2 MiaoMiao2 librelink patched oopalgorithm direct connection Nowadays, having used the patched app for months and comparing it with my first results using Libre 2 + MM2, I can strongly assure that **THE PATCHED APP GIVES FAR BETTER RESULTS than the MM2**, having this last one as a great disadvantage the false \"calibrations\" in xDrip+."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1411", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1411, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1411, "title": "xDrip lost connection to sensor and forgot any past values", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1411", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1411", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "xDrip was running fine for a very long time. Suddenly it lost the connection to the G6 in the middle of the night. A simple \"restart collector\" fixed the issue. But it also forgot the whole history.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": ["Glucose Retention → 99 days", "Extra tags for logging → DailyIntentService:v,DatabaseUtil:v,UserError:v,BgReading:v"], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I changed retention to 99 days now.", "text": "xDrip lost connection to sensor and forgot any past values xDrip was running fine for a very long time. Suddenly it lost the connection to the G6 in the middle of the night. A simple \"restart collector\" fixed the issue. But it also forgot the whole history.   G6  I changed retention to 99 days now."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1415", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1415, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1415, "title": "Unable to fully perform calibration on 8K series G6 transmitter with latest nightly (67014b0-20202.07.25)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1415", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1415", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "All attempts to calibrate result in 'Got invalid impossible slope calibration!'. The calibration is accepted by the transmitter but xdrip doesn't register as such and stays in 'initial calibration' stage. Was working on previous transmitter (81 series).", "cause": "The issue is caused by the Firefly firmware (8G and later transmitters) in combination with xDrip, which has limitations on calibration when the difference between current BG and calibration value is too large (more than 15-20%). Additionally, xDrip issues confusing messages when calibrating an 8KXXXX transmitter, and the calibration command is called initial calibration even for subsequent calibrations.", "fix": "Workaround: calibrate in MAX 20% steps and wait at least 12 hours between calibrations. Also, use the syringe icon for entering calibrations and follow settings as per issue #1310. The thread does not provide a definitive fix; it suggests that the confusing messages need to be addressed by developers.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6", "8K series G6 transmitter", "81 series"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode", "Firefly firmware"], "evidence_quote": "You cannot calibrate with too big differences of current BG vs the calibration value. As a rule of thumb don't enter calibrations with more than 15-20% difference. This is a limitation of the Firefly firmware (8G and later transmitters) in combination with xDrip (unfortunately). Workaround if your real BG is *really* that far off => calibrate in MAX 20% steps and always wait a few hours until the next calibration.", "text": "Unable to fully perform calibration on 8K series G6 transmitter with latest nightly (67014b0-20202.07.25) All attempts to calibrate result in 'Got invalid impossible slope calibration!'. The calibration is accepted by the transmitter but xdrip doesn't register as such and stays in 'initial calibration' stage. Was working on previous transmitter (81 series). The issue is caused by the Firefly firmware (8G and later transmitters) in combination with xDrip, which has limitations on calibration when the difference between current BG and calibration value is too large (more than 15-20%). Additionally, xDrip issues confusing messages when calibrating an 8KXXXX transmitter, and the calibration command is called initial calibration even for subsequent calibrations. Workaround: calibrate in MAX 20% steps and wait at least 12 hours between calibrations. Also, use the syringe icon for entering calibrations and follow settings as per issue #1310. The thread does not provide a definitive fix; it suggests that the confusing messages need to be addressed by developers. G6 8K series G6 transmitter 81 series native mode Firefly firmware You cannot calibrate with too big differences of current BG vs the calibration value. As a rule of thumb don't enter calibrations with more than 15-20% difference. This is a limitation of the Firefly firmware (8G and later transmitters) in combination with xDrip (unfortunately). Workaround if your real BG is *really* that far off => calibrate in MAX 20% steps and always wait a few hours until the next calibration."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1416", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1416, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1416, "title": "FR: Last day to start, or restart, a sensor (effectively, transmitter expiry) notification", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1416", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1416", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Users often start a new sensor and wait through the 2-hour warm-up only to find it doesn't work because they have passed day 99 of the transmitter's life. There is no warning to inform them of the last day they can start or restart a sensor.", "cause": "The transmitter will not start a brand new sensor after day 99 (and 23 hours and 59 minutes), even though the transmitter itself expires on day 110. Users are unaware of this limitation and may attempt to start a sensor too late.", "fix": "The issue was closed as a nice-to-have, not a necessity. No specific fix was implemented.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Closing this as it is a nice-to-have, not a necessity.", "text": "FR: Last day to start, or restart, a sensor (effectively, transmitter expiry) notification Users often start a new sensor and wait through the 2-hour warm-up only to find it doesn't work because they have passed day 99 of the transmitter's life. There is no warning to inform them of the last day they can start or restart a sensor. The transmitter will not start a brand new sensor after day 99 (and 23 hours and 59 minutes), even though the transmitter itself expires on day 110. Users are unaware of this limitation and may attempt to start a sensor too late. The issue was closed as a nice-to-have, not a necessity. No specific fix was implemented. Dexcom  Closing this as it is a nice-to-have, not a necessity."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1418", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1418, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1418, "title": "Alarm sounds continuously", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1418", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1418", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The app's alarm sounds continuously instead of sounding once then repeating only as configured by the 'Re-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged' setting. Clicking the notification or selecting a snooze time does not stop the alarm. One user reports the continuous sound only occurs on alerts with both 'Override Phone Silent' and 'Force Speaker' enabled.", "cause": null, "fix": "Upgrade to a xDrip release after April 12, 2022; the reporter confirmed the issue appears fixed in later releases. No exact code fix is described in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S10"], "android_versions": ["Android Version 11", "Android 6", "Android 8", "Android 9", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "This appears to be fixed in later releases. Thanks for the support!", "text": "Alarm sounds continuously The app's alarm sounds continuously instead of sounding once then repeating only as configured by the 'Re-raise every x minutes if unacknowledged' setting. Clicking the notification or selecting a snooze time does not stop the alarm. One user reports the continuous sound only occurs on alerts with both 'Override Phone Silent' and 'Force Speaker' enabled.  Upgrade to a xDrip release after April 12, 2022; the reporter confirmed the issue appears fixed in later releases. No exact code fix is described in the thread. Samsung Galaxy S10 Android Version 11 Android 6 Android 8 Android 9 Android 11  This appears to be fixed in later releases. Thanks for the support!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1427", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1427, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1427, "title": "Miband 4 - Bug Report: Screen Brightness", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1427", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1427", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The screen goes dark for the watch face upload (as intended) but after that it stays dark for about 20s to 60s. It seems to switch back to day mode when the next full minute is reached.", "cause": "The phone can't wake up in time after the thread was sent to sleep during the 7-second delay before restoring screen brightness.", "fix": "The issue is solved in the build available at https://bigdigital.home.blog, and the fix is part of PR #1659 which is not merged yet.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Miband", "Mi Smart Band 4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["miband"], "evidence_quote": "Indeed, seems that your phone can't \"wakeup\" in time after the thread was sent to sleep. I'll try to implement this delay in another way and share a test application again.", "text": "Miband 4 - Bug Report: Screen Brightness The screen goes dark for the watch face upload (as intended) but after that it stays dark for about 20s to 60s. It seems to switch back to day mode when the next full minute is reached. The phone can't wake up in time after the thread was sent to sleep during the 7-second delay before restoring screen brightness. The issue is solved in the build available at https://bigdigital.home.blog, and the fix is part of PR #1659 which is not merged yet. Miband Mi Smart Band 4 miband Indeed, seems that your phone can't \"wakeup\" in time after the thread was sent to sleep. I'll try to implement this delay in another way and share a test application again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1430", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1430, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1430, "title": "Implement the receiption of scanned Libre 2 values via patched LibreLink", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1430", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1430", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The patched LibreLink sends an Intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' with scanned values (historic and realtime), but xDrip+ does not accept this intent, leaving a gap that could be filled with scanned values.", "cause": "xDrip+ does not implement reception of the SENSOR_SCAN intent from the patched LibreLink; the intent lacks the current 15 minute-by-minute values, and the patch cannot be modified by others.", "fix": "No fix implemented; issue closed as not feasible because the vendor app patch cannot be modified by others and Libre 2 EU is being phased out.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["patched LibreLink", "SENSOR_SCAN intent"], "evidence_quote": "I don't think the vendor app patch can be modified by anyone else than the original team. And I'm pretty sure they won't be working on it since there are other solutions available, furthermore as Libre 2 EU will slowly disappear for Libre 3.", "text": "Implement the receiption of scanned Libre 2 values via patched LibreLink The patched LibreLink sends an Intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' with scanned values (historic and realtime), but xDrip+ does not accept this intent, leaving a gap that could be filled with scanned values. xDrip+ does not implement reception of the SENSOR_SCAN intent from the patched LibreLink; the intent lacks the current 15 minute-by-minute values, and the patch cannot be modified by others. No fix implemented; issue closed as not feasible because the vendor app patch cannot be modified by others and Libre 2 EU is being phased out. Libre 2 patched LibreLink SENSOR_SCAN intent I don't think the vendor app patch can be modified by anyone else than the original team. And I'm pretty sure they won't be working on it since there are other solutions available, furthermore as Libre 2 EU will slowly disappear for Libre 3."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1436", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1436, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1436, "title": "problems writing to influxDB", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1436", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1436", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Writing to InfluxDB on a Raspberry Pi 4 with authentication fails with a NullPointerException about okhttpUrl.host() on a null object reference, despite entering the IP address, port, and auth.", "cause": "The InfluxDB URI was entered with curly braces around the IP and port (e.g., http://{192.168.1.xxx}:{8086}), which is not a valid URL and causes a parsing problem.", "fix": "Remove the curly braces from the InfluxDB URI so it is a valid URL (e.g., http://192.168.1.xxx:8086).", "settings_changed": ["InfluxDB URI → http://192.168.1.xxx:8086 (curly braces removed)"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["influxdb"], "evidence_quote": "`http://{192.168.1.xxx}:{8086}` is not a valid URL. Please remove the curly brackets (`{`, `}`) and try it again.", "text": "problems writing to influxDB Writing to InfluxDB on a Raspberry Pi 4 with authentication fails with a NullPointerException about okhttpUrl.host() on a null object reference, despite entering the IP address, port, and auth. The InfluxDB URI was entered with curly braces around the IP and port (e.g., http://{192.168.1.xxx}:{8086}), which is not a valid URL and causes a parsing problem. Remove the curly braces from the InfluxDB URI so it is a valid URL (e.g., http://192.168.1.xxx:8086).  influxdb `http://{192.168.1.xxx}:{8086}` is not a valid URL. Please remove the curly brackets (`{`, `}`) and try it again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1438", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1438, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1438, "title": "failed to register application for bluetooth scan during reconnect to BlueJay watch", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1438", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1438", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After the BlueJay watch was in range of the phone, no values were transferred to xDrip. A scan in the BlueJay Admin panel is not successful and prints the error 'Failed to register application for bluetooth scan' with BleScanException code 6. The issue occurs during reconnect after the watch has been out of range for a while.", "cause": "The Bluetooth of the Android phone has crashed, and a restart is often the only way to fix it. The issue is likely a problem with xDrip, as it worked previously and no OS updates were performed.", "fix": "Restarting the phone resolves the issue. Disabling and enabling Bluetooth allows the scan to work but does not restore data transfer. The maintainer suggests that a restart is often the only way to fix the crashed Bluetooth.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["BlueJay", "Libre Honor 7s"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1.0"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth scan", "ScanMeister"], "evidence_quote": "This probably means the bluetooth of your android phone has crashed, a restart is often the only way to fix it.", "text": "failed to register application for bluetooth scan during reconnect to BlueJay watch After the BlueJay watch was in range of the phone, no values were transferred to xDrip. A scan in the BlueJay Admin panel is not successful and prints the error 'Failed to register application for bluetooth scan' with BleScanException code 6. The issue occurs during reconnect after the watch has been out of range for a while. The Bluetooth of the Android phone has crashed, and a restart is often the only way to fix it. The issue is likely a problem with xDrip, as it worked previously and no OS updates were performed. Restarting the phone resolves the issue. Disabling and enabling Bluetooth allows the scan to work but does not restore data transfer. The maintainer suggests that a restart is often the only way to fix the crashed Bluetooth. BlueJay Libre Honor 7s Android 8.1.0 bluetooth scan ScanMeister This probably means the bluetooth of your android phone has crashed, a restart is often the only way to fix it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1441", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1441, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1441, "title": "Xdrip+ mi band 4", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1441", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1441", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "We connected xdrip and mi band 4, xdrip find it but it doesn't show readings on the screen except that sometimes the alarm goes off when on the phone.", "cause": null, "fix": "For the issue of not finding the band in the modified version, bigdigital suggests to regenerate auth code and connect the band from scratch: open patched MiFit app, unpair the band, delete all files in /sdcard/freemyband, pair again, then in xdrip miband menu switch off 'Use miband', clear 'mac address' and 'auth key', switch on 'Use miband', and ensure the mac address is correct. For the issue of 'Update BG manually' failing, Otter3eso57 suggests enabling or disabling the 'high MTU value' option under Settings->Smart Watch Features->MiBand, which resolved it for klettervirus.", "settings_changed": ["Use miband → off then on", "mac address → cleared", "auth key → cleared", "high MTU value → enabled/disabled"], "devices": ["mi band 4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["MiBand", "MiFit", "freemyband"], "evidence_quote": "have you tried enabling or disabling the \"high MTU value\" option under Settings->Smart Watch Features->MiBand?", "text": "Xdrip+ mi band 4 We connected xdrip and mi band 4, xdrip find it but it doesn't show readings on the screen except that sometimes the alarm goes off when on the phone.  For the issue of not finding the band in the modified version, bigdigital suggests to regenerate auth code and connect the band from scratch: open patched MiFit app, unpair the band, delete all files in /sdcard/freemyband, pair again, then in xdrip miband menu switch off 'Use miband', clear 'mac address' and 'auth key', switch on 'Use miband', and ensure the mac address is correct. For the issue of 'Update BG manually' failing, Otter3eso57 suggests enabling or disabling the 'high MTU value' option under Settings->Smart Watch Features->MiBand, which resolved it for klettervirus. mi band 4 MiBand MiFit freemyband have you tried enabling or disabling the \"high MTU value\" option under Settings->Smart Watch Features->MiBand?"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1442", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1442, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1442, "title": "Xdrip dropping Miaomiao connection", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1442", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1442", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After a reasonably long period running relatively smoothly, I am now losing Bluetooth connection to my Miaomiao every hour or two. Restarting Bluetooth and clearing the cache works temporarily. The Xdrip connection to my Miband also fails at the same time and reverts to the standard watchface until connection is remade.", "cause": "The Miaomiao connection problems were traced to the UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app causing Bluetooth conflicts.", "fix": "The user resolved the Miaomiao connection issue by identifying the UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app as the cause of Bluetooth conflicts. The Miband connection issue was solved in the latest release.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Miaomiao", "Miband 4", "Libre 1"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "Miaomiao connection problems traced to UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app causing Bluetooth conflicts.", "text": "Xdrip dropping Miaomiao connection After a reasonably long period running relatively smoothly, I am now losing Bluetooth connection to my Miaomiao every hour or two. Restarting Bluetooth and clearing the cache works temporarily. The Xdrip connection to my Miband also fails at the same time and reverts to the standard watchface until connection is remade. The Miaomiao connection problems were traced to the UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app causing Bluetooth conflicts. The user resolved the Miaomiao connection issue by identifying the UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app as the cause of Bluetooth conflicts. The Miband connection issue was solved in the latest release. Miaomiao Miband 4 Libre 1 Android 10 Bluetooth Miaomiao connection problems traced to UK Gov NHS Covid tracking app causing Bluetooth conflicts."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1446", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1446, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1446, "title": "Bug report: Miao2 & Miband bluetooth conection problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1446", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1446", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "xDrip loses Bluetooth connection to Miao Miao 2 or Mi Band 5 usually once every two days, and it never reconnects automatically. The user has to manually reconnect via the 'Bluetooth Scan' menu.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Miao Miao 2", "Mi Band 5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["miband"], "evidence_quote": "Xdrip loses bluetooth Miao Miao 2 or Mi band5 usally one time in two days. And it never connect it again by it self. I have to connect it again in 'Bluetooth Scan' menu.", "text": "Bug report: Miao2 & Miband bluetooth conection problem xDrip loses Bluetooth connection to Miao Miao 2 or Mi Band 5 usually once every two days, and it never reconnects automatically. The user has to manually reconnect via the 'Bluetooth Scan' menu.   Miao Miao 2 Mi Band 5 miband Xdrip loses bluetooth Miao Miao 2 or Mi band5 usally one time in two days. And it never connect it again by it self. I have to connect it again in 'Bluetooth Scan' menu."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-145", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 145, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 145, "title": "Huawei SmartWatch as a collector", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/145", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/145", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user reports that the Huawei SmartWatch does not work as a standalone collector for xDrip+ with the G5 sensor, despite trying various debug settings.", "cause": "The thread indicates that the G5 BT settings need to be set on the watch itself, not on the phone, and that the watch may require ROM patches to work correctly with the G5.", "fix": "The fix is to apply patches to the Huawei watch's ROM as described in the provided 'care pack' and PDF guide, which makes the watch work correctly with the G5.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Huawei SmartWatch", "G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["G5", "watch collector", "BT settings"], "evidence_quote": "The Huawei watch is now supported but you will need to apply patches to its rom to make it work correctly. First step is to download the \"care pack\" I have provided and look at the PDF guide for instructions of how to do it.", "text": "Huawei SmartWatch as a collector The user reports that the Huawei SmartWatch does not work as a standalone collector for xDrip+ with the G5 sensor, despite trying various debug settings. The thread indicates that the G5 BT settings need to be set on the watch itself, not on the phone, and that the watch may require ROM patches to work correctly with the G5. The fix is to apply patches to the Huawei watch's ROM as described in the provided 'care pack' and PDF guide, which makes the watch work correctly with the G5. Huawei SmartWatch G5 G5 watch collector BT settings The Huawei watch is now supported but you will need to apply patches to its rom to make it work correctly. First step is to download the \"care pack\" I have provided and look at the PDF guide for instructions of how to do it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1453", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1453, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1453, "title": "shift of calibration point in graph", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1453", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1453", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When entering a calibration reading, the red dot (calibration point) on the xDrip graph appears shifted about 10 minutes later than the actual time, even though the time information shows the current time. The user asks if this is due to the Libre's delay or a bug.", "cause": "The delay is intentional. The graph displays all data in terms of the delayed interstitial fluid response, so blood glucose readings are shifted to align with the Libre readings, even if not used for calibration.", "fix": "No fix was provided; the behavior is intentional. The thread suggests that a tutorial screen might be needed to inform users, and there is discussion of possibly allowing the main screen to show current/estimated BG values instead, but no code change was made.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Miao Miao 2", "Libre", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode"], "evidence_quote": "The delay is intentional.", "text": "shift of calibration point in graph When entering a calibration reading, the red dot (calibration point) on the xDrip graph appears shifted about 10 minutes later than the actual time, even though the time information shows the current time. The user asks if this is due to the Libre's delay or a bug. The delay is intentional. The graph displays all data in terms of the delayed interstitial fluid response, so blood glucose readings are shifted to align with the Libre readings, even if not used for calibration. No fix was provided; the behavior is intentional. The thread suggests that a tutorial screen might be needed to inform users, and there is discussion of possibly allowing the main screen to show current/estimated BG values instead, but no code change was made. Miao Miao 2 Libre Dexcom G6 native mode The delay is intentional."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1459", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1459, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1459, "title": "Android 10 (LOS17) no connection to transmitter: \"No valid timestamp stored for transmitter: 8K****\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1459", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1459", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After attempting to extend sensor life by stopping the sensor after disabling Bluetooth, the OB Collector fails to bond with the transmitter, logging 'No valid timestamp stored for transmitter: 8K****' and showing 'Scanning Errors' every 5 minutes. Restarting collector, rebooting phone, forgetting transmitter, and reinstalling xDrip+ did not fix it.", "cause": "The invalid timestamp log is a symptom of not having proper connectivity established between the device and the transmitter, requiring correction of xDrip settings. The thread also suggests that stopping the sensor after disabling Bluetooth may have caused the transmitter to stop working.", "fix": "One user resolved it by starting a new sensor through a modified version of the official Dexcom app (remove xDrip+ first), then deinstalling that app and reinstalling xDrip+. Another maintainer suggests correcting xDrip settings and provides links to Facebook group and Gitter for detailed instructions.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["OB Collector"], "evidence_quote": "The invalid timestap log is a symptom of not having proper connectivity established between the device and the transmitter. It requires correcting the xDrip settings.", "text": "Android 10 (LOS17) no connection to transmitter: \"No valid timestamp stored for transmitter: 8K****\" After attempting to extend sensor life by stopping the sensor after disabling Bluetooth, the OB Collector fails to bond with the transmitter, logging 'No valid timestamp stored for transmitter: 8K****' and showing 'Scanning Errors' every 5 minutes. Restarting collector, rebooting phone, forgetting transmitter, and reinstalling xDrip+ did not fix it. The invalid timestamp log is a symptom of not having proper connectivity established between the device and the transmitter, requiring correction of xDrip settings. The thread also suggests that stopping the sensor after disabling Bluetooth may have caused the transmitter to stop working. One user resolved it by starting a new sensor through a modified version of the official Dexcom app (remove xDrip+ first), then deinstalling that app and reinstalling xDrip+. Another maintainer suggests correcting xDrip settings and provides links to Facebook group and Gitter for detailed instructions. Dexcom G6 Android 10 OB Collector The invalid timestap log is a symptom of not having proper connectivity established between the device and the transmitter. It requires correcting the xDrip settings."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1474", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1474, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1474, "title": "Freestyle Libre 3 support", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1474", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1474", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User reports Freestyle Libre 3 launched in Europe providing readings through Bluetooth instead of NFC, and asks if there is any move to support it.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Freestyle Libre 3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "nfc", "native", "oop external app"], "evidence_quote": "It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app.", "text": "Freestyle Libre 3 support User reports Freestyle Libre 3 launched in Europe providing readings through Bluetooth instead of NFC, and asks if there is any move to support it.   Freestyle Libre 3 bluetooth nfc native oop external app It is unlikely that xDrip will support L3, natively. Likely, it will be implemented similar to L2 OOP external app."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1477", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1477, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1477, "title": "upload basal rate to Tidepool", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1477", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1477", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Basal rate information is not uploaded to Tidepool from xDrip, even though other data syncs correctly. Users report that basal injections appear as bolus injections in Tidepool, and some users do not see basal rates at all.", "cause": "The issue was initially thought to be on the Tidepool side, as Tidepool had not yet supported basal uploads in Blip. Later, it was implemented/activated in xDrip with commit 5058163 and released with version 2022.04.30.", "fix": "Update xDrip to version 2022.04.30 or later, which includes the implementation/activation of basal rate upload to Tidepool.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tidepool"], "evidence_quote": "This was implemented/activated with 5058163 and released with [2022.04.30](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2022.04.30).", "text": "upload basal rate to Tidepool Basal rate information is not uploaded to Tidepool from xDrip, even though other data syncs correctly. Users report that basal injections appear as bolus injections in Tidepool, and some users do not see basal rates at all. The issue was initially thought to be on the Tidepool side, as Tidepool had not yet supported basal uploads in Blip. Later, it was implemented/activated in xDrip with commit 5058163 and released with version 2022.04.30. Update xDrip to version 2022.04.30 or later, which includes the implementation/activation of basal rate upload to Tidepool.  tidepool This was implemented/activated with 5058163 and released with [2022.04.30](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2022.04.30)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1479", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1479, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1479, "title": "Bolus Calculator on Xdrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1479", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1479", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user asks if there is a bolus calculator function in the app, suggesting a feature to input carbs and show insulin dose based on carb ratio.", "cause": null, "fix": "Enable the 'show insulin / carbo ratio' option to see the bolus estimation. Also, enable 'Predictive Simulation' and 'Show Bolus Wizard Preview'.", "settings_changed": ["show insulin / carbo ratio → enabled", "Predictive Simulation → enabled", "Show Bolus Wizard Preview → enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "But I already found the setting, and I couldn't see it beacause I had to enable the \"show insulin / carbo ratio\" option.", "text": "Bolus Calculator on Xdrip The user asks if there is a bolus calculator function in the app, suggesting a feature to input carbs and show insulin dose based on carb ratio.  Enable the 'show insulin / carbo ratio' option to see the bolus estimation. Also, enable 'Predictive Simulation' and 'Show Bolus Wizard Preview'.   But I already found the setting, and I couldn't see it beacause I had to enable the \"show insulin / carbo ratio\" option."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-148", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 148, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 148, "title": "Spoken reading for partially sighted users", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/148", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/148", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A partially sighted user requests an easy way to hear their blood glucose reading and trend on demand, e.g., by pressing and holding the home button, because continuous speech every five minutes would be annoying.", "cause": null, "fix": "Tasker support was added in the Jan 1st Nightly, allowing speaking the current reading, switching speaking readings on/off, and switching speaking of alerts on/off via the 'SPEAK NOW' configuration button from tasker 3rd party plugins.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tasker"], "evidence_quote": "The Jan 1st Nightly includes Tasker support for speaking the current reading, switching speaking readings on/off and also switching speaking of alerts on/off. See the `SPEAK NOW` configuration button from tasker 3rd party plugins and the other related ones.", "text": "Spoken reading for partially sighted users A partially sighted user requests an easy way to hear their blood glucose reading and trend on demand, e.g., by pressing and holding the home button, because continuous speech every five minutes would be annoying.  Tasker support was added in the Jan 1st Nightly, allowing speaking the current reading, switching speaking readings on/off, and switching speaking of alerts on/off via the 'SPEAK NOW' configuration button from tasker 3rd party plugins. Dexcom G4 tasker The Jan 1st Nightly includes Tasker support for speaking the current reading, switching speaking readings on/off and also switching speaking of alerts on/off. See the `SPEAK NOW` configuration button from tasker 3rd party plugins and the other related ones."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1486", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1486, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1486, "title": "notification for Dexcom transmitter expiry", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1486", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1486", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users want a notification for Dexcom transmitter expiry similar to the Dexcom receiver's four and two week warnings. One user wasted a sensor because they were not notified that the transmitter needed replacement after 3 months.", "cause": null, "fix": "The issue was addressed by adding a warning when starting a sensor close to transmitter end of life, as described in the closing comment: 'Starting a sensor, as you get close to transmitter end of life, you will get a warning that your transmitter will not work soon providing detail about when.'", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Starting a sensor, as you get close to transmitter end of life, you will get a warning that your transmitter will not work soon providing detail about when.", "text": "notification for Dexcom transmitter expiry Users want a notification for Dexcom transmitter expiry similar to the Dexcom receiver's four and two week warnings. One user wasted a sensor because they were not notified that the transmitter needed replacement after 3 months.  The issue was addressed by adding a warning when starting a sensor close to transmitter end of life, as described in the closing comment: 'Starting a sensor, as you get close to transmitter end of life, you will get a warning that your transmitter will not work soon providing detail about when.' Dexcom G6  Starting a sensor, as you get close to transmitter end of life, you will get a warning that your transmitter will not work soon providing detail about when."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1489", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1489, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1489, "title": "Freestyle Libre1 + Miaomiao1 + xDrip Connection problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1489", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1489", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user reports frequent disconnections between Freestyle Libre1 and Miaomiao1, with xDrip showing 'No sensor has been found' errors. The issue persists across multiple sensors and firmware updates, and sometimes requires resetting the Miaomiao1.", "cause": "The thread suggests the problem is likely a defective Miaomiao1 device, as the issue occurs with multiple sensors and also with the Tomato app, indicating it is not an xDrip issue.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a definitive fix. The users contacted the vendor for a replacement, and one user reported that after swimming with Miao2 they had a similar problem, but with Miao1 it was okay.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Freestyle Libre1", "Miaomiao1", "Miaomiao2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["miaomiao", "tomato"], "evidence_quote": "If Tomato doesn't work neither it's a device issue to be addressed by the vendor. Not here.", "text": "Freestyle Libre1 + Miaomiao1 + xDrip Connection problem The user reports frequent disconnections between Freestyle Libre1 and Miaomiao1, with xDrip showing 'No sensor has been found' errors. The issue persists across multiple sensors and firmware updates, and sometimes requires resetting the Miaomiao1. The thread suggests the problem is likely a defective Miaomiao1 device, as the issue occurs with multiple sensors and also with the Tomato app, indicating it is not an xDrip issue. The thread does not provide a definitive fix. The users contacted the vendor for a replacement, and one user reported that after swimming with Miao2 they had a similar problem, but with Miao1 it was okay. Freestyle Libre1 Miaomiao1 Miaomiao2 miaomiao tomato If Tomato doesn't work neither it's a device issue to be addressed by the vendor. Not here."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1491", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1491, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1491, "title": "Bluetooth issue (serious?)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1491", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1491", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Bluetooth connection breaks down after minutes to hours, causing hundreds of missed readings, and does not recover without deleting the Dexcom transmitter from the Bluetooth device list and restarting the phone. This started after switching to a Firefly transmitter.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Possible factors discussed include the Firefly transmitter behaving differently, OB1 authentication issues, and settings related to OB1 bonding.", "fix": "One user (Davud2020) reported that setting specific options resolved the issue: Settings-->G5/G6 Debug Settings: Use the OB1 Collector, Native Algorithm, Minimize Scanning, Avoid Scanning, G6 Support, Allow OB1 initiate bonding; and Less common settings-->Bluetooth Settings: Turn Bluetooth on, Bluetooth Watchdog, Trust Auto-Connect. However, the original reporter oblanke changed settings to match but did not confirm resolution before the issue was closed due to inactivity.", "settings_changed": ["Use the OB1 Collector → true", "Native Algorithm → true", "Minimize Scanning → true", "Avoid Scanning → true", "G6 Support → true", "Allow OB1 initiate bonding → true", "Turn Bluetooth on → true", "Bluetooth Watchdog → true", "Trust Auto-Connect → true"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Firefly transmitter", "Huawei P10", "Samsung Note 10+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1", "G5/G6", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "I had to setup. Settings-->G5/G6 Debug Settings Use the OB1 Collector Native Algorithm Minimize Scanning Avoid Scanning G6 Support Allow OB1 initiate bonding Less common settings-->Bluetooth Settings Turn Bluetooth on Bluetooth Watchdog Trust Auto-Connect", "text": "Bluetooth issue (serious?) Bluetooth connection breaks down after minutes to hours, causing hundreds of missed readings, and does not recover without deleting the Dexcom transmitter from the Bluetooth device list and restarting the phone. This started after switching to a Firefly transmitter. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Possible factors discussed include the Firefly transmitter behaving differently, OB1 authentication issues, and settings related to OB1 bonding. One user (Davud2020) reported that setting specific options resolved the issue: Settings-->G5/G6 Debug Settings: Use the OB1 Collector, Native Algorithm, Minimize Scanning, Avoid Scanning, G6 Support, Allow OB1 initiate bonding; and Less common settings-->Bluetooth Settings: Turn Bluetooth on, Bluetooth Watchdog, Trust Auto-Connect. However, the original reporter oblanke changed settings to match but did not confirm resolution before the issue was closed due to inactivity. Dexcom G6 Firefly transmitter Huawei P10 Samsung Note 10+ OB1 G5/G6 collector I had to setup. Settings-->G5/G6 Debug Settings Use the OB1 Collector Native Algorithm Minimize Scanning Avoid Scanning G6 Support Allow OB1 initiate bonding Less common settings-->Bluetooth Settings Turn Bluetooth on Bluetooth Watchdog Trust Auto-Connect"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1495", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1495, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1495, "title": "\"Samsung Workaround\" is set by default for all phones", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1495", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1495", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The 'Samsung Workaround' setting is enabled by default on non-Samsung phones, which is confusing and may cause connectivity issues for some users.", "cause": "The setting is enabled by default for all devices, but the actual workaround only activates on Samsung devices or specific models listed in the code. The default being on is not harmful, but it confuses users.", "fix": "No code change was made; the maintainer explained that the setting should be left enabled because the workaround only engages on Samsung devices. The issue was closed with the understanding that the setting is fine as default.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["source wizard", "samsung workaround", "buggy samsung"], "evidence_quote": "The `Buggy Samsung Workaround` feature doesn't engage unless the phone is a samsung (or specifically listed device) and the wakeup jitter is detected to be a problem. The setting `Samsung Workarounds` allows this to happen. The only effect of changing this setting to off would be to disable the workarounds on a samsung which is likely not a good thing to do.", "text": "\"Samsung Workaround\" is set by default for all phones The 'Samsung Workaround' setting is enabled by default on non-Samsung phones, which is confusing and may cause connectivity issues for some users. The setting is enabled by default for all devices, but the actual workaround only activates on Samsung devices or specific models listed in the code. The default being on is not harmful, but it confuses users. No code change was made; the maintainer explained that the setting should be left enabled because the workaround only engages on Samsung devices. The issue was closed with the understanding that the setting is fine as default. Dexcom G6 source wizard samsung workaround buggy samsung The `Buggy Samsung Workaround` feature doesn't engage unless the phone is a samsung (or specifically listed device) and the wakeup jitter is detected to be a problem. The setting `Samsung Workarounds` allows this to happen. The only effect of changing this setting to off would be to disable the workarounds on a samsung which is likely not a good thing to do."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1497", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1497, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1497, "title": "Buttons Silence alarms not working", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1497", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1497", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The 'Buttons silence alarms' feature is not working on a Samsung S10 Plus with Android 10, making it difficult to silence alarms at night. It used to work on an S7.", "cause": "Android restricts apps from capturing global button presses when the phone is locked or the app is not in the foreground, and newer Android versions have tightened these restrictions.", "fix": "Use the ascending volume profile as an alternative: Settings -> Alarms and Alerts -> Glucose Alerts Settings -> Alert Volume Profile, which starts the alarm at a low volume and gradually increases it, allowing the user to snooze before it gets loud.", "settings_changed": ["Alert Volume Profile → ascending volume profile"], "devices": ["Samsung S10 Plus", "S7"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "If you choose the ascending volume profile, the alarm starts at very low volume. Your selected sound file plays at the very low volume. Then, in 1 minute, the same sound file is played at slightly higher volume.", "text": "Buttons Silence alarms not working The 'Buttons silence alarms' feature is not working on a Samsung S10 Plus with Android 10, making it difficult to silence alarms at night. It used to work on an S7. Android restricts apps from capturing global button presses when the phone is locked or the app is not in the foreground, and newer Android versions have tightened these restrictions. Use the ascending volume profile as an alternative: Settings -> Alarms and Alerts -> Glucose Alerts Settings -> Alert Volume Profile, which starts the alarm at a low volume and gradually increases it, allowing the user to snooze before it gets loud. Samsung S10 Plus S7 Android 10  If you choose the ascending volume profile, the alarm starts at very low volume. Your selected sound file plays at the very low volume. Then, in 1 minute, the same sound file is played at slightly higher volume."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1502", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1502, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1502, "title": "New mongodb uri format is not supported by xDrip+", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1502", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1502", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After migrating from mlab to MongoDB Atlas, xDrip+ can no longer upload directly to the database. The new 'mongo+srv://' URI prefix can be set in the cloud parameters, but the logs show it is subsequently rejected.", "cause": "The thread identifies that direct-to-Mongo uploads are not supported by Nightscout (they only worked incidentally after the REST API was introduced) and that MongoDB Atlas's mongo+srv URI scheme is not usable from xDrip+, so direct MongoDB injection is not a viable path.", "fix": "The maintainers recommend removing MongoDB upload entirely or gating it behind engineering mode, and using Nightscout's REST API for uploading instead of direct Mongo.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["xDrip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["mongodb", "mongo+srv", "rest api", "nightscout", "engineering mode"], "evidence_quote": "Nightscout does not support direct to Mongo uploads anymore (it never really did, the fact it worked after REST API was introduce was incidental), so the \"correct\" fix here is to remove the Mongo uploads entirely and/or label it as something no Nightscout user should use.", "text": "New mongodb uri format is not supported by xDrip+ After migrating from mlab to MongoDB Atlas, xDrip+ can no longer upload directly to the database. The new 'mongo+srv://' URI prefix can be set in the cloud parameters, but the logs show it is subsequently rejected. The thread identifies that direct-to-Mongo uploads are not supported by Nightscout (they only worked incidentally after the REST API was introduced) and that MongoDB Atlas's mongo+srv URI scheme is not usable from xDrip+, so direct MongoDB injection is not a viable path. The maintainers recommend removing MongoDB upload entirely or gating it behind engineering mode, and using Nightscout's REST API for uploading instead of direct Mongo. xDrip mongodb mongo+srv rest api nightscout engineering mode Nightscout does not support direct to Mongo uploads anymore (it never really did, the fact it worked after REST API was introduce was incidental), so the \"correct\" fix here is to remove the Mongo uploads entirely and/or label it as something no Nightscout user should use."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1503", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1503, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1503, "title": "Notification Channel settings missing on new phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1503", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1503", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On a new Pixel 5 phone, the user cannot configure the glucose alerts notification channel (bgAlertChannel) as they could on their old Pixel 2 XL. The channel only shows a toggle to enable/disable, not the individual alert settings, preventing alarms from vibrating and breaking through Do Not Disturb mode.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is suggested that Android 11 may not expose notification channel settings until a notification fires, and that xDrip may not be registering the channel properly. Later, a maintainer notes that notification channels cannot be transferred to a new phone and may behave differently across devices, but the exact cause is not established.", "fix": "The issue was resolved after updating to the 2026.07.12 release of xDrip, as reported by a maintainer. The maintainer also mentions that xDrip has made improvements to reduce dependence on notification channels and plans to add full control of alerts without needing them.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 2 XL", "Pixel 5"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "After updating to the 2026.07.12 release, the problem has been resolved.", "text": "Notification Channel settings missing on new phone On a new Pixel 5 phone, the user cannot configure the glucose alerts notification channel (bgAlertChannel) as they could on their old Pixel 2 XL. The channel only shows a toggle to enable/disable, not the individual alert settings, preventing alarms from vibrating and breaking through Do Not Disturb mode. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is suggested that Android 11 may not expose notification channel settings until a notification fires, and that xDrip may not be registering the channel properly. Later, a maintainer notes that notification channels cannot be transferred to a new phone and may behave differently across devices, but the exact cause is not established. The issue was resolved after updating to the 2026.07.12 release of xDrip, as reported by a maintainer. The maintainer also mentions that xDrip has made improvements to reduce dependence on notification channels and plans to add full control of alerts without needing them. Pixel 2 XL Pixel 5 Android 11  After updating to the 2026.07.12 release, the problem has been resolved."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1504", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1504, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1504, "title": "Dexcom G6 Battery Status Packet Error - 8Q Transmitter", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1504", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1504", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "With an 8Q transmitter, the 'Transmitter Days', 'Resistance' and 'Temperature' values are all wrong. The issue is in the handling of the battery status packet.", "cause": "The battery status packet handling is incorrect for the new Firefly transmitters, which have packet sizes of 10 and 12, whereas the code likely assumed a different size.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by modifying the code in BatteryInfoRxMessage.java. The fix is implemented in xDrip, and the temperature is shown correctly starting with version 2021.07.10.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "8Q transmitter"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["G5Model", "Firefly"], "evidence_quote": "I've modified the code as follows and fixed the issue: [BatteryInfoRxMessage.txt]", "text": "Dexcom G6 Battery Status Packet Error - 8Q Transmitter With an 8Q transmitter, the 'Transmitter Days', 'Resistance' and 'Temperature' values are all wrong. The issue is in the handling of the battery status packet. The battery status packet handling is incorrect for the new Firefly transmitters, which have packet sizes of 10 and 12, whereas the code likely assumed a different size. The issue was resolved by modifying the code in BatteryInfoRxMessage.java. The fix is implemented in xDrip, and the temperature is shown correctly starting with version 2021.07.10. Dexcom G6 8Q transmitter G5Model Firefly I've modified the code as follows and fixed the issue: [BatteryInfoRxMessage.txt]"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1510", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1510, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1510, "title": "Bad Battery life on Watch since 'Nightly build 1st Oct 2020'", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1510", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1510", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After updating to the Nightly build of 1st Oct 2020, the watch battery life degraded significantly (e.g., 14% after 12h instead of 60%). Reverting to the 4th Sep 2020 build restored battery life.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It speculates about excessive alarms and wakelocks related to Bluetooth, possibly linked to the JodaTime change in the 2020.10.01 build, but no confirmation is provided.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix. Users report that reverting to an older build (e.g., 2020.09.04) improves battery life, and one user mentions that removing the complication and force stopping xDrip on the watch reduces consumption, but these are workarounds, not an official fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["TicWatch C2", "TicWatch Pro 2020", "TicWatch S2 Glacier"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear", "bluetooth", "wakelocks", "alarms"], "evidence_quote": "After Oct. update the watch had 14% Battery after 12h, before around 60%. Now I am back on '_Nightly build 4th Sep 2020_' and after 12h it shows me 60% again.", "text": "Bad Battery life on Watch since 'Nightly build 1st Oct 2020' After updating to the Nightly build of 1st Oct 2020, the watch battery life degraded significantly (e.g., 14% after 12h instead of 60%). Reverting to the 4th Sep 2020 build restored battery life. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It speculates about excessive alarms and wakelocks related to Bluetooth, possibly linked to the JodaTime change in the 2020.10.01 build, but no confirmation is provided. The thread does not state a definitive fix. Users report that reverting to an older build (e.g., 2020.09.04) improves battery life, and one user mentions that removing the complication and force stopping xDrip on the watch reduces consumption, but these are workarounds, not an official fix. TicWatch C2 TicWatch Pro 2020 TicWatch S2 Glacier wear bluetooth wakelocks alarms After Oct. update the watch had 14% Battery after 12h, before around 60%. Now I am back on '_Nightly build 4th Sep 2020_' and after 12h it shows me 60% again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1511", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1511, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1511, "title": "Wear OS Watch Collects, but does not update phone BG (SW3 / SWR50 / Huawei Watch 1)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1511", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1511", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On a new phone (Galaxy Note 20, Android 10), the Sony Smart Watch 3 collects glucose readings but does not sync them back to the phone. The phone status shows 'watch received glucose', but BG is not updated. Treatments on the watch do sync. The issue persists after factory resetting the watch and reinstalling xDrip.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a single root cause. It suggests possible issues with Google Play Services versions, trust agents/Smart Lock, or a missing location permission on the watch. The user old-square-eyes eventually resolved it after a location permission prompt appeared, and daclaw2k found that disabling Smart Lock (Trust agents) fixed it for them.", "fix": "Multiple workarounds were reported: 1) For daclaw2k, turning OFF Smart Lock in Settings > Security > Trust agents on the phone fixed the issue. 2) For old-square-eyes, the issue resolved after a location permission prompt appeared on the watch and was accepted, possibly after reinstalling xDrip prefs. 3) Another user found that flashing an older Google Play Services version helped temporarily.", "settings_changed": ["Smart Lock → OFF"], "devices": ["Sony Smart Watch 3", "SWR50", "Huawei Watch 1", "Galaxy Note 20", "Galaxy S8", "Galaxy S20+", "Google Pixel 3XL"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["wear", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "On my Google Pixel 3XL in the Settings under Security -> Trust agents -> Turning OFF Smart Lock seems to have fixed the problems between watch and phone for me.", "text": "Wear OS Watch Collects, but does not update phone BG (SW3 / SWR50 / Huawei Watch 1) On a new phone (Galaxy Note 20, Android 10), the Sony Smart Watch 3 collects glucose readings but does not sync them back to the phone. The phone status shows 'watch received glucose', but BG is not updated. Treatments on the watch do sync. The issue persists after factory resetting the watch and reinstalling xDrip. The thread does not definitively identify a single root cause. It suggests possible issues with Google Play Services versions, trust agents/Smart Lock, or a missing location permission on the watch. The user old-square-eyes eventually resolved it after a location permission prompt appeared, and daclaw2k found that disabling Smart Lock (Trust agents) fixed it for them. Multiple workarounds were reported: 1) For daclaw2k, turning OFF Smart Lock in Settings > Security > Trust agents on the phone fixed the issue. 2) For old-square-eyes, the issue resolved after a location permission prompt appeared on the watch and was accepted, possibly after reinstalling xDrip prefs. 3) Another user found that flashing an older Google Play Services version helped temporarily. Sony Smart Watch 3 SWR50 Huawei Watch 1 Galaxy Note 20 Galaxy S8 Galaxy S20+ Google Pixel 3XL Android 10 Android 9 wear collector On my Google Pixel 3XL in the Settings under Security -> Trust agents -> Turning OFF Smart Lock seems to have fixed the problems between watch and phone for me."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1517", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1517, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1517, "title": "Collector not receiving data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1517", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1517", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user reports that xDrip connects to the Bubble reader for a Libre sensor, but the 'Collecting Initial Readings' never passes the 'Data Collector Running' stage, with an hourglass icon before 'Receiving Data from Bubble Collector'. Data packets are sent but have checksum errors.", "cause": "The issue is a bug in the xDrip code supporting the Bubble transmitter, related to checksum calculation, as stated by a maintainer. The Bubble dev team is needed to fix it.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Bubble", "Libre"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["bubble collector"], "evidence_quote": "It is a bug in the xDrip code supporting the bubble transmitter and has nothing to do with the removal of the Diabox app from Play Store. But only the @bubbledevteam can fix it. It looks like it is related to the checksum calculation.", "text": "Collector not receiving data The user reports that xDrip connects to the Bubble reader for a Libre sensor, but the 'Collecting Initial Readings' never passes the 'Data Collector Running' stage, with an hourglass icon before 'Receiving Data from Bubble Collector'. Data packets are sent but have checksum errors. The issue is a bug in the xDrip code supporting the Bubble transmitter, related to checksum calculation, as stated by a maintainer. The Bubble dev team is needed to fix it.  Bubble Libre Android 10 Android 9 bubble collector It is a bug in the xDrip code supporting the bubble transmitter and has nothing to do with the removal of the Diabox app from Play Store. But only the @bubbledevteam can fix it. It looks like it is related to the checksum calculation."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1518", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1518, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1518, "title": "xdrip+ not synchronising all glucose data points from Nightscout when the measurement insert rate is > 1/5 minutes (libre)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1518", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1518", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When using xDrip+ as a Nightscout follower with a Libre sensor and glimp as uploader, the BG graph has missing data points. The follower does not query enough data from Nightscout, resulting in gaps in the graph, especially when data is inserted more frequently than every 5 minutes.", "cause": "The MissedReadingsEstimator assumes one reading every five minutes (DEXCOM_PERIOD), so the follower requests too few entries when the uploader inserts data more frequently (e.g., every minute).", "fix": "The issue was addressed by changing the NUM_VALUES constant in BgGraphBuilder.java to not divide by 5 (i.e., (60) * 24 instead of (60/5)*24) and by adding de-duplication to the expected 5-minute window when the brief_mode parameter is set. The fix was included in the 2022.07.21 release and the Aug 1st nightly.", "settings_changed": ["NUM_VALUES → (60) * 24"], "devices": ["Libre 1", "Libre 3", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout follower", "glimp", "Miao Miao", "web service"], "evidence_quote": "The issue is mostly because of the bug in the nightscout follower code which allows records to be stored at a higher frequency than the collector would typically allow. I think the best way to address this is a de-duplicator in BgReading which I will work on.", "text": "xdrip+ not synchronising all glucose data points from Nightscout when the measurement insert rate is > 1/5 minutes (libre) When using xDrip+ as a Nightscout follower with a Libre sensor and glimp as uploader, the BG graph has missing data points. The follower does not query enough data from Nightscout, resulting in gaps in the graph, especially when data is inserted more frequently than every 5 minutes. The MissedReadingsEstimator assumes one reading every five minutes (DEXCOM_PERIOD), so the follower requests too few entries when the uploader inserts data more frequently (e.g., every minute). The issue was addressed by changing the NUM_VALUES constant in BgGraphBuilder.java to not divide by 5 (i.e., (60) * 24 instead of (60/5)*24) and by adding de-duplication to the expected 5-minute window when the brief_mode parameter is set. The fix was included in the 2022.07.21 release and the Aug 1st nightly. Libre 1 Libre 3 Libre 2 nightscout follower glimp Miao Miao web service The issue is mostly because of the bug in the nightscout follower code which allows records to be stored at a higher frequency than the collector would typically allow. I think the best way to address this is a de-duplicator in BgReading which I will work on."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1519", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1519, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1519, "title": "FEATURE: Multiple Carbs profiles and other food ingredients", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1519", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1519", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The issue is a feature request to register multiple types of carbs, fats, and protein based on a food database from a Nightscout server, to improve blood glucose predictions. The discussion also highlights the need for both quick and comprehensive meal registration interfaces.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "as follow up discussion point from #1388 i will start implementing a feature to register multiple types of carbs, fats and protein (based on the food database available on a nightscout server).", "text": "FEATURE: Multiple Carbs profiles and other food ingredients The issue is a feature request to register multiple types of carbs, fats, and protein based on a food database from a Nightscout server, to improve blood glucose predictions. The discussion also highlights the need for both quick and comprehensive meal registration interfaces.     as follow up discussion point from #1388 i will start implementing a feature to register multiple types of carbs, fats and protein (based on the food database available on a nightscout server)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1522", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1522, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1522, "title": "Code Review: refactor code", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1522", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1522", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The issue is a code review request listing many refactoring tasks for the xDrip codebase, including cleanup of Gradle files, removal of local AAR files, migration to AndroidX, upgrading dependencies, and addressing security-related tasks.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Over the last couple of days I spent some time to understand the xDrip code. After some reviewing I found the following issues which I like to address soon:", "text": "Code Review: refactor code The issue is a code review request listing many refactoring tasks for the xDrip codebase, including cleanup of Gradle files, removal of local AAR files, migration to AndroidX, upgrading dependencies, and addressing security-related tasks.     Over the last couple of days I spent some time to understand the xDrip code. After some reviewing I found the following issues which I like to address soon:"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1527", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1527, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1527, "title": "Continual pairing requests after recent Android update.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1527", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1527", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Constant Android pairing request notifications that cannot be silenced or connected, with errors like 'Could not read reply to auth challenge.....' and 'Prompting user to notice pairing request with sound. On android 10+ you have to manually pair when requested.' The issue persists even after updating xDrip to the Nov 27 daily, and disconnections occur multiple times a day on a Moto G8 Power.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that the issue may be related to Android updates and specific phone models, but no clear cause is identified.", "fix": "The thread suggests that updating to an xDrip release of November 27, 2020 or later should prevent frequent pair requests. Additionally, uninstalling and reinstalling the newest daily and clicking pair again seemed to help temporarily. Switching back to a OnePlus 6t resolved the issue on that phone. Airplane mode can also fix the connection issue temporarily.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6", "Moto G8 Power", "OnePlus 6t"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "There should be no frequent pair request as soon as you update to an xDrip release of November 27, 2020 or later.", "text": "Continual pairing requests after recent Android update. Constant Android pairing request notifications that cannot be silenced or connected, with errors like 'Could not read reply to auth challenge.....' and 'Prompting user to notice pairing request with sound. On android 10+ you have to manually pair when requested.' The issue persists even after updating xDrip to the Nov 27 daily, and disconnections occur multiple times a day on a Moto G8 Power. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests that the issue may be related to Android updates and specific phone models, but no clear cause is identified. The thread suggests that updating to an xDrip release of November 27, 2020 or later should prevent frequent pair requests. Additionally, uninstalling and reinstalling the newest daily and clicking pair again seemed to help temporarily. Switching back to a OnePlus 6t resolved the issue on that phone. Airplane mode can also fix the connection issue temporarily. G6 Moto G8 Power OnePlus 6t  There should be no frequent pair request as soon as you update to an xDrip release of November 27, 2020 or later."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1537", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1537, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1537, "title": "The glucose readings aren't added in 5 minute intervals anymore", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1537", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1537", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Glucose readings on the xDrip graph are not spaced evenly at 5-minute intervals; intervals vary from 2 to 8 minutes, making the dots unevenly spaced, though the data table and logs show correct 5-minute timestamps.", "cause": "The FUZZER constant (2.5 minutes) used to place readings on a grid causes time shifts when the fractional part of the division is near 0 or 1, leading to occasional 2.5-minute shifts in graph display.", "fix": "Update to xDrip release 2022.08.18 or later, which is supposed to fix the issue. Alternatively, lower the fuzzer to 37.5 seconds in engineering mode via advanced display settings.", "settings_changed": ["FUZZER → 37.5 seconds (via engineering mode option)"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["FUZZER", "BgGraphBuilder"], "evidence_quote": "This is supposed to have been fixed with August 18, 2022. https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2022.08.18 Please update to that release or any after that, and please report if you ever still experience the reported issue.", "text": "The glucose readings aren't added in 5 minute intervals anymore Glucose readings on the xDrip graph are not spaced evenly at 5-minute intervals; intervals vary from 2 to 8 minutes, making the dots unevenly spaced, though the data table and logs show correct 5-minute timestamps. The FUZZER constant (2.5 minutes) used to place readings on a grid causes time shifts when the fractional part of the division is near 0 or 1, leading to occasional 2.5-minute shifts in graph display. Update to xDrip release 2022.08.18 or later, which is supposed to fix the issue. Alternatively, lower the fuzzer to 37.5 seconds in engineering mode via advanced display settings. Dexcom G6 FUZZER BgGraphBuilder This is supposed to have been fixed with August 18, 2022. https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2022.08.18 Please update to that release or any after that, and please report if you ever still experience the reported issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1547", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1547, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1547, "title": "Android 11 Restore is empty (zip and sqlite is correct)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1547", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1547", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After upgrading to Android 11 on a Pocophone F2 Pro, restoring a backup created on Android 11 results in empty data (sgv, treatments etc.), while the same backup and APK restore correctly on Android 10. The preferences files import works.", "cause": "The thread suggests it is due to the new file handling restrictions in Android 11, but no definitive root cause is confirmed.", "fix": "No confirmed fix. A manifest flag was added in PR #1548 but did not help. A suggestion was made to attempt importing the database file 3-4 times, but it is not confirmed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "This is the new restriction on file handling in Android 11. As xDrip is most likely not targeting Android 11 any time soon (target is still 23), we could add a flag to the manifest that most likely should still allow to import backups.", "text": "Android 11 Restore is empty (zip and sqlite is correct) After upgrading to Android 11 on a Pocophone F2 Pro, restoring a backup created on Android 11 results in empty data (sgv, treatments etc.), while the same backup and APK restore correctly on Android 10. The preferences files import works. The thread suggests it is due to the new file handling restrictions in Android 11, but no definitive root cause is confirmed. No confirmed fix. A manifest flag was added in PR #1548 but did not help. A suggestion was made to attempt importing the database file 3-4 times, but it is not confirmed. Android 11 Android 10  This is the new restriction on file handling in Android 11. As xDrip is most likely not targeting Android 11 any time soon (target is still 23), we could add a flag to the manifest that most likely should still allow to import backups."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1555", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1555, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1555, "title": "enhance translations at crowdin with screenshots", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1555", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1555", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The issue requests enhancing translations at Crowdin with screenshots, noting that translators lack context for strings, making it difficult to understand their meaning.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "That would be great help for the translators, because without the context many times I did not have any clue, what that string might mean.", "text": "enhance translations at crowdin with screenshots The issue requests enhancing translations at Crowdin with screenshots, noting that translators lack context for strings, making it difficult to understand their meaning.     That would be great help for the translators, because without the context many times I did not have any clue, what that string might mean."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1558", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1558, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1558, "title": "App crashes", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1558", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1558", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The app crashes immediately after starting, especially when starting a sensor or when a sensor has already been started. The issue occurred after updating to a newer version than the December 10 build, and was resolved after trying the latest version.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is suggested that the issue may be related to receiving too much data after updating to a newer version.", "fix": "The user reported that the latest version (with enhanced crash reporter) is working now, and after starting a new sensor it still works. The issue was closed as fixed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre Bluetooth", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Libre Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "I have tried the latest version, it is working now, not crashing, still getting message about received to much data, but now it is working, waiting till tomorrow or friday if app is still working, it crashed last time also after starting a new sensor", "text": "App crashes The app crashes immediately after starting, especially when starting a sensor or when a sensor has already been started. The issue occurred after updating to a newer version than the December 10 build, and was resolved after trying the latest version. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is suggested that the issue may be related to receiving too much data after updating to a newer version. The user reported that the latest version (with enhanced crash reporter) is working now, and after starting a new sensor it still works. The issue was closed as fixed. Libre Bluetooth Dexcom G6 Android 10 Libre Bluetooth I have tried the latest version, it is working now, not crashing, still getting message about received to much data, but now it is working, waiting till tomorrow or friday if app is still working, it crashed last time also after starting a new sensor"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1561", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1561, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1561, "title": "[Feature Request] please add Lyumjev to multiple insulin types", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1561", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1561", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Users request that Lyumjev insulin be added to xDrip's insulin types, as more people are using it.", "cause": "The maintainer tolot27 states that the exact function/values to calculate the maximum and duration of action for Lyumjev are needed, and sufficient data to determine a fitting function was not found.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "We still need the exact function/values to calculate the maximum and duration of action.", "text": "[Feature Request] please add Lyumjev to multiple insulin types Users request that Lyumjev insulin be added to xDrip's insulin types, as more people are using it. The maintainer tolot27 states that the exact function/values to calculate the maximum and duration of action for Lyumjev are needed, and sufficient data to determine a fitting function was not found.    We still need the exact function/values to calculate the maximum and duration of action."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-157", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 157, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 157, "title": "Enable 640G as full data source via 640G Uploader application to allow Sync following to work correctly", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/157", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/157", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Users with a Medtronic 640G/Enlite want xDrip to include the Nightscout Medtronic/600SeriesAndroidUploader as a data source in master mode, so readings can be sent directly to xDrip followers and smartwatches with audible alarms. The Medtronic 640G's own alarms are quiet or not perceived, making xDrip's loud alarms desirable.", "cause": "xDrip did not have the Medtronic 600SeriesAndroidUploader/uploader integrated as a source, so it could receive data only in follower mode, not master mode, preventing direct forwarding to followers.", "fix": "Developer jamorham implemented the 640G uploader as a source in xDrip and released it in the 21 Aug version; the issue was then closed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic 640G"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["600seriesandroiduploader", "medtronic", "nightscout", "master mode", "follower mode", "broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "Okay, I believe the request that this issue ticket relates to is now resolved. I will mark it closed.", "text": "Enable 640G as full data source via 640G Uploader application to allow Sync following to work correctly Users with a Medtronic 640G/Enlite want xDrip to include the Nightscout Medtronic/600SeriesAndroidUploader as a data source in master mode, so readings can be sent directly to xDrip followers and smartwatches with audible alarms. The Medtronic 640G's own alarms are quiet or not perceived, making xDrip's loud alarms desirable. xDrip did not have the Medtronic 600SeriesAndroidUploader/uploader integrated as a source, so it could receive data only in follower mode, not master mode, preventing direct forwarding to followers. Developer jamorham implemented the 640G uploader as a source in xDrip and released it in the 21 Aug version; the issue was then closed. Medtronic 640G 600seriesandroiduploader medtronic nightscout master mode follower mode broadcast Okay, I believe the request that this issue ticket relates to is now resolved. I will mark it closed."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1573", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1573, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1573, "title": "xDrip cannot start a G6 sensor in no-code mode with a new (8J) transmitter", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1573", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1573", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "With newer transmitters (8J), after entering 0000 as the calibration code in no-code mode, no readings are ever provided after the warm-up period, and the transmitter eventually issues an error. The Dexcom app can start a sensor with a new transmitter in no-code mode, but xDrip cannot.", "cause": "The issue is likely due to more security measures for anti-restart that Dexcom has put into their new transmitters (as suspected by Jon). Additionally, calibration errors may occur after warm-up in no-code mode, which are not specific to xDrip but also occur with the Dexcom app.", "fix": "One user (Navid200) successfully restarted using 0000 through xDrip after re-enabling 'Double Calibration' under Advanced Calibrations. However, later he lost connectivity and had to forget the device and re-pair. Another user (nickb24) overcame calibration errors by entering 3 glucose values at the same time with the same value, after checking the transmitter queue. The thread also suggests improving error messages to indicate waiting at least 15 minutes before another calibration.", "settings_changed": ["Double Calibration → enabled", "Double Calibration → disabled"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["native mode", "no-code mode", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "The only thing I did differently this time is that I re-enabled \"Double Calibration\" under Advanced Calibrations. Previously, I had it disabled when a restart with code 0000 had failed.", "text": "xDrip cannot start a G6 sensor in no-code mode with a new (8J) transmitter With newer transmitters (8J), after entering 0000 as the calibration code in no-code mode, no readings are ever provided after the warm-up period, and the transmitter eventually issues an error. The Dexcom app can start a sensor with a new transmitter in no-code mode, but xDrip cannot. The issue is likely due to more security measures for anti-restart that Dexcom has put into their new transmitters (as suspected by Jon). Additionally, calibration errors may occur after warm-up in no-code mode, which are not specific to xDrip but also occur with the Dexcom app. One user (Navid200) successfully restarted using 0000 through xDrip after re-enabling 'Double Calibration' under Advanced Calibrations. However, later he lost connectivity and had to forget the device and re-pair. Another user (nickb24) overcame calibration errors by entering 3 glucose values at the same time with the same value, after checking the transmitter queue. The thread also suggests improving error messages to indicate waiting at least 15 minutes before another calibration. Dexcom G6 Android 9 native mode no-code mode collector The only thing I did differently this time is that I re-enabled \"Double Calibration\" under Advanced Calibrations. Previously, I had it disabled when a restart with code 0000 had failed."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1574", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1574, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1574, "title": "Invalid slope caliberation + connection at night + question ", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1574", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1574", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User reports being unable to calibrate in xDrip; calibration attempts revert without success. Also, at night (when sleeping), xDrip loses connection for 100-200 minutes each night, while the Dexcom receiver works fine.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Possible causes mentioned include phone 'sleeping' (battery optimization) and user behaviors with G6 calibration, but no confirmed cause.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include excluding xDrip from battery optimization, and for calibration, limiting corrections to 20% of the reading and avoiding frequent calibrations, but these are recommendations, not confirmed resolutions.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "You should never calibrate a CGM if your trend is not flat or very close to flat. If you restart a G6, using the original calibration code, you will interfere with factory calibration mechanism of G6. The result is that after the 2-hour warm-up, you will experience a significant error. The readings will be much higher than they should be. To calibrate, you need to limit the calibration to small values. The recommendation is to limit the correction to 20% of the reading.", "text": "Invalid slope caliberation + connection at night + question  User reports being unable to calibrate in xDrip; calibration attempts revert without success. Also, at night (when sleeping), xDrip loses connection for 100-200 minutes each night, while the Dexcom receiver works fine. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Possible causes mentioned include phone 'sleeping' (battery optimization) and user behaviors with G6 calibration, but no confirmed cause. No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include excluding xDrip from battery optimization, and for calibration, limiting corrections to 20% of the reading and avoiding frequent calibrations, but these are recommendations, not confirmed resolutions. Dexcom G6  You should never calibrate a CGM if your trend is not flat or very close to flat. If you restart a G6, using the original calibration code, you will interfere with factory calibration mechanism of G6. The result is that after the 2-hour warm-up, you will experience a significant error. The readings will be much higher than they should be. To calibrate, you need to limit the calibration to small values. The recommendation is to limit the correction to 20% of the reading."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1575", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1575, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1575, "title": "G6 values discarded after transmitter change and warmup due to small time sync difference", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1575", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1575", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After changing the transmitter and starting a new sensor using the hardware receiver, after warmup the hardware receiver got results but xdrip+ showed no readings. The log showed values received but discarded as invalid, with messages like 'invalid timestamp comparison for transmitter id' and 'No sensor, ignoring this bg reading'.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. The reporter observed a time difference between the hardware receiver and phone (3 minutes) and suspected it, but later agreed the actual reason might be something else. Maintainers suggested it might be related to Firefly G6 connectivity issues or other overlooked problems.", "fix": "The reporter found that correcting the time on the hardware receiver resolved the issue in that instance. However, the thread does not confirm a definitive fix; it suggests ensuring correct time on both devices and possibly restarting the collector if readings are missed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1 collector", "native algorithm", "minimize scanning", "G6", "allow OB1 initiate bonding"], "evidence_quote": "I then noticed a time difference between hardware receiver and smartphone of 3 minutes. I updated the time on the hardware receiver and soon started getting results.", "text": "G6 values discarded after transmitter change and warmup due to small time sync difference After changing the transmitter and starting a new sensor using the hardware receiver, after warmup the hardware receiver got results but xdrip+ showed no readings. The log showed values received but discarded as invalid, with messages like 'invalid timestamp comparison for transmitter id' and 'No sensor, ignoring this bg reading'. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. The reporter observed a time difference between the hardware receiver and phone (3 minutes) and suspected it, but later agreed the actual reason might be something else. Maintainers suggested it might be related to Firefly G6 connectivity issues or other overlooked problems. The reporter found that correcting the time on the hardware receiver resolved the issue in that instance. However, the thread does not confirm a definitive fix; it suggests ensuring correct time on both devices and possibly restarting the collector if readings are missed. G6 OB1 collector native algorithm minimize scanning G6 allow OB1 initiate bonding I then noticed a time difference between hardware receiver and smartphone of 3 minutes. I updated the time on the hardware receiver and soon started getting results."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1576", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1576, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1576, "title": "Skagen Falster 3 Smartwatch Patch", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1576", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1576", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The Skagen Falster 3 cannot be used as a collector. When the phone is out of range, the watch no longer receives updates, and no error messages appear on the watch.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Skagen Falster 3", "Pixel 4", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android V 11"], "driver_tags": ["wear", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "The watch faces work fine, i can see my readings and everything, but it will not work as a collector. as soon as my phone is out of range i no longer get updates.", "text": "Skagen Falster 3 Smartwatch Patch The Skagen Falster 3 cannot be used as a collector. When the phone is out of range, the watch no longer receives updates, and no error messages appear on the watch.   Skagen Falster 3 Pixel 4 Dexcom G6 Android V 11 wear collector The watch faces work fine, i can see my readings and everything, but it will not work as a collector. as soon as my phone is out of range i no longer get updates."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1577", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1577, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1577, "title": "Capture G6 session from another smartphone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1577", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1577", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User started a new Dexcom G6 sensor with a new transmitter on a separate phone, but when trying to switch the new sensor session to the loop smartphone, xDrip+ requires stopping the old sensor session first, which sends a 'stop sensor' command to the old transmitter and kills the running session, causing a data pause.", "cause": "xDrip+ sends a 'stop sensor' command to the transmitter when stopping a sensor session, which kills the running sensor session, preventing the user from switching to a new already-started session without stopping the old one.", "fix": "The thread suggests using the 'clear transmitter queue' command to avoid sending the queued stop command, but the user notes that Bluetooth must be disabled before stopping the sensor to prevent the transmitter from receiving the queued command. The maintainer states that capturing a session started from another phone is possible with existing code if collection is disabled on the other phone.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["transmitter", "xDrip+"], "evidence_quote": "To avoid that the transmitter received the queued command, it‘s necessary to disable bluetooth before stopping the sensor.", "text": "Capture G6 session from another smartphone User started a new Dexcom G6 sensor with a new transmitter on a separate phone, but when trying to switch the new sensor session to the loop smartphone, xDrip+ requires stopping the old sensor session first, which sends a 'stop sensor' command to the old transmitter and kills the running session, causing a data pause. xDrip+ sends a 'stop sensor' command to the transmitter when stopping a sensor session, which kills the running sensor session, preventing the user from switching to a new already-started session without stopping the old one. The thread suggests using the 'clear transmitter queue' command to avoid sending the queued stop command, but the user notes that Bluetooth must be disabled before stopping the sensor to prevent the transmitter from receiving the queued command. The maintainer states that capturing a session started from another phone is possible with existing code if collection is disabled on the other phone. Dexcom G6 transmitter xDrip+ To avoid that the transmitter received the queued command, it‘s necessary to disable bluetooth before stopping the sensor."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1580", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1580, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1580, "title": "treatment bg values are silently used for calibration despite answering \"no\" or setting to \"never\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1580", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1580", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip uses treatment BG values for calibration even when the user answers 'No' to the prompt or sets the setting to 'Never'. The calibration is inserted into the queue and sent to the transmitter, which can cause sensors to be dangerously off.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify the root cause, but it is confirmed as a bug by a maintainer who says 'I just tested and can see the problem' and plans to open a PR to fix it.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a fix, but a workaround is suggested: uncheck 'Automatic Calibration' in Settings -> Less common settings -> Advanced Calibration, and on the same page tap 'Use Treatment BG Values' and check 'Automatic mode'. The user also mentions avoiding entering BG values in xDrip and using the Dexcom device for calibration.", "settings_changed": ["Automatic Calibration → unchecked", "Use Treatment BG Values → Automatic mode"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native G6"], "evidence_quote": "I just tested and can see the problem. Thanks so much for reporting this. I will open a PR to fix this.", "text": "treatment bg values are silently used for calibration despite answering \"no\" or setting to \"never\" xDrip uses treatment BG values for calibration even when the user answers 'No' to the prompt or sets the setting to 'Never'. The calibration is inserted into the queue and sent to the transmitter, which can cause sensors to be dangerously off. The thread does not explicitly identify the root cause, but it is confirmed as a bug by a maintainer who says 'I just tested and can see the problem' and plans to open a PR to fix it. The thread does not provide a fix, but a workaround is suggested: uncheck 'Automatic Calibration' in Settings -> Less common settings -> Advanced Calibration, and on the same page tap 'Use Treatment BG Values' and check 'Automatic mode'. The user also mentions avoiding entering BG values in xDrip and using the Dexcom device for calibration. Dexcom G6 native G6 I just tested and can see the problem. Thanks so much for reporting this. I will open a PR to fix this."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1587", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1587, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1587, "title": "Xdrip stops receiving data from G6 after Bluetooth failed to register error and requires reboot.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1587", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1587", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "xDrip stops receiving data from the Dexcom G6 after 6-24 hours, with the G5/G6 Status Bluetooth Link showing 'Failed to register application for bluetooth scan' in red. A phone reboot is required to start receiving data again.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": ["Minimize Scanning → disabled", "WearOS integration → disabled"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["ob1 collector", "native algorithm", "rxandroidble", "aaps", "bluejay", "wearos"], "evidence_quote": "XDrip fails to receive data from G6 device after 6-24 hours with the \"Failed to register application for bluetooth scan\" and requires a phone reboot to begin receiving data again.", "text": "Xdrip stops receiving data from G6 after Bluetooth failed to register error and requires reboot. xDrip stops receiving data from the Dexcom G6 after 6-24 hours, with the G5/G6 Status Bluetooth Link showing 'Failed to register application for bluetooth scan' in red. A phone reboot is required to start receiving data again.   Dexcom G6 Android 11 Android 10 ob1 collector native algorithm rxandroidble aaps bluejay wearos XDrip fails to receive data from G6 device after 6-24 hours with the \"Failed to register application for bluetooth scan\" and requires a phone reboot to begin receiving data again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1597", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1597, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1597, "title": "Syncing Libre2 raw data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1597", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1597", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "xDrip+ with a patched LibreLink app shows Libre2 raw data as small white points on the master device, but these raw data points are not synced to other phones via xDrip sync, nor uploaded to Nightscout.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["patched LibreLink app", "xdrip sync"], "evidence_quote": "I've been unable to sync raw data (the white points) between devices, is it possible? It would be an interesting enhancement if it's not possible right now.", "text": "Syncing Libre2 raw data xDrip+ with a patched LibreLink app shows Libre2 raw data as small white points on the master device, but these raw data points are not synced to other phones via xDrip sync, nor uploaded to Nightscout.   Libre2 patched LibreLink app xdrip sync I've been unable to sync raw data (the white points) between devices, is it possible? It would be an interesting enhancement if it's not possible right now."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-161", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 161, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 161, "title": "Hello, Can you build in xDrip An automatic screen wake-up at high and low blood glucose values with threshold input? And a screen duration on switch via hook as with voice announcement?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/161", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/161", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user requests a feature to automatically wake the screen on high or low blood glucose values with threshold input and a screen duration switch, similar to voice announcement. They also report that the Android Uploader app stops in the background, causing missed readings, and ask for a way to prevent it from stopping.", "cause": "The Android Uploader (600SeriesAndroidUploader) has a failover timer that restarts it after 20 minutes, causing gaps in data transmission. The screen wake feature is not available because the phone's charging port is occupied by the Enlite Contour Next 2.4 meter, preventing the use of Daydream or keep-screen-on features.", "fix": "For missed reading alerts, disable the 'Missed Reading Alerts' in Settings->Alarms and Alerts. For the Android Uploader stopping, the issue is in the 600SeriesAndroidUploader repo, not xDrip, and may be due to a failover timer. No direct fix is provided in xDrip.", "settings_changed": ["Missed Reading Alerts → disabled"], "devices": ["Enlite Contour Next 2.4", "Android Uploader"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["600series uploader", "broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "In order to not having to do that you can go to \"Settings->Alarms and Alerts->Missed Reading Alerts\" and disable that alert. Then it won't alarm on missed readings.", "text": "Hello, Can you build in xDrip An automatic screen wake-up at high and low blood glucose values with threshold input? And a screen duration on switch via hook as with voice announcement? The user requests a feature to automatically wake the screen on high or low blood glucose values with threshold input and a screen duration switch, similar to voice announcement. They also report that the Android Uploader app stops in the background, causing missed readings, and ask for a way to prevent it from stopping. The Android Uploader (600SeriesAndroidUploader) has a failover timer that restarts it after 20 minutes, causing gaps in data transmission. The screen wake feature is not available because the phone's charging port is occupied by the Enlite Contour Next 2.4 meter, preventing the use of Daydream or keep-screen-on features. For missed reading alerts, disable the 'Missed Reading Alerts' in Settings->Alarms and Alerts. For the Android Uploader stopping, the issue is in the 600SeriesAndroidUploader repo, not xDrip, and may be due to a failover timer. No direct fix is provided in xDrip. Enlite Contour Next 2.4 Android Uploader 600series uploader broadcast In order to not having to do that you can go to \"Settings->Alarms and Alerts->Missed Reading Alerts\" and disable that alert. Then it won't alarm on missed readings."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1611", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1611, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1611, "title": "Wear OS collector to send data to NightScout", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1611", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1611", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "On Wear OS watches without Google services (e.g., Xiaomi Mi Watch), xDrip standalone collector works but there is no option to send readings to NightScout (Nightscout Uploader) from the watch.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Xiaomi Mi Watch", "Libre1", "Libre2", "Libre3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["WearOS", "Nightscout Uploader", "Nightscout Follower", "standalone collector"], "evidence_quote": "Would be great to have an option to send readings to NightScout from WearOS collector in case Google services are missing.", "text": "Wear OS collector to send data to NightScout On Wear OS watches without Google services (e.g., Xiaomi Mi Watch), xDrip standalone collector works but there is no option to send readings to NightScout (Nightscout Uploader) from the watch.   Xiaomi Mi Watch Libre1 Libre2 Libre3 WearOS Nightscout Uploader Nightscout Follower standalone collector Would be great to have an option to send readings to NightScout from WearOS collector in case Google services are missing."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1625", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1625, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1625, "title": "Always On Display Widget - Testers wanted", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1625", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1625", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users testing the new xDrip Always On Display widget report that the widget sometimes jumps, overlaps the clock or fingerprint icon, and lags briefly when unlocking; in some cases the clock or glucose values are unreadable because they overlap.", "cause": "The widget intentionally moves around to reduce screen burn-in, but the positions of the clock/fingerprint icons on the Always On Display vary between Android versions and phone models, causing the widget to overlap them.", "fix": "Der-Schubi contributed pull request #3153 to let users choose where on screen the AOD widget moves, and as of the February 07, 2024 release users can control where the widget moves. Documentation is available at https://navid200.github.io/xDrip/docs/Display/AOD.html.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S20+", "Oneplus 8 Pro", "Pixel 5", "Samsung S20 Ultra", "Nokia 8", "Samsung S9", "Pocofone F2 Pro", "Samsung Galaxy S20", "Samsung S22Ultra", "Pixel 6a"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Thanks to @Der-Schubi, you can now (as of the February 07, 2024 release) control where on screen the widget moves.", "text": "Always On Display Widget - Testers wanted Users testing the new xDrip Always On Display widget report that the widget sometimes jumps, overlaps the clock or fingerprint icon, and lags briefly when unlocking; in some cases the clock or glucose values are unreadable because they overlap. The widget intentionally moves around to reduce screen burn-in, but the positions of the clock/fingerprint icons on the Always On Display vary between Android versions and phone models, causing the widget to overlap them. Der-Schubi contributed pull request #3153 to let users choose where on screen the AOD widget moves, and as of the February 07, 2024 release users can control where the widget moves. Documentation is available at https://navid200.github.io/xDrip/docs/Display/AOD.html. Samsung Galaxy S20+ Oneplus 8 Pro Pixel 5 Samsung S20 Ultra Nokia 8 Samsung S9 Pocofone F2 Pro Samsung Galaxy S20 Samsung S22Ultra Pixel 6a Android 11 Android 9  Thanks to @Der-Schubi, you can now (as of the February 07, 2024 release) control where on screen the widget moves."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1629", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1629, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1629, "title": "Last BG value not shown on Main Screen and Widget", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1629", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1629", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The current BG Level and Arrow is missing from both the main display and the widget on a Samsung S21 Ultra.", "cause": "The issue was resolved by turning the sensor on in xDrip, even though there wasn't one physically connected.", "fix": "Turn the sensor on in xDrip (even though there isn't one physically connected).", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Patched Dexcom G6 App", "Samsung S21 Ultra"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["640G/Eversource Option"], "evidence_quote": "Oh wow...it's started working! Here's what I did: I just went and turned the sensor on. Even though there isn't one!", "text": "Last BG value not shown on Main Screen and Widget The current BG Level and Arrow is missing from both the main display and the widget on a Samsung S21 Ultra. The issue was resolved by turning the sensor on in xDrip, even though there wasn't one physically connected. Turn the sensor on in xDrip (even though there isn't one physically connected). Patched Dexcom G6 App Samsung S21 Ultra Android 11 640G/Eversource Option Oh wow...it's started working! Here's what I did: I just went and turned the sensor on. Even though there isn't one!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1631", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1631, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1631, "title": "New feature: Import settings from file system", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1631", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1631", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Export settings saves to the Downloads folder, but importing from that location fails with an error message and settings are not restored. The user suggests allowing file selection instead of auto-checking one location.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suggested it may be an Android 11 issue, but not confirmed.", "fix": "The user reported that after trying again later, importing worked on the first, second, and third tries. No specific fix was provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Ït worked on the first try, the second try, and the third try now.", "text": "New feature: Import settings from file system Export settings saves to the Downloads folder, but importing from that location fails with an error message and settings are not restored. The user suggests allowing file selection instead of auto-checking one location. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is suggested it may be an Android 11 issue, but not confirmed. The user reported that after trying again later, importing worked on the first, second, and third tries. No specific fix was provided. Android 11  Ït worked on the first try, the second try, and the third try now."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1632", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1632, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1632, "title": "Dexcom sensor state inconsistently shown", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1632", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1632", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The Dexcom sensor state is not consistently shown across the main screen, menu and system status. After a sensor session ends the main screen says 'Stopped' while the menu still shows 'Stop sensor'; after starting a new sensor, xDrip can still show 'stopped' and warm-up messages even though the sensor has started. This is confusing, especially at sensor session beginnings/ends.", "cause": "The thread identifies the original inconsistency as partly a hang-over from when xDrip supported coexisting native and non-native data: within xDrip, a sensor session isn't strictly tied to the native Dexcom session.", "fix": "A nightly update added transitional states (for example, showing 'Starting Sensor' instead of 'Stopped' when a sensor is about to be started), which Navid states addressed the original menu/main-screen inconsistency. For sensor replacement cases, the thread describes a workaround: after stopping, wait for the transmitter to perform a final read, remove it, and keep it disconnected for at least 10 minutes before inserting it in a new sensor.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1.0"], "driver_tags": ["native mode", "non-native", "Dexcom receiver"], "evidence_quote": "The latest nightly includes some transitional states which I think should resolve most of the problems described in this issue. For example when a sensor is about to be started it will say `Starting Sensor` instead of its current actual state, eg `Stopped`", "text": "Dexcom sensor state inconsistently shown The Dexcom sensor state is not consistently shown across the main screen, menu and system status. After a sensor session ends the main screen says 'Stopped' while the menu still shows 'Stop sensor'; after starting a new sensor, xDrip can still show 'stopped' and warm-up messages even though the sensor has started. This is confusing, especially at sensor session beginnings/ends. The thread identifies the original inconsistency as partly a hang-over from when xDrip supported coexisting native and non-native data: within xDrip, a sensor session isn't strictly tied to the native Dexcom session. A nightly update added transitional states (for example, showing 'Starting Sensor' instead of 'Stopped' when a sensor is about to be started), which Navid states addressed the original menu/main-screen inconsistency. For sensor replacement cases, the thread describes a workaround: after stopping, wait for the transmitter to perform a final read, remove it, and keep it disconnected for at least 10 minutes before inserting it in a new sensor. Dexcom G6 Android 8.1.0 native mode non-native Dexcom receiver The latest nightly includes some transitional states which I think should resolve most of the problems described in this issue. For example when a sensor is about to be started it will say `Starting Sensor` instead of its current actual state, eg `Stopped`"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1635", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1635, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1635, "title": "Deadlocks messages on actual nightly", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1635", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1635", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since some nightlys I see deadlocks messages. The issue is reported by multiple users with different setups.", "cause": null, "fix": "Upgrade to Nightly build 8th Feb 2021 which should have addressed this problem.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Libre2+OOP2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Wear collection"], "evidence_quote": "Please try [Nightly build 8th Feb 2021] which should have addressed this problem.", "text": "Deadlocks messages on actual nightly Since some nightlys I see deadlocks messages. The issue is reported by multiple users with different setups.  Upgrade to Nightly build 8th Feb 2021 which should have addressed this problem. Dexcom G6 Libre2+OOP2 Wear collection Please try [Nightly build 8th Feb 2021] which should have addressed this problem."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1636", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1636, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1636, "title": "Error: xDrip looses connection often for up to 1hr, error in the logs: \"No Transmitter mac address\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1636", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1636", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since the last nightlies (from January) xDrip has issues again in connecting the transmitter. It has downtimes of over an hour in between until it is able to reconnect. The error message shown in the logs is \"No transmitter mac address\" followed by a note that location permission is missing. xDrip has the location permission enabled.", "cause": "The error messages for location services are for the smart watch. The user was not using the smart watch as a collector, but the watch was causing the location permission errors.", "fix": "Grant xDrip on the watch location permissions, even though the watch is not used as a collector. The user also changed several settings: unchecked Samsung Workarounds, unchecked minimize scanning, checked allow OB1 disconnect, and granted location permissions on the watch.", "settings_changed": ["Samsung Workarounds → unchecked", "minimize scanning → unchecked", "allow OB1 disconnect → checked", "location permission on watch → granted"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Ticwatch Pro 2020"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The error messages for location services you are seeing are for your smart watch. If you are not using your smart watch as a collector I would disable that setting from the smart watch.", "text": "Error: xDrip looses connection often for up to 1hr, error in the logs: \"No Transmitter mac address\" Since the last nightlies (from January) xDrip has issues again in connecting the transmitter. It has downtimes of over an hour in between until it is able to reconnect. The error message shown in the logs is \"No transmitter mac address\" followed by a note that location permission is missing. xDrip has the location permission enabled. The error messages for location services are for the smart watch. The user was not using the smart watch as a collector, but the watch was causing the location permission errors. Grant xDrip on the watch location permissions, even though the watch is not used as a collector. The user also changed several settings: unchecked Samsung Workarounds, unchecked minimize scanning, checked allow OB1 disconnect, and granted location permissions on the watch. Dexcom G6 Ticwatch Pro 2020 Android 10  The error messages for location services you are seeing are for your smart watch. If you are not using your smart watch as a collector I would disable that setting from the smart watch."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1647", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1647, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1647, "title": "xDrip confuses G5 with a G6 and performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1647", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1647", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In native mode with a Dexcom G5, xDrip (releases February 3 and February 11, 2021) logs that calibrations are rejected even though the G5 transmitter accepted them; the calibration graph/table are unavailable/empty and only \"Initial calibration\" remains in the top-left menu. The title also reports that xDrip performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6.", "cause": "The thread states that xDrip confuses the Dexcom G5 with a G6 (specifically a Firefly G6, which does not send raw data) and treats it accordingly; this is attributed to a regression in the February 3–11, 2021 xDrip releases, though no deeper root cause is identified in the thread.", "fix": "Navid200's stated solution/workaround is to go back to the January 29, 2021 xDrip release; trying the February 17, 2021 nightly was also suggested and initially seemed to resolve the issue. Later reports indicate day-6/day-9 restart behavior varied by version and no permanent code fix is described in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode"], "evidence_quote": "The only solution I am aware of, until a developer addresses this, is to go back to the release of January 29, 2021.", "text": "xDrip confuses G5 with a G6 and performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6 In native mode with a Dexcom G5, xDrip (releases February 3 and February 11, 2021) logs that calibrations are rejected even though the G5 transmitter accepted them; the calibration graph/table are unavailable/empty and only \"Initial calibration\" remains in the top-left menu. The title also reports that xDrip performs a preemptive restart on day 9 as well as on day 6. The thread states that xDrip confuses the Dexcom G5 with a G6 (specifically a Firefly G6, which does not send raw data) and treats it accordingly; this is attributed to a regression in the February 3–11, 2021 xDrip releases, though no deeper root cause is identified in the thread. Navid200's stated solution/workaround is to go back to the January 29, 2021 xDrip release; trying the February 17, 2021 nightly was also suggested and initially seemed to resolve the issue. Later reports indicate day-6/day-9 restart behavior varied by version and no permanent code fix is described in the thread. Dexcom G5 native mode The only solution I am aware of, until a developer addresses this, is to go back to the release of January 29, 2021."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1653", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1653, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1653, "title": "Can we rename \"HbA1c est\" to \"GMI\", and update the formula?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1653", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1653", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The HbA1c estimation in xDrip is based on average glucose over selected time periods (e.g., today, 7 days) which is not statistically valid for estimating A1C, as A1C reflects average glucose over the past 90 days. This could mislead users.", "cause": "The formula used for HbA1c estimation is applied to averages over periods shorter than 90 days, which is an incorrect use of the formula.", "fix": "The thread discusses renaming 'HbA1c est' to 'GMI' and updating the formula, but no final resolution was reached. The issue was put on hold pending wider adoption of GMI.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I have put a hold on this to see if the new (updated) formula is used universally or not. We should not update if no one picks it up.", "text": "Can we rename \"HbA1c est\" to \"GMI\", and update the formula? The HbA1c estimation in xDrip is based on average glucose over selected time periods (e.g., today, 7 days) which is not statistically valid for estimating A1C, as A1C reflects average glucose over the past 90 days. This could mislead users. The formula used for HbA1c estimation is applied to averages over periods shorter than 90 days, which is an incorrect use of the formula. The thread discusses renaming 'HbA1c est' to 'GMI' and updating the formula, but no final resolution was reached. The issue was put on hold pending wider adoption of GMI.   I have put a hold on this to see if the new (updated) formula is used universally or not. We should not update if no one picks it up."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1661", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1661, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1661, "title": "FR: upload and download xdrip config from / to central server", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1661", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1661", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After a phone outage, the user had to manually restore the entire xDrip configuration (data collector, uploads, alarms, etc.), which was a lot of work. They want to store and restore the whole xDrip config (and possibly the whole database) on a central config server.", "cause": null, "fix": "The thread discusses implementing a WebDAV backup/restore feature. The user (gruoner) states they implemented a webdav upload/restore feature, and later a PR #2269 was opened. Additionally, xDrip can now create a backup on Google Drive and restore from it, but the user notes that doesn't address their need because they use an Android device without Google apps.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "i'm currently working on a webdav backup/restore feature (it's useless to upload all of xdrip's db entities (tables) to dedicated nightscout mongo-collections, so i will use the existing backup/restore functions and add just a webdav protocol handling).", "text": "FR: upload and download xdrip config from / to central server After a phone outage, the user had to manually restore the entire xDrip configuration (data collector, uploads, alarms, etc.), which was a lot of work. They want to store and restore the whole xDrip config (and possibly the whole database) on a central config server.  The thread discusses implementing a WebDAV backup/restore feature. The user (gruoner) states they implemented a webdav upload/restore feature, and later a PR #2269 was opened. Additionally, xDrip can now create a backup on Google Drive and restore from it, but the user notes that doesn't address their need because they use an Android device without Google apps.   i'm currently working on a webdav backup/restore feature (it's useless to upload all of xdrip's db entities (tables) to dedicated nightscout mongo-collections, so i will use the existing backup/restore functions and add just a webdav protocol handling)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1687", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1687, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1687, "title": "Bluetooth, Android 10, disconnects when not on charge", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1687", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1687", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Since update to Android 10, there are frequent disconnects. When the phone is on charge, there is no disconnect. The Dexcom app has no issue on the same phone.", "cause": "The thread suggests that Android's battery optimization interferes with xDrip running in the background, especially on OPPO's Color OS with strict battery saving management. The issue is likely due to vendor-specific adaptations to Android.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Suggestions include disabling battery optimization, disabling Nightscout upload, and whitelisting xDrip, but these did not resolve the issue. The issue was closed without a solution.", "settings_changed": ["Battery optimization → disabled", "Nightscout Sync (REST-API) → disabled"], "devices": ["G6 8P", "Oppo Reno 2", "Moto E7"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Nightscout", "API Upload"], "evidence_quote": "Every time I have seen this behavior, after an upgrade to Android 10, it has been resolved after the battery optimization was disabled and after the xDrip settings were corrected to match the recommended Android 10 xDrip settings. This is the only case I have seen where the problem has persisted.", "text": "Bluetooth, Android 10, disconnects when not on charge Since update to Android 10, there are frequent disconnects. When the phone is on charge, there is no disconnect. The Dexcom app has no issue on the same phone. The thread suggests that Android's battery optimization interferes with xDrip running in the background, especially on OPPO's Color OS with strict battery saving management. The issue is likely due to vendor-specific adaptations to Android. The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Suggestions include disabling battery optimization, disabling Nightscout upload, and whitelisting xDrip, but these did not resolve the issue. The issue was closed without a solution. G6 8P Oppo Reno 2 Moto E7 Android 10 Nightscout API Upload Every time I have seen this behavior, after an upgrade to Android 10, it has been resolved after the battery optimization was disabled and after the xDrip settings were corrected to match the recommended Android 10 xDrip settings. This is the only case I have seen where the problem has persisted."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1690", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1690, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1690, "title": "xDrip detect future data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1690", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1690", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "On the main page xDrip shows the last glucose update was 182 minutes ago, and the Status page reports \"Your device has future data on it, Please double check the time and timezone on this phone\". The log viewer shows NonMonotonicSequenceException errors caused by non-increasing timestamps, and readings are not passed to Nightscout or fetched from Miao Miao. Restarting the collector, forgetting the device and deleting future data do not help.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["FreeStyle Libre 1", "Miao Miao 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In Status page I can see message \"Your device has future data on it, Please double check the time and timezone on this phone\" Restarting collector, forgetting device, deleting future data do not help.", "text": "xDrip detect future data On the main page xDrip shows the last glucose update was 182 minutes ago, and the Status page reports \"Your device has future data on it, Please double check the time and timezone on this phone\". The log viewer shows NonMonotonicSequenceException errors caused by non-increasing timestamps, and readings are not passed to Nightscout or fetched from Miao Miao. Restarting the collector, forgetting the device and deleting future data do not help.   FreeStyle Libre 1 Miao Miao 2 Android 10  In Status page I can see message \"Your device has future data on it, Please double check the time and timezone on this phone\" Restarting collector, forgetting device, deleting future data do not help."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1692", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1692, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1692, "title": "Original Dexcom Reciver loses connection.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1692", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1692", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "With xDrip version 210204 or newer, the original Dexcom receiver cannot establish a connection to the transmitter; xDrip itself still works. After going back to version 210203, the receiver reconnects and shows the new value.", "cause": "A change in xDrip code between 2021.02.03 and 2021.02.04 is the regression point; newer xDrip builds interfere with the original receiver because disabling xDrip's collection restores receiver operation. Low transmitter battery was initially suspected but ruled out when the problem continued with higher-voltage transmitters.", "fix": "No permanent code fix is offered; the workaround is to stay on xDrip version 210203, the last version where the original Dexcom receiver still works. With newer versions, temporarily selecting Settings -> Hardware Data Source -> Disable Collection lets the receiver connect again, but stops xDrip readings.", "settings_changed": ["Hardware Data Source → Disable Collection", "Hardware Data Source → G5/G6 Transmitter"], "devices": ["original Dexcom receiver", "Samsung S10", "transmitter"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["dexcom collector", "g5/g6 transmitter"], "evidence_quote": "Something changed, in the xDrip code, from Feb. 3 to Feb. 4 that is causing this considering that the same transmitter works fine with the same receiver with one version and not with the other.", "text": "Original Dexcom Reciver loses connection. With xDrip version 210204 or newer, the original Dexcom receiver cannot establish a connection to the transmitter; xDrip itself still works. After going back to version 210203, the receiver reconnects and shows the new value. A change in xDrip code between 2021.02.03 and 2021.02.04 is the regression point; newer xDrip builds interfere with the original receiver because disabling xDrip's collection restores receiver operation. Low transmitter battery was initially suspected but ruled out when the problem continued with higher-voltage transmitters. No permanent code fix is offered; the workaround is to stay on xDrip version 210203, the last version where the original Dexcom receiver still works. With newer versions, temporarily selecting Settings -> Hardware Data Source -> Disable Collection lets the receiver connect again, but stops xDrip readings. original Dexcom receiver Samsung S10 transmitter Android 11 dexcom collector g5/g6 transmitter Something changed, in the xDrip code, from Feb. 3 to Feb. 4 that is causing this considering that the same transmitter works fine with the same receiver with one version and not with the other."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1700", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1700, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1700, "title": "Local Broadcast of calibation from AAPS aren't  registered in calibation data table or graph.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1700", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1700", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When using the calibration feature of AAPS, the toast notification 'Calibration sent to Xdrip+' appears in AAPS and a 'jamorham nsreceiver' event log says 'Processing broadcasted calibation: X.XX offset ms: YY' in Xdrip+ log, but the calibration is not taken into account as it is not visible in Calibration Data table or Calibration graph. No other event related to the calibration is visible in the log after that. Out of about 20 attempts, it worked normally only 2 times, but the reason for those successes is unknown.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["local broadcast", "inter-app", "calibration"], "evidence_quote": "When using the calibation feature of AAPS, I get the toast notification \"Calibration sent to Xdrip+\" in AAPS and I can see a 'jamorham nsreceiver' event log saying \"Processing broadcasted calibation: X.XX offset ms: YY\" in Xdrip+ log, but the calibation isn't taken into account as it is not visible in Calibation Data table or Calibation graph.", "text": "Local Broadcast of calibation from AAPS aren't  registered in calibation data table or graph. When using the calibration feature of AAPS, the toast notification 'Calibration sent to Xdrip+' appears in AAPS and a 'jamorham nsreceiver' event log says 'Processing broadcasted calibation: X.XX offset ms: YY' in Xdrip+ log, but the calibration is not taken into account as it is not visible in Calibration Data table or Calibration graph. No other event related to the calibration is visible in the log after that. Out of about 20 attempts, it worked normally only 2 times, but the reason for those successes is unknown.   Libre 2 Android 10 local broadcast inter-app calibration When using the calibation feature of AAPS, I get the toast notification \"Calibration sent to Xdrip+\" in AAPS and I can see a 'jamorham nsreceiver' event log saying \"Processing broadcasted calibation: X.XX offset ms: YY\" in Xdrip+ log, but the calibation isn't taken into account as it is not visible in Calibation Data table or Calibation graph."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1705", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1705, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1705, "title": "Importing data didn't display data and wiped settings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1705", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1705", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After wiping xDrip app data and cache, restoring settings and importing the exported database reports success, but no data is imported and the restored settings are wiped again. Repeating the import gives the same blank screen and cleared settings. Other users report the same on Android 11/12: the import says success but no data appears.", "cause": null, "fix": "Switch to the new Google Drive cloud backup methodology instead of the legacy zip import/export. On the old phone, create a Cloud Backup via the three-dots menu > Import/Export features > Cloud Backup. On the new phone, download that backup file, then in Cloud Backup > SELECT BACKUP LOCATION choose USE ALTERNATE FILE to select the downloaded file and tap RESTORE FROM BACKUP. One user also succeeded by restoring the zip on an older Android 8 phone, uploading it to Google Drive, and restoring from there on the Android 11 phone.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Galaxy Note 10+", "Samsung Galaxy S10e"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 10", "Android 12", "Android 8.1", "Android 8", "Android 5.5"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The solution is to switch to the new backup methodology to Google Drive. That means when you buy a new phone, backup the database from the old phone using the new backup methodology, Google Drive Backup. Then, restore it on the new phone using the Google Drive Backup methodology. If you do that and it doesn't work, please let us know.", "text": "Importing data didn't display data and wiped settings After wiping xDrip app data and cache, restoring settings and importing the exported database reports success, but no data is imported and the restored settings are wiped again. Repeating the import gives the same blank screen and cleared settings. Other users report the same on Android 11/12: the import says success but no data appears.  Switch to the new Google Drive cloud backup methodology instead of the legacy zip import/export. On the old phone, create a Cloud Backup via the three-dots menu > Import/Export features > Cloud Backup. On the new phone, download that backup file, then in Cloud Backup > SELECT BACKUP LOCATION choose USE ALTERNATE FILE to select the downloaded file and tap RESTORE FROM BACKUP. One user also succeeded by restoring the zip on an older Android 8 phone, uploading it to Google Drive, and restoring from there on the Android 11 phone. Galaxy Note 10+ Samsung Galaxy S10e Android 11 Android 10 Android 12 Android 8.1 Android 8 Android 5.5  The solution is to switch to the new backup methodology to Google Drive. That means when you buy a new phone, backup the database from the old phone using the new backup methodology, Google Drive Backup. Then, restore it on the new phone using the Google Drive Backup methodology. If you do that and it doesn't work, please let us know."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-171", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 171, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 171, "title": "Broken Watchface with patched/Nfc enabled Sony watch", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/171", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/171", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After patching a Sony SmartWatch 3 to enable NFC for reading a Libre CGM, the xDrip+ watchface stopped working: it stays empty, receives no data, sometimes no time or battery status. Newer xDrip+ versions also cause xdrip-prefs to crash when changing settings. An older version from June 2017 works.", "cause": "The watchface issue is likely due to outdated Google Play services on the watch (requires version 9.x, found 7.8.9). The xdrip-prefs crash is the same as issue #167 and is fixed in the Sept 8th nightly.", "fix": "Update Google Play services on the watch to version 9.8.41 by installing the APK with 'adb install -r' (to upgrade). Also install the latest nightly build of xDrip+ to fix the prefs crash.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Sony SmartWatch 3", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NFC", "patched watch", "watchface"], "evidence_quote": "Wuhu, seems to work now. Had to install the 9.8.41 version of play services. Older versions got me crashes and atempts to update, newer version i got error messages \"old sdk\" while installation. Watchface works now with the newest nightly build of xdrip+, also the syncing between watch and phone.", "text": "Broken Watchface with patched/Nfc enabled Sony watch After patching a Sony SmartWatch 3 to enable NFC for reading a Libre CGM, the xDrip+ watchface stopped working: it stays empty, receives no data, sometimes no time or battery status. Newer xDrip+ versions also cause xdrip-prefs to crash when changing settings. An older version from June 2017 works. The watchface issue is likely due to outdated Google Play services on the watch (requires version 9.x, found 7.8.9). The xdrip-prefs crash is the same as issue #167 and is fixed in the Sept 8th nightly. Update Google Play services on the watch to version 9.8.41 by installing the APK with 'adb install -r' (to upgrade). Also install the latest nightly build of xDrip+ to fix the prefs crash. Sony SmartWatch 3 Libre NFC patched watch watchface Wuhu, seems to work now. Had to install the 9.8.41 version of play services. Older versions got me crashes and atempts to update, newer version i got error messages \"old sdk\" while installation. Watchface works now with the newest nightly build of xdrip+, also the syncing between watch and phone."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1730", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1730, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1730, "title": " xDrip occupies too much storage space on the phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1730", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1730", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip occupies too much storage space on the phone, increasing from 791 MB to 836 MB in one day. The database backup is 768 MB uncompressed.", "cause": "The xDrip app had a bug that reset the application at least 30 times a day, preventing it from reaching 24 hours to clean old data, so it kept loading more and more data.", "fix": "Generate a backup of the data for repair, uninstall and reinstall the application.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1.0"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Solucionado Gracias a un desarrollador argentino hemos encontrado el inconveniente se daba en que xdrip contenia un fallo que reseteaba la aplicacion al menos 30 veces al dia, por lo cual no podia llegar a 24 horas para limpiar datos viejos y asi iba cargando cada vez mas y mas datos. La solucion consistio en generar un backup de los datos para su reparacion, desinstalar y reinstalar la aplicacion.", "text": " xDrip occupies too much storage space on the phone xDrip occupies too much storage space on the phone, increasing from 791 MB to 836 MB in one day. The database backup is 768 MB uncompressed. The xDrip app had a bug that reset the application at least 30 times a day, preventing it from reaching 24 hours to clean old data, so it kept loading more and more data. Generate a backup of the data for repair, uninstall and reinstall the application. Android 8.1.0  Solucionado Gracias a un desarrollador argentino hemos encontrado el inconveniente se daba en que xdrip contenia un fallo que reseteaba la aplicacion al menos 30 veces al dia, por lo cual no podia llegar a 24 horas para limpiar datos viejos y asi iba cargando cada vez mas y mas datos. La solucion consistio en generar un backup de los datos para su reparacion, desinstalar y reinstalar la aplicacion."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1749", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1749, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1749, "title": "Indexes are not used efficiently", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1749", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1749", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip gets slower over time as the database grows, indicating that indexes are not used efficiently.", "cause": "The thread suggests that the lack of running the ANALYZE command on the SQLite database may lead to outdated index statistics, causing the query optimizer to not use indexes effectively.", "fix": "The thread suggests running ANALYZE on database connection close, and possibly revising the ORM layer and queries. A later comment references a pull request #2052 as providing a solution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "As far as I can tell, we never run the ANALYZE command, so maybe running it is a good thing.", "text": "Indexes are not used efficiently xDrip gets slower over time as the database grows, indicating that indexes are not used efficiently. The thread suggests that the lack of running the ANALYZE command on the SQLite database may lead to outdated index statistics, causing the query optimizer to not use indexes effectively. The thread suggests running ANALYZE on database connection close, and possibly revising the ORM layer and queries. A later comment references a pull request #2052 as providing a solution.   As far as I can tell, we never run the ANALYZE command, so maybe running it is a good thing."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1754", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1754, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1754, "title": "Support Novopen 6 / Echo Plus", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1754", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1754", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The Novopen 6 is released in Denmark probably globally also. It works with NFC and should be build to work with all the apps that wants to use it. If needed I could buy one and send it to someone who could get it to work with xdrip?", "cause": "Novo Nordisk cannot support the technical integration with their medical devices because Nightscout is an open-source solution that is not regulated by authorities. The integration is subject to medical device regulations.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Novopen 6", "NovoPen Echo Plus"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NFC"], "evidence_quote": "Novo Nordisk cannot at this point support the technical integration with our medical devices. We will encourage Nightscout to engage with the regulatory authorities, and we are happy to further engage in discussions about integrations with our devices.", "text": "Support Novopen 6 / Echo Plus The Novopen 6 is released in Denmark probably globally also. It works with NFC and should be build to work with all the apps that wants to use it. If needed I could buy one and send it to someone who could get it to work with xdrip? Novo Nordisk cannot support the technical integration with their medical devices because Nightscout is an open-source solution that is not regulated by authorities. The integration is subject to medical device regulations.  Novopen 6 NovoPen Echo Plus NFC Novo Nordisk cannot at this point support the technical integration with our medical devices. We will encourage Nightscout to engage with the regulatory authorities, and we are happy to further engage in discussions about integrations with our devices."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1758", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1758, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1758, "title": "After NFC Scan of Libre 2 no BG readings appear in xDrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1758", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1758", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating xDrip to build 11 June 2021, NFC scan of FSL2 sensor running via OOPAlgorithm2 causes BT connection to sensor to be disabled and needs re-establishing. Also, after a BT loss of about 15 minutes, an NFC scan does not fill in missing records, which the May 21 version did. Other users report similar issues with Libre 1 and Libre 2, including NFC scan doing nothing when there are missing data points, and error messages like 'sensor clock didn't advance'.", "cause": "Two issues were identified: 1) Not always using only the first 0x158 bytes of the data. 2) In the case of Libre2, not allowing flags == 0 as a legal packet.", "fix": "A fix was provided in a test APK that ensures only the first 0x158 bytes of data are used and allows flags == 0 as a legal packet for Libre2. Users were instructed to download the APK, remove the .zip extension, backup settings and db, uninstall the current version, and install the new one.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "Libre 1"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OOPAlgorithm2", "OOP2", "NFC scan", "Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "There have been two issues here: 1) Make sure we always use only the first 0x158 bytes of the data. 2) In the case of libre2, also allow flags == 0 as a legal packet. The following link should solve both.", "text": "After NFC Scan of Libre 2 no BG readings appear in xDrip After updating xDrip to build 11 June 2021, NFC scan of FSL2 sensor running via OOPAlgorithm2 causes BT connection to sensor to be disabled and needs re-establishing. Also, after a BT loss of about 15 minutes, an NFC scan does not fill in missing records, which the May 21 version did. Other users report similar issues with Libre 1 and Libre 2, including NFC scan doing nothing when there are missing data points, and error messages like 'sensor clock didn't advance'. Two issues were identified: 1) Not always using only the first 0x158 bytes of the data. 2) In the case of Libre2, not allowing flags == 0 as a legal packet. A fix was provided in a test APK that ensures only the first 0x158 bytes of data are used and allows flags == 0 as a legal packet for Libre2. Users were instructed to download the APK, remove the .zip extension, backup settings and db, uninstall the current version, and install the new one. Libre 2 Libre 1 OOPAlgorithm2 OOP2 NFC scan Bluetooth There have been two issues here: 1) Make sure we always use only the first 0x158 bytes of the data. 2) In the case of libre2, also allow flags == 0 as a legal packet. The following link should solve both."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1770", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1770, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1770, "title": "Backfilled data incompletely fetched from Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1770", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1770", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip does not fetch all backfilled data from Nightscout, resulting in gaps in the follower's data even though the data is present on Nightscout. The log shows 'Cannot inject display glucose value as time difference too great' messages.", "cause": "The follower remembers the last reading time and only requests data from that point onward. If the collector uploads recent data first and then backfills older data, the follower misses the backfilled data because it doesn't request data before its last reading.", "fix": "No fix was provided. The issue was closed with a comment suggesting that using Nightscout as a repository and accessing it via browser may be sufficient, and asking if there is a reason the follower needs backfill.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 7", "Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Nightscout", "follower", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "xDrip remembers the last time that it was doing the last read. (In other words, if xDrip is reading now, and the last read is from 10:00:00, than xDrip will read again asking for data from 10:00:00 and after it).", "text": "Backfilled data incompletely fetched from Nightscout xDrip does not fetch all backfilled data from Nightscout, resulting in gaps in the follower's data even though the data is present on Nightscout. The log shows 'Cannot inject display glucose value as time difference too great' messages. The follower remembers the last reading time and only requests data from that point onward. If the collector uploads recent data first and then backfills older data, the follower misses the backfilled data because it doesn't request data before its last reading. No fix was provided. The issue was closed with a comment suggesting that using Nightscout as a repository and accessing it via browser may be sufficient, and asking if there is a reason the follower needs backfill. Android 7 Android 10 Nightscout follower collector xDrip remembers the last time that it was doing the last read. (In other words, if xDrip is reading now, and the last read is from 10:00:00, than xDrip will read again asking for data from 10:00:00 and after it)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1778", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1778, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1778, "title": "G6 Timestamp Issue when newly activated.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1778", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1778", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When first activating a G6 transmitter, xDrip incorrectly reports timestamps as negative for the first few hours because the transmitter's internal time starts from 0ms. This prevents xDrip from generating packets that need a timestamp (like backfill requests) for the first few hours after activation.", "cause": "The transmitter timestamp before transmitter start is being requested, likely from backfilling. The backfill window is not capped to the transmitter start time, so requests are made for times before the transmitter's internal clock reaches zero.", "fix": "Cap the backfill window to the transmitter start (or session start) time. The fix was implemented in the Nightly build of March 10, 2024, and tested successfully with G6 and G7.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Dexcom G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["backfill"], "evidence_quote": "I expect this will come from backfilling and simply capping the backfill window to the transmitter start (or session start) would resolve the issue.", "text": "G6 Timestamp Issue when newly activated. When first activating a G6 transmitter, xDrip incorrectly reports timestamps as negative for the first few hours because the transmitter's internal time starts from 0ms. This prevents xDrip from generating packets that need a timestamp (like backfill requests) for the first few hours after activation. The transmitter timestamp before transmitter start is being requested, likely from backfilling. The backfill window is not capped to the transmitter start time, so requests are made for times before the transmitter's internal clock reaches zero. Cap the backfill window to the transmitter start (or session start) time. The fix was implemented in the Nightly build of March 10, 2024, and tested successfully with G6 and G7. Dexcom G6 Dexcom G7 backfill I expect this will come from backfilling and simply capping the backfill window to the transmitter start (or session start) would resolve the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1789", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1789, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1789, "title": "xDrip+ stop pairing, won't send pair request, when using Fitbit versa lite", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1789", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1789", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip+ stops pairing with the Dexcom G6 transmitter and does not send a pairing request notification, even though the log says it did. The issue occurs when using a Fitbit Versa Lite watch with the Fitbit app installed. Uninstalling the Fitbit app resolves the issue temporarily, but it returns after reinstalling. The problem has been occurring intermittently for months.", "cause": "The thread suggests the issue is caused by interference from the Fitbit app, possibly related to how it intercepts Bluetooth pairing requests. However, the exact mechanism is not confirmed, and later comments indicate the issue may also occur without the Fitbit app, suggesting multiple causes.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Workarounds include uninstalling the Fitbit app, disabling the smartwatch, restarting the phone, and updating to the latest Nightly version. The maintainer suggests that the issue is due to Fitbit app interference and that xDrip cannot fix it, recommending to keep xDrip updated and to use discussions for further help.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Fitbit Versa Lite", "Moto G Power (2020)", "Fossil Sport", "Samsung Galaxy S10e", "Ticwatch Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["companion app"], "evidence_quote": "This issue was rather about the interference caused by fitbit. And it looks like that is something to do with the fitbit app and not xDrip.", "text": "xDrip+ stop pairing, won't send pair request, when using Fitbit versa lite xDrip+ stops pairing with the Dexcom G6 transmitter and does not send a pairing request notification, even though the log says it did. The issue occurs when using a Fitbit Versa Lite watch with the Fitbit app installed. Uninstalling the Fitbit app resolves the issue temporarily, but it returns after reinstalling. The problem has been occurring intermittently for months. The thread suggests the issue is caused by interference from the Fitbit app, possibly related to how it intercepts Bluetooth pairing requests. However, the exact mechanism is not confirmed, and later comments indicate the issue may also occur without the Fitbit app, suggesting multiple causes. The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Workarounds include uninstalling the Fitbit app, disabling the smartwatch, restarting the phone, and updating to the latest Nightly version. The maintainer suggests that the issue is due to Fitbit app interference and that xDrip cannot fix it, recommending to keep xDrip updated and to use discussions for further help. Dexcom G6 Fitbit Versa Lite Moto G Power (2020) Fossil Sport Samsung Galaxy S10e Ticwatch Pro Android 11 companion app This issue was rather about the interference caused by fitbit. And it looks like that is something to do with the fitbit app and not xDrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1791", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1791, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1791, "title": "not possible to scroll in preferences page or open subpreferences", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1791", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1791", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On Android 12, when trying to navigate or change preferences, the window always returns up when scrolling down, and entering another preference section returns to the first preference page, making it impossible to scroll or open subpreferences.", "cause": "The issue occurs when the lockscreen wallpaper feature is turned on in Android 12 beta.", "fix": "Disable the lockscreen wallpaper feature in Android 12 settings.", "settings_changed": ["lockscreen wallpaper → off"], "devices": ["Pixel 4a"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I have found this happens if the lockscreen wallpaper feature is turned on when running Android 12 beta.", "text": "not possible to scroll in preferences page or open subpreferences On Android 12, when trying to navigate or change preferences, the window always returns up when scrolling down, and entering another preference section returns to the first preference page, making it impossible to scroll or open subpreferences. The issue occurs when the lockscreen wallpaper feature is turned on in Android 12 beta. Disable the lockscreen wallpaper feature in Android 12 settings. Pixel 4a Android 12  I have found this happens if the lockscreen wallpaper feature is turned on when running Android 12 beta."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1793", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1793, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1793, "title": "Different notification channels for persistent foreground collector notification and number icon", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1793", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1793", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The persistent notification for the foreground collector and the number icon use the same notification channel, so hiding one hides the other. The user wants to hide the persistent collector notification while keeping the number icon.", "cause": "The persistent foreground collector notification and the number icon share the same notification channel (Ongoing notification), so Android cannot hide one without the other.", "fix": "A separate notification channel was created for the number icon, but this results in two notifications. Instead, the developer made the existing notification very small as an alternative.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I created a separate notification channel for the number icon. The problem is that we will end up with two different notifications! After you disable the persistent notification, you will have one notification. There is no way to eliminate the notification. Showing the number icon is done through a notification. So, I decided to follow your other preferences of having the option of making the existing notification very small.", "text": "Different notification channels for persistent foreground collector notification and number icon The persistent notification for the foreground collector and the number icon use the same notification channel, so hiding one hides the other. The user wants to hide the persistent collector notification while keeping the number icon. The persistent foreground collector notification and the number icon share the same notification channel (Ongoing notification), so Android cannot hide one without the other. A separate notification channel was created for the number icon, but this results in two notifications. Instead, the developer made the existing notification very small as an alternative. Android 11  I created a separate notification channel for the number icon. The problem is that we will end up with two different notifications! After you disable the persistent notification, you will have one notification. There is no way to eliminate the notification. Showing the number icon is done through a notification. So, I decided to follow your other preferences of having the option of making the existing notification very small."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1795", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1795, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1795, "title": "Request for fingerstick data entry", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1795", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1795", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Users of xDrip cannot use a CGM due to warm-up, dead batteries, etc., and when entering fingerstick data, xDrip telemetry ceases to display after 24 hours, losing insulin treatment input, carb treatment, IOB, and predictive trends.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Occasionally xdrip users cannot use a CGM due to warm-up, dead batteries, etc. Entering fingerstick data can maintain diabetic control (old school) until a CGM is brought back online. Bg prediction, IOB, and carb recommendations are available for 24 hours. However, subsequently all telemetry ceases to display.", "text": "Request for fingerstick data entry Users of xDrip cannot use a CGM due to warm-up, dead batteries, etc., and when entering fingerstick data, xDrip telemetry ceases to display after 24 hours, losing insulin treatment input, carb treatment, IOB, and predictive trends.     Occasionally xdrip users cannot use a CGM due to warm-up, dead batteries, etc. Entering fingerstick data can maintain diabetic control (old school) until a CGM is brought back online. Bg prediction, IOB, and carb recommendations are available for 24 hours. However, subsequently all telemetry ceases to display."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1796", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1796, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1796, "title": "Issues with nightly build 2021.08.01", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1796", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1796", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The glycemic value is not shown on the main screen and in the system notification, even though the sensor is active and the graph shows readings. Some users also report that the blood glucose data table and calibration table could not be called up.", "cause": "The issue was introduced in the nightly build 2021.08.01 and was resolved in subsequent builds. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated in the thread.", "fix": "Users were advised to try the latest nightly build (2021.08.02) which resolved the issue for most. For those still experiencing problems, rolling back to the 2021.07.31 build was recommended. A subsequent build (2021.08.02b) fixed the related issue with BG and calibration tables.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Please try the latest nightly, it is also available here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/download/2021.08.02/xDrip-plus-20210802-0af3ba0.apk If it doesn't work just roll back to the 31st July version by simply installing that over the top.", "text": "Issues with nightly build 2021.08.01 The glycemic value is not shown on the main screen and in the system notification, even though the sensor is active and the graph shows readings. Some users also report that the blood glucose data table and calibration table could not be called up. The issue was introduced in the nightly build 2021.08.01 and was resolved in subsequent builds. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated in the thread. Users were advised to try the latest nightly build (2021.08.02) which resolved the issue for most. For those still experiencing problems, rolling back to the 2021.07.31 build was recommended. A subsequent build (2021.08.02b) fixed the related issue with BG and calibration tables. Dexcom G5 Android 11 Android 12  Please try the latest nightly, it is also available here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/download/2021.08.02/xDrip-plus-20210802-0af3ba0.apk If it doesn't work just roll back to the 31st July version by simply installing that over the top."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1797", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1797, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1797, "title": "Tasker plugin vanished", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1797", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1797", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating to version 2021.08.02, the Tasker plugin no longer registers with Tasker. Tasker fires a 'Missing Plugin' notification when a task calls xDrip+, and the task does not fire. Reverting to 2021.07.31 restores the plugin.", "cause": "The issue was caused by package renaming changes that affected the Tasker plugin's registration with Tasker.", "fix": "The fix was to exclude Tasker from package renaming, which was done in version 2021.08.02c. The user confirmed that this version resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tasker"], "evidence_quote": "Issue is solved by excluding Tasker from package renaming.", "text": "Tasker plugin vanished After updating to version 2021.08.02, the Tasker plugin no longer registers with Tasker. Tasker fires a 'Missing Plugin' notification when a task calls xDrip+, and the task does not fire. Reverting to 2021.07.31 restores the plugin. The issue was caused by package renaming changes that affected the Tasker plugin's registration with Tasker. The fix was to exclude Tasker from package renaming, which was done in version 2021.08.02c. The user confirmed that this version resolved the issue.  tasker Issue is solved by excluding Tasker from package renaming."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1799", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1799, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1799, "title": "Current bg level notification on WearOS", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1799", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1799", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "On WearOS, the user only receives low alarm, high alarm, or bg reading missed alert notifications, but not the current bg level notification that appears on the phone. The user suspects the graph in the notification might prevent the watch from rendering it, and asks if the graph can be removed.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive cause. It is speculated that the graph in the notification might not be renderable on the watch, but this is not confirmed.", "fix": "No fix is provided. The issue was converted to a discussion because no active developer supports WearOS.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Moto 360 2nd gen"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear", "wear os"], "evidence_quote": "Maybe my Moto 360 2nd gen cannot render this graph (phone can and shows notification) and won't show notification at all. Adding a checkbox to show/hide graph from notifications and just show bg level and trend might fix this problem but I'm not 100% sure that is the problem.", "text": "Current bg level notification on WearOS On WearOS, the user only receives low alarm, high alarm, or bg reading missed alert notifications, but not the current bg level notification that appears on the phone. The user suspects the graph in the notification might prevent the watch from rendering it, and asks if the graph can be removed. The thread does not establish a definitive cause. It is speculated that the graph in the notification might not be renderable on the watch, but this is not confirmed. No fix is provided. The issue was converted to a discussion because no active developer supports WearOS. Moto 360 2nd gen wear wear os Maybe my Moto 360 2nd gen cannot render this graph (phone can and shows notification) and won't show notification at all. Adding a checkbox to show/hide graph from notifications and just show bg level and trend might fix this problem but I'm not 100% sure that is the problem."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1813", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1813, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1813, "title": "\"Motion Tracking\" feature in S21 phone not working", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1813", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1813", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Motion Tracking feature in xDrip+ does not work on Samsung Galaxy S21 5G / Android 11, while it worked on Samsung Galaxy S9 / Android 9. It is automatically disabled with a note that it may be incompatible with the phone.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests possible permission issues (Activity Recognition, Change system setting) and Android 10 changes to the Activity API, but no confirmed cause.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a confirmed fix. A user noted that 'Change system setting' permission was not allowed on the new phone and was testing if allowing it helps, but no outcome is reported. The issue was closed without resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S21 5G", "Samsung Galaxy S9"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["BYODA"], "evidence_quote": "But then I noticed that \"Change system setting\" was not \"Allow permissions\" in the new phone and allowed in the old phone. I am now testing with that if it helps.", "text": "\"Motion Tracking\" feature in S21 phone not working Motion Tracking feature in xDrip+ does not work on Samsung Galaxy S21 5G / Android 11, while it worked on Samsung Galaxy S9 / Android 9. It is automatically disabled with a note that it may be incompatible with the phone. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It suggests possible permission issues (Activity Recognition, Change system setting) and Android 10 changes to the Activity API, but no confirmed cause. The thread does not provide a confirmed fix. A user noted that 'Change system setting' permission was not allowed on the new phone and was testing if allowing it helps, but no outcome is reported. The issue was closed without resolution. Samsung Galaxy S21 5G Samsung Galaxy S9 Android 11 Android 9 BYODA But then I noticed that \"Change system setting\" was not \"Allow permissions\" in the new phone and allowed in the old phone. I am now testing with that if it helps."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1831", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1831, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1831, "title": "Android 10 NightScoutFollowService exception", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1831", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1831", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On Android 10, xDrip+ throws an exception in event logs: 'Got exception trying to use Android 10+ service starting for NightscoutFollowService java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: foregroundServiceType 0x0000....08 is not subset of foregroundServiceType attribute 0x00000000 in service element of manifest file'. Additionally, sending BG from xDrip to Android APS is not working or works only once.", "cause": "The data sync services of xDrip do not have the right foregroundServiceType in the manifest, causing the exception. However, the root cause of the BG sending issue is different and not identified in the thread.", "fix": "A fix was provided via a new APK (xDrip_20210923_7282febf4_DataForegroundServiceTypes_debug.apk) which resolved the exception. The BG sending issue was not resolved; the maintainer suggested using one xDrip instance as primary BG collector and broadcaster to AAPS, or considering issue #1649.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtronic 640", "Jelly 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["NightscoutFollowService", "broadcaster", "Android APS"], "evidence_quote": "The exception should be gone but I'm sure, the root cause of your problem is different because regardless of the exception, NightscoutFollowService is started, anyway.", "text": "Android 10 NightScoutFollowService exception On Android 10, xDrip+ throws an exception in event logs: 'Got exception trying to use Android 10+ service starting for NightscoutFollowService java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: foregroundServiceType 0x0000....08 is not subset of foregroundServiceType attribute 0x00000000 in service element of manifest file'. Additionally, sending BG from xDrip to Android APS is not working or works only once. The data sync services of xDrip do not have the right foregroundServiceType in the manifest, causing the exception. However, the root cause of the BG sending issue is different and not identified in the thread. A fix was provided via a new APK (xDrip_20210923_7282febf4_DataForegroundServiceTypes_debug.apk) which resolved the exception. The BG sending issue was not resolved; the maintainer suggested using one xDrip instance as primary BG collector and broadcaster to AAPS, or considering issue #1649. Medtronic 640 Jelly 2 Android 10 NightscoutFollowService broadcaster Android APS The exception should be gone but I'm sure, the root cause of your problem is different because regardless of the exception, NightscoutFollowService is started, anyway."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1836", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1836, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1836, "title": "Unable to start crash reporter as app is restarting too frequently", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1836", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1836", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After installing xDrip on a Samsung S21 to read from MiaoMiao/Libre, xDrip receives readings but closes as soon as the user taps Settings or History. Installing an older xDrip version (2021.01.02) made it worse, with xDrip crashing immediately on launch.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung S21", "MiaoMiao", "Libre"], "android_versions": ["Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["miaomiao", "libre"], "evidence_quote": "I followed the normal steps to set up xdrip, installed it, then it requested 2 callobration test results which I did provide and i started getting readings. When I tried to access settings to set up follower phones and set other functions, xDrip kept crashing the moment i press in settings.", "text": "Unable to start crash reporter as app is restarting too frequently After installing xDrip on a Samsung S21 to read from MiaoMiao/Libre, xDrip receives readings but closes as soon as the user taps Settings or History. Installing an older xDrip version (2021.01.02) made it worse, with xDrip crashing immediately on launch.   Samsung S21 MiaoMiao Libre Android 11 miaomiao libre I followed the normal steps to set up xdrip, installed it, then it requested 2 callobration test results which I did provide and i started getting readings. When I tried to access settings to set up follower phones and set other functions, xDrip kept crashing the moment i press in settings."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1839", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1839, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1839, "title": "Invalid slope/intercept values generated from BG report", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1839", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1839", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When blood glucose test result is entered (either manual or from bluetooth-enabled meter) xdrip can generate invalid slope/intercept values for calibration when 'Non-fixed Libre slopes' option is enabled. These values will be then ignored with 'invalid intercept value' error, so impossible to use for calibration.", "cause": "The slope/intercept calculation code does not check the generated values against the current calibration plugin's sanity limits, so it can produce intercept values above the hardcoded limit (e.g., 44), which are then rejected as invalid.", "fix": "The thread does not state a definitive fix. Workarounds mentioned include disabling 'Non-fixed Libre slopes' for first calibration, using fixed slope for first calibration at low range BG, and then re-enabling non-fixed slope for subsequent calibrations. Also, using an OOP (out-of-process) algorithm is suggested as an alternative.", "settings_changed": ["Non-fixed Libre slopes → disabled for first calibration", "Non-fixed Libre slopes → enabled after first calibration"], "devices": ["Libre 1", "miao2", "contour plus one"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Non-fixed Libre slopes", "OOP1", "vendor algorithm"], "evidence_quote": "In order to get it to work normally I usually deselect Non Fixed Slope to force slope to 1, then perform first calibration but deselect double calibration (which just duplicates the same value). Then I enable Non Fixed Slope to perform the next calibration.", "text": "Invalid slope/intercept values generated from BG report When blood glucose test result is entered (either manual or from bluetooth-enabled meter) xdrip can generate invalid slope/intercept values for calibration when 'Non-fixed Libre slopes' option is enabled. These values will be then ignored with 'invalid intercept value' error, so impossible to use for calibration. The slope/intercept calculation code does not check the generated values against the current calibration plugin's sanity limits, so it can produce intercept values above the hardcoded limit (e.g., 44), which are then rejected as invalid. The thread does not state a definitive fix. Workarounds mentioned include disabling 'Non-fixed Libre slopes' for first calibration, using fixed slope for first calibration at low range BG, and then re-enabling non-fixed slope for subsequent calibrations. Also, using an OOP (out-of-process) algorithm is suggested as an alternative. Libre 1 miao2 contour plus one Non-fixed Libre slopes OOP1 vendor algorithm In order to get it to work normally I usually deselect Non Fixed Slope to force slope to 1, then perform first calibration but deselect double calibration (which just duplicates the same value). Then I enable Non Fixed Slope to perform the next calibration."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-184", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 184, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 184, "title": "InfluxDB - change or add numeric field for \"direction\"", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/184", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/184", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user reports that the 'direction' field in InfluxDB is stored as a string, which cannot be visualized in Grafana with alerts or color mapping. They request adding a numeric field for direction to enable better visualization.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["influxdb", "grafana"], "evidence_quote": "Field \"Direction\" is now string, but Grafana can not visuale this filed (only on single stat as a text, without alerts, without mapping/colors)", "text": "InfluxDB - change or add numeric field for \"direction\" The user reports that the 'direction' field in InfluxDB is stored as a string, which cannot be visualized in Grafana with alerts or color mapping. They request adding a numeric field for direction to enable better visualization.    influxdb grafana Field \"Direction\" is now string, but Grafana can not visuale this filed (only on single stat as a text, without alerts, without mapping/colors)"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1848", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1848, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1848, "title": "Option to show Master battery level on xDrip+ Sync Followers", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1848", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1848", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "As xDrip+ Sync Followers, we cannot see the battery level of the Master device (our son's phone). This causes missed readings when his phone battery dies, potentially leading to hypoglycemia if his blood sugar drops during that time.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Palm Phone PVG100"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1"], "driver_tags": ["xDrip Sync Master", "xDrip Sync Follower", "Google Cloud Messaging"], "evidence_quote": "As xDrip+ Sync Followers, we'd like to be able to see the battery level of the Master device. That would be incredibly useful as we could tell our son in advance when to plug his phone.", "text": "Option to show Master battery level on xDrip+ Sync Followers As xDrip+ Sync Followers, we cannot see the battery level of the Master device (our son's phone). This causes missed readings when his phone battery dies, potentially leading to hypoglycemia if his blood sugar drops during that time.   Dexcom G6 Palm Phone PVG100 Android 8.1 xDrip Sync Master xDrip Sync Follower Google Cloud Messaging As xDrip+ Sync Followers, we'd like to be able to see the battery level of the Master device. That would be incredibly useful as we could tell our son in advance when to plug his phone."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1849", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1849, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1849, "title": "Dexcom Share: Ability to Specify Seconds Until Polling Retry or Allow Double Poll Retry", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1849", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1849", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When following a Dexcom G6 via Dexcom Share, the xDrip follower polls every 5 minutes; if the reading hasn't reached the Dexcom Share servers yet (often in low cellular signal areas), it waits a hard-coded 20 seconds, retries once, and if that still fails it waits another 5 minutes. This causes readings to be 5–10 minutes behind 30–40% of the time.", "cause": "xDrip polls the Dexcom Share server at the expected reading time, but the reading is frequently not yet uploaded (especially with low cellular signal), and the single hard-coded 20-second retry is too short; when that fails xDrip gives up until the next 5-minute cycle. A contributor also suspected a bug in the shared anticipation code (`Anticipate.java`).", "fix": "Workaround used by some participants: set the follower phone's system time 10–15 seconds behind real time. A maintainer implemented an optional delay for the Dexcom Share follower in PR #3663, but it was never merged and the issue/PR were closed.", "settings_changed": ["System time → 10-15 seconds behind real time"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dexcom share", "dex share", "dexcom share follow", "dexcom share follower", "nightscout follow", "nightscout follower", "byoda", "xdrip sync"], "evidence_quote": "What has alleviated having to manually restart the collector 50+ times each day was to use @olorinmaia suggestion to set the parent follower phone's system time 10-15 seconds behind real time.", "text": "Dexcom Share: Ability to Specify Seconds Until Polling Retry or Allow Double Poll Retry When following a Dexcom G6 via Dexcom Share, the xDrip follower polls every 5 minutes; if the reading hasn't reached the Dexcom Share servers yet (often in low cellular signal areas), it waits a hard-coded 20 seconds, retries once, and if that still fails it waits another 5 minutes. This causes readings to be 5–10 minutes behind 30–40% of the time. xDrip polls the Dexcom Share server at the expected reading time, but the reading is frequently not yet uploaded (especially with low cellular signal), and the single hard-coded 20-second retry is too short; when that fails xDrip gives up until the next 5-minute cycle. A contributor also suspected a bug in the shared anticipation code (`Anticipate.java`). Workaround used by some participants: set the follower phone's system time 10–15 seconds behind real time. A maintainer implemented an optional delay for the Dexcom Share follower in PR #3663, but it was never merged and the issue/PR were closed. Dexcom G6 dexcom share dex share dexcom share follow dexcom share follower nightscout follow nightscout follower byoda xdrip sync What has alleviated having to manually restart the collector 50+ times each day was to use @olorinmaia suggestion to set the parent follower phone's system time 10-15 seconds behind real time."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1850", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1850, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1850, "title": "Xdrip variant crash", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1850", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1850", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When going to settings, alarm and alerts, glucose level alert list, xdrip crashes and restarts. Same behavior on settings for missed reading alert. Also, recent xdrip variants don't have separate names like they have before; both xdrip on the phone have the same name, just 'xdrip'.", "cause": "Something wrong with the automated build process.", "fix": "Updated binaries provided in release 2021.10.13-variants resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Try these updated binaries. I think this should resolve the issue: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2021.10.13-variants", "text": "Xdrip variant crash When going to settings, alarm and alerts, glucose level alert list, xdrip crashes and restarts. Same behavior on settings for missed reading alert. Also, recent xdrip variants don't have separate names like they have before; both xdrip on the phone have the same name, just 'xdrip'. Something wrong with the automated build process. Updated binaries provided in release 2021.10.13-variants resolved the issue.   Try these updated binaries. I think this should resolve the issue: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2021.10.13-variants"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1857", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1857, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1857, "title": "Sending activity level and heart beat rate to nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1857", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1857", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests that activity level and heart rate data collected in xDrip be uploaded to Nightscout, as these are important for low predictions and determining activity state, especially for children.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Fitbit Versa 3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["engineering mode", "smartwatch sensors", "NightscoutUploader"], "evidence_quote": "I enabled engineering mode, but nothing happened about activity level.", "text": "Sending activity level and heart beat rate to nightscout The user requests that activity level and heart rate data collected in xDrip be uploaded to Nightscout, as these are important for low predictions and determining activity state, especially for children.   Fitbit Versa 3 engineering mode smartwatch sensors NightscoutUploader I enabled engineering mode, but nothing happened about activity level."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1859", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1859, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1859, "title": "XDrip+ is causing audio to pause", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1859", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1859", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "XDrip+ version c98a3c4-2021.10.17 is causing audio to pause when playing music/podcasts over Bluetooth. The pause happens when a connection is made with the G6 transmitter every 5 minutes, and is reproducible with all Bluetooth headphones and car Bluetooth. It also persisted after switching to the native Dexcom app.", "cause": "The thread identifies the Roku app installed on the phone, not XDrip+ or the Dexcom app, as the cause of the periodic Bluetooth audio pauses.", "fix": "Uninstall the Roku app completely. Removing media/file permission and clearing storage/cache did not help; only full uninstallation resolved the issue, as confirmed by several users.", "settings_changed": ["Gabeldorsche → ON", "disable BT A2DP Hardware offload → ON", "AVRCP version → 1.4", "dex source → none", "media & file permission → removed"], "devices": ["G6 transmitter", "Pixel 4a", "Samsung S20 FE", "pixel 5", "Samsung Galaxy S8+"], "android_versions": ["Android 11", "Android 12", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "UPDATE: The issue seems to be coming for the Roku app. Deleting the Roku app resolves the issue.", "text": "XDrip+ is causing audio to pause XDrip+ version c98a3c4-2021.10.17 is causing audio to pause when playing music/podcasts over Bluetooth. The pause happens when a connection is made with the G6 transmitter every 5 minutes, and is reproducible with all Bluetooth headphones and car Bluetooth. It also persisted after switching to the native Dexcom app. The thread identifies the Roku app installed on the phone, not XDrip+ or the Dexcom app, as the cause of the periodic Bluetooth audio pauses. Uninstall the Roku app completely. Removing media/file permission and clearing storage/cache did not help; only full uninstallation resolved the issue, as confirmed by several users. G6 transmitter Pixel 4a Samsung S20 FE pixel 5 Samsung Galaxy S8+ Android 11 Android 12 Android 9  UPDATE: The issue seems to be coming for the Roku app. Deleting the Roku app resolves the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1890", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1890, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1890, "title": "G6 On new sensor start, data with timestamp before new sensor was started is sent to NS and AAPS", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1890", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1890", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When a new G6 sensor is started, xDrip sends old data (data accumulated before the new sensor was started) to Nightscout and over the local broadcast. AAPS receives these duplicate Bg values and stops the loop.", "cause": "After starting a new G6 sensor, xDrip requests a backfill on the first reading; because de-duplication is filtered by sensor session, backfilled readings from the old sensor with slightly different timestamps are accepted and then broadcast/uploaded to NS/AAPS.", "fix": "Cap the backfill window start to the current sensor session start (commit 6f7c3660d6e140d914f24a155a0bcffa810ab4d8) so no data from before the current sensor session is backfilled; released in the January 14, 2022 nightly. The same change still needs to be applied to the wear collector before the issue can be fully closed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["broadcast", "backfill", "g5 native", "aaps", "ns", "wear collector"], "evidence_quote": "What I have done is capped the backfill window start to the current sensor session start which I'm thinking will have a similar effect.", "text": "G6 On new sensor start, data with timestamp before new sensor was started is sent to NS and AAPS When a new G6 sensor is started, xDrip sends old data (data accumulated before the new sensor was started) to Nightscout and over the local broadcast. AAPS receives these duplicate Bg values and stops the loop. After starting a new G6 sensor, xDrip requests a backfill on the first reading; because de-duplication is filtered by sensor session, backfilled readings from the old sensor with slightly different timestamps are accepted and then broadcast/uploaded to NS/AAPS. Cap the backfill window start to the current sensor session start (commit 6f7c3660d6e140d914f24a155a0bcffa810ab4d8) so no data from before the current sensor session is backfilled; released in the January 14, 2022 nightly. The same change still needs to be applied to the wear collector before the issue can be fully closed. G6 broadcast backfill g5 native aaps ns wear collector What I have done is capped the backfill window start to the current sensor session start which I'm thinking will have a similar effect."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1891", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1891, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1891, "title": "Number wall on lock screen causing other apps to restart", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1891", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1891", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "External Android apps appear to restart at the precise Xdrip+ polling interval: Chrome web content refreshes and clears unsubmitted input fields, social media feeds refresh to the top of the scroll, and YouTube videos stop and reset to the beginning. The reported symptom was later narrowed to the xDrip+ lock screen number wall refreshing every 5 minutes.", "cause": "The xDrip+ lock screen number wall refresh on Android 12 interrupts other apps, causing them to restart. Disabling the lock screen number display resolves it.", "fix": "Disable the xDrip+ lock screen number display / Number Wall feature. Removing the value from the lock screen was reported to 100% fix the issue.", "settings_changed": ["lockscreen number display → disabled"], "devices": ["Pixel 6 Pro", "Pixel 5", "Pixel 4a", "Pixel 6", "Pixel 4XL"], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["dexcom share", "640g/eversense", "miaomiao", "freestyle libre"], "evidence_quote": "Removing the value from the lock screen has 100% fixed the issue.", "text": "Number wall on lock screen causing other apps to restart External Android apps appear to restart at the precise Xdrip+ polling interval: Chrome web content refreshes and clears unsubmitted input fields, social media feeds refresh to the top of the scroll, and YouTube videos stop and reset to the beginning. The reported symptom was later narrowed to the xDrip+ lock screen number wall refreshing every 5 minutes. The xDrip+ lock screen number wall refresh on Android 12 interrupts other apps, causing them to restart. Disabling the lock screen number display resolves it. Disable the xDrip+ lock screen number display / Number Wall feature. Removing the value from the lock screen was reported to 100% fix the issue. Pixel 6 Pro Pixel 5 Pixel 4a Pixel 6 Pixel 4XL Android 12 Android 13 dexcom share 640g/eversense miaomiao freestyle libre Removing the value from the lock screen has 100% fixed the issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-1892", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 1892, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 1892, "title": "Problem Parsing Package on any attempted update", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1892", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/1892", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Every time I go to update xDrip (I'm running version 17cbcf0-2021.03.08) I get a pop up saying \"There was a problem parsing the package.\" Running on Android 12 December update on a Pixel 4 XL.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It is suggested that the error is raised by the Android package manager during installation, possibly due to a connection problem or an issue with the package, but no specific cause is confirmed.", "fix": "The user was able to install the update by installing it from the files app rather than directly through xDrip. The issue was not reproducible afterwards and was closed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel 4 XL"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I was able to install it over. The difference was that I installed it from the files app rather than directly through xdrip", "text": "Problem Parsing Package on any attempted update Every time I go to update xDrip (I'm running version 17cbcf0-2021.03.08) I get a pop up saying \"There was a problem parsing the package.\" Running on Android 12 December update on a Pixel 4 XL. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It is suggested that the error is raised by the Android package manager during installation, possibly due to a connection problem or an issue with the package, but no specific cause is confirmed. The user was able to install the update by installing it from the files app rather than directly through xDrip. The issue was not reproducible afterwards and was closed. Pixel 4 XL Android 12  I was able to install it over. The difference was that I installed it from the files app rather than directly through xdrip"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-193", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 193, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 193, "title": "Missed Readings override silent", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/193", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/193", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Missed reading alert does not sound when phone is on silent mode; it only vibrates. The alert seems to use the sound from 'Other Alerts' but does not respect the override silent mode setting.", "cause": "The missed reading alert does not make a sound when the phone's ring/notification volume is set to 0, because it does not use a volume profile. This is a known limitation affecting several alerts, not specific to missed readings.", "fix": "To make the missed reading alert override silent mode, enable 'Override Do Not Disturb' for xDrip in Android settings (Settings > Apps & notifications > Notifications > xDrip+). Then ensure override silent mode is enabled for the missed reading alert. However, if the phone's ring volume is set to 0, the alert will still not sound; raise the volume until the volume issue is fixed.", "settings_changed": ["Override Do Not Disturb → enabled (for xDrip in Android settings)"], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 11", "Android 12"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In the phone Android settings, please go to: Settings Apps & notifications -> Notifications -> xDrip+ Make sure \"Override Do Not Disturb\" is enabled.", "text": "Missed Readings override silent Missed reading alert does not sound when phone is on silent mode; it only vibrates. The alert seems to use the sound from 'Other Alerts' but does not respect the override silent mode setting. The missed reading alert does not make a sound when the phone's ring/notification volume is set to 0, because it does not use a volume profile. This is a known limitation affecting several alerts, not specific to missed readings. To make the missed reading alert override silent mode, enable 'Override Do Not Disturb' for xDrip in Android settings (Settings > Apps & notifications > Notifications > xDrip+). Then ensure override silent mode is enabled for the missed reading alert. However, if the phone's ring volume is set to 0, the alert will still not sound; raise the volume until the volume issue is fixed. Android 10 Android 11 Android 12  In the phone Android settings, please go to: Settings Apps & notifications -> Notifications -> xDrip+ Make sure \"Override Do Not Disturb\" is enabled."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-194", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 194, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 194, "title": "Feature Request: Allow user to choose if Nightscout upload uses noise smoothed or unprocessed data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/194", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/194", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "xDrip uploads to Nightscout always use unprocessed data, while xDrip displays data smoothed for noise, causing a mismatch for users who rely on Nightscout for data display.", "cause": "The uploads currently always use unprocessed data, while xDrip displays data smoothed for noise.", "fix": "A toggle was added in the REST-API settings under Cloud Upload -> Rest API -> Send Display Glucose, allowing the user to choose whether to upload display (smoothed) glucose or unprocessed data. The default behavior was initially set to off, but the user suggested making it default to enabled.", "settings_changed": ["Send Display Glucose → enabled (toggle flipped on)"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Nightscout upload", "REST-API"], "evidence_quote": "Enable it within the REST-API settings in xDrip.", "text": "Feature Request: Allow user to choose if Nightscout upload uses noise smoothed or unprocessed data xDrip uploads to Nightscout always use unprocessed data, while xDrip displays data smoothed for noise, causing a mismatch for users who rely on Nightscout for data display. The uploads currently always use unprocessed data, while xDrip displays data smoothed for noise. A toggle was added in the REST-API settings under Cloud Upload -> Rest API -> Send Display Glucose, allowing the user to choose whether to upload display (smoothed) glucose or unprocessed data. The default behavior was initially set to off, but the user suggested making it default to enabled.  Nightscout upload REST-API Enable it within the REST-API settings in xDrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2029", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2029, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2029, "title": "Number wall pops when notifications arrive", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2029", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2029", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After disabling the 'Number wall on lock screen' option, the number wall still pops up with a black background when the phone is locked and a new notification arrives, waking the phone for a few seconds. Changing wallpapers did not help.", "cause": "The issue was caused by xDrip being enabled in Android accessibility settings for Always On Display.", "fix": "Disable 'Use xDrip+' under the menu Accessibility > xDrip+.", "settings_changed": ["Use xDrip+ → disabled"], "devices": ["Pixel 5a"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["number wall"], "evidence_quote": "I disabled \"Use xDrip+\" under the menu Accessibility > xDrip+ and the problem seems to be solved!", "text": "Number wall pops when notifications arrive After disabling the 'Number wall on lock screen' option, the number wall still pops up with a black background when the phone is locked and a new notification arrives, waking the phone for a few seconds. Changing wallpapers did not help. The issue was caused by xDrip being enabled in Android accessibility settings for Always On Display. Disable 'Use xDrip+' under the menu Accessibility > xDrip+. Pixel 5a Android 12 number wall I disabled \"Use xDrip+\" under the menu Accessibility > xDrip+ and the problem seems to be solved!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-205", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 205, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 205, "title": "Alarms being cut-off and canceled", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/205", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/205", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "High/Low alarms will not sound properly. When triggered I get a fraction of a second of sound only, so all I hear is a brief beep. The alarms are then snoozed (without me cancelling them) for 30 mins. Pressing the Test Alarm button in settings also gives beep only.", "cause": "The app Battery Doctor, which the user installed to improve battery life, was snoozing the alerts.", "fix": "Delete the Battery Doctor app. The user confirmed that after uninstalling Battery Doctor, the alarms worked correctly. The latest nightly also contains a workaround that ignores alert cancellations within 3 seconds of being raised.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.0"], "driver_tags": ["OB1 collector", "G5 collector"], "evidence_quote": "I have fixed the problem. The App that was snoozing the alerts was Battery Doctor (which I installed to try to improve the battery life on the S6). Deleted the App and Xdrip alarms now working.", "text": "Alarms being cut-off and canceled High/Low alarms will not sound properly. When triggered I get a fraction of a second of sound only, so all I hear is a brief beep. The alarms are then snoozed (without me cancelling them) for 30 mins. Pressing the Test Alarm button in settings also gives beep only. The app Battery Doctor, which the user installed to improve battery life, was snoozing the alerts. Delete the Battery Doctor app. The user confirmed that after uninstalling Battery Doctor, the alarms worked correctly. The latest nightly also contains a workaround that ignores alert cancellations within 3 seconds of being raised. G5 Android 7.0 OB1 collector G5 collector I have fixed the problem. The App that was snoozing the alerts was Battery Doctor (which I installed to try to improve the battery life on the S6). Deleted the App and Xdrip alarms now working."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-210", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 210, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 210, "title": "Stuck on collecting inital readings screen while connecting to Bluecon", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/210", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/210", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "On data collector running. In logs only Error code 1(sqlite_error), error or missing database. The app gets stuck on the screen that says it needs 2 readings while connecting to Bluecon.", "cause": "The issue may be caused by the Blucon being paired with an iPhone when trying to use it with an Android phone, or by not waiting long enough for the two readings (which take 10 minutes).", "fix": "Make sure your Blucon is not paired with your iPhone when trying with android phone, so delete pairing. Wait enough time for the 2 values (10 minutes).", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Bluecon", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Libre Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "make sure your Blucon is not paired with your iPhone when trying with android phone. so delete pairing. 2 values need 10minutes so you need to wait enough.", "text": "Stuck on collecting inital readings screen while connecting to Bluecon On data collector running. In logs only Error code 1(sqlite_error), error or missing database. The app gets stuck on the screen that says it needs 2 readings while connecting to Bluecon. The issue may be caused by the Blucon being paired with an iPhone when trying to use it with an Android phone, or by not waiting long enough for the two readings (which take 10 minutes). Make sure your Blucon is not paired with your iPhone when trying with android phone, so delete pairing. Wait enough time for the 2 values (10 minutes). Bluecon Libre Libre Bluetooth make sure your Blucon is not paired with your iPhone when trying with android phone. so delete pairing. 2 values need 10minutes so you need to wait enough."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2111", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2111, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2111, "title": "OB1 Collector long WakeUp", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2111", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2111", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After updating OnePlus 8T to OxygenOS 12, the OB1 Collector has a very long wake-up time, causing missing readings (pattern of 3 readings, one missing, 3 readings). Manually restarting the collector works.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is speculated that changes in the Android kernel or OxygenOS 12 power management prevent xDrip from operating in the background, but no conclusive cause is identified.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include excluding xDrip from power saving options, allowing background activity, and disabling Bluetooth battery optimization, but the user reports these did not resolve the issue. No code change or setting is confirmed to fix it.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["OnePlus 8T"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["OB1 Collector"], "evidence_quote": "I Updated my OnePlus 8T to the OxygenOS 12, and since the Update, the OB1 Collector has a very long WakeUp Time. So there are 3 Readings, one missing, and Three Readings again.", "text": "OB1 Collector long WakeUp After updating OnePlus 8T to OxygenOS 12, the OB1 Collector has a very long wake-up time, causing missing readings (pattern of 3 readings, one missing, 3 readings). Manually restarting the collector works. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. It is speculated that changes in the Android kernel or OxygenOS 12 power management prevent xDrip from operating in the background, but no conclusive cause is identified. No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include excluding xDrip from power saving options, allowing background activity, and disabling Bluetooth battery optimization, but the user reports these did not resolve the issue. No code change or setting is confirmed to fix it. OnePlus 8T Android 12 OB1 Collector I Updated my OnePlus 8T to the OxygenOS 12, and since the Update, the OB1 Collector has a very long WakeUp Time. So there are 3 Readings, one missing, and Three Readings again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2146", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2146, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2146, "title": "xDrip updater only works for the Nightly channel", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2146", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2146", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When checking for updates on Stable, Beta, or Alpha channels, no update pop-up appears, even though a newer build exists. Only the Nightly channel detects updates.", "cause": "The version number for the January 31, 2022 release on the update server (xdrip-plus-updates.appspot.com) was labeled incorrectly, causing xDrip to reject it due to an integer overflow issue. The actual APK file self-identifies correctly, but the server metadata was wrong.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by promoting the current nightly build to the alpha channel, and later updating the Beta and Stable channels to the May 19, 2022 build. The update server metadata was corrected.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "It seems to be working for the nightly build urls, and the actual contents of the January release are fine (if you install the apk, it correctly self-identifies as 2122013118); it's just **labeled** wrong, so xdrip rejects it.", "text": "xDrip updater only works for the Nightly channel When checking for updates on Stable, Beta, or Alpha channels, no update pop-up appears, even though a newer build exists. Only the Nightly channel detects updates. The version number for the January 31, 2022 release on the update server (xdrip-plus-updates.appspot.com) was labeled incorrectly, causing xDrip to reject it due to an integer overflow issue. The actual APK file self-identifies correctly, but the server metadata was wrong. The issue was resolved by promoting the current nightly build to the alpha channel, and later updating the Beta and Stable channels to the May 19, 2022 build. The update server metadata was corrected.   It seems to be working for the nightly build urls, and the actual contents of the January release are fine (if you install the apk, it correctly self-identifies as 2122013118); it's just **labeled** wrong, so xdrip rejects it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-216", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 216, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 216, "title": "Xdrip+ with Blucon Nightrider on Full-Android-Smartwatch (No.1 D6, Android 5.1): Bluetooth issue", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/216", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/216", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After installing xDrip+ on a smartwatch with Android 5.1 (No.1 D6), connecting to the Blucon Nightrider initially gave 'Invalid PIN' errors. Once connected, when the Nightrider leaves Bluetooth range, xDrip+ often fails to reconnect, even after 30 minutes, toggling Bluetooth, or restarting the collector. Rebooting the watch or switching the Blucon off/on usually restores connection. On a tablet with Android 7.0, reconnection happens within 1-3 minutes without action.", "cause": "The issue appears to be specific to the No.1 D6 smartwatch, as xDrip+ works fine on other devices (Ourtime X01 Air, Finow Q1 Pro, Finow M9, Microwear H5). The thread does not identify a definitive root cause beyond device-specific Bluetooth behavior.", "fix": "No fix was found for the No.1 D6; the issue was closed as it was deemed specific to that device. Users with similar issues on other Android 5.1 smartwatches (e.g., Ourtime X01S) reported partial success by pairing via system Bluetooth first, but reconnection remained unreliable.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Blucon Nightrider", "No.1 D6", "Ourtime X01 Air", "Ourtime X01S", "Microwear H5", "Finow Q1 Pro", "Finow M9"], "android_versions": ["Android 5.1", "Android 7.0", "Android 6", "Android 4.4"], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "I close this issue, as xDrip+ is working fine on Ourtime X01 Air, Finow Q1 Pro, Finow M9 and Microwear H5. So it seems to be a problem just with the No.1 D6, which needn't be analyzed any further.", "text": "Xdrip+ with Blucon Nightrider on Full-Android-Smartwatch (No.1 D6, Android 5.1): Bluetooth issue After installing xDrip+ on a smartwatch with Android 5.1 (No.1 D6), connecting to the Blucon Nightrider initially gave 'Invalid PIN' errors. Once connected, when the Nightrider leaves Bluetooth range, xDrip+ often fails to reconnect, even after 30 minutes, toggling Bluetooth, or restarting the collector. Rebooting the watch or switching the Blucon off/on usually restores connection. On a tablet with Android 7.0, reconnection happens within 1-3 minutes without action. The issue appears to be specific to the No.1 D6 smartwatch, as xDrip+ works fine on other devices (Ourtime X01 Air, Finow Q1 Pro, Finow M9, Microwear H5). The thread does not identify a definitive root cause beyond device-specific Bluetooth behavior. No fix was found for the No.1 D6; the issue was closed as it was deemed specific to that device. Users with similar issues on other Android 5.1 smartwatches (e.g., Ourtime X01S) reported partial success by pairing via system Bluetooth first, but reconnection remained unreliable. Blucon Nightrider No.1 D6 Ourtime X01 Air Ourtime X01S Microwear H5 Finow Q1 Pro Finow M9 Android 5.1 Android 7.0 Android 6 Android 4.4 Bluetooth I close this issue, as xDrip+ is working fine on Ourtime X01 Air, Finow Q1 Pro, Finow M9 and Microwear H5. So it seems to be a problem just with the No.1 D6, which needn't be analyzed any further."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2173", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2173, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2173, "title": "Y-axis scaling can lead to confusing views", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2173", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2173", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The y-axis (BG value) is auto-scaled to the highest level within the last 24h, which can make steep slopes appear flatter than they are and give confusing impressions. A single bad point can make the graph useless for 24 hours.", "cause": "The y-axis scaling is based on the highest value in the last 24 hours, which can be skewed by a single high reading (even a bad one) and remains scaled for 24 hours.", "fix": "Navid200 is testing a candidate that pans the main screen instead of changing the axis min/max, so slopes never change. The main screen keeps tracking recent readings and auto-pans based on readings from the past 3 hours, but the y-axis range is user-controlled. Additionally, a PR was opened to avoid resizing the vertical axis for readings marked as bad.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I finally have a candidate that I am testing. It pans instead of changing the axis min/max. Therefore, the slopes never change.", "text": "Y-axis scaling can lead to confusing views The y-axis (BG value) is auto-scaled to the highest level within the last 24h, which can make steep slopes appear flatter than they are and give confusing impressions. A single bad point can make the graph useless for 24 hours. The y-axis scaling is based on the highest value in the last 24 hours, which can be skewed by a single high reading (even a bad one) and remains scaled for 24 hours. Navid200 is testing a candidate that pans the main screen instead of changing the axis min/max, so slopes never change. The main screen keeps tracking recent readings and auto-pans based on readings from the past 3 hours, but the y-axis range is user-controlled. Additionally, a PR was opened to avoid resizing the vertical axis for readings marked as bad. Libre 2  I finally have a candidate that I am testing. It pans instead of changing the axis min/max. Therefore, the slopes never change."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-229", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 229, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 229, "title": "Dexcom Clarity Uploader", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/229", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/229", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using upload to Dexcom servers it works with Dexcom Follow mobile app, but no data are visible in Clarity web app.", "cause": "xDrip+ does not send data to Dexcom Clarity; Dexcom has no public API for writing data to Clarity and locks the API to its own apps, so implementing the feature is not possible without reverse engineering.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["dexcom follow", "clarity", "diasend"], "evidence_quote": "Dexcom has no public API for writing data to Clarity. Obviously, there is good API but locked for their own apps.", "text": "Dexcom Clarity Uploader When using upload to Dexcom servers it works with Dexcom Follow mobile app, but no data are visible in Clarity web app. xDrip+ does not send data to Dexcom Clarity; Dexcom has no public API for writing data to Clarity and locks the API to its own apps, so implementing the feature is not possible without reverse engineering.   dexcom follow clarity diasend Dexcom has no public API for writing data to Clarity. Obviously, there is good API but locked for their own apps."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2292", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2292, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2292, "title": "When CamAPS reports reports ≤2.2 or ≥22.3 xdrip leaves an empty gap", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2292", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2292", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When CamAPS reports glucose values ≤2.2 or ≥22.3, xDrip leaves an empty gap in data, with logs showing 'Did not find any matches'.", "cause": "The value is being read but capped at 400, causing the gap for high values.", "fix": "Raise the limit in the nightly build; the Sept 2nd Nightly raises this limit, and it resolves the issue.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["CamAPS"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["companion"], "evidence_quote": "I can fix that. Its currently capped at 400 but I will raise the limit. It shows the value is being read properly now though.", "text": "When CamAPS reports reports ≤2.2 or ≥22.3 xdrip leaves an empty gap When CamAPS reports glucose values ≤2.2 or ≥22.3, xDrip leaves an empty gap in data, with logs showing 'Did not find any matches'. The value is being read but capped at 400, causing the gap for high values. Raise the limit in the nightly build; the Sept 2nd Nightly raises this limit, and it resolves the issue. CamAPS companion I can fix that. Its currently capped at 400 but I will raise the limit. It shows the value is being read properly now though."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-231", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 231, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 231, "title": "Nightly build 20171203 failing to receive transmitter readings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/231", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/231", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When trying to start a new sensor, xDrip+ appears to hang in the receive three sensor readings state and can take a long time to progress to calibration, sometimes never doing so. It hung like this for 24 hours and took a reinstall and six hour wait before it would calibrate. Following calibration, it only took readings every ten minutes and then lost connectivity and wouldn’t reconnect.", "cause": "The issue appears to be affected by Android Wear. When Wear is installed, even without a watch connected, even if xDrip+ is not set to use Wear, it loses connectivity to the transmitter. As soon as Wear is uninstalled, everything works.", "fix": "Uninstall Android Wear (or avoid having it installed) to restore connectivity. The user also found that a clean uninstall and forget of all watches helped, but reinstalling Wear caused issues again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1"], "driver_tags": ["OB1 G5 collector"], "evidence_quote": "It seems to be affected by Android Wear. When Wear is installed, even without a watch connected, even if xDrip+ is not set to use Wear, it loses connectivity to the transmitter. As soon as i uninstall Wear, everything works.", "text": "Nightly build 20171203 failing to receive transmitter readings When trying to start a new sensor, xDrip+ appears to hang in the receive three sensor readings state and can take a long time to progress to calibration, sometimes never doing so. It hung like this for 24 hours and took a reinstall and six hour wait before it would calibrate. Following calibration, it only took readings every ten minutes and then lost connectivity and wouldn’t reconnect. The issue appears to be affected by Android Wear. When Wear is installed, even without a watch connected, even if xDrip+ is not set to use Wear, it loses connectivity to the transmitter. As soon as Wear is uninstalled, everything works. Uninstall Android Wear (or avoid having it installed) to restore connectivity. The user also found that a clean uninstall and forget of all watches helped, but reinstalling Wear caused issues again. Dexcom G5 Android 8.1 OB1 G5 collector It seems to be affected by Android Wear. When Wear is installed, even without a watch connected, even if xDrip+ is not set to use Wear, it loses connectivity to the transmitter. As soon as i uninstall Wear, everything works."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-242", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 242, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 242, "title": "Phone does not receive readings or it lost a lot of them", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/242", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/242", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User reports that after first four days of working perfectly, the phone (Aquarius U) intermittently stops receiving readings from the FreeStyle sensor via Blucon; at night it loses many readings, with only a few values over hours, and sometimes only initial readings or a single reading before stopping.", "cause": "The developers examined logs and their opinion so far is that there is probably a fault with the Blucon device. No definitive root cause was confirmed; the problem later resolved on its own without explanation.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": ["Run collector in foreground → ON", "bluetooth watchdog → disabled", "bluetooth wakelocks → disabled"], "devices": ["Blucon", "FreeStyle sensor", "Aquarius U"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.1.1"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "The developers have looked over the logs and the opinion so far is that there is probably a fault with the blucon device.", "text": "Phone does not receive readings or it lost a lot of them User reports that after first four days of working perfectly, the phone (Aquarius U) intermittently stops receiving readings from the FreeStyle sensor via Blucon; at night it loses many readings, with only a few values over hours, and sometimes only initial readings or a single reading before stopping. The developers examined logs and their opinion so far is that there is probably a fault with the Blucon device. No definitive root cause was confirmed; the problem later resolved on its own without explanation.  Blucon FreeStyle sensor Aquarius U Android 7.1.1 bluetooth collector The developers have looked over the logs and the opinion so far is that there is probably a fault with the blucon device."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2435", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2435, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2435, "title": "A couple of odd issues since the August 3rd Release. The job text is now fixed. Smoothed heart rate line is broken. ", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2435", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2435", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Since the August 3rd release of xDrip+, the IoB text at the top of the main screen is flaky or missing, and the smoothed heart rate graph line is broken and discontinuous. The steps graphics are also smaller. These issues are present in nightly releases after August 3rd but not in the August 3rd release itself.", "cause": "The IoB issue was a bug introduced in releases after August 3rd, fixed in the Dec 9th Nightly. The heart rate graph issue is related to the 'smooth heart rate graph' option being checked.", "fix": "For the IoB issue, update to the Dec 9th Nightly (2022.12.09) or later. For the heart rate graph issue, uncheck the 'smooth heart rate graph' option in the Smartwatch Sensors settings, or wait for a future fix.", "settings_changed": ["smooth heart rate graph → unchecked"], "devices": ["Fitbit Sense", "Samsung Galaxy S20"], "android_versions": ["Android 12"], "driver_tags": ["smartwatch sensors", "xdrip web service"], "evidence_quote": "It looks like the heart rate graph issue is related to the \"smooth heart rate graph\" option being checked. Unchecking that option clears the issue up but creates a very jagged heartbeat line.", "text": "A couple of odd issues since the August 3rd Release. The job text is now fixed. Smoothed heart rate line is broken.  Since the August 3rd release of xDrip+, the IoB text at the top of the main screen is flaky or missing, and the smoothed heart rate graph line is broken and discontinuous. The steps graphics are also smaller. These issues are present in nightly releases after August 3rd but not in the August 3rd release itself. The IoB issue was a bug introduced in releases after August 3rd, fixed in the Dec 9th Nightly. The heart rate graph issue is related to the 'smooth heart rate graph' option being checked. For the IoB issue, update to the Dec 9th Nightly (2022.12.09) or later. For the heart rate graph issue, uncheck the 'smooth heart rate graph' option in the Smartwatch Sensors settings, or wait for a future fix. Fitbit Sense Samsung Galaxy S20 Android 12 smartwatch sensors xdrip web service It looks like the heart rate graph issue is related to the \"smooth heart rate graph\" option being checked. Unchecking that option clears the issue up but creates a very jagged heartbeat line."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-248", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 248, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 248, "title": "New feature request - Add GVI and PGS calculations in Statistics and History", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/248", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/248", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The issue requests adding GVI and PGS calculations to xDrip+ Statistics and History, similar to Nightscout. Later, a user reports discrepancies in results between Nightscout and xDrip+ due to filtering of low BG values.", "cause": "The discrepancy was caused by xDrip excluding BG values below a sensor threshold (e.g., <39) from calculations, while Nightscout did not exclude them. Additionally, the PGS calculation in xDrip uses user-defined upper and lower limits, which can lead to inconsistent results compared to the intended fixed range.", "fix": "AdrianLxM added the same two filter passes to xDrip as used in Nightscout, which resolved the discrepancies. For PGS, it was suggested to use a fixed range of 70-180 mg/dL instead of user-defined limits, but this was not implemented in the thread.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I've added the same two filter passes to xDrip like you did to Nightscout now.", "text": "New feature request - Add GVI and PGS calculations in Statistics and History The issue requests adding GVI and PGS calculations to xDrip+ Statistics and History, similar to Nightscout. Later, a user reports discrepancies in results between Nightscout and xDrip+ due to filtering of low BG values. The discrepancy was caused by xDrip excluding BG values below a sensor threshold (e.g., <39) from calculations, while Nightscout did not exclude them. Additionally, the PGS calculation in xDrip uses user-defined upper and lower limits, which can lead to inconsistent results compared to the intended fixed range. AdrianLxM added the same two filter passes to xDrip as used in Nightscout, which resolved the discrepancies. For PGS, it was suggested to use a fixed range of 70-180 mg/dL instead of user-defined limits, but this was not implemented in the thread.   I've added the same two filter passes to xDrip like you did to Nightscout now."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2514", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2514, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2514, "title": "moved from heroku to google fine but looking to find the data api", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2514", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2514", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After migrating from Heroku to Google Cloud, the user's Fitbit clock face (from pedantic avenger) requests a DATA API URL and fails with the new host. Another user reports that xDrip as follower gets 'NS entries download was not succesful:401 unautorized' when using the NS follower box.", "cause": "The thread explains that Heroku did not impose a limit on outgoing bandwidth, but on Google Cloud, if outgoing bandwidth goes over 1GB/month, it will not be free. To minimize egress by default, the AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES variable is set to 'denied', which blocks unauthenticated read access, causing devices like Fitbit and xDrip that do not use tokens to fail.", "fix": "Change the Nightscout variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES from 'denied' to 'readable' and restart the server. This is a workaround for devices that cannot use tokens. The thread also suggests using apps/devices that support tokens as the proper solution.", "settings_changed": ["AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES → readable"], "devices": ["Fitbit"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout", "xdrip"], "evidence_quote": "The variable name is the following. AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES The value it is set to now on your system must be: denied If you want to try the experiment, change it to: readable", "text": "moved from heroku to google fine but looking to find the data api After migrating from Heroku to Google Cloud, the user's Fitbit clock face (from pedantic avenger) requests a DATA API URL and fails with the new host. Another user reports that xDrip as follower gets 'NS entries download was not succesful:401 unautorized' when using the NS follower box. The thread explains that Heroku did not impose a limit on outgoing bandwidth, but on Google Cloud, if outgoing bandwidth goes over 1GB/month, it will not be free. To minimize egress by default, the AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES variable is set to 'denied', which blocks unauthenticated read access, causing devices like Fitbit and xDrip that do not use tokens to fail. Change the Nightscout variable AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES from 'denied' to 'readable' and restart the server. This is a workaround for devices that cannot use tokens. The thread also suggests using apps/devices that support tokens as the proper solution. Fitbit nightscout xdrip The variable name is the following. AUTH_DEFAULT_ROLES The value it is set to now on your system must be: denied If you want to try the experiment, change it to: readable"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-255", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 255, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 255, "title": "Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/255", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/255", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Blucon sensor cannot pair with an Android tablet or a standalone Android smartwatch, showing wrong password key when pairing from Bluetooth settings, and not bonding when pairing from xDrip.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Blucon"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Blucon"], "evidence_quote": "Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet", "text": "Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet Blucon sensor cannot pair with an Android tablet or a standalone Android smartwatch, showing wrong password key when pairing from Bluetooth settings, and not bonding when pairing from xDrip.   Blucon Blucon Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-257", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 257, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 257, "title": "xDrip did not spoke the trend after activating the setting in last nigthly (05.01)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/257", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/257", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After activating the setting 'bg_to_speech_trend', the trend is not spoken; only the glucose value is spoken (e.g., 'Calculated text: 102'). The user expects to hear the glucose value and the trend arrow.", "cause": "In BgToSpeech.java, the trend is only added when mgdl is not used (i.e., only in mmol/L mode). The code places the trend addition inside an else clause that handles non-mgdl, so when mgdl is used, the trend is omitted.", "fix": "Move the trend addition code to the end of the constructText method so it is added regardless of mgdl usage. Also, the fix for repeat twice was committed. The user also contributed a pull request for translation.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In bgSpeach the constructtext is not right maintained, because the trend will be added only if not mgdl is used (so only in mol it will be add). I'll change that, and will also try to implement translation, and will made than a Pull request if ok for you.", "text": "xDrip did not spoke the trend after activating the setting in last nigthly (05.01) After activating the setting 'bg_to_speech_trend', the trend is not spoken; only the glucose value is spoken (e.g., 'Calculated text: 102'). The user expects to hear the glucose value and the trend arrow. In BgToSpeech.java, the trend is only added when mgdl is not used (i.e., only in mmol/L mode). The code places the trend addition inside an else clause that handles non-mgdl, so when mgdl is used, the trend is omitted. Move the trend addition code to the end of the constructText method so it is added regardless of mgdl usage. Also, the fix for repeat twice was committed. The user also contributed a pull request for translation.   In bgSpeach the constructtext is not right maintained, because the trend will be added only if not mgdl is used (so only in mol it will be add). I'll change that, and will also try to implement translation, and will made than a Pull request if ok for you."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2597", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2597, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2597, "title": "Tidepool Authentication API Deprecation", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2597", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2597", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Tidepool has deprecated its legacy authentication API after replacing it with Keycloak, and the old endpoints are being retired. xDrip's current integration uses these deprecated endpoints and starts a new auth session every time a fresh token is needed instead of refreshing the session token directly.", "cause": "Tidepool replaced its legacy authentication system with Keycloak in December 2022, deprecating the old API endpoints. xDrip was using the old flow and creating a new auth session for each token instead of using refresh tokens.", "fix": "xDrip implemented the new OpenID Connect authorization code flow with refresh tokens against Tidepool's Keycloak server. After a Keycloak bug causing 'invalid_grant' logouts was fixed and deployed, the new authentication mechanism was switched on as the default in xDrip and released on September 23.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tidepool", "keycloak", "openid connect", "appauth-android"], "evidence_quote": "@jamorham go ahead. The system has been stable since I notified you of the fix.", "text": "Tidepool Authentication API Deprecation Tidepool has deprecated its legacy authentication API after replacing it with Keycloak, and the old endpoints are being retired. xDrip's current integration uses these deprecated endpoints and starts a new auth session every time a fresh token is needed instead of refreshing the session token directly. Tidepool replaced its legacy authentication system with Keycloak in December 2022, deprecating the old API endpoints. xDrip was using the old flow and creating a new auth session for each token instead of using refresh tokens. xDrip implemented the new OpenID Connect authorization code flow with refresh tokens against Tidepool's Keycloak server. After a Keycloak bug causing 'invalid_grant' logouts was fixed and deployed, the new authentication mechanism was switched on as the default in xDrip and released on September 23.  tidepool keycloak openid connect appauth-android @jamorham go ahead. The system has been stable since I notified you of the fix."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2607", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2607, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2607, "title": "Snooze locked phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2607", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2607", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Snoozing an xDrip 'Low Alert' using the volume button of the phone no longer works. The user has to unlock the screen and swipe to snooze the sound. When the alert rings when the screen is already unlocked, volume buttons do not snooze; they only work after locking and unlocking the screen.", "cause": "The thread explains that snoozing an alert via volume buttons when the phone is locked has never been possible (see issue #73). The behavior is due to Android limitations: you cannot receive those broadcasts unless the screen is on or there is active audio playing.", "fix": "To snooze an alert while the phone is locked, change Android notification settings to show notification details on lock screen, and enable the xDrip setting that turns the screen on when there is a notification. Then, when an alert triggers, swipe the notification right to snooze.", "settings_changed": ["Android notification settings → show notification details on lock screen", "xDrip setting that turns the screen on when there is a notification → enabled"], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy S10e"], "android_versions": ["Android 12", "Android 8"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "By default, you cannot snooze an alert when your phone is locked.  But, you can change a few settings to make it possible. First, you need to change an Android notifications setting so that it would show notification details on lock screen. Then, there is a relatively new xDrip setting that turns the screen on when there is a notidication. After that, as soon as an alert triggers, you will see the notification on the screen of your phone, and swiping it right will snooze the alert with your phone still locked.", "text": "Snooze locked phone Snoozing an xDrip 'Low Alert' using the volume button of the phone no longer works. The user has to unlock the screen and swipe to snooze the sound. When the alert rings when the screen is already unlocked, volume buttons do not snooze; they only work after locking and unlocking the screen. The thread explains that snoozing an alert via volume buttons when the phone is locked has never been possible (see issue #73). The behavior is due to Android limitations: you cannot receive those broadcasts unless the screen is on or there is active audio playing. To snooze an alert while the phone is locked, change Android notification settings to show notification details on lock screen, and enable the xDrip setting that turns the screen on when there is a notification. Then, when an alert triggers, swipe the notification right to snooze. Samsung Galaxy S10e Android 12 Android 8  By default, you cannot snooze an alert when your phone is locked.  But, you can change a few settings to make it possible. First, you need to change an Android notifications setting so that it would show notification details on lock screen. Then, there is a relatively new xDrip setting that turns the screen on when there is a notidication. After that, as soon as an alert triggers, you will see the notification on the screen of your phone, and swiping it right will snooze the alert with your phone still locked."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-262", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 262, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 262, "title": "Feature Request - multiple glucose levels/settings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/262", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/262", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests the ability to define more than the current three glucose ranges (low, in range, high) to have more colors on the graph, e.g., yellow for low, green for normal, orange for medium high, and red for high. They also ask if this would carry over to watch faces like Pebble.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pebble"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Not sure what to call it; might have to be alert levels; but maybe more a T2 than T1's add more levels, then we can have more colors on the graph.", "text": "Feature Request - multiple glucose levels/settings The user requests the ability to define more than the current three glucose ranges (low, in range, high) to have more colors on the graph, e.g., yellow for low, green for normal, orange for medium high, and red for high. They also ask if this would carry over to watch faces like Pebble.   Pebble  Not sure what to call it; might have to be alert levels; but maybe more a T2 than T1's add more levels, then we can have more colors on the graph."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-263", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 263, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 263, "title": "Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet  #255", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/263", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/263", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Blucon cannot pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet. The user reports that when pairing via xDrip, it says wrong PIN even when entered correctly, and the smartwatch tries to bond simultaneously in xDrip and Bluetooth settings.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Blucon"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "if i go first at xdrip and do bluetooth scan i insert the blucon's pin and then it tries to paired automatically and says at xdrip screen meny wrong pin even i insert it correctly.", "text": "Blucon can not pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet  #255 Blucon cannot pair at a standalone smartwatch and an android tablet. The user reports that when pairing via xDrip, it says wrong PIN even when entered correctly, and the smartwatch tries to bond simultaneously in xDrip and Bluetooth settings.   Blucon  if i go first at xdrip and do bluetooth scan i insert the blucon's pin and then it tries to paired automatically and says at xdrip screen meny wrong pin even i insert it correctly."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2641", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2641, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2641, "title": "Only one Bluetooth device for 'speak reading' ?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2641", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2641", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip only allows one Bluetooth device to trigger 'speak readings' or vehicle mode, so when switching between multiple Bluetooth audio devices (e.g., car and work earbuds), the user must manually re-pair xDrip to the active device each time.", "cause": "The xDrip app only allows specifying one Bluetooth device (MAC address) to trigger vehicle mode or speak readings, rather than supporting a list of devices.", "fix": "Use an automation app like Tasker to create a profile that triggers 'speak readings' when any of multiple Bluetooth devices are connected, and turns it off when disconnected.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "vehicle mode", "speak readings", "text to speech"], "evidence_quote": "As I said previously on this thread, you can easily use Tasker to be able to trigger multiple Bluetooth connections that you have. It is very simple to create a single profile to trigger any Bluetooth connection made. For instance, I have 3 sets of earbuds and a car listed to start \"speak readings\" whenever any one of them is connected, and turn off \"speak readings\" when they are disconnected.", "text": "Only one Bluetooth device for 'speak reading' ? xDrip only allows one Bluetooth device to trigger 'speak readings' or vehicle mode, so when switching between multiple Bluetooth audio devices (e.g., car and work earbuds), the user must manually re-pair xDrip to the active device each time. The xDrip app only allows specifying one Bluetooth device (MAC address) to trigger vehicle mode or speak readings, rather than supporting a list of devices. Use an automation app like Tasker to create a profile that triggers 'speak readings' when any of multiple Bluetooth devices are connected, and turns it off when disconnected.  bluetooth vehicle mode speak readings text to speech As I said previously on this thread, you can easily use Tasker to be able to trigger multiple Bluetooth connections that you have. It is very simple to create a single profile to trigger any Bluetooth connection made. For instance, I have 3 sets of earbuds and a car listed to start \"speak readings\" whenever any one of them is connected, and turn off \"speak readings\" when they are disconnected."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-266", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 266, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 266, "title": "Upload of \"eventType: Sensor Start\" to the Nightscout treatments works only to 1st NS site", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/266", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/266", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When starting a new Dexcom sensor, if there is more than one Nightscout site (REST-API) in the Base URL settings (space delimited), the upload of the \"eventType: Sensor Start\" works only for the first NS site. All other NS sites are missing this data. This also affects other treatments and events such as carbs, insulin, and CGM sensor start/stop, which only go to the first URL specified.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["G5/G6 Transmitter", "Native Algorithm"], "evidence_quote": "Where there are two space separated URLs specified as the Base URL in xDrip settings; - glucose values (type sgv) are uploaded to both nightscout instances - CGM calibration events are uploaded to both nightscout instances - other treatments and events (for instance I've experienced it with:- carbs, insulin, CGM sensor start/stop) only go to the first URL specified", "text": "Upload of \"eventType: Sensor Start\" to the Nightscout treatments works only to 1st NS site When starting a new Dexcom sensor, if there is more than one Nightscout site (REST-API) in the Base URL settings (space delimited), the upload of the \"eventType: Sensor Start\" works only for the first NS site. All other NS sites are missing this data. This also affects other treatments and events such as carbs, insulin, and CGM sensor start/stop, which only go to the first URL specified.   Dexcom G6 Libre G5/G6 Transmitter Native Algorithm Where there are two space separated URLs specified as the Base URL in xDrip settings; - glucose values (type sgv) are uploaded to both nightscout instances - CGM calibration events are uploaded to both nightscout instances - other treatments and events (for instance I've experienced it with:- carbs, insulin, CGM sensor start/stop) only go to the first URL specified"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-267", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 267, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 267, "title": "How to track/monitor more than one persons with one one smartphone (xDrip+ app)?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/267", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/267", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The user wants to follow more than one person (two Dexcom G4) with one phone, for example one xDrip Parakeet for person 1 and another xDrip Bluetooth or Parakeet feed for person 2. They ask if multiple instances of xDrip can be installed or if there is another way to monitor two people while carrying only one smartphone.", "cause": "A phone can run two xDrip instances, but the second one must be a specially built 'variant' because a normal second install of the same app is not possible under the same Android application identity/signing key. If someone else builds that variant, you will not have the original signing key and therefore cannot later build/install that exact same variant yourself.", "fix": "Run two xDrip instances on one phone: keep one as a normal xDrip Bluetooth installation and install the second one as an xDrip variant that can be an xDrip follower or read from a parakeet. To create the variant yourself, change the applicationId/package name (including in /wear/build.gradle for release builds); otherwise use the variant nightly builds supplied by jamorham from the shared Google Drive folder. Official and variant builds can coexist on the same phone.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["dexcom G4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["parakeet", "bluetooth", "follower", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "One phone can run two instances of xDrip.\nOne can be a normal xDrip installation using BT.\nThe second one can read data from another xDrip (that is be an xDrip follower) or read data from a parakeet.\nIn order to install the second application you need to make a small change when building xDrip.", "text": "How to track/monitor more than one persons with one one smartphone (xDrip+ app)? The user wants to follow more than one person (two Dexcom G4) with one phone, for example one xDrip Parakeet for person 1 and another xDrip Bluetooth or Parakeet feed for person 2. They ask if multiple instances of xDrip can be installed or if there is another way to monitor two people while carrying only one smartphone. A phone can run two xDrip instances, but the second one must be a specially built 'variant' because a normal second install of the same app is not possible under the same Android application identity/signing key. If someone else builds that variant, you will not have the original signing key and therefore cannot later build/install that exact same variant yourself. Run two xDrip instances on one phone: keep one as a normal xDrip Bluetooth installation and install the second one as an xDrip variant that can be an xDrip follower or read from a parakeet. To create the variant yourself, change the applicationId/package name (including in /wear/build.gradle for release builds); otherwise use the variant nightly builds supplied by jamorham from the shared Google Drive folder. Official and variant builds can coexist on the same phone. dexcom G4 parakeet bluetooth follower collector One phone can run two instances of xDrip.\nOne can be a normal xDrip installation using BT.\nThe second one can read data from another xDrip (that is be an xDrip follower) or read data from a parakeet.\nIn order to install the second application you need to make a small change when building xDrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2823", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2823, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2823, "title": "Carelink login not working with xdrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2823", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2823", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "CareLink server only works with Medtronic applications; xDrip can no longer connect to the server (carelink.minimed.eu). Users report a 400 error when downloading data from CareLink, even after changing username/password and trying old and new xDrip versions.", "cause": "CareLink changed its API to require patient information in the payload for care partner accounts. Previously the payload contained only username and role, but after the update it also requires a patientId. This change affects standalone CGM users and multi-patient follow scenarios.", "fix": "The latest release (2023.05.26) addresses the issue. For a temporary workaround, use the patient account instead of the care partner account. A more permanent fix was implemented in the latest release.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["carelink", "care partner", "patient account"], "evidence_quote": "Please try the latest release: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2023.05.26", "text": "Carelink login not working with xdrip CareLink server only works with Medtronic applications; xDrip can no longer connect to the server (carelink.minimed.eu). Users report a 400 error when downloading data from CareLink, even after changing username/password and trying old and new xDrip versions. CareLink changed its API to require patient information in the payload for care partner accounts. Previously the payload contained only username and role, but after the update it also requires a patientId. This change affects standalone CGM users and multi-patient follow scenarios. The latest release (2023.05.26) addresses the issue. For a temporary workaround, use the patient account instead of the care partner account. A more permanent fix was implemented in the latest release.  carelink care partner patient account Please try the latest release: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2023.05.26"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-2917", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 2917, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 2917, "title": "Samsung, Dexcom, and recent Android patch", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2917", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/2917", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Some Samsung phones have difficulty after a recent (June 2023) Samsung patch, affecting Bluetooth operation. Users report irregular readings, signal dropping in and out, and connectivity issues with xDrip and other apps.", "cause": "The thread indicates the issue is likely caused by a Samsung system update (June 2023 patch) that affects Bluetooth operation, and is not specific to xDrip as many apps have this problem. A later Samsung update on July 24th was expected to fix it.", "fix": "The thread suggests trying the latest xDrip Nightly release (2023.07.02) which improved connectivity for some, and enabling OB1 debugging for logs. A user reported that after a subsequent Samsung update on July 24th, the issue was resolved. Another user found that changing Bluetooth battery optimization setting improved connection.", "settings_changed": ["Bluetooth battery optimization → changed (from battery optimization to not optimized)"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Freestyle Libre 2", "Samsung A53", "Samsung S20+"], "android_versions": ["Android 13"], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth", "OB1 debugging"], "evidence_quote": "Today Samsung push update for A53, and after update its working ;-)", "text": "Samsung, Dexcom, and recent Android patch Some Samsung phones have difficulty after a recent (June 2023) Samsung patch, affecting Bluetooth operation. Users report irregular readings, signal dropping in and out, and connectivity issues with xDrip and other apps. The thread indicates the issue is likely caused by a Samsung system update (June 2023 patch) that affects Bluetooth operation, and is not specific to xDrip as many apps have this problem. A later Samsung update on July 24th was expected to fix it. The thread suggests trying the latest xDrip Nightly release (2023.07.02) which improved connectivity for some, and enabling OB1 debugging for logs. A user reported that after a subsequent Samsung update on July 24th, the issue was resolved. Another user found that changing Bluetooth battery optimization setting improved connection. Dexcom G6 Freestyle Libre 2 Samsung A53 Samsung S20+ Android 13 Bluetooth OB1 debugging Today Samsung push update for A53, and after update its working ;-)"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-296", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 296, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 296, "title": "BT Glucose Meters and Initial Calibration problems", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/296", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/296", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When performing a finger prick with a Bluetooth glucose meter (e.g., Contour Next One) while xDrip is set to Auto Calibration and the initial calibration screen is open, the incoming BT reading overwrites the initial calibration prompt with a normal calibration prompt, causing the initial calibration screen to close or hide. Selecting yes records the value as a normal blood glucose reading, not as an initial calibration, and it never becomes a calibration because there is no data around it.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is implied that xDrip's handling of BT readings does not distinguish between initial calibration and normal calibration, so incoming readings are treated as normal readings even when an initial calibration is pending.", "fix": "The suggested workaround from the maintainer is to tap on the square marker of the reading and choose to use it as a calibration, confirming that you want to use the point as a calibration. This allows manual calibration instead of relying on automatic calibration before initial calibrations are entered.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Contour Next One", "Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["non-native", "standard xdrip mode", "BT meter"], "evidence_quote": "In that case, you can tap on the square marker and tap on calibrate and confirm that you want to use the point as a calibration.", "text": "BT Glucose Meters and Initial Calibration problems When performing a finger prick with a Bluetooth glucose meter (e.g., Contour Next One) while xDrip is set to Auto Calibration and the initial calibration screen is open, the incoming BT reading overwrites the initial calibration prompt with a normal calibration prompt, causing the initial calibration screen to close or hide. Selecting yes records the value as a normal blood glucose reading, not as an initial calibration, and it never becomes a calibration because there is no data around it. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but it is implied that xDrip's handling of BT readings does not distinguish between initial calibration and normal calibration, so incoming readings are treated as normal readings even when an initial calibration is pending. The suggested workaround from the maintainer is to tap on the square marker of the reading and choose to use it as a calibration, confirming that you want to use the point as a calibration. This allows manual calibration instead of relying on automatic calibration before initial calibrations are entered. Contour Next One Dexcom G5 non-native standard xdrip mode BT meter In that case, you can tap on the square marker and tap on calibrate and confirm that you want to use the point as a calibration."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-302", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 302, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 302, "title": "Feature request - Add Basal input and tracking", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/302", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/302", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User asks for a second type of insulin input so that basal insulin could be entered, tracked, and graphed. Many commenters second the request, particularly for MDI users of long-acting insulins such as Lantus or Levemir, and ask for configurable onset delay and duration.", "cause": "xDrip at the time lacked a basal insulin entry and tracking option, so users could not record or graph basal doses in the app.", "fix": "The capability to enter basal insulin now exists in xDrip, as stated when the issue was closed. PR #1388 was noted as adding more insulin types including basal insulins; visualization of basal insulin was intentionally not included to avoid changing business logic.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["mdi", "csii", "pump"], "evidence_quote": "This issue, based on its title, was about adding the ability to enter basal insulin.  That capability already exists now.  Hence, I am closing this issue.", "text": "Feature request - Add Basal input and tracking User asks for a second type of insulin input so that basal insulin could be entered, tracked, and graphed. Many commenters second the request, particularly for MDI users of long-acting insulins such as Lantus or Levemir, and ask for configurable onset delay and duration. xDrip at the time lacked a basal insulin entry and tracking option, so users could not record or graph basal doses in the app. The capability to enter basal insulin now exists in xDrip, as stated when the issue was closed. PR #1388 was noted as adding more insulin types including basal insulins; visualization of basal insulin was intentionally not included to avoid changing business logic.  mdi csii pump This issue, based on its title, was about adding the ability to enter basal insulin.  That capability already exists now.  Hence, I am closing this issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-304", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 304, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 304, "title": "direct connection from blucon to watch fails", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/304", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/304", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When the phone is out of range, the watch does not receive measurement results despite 'Enable Collector' and 'Force Collector' settings being set. The log shows 'syncBGData new BgReading calibrationUuid not found by byuuid'.", "cause": "The Ticwatch E does not reliably collect data directly from the Blucon or Bluereader; the connection is unstable and stops after a while. It may be due to a bug in xDrip+ or the need for a patch for certain Wear OS devices.", "fix": "One user reported success by updating the Ticwatch to Android 8.0, using the nightly xDrip+ from 21st May, and performing a Bluetooth dance: turn off phone Bluetooth, reset Blucon, pair watch to Blucon, turn phone Bluetooth back on, then enable 'Enable wear collection service', 'Force wear collection service', and 'Only use wear' in the Android Wear Integration menu. However, this fix was not stable for all users.", "settings_changed": ["Enable wear collection service", "Force wear collection service", "Only use wear"], "devices": ["Blucon", "Ticwatch E", "Bluereader", "MiaoMiao", "Libre"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0", "Android 8.1.0", "Android 7.1.1"], "driver_tags": ["wear collection service", "force wear collection service", "only use wear"], "evidence_quote": "Then I performed a little Bluetooth dance as follows: 1. Turn OFF phone bluetooth to disconnect phone and watch 2. Use the metal pin that comes with the Blucon to \"reset\" it 3. On watch, scan for available devices 4. Select BLUXXXXX, and type in the PIN code when prompted 5. Turn phone bluetooth back on 6. Then select all of the following in the \"Android Wear Integration\" menu in the xDrip settings on the phone: - Enable wear collection service - Force wear collection service - Only use wear", "text": "direct connection from blucon to watch fails When the phone is out of range, the watch does not receive measurement results despite 'Enable Collector' and 'Force Collector' settings being set. The log shows 'syncBGData new BgReading calibrationUuid not found by byuuid'. The Ticwatch E does not reliably collect data directly from the Blucon or Bluereader; the connection is unstable and stops after a while. It may be due to a bug in xDrip+ or the need for a patch for certain Wear OS devices. One user reported success by updating the Ticwatch to Android 8.0, using the nightly xDrip+ from 21st May, and performing a Bluetooth dance: turn off phone Bluetooth, reset Blucon, pair watch to Blucon, turn phone Bluetooth back on, then enable 'Enable wear collection service', 'Force wear collection service', and 'Only use wear' in the Android Wear Integration menu. However, this fix was not stable for all users. Blucon Ticwatch E Bluereader MiaoMiao Libre Android 8.0 Android 8.1.0 Android 7.1.1 wear collection service force wear collection service only use wear Then I performed a little Bluetooth dance as follows: 1. Turn OFF phone bluetooth to disconnect phone and watch 2. Use the metal pin that comes with the Blucon to \"reset\" it 3. On watch, scan for available devices 4. Select BLUXXXXX, and type in the PIN code when prompted 5. Turn phone bluetooth back on 6. Then select all of the following in the \"Android Wear Integration\" menu in the xDrip settings on the phone: - Enable wear collection service - Force wear collection service - Only use wear"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-311", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 311, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 311, "title": "Feature request - Falling and rising fast alarm", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/311", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/311", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User requests a feature to add glucose values to the falling and rising fast alarm, so that the alarm only rings when glucose is below/above certain thresholds, to avoid expected alarms at high glucose levels.", "cause": null, "fix": "The maintainer suggests using the existing Forecasted Low alarm for falling fast, and mentions a predicted high alarm pull request for rising fast, but no concrete fix is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The functionality you are asking for by adding a value to fast rising can effectively be accomplished by using the existing predicted low alarm as already explained.", "text": "Feature request - Falling and rising fast alarm User requests a feature to add glucose values to the falling and rising fast alarm, so that the alarm only rings when glucose is below/above certain thresholds, to avoid expected alarms at high glucose levels.  The maintainer suggests using the existing Forecasted Low alarm for falling fast, and mentions a predicted high alarm pull request for rising fast, but no concrete fix is provided.   The functionality you are asking for by adding a value to fast rising can effectively be accomplished by using the existing predicted low alarm as already explained."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-316", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 316, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 316, "title": "xDrip+ can backfill a \"flat line\" of Libre values to Nightscout on restarting", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/316", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/316", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After restarting the Libre Alarm app and SW3 in the morning, xDrip+ sends a flat line of glucose values to Nightscout, all equal to the first reading after restart, instead of the actual 8-hour history it sees.", "cause": "The issue is caused by readings not being sorted before sending to Nightscout, as explained by tzachi-dar: 'According to what I understand from getDisplayGlucose() it seems that it depends on readings arriving at order. ... However in the function CalculateFromDataTransferObject This is not the case. We need to sort values, before sending them up.'", "fix": "Update to the March 6th nightly (Code 1803061753) and keep 'Send Display Glucose' enabled in Nightscout Sync settings. This resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["Send Display Glucose → ON"], "devices": ["Freestyle Libre", "Sony SW3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Libre Alarm", "Nightscout Sync (REST-API)"], "evidence_quote": "I am delighted to confirm that, with the Code: [1803061753 APK](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2018.03.06) (from yesterday), and with ``Settings | Cloud Upload | Nightscout Sync (REST-API) | Send Display Glucose = \"ON\"``, I see the same data on Nightscout as I do in the xDrip+ UI. Success!", "text": "xDrip+ can backfill a \"flat line\" of Libre values to Nightscout on restarting After restarting the Libre Alarm app and SW3 in the morning, xDrip+ sends a flat line of glucose values to Nightscout, all equal to the first reading after restart, instead of the actual 8-hour history it sees. The issue is caused by readings not being sorted before sending to Nightscout, as explained by tzachi-dar: 'According to what I understand from getDisplayGlucose() it seems that it depends on readings arriving at order. ... However in the function CalculateFromDataTransferObject This is not the case. We need to sort values, before sending them up.' Update to the March 6th nightly (Code 1803061753) and keep 'Send Display Glucose' enabled in Nightscout Sync settings. This resolved the issue. Freestyle Libre Sony SW3 Libre Alarm Nightscout Sync (REST-API) I am delighted to confirm that, with the Code: [1803061753 APK](https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/releases/tag/2018.03.06) (from yesterday), and with ``Settings | Cloud Upload | Nightscout Sync (REST-API) | Send Display Glucose = \"ON\"``, I see the same data on Nightscout as I do in the xDrip+ UI. Success!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3219", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3219, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3219, "title": "Vehicle mode does not stop after bluetooth is disconnected, causing 'speak readings' to continue.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3219", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3219", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Vehicle mode does not stop after bluetooth is disconnected, causing 'speak readings' to continue. Users report that after updating to Android 14, xDrip no longer exits Vehicle mode when leaving the car, and the log shows repeated 'Vehicle mode: Enabled' prints without a corresponding 'Disabled' print.", "cause": "The issue appears to be related to Android 14 updates on various devices, as multiple users report the problem after updating to Android 14. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but it is implied that the Android update broke the bluetooth disconnect detection that triggers Vehicle mode exit.", "fix": "The fix is to update to the xDrip release of May 12, 2024 or any after that. Users confirm that this version fixed the problem. As a temporary workaround, users can disable 'Vehicle mode' under xDrip+ Motion tracking to stop the ongoing speak readings.", "settings_changed": ["Vehicle mode → disabled"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 14", "Android 15"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "Please try the xDrip release of May 12, 2024 or any after that and if the problem persists, please report it here.", "text": "Vehicle mode does not stop after bluetooth is disconnected, causing 'speak readings' to continue. Vehicle mode does not stop after bluetooth is disconnected, causing 'speak readings' to continue. Users report that after updating to Android 14, xDrip no longer exits Vehicle mode when leaving the car, and the log shows repeated 'Vehicle mode: Enabled' prints without a corresponding 'Disabled' print. The issue appears to be related to Android 14 updates on various devices, as multiple users report the problem after updating to Android 14. The exact root cause is not explicitly stated, but it is implied that the Android update broke the bluetooth disconnect detection that triggers Vehicle mode exit. The fix is to update to the xDrip release of May 12, 2024 or any after that. Users confirm that this version fixed the problem. As a temporary workaround, users can disable 'Vehicle mode' under xDrip+ Motion tracking to stop the ongoing speak readings. Dexcom G6 Android 14 Android 15 bluetooth Please try the xDrip release of May 12, 2024 or any after that and if the problem persists, please report it here."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3243", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3243, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3243, "title": "Remove duplicate Norwegian language in Crowdin and xDrip+", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3243", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3243", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "There are duplicate Norwegian language entries in Crowdin and xDrip+ ('Norwegian' and 'Norwegian Bokmal'), causing confusion for Norwegian users. The 'Norwegian' option is only 45% translated and is essentially an unfinished version of Norwegian Bokmål, while 'Norwegian Bokmal' is 100% translated and is the default system language for Norwegian phones.", "cause": "The 'no' language was added to Crowdin and xDrip+ by mistake, possibly due to a misunderstanding that there were two distinct Norwegian languages. In reality, Norwegian Bokmål (nb) is the standard written language, and 'no' is not a valid ISO code for Norwegian; it is just an incomplete duplicate of nb.", "fix": "Remove the 'no' language from Crowdin and xDrip+, change the forced language option value from 'no' to 'nb', create a legacy settings update feature to migrate users who had selected 'Norsk' (no) to 'nb', and remove the 'no' translated strings from the source tree. Also rename the display name for 'nb' to 'Norsk bokmål'.", "settings_changed": ["Force language option value → nb (from no)", "Display name for nb → Norsk bokmål"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "To resolve 3, we should change this language value to `nb` and then create a legacy settings update feature to move anyone from `no` forced language to `nb` forced language. After this is done we can also remove the `no` translated strings from the xDrip source tree as these would never be accessed.", "text": "Remove duplicate Norwegian language in Crowdin and xDrip+ There are duplicate Norwegian language entries in Crowdin and xDrip+ ('Norwegian' and 'Norwegian Bokmal'), causing confusion for Norwegian users. The 'Norwegian' option is only 45% translated and is essentially an unfinished version of Norwegian Bokmål, while 'Norwegian Bokmal' is 100% translated and is the default system language for Norwegian phones. The 'no' language was added to Crowdin and xDrip+ by mistake, possibly due to a misunderstanding that there were two distinct Norwegian languages. In reality, Norwegian Bokmål (nb) is the standard written language, and 'no' is not a valid ISO code for Norwegian; it is just an incomplete duplicate of nb. Remove the 'no' language from Crowdin and xDrip+, change the forced language option value from 'no' to 'nb', create a legacy settings update feature to migrate users who had selected 'Norsk' (no) to 'nb', and remove the 'no' translated strings from the source tree. Also rename the display name for 'nb' to 'Norsk bokmål'.   To resolve 3, we should change this language value to `nb` and then create a legacy settings update feature to move anyone from `no` forced language to `nb` forced language. After this is done we can also remove the `no` translated strings from the xDrip source tree as these would never be accessed."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-325", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 325, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 325, "title": "Android Wear Complication displays \"Null, Null\" with NSClient follower", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/325", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/325", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When using xDrip+ as a Sync follower with NSClient app as local broadcaster, BG data displays on the phone app and on xDrip+ watchfaces, but the xDrip+ watch complication shows 'Null, Null'.", "cause": "The issue is likely in the code path when using NSClient with the phone in follower mode, which isn't populating the complication correctly. A workaround was found by gregorybel, but the root cause is not fully identified.", "fix": "A dirty workaround was provided by gregorybel in a branch, but no official fix is stated. Users are advised to update to the latest nightly and reinstall the watch app, but this did not resolve the issue for all.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pixel XL", "Ticwatch e", "Michael Kors Access Greyson", "Skagen Falster", "Pixel 2", "Fossil Explorist", "Fossil Gen 5", "Dexcom G6", "iPhone SE", "iPhone 6"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1", "Android 9", "Android 11"], "driver_tags": ["NSClient", "Sync follower", "Nightscout follower", "AAPS"], "evidence_quote": "I expect that is the code path which isn't populating the complication correctly. I will check it out.", "text": "Android Wear Complication displays \"Null, Null\" with NSClient follower When using xDrip+ as a Sync follower with NSClient app as local broadcaster, BG data displays on the phone app and on xDrip+ watchfaces, but the xDrip+ watch complication shows 'Null, Null'. The issue is likely in the code path when using NSClient with the phone in follower mode, which isn't populating the complication correctly. A workaround was found by gregorybel, but the root cause is not fully identified. A dirty workaround was provided by gregorybel in a branch, but no official fix is stated. Users are advised to update to the latest nightly and reinstall the watch app, but this did not resolve the issue for all. Pixel XL Ticwatch e Michael Kors Access Greyson Skagen Falster Pixel 2 Fossil Explorist Fossil Gen 5 Dexcom G6 iPhone SE iPhone 6 Android 8.1 Android 9 Android 11 NSClient Sync follower Nightscout follower AAPS I expect that is the code path which isn't populating the complication correctly. I will check it out."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3250", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3250, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3250, "title": "Invalid G7 start time sent to AAPS", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3250", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3250", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The Classic Status Page shows the start date of the previous sensor while the G5/G6/G7 status page and home screen show the correct sensor age; AAPS shows the same (incorrect) age as the Classic Status Page.", "cause": "xDrip maintains its own internal 'Sensor Start' time for the Classic Status Page and for what it sends to AAPS instead of using the G7 transmitter's reported start. If the old sensor session is not stopped in xDrip when switching to a new G7, that internal timer is not reset and an invalid old start time keeps being broadcast.", "fix": "Use Navid200's PR #3263, which makes xDrip stop basing the displayed/broadcast sensor start on the xDrip session start and instead read the G7 transmitter's start time to update the Classic Status Page and AAPS broadcast. Testers confirmed it corrects the Classic Status Page and AAPS sensor-age/treatment output.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["aaps", "broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "That PR stops caring about when you start the xDrip session. It looks at the transmitter and updates the classic status page and what is sends to AAPS from it.", "text": "Invalid G7 start time sent to AAPS The Classic Status Page shows the start date of the previous sensor while the G5/G6/G7 status page and home screen show the correct sensor age; AAPS shows the same (incorrect) age as the Classic Status Page. xDrip maintains its own internal 'Sensor Start' time for the Classic Status Page and for what it sends to AAPS instead of using the G7 transmitter's reported start. If the old sensor session is not stopped in xDrip when switching to a new G7, that internal timer is not reset and an invalid old start time keeps being broadcast. Use Navid200's PR #3263, which makes xDrip stop basing the displayed/broadcast sensor start on the xDrip session start and instead read the G7 transmitter's start time to update the Classic Status Page and AAPS broadcast. Testers confirmed it corrects the Classic Status Page and AAPS sensor-age/treatment output. G7 aaps broadcast That PR stops caring about when you start the xDrip session. It looks at the transmitter and updates the classic status page and what is sends to AAPS from it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3398", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3398, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3398, "title": "xDrip can show an overlap when switching hardware data source", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3398", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3398", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When switching the hardware data source from a G6 collector to Nightscout follower, xDrip shows overlapping readings (backfilled data overlaps with existing data). The overlap occurs when switching from G6 collector to Nightscout follower, but not when switching from Nightscout follower to G6 collector.", "cause": "The overlap is caused by xDrip backfilling data for a time period that already has readings, even if the timestamps are not exactly the same. The backfill does not check for existing data in the same time period.", "fix": "Starting with the xDrip Nightly release of July 17, 2024, xDrip will only backfill (G6 or G7) starting from the last existing reading. This avoids the possibility of an overlap. As of the 2025.03.23 release, this is fixed for G7 to G7 switch as well.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6", "G7", "Dexcom One", "One+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Nightscout follower", "G6 collector", "G7"], "evidence_quote": "Starting with the xDrip Nightly release of July 17, 2024, xDrip will only backfill (G6 or G7) starting from the last existing reading. This will avoid the possibility of an overlap.", "text": "xDrip can show an overlap when switching hardware data source When switching the hardware data source from a G6 collector to Nightscout follower, xDrip shows overlapping readings (backfilled data overlaps with existing data). The overlap occurs when switching from G6 collector to Nightscout follower, but not when switching from Nightscout follower to G6 collector. The overlap is caused by xDrip backfilling data for a time period that already has readings, even if the timestamps are not exactly the same. The backfill does not check for existing data in the same time period. Starting with the xDrip Nightly release of July 17, 2024, xDrip will only backfill (G6 or G7) starting from the last existing reading. This avoids the possibility of an overlap. As of the 2025.03.23 release, this is fixed for G7 to G7 switch as well. G6 G7 Dexcom One One+ Nightscout follower G6 collector G7 Starting with the xDrip Nightly release of July 17, 2024, xDrip will only backfill (G6 or G7) starting from the last existing reading. This will avoid the possibility of an overlap."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-342", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 342, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 342, "title": "Feature Request: New alarm type for make benefit of a peaceful night's sleep.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/342", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/342", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Dexcom users trying to extend sensor life are woken by high and low alarms that fire on a hair trigger when small amounts of sensor noise creep into glucose readings, causing sleep deprivation.", "cause": "Sensor noise creeps into glucose readings and triggers alarms on a hair trigger, even when settings intended to avoid false alarms are used.", "fix": "Widen the thresholds of the pre and main low alarms (to 4.0 and 3.6 respectively) and switch back to phone as collector from SW3 on OB1G5; these changes were reported to make the low alert behave correctly.", "settings_changed": ["Pre low alarm threshold → 4.0", "Main low alarm threshold → 3.6", "collector → phone"], "devices": ["Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["collector", "ob1g5", "xbridge"], "evidence_quote": "OK I did two things and my low alert just behaved correctly. I widened the threshold of my pre and main low alarms (4.0 and 3.6 respectively). Secondly I switched back to phone as collector, from my SW3 on OB1G5.", "text": "Feature Request: New alarm type for make benefit of a peaceful night's sleep. Dexcom users trying to extend sensor life are woken by high and low alarms that fire on a hair trigger when small amounts of sensor noise creep into glucose readings, causing sleep deprivation. Sensor noise creeps into glucose readings and triggers alarms on a hair trigger, even when settings intended to avoid false alarms are used. Widen the thresholds of the pre and main low alarms (to 4.0 and 3.6 respectively) and switch back to phone as collector from SW3 on OB1G5; these changes were reported to make the low alert behave correctly. Dexcom G5 collector ob1g5 xbridge OK I did two things and my low alert just behaved correctly. I widened the threshold of my pre and main low alarms (4.0 and 3.6 respectively). Secondly I switched back to phone as collector, from my SW3 on OB1G5."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-343", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 343, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 343, "title": "New upgrade broke high values", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/343", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/343", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating, values above 300 show up as a low 30. For example, 319 on Freestyle Libre shows as 31. Everything above 270 shows up as 27 (low).", "cause": "The issue is caused by a numerical overflow due to values beyond the 12-bit coding. The 13th bit was removed from the calculation, causing high values to wrap around and appear as low values.", "fix": "Enable the 13th bit mask in xDrip settings: Settings -> Less Common Settings -> Calibration Settings -> use 13 bit ads mask. Alternatively, use another algorithm as described in LibreOOPAlgorithm. The 13bit mask mode is enabled by default in the latest nightly.", "settings_changed": ["use 13 bit ads mask → enabled"], "devices": ["Freestyle Libre", "AmbrosiaSys BluCon"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["13 bit mask", "blucon"], "evidence_quote": "Due to very bad lack the 13 bit was removed from the calculation therefore the numbers got smaller again. @KevinDenys What you can immediately do is 1) return to use the 13'th bit  2) use another algorithm for calculating bg. To return the 13'th bit do: in xDrip settings->less common settings->calibration settings->use 13 bit ads mask.", "text": "New upgrade broke high values After updating, values above 300 show up as a low 30. For example, 319 on Freestyle Libre shows as 31. Everything above 270 shows up as 27 (low). The issue is caused by a numerical overflow due to values beyond the 12-bit coding. The 13th bit was removed from the calculation, causing high values to wrap around and appear as low values. Enable the 13th bit mask in xDrip settings: Settings -> Less Common Settings -> Calibration Settings -> use 13 bit ads mask. Alternatively, use another algorithm as described in LibreOOPAlgorithm. The 13bit mask mode is enabled by default in the latest nightly. Freestyle Libre AmbrosiaSys BluCon 13 bit mask blucon Due to very bad lack the 13 bit was removed from the calculation therefore the numbers got smaller again. @KevinDenys What you can immediately do is 1) return to use the 13'th bit  2) use another algorithm for calculating bg. To return the 13'th bit do: in xDrip settings->less common settings->calibration settings->use 13 bit ads mask."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-351", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 351, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 351, "title": "Insulin Fiasp Prediction", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/351", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/351", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Fiasp has a different curve for prediction values; it starts quicker and may not last as long as Novolog. Users report that predictions are wrong with the actual insulin model, and the insulin action graph does not reflect the actual duration or peak time.", "cause": "The thread suggests that different insulins (like Fiasp) have different action curves, and the current model assumes a symmetrical curve with peak at half duration, which does not match Fiasp's early peak.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Users suggest adjusting the insulin duration setting in predictive settings to better match Fiasp's action, and one user proposes adding a field for peak time to create an asymmetrical triangle model.", "settings_changed": ["Insulin duration → 3h", "Insulin duration → 3.5h", "Insulin duration → 1.67h"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The main issue is that Fiasp is not a simmetrical curve, the peak is very erly compared to its duration. Reading the comments here i'll try to put the duration of fiasp to 1.67 h getting the peak at 50 min and check the predictions.", "text": "Insulin Fiasp Prediction Fiasp has a different curve for prediction values; it starts quicker and may not last as long as Novolog. Users report that predictions are wrong with the actual insulin model, and the insulin action graph does not reflect the actual duration or peak time. The thread suggests that different insulins (like Fiasp) have different action curves, and the current model assumes a symmetrical curve with peak at half duration, which does not match Fiasp's early peak. No definitive fix is provided. Users suggest adjusting the insulin duration setting in predictive settings to better match Fiasp's action, and one user proposes adding a field for peak time to create an asymmetrical triangle model.   The main issue is that Fiasp is not a simmetrical curve, the peak is very erly compared to its duration. Reading the comments here i'll try to put the duration of fiasp to 1.67 h getting the peak at 50 min and check the predictions."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3582", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3582, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3582, "title": "xDrip followers sync feature dead after Google FCM API removed on 22.07.2024", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3582", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3582", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After Google removed the old FCM API, communication between xDrip master and followers is broken using the default sync; followers do not receive data.", "cause": "Google deprecated and removed the old FCM (Firebase Cloud Messaging) API on 2024-07-22, which xDrip's default master/follower sync relied on.", "fix": "Update to release 2024.09.15b or any later version and enable the setting 'Use xDrip Cloud' on the xDrip Sync Settings page on both the master and all followers.", "settings_changed": ["Use xDrip Cloud → enabled"], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 6"], "driver_tags": ["companion app", "default sync", "desert sync", "fcm", "nightscout", "xdrip cloud"], "evidence_quote": "Update to the release of 2024.09.15b or any after that.\n\nMake sure to enable the setting `Use xDrip Cloud` on the xDrip Sync Settings page on the master and followers.", "text": "xDrip followers sync feature dead after Google FCM API removed on 22.07.2024 After Google removed the old FCM API, communication between xDrip master and followers is broken using the default sync; followers do not receive data. Google deprecated and removed the old FCM (Firebase Cloud Messaging) API on 2024-07-22, which xDrip's default master/follower sync relied on. Update to release 2024.09.15b or any later version and enable the setting 'Use xDrip Cloud' on the xDrip Sync Settings page on both the master and all followers. Android 6 companion app default sync desert sync fcm nightscout xdrip cloud Update to the release of 2024.09.15b or any after that.\n\nMake sure to enable the setting `Use xDrip Cloud` on the xDrip Sync Settings page on the master and followers."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3749", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3749, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3749, "title": "System Status - No \"Sensor Start/Age\" display after xdrip update", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3749", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3749", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After an automatic xdrip update to version dfcbe80-2024.09.17, the Classic Status Page no longer displays the sensor start date and sensor age. This occurs with both 'Libre (patched App)' and 'Nightscout Follower' data sources. Reinstalling the previous version restores the display.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Navid200 speculates that xDrip may not know when a Libre session started because the session runs on the Libre device, not xDrip, but this is not confirmed.", "fix": "The thread does not state a final fix. A PR (#3750) was opened but marked as draft pending discussion. The user found that reverting to the previous version (06.11) restored the display, but this is a workaround, not a fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre3", "Libre2"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": ["Libre patched", "Nightscout Follower", "juggluco", "broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "I reinstalled the previous version again, to make sure it's an xdrip issue. It is - previous version instantly showed sensor start date and age again.", "text": "System Status - No \"Sensor Start/Age\" display after xdrip update After an automatic xdrip update to version dfcbe80-2024.09.17, the Classic Status Page no longer displays the sensor start date and sensor age. This occurs with both 'Libre (patched App)' and 'Nightscout Follower' data sources. Reinstalling the previous version restores the display. The thread does not definitively establish a root cause. Navid200 speculates that xDrip may not know when a Libre session started because the session runs on the Libre device, not xDrip, but this is not confirmed. The thread does not state a final fix. A PR (#3750) was opened but marked as draft pending discussion. The user found that reverting to the previous version (06.11) restored the display, but this is a workaround, not a fix. Libre3 Libre2 Android 10 Libre patched Nightscout Follower juggluco broadcast I reinstalled the previous version again, to make sure it's an xdrip issue. It is - previous version instantly showed sensor start date and age again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3787", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3787, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3787, "title": "Companion App - Incorrect deltas / trend arrows and issues with the time it syncs", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3787", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3787", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using the Companion App source, xDrip shows incorrect deltas and trend arrows, and reading sync timing is off. For example, readings 1 minute apart can show a delta of +41 mg/dl instead of the expected +10, with the widget sometimes showing the correct delta but a wrong arrow while the app and notification show incorrect values.", "cause": "Navid (maintainer) states that for Companion App mode with a Dexcom device, the problem is 99% likely caused by Companion Bluetooth not being enabled. Another participant explains that xDrip reads notification data which may be stale, causing readings to sometimes be treated as only 1 minute apart and producing inflated deltas.", "fix": "Enable Companion Bluetooth as described at the xDrip docs for companion app mode with Dexcom devices. However, this is disputed in the thread and no confirmed resolution is given.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom One+", "eversense", "Medtronic", "G7"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["companion app", "companion mode", "companion bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "If you are using the companion app mode with a Dexcom device and experience the problem described here, it is 99% likely you have not enabled Companion Bluetooth.", "text": "Companion App - Incorrect deltas / trend arrows and issues with the time it syncs When using the Companion App source, xDrip shows incorrect deltas and trend arrows, and reading sync timing is off. For example, readings 1 minute apart can show a delta of +41 mg/dl instead of the expected +10, with the widget sometimes showing the correct delta but a wrong arrow while the app and notification show incorrect values. Navid (maintainer) states that for Companion App mode with a Dexcom device, the problem is 99% likely caused by Companion Bluetooth not being enabled. Another participant explains that xDrip reads notification data which may be stale, causing readings to sometimes be treated as only 1 minute apart and producing inflated deltas. Enable Companion Bluetooth as described at the xDrip docs for companion app mode with Dexcom devices. However, this is disputed in the thread and no confirmed resolution is given. Dexcom One+ eversense Medtronic G7 companion app companion mode companion bluetooth If you are using the companion app mode with a Dexcom device and experience the problem described here, it is 99% likely you have not enabled Companion Bluetooth."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-380", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 380, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 380, "title": "Consistent REST-API problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/380", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/380", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Users are receiving consistent error messages (pop-up) on their Android smartphone when uploading to Nightscout via REST API. Some BG readings go through sporadically and laggy, and treatments do not show up in Nightscout.", "cause": "The issue was caused by an Azure App Service deployment that affected Android apps with older HTTP clients, leading to connection failures. The specific cause was the site config setting \"http20Enabled\" being set to true, which caused problems with HTTP/2.", "fix": "The workaround is to change the Azure site config setting \"http20Enabled\" to false via resources.azure.com, and optionally replace https with http in the REST API cloud upload URL in xDrip+, then restart the Azure site.", "settings_changed": ["http20Enabled → false"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["rest api", "nightscout", "azure"], "evidence_quote": "Customers experiencing this issue can self-mitigate by updating the site config setting \"http20Enabled\" to false via resources.azure.com.", "text": "Consistent REST-API problem Users are receiving consistent error messages (pop-up) on their Android smartphone when uploading to Nightscout via REST API. Some BG readings go through sporadically and laggy, and treatments do not show up in Nightscout. The issue was caused by an Azure App Service deployment that affected Android apps with older HTTP clients, leading to connection failures. The specific cause was the site config setting \"http20Enabled\" being set to true, which caused problems with HTTP/2. The workaround is to change the Azure site config setting \"http20Enabled\" to false via resources.azure.com, and optionally replace https with http in the REST API cloud upload URL in xDrip+, then restart the Azure site.  rest api nightscout azure Customers experiencing this issue can self-mitigate by updating the site config setting \"http20Enabled\" to false via resources.azure.com."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3841", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3841, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3841, "title": "AAPS 3.3.x and Libre 2/3 identifier sent from Xdrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3841", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3841", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "With AAPS 3.3.x, SMB cannot be enabled for Libre 2 & 3 because AAPS reports 'active BG source doesn't support advanced filtering.' The issue is that xDrip sends an incorrect identifier for Libre sensors, such as LIBRE_1_OTHER or LIBRE_1_LIMMITER, instead of the expected 'Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3'.", "cause": "xDrip sends an incorrect source identifier in the broadcast to AAPS. AAPS expects 'Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3' in com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.Extras.SourceInfo, but xDrip sends identifiers like LIBRE_1_OTHER or LIBRE_1_LIMMITER (as seen in AAPS logs).", "fix": "Update xDrip to send the correct identifiers ('Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3') in the SourceInfo broadcast. This was reportedly fixed in a nightly commit (f6bd8e58c921c585f198e96ce14482fa7019e097). Users should also upgrade to the latest AAPS 3.3.1.3 to include the 'Libre2 Native' identifier.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "Libre 3", "FreeStyle Libre 2 plus"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Libre Bluetooth", "LimiTTer", "OOP", "Juggluco", "patched Libre broadcast"], "evidence_quote": "AAPS expects `Libre2` or `Libre2 Native` or `Libre3` in `com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.Extras.SourceInfo` to be able to properly identify Libre 2 or 3 for full SMB support in AAPS 3.3", "text": "AAPS 3.3.x and Libre 2/3 identifier sent from Xdrip With AAPS 3.3.x, SMB cannot be enabled for Libre 2 & 3 because AAPS reports 'active BG source doesn't support advanced filtering.' The issue is that xDrip sends an incorrect identifier for Libre sensors, such as LIBRE_1_OTHER or LIBRE_1_LIMMITER, instead of the expected 'Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3'. xDrip sends an incorrect source identifier in the broadcast to AAPS. AAPS expects 'Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3' in com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.Extras.SourceInfo, but xDrip sends identifiers like LIBRE_1_OTHER or LIBRE_1_LIMMITER (as seen in AAPS logs). Update xDrip to send the correct identifiers ('Libre2', 'Libre2 Native', or 'Libre3') in the SourceInfo broadcast. This was reportedly fixed in a nightly commit (f6bd8e58c921c585f198e96ce14482fa7019e097). Users should also upgrade to the latest AAPS 3.3.1.3 to include the 'Libre2 Native' identifier. Libre 2 Libre 3 FreeStyle Libre 2 plus Libre Bluetooth LimiTTer OOP Juggluco patched Libre broadcast AAPS expects `Libre2` or `Libre2 Native` or `Libre3` in `com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.Extras.SourceInfo` to be able to properly identify Libre 2 or 3 for full SMB support in AAPS 3.3"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-3842", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 3842, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 3842, "title": "Libre 2plus / 2+ additional sensor life not recognised", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3842", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/3842", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "xDrip+ does not recognize the Libre 2+ sensor's increased standard life from 14 to 15 days. End-of-life prediction is incorrect, saying the sensor will expire a day early, and after it keeps running beyond 15 days xDrip reports age like 15.1 days and no longer offers an end time.", "cause": "xDrip+ does not differentiate between the Libre 2 and the Libre 2+ sensor, and continues to use the Libre 2's 14-day lifespan for Libre 2+ sensors.", "fix": "Update to the 2025.07.16 xDrip release, which addresses this by recognizing the Libre 2+ sensor and its 15-day lifespan (PR #4080). Testing of the fix confirmed the sensor is identified as 2plus and shows the correct end time of about 14.9/15 days.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2+", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["librelink", "juggluco", "miaomiao"], "evidence_quote": "This should be addressed as of the 2025.07.16 release.", "text": "Libre 2plus / 2+ additional sensor life not recognised xDrip+ does not recognize the Libre 2+ sensor's increased standard life from 14 to 15 days. End-of-life prediction is incorrect, saying the sensor will expire a day early, and after it keeps running beyond 15 days xDrip reports age like 15.1 days and no longer offers an end time. xDrip+ does not differentiate between the Libre 2 and the Libre 2+ sensor, and continues to use the Libre 2's 14-day lifespan for Libre 2+ sensors. Update to the 2025.07.16 xDrip release, which addresses this by recognizing the Libre 2+ sensor and its 15-day lifespan (PR #4080). Testing of the fix confirmed the sensor is identified as 2plus and shows the correct end time of about 14.9/15 days. Libre 2+ Libre 2 librelink juggluco miaomiao This should be addressed as of the 2025.07.16 release."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-385", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 385, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 385, "title": "Apparent calibration or data processing issue reported (with Libre/Blucon)", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/385", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/385", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The app sometimes seems to get into a dormant state, especially at low glucose levels, and does not move from a level (e.g., showing 77 when actual blood glucose is 33). Calibration entries at low values are rejected as out of range.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Developers suggest it may be a calibration slope mismatch or that raw sensor data is staying the same, but they cannot reproduce it and consider it unlikely an algorithm issue.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include calibrating on stable values that are low-normal and highish-normal, and resetting all calibrations (Stop Sensor > Don't Stop, Just Reset all Calibrations) as a workaround.", "settings_changed": ["Stop Sensor > Don't Stop, Just Reset all Calibrations"], "devices": ["Libre", "Blucon"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["blucon/libre integration"], "evidence_quote": "The main reason this issue doesn't have any real way to resolve it is that what is being reported doesn't make any sense, hasn't been reported before and may well be an issue out of our control. We certainly don't have any way to reproduce it.", "text": "Apparent calibration or data processing issue reported (with Libre/Blucon) The app sometimes seems to get into a dormant state, especially at low glucose levels, and does not move from a level (e.g., showing 77 when actual blood glucose is 33). Calibration entries at low values are rejected as out of range. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Developers suggest it may be a calibration slope mismatch or that raw sensor data is staying the same, but they cannot reproduce it and consider it unlikely an algorithm issue. No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include calibrating on stable values that are low-normal and highish-normal, and resetting all calibrations (Stop Sensor > Don't Stop, Just Reset all Calibrations) as a workaround. Libre Blucon blucon/libre integration The main reason this issue doesn't have any real way to resolve it is that what is being reported doesn't make any sense, hasn't been reported before and may well be an issue out of our control. We certainly don't have any way to reproduce it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-39", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 39, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 39, "title": "Erratic xDrip battery estimates", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/39", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/39", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After updating the circuit to xBridge2 firmware with battery charge indicator resistors, the battery percentage readings are erratic: overnight it wouldn't charge above 40%, then depleted quickly to 20%, then jumped to 79% when plugged into a 1A charger, charged to 100% quickly, but dropped to 84% immediately after disconnecting.", "cause": "The xBridge2 battery indication is not a truly accurate measurement of battery capacity; it is only an indication based on battery voltage, not current in/out. The circuit design and off-the-shelf components cannot provide accurate readings.", "fix": "Use the Adafruit charger's red/green LED to know when charging is complete; do not remove the bridge from charging until the green LED is lit. The indication will then stay at 100% for a fair period. Under the current design, only a rough indication is possible.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["xBridge2", "Wixel"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xBridge2"], "evidence_quote": "the xBridge2 battery indication is NOT a truly accurate measurement of battery capacity, it is only an indication.based on battery voltage, not a measurement based on current in/out like most mobile phones.", "text": "Erratic xDrip battery estimates After updating the circuit to xBridge2 firmware with battery charge indicator resistors, the battery percentage readings are erratic: overnight it wouldn't charge above 40%, then depleted quickly to 20%, then jumped to 79% when plugged into a 1A charger, charged to 100% quickly, but dropped to 84% immediately after disconnecting. The xBridge2 battery indication is not a truly accurate measurement of battery capacity; it is only an indication based on battery voltage, not current in/out. The circuit design and off-the-shelf components cannot provide accurate readings. Use the Adafruit charger's red/green LED to know when charging is complete; do not remove the bridge from charging until the green LED is lit. The indication will then stay at 100% for a fair period. Under the current design, only a rough indication is possible. xBridge2 Wixel xBridge2 the xBridge2 battery indication is NOT a truly accurate measurement of battery capacity, it is only an indication.based on battery voltage, not a measurement based on current in/out like most mobile phones."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-40", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 40, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 40, "title": "What should we do when parseInt in EditAlertActivity returns null", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/40", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/40", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A NullPointerException occurs in EditAlertActivity.java line 795 when parseInt returns null and is cast to int, causing a crash in the onTouch listener.", "cause": "The parseInt call can return null, and the code casts it to int without null check, leading to a NullPointerException.", "fix": "The issue was resolved by a commit that likely added a null check or fallback to default value. The thread suggests using a try-catch or checking for null and using SnoozeActivity.getDefaultSnooze(above) as fallback.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Should now be resolved by: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/f4502664f76a2f3d4b1eec9fa101d23390908f1a", "text": "What should we do when parseInt in EditAlertActivity returns null A NullPointerException occurs in EditAlertActivity.java line 795 when parseInt returns null and is cast to int, causing a crash in the onTouch listener. The parseInt call can return null, and the code casts it to int without null check, leading to a NullPointerException. The issue was resolved by a commit that likely added a null check or fallback to default value. The thread suggests using a try-catch or checking for null and using SnoozeActivity.getDefaultSnooze(above) as fallback.   Should now be resolved by: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/f4502664f76a2f3d4b1eec9fa101d23390908f1a"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-403", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 403, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 403, "title": "Rest-Api - Nightscout data download not working", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/403", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/403", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "With 'Also try to download data from Nightscout' activated, no data from Nightscout is downloaded. Users report that treatments are downloaded but BG data is not.", "cause": "xDrip cannot download BG readings from Nightscout; the capability does not exist.", "fix": "No fix; the feature is not implemented. Workaround: transfer database from old phone to new phone. A pull request was opened to rename the menu item to avoid confusion.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout sync (rest-api)", "cloud upload agent"], "evidence_quote": "xDrip cannot download BG readings from Nightscout. You will need to transfer database from the old phone to the new phone. I have opened a pull request to change the menu to avoid this confusion as suggested by Patrick. I am closing this issue as the capability does not exist.", "text": "Rest-Api - Nightscout data download not working With 'Also try to download data from Nightscout' activated, no data from Nightscout is downloaded. Users report that treatments are downloaded but BG data is not. xDrip cannot download BG readings from Nightscout; the capability does not exist. No fix; the feature is not implemented. Workaround: transfer database from old phone to new phone. A pull request was opened to rename the menu item to avoid confusion.  nightscout sync (rest-api) cloud upload agent xDrip cannot download BG readings from Nightscout. You will need to transfer database from the old phone to the new phone. I have opened a pull request to change the menu to avoid this confusion as suggested by Patrick. I am closing this issue as the capability does not exist."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-408", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 408, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 408, "title": "Medtrum CGM", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/408", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/408", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User asks if the Medtrum CGM (A6) can be used with xDrip.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Medtrum A6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "It doesn't currently work with xDrip. To make it work we would basically need to have physical access to a device to reliably implement support for it.", "text": "Medtrum CGM User asks if the Medtrum CGM (A6) can be used with xDrip.   Medtrum A6  It doesn't currently work with xDrip. To make it work we would basically need to have physical access to a device to reliably implement support for it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-4173", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4173, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 4173, "title": "New Polish Libre 2 14 day Sensor 7F 0E 30", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/4173", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/4173", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "xDrip does not properly recognize the latest Libre 2 sensors in Poland with serial numbers starting with 301, treating them as Libre 1 fallback. NFC scanning gives 'Incorrect NFC data' and logs show 0x7f0e30.", "cause": "xDrip does not recognize the new sensor type (0x7f0e30) and treats it as Libre 1 fallback.", "fix": "A test release (based on PR #4180) with an updated OOP2 and enabling a setting (switched off by default) in the test version resolved the issue. The sensor is recognized as Libre2Plus and readings work. The fix was included in the 2025.09.26 release.", "settings_changed": ["NFC scan features → enabled"], "devices": ["Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 15"], "driver_tags": ["OOP2", "Libre Bluetooth", "NFC"], "evidence_quote": "As of the 2025.09.26 release, this sensor is recognized.", "text": "New Polish Libre 2 14 day Sensor 7F 0E 30 xDrip does not properly recognize the latest Libre 2 sensors in Poland with serial numbers starting with 301, treating them as Libre 1 fallback. NFC scanning gives 'Incorrect NFC data' and logs show 0x7f0e30. xDrip does not recognize the new sensor type (0x7f0e30) and treats it as Libre 1 fallback. A test release (based on PR #4180) with an updated OOP2 and enabling a setting (switched off by default) in the test version resolved the issue. The sensor is recognized as Libre2Plus and readings work. The fix was included in the 2025.09.26 release. Libre 2 Android 15 OOP2 Libre Bluetooth NFC As of the 2025.09.26 release, this sensor is recognized."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-4215", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 4215, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 4215, "title": "Libre sensor \"wait 60 minutes\" on already running sensor", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/4215", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/4215", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users report that when starting an already-running Libre 2/2+ sensor in xDrip+ (e.g., after scanning with NFC and selecting \"Not today\"), xDrip+ displays a \"wait 60 minutes\" warmup message and delays calibration and data transmission to AAPS, even though the sensor has been running for days.", "cause": "The thread identifies that a code change introduced between nightly builds 2025.03.12 and 2025.03.23 caused this behavior, but the exact root cause is not fully established. It is suspected to relate to overlapping backfills or the handling of sensor start times.", "fix": "A fix was attempted via PR #4253 and released in the 2025.11.28 Nightly, but the issue persisted for some users. Later, it was reported as resolved (not persisting beyond once on a new installation) and the issue was closed. The thread does not specify a precise configuration change.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "Libre 2+"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Libre Bluetooth hardware data source", "OOP2", "NFC"], "evidence_quote": "I just updated to 2025.12.02 as I saw Libre mentioned in the changelog. Stopped the sensor in xDrip+, NFC scanned, did \"Start sensor\", said \"Not today\" and went to \"Please wait while sensor warms up! (60 minutes) status.", "text": "Libre sensor \"wait 60 minutes\" on already running sensor Users report that when starting an already-running Libre 2/2+ sensor in xDrip+ (e.g., after scanning with NFC and selecting \"Not today\"), xDrip+ displays a \"wait 60 minutes\" warmup message and delays calibration and data transmission to AAPS, even though the sensor has been running for days. The thread identifies that a code change introduced between nightly builds 2025.03.12 and 2025.03.23 caused this behavior, but the exact root cause is not fully established. It is suspected to relate to overlapping backfills or the handling of sensor start times. A fix was attempted via PR #4253 and released in the 2025.11.28 Nightly, but the issue persisted for some users. Later, it was reported as resolved (not persisting beyond once on a new installation) and the issue was closed. The thread does not specify a precise configuration change. Libre 2 Libre 2+ Libre Bluetooth hardware data source OOP2 NFC I just updated to 2025.12.02 as I saw Libre mentioned in the changelog. Stopped the sensor in xDrip+, NFC scanned, did \"Start sensor\", said \"Not today\" and went to \"Please wait while sensor warms up! (60 minutes) status."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-436", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 436, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 436, "title": "Ticwatch E", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/436", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/436", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "A Ticwatch E with Wear 2.0 paired with Dexcom G5 but does not work as a standalone collector; data values are not received when used as a standalone collector.", "cause": "The thread suggests the issue is due to a known bug with Wear 2.0 watches out of the box, and later comments indicate that the Ticwatch E cannot work as a collector without a dedicated patch, regardless of Android version.", "fix": "One user reported that updating the Ticwatch E to Android 8.0 made it work as a collector, but another user tried both official and unofficial Android 8.0 updates and could not get the collector service running. The thread does not provide a definitive fix; it suggests asking an xDrip developer for a dedicated patch or using a different watch.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Ticwatch E", "Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0"], "driver_tags": ["standalone collector", "collector service"], "evidence_quote": "i had the same issue but found a solution. i have updated the ticwatch to android 8.0 and now it works as a collector.", "text": "Ticwatch E A Ticwatch E with Wear 2.0 paired with Dexcom G5 but does not work as a standalone collector; data values are not received when used as a standalone collector. The thread suggests the issue is due to a known bug with Wear 2.0 watches out of the box, and later comments indicate that the Ticwatch E cannot work as a collector without a dedicated patch, regardless of Android version. One user reported that updating the Ticwatch E to Android 8.0 made it work as a collector, but another user tried both official and unofficial Android 8.0 updates and could not get the collector service running. The thread does not provide a definitive fix; it suggests asking an xDrip developer for a dedicated patch or using a different watch. Ticwatch E Dexcom G5 Android 8.0 standalone collector collector service i had the same issue but found a solution. i have updated the ticwatch to android 8.0 and now it works as a collector."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-459", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 459, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 459, "title": "Samsung Bluetooth very unstable", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/459", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/459", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Samsung S9 with Libre and miaomiao will not stay connected and eventually cannot connect at all. Other Samsung phones (S9+, A5 2017, S6 edge) also experience unstable Bluetooth connections, with connections dropping after some time and failing to reconnect.", "cause": "The thread identifies a possible issue with Android 8.0 (Oreo) on Samsung devices causing Bluetooth problems, possibly related to a June 5 security patch. A user also found that the 'Allow blucon unbonding' option, which defaults to enabled, may cause pairing failures due to a bug in the code.", "fix": "Several workarounds are suggested: clearing the Bluetooth cache on the phone, disabling the 'Allow blucon unbonding' option (which resolved issues for one user), and using Glimp to maintain the Bluetooth connection. A Samsung security patch (G950FXXU2CRF1) was reported to fix issues on S8.", "settings_changed": ["Allow blucon unbonding → off"], "devices": ["Samsung S9", "Libre", "miaomiao", "Samsung S9+", "Samsung A5 2017", "Samsung S6 edge", "Dexcom G5", "blucon"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0", "Android 6.0.1"], "driver_tags": ["miaomiao", "blucon", "G5"], "evidence_quote": "I had horrible problems with it lately (on and off for months, after working great for a while), and then found a new option had been added: \"Allow blucon unbonding\", which defaults to enabled.  Turning this off seems to fix everything.", "text": "Samsung Bluetooth very unstable Samsung S9 with Libre and miaomiao will not stay connected and eventually cannot connect at all. Other Samsung phones (S9+, A5 2017, S6 edge) also experience unstable Bluetooth connections, with connections dropping after some time and failing to reconnect. The thread identifies a possible issue with Android 8.0 (Oreo) on Samsung devices causing Bluetooth problems, possibly related to a June 5 security patch. A user also found that the 'Allow blucon unbonding' option, which defaults to enabled, may cause pairing failures due to a bug in the code. Several workarounds are suggested: clearing the Bluetooth cache on the phone, disabling the 'Allow blucon unbonding' option (which resolved issues for one user), and using Glimp to maintain the Bluetooth connection. A Samsung security patch (G950FXXU2CRF1) was reported to fix issues on S8. Samsung S9 Libre miaomiao Samsung S9+ Samsung A5 2017 Samsung S6 edge Dexcom G5 blucon Android 8.0 Android 6.0.1 miaomiao blucon G5 I had horrible problems with it lately (on and off for months, after working great for a while), and then found a new option had been added: \"Allow blucon unbonding\", which defaults to enabled.  Turning this off seems to fix everything."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-461", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 461, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 461, "title": "local web service for pebble always returns 0 for iob", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/461", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/461", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The local web service endpoint http://127.0.0.1:17580/pebble always returns 0 for iob, while the corresponding Nightscout URL returns the correct iob value. The user wants to use the local service to get iob data for a Fitbit Versa watchface, especially when without internet.", "cause": "xDrip only calculates its simulation IoB when the main graph is displayed as it is quite CPU intensive. The local web service's pebble endpoint had iob hardcoded to 0.", "fix": "A pull request (https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/2897) was submitted and merged that implements IoB reporting in the /pebble endpoint.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Fitbit Versa"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["local web service", "pebble"], "evidence_quote": "I've submitted a PR that implements this functionality: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/2897", "text": "local web service for pebble always returns 0 for iob The local web service endpoint http://127.0.0.1:17580/pebble always returns 0 for iob, while the corresponding Nightscout URL returns the correct iob value. The user wants to use the local service to get iob data for a Fitbit Versa watchface, especially when without internet. xDrip only calculates its simulation IoB when the main graph is displayed as it is quite CPU intensive. The local web service's pebble endpoint had iob hardcoded to 0. A pull request (https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/2897) was submitted and merged that implements IoB reporting in the /pebble endpoint. Fitbit Versa local web service pebble I've submitted a PR that implements this functionality: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/2897"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-462", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 462, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 462, "title": "FR: DesertSync with 2 Masters/data sources", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/462", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/462", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user wants to use two devices (a smartwatch and a smartphone) to collect data via NFC and/or MiaoMiao, with the smartwatch normally acting as master and the smartphone taking over if the watch runs out of power. However, with two masters enabled, followers only follow one randomly, and one master doesn't get data because the MiaoMiao only allows one Bluetooth peer at a time.", "cause": "The thread suggests that the limitation is due to the device (e.g., MiaoMiao or Dexcom transmitter) only allowing one peer at a time, and that having two masters is not supported by the device, not an xDrip issue.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include using Nightscout follow instead of xDrip sync, and a comment notes that as of a few Nightly releases ago, treatments can be uploaded from both master and follower. The issue was closed as unclear.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["MiaoMiao", "G6", "Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["DesertSync", "Nightscout", "xDrip sync", "NFC", "Bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "As far as having two masters, this seems to be possibly a limitation by the device. You cannot have more than one device collecting from a Dexcom transmitter both on the mobile slot. This is not an xDrip issue.", "text": "FR: DesertSync with 2 Masters/data sources The user wants to use two devices (a smartwatch and a smartphone) to collect data via NFC and/or MiaoMiao, with the smartwatch normally acting as master and the smartphone taking over if the watch runs out of power. However, with two masters enabled, followers only follow one randomly, and one master doesn't get data because the MiaoMiao only allows one Bluetooth peer at a time. The thread suggests that the limitation is due to the device (e.g., MiaoMiao or Dexcom transmitter) only allowing one peer at a time, and that having two masters is not supported by the device, not an xDrip issue. No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include using Nightscout follow instead of xDrip sync, and a comment notes that as of a few Nightly releases ago, treatments can be uploaded from both master and follower. The issue was closed as unclear. MiaoMiao G6 Libre DesertSync Nightscout xDrip sync NFC Bluetooth As far as having two masters, this seems to be possibly a limitation by the device. You cannot have more than one device collecting from a Dexcom transmitter both on the mobile slot. This is not an xDrip issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-486", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 486, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 486, "title": "Newest Android update 8.0", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/486", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/486", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating a Samsung S7 Edge to Android 8.0 (Oreo) with Samsung Experience 9.0, replacing a Libre sensor with a BluCon transmitter fails to connect: the phone receives no initial data, never reaches calibration, and the transmitter never shows connected in xDrip, despite Bluetooth pairing working. The issue persists after clearing app cache/data and reinstalling, and the same setup works on a Samsung Note 4 with Android 6.0.1.", "cause": "The thread identifies the cause as a combination of Android 8.0 (Oreo) Bluetooth stack issues and the BLE module used in the BluCon (HM-10 or similar), which is incompatible with Oreo. Some users also note that the issue may be related to the xDrip version, as reverting to an older version helped.", "fix": "The thread suggests several workarounds: clearing Bluetooth app cache/data and reinstalling xDrip (temporary), reverting to an older xDrip version (e.g., 2018.01.22) which works with random disconnects, or using the latest nightly with OB1 collector (though not fully successful for all). The issue was marked as resolved by a maintainer after changes for Android 8.0 pairing, but no single definitive fix is stated.", "settings_changed": ["Bluetooth app cache and data → cleared", "xDrip version → reverted to 2018.01.22"], "devices": ["Samsung S7 Edge", "BluCon", "Libre sensor", "Samsung Note 4", "MiaoMiao"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0", "Android 6.0.1"], "driver_tags": ["blucon", "miaomiao", "OB1 collector"], "evidence_quote": "I made some changes specifically for pairing issues on Android 8.0 in the last few days, try the latest nightly and use the OB1 collector.", "text": "Newest Android update 8.0 After updating a Samsung S7 Edge to Android 8.0 (Oreo) with Samsung Experience 9.0, replacing a Libre sensor with a BluCon transmitter fails to connect: the phone receives no initial data, never reaches calibration, and the transmitter never shows connected in xDrip, despite Bluetooth pairing working. The issue persists after clearing app cache/data and reinstalling, and the same setup works on a Samsung Note 4 with Android 6.0.1. The thread identifies the cause as a combination of Android 8.0 (Oreo) Bluetooth stack issues and the BLE module used in the BluCon (HM-10 or similar), which is incompatible with Oreo. Some users also note that the issue may be related to the xDrip version, as reverting to an older version helped. The thread suggests several workarounds: clearing Bluetooth app cache/data and reinstalling xDrip (temporary), reverting to an older xDrip version (e.g., 2018.01.22) which works with random disconnects, or using the latest nightly with OB1 collector (though not fully successful for all). The issue was marked as resolved by a maintainer after changes for Android 8.0 pairing, but no single definitive fix is stated. Samsung S7 Edge BluCon Libre sensor Samsung Note 4 MiaoMiao Android 8.0 Android 6.0.1 blucon miaomiao OB1 collector I made some changes specifically for pairing issues on Android 8.0 in the last few days, try the latest nightly and use the OB1 collector."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-496", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 496, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 496, "title": "best smart watch to use as collector?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/496", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/496", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user asks for the best smartwatch to use as a collector when the phone is out of range, without specifying a sensor initially.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre", "Blucon", "MiaoMiao", "Finowatch Q1 PRO", "Gear S2", "Gear S3 Frontier", "LG Watch Sport", "Sony Smartwatch 3", "Zeblaze Thor 4", "Kospet Optimus Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 7"], "driver_tags": ["collector", "bluetooth", "native Android", "Android Wear"], "evidence_quote": "To use a watch as a collector, see the wiki here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/wiki/Patching-Android-Wear-devices-for-use-with-the-G5 The only watch to work as a collector \" out of the box\" is the SSW3. The others must be tweaked.", "text": "best smart watch to use as collector? The user asks for the best smartwatch to use as a collector when the phone is out of range, without specifying a sensor initially.   Libre Blucon MiaoMiao Finowatch Q1 PRO Gear S2 Gear S3 Frontier LG Watch Sport Sony Smartwatch 3 Zeblaze Thor 4 Kospet Optimus Pro Android 7 collector bluetooth native Android Android Wear To use a watch as a collector, see the wiki here: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/wiki/Patching-Android-Wear-devices-for-use-with-the-G5 The only watch to work as a collector \" out of the box\" is the SSW3. The others must be tweaked."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-499", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 499, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 499, "title": "Follower not getting readings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/499", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/499", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The follower device is not receiving any readings from the master, while the watch and master are fine. The follower's xDrip menu only shows 4 options. The issue persists after uninstalling/reinstalling, clearing cache, and rolling back versions. Some users also see 'Maximum Sync Queue size Exceeded' on the master.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the problem is likely due to Google Play services issues on the master, or a failed QR scan during follower setup, or a full sync queue. Later, it is suggested that the master/follower data transfer relies on internet connectivity, not Bluetooth.", "fix": "The thread provides several workarounds: clearing Google Play services data on the master, clearing xDrip app data on the master and re-setting up, changing the sync key on both devices, or using a Nightscout follower as a workaround.", "settings_changed": ["Sync Key → new custom sync key (longer than 16 characters)"], "devices": ["Libre", "MiowMiew", "Wear Watch"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0", "Android 7.0", "Android 8"], "driver_tags": ["forced collector", "master", "follower", "sync"], "evidence_quote": "I fixed the issue on the Master. Go to Settings - Apps - Xdrip - Storage - Clear Data - Then set up everything again.", "text": "Follower not getting readings The follower device is not receiving any readings from the master, while the watch and master are fine. The follower's xDrip menu only shows 4 options. The issue persists after uninstalling/reinstalling, clearing cache, and rolling back versions. Some users also see 'Maximum Sync Queue size Exceeded' on the master. The thread identifies that the problem is likely due to Google Play services issues on the master, or a failed QR scan during follower setup, or a full sync queue. Later, it is suggested that the master/follower data transfer relies on internet connectivity, not Bluetooth. The thread provides several workarounds: clearing Google Play services data on the master, clearing xDrip app data on the master and re-setting up, changing the sync key on both devices, or using a Nightscout follower as a workaround. Libre MiowMiew Wear Watch Android 8.0 Android 7.0 Android 8 forced collector master follower sync I fixed the issue on the Master. Go to Settings - Apps - Xdrip - Storage - Clear Data - Then set up everything again."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-509", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 509, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 509, "title": "Miaomiao connected but no data received", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/509", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/509", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Miaomiao connects to xDrip+ but no data is transferred; system status fields (Tomato Battery, Hardware, Firmware, Libre SN) are empty and no glucose values are available. Some users get a few readings then stop, or only get data when the Tomato app runs in parallel.", "cause": "The thread identifies multiple possible causes: the libreOOPAlgorithm interfering with the connection (deactivating it fixed for some), the Tomato app not being well connected to the sensor, or a problem with the OOP algorithm. For the original reporter, the cause was never definitively established.", "fix": "For some users, disabling the libreOOPAlgorithm (settings->less common setting->other misc options) resolved the issue. Others found that restarting the libreOOPAlgorithm app or resetting calibrations and restarting the Miaomiao helped. The original reporter did not find a fix and switched to Libre 2.", "settings_changed": ["libreOOPAlgorithm → disabled", "OOP algorithm → disabled"], "devices": ["Miaomiao", "Libre 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.1.1"], "driver_tags": ["libreOOPAlgorithm", "Tomato app", "xDrip+", "Miaomiao"], "evidence_quote": "After deactivating the libreOOPAlgorithm it went back to work! So whoever has similar problems, check for that too!", "text": "Miaomiao connected but no data received Miaomiao connects to xDrip+ but no data is transferred; system status fields (Tomato Battery, Hardware, Firmware, Libre SN) are empty and no glucose values are available. Some users get a few readings then stop, or only get data when the Tomato app runs in parallel. The thread identifies multiple possible causes: the libreOOPAlgorithm interfering with the connection (deactivating it fixed for some), the Tomato app not being well connected to the sensor, or a problem with the OOP algorithm. For the original reporter, the cause was never definitively established. For some users, disabling the libreOOPAlgorithm (settings->less common setting->other misc options) resolved the issue. Others found that restarting the libreOOPAlgorithm app or resetting calibrations and restarting the Miaomiao helped. The original reporter did not find a fix and switched to Libre 2. Miaomiao Libre 2 Android 7.1.1 libreOOPAlgorithm Tomato app xDrip+ Miaomiao After deactivating the libreOOPAlgorithm it went back to work! So whoever has similar problems, check for that too!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-516", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 516, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 516, "title": "tizen collectors?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/516", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/516", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user asks if it is possible for Tizen watches to act as standalone collectors for xDrip, and later notes that they are using Wearable Widgets on a Samsung Frontier S3 but would prefer a standalone collector app similar to the Android Wear one.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Frontier S3", "TicWatch S"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wearable widget", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "no, only android watches. there is no xdrip/collector version for tizen watches.", "text": "tizen collectors? The user asks if it is possible for Tizen watches to act as standalone collectors for xDrip, and later notes that they are using Wearable Widgets on a Samsung Frontier S3 but would prefer a standalone collector app similar to the Android Wear one.   Samsung Frontier S3 TicWatch S wearable widget collector no, only android watches. there is no xdrip/collector version for tizen watches."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-527", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 527, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 527, "title": "Bluereader doesn't show predictive simulations?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/527", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/527", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user reports that the Bolus Wizard Preview (predictive simulations) does not appear on the main page even after setting Carb Ratio, Insulin Sensitivity, and CHO Absorption Rate. Additionally, the BlueReader battery values on the main page have a black contour making them almost unreadable.", "cause": "The predictive simulation not showing was due to a missing setting: 'Always show Bolus Wizard Preview' was not enabled. The black contour issue was not definitively resolved; it was speculated to be related to the user's font size set to 'Very large' and possibly a modified DPI, but no root cause was confirmed.", "fix": "Enable the setting: Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> Always show Bolus Wizard Preview. For the battery text readability, no fix was provided in the thread.", "settings_changed": ["Always show Bolus Wizard Preview → ON"], "devices": ["FreeStyle", "BlueReader"], "android_versions": ["Android 6.0.1"], "driver_tags": ["bluereader"], "evidence_quote": "Try: `Settings` -> `xDrip+ Display Settings` -> `Always show Bolus Wizard Preview`", "text": "Bluereader doesn't show predictive simulations? The user reports that the Bolus Wizard Preview (predictive simulations) does not appear on the main page even after setting Carb Ratio, Insulin Sensitivity, and CHO Absorption Rate. Additionally, the BlueReader battery values on the main page have a black contour making them almost unreadable. The predictive simulation not showing was due to a missing setting: 'Always show Bolus Wizard Preview' was not enabled. The black contour issue was not definitively resolved; it was speculated to be related to the user's font size set to 'Very large' and possibly a modified DPI, but no root cause was confirmed. Enable the setting: Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> Always show Bolus Wizard Preview. For the battery text readability, no fix was provided in the thread. FreeStyle BlueReader Android 6.0.1 bluereader Try: `Settings` -> `xDrip+ Display Settings` -> `Always show Bolus Wizard Preview`"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-547", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 547, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 547, "title": "Since I installed last nights version, I no longer get data on my watch.", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/547", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/547", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating xDrip+ to a newer nightly, the user no longer gets xDrip notifications / glucose readings on their Gear 2 watch via the Notification feature, although readings still appear on the phone.", "cause": "The thread identifies a regression in xDrip nightly versions: the Android Notifications function was broken after the 7/15/18 version, and bisection showed the 8/9/18 nightly was the first broken version.", "fix": "The reporter's workaround is to reinstall the xDrip+ 7/15/18 version, which restores notifications to the watch; versions from 8/9/18 onward remained broken. Another user fixed a similar issue by uninstalling xDrip from the watch, resyncing apps, and reinstalling it.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Gear 2", "Samsung S7", "G5 sensor", "Samsung Gear S3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["android notifications", "notification feature", "samsung gear app", "wear os", "tizen"], "evidence_quote": "Reinstalled the 7/15 version yet again, and data is now being sent to my watch again. So, sometime after that version,Android Notifications function got broken.   PLEASE FIX.", "text": "Since I installed last nights version, I no longer get data on my watch. After updating xDrip+ to a newer nightly, the user no longer gets xDrip notifications / glucose readings on their Gear 2 watch via the Notification feature, although readings still appear on the phone. The thread identifies a regression in xDrip nightly versions: the Android Notifications function was broken after the 7/15/18 version, and bisection showed the 8/9/18 nightly was the first broken version. The reporter's workaround is to reinstall the xDrip+ 7/15/18 version, which restores notifications to the watch; versions from 8/9/18 onward remained broken. Another user fixed a similar issue by uninstalling xDrip from the watch, resyncing apps, and reinstalling it. Gear 2 Samsung S7 G5 sensor Samsung Gear S3 android notifications notification feature samsung gear app wear os tizen Reinstalled the 7/15 version yet again, and data is now being sent to my watch again. So, sometime after that version,Android Notifications function got broken.   PLEASE FIX."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-553", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 553, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 553, "title": "Speak Readings>\"Or per number of minutes\" text is too large", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/553", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/553", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The text for 'Speak Readings' and 'Or per number of minutes' is too large compared to other text on that page, making it impossible to see the current setting (number of minutes). The font size is out of proportion to all other text.", "cause": "The standard text size while rendering the SeekBar is bigger than other Preferences types, as observed in all Prefs where the seekbar is used.", "fix": "No definitive fix was stated. A workaround is to rotate the phone to see the setting completely. A potential fix suggested by MasterPlexus is adding android:textSize=\"5sp\" to all SeekBarPreference's in pref_advanced_settings.xml, but this was not confirmed by jamorham. Jamorham suggested a custom layout for SeekBarPreference but encountered a crash.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Gear 2", "S7"], "android_versions": ["Android 8.0.0"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "The only outsized fonts on that page seem to be the two lines that I mentioned in the OP.", "text": "Speak Readings>\"Or per number of minutes\" text is too large The text for 'Speak Readings' and 'Or per number of minutes' is too large compared to other text on that page, making it impossible to see the current setting (number of minutes). The font size is out of proportion to all other text. The standard text size while rendering the SeekBar is bigger than other Preferences types, as observed in all Prefs where the seekbar is used. No definitive fix was stated. A workaround is to rotate the phone to see the setting completely. A potential fix suggested by MasterPlexus is adding android:textSize=\"5sp\" to all SeekBarPreference's in pref_advanced_settings.xml, but this was not confirmed by jamorham. Jamorham suggested a custom layout for SeekBarPreference but encountered a crash. Gear 2 S7 Android 8.0.0  The only outsized fonts on that page seem to be the two lines that I mentioned in the OP."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-566", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 566, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 566, "title": "[HELP!] Xdrip early G5 transmitter death?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/566", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/566", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "A new G5 transmitter (28 days old) used only with xDrip OB1 shows voltage A at 250, and later dies early. Subsequent transmitters also die early (around 60 days), while a transmitter first used with the Dexcom app lasted longer.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user speculates that not using native mode on the G5 transmitter from the start may cause early battery drain, but maintainers dispute this, stating xDrip cannot affect transmitter power consumption.", "fix": "No definitive fix is stated. One user reports that enabling 'G5 Native' in xDrip made the transmitter last longer, but this is anecdotal and disputed.", "settings_changed": ["G5 Native → enabled"], "devices": ["Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1", "native mode", "non-native mode"], "evidence_quote": "On my latest transmitter, I enabled 'G5 Native' in xdrip, and the transmitter seems to be lasting much longer.", "text": "[HELP!] Xdrip early G5 transmitter death? A new G5 transmitter (28 days old) used only with xDrip OB1 shows voltage A at 250, and later dies early. Subsequent transmitters also die early (around 60 days), while a transmitter first used with the Dexcom app lasted longer. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. One user speculates that not using native mode on the G5 transmitter from the start may cause early battery drain, but maintainers dispute this, stating xDrip cannot affect transmitter power consumption. No definitive fix is stated. One user reports that enabling 'G5 Native' in xDrip made the transmitter last longer, but this is anecdotal and disputed. Dexcom G5 OB1 native mode non-native mode On my latest transmitter, I enabled 'G5 Native' in xdrip, and the transmitter seems to be lasting much longer."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-571", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 571, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 571, "title": "Samsung Galaxy watch feature request", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/571", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/571", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users report that after updating to the latest nightly build, xDrip notifications became persistent and can no longer be dismissed, so they are no longer forwarded to Samsung Galaxy/Gear watches. Previously, notifications were dismissable and updated every 5 minutes, allowing glucose readings and graphs to appear on the watch.", "cause": "The change in notification behavior (from dismissable to persistent) in a nightly build caused the notifications to stop being sent to Tizen-based Samsung watches.", "fix": "No official fix was provided. Workarounds include using the Wearable Widgets app to display the xDrip widget on the watch, or using a combination of Tasker and AutoNotification with Watchmaker (as described in a guide by FreDiabetics). Some users downgraded to the 7/15/18 version of xDrip to restore notification forwarding.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung Galaxy Watch", "Gear S3", "Samsung Galaxy Watch", "Miaomiao2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wearable widgets", "notification", "Tizen", "Tasker", "AutoNotification", "Watchmaker"], "evidence_quote": "I've been begging for that to be fixed, for months now (I first posted Aug 13, 2018). If you use the 7/15/18 version, notifications to a Tizen watch will work--I don't know about to other watch OS's.", "text": "Samsung Galaxy watch feature request Users report that after updating to the latest nightly build, xDrip notifications became persistent and can no longer be dismissed, so they are no longer forwarded to Samsung Galaxy/Gear watches. Previously, notifications were dismissable and updated every 5 minutes, allowing glucose readings and graphs to appear on the watch. The change in notification behavior (from dismissable to persistent) in a nightly build caused the notifications to stop being sent to Tizen-based Samsung watches. No official fix was provided. Workarounds include using the Wearable Widgets app to display the xDrip widget on the watch, or using a combination of Tasker and AutoNotification with Watchmaker (as described in a guide by FreDiabetics). Some users downgraded to the 7/15/18 version of xDrip to restore notification forwarding. Samsung Galaxy Watch Gear S3 Samsung Galaxy Watch Miaomiao2 wearable widgets notification Tizen Tasker AutoNotification Watchmaker I've been begging for that to be fixed, for months now (I first posted Aug 13, 2018). If you use the 7/15/18 version, notifications to a Tizen watch will work--I don't know about to other watch OS's."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-609", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 609, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 609, "title": "Android 9.0 xDrip+ won't connect", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/609", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/609", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After phone updated to Android Pie 9.0 on Oneplus 6, xDrip+ cannot connect to Blucon. It finds Blucon but connection status is not connected and no values are shown. Disconnecting, uninstalling app, resetting phone, resetting Blucon, and replacing Libre sensor did not help.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the issue is related to Android 9.0 and Bluetooth settings. Specifically, the 'Trust Auto-connect' option (or 'Trust Android Auto Connect') being enabled can prevent connection. Also, other devices like Fitbit keeping Bluetooth connection alive can interfere. The thread does not establish a single definitive root cause but points to these settings and potential OS issues.", "fix": "Turn off 'Trust Auto-connect' option in xDrip+ settings (under Less common settings -> Bluetooth settings). Also, some users found success by disabling the OB1 Collector (Settings -> G5/G6 Debug Settings -> Use The OB1 Collector) and by disabling 'close GATT on ble disconnect' (though this was suggested as better enabled). Additionally, turning off Fitbit's keep Bluetooth connection alive option helped one user.", "settings_changed": ["Trust Auto-connect → off", "Use The OB1 Collector → off", "close GATT on ble disconnect → enabled"], "devices": ["Blucon", "Oneplus 6", "Libre sensor", "Miaomiao", "Fitbit"], "android_versions": ["Android 9.0", "Android 9", "Android Pie"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "OB1 Collector", "Trust Auto-connect", "close GATT on ble disconnect"], "evidence_quote": "You have to turn off \"Trust Auto-connect\" option in the settings. This worked for me.", "text": "Android 9.0 xDrip+ won't connect After phone updated to Android Pie 9.0 on Oneplus 6, xDrip+ cannot connect to Blucon. It finds Blucon but connection status is not connected and no values are shown. Disconnecting, uninstalling app, resetting phone, resetting Blucon, and replacing Libre sensor did not help. The thread identifies that the issue is related to Android 9.0 and Bluetooth settings. Specifically, the 'Trust Auto-connect' option (or 'Trust Android Auto Connect') being enabled can prevent connection. Also, other devices like Fitbit keeping Bluetooth connection alive can interfere. The thread does not establish a single definitive root cause but points to these settings and potential OS issues. Turn off 'Trust Auto-connect' option in xDrip+ settings (under Less common settings -> Bluetooth settings). Also, some users found success by disabling the OB1 Collector (Settings -> G5/G6 Debug Settings -> Use The OB1 Collector) and by disabling 'close GATT on ble disconnect' (though this was suggested as better enabled). Additionally, turning off Fitbit's keep Bluetooth connection alive option helped one user. Blucon Oneplus 6 Libre sensor Miaomiao Fitbit Android 9.0 Android 9 Android Pie bluetooth OB1 Collector Trust Auto-connect close GATT on ble disconnect You have to turn off \"Trust Auto-connect\" option in the settings. This worked for me."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-616", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 616, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 616, "title": "Eversense Integration", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/616", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/616", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The current Eversense integration in xDrip uses the Esel companion app, which requires root (su access) and a running Roche/Senseonics Eversense app, so a smartwatch standalone solution is not possible. The user asks whether xDrip could integrate Bluetooth communication with the Eversense Transmitter as a standalone alternative.", "cause": null, "fix": "BernhardRo's workaround: disassemble the Eversense App and add a ContentProvider for glucose measurements, then modify ESEL to use that ContentProvider as BG input and pass it to xDrip; this requires no root but still requires the (modified) Eversense APK. Files are at https://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk; later he also points to https://cr4ck3d3v3r53n53.club/ for patched APKs.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Eversense", "Eversense Transmitter", "EversenseXL"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["esel", "companion app", "eversense app", "contentprovider", "modified apk", "bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "I have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements. Then I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required.", "text": "Eversense Integration The current Eversense integration in xDrip uses the Esel companion app, which requires root (su access) and a running Roche/Senseonics Eversense app, so a smartwatch standalone solution is not possible. The user asks whether xDrip could integrate Bluetooth communication with the Eversense Transmitter as a standalone alternative.  BernhardRo's workaround: disassemble the Eversense App and add a ContentProvider for glucose measurements, then modify ESEL to use that ContentProvider as BG input and pass it to xDrip; this requires no root but still requires the (modified) Eversense APK. Files are at https://github.com/BernhardRo/Esel/tree/master/apk; later he also points to https://cr4ck3d3v3r53n53.club/ for patched APKs. Eversense Eversense Transmitter EversenseXL esel companion app eversense app contentprovider modified apk bluetooth I have found a solution now, which works for me: with dissassembling the Eversense App, I have added an ContentProvider, providing the glucose measurements. Then I have modified ESEL to use this ContentProvider as BG input and passes it to xDrip. This works fine, for me. Advantage: no root required."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-618", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 618, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 618, "title": "Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/618", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/618", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User wants to integrate Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite with xDrip+ but only finds 'AmazFit Sync Service' in Settings - Smart Watch Properties, with no further options to integrate the watch.", "cause": "The Amazfit Bip runs its own OS and is less powerful, unlike Pace, Stratos, and Verge which run Android. The Amazfit Service in the master repository is not up to date.", "fix": "For Pace/Stratos, install the watchface on the watch and activate the service on the phone, using the latest release of Klaus3d3's fork until a new pull request is made. For Bip, no direct integration; workaround involves using the app 'Tool & Amazfit' to receive notifications with BG and delta values, with settings described in a linked guide.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite", "Amazfit Pace", "Amazfit Stratos", "Amazfit Bip"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["AmazFit Sync Service", "watchface", "notification"], "evidence_quote": "The watchface needs to be installed to the watch and on phones side you must activate the service. The Amazfit Service in this master repository is not up to date. Therefor use the latest release of my fork until i made a new pull request.", "text": "Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite User wants to integrate Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite with xDrip+ but only finds 'AmazFit Sync Service' in Settings - Smart Watch Properties, with no further options to integrate the watch. The Amazfit Bip runs its own OS and is less powerful, unlike Pace, Stratos, and Verge which run Android. The Amazfit Service in the master repository is not up to date. For Pace/Stratos, install the watchface on the watch and activate the service on the phone, using the latest release of Klaus3d3's fork until a new pull request is made. For Bip, no direct integration; workaround involves using the app 'Tool & Amazfit' to receive notifications with BG and delta values, with settings described in a linked guide. Xiaomi Huami Amazfit Bip Lite Amazfit Pace Amazfit Stratos Amazfit Bip AmazFit Sync Service watchface notification The watchface needs to be installed to the watch and on phones side you must activate the service. The Amazfit Service in this master repository is not up to date. Therefor use the latest release of my fork until i made a new pull request."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-621", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 621, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 621, "title": "Error: bgreadinginsertfromjson passed a null or zero length json", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/621", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/621", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using xDrip as a Nightscout viewer with Loop, treatment data is received but entry data (sgv) is not. The event log repeatedly shows 'bgreadinginsertfromjson passed a null or zero length json' every 5 minutes.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is speculated that Azure server settings (HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets) may be involved, but it is not confirmed.", "fix": "Turning on HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets at the Azure server host level resolved the issue for one user, and another user confirmed it worked after doing the same and updating clients. The exact fix is enabling HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets on the Azure hosting.", "settings_changed": ["HTTP 2.0 → on", "WebSockets → on"], "devices": [], "android_versions": ["Android 8.1", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["nsclient", "nightscout"], "evidence_quote": "I'm on Azure for Nightscout, and I needed to turn on HTTP 2.0 and Websockets at the server host level - and now AndroidAPS / NSClient works consistently.", "text": "Error: bgreadinginsertfromjson passed a null or zero length json When using xDrip as a Nightscout viewer with Loop, treatment data is received but entry data (sgv) is not. The event log repeatedly shows 'bgreadinginsertfromjson passed a null or zero length json' every 5 minutes. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. It is speculated that Azure server settings (HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets) may be involved, but it is not confirmed. Turning on HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets at the Azure server host level resolved the issue for one user, and another user confirmed it worked after doing the same and updating clients. The exact fix is enabling HTTP 2.0 and WebSockets on the Azure hosting. Android 8.1 Android 9 nsclient nightscout I'm on Azure for Nightscout, and I needed to turn on HTTP 2.0 and Websockets at the server host level - and now AndroidAPS / NSClient works consistently."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-633", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 633, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 633, "title": "xdrip showing 212 and up while real bg was 54", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/633", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/633", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip showed BG values of 212 and above while a fingerstick measurement was 54, indicating a dangerous discrepancy. The issue occurred after an old sensor stopped functioning and was replaced without stopping/restarting the sensor in xDrip.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the sensor was replaced without stopping/restarting it in xDrip, leading to invalid calibration data with extreme intercept values (e.g., 123) that caused incorrect BG calculations.", "fix": "The thread suggests implementing checks to reject bad calibration data (e.g., intercept > 30 or 40) and to detect when a new sensor is started. The issue was resolved by PR #887.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["libre"], "evidence_quote": "I have created https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/638 as a proof of concept of what I things that should be done.", "text": "xdrip showing 212 and up while real bg was 54 xDrip showed BG values of 212 and above while a fingerstick measurement was 54, indicating a dangerous discrepancy. The issue occurred after an old sensor stopped functioning and was replaced without stopping/restarting the sensor in xDrip. The thread identifies that the sensor was replaced without stopping/restarting it in xDrip, leading to invalid calibration data with extreme intercept values (e.g., 123) that caused incorrect BG calculations. The thread suggests implementing checks to reject bad calibration data (e.g., intercept > 30 or 40) and to detect when a new sensor is started. The issue was resolved by PR #887. Libre libre I have created https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/pull/638 as a proof of concept of what I things that should be done."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-639", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 639, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 639, "title": "Inversed Pebble watchface", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/639", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/639", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "In the latest release, the Pebble watchface 'Classic trend' has an inversed upper part (white background instead of black). The user asks if it is possible to switch it back to black background.", "cause": "The issue is caused by a setting in the watch face that controls whether the top and bottom background colors are the same. When this setting is not enabled, the top part appears white (inversed).", "fix": "In the watch face settings, turn on the option 'Same background colour top and bottom'. If it is already on, turn it off, save, then turn it on again. This should make the whole screen black background.", "settings_changed": ["Same background colour top and bottom → on"], "devices": ["Pebble classic"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["pebble"], "evidence_quote": "Once I had change the setting for Same background colour top and bottom, and saved it, the whole screen was black background.", "text": "Inversed Pebble watchface In the latest release, the Pebble watchface 'Classic trend' has an inversed upper part (white background instead of black). The user asks if it is possible to switch it back to black background. The issue is caused by a setting in the watch face that controls whether the top and bottom background colors are the same. When this setting is not enabled, the top part appears white (inversed). In the watch face settings, turn on the option 'Same background colour top and bottom'. If it is already on, turn it off, save, then turn it on again. This should make the whole screen black background. Pebble classic pebble Once I had change the setting for Same background colour top and bottom, and saved it, the whole screen was black background."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-642", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 642, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 642, "title": "Maximum Sync Queue Size Exceeded", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/642", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/642", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User keeps getting a 'Maximum Sync Queue Size Exceeded' error message. Clearing xDrip data temporarily fixes it, but the error returns after a few weeks. When the queue size is exceeded, followers don't get any data.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It is suggested that disabling background data access for xDrip might be related, but users report background data is enabled. Later, it is suggested that the error may be due to xDrip sync being enabled on the master when followers are using Nightscout follower, but the user reports the master is Diabox and they are only a follower.", "fix": "The thread suggests that if followers are using Nightscout follower, disabling xDrip sync on the master (deselecting 'Be master for followers') can stop the error. However, the user reports the master is Diabox, so this may not apply. The issue was closed after asking if it still occurs with the latest nightly, but no explicit resolution is confirmed.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip+ sync follower", "nightscout follower"], "evidence_quote": "If your followers are using the Nightscout follower option, you can disable the xDrip sync on the master, which will stop getting the max sync queue size exceeded error. On the master, go to the following page: Settings -> xDrip+ Sync Settings, and deselect \"Be master for followers\".", "text": "Maximum Sync Queue Size Exceeded User keeps getting a 'Maximum Sync Queue Size Exceeded' error message. Clearing xDrip data temporarily fixes it, but the error returns after a few weeks. When the queue size is exceeded, followers don't get any data. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. It is suggested that disabling background data access for xDrip might be related, but users report background data is enabled. Later, it is suggested that the error may be due to xDrip sync being enabled on the master when followers are using Nightscout follower, but the user reports the master is Diabox and they are only a follower. The thread suggests that if followers are using Nightscout follower, disabling xDrip sync on the master (deselecting 'Be master for followers') can stop the error. However, the user reports the master is Diabox, so this may not apply. The issue was closed after asking if it still occurs with the latest nightly, but no explicit resolution is confirmed.  xdrip+ sync follower nightscout follower If your followers are using the Nightscout follower option, you can disable the xDrip sync on the master, which will stop getting the max sync queue size exceeded error. On the master, go to the following page: Settings -> xDrip+ Sync Settings, and deselect \"Be master for followers\"."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-651", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 651, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 651, "title": "10.28.2018 Nightly Wear OS Null Null Complication problem", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/651", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/651", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating to the 10.28.2018 nightly, the xDrip+ complication on Wear OS watch faces shows 'null null' instead of the correct data. The issue occurs on both Ticwatch Pro and Ticwatch E watches. The xDrip+ watch faces themselves sync and work correctly.", "cause": "The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. The user initially suspected the 10.28.2018 Wear OS app, but a maintainer stated nothing changed in the wear component between 23rd and 28th Oct. Later, the user found that adding a calibration fixes the issue, implying the cause may be related to missing calibration data, but this is not explicitly stated as a root cause.", "fix": "Add a single calibration on the phone app. This resolved the null null complication issue for the original reporter. For a later user with a similar issue, adding a calibration only worked temporarily, and they reported the issue recurring after a few minutes.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Ticwatch Pro", "Ticwatch E", "MiaoMiao", "Mi Max 3", "Fossil Gen 5"], "android_versions": ["Oreo 8.1"], "driver_tags": ["wear OS", "complication", "Nightscout", "oop1"], "evidence_quote": "The SIMPLE FIX is to ADD a single CALIBRATION (the same reasoning as starting a new sensor where you are forced to add 2 calibrations).", "text": "10.28.2018 Nightly Wear OS Null Null Complication problem After updating to the 10.28.2018 nightly, the xDrip+ complication on Wear OS watch faces shows 'null null' instead of the correct data. The issue occurs on both Ticwatch Pro and Ticwatch E watches. The xDrip+ watch faces themselves sync and work correctly. The thread does not definitively identify a root cause. The user initially suspected the 10.28.2018 Wear OS app, but a maintainer stated nothing changed in the wear component between 23rd and 28th Oct. Later, the user found that adding a calibration fixes the issue, implying the cause may be related to missing calibration data, but this is not explicitly stated as a root cause. Add a single calibration on the phone app. This resolved the null null complication issue for the original reporter. For a later user with a similar issue, adding a calibration only worked temporarily, and they reported the issue recurring after a few minutes. Ticwatch Pro Ticwatch E MiaoMiao Mi Max 3 Fossil Gen 5 Oreo 8.1 wear OS complication Nightscout oop1 The SIMPLE FIX is to ADD a single CALIBRATION (the same reasoning as starting a new sensor where you are forced to add 2 calibrations)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-659", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 659, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 659, "title": "Pebble delta disappears on refresh", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/659", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/659", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Using the 'Pebble Trend Clay Version', if 'display delta' is enabled under Pebble Integration in xDrip, the delta initially appears on the watchface but disappears whenever the watchface refreshes (e.g., once a minute has passed or time changes). Saving settings in the Pebble app temporarily brings it back until the next refresh.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. The watchface creator mentions there are issues on the xDrip side where messages to the Pebble are built, but no specific cause is confirmed.", "fix": "No resolution is provided in the thread. The issue was closed without a fix; the reporter switched to another watchface.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pebble"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["pebble"], "evidence_quote": "I do know there are some issues on the xDrip side where the messages to the pebble are built, so I need to get that sorted.", "text": "Pebble delta disappears on refresh Using the 'Pebble Trend Clay Version', if 'display delta' is enabled under Pebble Integration in xDrip, the delta initially appears on the watchface but disappears whenever the watchface refreshes (e.g., once a minute has passed or time changes). Saving settings in the Pebble app temporarily brings it back until the next refresh. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. The watchface creator mentions there are issues on the xDrip side where messages to the Pebble are built, but no specific cause is confirmed. No resolution is provided in the thread. The issue was closed without a fix; the reporter switched to another watchface. Pebble pebble I do know there are some issues on the xDrip side where the messages to the pebble are built, so I need to get that sorted."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-674", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 674, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 674, "title": "G6 sensor errors", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/674", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/674", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Getting G6 \"sensor errors\" and no BG results. Reboot, restart sensor not working. The issue persists and the fallback option keeps reverting to native mode.", "cause": "The G6 transmitter cuts the feed and sends sensor errors message, which seems to be a feature of the G6. The fallback option unchecks itself possibly due to being in native mode.", "fix": "Turn on the xdrip algo fallback option to see values. Some users found that toggling Bluetooth off/on, restarting collector and phone, and checking the fallback option helped after a few minutes, but it may revert.", "settings_changed": ["xdrip algo fallback option → on"], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode", "fallback to xdrip"], "evidence_quote": "Turn on the xdrip algo fallback option if u need to see values.", "text": "G6 sensor errors Getting G6 \"sensor errors\" and no BG results. Reboot, restart sensor not working. The issue persists and the fallback option keeps reverting to native mode. The G6 transmitter cuts the feed and sends sensor errors message, which seems to be a feature of the G6. The fallback option unchecks itself possibly due to being in native mode. Turn on the xdrip algo fallback option to see values. Some users found that toggling Bluetooth off/on, restarting collector and phone, and checking the fallback option helped after a few minutes, but it may revert. G6 native mode fallback to xdrip Turn on the xdrip algo fallback option if u need to see values."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-682", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 682, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 682, "title": "Red On Black", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/682", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/682", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "During low blood sugar warnings, red text on black background is extremely difficult to read. User has tried changing color settings but the red text seems preset.", "cause": "The thread identifies that dark red on black has no significant contrast, making it hard to read regardless of vision.", "fix": "As a workaround, change the background color from black to gray via Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> xDrip+ Color Settings, specifically the 'Main Chart Background' color. Also, enable the Extra Alerts (xDrip+) alarm to get an alarm when predicted glucose drops below the Low value, and assign a specific sound clip to the alarm to avoid needing to read the text.", "settings_changed": ["Main Chart Background → gray"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "But, it is possible to change the background color. If you change the background color from black to gray, you may get better contrast. You can change colors: Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> xDrip+ Color Settings The background color is \"Main Chart Background\".", "text": "Red On Black During low blood sugar warnings, red text on black background is extremely difficult to read. User has tried changing color settings but the red text seems preset. The thread identifies that dark red on black has no significant contrast, making it hard to read regardless of vision. As a workaround, change the background color from black to gray via Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> xDrip+ Color Settings, specifically the 'Main Chart Background' color. Also, enable the Extra Alerts (xDrip+) alarm to get an alarm when predicted glucose drops below the Low value, and assign a specific sound clip to the alarm to avoid needing to read the text.   But, it is possible to change the background color. If you change the background color from black to gray, you may get better contrast. You can change colors: Settings -> xDrip+ Display Settings -> xDrip+ Color Settings The background color is \"Main Chart Background\"."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-684", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 684, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 684, "title": "G6 uploaded as G5", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/684", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/684", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The uploaded device String using a Dexcom G6 is \"xDrip-Dexcom G5 Native\" but should be \"xDrip-Dexcom-G6 Native\".", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native"], "evidence_quote": "The uploaded device String using a Dexcom G6 is \"xDrip-Dexcom G5 Native\" but should be \"xDrip-Dexcom-G6 Native\".", "text": "G6 uploaded as G5 The uploaded device String using a Dexcom G6 is \"xDrip-Dexcom G5 Native\" but should be \"xDrip-Dexcom-G6 Native\".   Dexcom G6 native The uploaded device String using a Dexcom G6 is \"xDrip-Dexcom G5 Native\" but should be \"xDrip-Dexcom-G6 Native\"."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-693", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 693, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 693, "title": "Play Store availability?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/693", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/693", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "xDrip+ is not available on the Google Play Store, which prevents installation on phones with Android for Work/Android Enterprise policies that disallow installing from external sources.", "cause": "The thread discusses various reasons: Google Play Store restrictions (e.g., requirement to target latest SDK versions, restrictions on sending text messages), potential FDA restrictions, and costs/update difficulties. However, no single root cause is definitively established.", "fix": "No resolution is provided. The maintainer (jamorham) states that standard side-loading is efficient and does not see an advantage to providing a stripped-down version for app stores. He mentions investigating the 'unreleased apps' section but no concrete fix is given.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Google play store apps are subject to many restrictions, for example it is a requirement to target the latest sdk versions/libraries even though that will likely break the app which is why I don't do it.", "text": "Play Store availability? xDrip+ is not available on the Google Play Store, which prevents installation on phones with Android for Work/Android Enterprise policies that disallow installing from external sources. The thread discusses various reasons: Google Play Store restrictions (e.g., requirement to target latest SDK versions, restrictions on sending text messages), potential FDA restrictions, and costs/update difficulties. However, no single root cause is definitively established. No resolution is provided. The maintainer (jamorham) states that standard side-loading is efficient and does not see an advantage to providing a stripped-down version for app stores. He mentions investigating the 'unreleased apps' section but no concrete fix is given.   Google play store apps are subject to many restrictions, for example it is a requirement to target the latest sdk versions/libraries even though that will likely break the app which is why I don't do it."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-696", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 696, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 696, "title": "Ticwatch Pro as collector gets unpaired", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/696", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/696", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When using a Ticwatch Pro as a collector with xDrip, it connects to a Dexcom G6 transmitter the first time, pairs successfully, and receives data, but after about 5 minutes it gets unpaired and no data is received. The issue repeats, requiring re-pairing each time.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Ticwatch Pro", "Dexcom G6", "Fossil gen 4", "MiaoMiao", "G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["collector", "standalone"], "evidence_quote": "Using ticwatch pro with latest updates and latest nightly release of xdrip when configured to work as collector the first time it connects to dexcom G6 it asks for pairing , I accept , it gets data, all fine, but after 5 minutes when it tries to connect again it gets Unpaired and no data received.", "text": "Ticwatch Pro as collector gets unpaired When using a Ticwatch Pro as a collector with xDrip, it connects to a Dexcom G6 transmitter the first time, pairs successfully, and receives data, but after about 5 minutes it gets unpaired and no data is received. The issue repeats, requiring re-pairing each time.   Ticwatch Pro Dexcom G6 Fossil gen 4 MiaoMiao G5 collector standalone Using ticwatch pro with latest updates and latest nightly release of xdrip when configured to work as collector the first time it connects to dexcom G6 it asks for pairing , I accept , it gets data, all fine, but after 5 minutes when it tries to connect again it gets Unpaired and no data received."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-703", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 703, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 703, "title": "what watch?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/703", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/703", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user asks what watches people use as a collector for xDrip, mentioning that their LG Watch Sport and Sony Smartwatch 3 both work but the LG is chunky and the Sony's always-on screen is too dark.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["LG Watch Sport", "Sony Smartwatch 3", "Ticwatch Pro", "Ticwatch E", "Ticwatch C2", "Huawei Watch2 sport"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["miaomiao", "blucon", "nfc"], "evidence_quote": "I have a Ticwatch Pro and Ticwatch E in combination with miaomiao Bluetooth transmitter. Flawless combo.", "text": "what watch? The user asks what watches people use as a collector for xDrip, mentioning that their LG Watch Sport and Sony Smartwatch 3 both work but the LG is chunky and the Sony's always-on screen is too dark.   LG Watch Sport Sony Smartwatch 3 Ticwatch Pro Ticwatch E Ticwatch C2 Huawei Watch2 sport miaomiao blucon nfc I have a Ticwatch Pro and Ticwatch E in combination with miaomiao Bluetooth transmitter. Flawless combo."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-705", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 705, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 705, "title": "huawei EMUI Bluetooth issues and missed readings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/705", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/705", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Users with Huawei phones running EMUI experience missed readings due to BLE scanning issues when the screen is off. The log shows 'App is scanning too frequently on screen off'. Readings resume when the screen is woken.", "cause": "Huawei EMUI software performs its own BLE management, causing issues with scanning and connecting when the screen is off, leading to missed readings.", "fix": "For Huawei EMUI, set the app to manage manually in battery settings, enable auto-launch, secondary launch, and run in background, disable battery optimization for xDrip, lock the app in the app switcher, and on some devices set battery mode to Performance instead of Power Saving. On older EMUI versions without these options, the issue may persist and require a different phone.", "settings_changed": ["Minimize Scanning → enabled", "App launch → Manage manually", "Auto-launch → activated", "Secondary launch → activated", "Run in background → activated", "Battery optimization → don't allow", "Battery mode → Performance"], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.0.0", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["OB1", "G5", "G6"], "evidence_quote": "In Settings>Battery it needs to be put in Performance mode. I had it in Power Saveing mode.", "text": "huawei EMUI Bluetooth issues and missed readings Users with Huawei phones running EMUI experience missed readings due to BLE scanning issues when the screen is off. The log shows 'App is scanning too frequently on screen off'. Readings resume when the screen is woken. Huawei EMUI software performs its own BLE management, causing issues with scanning and connecting when the screen is off, leading to missed readings. For Huawei EMUI, set the app to manage manually in battery settings, enable auto-launch, secondary launch, and run in background, disable battery optimization for xDrip, lock the app in the app switcher, and on some devices set battery mode to Performance instead of Power Saving. On older EMUI versions without these options, the issue may persist and require a different phone. Dexcom G6 Dexcom G5 Android 7.0.0 Android 9 OB1 G5 G6 In Settings>Battery it needs to be put in Performance mode. I had it in Power Saveing mode."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-718", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 718, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 718, "title": "Suggestions: Insulin Treatment Protocols + Reminders", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/718", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/718", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests the ability to input more than one type of insulin for better blood sugar predictions, and also requests reminders for sensor life (e.g., Libre) on the last day, similar to the reader's reminder feature.", "cause": null, "fix": "The issue was closed as a duplicate, and a comment states that the capability to add multiple insulin types has already been added to xDrip.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I think the capability to add multiple insulin types already has been added to xDrip. I am hence closing this issue.", "text": "Suggestions: Insulin Treatment Protocols + Reminders The user requests the ability to input more than one type of insulin for better blood sugar predictions, and also requests reminders for sensor life (e.g., Libre) on the last day, similar to the reader's reminder feature.  The issue was closed as a duplicate, and a comment states that the capability to add multiple insulin types has already been added to xDrip. Libre  I think the capability to add multiple insulin types already has been added to xDrip. I am hence closing this issue."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-72", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 72, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 72, "title": "not working equipment anymore", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/72", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/72", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Since 2 days, no Bluetooth connection; green LED on Bluetooth board blinks every 5 minutes, yellow light on wixel is on, no glucose values. Bluetooth scan in xDrip+ does not show the module, and system status shows 'not connected'.", "cause": "The thread suggests possible causes: the wixel may have corrupted firmware or died, the BT module may be faulty, or the xBridge may be paired via Android instead of only via xDrip. Also, the wixel may go to sleep after capturing a packet if it cannot connect to the phone.", "fix": "The thread suggests: ensure xBridge is not paired via Android, unpair if so; reload the .wxl firmware on the wixel; try flashing new firmware on the BT module; or replace the modules. Also, use the 'Forget Device' button in System Status to remove the xBridge, then rescan and select it.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["wixel", "Bluetooth board", "HM-10", "xBridge"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["Bluetooth wixel", "xbridge wixel", "xBridge"], "evidence_quote": "If the yellow light never flashes at all on the wixel then there is a problem there. Check wiring but also try reloading the .wxl firmware file. Sometimes they get corrupted, sometimes wixels completely die.", "text": "not working equipment anymore Since 2 days, no Bluetooth connection; green LED on Bluetooth board blinks every 5 minutes, yellow light on wixel is on, no glucose values. Bluetooth scan in xDrip+ does not show the module, and system status shows 'not connected'. The thread suggests possible causes: the wixel may have corrupted firmware or died, the BT module may be faulty, or the xBridge may be paired via Android instead of only via xDrip. Also, the wixel may go to sleep after capturing a packet if it cannot connect to the phone. The thread suggests: ensure xBridge is not paired via Android, unpair if so; reload the .wxl firmware on the wixel; try flashing new firmware on the BT module; or replace the modules. Also, use the 'Forget Device' button in System Status to remove the xBridge, then rescan and select it. wixel Bluetooth board HM-10 xBridge Bluetooth wixel xbridge wixel xBridge If the yellow light never flashes at all on the wixel then there is a problem there. Check wiring but also try reloading the .wxl firmware file. Sometimes they get corrupted, sometimes wixels completely die."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-720", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 720, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 720, "title": "Suggest: Delete selected one calibration from calibration graph", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/720", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/720", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests a delete option for a selected calibration in the calibration graph, as the existing feature in the calibration data table is not friendly to find and not the desired place for deletion.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Add a Delete option for selected one calibration in calibration graph.", "text": "Suggest: Delete selected one calibration from calibration graph The user requests a delete option for a selected calibration in the calibration graph, as the existing feature in the calibration data table is not friendly to find and not the desired place for deletion.     Add a Delete option for selected one calibration in calibration graph."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-734", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 734, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 734, "title": "Unihertz Atom Bluetooth Connection Lost Dexcom G6", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/734", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/734", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After the phone is out of range from the Dexcom G6 sensor for about 15-20 minutes, xDrip gets stuck in the 'Scanning' state and cannot reconnect; the only way to reconnect is to reboot the phone. Restarting the collector does not resolve it.", "cause": "The Unihertz manufacturer's power saving additions to Android shut down xDrip (PowerSaveService forceStopThirdApp for com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip) even when background activity and battery optimization exemptions are enabled.", "fix": "Use Unihertz battery optimization clean-up: set Battery Saver to off, set xDrip to 'not optimized' under Settings > Apps & Notifications > Advanced > Special app access > Battery Optimization, and under Settings > Smart Assistant > App Blocker untoggle Start Blocker, Background Blocker and Background Cleanup for xDrip.", "settings_changed": ["Battery Saver → off", "Battery Optimization (xDrip) → not optimized", "Start Blocker → untoggled", "Background Blocker → untoggled", "Background Cleanup → untoggled"], "devices": ["Unihertz Atom", "Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["ob1g5service", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip.", "text": "Unihertz Atom Bluetooth Connection Lost Dexcom G6 After the phone is out of range from the Dexcom G6 sensor for about 15-20 minutes, xDrip gets stuck in the 'Scanning' state and cannot reconnect; the only way to reconnect is to reboot the phone. Restarting the collector does not resolve it. The Unihertz manufacturer's power saving additions to Android shut down xDrip (PowerSaveService forceStopThirdApp for com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip) even when background activity and battery optimization exemptions are enabled. Use Unihertz battery optimization clean-up: set Battery Saver to off, set xDrip to 'not optimized' under Settings > Apps & Notifications > Advanced > Special app access > Battery Optimization, and under Settings > Smart Assistant > App Blocker untoggle Start Blocker, Background Blocker and Background Cleanup for xDrip. Unihertz Atom Dexcom G6 ob1g5service collector my initial findings are that the problems are due to the manufacturers power saving additions to android which shut down xDrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-737", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 737, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 737, "title": "xDrip+ draining G5 transmitter batter", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/737", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/737", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "User reports rapid degradation of Dexcom G5 transmitter battery voltage and resistance after switching from a Galaxy S5 to a BLU Dash X2 phone. Transmitters are failing within weeks, with low battery warnings after about 24 days. User is not in native mode and has OB1 enabled.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Possible causes discussed include the phone causing connection drops, expired sensors drawing more battery, or an issue with xDrip's OB1 communication mode. One user suggests that not using G5 Native mode may lead to early transmitter death, and another speculates that preemptive restarts may be involved.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include trying native mode with a new transmitter, turning off preemptive restarts and restarting the sensor before day 9, or switching to a G4 transmitter with a bridge. The thread ends with a request to close the issue, implying no resolution.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G5", "G4", "BLU Dash X2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1", "native mode", "non-native mode"], "evidence_quote": "I suggest this path TO MITIGATE PROBLEM (if you have battery drainage) until fix: - turn Preemptive restarts OFF - day 9 (or earlier if more convenient): stop sensor, hard reset transmitter*, start sensor again", "text": "xDrip+ draining G5 transmitter batter User reports rapid degradation of Dexcom G5 transmitter battery voltage and resistance after switching from a Galaxy S5 to a BLU Dash X2 phone. Transmitters are failing within weeks, with low battery warnings after about 24 days. User is not in native mode and has OB1 enabled. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. Possible causes discussed include the phone causing connection drops, expired sensors drawing more battery, or an issue with xDrip's OB1 communication mode. One user suggests that not using G5 Native mode may lead to early transmitter death, and another speculates that preemptive restarts may be involved. No definitive fix is provided. Suggestions include trying native mode with a new transmitter, turning off preemptive restarts and restarting the sensor before day 9, or switching to a G4 transmitter with a bridge. The thread ends with a request to close the issue, implying no resolution. G5 G4 BLU Dash X2 OB1 native mode non-native mode I suggest this path TO MITIGATE PROBLEM (if you have battery drainage) until fix: - turn Preemptive restarts OFF - day 9 (or earlier if more convenient): stop sensor, hard reset transmitter*, start sensor again"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-740", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 740, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 740, "title": "When phone in Airport mode with bluetooth enabled miaomiao connectivity is very unstable", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/740", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/740", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When the phone is in airplane mode with Bluetooth enabled, xDrip+ consistently fails to read the miaomiao. It will only work if you refresh via Bluetooth scan and leave the app in the foreground. Disabling airplane mode resolves the connectivity problem.", "cause": "xDrip+ has built-in logic that checks if airplane mode is enabled and may not operate properly when airplane mode is on, even if Bluetooth is manually enabled.", "fix": "Use an ADB command to change the airplane_mode_radios setting so that airplane mode does not affect Bluetooth. The suggested command is: settings put global airplane_mode_radios cell,wimax. Additionally, ensure that after a reboot, you are not in airplane mode initially; enter airplane mode after being on cell, with Bluetooth still enabled.", "settings_changed": ["airplane_mode_radios → cell,wimax"], "devices": ["miaomiao"], "android_versions": ["Android 8"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "on my device I did an ADB session and used a couple of commands to make it so airplane mode doesn't affect bluetooth or wifi. This makes it so xdrip+ runs just fine while in airplane mode.", "text": "When phone in Airport mode with bluetooth enabled miaomiao connectivity is very unstable When the phone is in airplane mode with Bluetooth enabled, xDrip+ consistently fails to read the miaomiao. It will only work if you refresh via Bluetooth scan and leave the app in the foreground. Disabling airplane mode resolves the connectivity problem. xDrip+ has built-in logic that checks if airplane mode is enabled and may not operate properly when airplane mode is on, even if Bluetooth is manually enabled. Use an ADB command to change the airplane_mode_radios setting so that airplane mode does not affect Bluetooth. The suggested command is: settings put global airplane_mode_radios cell,wimax. Additionally, ensure that after a reboot, you are not in airplane mode initially; enter airplane mode after being on cell, with Bluetooth still enabled. miaomiao Android 8  on my device I did an ADB session and used a couple of commands to make it so airplane mode doesn't affect bluetooth or wifi. This makes it so xdrip+ runs just fine while in airplane mode."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-746", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 746, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 746, "title": "Starting G6 sensor and Xdrip not asking for code", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/746", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/746", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "When starting a Dexcom G6 sensor, xDrip does not ask for the sensor code and directly gives blood glucose values. The user is unsure whether to have 'Go on without calibrations' checked or unchecked, and whether to calibrate.", "cause": "The issue is caused by not using the OB1 collector with the G6 option enabled, or by not properly stopping and starting the sensor. Specifically, if the OB1 collector is turned off, xDrip will not prompt for the sensor code.", "fix": "Ensure the OB1 collector is enabled and the G6 option is enabled. Use the 'Stop Sensor' and 'Start Sensor' menu items to start a new sensor, and it will ask for the code. If the OB1 collector was turned on after starting the sensor, stop and start the sensor to force it to update the code.", "settings_changed": ["Restart Sensor → unchecked", "Preemptive restarts → checked", "Go on without calibrations → checked", "Use the OB1 Collector → Yes", "Native Algorithm → Yes", "Fallback to xDrip → No", "Minimize Scanning → No", "G6 Support → Yes", "Allow OB1 unbonding → Yes", "Allow OB1 initiate bonding → Yes"], "devices": ["G6 sensor", "Sony Smartwatch 3"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1 collector", "native algorithm", "G6"], "evidence_quote": "@jlecount If you are using the OB1 collector and have G6 option enabled then it should ask you for a code when starting a sensor.", "text": "Starting G6 sensor and Xdrip not asking for code When starting a Dexcom G6 sensor, xDrip does not ask for the sensor code and directly gives blood glucose values. The user is unsure whether to have 'Go on without calibrations' checked or unchecked, and whether to calibrate. The issue is caused by not using the OB1 collector with the G6 option enabled, or by not properly stopping and starting the sensor. Specifically, if the OB1 collector is turned off, xDrip will not prompt for the sensor code. Ensure the OB1 collector is enabled and the G6 option is enabled. Use the 'Stop Sensor' and 'Start Sensor' menu items to start a new sensor, and it will ask for the code. If the OB1 collector was turned on after starting the sensor, stop and start the sensor to force it to update the code. G6 sensor Sony Smartwatch 3 OB1 collector native algorithm G6 @jlecount If you are using the OB1 collector and have G6 option enabled then it should ask you for a code when starting a sensor."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-749", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 749, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 749, "title": "REQUEST: Wear OS app for use xDrip on my 5y.o. child smartwatch for using without smartphone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/749", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/749", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests a standalone Wear OS app to collect data via Bluetooth and send to followers, because their 5-year-old daughter cannot carry a smartphone.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Huawei Watch 2 LTE", "Finow Q1 Pro", "Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["wear app", "collector", "patches"], "evidence_quote": "No. I have given up. I use a telephone.", "text": "REQUEST: Wear OS app for use xDrip on my 5y.o. child smartwatch for using without smartphone The user requests a standalone Wear OS app to collect data via Bluetooth and send to followers, because their 5-year-old daughter cannot carry a smartphone.   Huawei Watch 2 LTE Finow Q1 Pro Dexcom G5 wear app collector patches No. I have given up. I use a telephone."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-751", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 751, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 751, "title": "Feature Request: Smart Band integration for Xiaomi Mi Band 3", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/751", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/751", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The user requests integration of notifications into the Xiaomi Mi Band 3 smart band, specifically a continuous notification every 5 or 10 minutes displaying the latest glucose level and trend arrow, not just high/low alerts.", "cause": null, "fix": "A user (bigdigital) developed a custom xDrip integration for Mi Band, providing instructions and a new version that works with Mi Band 2, 3, and 4. The integration sends glucose level and trend arrow notifications to the band. For Mi Band 2 and 3, it works with MiFit using the 'bg reading as notifications' option. The fix is to use this custom integration.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Xiaomi Mi Band 3", "Mi Band 2", "Mi Band 4"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["MiFit", "MiBandTools", "Gadgetbridge"], "evidence_quote": "Today i've released a new version https://bigdigital.home.blog/2020/01/23/future-of-the-xdrip-miband-project/ which should work better for mibandv4 . The v2 and v3 would work as before . If this version would be stable, i’ll create a pull request for the Xdrip master record.", "text": "Feature Request: Smart Band integration for Xiaomi Mi Band 3 The user requests integration of notifications into the Xiaomi Mi Band 3 smart band, specifically a continuous notification every 5 or 10 minutes displaying the latest glucose level and trend arrow, not just high/low alerts.  A user (bigdigital) developed a custom xDrip integration for Mi Band, providing instructions and a new version that works with Mi Band 2, 3, and 4. The integration sends glucose level and trend arrow notifications to the band. For Mi Band 2 and 3, it works with MiFit using the 'bg reading as notifications' option. The fix is to use this custom integration. Xiaomi Mi Band 3 Mi Band 2 Mi Band 4 MiFit MiBandTools Gadgetbridge Today i've released a new version https://bigdigital.home.blog/2020/01/23/future-of-the-xdrip-miband-project/ which should work better for mibandv4 . The v2 and v3 would work as before . If this version would be stable, i’ll create a pull request for the Xdrip master record."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-754", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 754, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 754, "title": "Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch does not upload data to Nightscout", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/754", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/754", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch with Android 7.1 refuses to upload any data to Azure (Nightscout) despite receiving Bluetooth data from the transmitter (Blukon). Battery options and app permissions were checked. Setting the watch as a follower also shows nothing.", "cause": null, "fix": "The problem was solved by switching to Heroku for Nightscout hosting.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch", "Blukon"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.1"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "At heroku it does upload so problem Solved!!!!!", "text": "Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch does not upload data to Nightscout The Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch with Android 7.1 refuses to upload any data to Azure (Nightscout) despite receiving Bluetooth data from the transmitter (Blukon). Battery options and app permissions were checked. Setting the watch as a follower also shows nothing.  The problem was solved by switching to Heroku for Nightscout hosting. Kospet Hope 4g smartwatch Blukon Android 7.1  At heroku it does upload so problem Solved!!!!!"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-76", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 76, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 76, "title": "Default Minimum Slope needs correcting", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/76", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/76", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "The default minimum slope for the calibration algorithm is problematic, causing some sensors to be unable to calibrate properly and potentially being discarded as useless. Users may need to enable engineering mode and use a special DexParametersAdrian class to get their calibration slopes to fit the data.", "cause": "The default slope parameters in the calibration algorithm are too narrow, preventing some sensors from calibrating correctly.", "fix": "The default slope parameters were widened by making the 'Adrian slope parameters' the default, as added in commit be27a9ea07163f2d2718a72ee31da4f501f40fa2. The old parameters remain available through engineering mode.", "settings_changed": ["LOW_SLOPE_1 → 0.75", "LOW_SLOPE_2 → 0.70", "HIGH_SLOPE_1 → 1.5", "HIGH_SLOPE_2 → 1.6", "DEFAULT_LOW_SLOPE_LOW → 0.75", "DEFAULT_LOW_SLOPE_HIGH → 0.70", "DEFAULT_SLOPE → 1", "DEFAULT_HIGH_SLOPE_HIGH → 1.5", "DEFAULT_HIGH_SLOPE_LOW → 1.4"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["calibration", "engineering mode", "DexParametersAdrian", "Datricsae"], "evidence_quote": "Widening of the slope parameters by making the \"Adrian slope parameters\" the default was added in this commit: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/be27a9ea07163f2d2718a72ee31da4f501f40fa2", "text": "Default Minimum Slope needs correcting The default minimum slope for the calibration algorithm is problematic, causing some sensors to be unable to calibrate properly and potentially being discarded as useless. Users may need to enable engineering mode and use a special DexParametersAdrian class to get their calibration slopes to fit the data. The default slope parameters in the calibration algorithm are too narrow, preventing some sensors from calibrating correctly. The default slope parameters were widened by making the 'Adrian slope parameters' the default, as added in commit be27a9ea07163f2d2718a72ee31da4f501f40fa2. The old parameters remain available through engineering mode.  calibration engineering mode DexParametersAdrian Datricsae Widening of the slope parameters by making the \"Adrian slope parameters\" the default was added in this commit: https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/commit/be27a9ea07163f2d2718a72ee31da4f501f40fa2"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-772", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 772, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 772, "title": "Nightscout follower ", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/772", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/772", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "User tried to use the source nightscout follow, entered their website in every way they can think of, but it won't pull the data. Another user reports that after switching to nightscout follow, it downloads one data point then stops, and they have to restart the collector to get another.", "cause": null, "fix": "Install the latest nightly build, which is more tolerant with the formats for the nightscout follower URL. The Nightscout following data source is included in the Source Wizard (20th Feb nightly), select 'Other' then you will see the option. Later updates resolved remaining issues.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G5", "Pixel 3", "Pixel 3XL"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout follower", "source wizard"], "evidence_quote": "Please install the latest nightly, it is a lot more tolerant with the formats for the nightscout follower URL.", "text": "Nightscout follower  User tried to use the source nightscout follow, entered their website in every way they can think of, but it won't pull the data. Another user reports that after switching to nightscout follow, it downloads one data point then stops, and they have to restart the collector to get another.  Install the latest nightly build, which is more tolerant with the formats for the nightscout follower URL. The Nightscout following data source is included in the Source Wizard (20th Feb nightly), select 'Other' then you will see the option. Later updates resolved remaining issues. Dexcom G5 Pixel 3 Pixel 3XL nightscout follower source wizard Please install the latest nightly, it is a lot more tolerant with the formats for the nightscout follower URL."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-780", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 780, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 780, "title": "Android 9.0 Pie (ZTE Axon 9 Pro) blocking wakeups from Doze", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/780", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/780", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After updating to Android 9.0 Pie, XDrip fails to receive data whenever the phone is on battery and screen is off (dozed). With screen on or on connected power, it works perfectly.", "cause": null, "fix": "An update of Android Pie on the ZTE Axon 9 Pro (to build number ZTE_A2019G_ProV2.1.0B03) fixed the dozing issue, with all battery optimizations disabled.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["ZTE Axon 9 Pro"], "android_versions": ["Android 9.0 Pie"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "first update of Android Pie on my ZTE Axon 9 Pro (to build number ZTE_A2019G_ProV2.1.0B03) fixed dozing issue... XDrip is now working!!! (with all battery optimizations disabled, of course).", "text": "Android 9.0 Pie (ZTE Axon 9 Pro) blocking wakeups from Doze After updating to Android 9.0 Pie, XDrip fails to receive data whenever the phone is on battery and screen is off (dozed). With screen on or on connected power, it works perfectly.  An update of Android Pie on the ZTE Axon 9 Pro (to build number ZTE_A2019G_ProV2.1.0B03) fixed the dozing issue, with all battery optimizations disabled. ZTE Axon 9 Pro Android 9.0 Pie  first update of Android Pie on my ZTE Axon 9 Pro (to build number ZTE_A2019G_ProV2.1.0B03) fixed dozing issue... XDrip is now working!!! (with all battery optimizations disabled, of course)."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-785", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 785, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 785, "title": "samsung s8 and sony smartwatch 3 sensor stopped, calibration rejected and no active session but its running fine", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/785", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/785", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "After starting a new transmitter, the sensor stopped, calibration rejected, and no active session is reported, but it is running fine. The issue persists over time.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["samsung s8", "sony smartwatch 3"], "android_versions": ["Android 8"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "this happened when I started a new transmitter. Everything has been running fine eventhough it reports these things.", "text": "samsung s8 and sony smartwatch 3 sensor stopped, calibration rejected and no active session but its running fine After starting a new transmitter, the sensor stopped, calibration rejected, and no active session is reported, but it is running fine. The issue persists over time.   samsung s8 sony smartwatch 3 Android 8  this happened when I started a new transmitter. Everything has been running fine eventhough it reports these things."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-79", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 79, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 79, "title": "Change \"4 minutes ago\" status line to read in seconds", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/79", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/79", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "The status line shows '4 minutes ago' for the time since last reading, which is not precise enough for users who want to know exactly when the next reading will arrive. Users find themselves repeatedly checking the phone when it shows '4 minutes ago' because they don't know the exact seconds remaining.", "cause": "The thread discusses that the exact time of the next reading is not known for all data sources (e.g., MongoDB or Parakeet), and for some BT devices the timing can vary due to disconnects/reconnects or clock sync issues. The maintainer notes that for G6 with xDrip as collector, the system status page shows scanning only in the last 5-10 seconds before the reading.", "fix": "The issue was closed without a code change. The maintainer suggests that users can look at a clock with a seconds hand when they see '4 minutes ago' to estimate the next reading, and for G6 collectors, the system status page shows scanning activity in the last seconds before a reading. No specific setting change was implemented.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["collector", "follower", "Nightscout", "Mongo", "BT", "G6"], "evidence_quote": "Regardless of all of that, all you need is to look at a clock with a seconds hand as soon as you see last connected 4 minutes. Then, looking at that clock, you can tell exactly when to expect the next reading.", "text": "Change \"4 minutes ago\" status line to read in seconds The status line shows '4 minutes ago' for the time since last reading, which is not precise enough for users who want to know exactly when the next reading will arrive. Users find themselves repeatedly checking the phone when it shows '4 minutes ago' because they don't know the exact seconds remaining. The thread discusses that the exact time of the next reading is not known for all data sources (e.g., MongoDB or Parakeet), and for some BT devices the timing can vary due to disconnects/reconnects or clock sync issues. The maintainer notes that for G6 with xDrip as collector, the system status page shows scanning only in the last 5-10 seconds before the reading. The issue was closed without a code change. The maintainer suggests that users can look at a clock with a seconds hand when they see '4 minutes ago' to estimate the next reading, and for G6 collectors, the system status page shows scanning activity in the last seconds before a reading. No specific setting change was implemented. G6 collector follower Nightscout Mongo BT G6 Regardless of all of that, all you need is to look at a clock with a seconds hand as soon as you see last connected 4 minutes. Then, looking at that clock, you can tell exactly when to expect the next reading."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-792", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 792, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 792, "title": "Encountered backfill data we don't recognise: 21 1 127", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/792", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/792", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When starting a new sensor, Sensor Status shows 'Sensor Failed 6' and logs continually show 'Encountered backfill data we don't recognise: 21 1 127'. xDrip keeps asking for calibrations which aren't accepted and prompt the same log error.", "cause": "In one case, the cause was mechanical: the sensing element was not introduced under the skin; it was still stuck in the inserter. In another case, a fresh new sensor resolved the issue, suggesting the sensor itself was faulty.", "fix": "Replace the sensor with a fresh new one. In one case, the issue resolved on its own after ignoring it overnight.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6"], "android_versions": ["Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["native G6 collector"], "evidence_quote": "In my case (September 12th) the cause of the error was mechanical - when peeling the sensor off after 24 hours, I found that no sensing element was present. It had not been introduced under the skin! Instead, it was still stuck in the white inserter contraption.", "text": "Encountered backfill data we don't recognise: 21 1 127 When starting a new sensor, Sensor Status shows 'Sensor Failed 6' and logs continually show 'Encountered backfill data we don't recognise: 21 1 127'. xDrip keeps asking for calibrations which aren't accepted and prompt the same log error. In one case, the cause was mechanical: the sensing element was not introduced under the skin; it was still stuck in the inserter. In another case, a fresh new sensor resolved the issue, suggesting the sensor itself was faulty. Replace the sensor with a fresh new one. In one case, the issue resolved on its own after ignoring it overnight. Dexcom G6 Android 9 native G6 collector In my case (September 12th) the cause of the error was mechanical - when peeling the sensor off after 24 hours, I found that no sensing element was present. It had not been introduced under the skin! Instead, it was still stuck in the white inserter contraption."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-800", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 800, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 800, "title": "Different arrows on watch and phone", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/800", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/800", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Watch and phone showing different arrows but same numbers. The wear arrow is the same as the one at the original dexcom receiver.", "cause": "The thread suggests that xDrip is sending the arrow derived by the G6 (Dexcom) to remote systems like the watch, rather than its own calculated arrow, leading to inconsistency. This is based on user deduction, not confirmed by developers.", "fix": "No definitive fix is provided. A workaround suggested is to change the Arrow trend to the new version by long pressing on the xDrip logo (blood drop) to open settings and activate the last option, but this only affects the app display, not the watch.", "settings_changed": ["Arrow trend → new version"], "devices": ["G6", "G5", "Pebble", "Ticwatch C2", "TicWatch E", "Fossil G5", "Zenwatch2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["native mode"], "evidence_quote": "I think the problem is that although the xDrip is working out what the arrow should be, it is in fact sending the arrow that the G6 has derived instead.", "text": "Different arrows on watch and phone Watch and phone showing different arrows but same numbers. The wear arrow is the same as the one at the original dexcom receiver. The thread suggests that xDrip is sending the arrow derived by the G6 (Dexcom) to remote systems like the watch, rather than its own calculated arrow, leading to inconsistency. This is based on user deduction, not confirmed by developers. No definitive fix is provided. A workaround suggested is to change the Arrow trend to the new version by long pressing on the xDrip logo (blood drop) to open settings and activate the last option, but this only affects the app display, not the watch. G6 G5 Pebble Ticwatch C2 TicWatch E Fossil G5 Zenwatch2 native mode I think the problem is that although the xDrip is working out what the arrow should be, it is in fact sending the arrow that the G6 has derived instead."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-806", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 806, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 806, "title": "Constant loss of signal - G5 with Nokia", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/806", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/806", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A friend using xDrip+ on a Nokia 2 with Android 7.1.1 and a G5 sensor experiences constant loss of signal, with breaks in reception but sometimes working for 20-30 minutes. The user also noticed that no values are lost when the phone is being used, but during the night or when the phone is not in use, there are no values.", "cause": "The thread suggests the Nokia might be cutting the connection temporarily to save battery, as it does not happen at night when the phone is likely connected to a power source.", "fix": "Updating to the latest nightly build and disabling the 'Minimize Scanning' option while using the 'OB1 collector' helped, but the issue is not entirely resolved; there are still some 10-20 minute interruptions. Additionally, adding xDrip to the phone's battery saving exclusions was suggested.", "settings_changed": ["Minimize Scanning → unchecked", "Use the OB1 collector → checked"], "devices": ["G5", "Nokia 2"], "android_versions": ["Android 7.1.1"], "driver_tags": ["OB1 collector", "Native Algorithm", "OB1 initiate bonding"], "evidence_quote": "Please update to the latest nightly and disable the `Minimize Scanning` option and use the `OB1 collector`", "text": "Constant loss of signal - G5 with Nokia A friend using xDrip+ on a Nokia 2 with Android 7.1.1 and a G5 sensor experiences constant loss of signal, with breaks in reception but sometimes working for 20-30 minutes. The user also noticed that no values are lost when the phone is being used, but during the night or when the phone is not in use, there are no values. The thread suggests the Nokia might be cutting the connection temporarily to save battery, as it does not happen at night when the phone is likely connected to a power source. Updating to the latest nightly build and disabling the 'Minimize Scanning' option while using the 'OB1 collector' helped, but the issue is not entirely resolved; there are still some 10-20 minute interruptions. Additionally, adding xDrip to the phone's battery saving exclusions was suggested. G5 Nokia 2 Android 7.1.1 OB1 collector Native Algorithm OB1 initiate bonding Please update to the latest nightly and disable the `Minimize Scanning` option and use the `OB1 collector`"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-808", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 808, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 808, "title": "Nightscout follower - 5 min. delay", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/808", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/808", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "While following Nightscout page, data is between 5 and 10 minutes old. xDrip+ appears to pull data with a delay or not frequently enough, and it never catches up to the current time, always being about 5 minutes behind.", "cause": "The issue is with the Dexcom servers, as stated by a commenter. Additionally, the Nightscout Follow logic in xDrip+ may not be polling frequently enough.", "fix": "Decrease the Dexcom Share polling interval by setting BRIDGE_INTERVAL to 15000 (15 seconds) in Nightwatch settings, which almost completely eliminated the lag. Alternatively, changing the grace value in NightscoutFollowService.java to something bigger than 10 seconds (e.g., Constants.SECOND_IN_MS * 30) might fix the problem, but this was not tested.", "settings_changed": ["BRIDGE_INTERVAL → 15000"], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["nightscout follower", "dexcom share", "bridge_interval"], "evidence_quote": "In the Nightwatch settings I've decreased the Dexcom Share polling interval to 15 seconds: `BRIDGE_INTERVAL = 15000` This almost completely eliminated the lag.", "text": "Nightscout follower - 5 min. delay While following Nightscout page, data is between 5 and 10 minutes old. xDrip+ appears to pull data with a delay or not frequently enough, and it never catches up to the current time, always being about 5 minutes behind. The issue is with the Dexcom servers, as stated by a commenter. Additionally, the Nightscout Follow logic in xDrip+ may not be polling frequently enough. Decrease the Dexcom Share polling interval by setting BRIDGE_INTERVAL to 15000 (15 seconds) in Nightwatch settings, which almost completely eliminated the lag. Alternatively, changing the grace value in NightscoutFollowService.java to something bigger than 10 seconds (e.g., Constants.SECOND_IN_MS * 30) might fix the problem, but this was not tested.  nightscout follower dexcom share bridge_interval In the Nightwatch settings I've decreased the Dexcom Share polling interval to 15 seconds: `BRIDGE_INTERVAL = 15000` This almost completely eliminated the lag."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-811", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 811, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 811, "title": "can't set alarms anymore", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/811", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/811", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Since returning to the master fork, the alarm list is empty with both nightlies from 23.02 and 04.03, and new alarms cannot be set. When trying to set an alert, a warning appears: 'Warning! No active Low Alert exists, without this there will be no alert on low glucose! Please add or enable a low alert.' and the list remains empty.", "cause": "The thread identifies that the AlertType table is missing the column 'force_speaker', causing an SQLiteException when inserting a new alert. This is likely because AlertType.fixUpTable() is missing from IdempotentMigrations, so the schema isn't properly set up before attempts to write data.", "fix": "The fix was to add AlertType.fixUpTable() to IdempotentMigrations, which was resolved in the March 7th nightly. The user confirmed it is working again after that update.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I think `AlertType.fixUpTable()` must be missing from `IdempotentMigrations` so the schema isn't properly set up before attempts are made to write the data. I can add this for the next nightly.", "text": "can't set alarms anymore Since returning to the master fork, the alarm list is empty with both nightlies from 23.02 and 04.03, and new alarms cannot be set. When trying to set an alert, a warning appears: 'Warning! No active Low Alert exists, without this there will be no alert on low glucose! Please add or enable a low alert.' and the list remains empty. The thread identifies that the AlertType table is missing the column 'force_speaker', causing an SQLiteException when inserting a new alert. This is likely because AlertType.fixUpTable() is missing from IdempotentMigrations, so the schema isn't properly set up before attempts to write data. The fix was to add AlertType.fixUpTable() to IdempotentMigrations, which was resolved in the March 7th nightly. The user confirmed it is working again after that update.   I think `AlertType.fixUpTable()` must be missing from `IdempotentMigrations` so the schema isn't properly set up before attempts are made to write the data. I can add this for the next nightly."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-812", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 812, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 812, "title": "Checksum error on US 14 day sensors", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/812", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/812", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "US 14 day sensors no longer work with xDrip. When scanning directly with NFC the error is: 'Read data but checksum is wrong.' When connected via the MiaoMiao: 'We have all the data we need 363 checksum_ok = false'.", "cause": "The thread suspects encryption different from international sensors, but no definitive cause is established.", "fix": "A solution for 14 days US sensors exists via a Medium article by miaomiaoreader, but the thread does not provide specific steps.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 14 day", "MiaoMiao"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NFC", "MiaoMiao"], "evidence_quote": "A solution for 14 days us sensors exists here: https://medium.com/@miaomiaoreader/how-to-make-libre-us-14-days-sensors-work-with-miaomiao2-on-xdrip-35b431a40940", "text": "Checksum error on US 14 day sensors US 14 day sensors no longer work with xDrip. When scanning directly with NFC the error is: 'Read data but checksum is wrong.' When connected via the MiaoMiao: 'We have all the data we need 363 checksum_ok = false'. The thread suspects encryption different from international sensors, but no definitive cause is established. A solution for 14 days US sensors exists via a Medium article by miaomiaoreader, but the thread does not provide specific steps. Libre 14 day MiaoMiao NFC MiaoMiao A solution for 14 days us sensors exists here: https://medium.com/@miaomiaoreader/how-to-make-libre-us-14-days-sensors-work-with-miaomiao2-on-xdrip-35b431a40940"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-813", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 813, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 813, "title": "Volume is way to high in build 0223-80e1023", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/813", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/813", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "Volume of the device (phone) is completely ignored by xDrip in the version from 23rd of Feb 2019. Changing the volume profile in xDrip between High and Medium doesn't make any difference; it's really really loud. The issue persists in later builds, and medium feels at least 50% higher than in older versions.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Volume of the device (phone) is completely ignored by xdrip in the version from 23rd of Feb 2019. Also changing the volume profile in xdrip it self between High and Medium doesn't make any difference. It's really really loud.", "text": "Volume is way to high in build 0223-80e1023 Volume of the device (phone) is completely ignored by xDrip in the version from 23rd of Feb 2019. Changing the volume profile in xDrip between High and Medium doesn't make any difference; it's really really loud. The issue persists in later builds, and medium feels at least 50% higher than in older versions.     Volume of the device (phone) is completely ignored by xdrip in the version from 23rd of Feb 2019. Also changing the volume profile in xdrip it self between High and Medium doesn't make any difference. It's really really loud."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-818", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 818, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 818, "title": "please some suggestions or solution for wrong readings", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/818", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/818", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Using xDrip with MiaoMiao on an international Libre 14-day sensor, reported glucose levels are over 100 points off compared to blood and the Libre scanner. The problem started about two sensors ago, no settings were changed, and calibrations do not keep the readings accurate.", "cause": "The calibration graph shows points far from the expected straight line; the developer says calibrations should only be done when BG is stable and not right after a meal, and suspects the sensor itself rather than a hardware/software problem.", "fix": "Calibrate only when BG is stable and not after meals, or install the external OOP algorithm and enable it in xDrip under settings -> less common settings -> other misc options -> out of process blukon algorithm to get readings close to the Libre reader without calibrations. To revert, disable the out of process libre algorithm.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["MiaoMiao", "international libre 14 days", "note 9"], "android_versions": ["android version 9"], "driver_tags": ["oop algorithm", "out of process blukon algorithm", "out of process libre algorithm", "native algorithm", "miaomiao"], "evidence_quote": "You need to install something that is called OOP algorithm from: https://drive.google.com/file/d/18zkgZq3ztNlgQZovKcE7ddO70PuawfBB/view?usp=drivesdk and then enable it on xdrip: On xdrip go to setting->less common settings->other misc options-> and set out of process blukon algorithm.", "text": "please some suggestions or solution for wrong readings Using xDrip with MiaoMiao on an international Libre 14-day sensor, reported glucose levels are over 100 points off compared to blood and the Libre scanner. The problem started about two sensors ago, no settings were changed, and calibrations do not keep the readings accurate. The calibration graph shows points far from the expected straight line; the developer says calibrations should only be done when BG is stable and not right after a meal, and suspects the sensor itself rather than a hardware/software problem. Calibrate only when BG is stable and not after meals, or install the external OOP algorithm and enable it in xDrip under settings -> less common settings -> other misc options -> out of process blukon algorithm to get readings close to the Libre reader without calibrations. To revert, disable the out of process libre algorithm. MiaoMiao international libre 14 days note 9 android version 9 oop algorithm out of process blukon algorithm out of process libre algorithm native algorithm miaomiao You need to install something that is called OOP algorithm from: https://drive.google.com/file/d/18zkgZq3ztNlgQZovKcE7ddO70PuawfBB/view?usp=drivesdk and then enable it on xdrip: On xdrip go to setting->less common settings->other misc options-> and set out of process blukon algorithm."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-822", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 822, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 822, "title": "Samsung Galaxy S10+ not receiving data", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/822", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/822", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "Samsung Galaxy S10+ not receiving data for 10 minutes at a time; if phone isn't turned on then nothing syncs, data backfills afterwards. Some users report no data with screen off, others report intermittent loss even with screen on.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a single root cause. Possible factors discussed include Samsung-specific power saving features, OB1 collector issues, and Smart Switch migration, but no definitive cause is confirmed.", "fix": "Several workarounds are suggested: turning off 'Minimize Scanning' in settings, disabling OB1 collector, disabling Samsung power saving features for xDrip, and for MM users disabling 'Trust AutoConnect' or enabling 'Use Scanning'. One user reports success after uninstalling and reinstalling xDrip.", "settings_changed": ["Minimize Scanning → off", "OB1 collector → off", "Trust AutoConnect → off", "Use Scanning → on"], "devices": ["G6", "MiaoMiao"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1", "G5", "G6", "MM", "collector"], "evidence_quote": "Got it working by turning the OB1 collector off despite using the G6.", "text": "Samsung Galaxy S10+ not receiving data Samsung Galaxy S10+ not receiving data for 10 minutes at a time; if phone isn't turned on then nothing syncs, data backfills afterwards. Some users report no data with screen off, others report intermittent loss even with screen on. The thread does not establish a single root cause. Possible factors discussed include Samsung-specific power saving features, OB1 collector issues, and Smart Switch migration, but no definitive cause is confirmed. Several workarounds are suggested: turning off 'Minimize Scanning' in settings, disabling OB1 collector, disabling Samsung power saving features for xDrip, and for MM users disabling 'Trust AutoConnect' or enabling 'Use Scanning'. One user reports success after uninstalling and reinstalling xDrip. G6 MiaoMiao OB1 G5 G6 MM collector Got it working by turning the OB1 collector off despite using the G6."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-830", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 830, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 830, "title": "xdrip api-secret correct url syntax", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/830", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/830", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "When using xDrip's local web service with an API secret set, requests like http://127.0.0.1:17580/status.json return 'Authentication failed - check api-secret', 'secret is required', and 'no secret supplied'. The service works without the secret.", "cause": "The API secret must be sent as a header, not as part of the URL (e.g., user:password@host syntax). The thread indicates that an API secret is not an authorization protocol that can be handled directly in the browser URL.", "fix": "Use a layer in between (e.g., an AJAX request with a JavaScript framework like jQuery) to set the 'api-secret' header. The secret should be the SHA1 hash in lowercase, as shown in the curl example: curl.exe -X DELETE -H \"api-secret: 911eea185f5c758ac275687da8b7eab50ad720e5\" -g https://...", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["api-secret", "local web service"], "evidence_quote": "So, the api secret should be part of the header. I'm not sure how you are sending the requests, but something has to put the api-secret in the header.", "text": "xdrip api-secret correct url syntax When using xDrip's local web service with an API secret set, requests like http://127.0.0.1:17580/status.json return 'Authentication failed - check api-secret', 'secret is required', and 'no secret supplied'. The service works without the secret. The API secret must be sent as a header, not as part of the URL (e.g., user:password@host syntax). The thread indicates that an API secret is not an authorization protocol that can be handled directly in the browser URL. Use a layer in between (e.g., an AJAX request with a JavaScript framework like jQuery) to set the 'api-secret' header. The secret should be the SHA1 hash in lowercase, as shown in the curl example: curl.exe -X DELETE -H \"api-secret: 911eea185f5c758ac275687da8b7eab50ad720e5\" -g https://...  api-secret local web service So, the api secret should be part of the header. I'm not sure how you are sending the requests, but something has to put the api-secret in the header."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-881", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 881, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 881, "title": "Bug: Pebble xDrip+ watchface keeps alarming about low smartphone battery", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/881", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/881", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The Pebble xDrip+ watchface keeps vibrating about low smartphone battery even though all battery alarms are turned off in xDrip+. The vibration occurs when the phone battery reaches 30% and repeats every 5-10 minutes, ignoring Pebble silence mode, and continues while charging until above 30%.", "cause": "The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A developer (jstevensog) initially suspected a bug in the watch face where it tracks phone battery with the same flag as watch battery, but later retracted that statement, saying he was wrong about the bug.", "fix": "No resolution is provided. The original reporter stopped using Pebble years ago and could not provide further information. A developer suggested trying the latest nightly and the 'All platforms' watch face, and disabling vibrations in the Pebble app settings, but this was not confirmed as a fix.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Pebble Time Steel"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["pebble", "watchface"], "evidence_quote": "Also, I was wrong about the bug in the watch face. Serves me right to take a sneaky look during work.", "text": "Bug: Pebble xDrip+ watchface keeps alarming about low smartphone battery The Pebble xDrip+ watchface keeps vibrating about low smartphone battery even though all battery alarms are turned off in xDrip+. The vibration occurs when the phone battery reaches 30% and repeats every 5-10 minutes, ignoring Pebble silence mode, and continues while charging until above 30%. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause. A developer (jstevensog) initially suspected a bug in the watch face where it tracks phone battery with the same flag as watch battery, but later retracted that statement, saying he was wrong about the bug. No resolution is provided. The original reporter stopped using Pebble years ago and could not provide further information. A developer suggested trying the latest nightly and the 'All platforms' watch face, and disabling vibrations in the Pebble app settings, but this was not confirmed as a fix. Pebble Time Steel pebble watchface Also, I was wrong about the bug in the watch face. Serves me right to take a sneaky look during work."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-889", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 889, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 889, "title": "Deleted calibration is not removed on watch in forced mode", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/889", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/889", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "When running the collector on the watch, a calibration deleted on the phone is not removed from the watch. The calibration remains on the watch and causes wrong data. 'Refresh DB' does not help, and 'Reset wear db' causes duplicate historical readings.", "cause": "The issue appears to be related to the watch running as collector and not syncing calibration deletions. The duplicates may be caused by merging data from watch and phone with different calibration sets, and possibly by the 'Rewrite History' setting.", "fix": "The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Suggestions include turning off 'Rewrite History' (which did not help), resetting wear DB followed by refresh DB (causes duplicates), and for Dexcom, resetting calibrations via 'Stop Sensor' and 'DON'T STOP, JUST RESET THE CALIBRATIONS' (not confirmed for Libre). The issue was closed due to inactivity.", "settings_changed": ["Rewrite History → off"], "devices": ["SW3", "Libre", "Miaomiao"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["collector", "Libre", "Miaomiao"], "evidence_quote": "I have now turned off \"rewrite history ticket\". It did not help...", "text": "Deleted calibration is not removed on watch in forced mode When running the collector on the watch, a calibration deleted on the phone is not removed from the watch. The calibration remains on the watch and causes wrong data. 'Refresh DB' does not help, and 'Reset wear db' causes duplicate historical readings. The issue appears to be related to the watch running as collector and not syncing calibration deletions. The duplicates may be caused by merging data from watch and phone with different calibration sets, and possibly by the 'Rewrite History' setting. The thread does not provide a definitive fix. Suggestions include turning off 'Rewrite History' (which did not help), resetting wear DB followed by refresh DB (causes duplicates), and for Dexcom, resetting calibrations via 'Stop Sensor' and 'DON'T STOP, JUST RESET THE CALIBRATIONS' (not confirmed for Libre). The issue was closed due to inactivity. SW3 Libre Miaomiao collector Libre Miaomiao I have now turned off \"rewrite history ticket\". It did not help..."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-896", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 896, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 896, "title": "Samsung s10e May patch caused constant reboots while using xdrip+", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/896", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/896", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "After May 24, the phone reboots every 1 to 10 minutes while using xDrip+. Stopping the sensor or deleting xDrip makes it work fine. The issue occurs on Samsung S10e and S10+ devices.", "cause": "Samsung introduced a significant bug in a system update that conflicts with xDrip's Samsung workarounds, causing constant reboots.", "fix": "Disable the 'Samsung workarounds' option in xDrip settings (Settings - Less common settings - Other misc options - Samsung Workarounds). Some users also found that a later Samsung update resolved the issue.", "settings_changed": ["Samsung workarounds → disabled"], "devices": ["Dexcom G5", "Samsung s10e", "Samsung s10 +"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["OB1 collector", "Samsung workarounds"], "evidence_quote": "Samsung appear to have introduced quite a significant bug this time... Try this: go in to xDrip settings and disable the `Samsung workarounds`", "text": "Samsung s10e May patch caused constant reboots while using xdrip+ After May 24, the phone reboots every 1 to 10 minutes while using xDrip+. Stopping the sensor or deleting xDrip makes it work fine. The issue occurs on Samsung S10e and S10+ devices. Samsung introduced a significant bug in a system update that conflicts with xDrip's Samsung workarounds, causing constant reboots. Disable the 'Samsung workarounds' option in xDrip settings (Settings - Less common settings - Other misc options - Samsung Workarounds). Some users also found that a later Samsung update resolved the issue. Dexcom G5 Samsung s10e Samsung s10 + OB1 collector Samsung workarounds Samsung appear to have introduced quite a significant bug this time... Try this: go in to xDrip settings and disable the `Samsung workarounds`"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-904", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 904, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 904, "title": "Tandem t:Slim X2 integration?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/904", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/904", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "A parent wants to connect to a Tandem t:Slim X2 pump to pull bolus/basal/Basal-IQ/Control-IQ information and sync it to xDrip followers and Nightscout/Tidepool. Currently there is no working xDrip integration with the Tandem t:Slim X2.", "cause": "Tandem had not opened the pump to the DIY community, and a BLE capture suggested that the Tandem app applies another layer of encryption/obfuscation on top of the normal BLE protocol layer, making direct integration very difficult.", "fix": "No code change was made in xDrip; the maintainer closed the issue stating xDrip cannot be changed to enable this. The workaround discussed is to use the external tconnectsync project to synchronize data from the t:connect Android app to Nightscout, optionally running it in Docker with the auto-update feature enabled.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Tandem t:Slim X2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["tandem", "t:connect", "tconnectsync", "nightscout", "tidepool", "xdrip", "bluetooth"], "evidence_quote": "As discussed above,  @jwoglom has done a brilliant job of creating a synchronizer between the tconnect mobile app and nightscout. Found here... \nhttps://github.com/jwoglom/tconnectsync", "text": "Tandem t:Slim X2 integration? A parent wants to connect to a Tandem t:Slim X2 pump to pull bolus/basal/Basal-IQ/Control-IQ information and sync it to xDrip followers and Nightscout/Tidepool. Currently there is no working xDrip integration with the Tandem t:Slim X2. Tandem had not opened the pump to the DIY community, and a BLE capture suggested that the Tandem app applies another layer of encryption/obfuscation on top of the normal BLE protocol layer, making direct integration very difficult. No code change was made in xDrip; the maintainer closed the issue stating xDrip cannot be changed to enable this. The workaround discussed is to use the external tconnectsync project to synchronize data from the t:connect Android app to Nightscout, optionally running it in Docker with the auto-update feature enabled. Tandem t:Slim X2 tandem t:connect tconnectsync nightscout tidepool xdrip bluetooth As discussed above,  @jwoglom has done a brilliant job of creating a synchronizer between the tconnect mobile app and nightscout. Found here... \nhttps://github.com/jwoglom/tconnectsync"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-907", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 907, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 907, "title": "Falling/Raising BG Falling Threshold Adjustment", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/907", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/907", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user reports that the available thresholds for xDrip to start alerting on rising or falling blood glucose are only 2 or 3 mg/dl per reading, which are too high for their low-carb lifestyle. They experience steady but gradual changes in blood sugar that do not trigger alerts until reaching high or low levels, making the feature unusable.", "cause": null, "fix": "The thread discusses the possibility of adding lower threshold values, but no specific fix is implemented or stated. A maintainer suggests using additional high/low alarms as a workaround, but the user finds this inadequate. No final resolution is provided.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "You can add another alarm set at 6.0 and another at 6.5. Now, you will get 2 alarms before your blood glucose reaches 7.0.", "text": "Falling/Raising BG Falling Threshold Adjustment The user reports that the available thresholds for xDrip to start alerting on rising or falling blood glucose are only 2 or 3 mg/dl per reading, which are too high for their low-carb lifestyle. They experience steady but gradual changes in blood sugar that do not trigger alerts until reaching high or low levels, making the feature unusable.  The thread discusses the possibility of adding lower threshold values, but no specific fix is implemented or stated. A maintainer suggests using additional high/low alarms as a workaround, but the user finds this inadequate. No final resolution is provided.   You can add another alarm set at 6.0 and another at 6.5. Now, you will get 2 alarms before your blood glucose reaches 7.0."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-91", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 91, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 91, "title": "Sugar Absorption model not quite complete", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/91", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/91", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The predicted BG system's carbohydrate absorption model is not accurate for different types of food, as demonstrated by treating a low with 20g of pure dextrose dissolved in water, which absorbed faster than the model predicted.", "cause": "The model uses a simple linear absorption model that does not account for food composition (fat, protein, fiber) or carbohydrate type, and absorption varies between individuals and days.", "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "xDrip+ implements the original DIYPS carbohydrate absorption model which is a simple linear absorption model.", "text": "Sugar Absorption model not quite complete The predicted BG system's carbohydrate absorption model is not accurate for different types of food, as demonstrated by treating a low with 20g of pure dextrose dissolved in water, which absorbed faster than the model predicted. The model uses a simple linear absorption model that does not account for food composition (fat, protein, fiber) or carbohydrate type, and absorption varies between individuals and days.    xDrip+ implements the original DIYPS carbohydrate absorption model which is a simple linear absorption model."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-936", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 936, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 936, "title": "https (ssl) support for local web services?", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/936", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/936", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "Garmin has removed http access from their web request API, breaking xDrip+ web services. Users report that the latest Garmin Connect Mobile app no longer works properly with xDrip+ local web services.", "cause": "Garmin intentionally removed http access in their Connect Mobile app, and xDrip's SSL support would require a certificate that fails chain verification because it isn't signed by a certification authority.", "fix": "Garmin fixed their app by including localhost (127.0.0.1) in the exceptions list for GCM, available in version 4.22, allowing Garmin apps to communicate with xDrip+ again.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Garmin"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["web services", "SSL", "http"], "evidence_quote": "Garmin has fixed their app Garmin Connect Mobile. With version 4.22 Garmin apps can communicate again with xDrip+.", "text": "https (ssl) support for local web services? Garmin has removed http access from their web request API, breaking xDrip+ web services. Users report that the latest Garmin Connect Mobile app no longer works properly with xDrip+ local web services. Garmin intentionally removed http access in their Connect Mobile app, and xDrip's SSL support would require a certificate that fails chain verification because it isn't signed by a certification authority. Garmin fixed their app by including localhost (127.0.0.1) in the exceptions list for GCM, available in version 4.22, allowing Garmin apps to communicate with xDrip+ again. Garmin web services SSL http Garmin has fixed their app Garmin Connect Mobile. With version 4.22 Garmin apps can communicate again with xDrip+."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-961", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 961, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 961, "title": "bug: missing save button in treatment profile editor", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/961", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/961", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "In the treatment profile editor, the save button is only visible after splitting or deleting a block. When a user changes a value and minimizes the keyboard instead of using the check button on the keyboard, the save button does not appear.", "cause": "The behavior is by design: minimizing the keyboard is equivalent to cancelling any edits made to the item being edited, whereas tapping the checkmark confirms the edit and makes the save button appear.", "fix": "No code change was made. The workaround is to tap the checkmark button on the keyboard after editing a value to confirm the edit, which makes the save button appear. Alternatively, if the keyboard is minimized, tap beside the value again to reopen the keyboard and then use the checkmark.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "Minimizing a keyboard, currently, is not equivalent to having tapped on the checkmark. It is equivalent to having changed your mind about editing the item you were on.", "text": "bug: missing save button in treatment profile editor In the treatment profile editor, the save button is only visible after splitting or deleting a block. When a user changes a value and minimizes the keyboard instead of using the check button on the keyboard, the save button does not appear. The behavior is by design: minimizing the keyboard is equivalent to cancelling any edits made to the item being edited, whereas tapping the checkmark confirms the edit and makes the save button appear. No code change was made. The workaround is to tap the checkmark button on the keyboard after editing a value to confirm the edit, which makes the save button appear. Alternatively, if the keyboard is minimized, tap beside the value again to reopen the keyboard and then use the checkmark.   Minimizing a keyboard, currently, is not equivalent to having tapped on the checkmark. It is equivalent to having changed your mind about editing the item you were on."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-962", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 962, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 962, "title": "feature request: sync predictive simulation settings from nightscout profile", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/962", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/962", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The user requests a feature to sync predictive simulation settings (insulin sensitivity and carb ratio) from the Nightscout profile into xDrip, so that these values do not have to be entered manually in xDrip.", "cause": null, "fix": null, "settings_changed": [], "devices": [], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "In xDrip predictive simulation settings are the profile values Insulin sensitivity and carb ratio. xDrip schould able to get this settings from the Nightscout Profile and also reread this settings If the Nightscout Profile has changed.", "text": "feature request: sync predictive simulation settings from nightscout profile The user requests a feature to sync predictive simulation settings (insulin sensitivity and carb ratio) from the Nightscout profile into xDrip, so that these values do not have to be entered manually in xDrip.     In xDrip predictive simulation settings are the profile values Insulin sensitivity and carb ratio. xDrip schould able to get this settings from the Nightscout Profile and also reread this settings If the Nightscout Profile has changed."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-963", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 963, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 963, "title": "G6 sensor restart problems with xDrip", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/963", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/963", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After restarting a Dexcom G6 sensor after 10 days, the user initially saw a warm-up period but then got a 'sensor failed start' message. A notification 'Auto Start Sensor Requesting Restart' appears but clicking it does nothing. Restarting the collector and re-pairing the transmitter did not help.", "cause": "The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but opasha suggests that the sensor's gold dot area and the transmitter's black rubber tips may be dirty, causing connection issues. Also, the 0000 method is said to do nothing.", "fix": "The proven method described by opasha: Stop sensor, remove transmitter for at least 15 minutes, clean the sensor's gold dots and the transmitter's black rubber tips, reconnect, start sensor as new with the same code (not 0000), wait 2 hours and a few minutes for warm-up. This method was confirmed to work by mrazek.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Dexcom G6", "Dexcom G5"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xDrip"], "evidence_quote": "This is the proven way to make it work: 1) Stop Sensor 2) Remove the transmitter with thin plastic (guitar pick or glucometer test strip) - set a time for 15 minutes - no less 3) Wipe down the sensor's two gold dot area - this gets sweat/oil/soap/water on it, so it needs to be completely cleaned to be functional - anything in the way will cause errors - MAKE SURE TO KEEP THE TRANSMITTER NEAR YOUR PHONE DURING THIS TIME. 4) Carefully clean the black rubber tips on your sensor on your arm - this is the point of contact those gold circle sensors make from your transmitter. Yes, they both need to be clean before contact with each other - I have tested this many times - the cleaner the contact, the longer your sensor can last - I have done 2 re-start sessions and got up to 27 days once. 5) After the 15 minutes are up and sensor and transmitter are cleaned, reconnect them and make sure your phone is still connected to your transmitter 6) Start Sensor as if brand new - enter the present time and date when asked and enter the same code for your transmitter - do not do the 0000 method - it does nothing 7) Wait 2 hours and a few minutes (for the final warm up) and it will automatically resume", "text": "G6 sensor restart problems with xDrip After restarting a Dexcom G6 sensor after 10 days, the user initially saw a warm-up period but then got a 'sensor failed start' message. A notification 'Auto Start Sensor Requesting Restart' appears but clicking it does nothing. Restarting the collector and re-pairing the transmitter did not help. The thread does not explicitly identify a root cause, but opasha suggests that the sensor's gold dot area and the transmitter's black rubber tips may be dirty, causing connection issues. Also, the 0000 method is said to do nothing. The proven method described by opasha: Stop sensor, remove transmitter for at least 15 minutes, clean the sensor's gold dots and the transmitter's black rubber tips, reconnect, start sensor as new with the same code (not 0000), wait 2 hours and a few minutes for warm-up. This method was confirmed to work by mrazek. Dexcom G6 Dexcom G5 xDrip This is the proven way to make it work: 1) Stop Sensor 2) Remove the transmitter with thin plastic (guitar pick or glucometer test strip) - set a time for 15 minutes - no less 3) Wipe down the sensor's two gold dot area - this gets sweat/oil/soap/water on it, so it needs to be completely cleaned to be functional - anything in the way will cause errors - MAKE SURE TO KEEP THE TRANSMITTER NEAR YOUR PHONE DURING THIS TIME. 4) Carefully clean the black rubber tips on your sensor on your arm - this is the point of contact those gold circle sensors make from your transmitter. Yes, they both need to be clean before contact with each other - I have tested this many times - the cleaner the contact, the longer your sensor can last - I have done 2 re-start sessions and got up to 27 days once. 5) After the 15 minutes are up and sensor and transmitter are cleaned, reconnect them and make sure your phone is still connected to your transmitter 6) Start Sensor as if brand new - enter the present time and date when asked and enter the same code for your transmitter - do not do the 0000 method - it does nothing 7) Wait 2 hours and a few minutes (for the final warm up) and it will automatically resume"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-980", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 980, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 980, "title": "Restart sensor and preemptive restarts option no longer works with new transmitter SN 81xxxx", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/980", "confidence": "high", "symptom": "With a new transmitter whose serial number starts with 81xxxx, preemptive sensor restart stops working; xDrip reports errors like 'Sensor Failed Start', 'Sensor marked FAILED', and 'Session Start Failed: Invalid'. The only workaround is to start the sensor using the Dexcom receiver and wait through the full two-hour warm-up. Other users with 81xxxx transmitters report that preemptive restart says 'not capable' or fails.", "cause": "Dexcom has restricted restart functionality in newer G6 transmitters. According to the maintainer, xDrip can currently only hard reset and perform preemptive restarts on G6 transmitters with firmware version 1.6.5.25, which includes all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX transmitters; transmitters with newer firmware (e.g., 1.6.5.27) cannot be restarted this way.", "fix": "No xDrip-side fix. The maintainer states that only G6 transmitters with firmware 1.6.5.25 (all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX) support hard reset/preemptive restart, and restarting other G6 transmitters requires temporarily removing the transmitter. A reported workaround is to start the sensor through the Dexcom receiver and wait through the warm-up period.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["G6"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["xdrip", "dexcom receiver", "official dexcom app", "non-native mode", "tandem x2"], "evidence_quote": "We currently can only hard reset, and perform preemptive restarts on, G6 if the firmware version is 1.6.5.25. This includes all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX transmitters.", "text": "Restart sensor and preemptive restarts option no longer works with new transmitter SN 81xxxx With a new transmitter whose serial number starts with 81xxxx, preemptive sensor restart stops working; xDrip reports errors like 'Sensor Failed Start', 'Sensor marked FAILED', and 'Session Start Failed: Invalid'. The only workaround is to start the sensor using the Dexcom receiver and wait through the full two-hour warm-up. Other users with 81xxxx transmitters report that preemptive restart says 'not capable' or fails. Dexcom has restricted restart functionality in newer G6 transmitters. According to the maintainer, xDrip can currently only hard reset and perform preemptive restarts on G6 transmitters with firmware version 1.6.5.25, which includes all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX transmitters; transmitters with newer firmware (e.g., 1.6.5.27) cannot be restarted this way. No xDrip-side fix. The maintainer states that only G6 transmitters with firmware 1.6.5.25 (all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX) support hard reset/preemptive restart, and restarting other G6 transmitters requires temporarily removing the transmitter. A reported workaround is to start the sensor through the Dexcom receiver and wait through the warm-up period. G6 xdrip dexcom receiver official dexcom app non-native mode tandem x2 We currently can only hard reset, and perform preemptive restarts on, G6 if the firmware version is 1.6.5.25. This includes all 80XXXX and some 81XXXX transmitters."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-985", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 985, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 985, "title": "Libre 2 NFC scan ", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/985", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/985", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "xDrip cannot scan Libre 2 with NFC and cannot retrieve history from patched LibreLink app, causing gaps in xDrip and Nightscout graphs when phone loses connection with sensor.", "cause": "Libre 2 data is encrypted and keys are not known, preventing direct NFC scan. Also, xDrip+ does not implement reception of the patched LibreLink intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' which contains scanned values.", "fix": "For Libre 2 EU, NFC scan is supported in xDrip+ (might require OOP2). For filling gaps from patched LibreLink, xDrip+ should implement receiving the intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' and handle scanned data, but this is not yet implemented.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Libre 2", "MiaoMiao3", "MiaoMiao2"], "android_versions": [], "driver_tags": ["NFC scan", "patched LibreLink", "intent", "OOP2", "MiaoMiao"], "evidence_quote": "The patched LibreLink sends also an Intent \"com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN\" with all the scanned values (historic and realtime). I tried it in a small test app and all the scanned values seem to be there. It's just xDrip+, which doesn't take this intent and fills the gap with the scanned values. Couldn't xDrip+ implement the reception of this patched LibreLink intent?", "text": "Libre 2 NFC scan  xDrip cannot scan Libre 2 with NFC and cannot retrieve history from patched LibreLink app, causing gaps in xDrip and Nightscout graphs when phone loses connection with sensor. Libre 2 data is encrypted and keys are not known, preventing direct NFC scan. Also, xDrip+ does not implement reception of the patched LibreLink intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' which contains scanned values. For Libre 2 EU, NFC scan is supported in xDrip+ (might require OOP2). For filling gaps from patched LibreLink, xDrip+ should implement receiving the intent 'com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN' and handle scanned data, but this is not yet implemented. Libre 2 MiaoMiao3 MiaoMiao2 NFC scan patched LibreLink intent OOP2 MiaoMiao The patched LibreLink sends also an Intent \"com.librelink.app.ThirdPartyIntegration.SENSOR_SCAN\" with all the scanned values (historic and realtime). I tried it in a small test app and all the scanned values seem to be there. It's just xDrip+, which doesn't take this intent and fills the gap with the scanned values. Couldn't xDrip+ implement the reception of this patched LibreLink intent?"}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-994", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 994, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 994, "title": "Screensaver shows bottom bar in Android 9.0", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/994", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/994", "confidence": "low", "symptom": "The screensaver in xDrip+ shows the very bright bottom navigation bar, which also slows down charging. The issue persists across several versions and on a Samsung S9+ with Android 10.", "cause": "The cause is not definitively established. The maintainer suspects it is a phone behavior rather than an xDrip issue, possibly related to Android navigation bar settings or day/night mode.", "fix": "No fix is provided. The maintainer suggests adjusting phone behavior, and the reporter notes that using day mode instead of night mode might affect the brightness, but no concrete resolution is given.", "settings_changed": [], "devices": ["Samsung S9+"], "android_versions": ["Android 10"], "driver_tags": [], "evidence_quote": "I don't think the Android control panel characteristics are a part of xDrip. I suspect this should be addressed by adjusting the behavior of the phone rather than the behavior of xDrip.", "text": "Screensaver shows bottom bar in Android 9.0 The screensaver in xDrip+ shows the very bright bottom navigation bar, which also slows down charging. The issue persists across several versions and on a Samsung S9+ with Android 10. The cause is not definitively established. The maintainer suspects it is a phone behavior rather than an xDrip issue, possibly related to Android navigation bar settings or day/night mode. No fix is provided. The maintainer suggests adjusting phone behavior, and the reporter notes that using day mode instead of night mode might affect the brightness, but no concrete resolution is given. Samsung S9+ Android 10  I don't think the Android control panel characteristics are a part of xDrip. I suspect this should be addressed by adjusting the behavior of the phone rather than the behavior of xDrip."}, {"id": "distilled:xdrip-996", "type": "distilled", "issue_id": 996, "repo": "NightscoutFoundation/xDrip", "number": 996, "title": "Unable to read Miaomiao data after upgrade to Android 10", "html_url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/996", "url": "https://github.com/NightscoutFoundation/xDrip/issues/996", "confidence": "medium", "symptom": "After upgrading to Android 10, xDrip can see the MiaoMiao device over Bluetooth but fails to connect or receive data. One user reports that switching to Wear collection produces only one reading before failing; another with Android 9 also reports the same problem. Some users later report nightly missed readings due to Bluetooth disconnects.", "cause": "The principal reported cause is an Android 10 Bluetooth communication issue with MiaoMiao: xDrip recognizes the MiaoMiao on Bluetooth scan and says 'communicating to device', but no data transfer occurs, while NFC reading works. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause, and one affected reporter is still on Android 9.", "fix": "No single official fix is given. User-stated workarounds include: restarting the phone, disabling/enabling Bluetooth, force-quitting xDrip and resetting the MiaoMiao (btdkomplex); following elrufoelrufo's instructions in issue #1001 (reedhuish); enabling 'trust auto connect', 'use scanning' and 'close gatt on ble disconnect' (James866); or disabling 'trust auto connect' (rodrigowebjump).", "settings_changed": ["trust auto connect → enabled", "use scanning → enabled", "close gatt on ble disconnect → enabled", "trust auto connect → disabled"], "devices": ["MiaoMiao", "Libre"], "android_versions": ["Android 10", "Android 9"], "driver_tags": ["bluetooth", "wear collection", "nfc"], "evidence_quote": "Oddly it started to work again after disabling bluetooth, force quitting xDrip, restarting the phone, and resetting the Miaomiao. It then continued to fail to take readings for another 10 minutes or so and then started working as if nothing was wrong.", "text": "Unable to read Miaomiao data after upgrade to Android 10 After upgrading to Android 10, xDrip can see the MiaoMiao device over Bluetooth but fails to connect or receive data. One user reports that switching to Wear collection produces only one reading before failing; another with Android 9 also reports the same problem. Some users later report nightly missed readings due to Bluetooth disconnects. The principal reported cause is an Android 10 Bluetooth communication issue with MiaoMiao: xDrip recognizes the MiaoMiao on Bluetooth scan and says 'communicating to device', but no data transfer occurs, while NFC reading works. The thread does not establish a definitive root cause, and one affected reporter is still on Android 9. No single official fix is given. User-stated workarounds include: restarting the phone, disabling/enabling Bluetooth, force-quitting xDrip and resetting the MiaoMiao (btdkomplex); following elrufoelrufo's instructions in issue #1001 (reedhuish); enabling 'trust auto connect', 'use scanning' and 'close gatt on ble disconnect' (James866); or disabling 'trust auto connect' (rodrigowebjump). MiaoMiao Libre Android 10 Android 9 bluetooth wear collection nfc Oddly it started to work again after disabling bluetooth, force quitting xDrip, restarting the phone, and resetting the Miaomiao. It then continued to fail to take readings for another 10 minutes or so and then started working as if nothing was wrong."}]};
